   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_a_mh.html"> √ aṃh    √ aṃh, “be narrow or distressing” Such a root is inferable from the derivatives: aṃhatí RV. aṃhú V.B. áṅghri ? B.+ áhi V.+ áṃhas V.+ aṃhīyas B.S. aghá V.+ ahī́ RV. The verb-form anāha RV1. is of wholly doubtful meaning and connection. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_ak_s.html"> √ 1 akṣ    √ 1 akṣ, “attain” Present I.ákṣat RV1., akṣase E1 Passive akṣya- Future Simple Future: akṣiṣyati, akṣyati Periphrastic Future: akṣitā, aṣṭā Aorist RAo: ācikṣat -iṣ-Ao: ā́kṣiṣus RV1 Perfect ānakṣa, ākṣāṇá ? RV1 Causative akṣaya- Desiderative ācikṣiṣa- Derivatives PPP: aṣṭa; 1Abs: akṣitvā, aṣṭvā Derived Nouns: akṣiṣṭha. JB. A secondary root-form from √ 1 aś, aṃś and occurring in a few isolated forms. Indra and Agni are called akṣiṣṭhau vahiṣṭhau devānām at JB. i. 304. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_ak_s.html"> √ 2 akṣ    √ 2 akṣ, “mutilate” Present V. -akṣṇoti etc. AV. ŚB Verbal Nouns -aṣṭa V.B.S Only used with prefix nis; does not appear to have anything to do with the preceding root. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_a_gg.html"> √ aṅg    √ aṅg, “move” Present I. aṅgatu C1 Perfect ānaṅga etc.etc Causative aṅgayati A single occurrence, doubtless artificial, in the Nalodya. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ac.html"> √ ac, añc    √ ac, añc, “bend” Present I. añcati etc. AV.B., -te B.; ácati etc V.B., -te etc. AV.B.S Passive acyate etc. V.B.+ añcyate Future Simple Future: añciṣyati Periphrastic Future: añcitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: āñcīt Perfect ānañca, acire JB Causative añcayati etc. C Desiderative añciciṣa- Verbal Nouns PPP: akná B.S., acita E., añcita E.+ akta; 2Abs: -ácya V.B.; -ā́cam B Derivatives -añc V.+ añká V.+ áñcana V.+ aṅku- V.+ -añcin B. áṅkas RV. -acana S.+ akṣṇá B.S. -áñcas RV. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_aj.html"> √ aj    √ aj, “drive” Present I. ájati -te. etc. V.B Passive ajyáte etc. RV Future ajiṣyati, ajitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: ājiṣus LŚS1 Perfect ajiṣus etc Desiderative ajijiṣa- Verbal Nouns PPP: -ajita ? ŚB.; 2Abs: -ajya S.; -áje RV Derivatives ágra? V.+ ajaka C. ájman V. -āja B.+ áj V. ájana V.+ -ájya V.B. ājí V.+ -ája RV. ajirá V.+ ájra? RV. ajá V.+ ájma RV. ajvin S. The form ajus only by very doubtful conjecture to RV. V. 6.10; ājiṣus variant to AV. āviṣus; ajita in -prajita, possible for prājita (or pra-jita, √ 1 ji ?). Meanings ájati ájate v drive. apa drive away. abhi drive near or together, join. ava drive down. ā bring near, fetch; approach. ud Ā drive out, take off. upa drive near or hither. nis drive out. vi drive asunder, rush through (A). sam drive together, unite; overthrow. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_a_jj.html"> √ añj    √ añj, “anoint” Present I. añjet S1 VII. anákti aṅkté etc. V.+ Passive ajyáye etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: aṅkṣyati añjiṣyati Periphrastic Future: aṅktā añjitā Aorist √-Ao: ajyāt; āñji RAo: āñjijat -iṣ-Ao: āñjīs TA Perfect ānañja B. anajā anajyāt RV.), ānajé etc. RV Causative añjayati etc. S.+ Desiderative añjijiṣa- Verbal Nouns PPP: aktá V.+; 1Abs: aṅktvā S., aktvā́ B. añjitvā; 2Abs: -ájya B.S Derivatives aṅga C. -ajya C. áṅjana V.+ aktā́ RV. aṅgya C. -āja E.+ áṅjas V.+ -akti E.+ añjaka C. ā́jya V.+ añjí V.B. aktú V.B. Meanings ákti aṅkté v PPP aktá smear, anoint, adorn (Ā refl.); glorify, extol; make clear, manifest. Caus. añjayati smear, anoint anu anoint abhi smear, anoint (Ā refl.), adorn. ā anoint, smooth, embellish, glorify. ni smear, anoint; Ā slip into, hide among (antar). prati anoint, adorn. vi Ā anoint throughout; anoint or adorn one's self with (I or A); make clear, bring to notice, betray. Caus. cause to become clear, reveal. abhivi P. become clear, appear. sam anoint, adorn, embellish, honour; join, unite; lick, devour; Ā feed on (I). Cf. abhivyakta, abhyakta, vyákta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_a_t.html"> √ aṭ    √ aṭ, “wander” Present I. aṭati -te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: aṭiṣyati E Periphrastic Future: aṭitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: āṭit Perfect āṭa Causative āṭaya- Desiderative aṭiṭiṣa- Intensive aṭaṭya- Verbal Nouns PPP: aṭita C.; 1Abs: aṭitvā C Derivatives -aṭa C. aṭavī ? C. āṭa PB.+ aṭana C. aṭyā C. aṭāṭyā C. Apparently a modern form of √ at ; āṭa in PB. is a proper name. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_a_n_th.html"> √ aṇṭh    √ aṇṭh “visit” Present VI. aṇṭhati C. Verbal Nouns PPP: aṇṭhita C. ( Bö.) Meaning Whitney: visit; Monier Williams: aṇṭhate, ānaṇṭhe, aṇṭhitum, to go, move, tend L. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_at.html"> √ at    √ at, “wander” Present I. atasi átant átamāna RV4 Verbal Nouns PPP: -atita C.; 2Abs: -atya S Derivatives atasí RV. átithi ? V.+ átya RV.B. -áti ? RV. atithín RV.C. Meanings ati átate v walk about, wander, run. sam go or come to (A). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ad.html"> √ ad    √ ad, “eat” Present I. adasva E II. átti etc. (ādat ādan) V.+, adāná RV Passive adyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future atsyati V.S Periphrastic Future: attā Aorist √-Ao: adyāsam JUB RAo: ādidat Perfect āda, āditha Causative ādayati B.+, adayate etc. S Verbal Nouns áttum V.+, -tave V., -tos V.; attvā́ya B Derivatives -ád V.+ attí B. attrín RV. -advan V. -ada AV.+ attavya C. áttri(átri) V.+ -advara ŚE. -adaka E.+ attṛ́ AV.+ ánna V.+ ā́dana RV. -adana V.+ áttra RV. ádman V.B.S. ādín V.+ adanīya C. attrá V. -ádya V.+ ādyá AV.+ Meanings atti v eat, feed on, consume, devour. Caus. ādayáti, te. ā, pra, vi, sam = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_an.html"> √ an    √ an, “breathe” Present I. ánati (anet ana ānat ánant) etc. AV.B., -te JB II. ániti etc. (anánti anyā́t ā́nīt) V.+ VI. anáti (3s.) AV Future Simple Future: aniṣyati B Periphrastic Future: anitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: āniṣus AV Perfect āna V Causative ānayati etc. AV.+, -te E Desiderative aniniṣat- Verbal Nouns anita B.; anitum B.; -anya B.; -ānam B.S Derivatives aná B.U. -ánana RV. ánila B.+ āná V.+ -anátha VS. ānana E+ Meanings ániti ánati v breathe, live. apa breathe out or away. ud breathe up, breathe away. pra breathe in, respire, live. Caus. revive. vi breathe, breathe through. sam breathe, live. anusam breathe after. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_am.html"> √ am    √ am, “injure” Present I. áme etc. V.B II. amīṣi amīti amánti āmīt amāte amīṣva V.B Passive amyate MS Aorist RAo: āmamat etc. V.B Perfect āmire ŚB. emāna emuṣá ? RV. (emūṣá ŚB.) Causative āmáyati etc. V.B Verbal Nouns PPP: ānta, amita Derivatives áma V.B. -ámana ŚB. āmá? V.+ -āmayitnu V. amáti V.B. aminá RV. ā́mana? AV.MS. ámati V.B. ámīva V.+ -āmaya V.+ ámatra RV. amla? E.+ -ā́mis? RV. Meanings amīti v press on, harm (only PPP emuṣám harmful, pernicious). Caus. āmáyati suffer, be sick. abhi & pari = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ay.html"> √ ay    √ ay, see √ 1 i 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_arc.html"> √ arc, ṛc    √ arc, ṛc, “shine, praise” Present I. árcati etc. V.+, arce RV1. arcase (1s.) RV1 Passive ṛcyáte V Future Simple Future: arciṣyati C. (ārkṣyánt ? ŚB.) Aorist RAo: ārcicat -iṣ-Ao: ārcīt Perfect ānarca E.+, ānṛcús V., ānarcus E.+, ānṛce RV1 Causative arcayati -te etc. V.+ (arcyate U.E.) Desiderative arciciṣa- Verbal Nouns PPP: arcita E.; Inf: arcitum E.; 1Abs: arcitvā E.; 2Abs: -arcya E.+; ṛcáse RV Derivatives árc RV. arcatra- RV. arcí V.+ -ṛca AV.+ arká V.+ arcátri RV. arcín RV. -ṛcas RV. arcā́ V.+ arcana E.+ arcitṛ E. -ṛkti? RV. (suv-) arcaka C. arcanīya E.+ arcís V.+ ṛkvá RV. arcya E.+ arcanā́nas V. ṛ́c V.+ ṛ́kvan V. Meanings árcati 1 v beam, shine, sing, praise, honour, adorn. Caus. arcayati, te, PPP arcita (q.v.) cause to shine; honour, salute. abhi sing, praise, honour. pra shine forth, intone, sing, honour. sam honour, worship, adorn. Cf. ṛcáse. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_arj.html"> √ arj    √ arj see √ 1 ṛj, ṛñj 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_art.html"> √ art    √ art see √ ṛt 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_arh.html"> √ arh    √ arh, “deserve” Present I. árhati etc. V.+, -te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: arhiṣyati Periphrastic Future: arhita Aorist etc. RAo: ārjihat -iṣ-Ao: ārhīt; Precative: arhyāsam Ao/Ps/3/sg: ārhi Perfect ānṛhús TS1., arhire RV1 Causative arhayati , etc. S.+ Desiderative arjihiṣa - Verbal Nouns arháse RV1 Derivatives arghá V.+ -árha V.+ arháṇā V.+ -arghya C. arhaṇa C. arhaṇīya C. Meanings árhati v (arhate) deserve, merit, have a right or be worthy to (A or Inf), be liable to, capable of (A); dare, be obliged or able to (Inf). Caus. arhayati honour or present with (I). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_av.html"> √ av    √ av, “favor” Present I. ávati etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: aviṣyáti V.B Periphrastic Future: avitā C Aorist √-Ao: avyās -āt V.B.S -iṣ-Ao: ā́vīt etc. (aviḍḍhi etc. aviṣat etc.) V.B.S Perfect ā́va ā́vitha etc. V.+ Causative ā́vayas -at V.B.U Verbal Nouns -ūta RV.; ávitave V.B.; -ávya RV Derivatives áva RV. avitṛ́ V.B.S. ávi ? V.+ oma RV. avana C. -avitra B.S. -avī? V. óman V.B. ávas V.B. áviṣṭha RV. ūtí V.+ omán V.+ avis -? RV. ū́ma V.B.S. Common in V.; quite rare in later language. Meanings ávati v PPP uta favour, like, delight in (A), accept; further, protect, aid, comfort, satiate. Caus. āvayati enjoy, eat, devour. upa caress, encourage, join (A or D). pra = S. Cf. ávant. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_az.html"> √ 1 aś, aṃś    √ 1 aś, aṃś, “attain” Present V. aśnóti aśnuté etc. V.+ IX ? aśniyāt, aśnīs M Future Simple Future: aśiṣyate aśnuviṣyāmahe ŚB1 Periphrastic Future: aśitā, aṣṭā Aorist √-Ao: ā́ṣṭa ā́śata aṣṭa V.B., aśyā́t aśītá etc. V.B.S., aṣṭu V. āśi Th Ao: aśema RV., aśemahi SV RAo: āśiśat -s-Ao: ākṣi V., ákṣat RV. (cf. √ 1 akṣ ) -iṣ-Ao: āśiṣṭa Perfect ānáṃśa ānaśús etc. V.+, ānaśé etc. V.+ (ānāśa ānaśma ānaśyām anáśāmahai RV., ānaśadhve S.) āśatus etc. āśāthe etc. RV Causative āśaya - Desiderative aśiśṣa- Intensive aśāśya- Verbal Nouns aṣṭum K.; áṣṭave V.B., aṣṭavai JB.S.; aśitum E.; -aṣṭa V.B Derivatives áṃśa V.+ aśana B.+ -aśnuva AGS. -āśa ŚŚS. áṣṭi V.+ aśī - VS1. -aśnuvín VS. ā́śā V.+ Compare √ 1 akṣ and √ 2 naś (to which latter the forms ānaṭ etc. are here referred). Derivatives more doubtfully referable to this root are: áśan RV. áśman V.+ áśva V.+ āśú V.+ aśáni V.+ áśri V.+ áṣṭrā V.+ ā́śīyas B. áśna RV. áśru V.+ āśiná RV. ā́śiṣṭha V.B.U. Meanings aśnóti aśnuté 1 v attain, reach, come to, arrive at (A); obtain, get, befall, betide; overcome; offer, bring. abhi reach, obtain, overwhelm. upa obtain, get. vi reach, attain, get; fill, penetrate. sam attain, get, receive; fall to one's share. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_az.html"> √ 2 aś    √ 2 aś, “eat” Present I. aśa R1 IX. aśnā́ti (aśāna) aśnīte etc. V.+ Passive aśyáte AV.+ Future Simple Future: aśiṣyáti etc. B.+ Periphrastic Future: aśitā Aorist √-Ao: aśyāt RAo: āśiśat -iṣ-Ao: ā́śīt etc. V.+ Perfect ā́śa V.+ (-āśvāṃs B.) Causative āśayati B.+ (ā́śita RV.); aśāpaya- MGS Desiderative áśiśiṣati etc. B.+ Intensive aśāśya- Verbal Nouns PPP: aśitá V.+; Inf: aśitum U.; 1Abs: aśitvā́ V.+; 2Abs: -áśya B Derivatives -áś AV. aśitavyá B.+ áśna V. āśi S. -áśana V.+ aśitṛ́ AV.+ aśni TA. āśyá AV. ? + aśanā́ B.U. aśitra B.+ -āśa E.+ áśiṣṭha B. -aśanīya S.+ aśúṣa RV. -āśaka B. aśiśiṣu S. -āśin B.+ -āśayitavya B. Doubtless ultimately the same with √ 1 aś . Meanings aśnā́ti v PPP aśitá 2 partake of, eat, drink, taste, enjoy. Caus. āśayati feed (2A). Des áśiśiṣati wish to eat. ati eat before (A). upa = S. pra the same; Caus. feed. sam = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_as.html"> √ 1 as    √ 1 as, “be” Present II. ásti sánti etc. (edhí) V.+ (sva sma smahe asate M., syāmahe C1.) Perfect ā́sa ā́sitha etc. V.+ Derivatives ásu V.+ ásta V.+-asti V.+-āsa(itiha-) AV.+ stí V.B. Meanings ásti 1 v be, exist, happen, become; be present or at hand; fall or belong to (G or D), be enough for (G), be able to (D); turn to, serve for (2D). astu or evamastu well, so be it. With na not be, be gone. Pers. or impers. with another fin. verb = I happen to or it happens that I, e.g. asti paśyasi do you happen to see ? asmi vikrīṇe I happen to sell. ati be beyond, surpass (A). api be in or with (L), fall or belong to (L or D); partake of (impers. w. G & L). abhi be above, rule, overcome, conquer. win; *fall to one's (G) share. upa be in or with, partake of (A). pari overtake; pass or spend (time). pra be prominent, excel. prati equal, emulate (A). sam equal, reach; be together with (saha). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_as.html"> √ 2 as    √ 2 as, “throw” Present I. asati etc. RV1. ( ?asan) E.+ IV. ásyati etc. V.+, asyate etc. RV.B Passive asyate etc. AV.+ Future Simple Future: asiṣyáti etc. RV.+ Periphrastic Future: asitā Aorist √-Ao: asyāt R1.; āsi C1 Th Ao: āsthat etc. AV1.K1.C. ( ?see √ sthā) RAo: āsiṣat -iṣ-Ao: āsiṣṭa Perfect ā́sa etc. RV.+, āse RV1 Causative āsayati etc. E.+ Desiderative asisiṣa- Verbal Nouns PPP: asta V.+, asita R1.; ástave B.,-tavaí B.; Inf: asitum E1.; 1Abs: asitvā S.; 2Abs: -ásya V.+;-ā́sam B.S.U Derivatives -ás V. ásira RV1. astrá V.+ -āsa AV.+ ásana V.+ ásiṣṭha V. -asya V.+ -āsin AV.+ asanā́ RV. -asti C. -asyā E.+ āsyá AV. -asanīya C. -astavya C. asrá TB1. -āsana C. así ? V.+ ástṛ V.B. Meanings ásyati 2 v (asati), PPP asta (q.v.) throw, cast, shoot at (L, D, or G), with (I). apa throw away, lay down, doff, leave, give up. abhi (also asati, te) throw, hurl; throw one's self upon, take to, practise, study, read; repeat, double, reduplicate (g.). ud throw up, lift, throw away; rise from (A). vyud spread, disperse, dismiss, give up. ni (also asati) throw or put down, lay aside, put or pour in (L), apply to (L), turn (the eyes) upon (L), deposit, commit to (loc), give up, relinquish; bring forward, mention. upani put down, bring forward, indicate, insinuate. vini (also asati) lay asunder, spread; put, place, turn upon or in, apply to (L), deposit, commit, entrust to (L). saṃni (also asati) put down (together), take off; put or place on (L), commit or entrust to (L or G); abandon, relinquish, give up, esp. the world, i.e. become an ascetic. nis throw out, send away, banish from (Ab); keep off, remove, destroy. parāṃ cast away, expose (a child); leave, reject, refute. pari cast or turn about, throw down, toss, upset (also Caus. ) put on (Ā). vipari overturn, upset, invert. transpose, change. pra cast forwards, hurl, throw or put in (L), throw down. prati throw towards or against; cast away, shake off. vi cast asunder, break in pieces, scatter. sam put together, join; P. be composed with (I). Cf. apāsya, abhyasta, upanyasta, nyasta, paryasta, vipáryasta, vyatyasta, vyasta, samasta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ah.html"> √ ah    √ ah, “say” Perfect ā́ha āhús V.+, āttha āhatus V.+ Derivatives -āha ? PB1. If nirāha is from this root, then perhaps svā́hā V.+ is also to be referred to it. Meanings (only pf. ā́ha) say, speak, tell (w. D or A of pers. & A of th.), call, name (2A); state, declare to be (A); attribute or adjudge (A) to (G). adhi speak or intercede for (D). anu recite, repeat. abhi speak to (A), answer, reply; tell (D of pers. & A of th.). nis speak out, express. pra pronounce, deliver; say tell, name, declare (= S.). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_aa_jch.html"> √ āñch    √ āñch, “tear” Present I. āñchati C Derivatives āñchana C. Found only in the Suśruta, and doubtless artificial. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_aap.html"> √ āp    √ āp, “obtain” Present V. āpnóti etc. AV.+, āpnute E Passive āpyáte etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: āpsyati B.+,-te B.R Periphrastic Future: āptā B Aorist √-Ao: āpyāsam AA. āpi B.+ Th Ao: ā́pat etc. V.+ (apeyam AV.) RAo: āpipan ŚB. (āpīpipat BAU.) -s-Ao: āpsīs E Perfect ā́pa āpitha etc. V.+, āpiré āpāná RV Causative āpayati etc. B.+,-te etc. B. (āpipayiṣet ŚB.) Desiderative ī́psati etc. AV.+, īpsate etc. B.E. (aipsīt etc. B.) Verbal Nouns PPP: āptá V.+; Inf: ā́ptum B.+; 1Abs: āptvā́ B.+; 2Abs: -āpya B.+ Derivatives -āpa B.+ -āpanīya S.+ -āptṛ C. īpsā E.+ -āpaka E.+ āpaneya U1. ā́pnāna ? RV.S. -īpsin U. -āpin U.+ āpí V.+ -āpayitavya U.C. īpsu S.+ āpyá AV.+ ā́pti AV.+ āpayitṛ U.C. āpipayiṣu E. āpana V.+ āptavya U.+ To a more original form of the root (āp is perhaps ā+ ap) doubtless belong also: ápas V. apás V.B. . ápnas, apna- RV.-apta ( ?án-) RV. BR. regard apás at RV.iii.6.7 as a verb form from this simpler root. Meanings āpnoti v (āpnute), PPP āptá (q.v.) obtain, reach, overtake, meet with, find; acquire, win, get, beget; pervade, occupy; befall, betide. P. become filled. Caus. āpayati cause to reach or attain, bring to, let a person (A) have or feel a thing (A). Des ī́psati, te (q.v.) anu attain. abhi reach to, attain; Caus. accomplish. ava reach, get at, meet, acquire, obtain, incur. samava the same. pari reach, acquire, make up, finish. pra reach, arrive at, come upon (A); obtain, win, get, catch, incur; befall, betide, exist, be; result or follow from a rule (also P.). Caus. cause to arrive at, bring to (2A or D of pers. & A of th.); announce, bring before the court (j.), obtain, get. anupra reach, attain, meet, follow, imitate; come, arrive. samanupra reach, attain, arrive. saṃpra reach, arrive at, come upon, obtain, win, catch. anusaṃpra = samanupra. vi pervade, occupy, reach up to (ā). sam reach, obtain, get, win; finish, accomplish. Caus. cause to reach or attain; achieve, finish, conclude. parisam P. be comprehended in, belong to (L). Cf. avāpta, āpāná, parisamāpta, paryāpta, prāpta, vyāpta, samāpta, saṃprāpra. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_aar.html"> √ ār    √ ār, “praise” ( ?) Present IV. ā́ryanti RV2 Verbal Nouns PPP: āritá RV Is perhaps a form of ā + √ ṛ “resort to, have recourse to”; ā́ryanti in both occurrences is accented as if it contained a preposition. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_aas.html"> √ ās    √ ās, “sit” Present I. āsati -te etc. E.+ II. ā́ste etc. (ā́sīna) V.+ (āsāná RV2.), āsti E IV. āsyati -te etc. E Passive āsyate E.+ Future Simple Future: āsiṣyate etc. B.+,-yáti TS Periphrastic Future: āsitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: āsiṣṭa etc. B.S Perfect āsā́ṃ cakre etc. B.+, āsāṃ cakāra E Causative āsayati B Desiderative āsisiṣa- Verbal Nouns PPP: āsitá B.+; Inf: āsitum B.+, āstum K.; 1Abs: āsitvā́ V.S.; 2Abs: -āsya C Derivatives āsá V.B. -āsya U.+ -āsanīya C. -āsti C. -āsā U. āsyā E.+ āsitavyá B.+ -āsaka E.+ āsana AV.+ -āsitṛ E. Meanings ā́ste 2 (āsti, āsati, āsate, āsyati, āsyate), v PPP āsitá (q.v.) & ā́sīna sit, seat one's self on (L); settle down, keep quiet, rest, lie, dwell, stay, remain; continue, keep on (w. nom of a PPP, Adj or subst., also Adv or ger.); belong to (G); be or turn to (D); also trans. keep, perform celebrate. Caus. āsayati cause to sit down. adhi sit or lie down upon (A), inhabit enter, get into, undergo; preside, rule anu sit near or round (A), sit down after another (A); worship, celebrate. ud sit apart, be indifferent or passive. upa be seated, esp. sit near or round (A); surround, invest; expect, wait for or on, honour, respect; partake of, enjoy, celebrate, perform, execute; get into, inhabit; undergo, take pains, endeavour to (PPP); keep on, continue (PPP or ger.). Caus. upāsayati cause to sit or to do homage.* paryupa sit upon or around, surround; revere, worship; partake of, enjoy. samupa be seated; perform, execute; celebrate, revere, wait upon, attend. pari sit or assemble round (A), endeavour at (A); keep quiet, i.e. do nothing. sam sit (together), assemble round (A), hold a meeting; abide, dwell in (L); take to, exercise (A); also = pratisam be a match for, withstand. Cf. adhṣāsita, udāsīna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_i.html"> √ 1 i, ī, ay    √ 1 i, ī, ay, “go” Present I. áyate etc. V.+, ayati etc. AV1. ? + II i. iye RV1. iyāte RV1., ī́mahe V.B., iyāná V.+, íyati RV1., -iyánt ŚB.M. (imi TA1.; aitat AV1.; yan RV1.; īyāná SV1.; īyámāna ŚB.; īmahi C.) éti yánti etc. V.+,-ité -iyate etc. B.+ IV. ī́yate etc. V.B.C V. see √ 2 i Passive īyate C Future Simple Future: eṣyáti etc. AV.+,-te etc. B.+; ayiṣyati etc. B.+ Periphrastic Future: etā́ etc. B.+ Aorist √-Ao: īyāt etc. B.+ (iyāsam GGS.) -s-Ao: (adhy-) aiṣṭa -iṣ-Ao: āyiṣṭa Perfect iyā́ya īyús etc. V.+ iyayitha (iyétha V.B., iyátha V.)-ayāṃ cakre E.+ Causative (praty-) āyayati etc. (-āyyate) C.; (adhy-) āpayati -te etc. TA.E.+ āpipat Desiderative ayiyiṣate , iyiṣati Intensive īyāyate PU1 Verbal Nouns PPP: itá V.+,-īta C.; Inf: étum B.+, étave étavaí V.B., étos V.B.S.; 1Abs: itvā́ B.U.; 2Abs: -ítya V.+,-īya C.;-áyya B.; áyase, ityaí, iyádhyai RV.;-ā́yam V.B Derivatives áya V.+ -it B.+ -etu RV. -āpaka C. ayátha RV.S. íti V.+ etavyá B.+ -āpya C. áyana V.+ ití V.B. etṛ́ V.+ -āpana E.+ -āya V.+ -itya B.S. éma VS. -āpayitṛ C. -āyin AV.+ ityā́ V.B. éman RV. -āpin C. -āyana AV.U. -ítvan V. -eya E.+ -āyaka C. āyú V.+ itvará RV.C. éva V.B. -āyana E. ā́yu V.+ -itha RV. -ā̆yitavya C. ā́yus V.+ īti E.+ -āyuka B. īya- RV. The last three derivatives only with prati; the four preceding, only with adhi. The forms most distinctly calling for the admisson of a root-form ī are, in the older language, ī́mahe V.B. (common in RV.), īyām and īyāte and īyus B.U., īyāná SV. (all single occurrences); in the later language,-īta, īti, -īya (all rare or sporadic). The present-stem ī́ya is improperly called intensive. Meanings éti áyate áyati 2 v (íyati), ité & iyate (only – ṃ), P. īyate, PPP itá (mostly – ṃ) go, come (punar again or back); go to or towards, approach (A); attain, get; go or come from (Ab); cease, pass away; go on, continue (w. Pr PPP); be engaged in (I); w. A of an abstrans. often = become or get w. a PPP or Adj (cf. gam); ī́yate, PPP īyāná (also w. pass. mg), 1. pl. īmahe move, speed, hasten to (A, D or L), approach with prayers, implore, ask, request (w. 2A). – accha go to, approach (A). ati go beyond or past; go in, enter; overstep, exceed, overwhelm; leave behind, neglect, escape. abhyati go beyond, pass, neglect. vyati = abhyati + overcome, vanquish; cease, deviate, decline from (Ab). adhi perceive, notice, call to mind; repeat, study, learn, recite (esp. Ā adhīté). Caus. adhyāpayati (te) cause to learn, teach (2A). samadhi Ā study, learn. anu go along or after, follow, pursue; obey, resemble, imitate (A). antar go within or between; remove, exclude from (Ab, r. G). apa go away, retire, escape, disappear. vyapa go asunder, part; cease, disappear. api enter, dissolve into (A); perish, die. abhi come up to, approach, appear; go against or along, enter (A); reach, meet, attain, get; betide, befall. ava go down, descend; go to, rush on (A); go off, depart; look at, consider, perceive, notice; learn, understand; know that – (2A or A & N w. iti); w. īmahe conciliate, beg pardon of (G), for (A). samava meet in (A); consider, regard as (A w. iva). ā come, go to (A or D), fall or get into (A); befall, betide; w. ūrdhvam rise. abhyā approach, come or go to (A), meet with (A or I); w. bhūyas come back. udā go up, rise; go out, come forth. upā come near, approach, betake one's self to or into (A), ask or beg for (2A). paryā walk about, circumambulate (A), return. pratyā return, come back to (A). samā approach together, gather, assemble at or in (A or L); meet, encounter (I samam); marry (I); come near, go to, enter (A). ud go up, rise, mount, increase; spring forth, appear, begin. apod retire, withdraw, abstain from (Ab). abhyud rise, come forth, appear. samud rise. upa come near, arrive, enter from (Ab) into (A), address one's self to (A), approach sex., marry; attain, get, meet with (A of an abstrans., cf. S.); befall, betide. abhyupa arrive at, come to, meet, encounter; attain, get undergo, incur (w. A of an abstrans. = upa); suppose, believe, assent. samupa come together, meet, encounter, approach sex., turn or address one's self to; attain, get; come forth, appear; befall, betide. ni go or fall into (A). nis come forth. parā go away, depart, die. pari walk about, circumambulate, surround; come to, attain, get. vipari turn about, return; fail. saṃpari circumambulate, enclose; ponder on, consider. pra go onward, set out, advance proceed; go to, attain, get; go on, succeed, prosper; go off, depart, die. anupra go after, seek for, follow. abhipra come near, go to, fall to one's (A) share; call to mind, think of, understand, consent to (A). saṃpra come together, meet. prati go towards or against, meet, encounter; come near or back; address one's self to (A); fall to one's (D) share; accept, assume, admit, acknowledge, approve, believe, become or be sure of, trust, confide. P. pratīyate be understood, result from, follow. Caus. pratyāyayati make understood, show, explain, prove, convince. vi go asunder, disperse, spread over, pervade; cease, disappear, perish. abhivi come from different parts to (A). sam come together, assemble, meet, encounter, approach sex. (A or sārdham, saha w. I), agree, harmonize with (I). anusam = seq. + pass into, enter (A). abhisam & upasam go or come (together) to (A). Cf. atīta, adhīta, antárita, anvita, ápīta, apeta, abhipreta, abhyatīta, abhyupeta, udita, udetos, upeta, parīta, pareta, pratīta, prādhīta, preta, prétya, viparīta, vīta, vyatīta, vyapeta, samanvita, samaveta, sámita, samupeta, sameta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_i.html"> √ 2 i, inv, in    √ 2 i, inv, in, “send” Present I. ínvati etc. V V. inóti etc. (invire) RV IX. inīmasi ? SV1 Verbal Nouns -inita ŚB Derivatives iná RV.C. -inva V.B. invaká B.+ énas V.+ Doubtless the same with the preceding root. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_i_gg.html"> √ iṅg    √ iṅg “stir” Present I. iṅgati -te E.+ Causative iṅgáyati etc. V.+ (iṅgyáte ŚB.) Verbal Nouns PPP: iṅgita E.+ Derivatives iṅga E.+ iṅgana S.+ iṅgya C. iñjanā C. Isolated forms as if from īṅg, iṅk, iñj are found in the Brāhmaṇas. Meanings iṅgati iṅgate v stir, move (intrans.). – Caus. iṅgáyati stir, move (trans.); shake, agitate. ud & sám Caus. = S. Caus. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ich.html"> √ ich    √ ich, See √ 1 iṣ . 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_i_t.html"> √ iṭ    √ iṭ A root iṭ, “wander”, is assumed by BR. on account of the proper name iṭant in KB., and the doubtful and obscure iṭátas at RV.X.171.1- which latter, however, is shown by its accent to be no participle. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_i_d.html"> √ iḍ    √ iḍ A root iḍ is perhaps to be assumed on account of the nouns íḍ V.+ and íḍā V.+ 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_idh.html"> √ idh, indh    √ idh, indh “kindle” Present I. inddhé indháte etc. V.+ (indhaté RV., índhāna V.; iṅkṣva AB.; inttām TA.) Passive idhyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: indhiṣyant S Periphrastic Future: indhitā Aorist √-Ao: idhaté ?. RV1., idhīmahi V., idhāna V -iṣ-Ao: aindhiṣṭa etc. B., indhiṣīya TS., idhiṣīmahi S Perfect īdhé īdhiré RV.ŚB. indhāṃ cakre Causative indhita C Desiderative indidhiṣa- Verbal Nouns PPP: iddhá V.+; 2Abs: -idhya S.+;-ídham, -ídhe RV Derivatives -idh V.+ -ídhya TS. édha V.+ índha V.B. -iddhi B. -idhra ? V.+ édhas AV.+ -indhaka E. idhmá V.+ -eddhṛ RV. indhana V.+ Meanings indh , inddhé v PPP iddhá kindle, set on fire, inflame; P. idhyáte be lighted, flame. anu kindle. abhi surround with flames, set on fire. ā kindle, burn (trans. & intrans.). pari kindle on all sides. sam kindle, burn (trans. & intrans.); inflame, rouse, strengthen. Cf. préddha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_in.html"> √ in, inv    √ in, inv See √ 2 i 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_inak_s.html"> √ inakṣ    √ inakṣ See √ 2 naś 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_iyak_s.html"> √ iyakṣ    √ iyakṣ See √ yaj 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_irajy.html"> √ irajy    √ irajy See √ ṛj 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_iradh.html"> √ iradh    √ iradh See √ rādh 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_il.html"> √ il    √ il, “be quiet” Present VI. ilati etc. C Future Simple Future: eliṣyati Periphrastic Future: elitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: ailīt Perfect iyela Causative iláyati etc. AV.B.S. (ailayīt AV.; ilitá ŚB.) Derivatives -ilaya B.S. In TS., īláyanti is once read. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_i_s.html"> √ 1 iṣ, ich    √ 1 iṣ, ich, “seek, desire” Present I.-eṣati -te etc. E.+ IV.-iṣyati E.+ VI. icháti -te etc. V.+ -iṣa -iṣant E.+ Passive iṣyate etc. E.+,-ti E Future Simple Future: eṣiṣyati etc. B.,-te B Periphrastic Future: eṣitā, eṣṭā Aorist RAo: aiṣiṣat -iṣ-Ao: aiṣīt aiṣiṣus etc. B.U Perfect iyeṣa īṣús, īṣe īṣire etc. B.+ Causative eṣayati etc., eṣita C. (ichayāmi R1.) Desiderative eṣiṣiṣa- Verbal Nouns PPP: iṣṭá V.+; Inf: éṣṭum B.+,-ṭavaí ŚB. eṣitum B.; 1Abs: iṣitvā, iṣṭvā; 2 Abs: -íṣya V.+ Derivatives -ichaka E.+ iṣirá V.B. eṣaka E. éṣaṇā B.+ ichā E.+ iṣṭí V.B. eṣin AV.+ eṣaṇīya C. ichu S.+ iṣmín RV -eṣya AB. eṣṭavyà B.+ íṣ V.B. éṣa V.+ eṣyà V.+ eṣitavya C. -iṣa RV. eṣá RV. éṣaṇa V.+ -eṣṭṛ E. iṣí V. -eṣiṣiṣu C. Compare the roots √ 2 iṣ and √ īṣ, eṣ The present-stems eṣa, iṣa, iṣya only later, unusual, and with certain prepositions. Meanings iccháti iccháte 2 v PPP iṣṭá (q.v.) seek, desire, like, choose; acknowledge, state, take for (2A); wish that (A & Inf or 2A); ask a thing (A) of some one (Ab or L); intend, be about or going to (Inf); w. na disagree, decline, refuse to (Inf), object to (A). P. iṣyate be liked, wanted, approved, recognised; pass for (N). anu seek, search, try., strive after, wish for. Caus. anveṣayati seek, wait for (A). paryanu seek about. samanu search. abhi seek for, strive after, exert one's self at (A); intend to (Inf). pari look about for (A). prati strive towards, seek after (A), receive, accept from (G); attend to, observe. vi seek. Cf. abhī́ṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_i_s.html"> √ 2 iṣ    √ 2 iṣ, “send” Present IV. íṣyati -te etc. V.+ VI. iṣe etc. RV IX. iṣṇā́ti etc. (iṣāṇa) V.B.S Future Simple Future: eṣiṣyati Periphrastic Future: eṣitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: praiṣīt E.+ (apraiṣit M.) Perfect īṣáthus īsus RV., īṣiré AV Causative iṣáyati-te etc. (iṣayádhyai RV.) -eṣayati -te etc. E.+ (eṣyate E.) Desiderative eṣiṣiṣa- Verbal Nouns PPP: iṣitá V.+; 1Abs: iṣitvā; 2Abs: -íṣya B.+;-éṣam B.; iṣádhyai RV Derivatives iṣáṇi RV. -eṣa V.+ -eṣya B.+ eṣitavya B.C. íṣu V.+ -eṣaka E. -eṣaṇa E.+ -eṣayitṛ E. -eṣitṛ C. Doubtless the same with √ 1 iṣ with causative meaning. In later language, almost only preṣaya. Meanings iṣati eṣati 1 v (– ṃ), íṣyati, iṣṇā́ti (also Ā), PPP ipitá send, impel, hurl, throw, raise (the voice), utter, proclaim; incite, promote, further; intrans. advance, strive; tend towards, aim at (D or L). anu follow, seek, look for (A). pra P & Ā drive forth, send out; call upon, summon, invite. Caus. preṣayati, te hurl, cast, send out, dismiss. anupra Caus. send forth after. saṃpra summon, invite; send forth, dismiss. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ii.html"> √ ī    √ ī, See √ 1 i . 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_iik_s.html"> √ īkṣ    √ īkṣ, “see” Present I. ī́kṣate etc. V.+,-ti etc. B.+ Passive īkṣyate etc. S.+ Future Simple Future: īkṣiṣyáte etc. B.+,-yáti B Periphrastic Future: īkṣitā Aorist √-Ao: aikṣi C RAo: aicikṣat -iṣ-Ao: aikṣiṣi etc. B. (aikṣīt C. ?) Perfect īkṣā́ṃ cakre etc. B.+, īkṣāṃ cakrus E Causative īkṣáyati etc. V. +,-te AV. (īkṣyate S.) Desiderative īcikṣiṣa- (in d.) Verbal Nouns PPP: īkṣitá B.+; Inf: īkṣitum E.+; 1Abs: īkṣitvā B.; 2Abs: -ī́kṣya B.+;-īkṣam B.S Derivatives ī́kṣa B.+ īkṣin E.+ īkṣaṇa RV ? S.+. -īkṣitavyà B.+ īkṣā B.+ -īkṣya E.+ īkṣaṇīya E.+ īkṣitṛ C. ī́ṣaka B.+ īkṣeṇyà RV. īcikṣiṣu C. Only three occurrences in RV., but growing rapidly common. Active forms sporadic Meanings ī́kṣate v (ī́kṣati), PPP īkṣitá (q.v.) look, view, behold, perceive, see (l. & f.), consider, regard, expect; *tell fortune to (D). Caus. īkṣayati cause to look at (A). apa look away, look off to, watch, regard, consider, wait for, expect, require. abhi look at (A). ava look at, view, consider, regard, expect, hope. anvava regard, consider. pratyava look at, inspect, examine. samava view, regard, consider. ud look up to, gaze at (A), wait, expect. samud look up to, gaze at, behold, perceive; think of, consider (A). upa look on, behold, observe; overlook, neglect. samupa the same. nis look at, perceive, contemplate. pari look round, investigate, scrutinize, examine. pra look at, behold, perceive; overlook, neglect. abhipra view, regard. utpra look up to (A), regard as (2A), suppose, imagine; transfer, use or call metaphorically (rh.). upapra P disregard, overlook. abhisaṃpra look at (A). prati look towards. behold, observe; wait, expect; bear with, tolerate (A). saṃprati wait, expect. vi regard, behold, deliberate, ponder, consider as (vat); inquire, perceive, discern. anuvi look about, behold; examine, try. abhivi & samabhivi regard, behold, perceive, observe. udvi look (up) to, perceive, observe, investigate. sam look upon, behold, observe, consider; think of, aim at (A); try, examine, find out, ascertain. abhisam & prasam behold, regard, consider. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ii_gkh.html"> √ īṅkh    √ īṅkh, “swing” Present I. īṅkhati etc. C.,-te AA Causative īṅkháyati -te etc. V.+ Derivatives -īṅkha V.+ -īṅkhana C. -īṅkhaya RV. The form eṅkṣva AB. is false. Meanings īṅkhati v Caus. īṅkháyati swing, shake. pra tremble, shake. Caus. swing (trans.); Ā swing (intrans.). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_iij.html"> √ īj    √ īj See √ ej . 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ii_d.html"> √ īḍ    √ īḍ, “praise” Present I. īḍāmahe V., īḍamāna S II. ī́ṭṭe ī́ḍate etc. (ī́ḍiṣva) V.B Passive īḍyate C Future Simple Future: īḍiṣyate Periphrastic Future: īḍitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aiḍiṣṭa Perfect īḍé RV., īḍire E.+ īḍāṃ cakre Causative aiḍayan C Desiderative īḍiḍiṣa- Verbal Nouns PPP: īḍitá V.+; Inf: īḍitum C Derivatives ī́ḍ RV. ī́ḍya V.+ īḍitavya B. īḍénya V.B. īḍitṛ́ AV. Only a few sporadic occurrences in the later language. Meanings ī́ṭṭe v PPP īḍitá 1 praise, implore, beg for (A, G, or D). pra , upapra, prati , sam & prasam praise, honour, worship. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_iir.html"> √ īr    √ īr, “set in motion” ? Present I. aírat etc. RV., ī́rate ( II. ī́rte ī́rate etc. V.B. (īráte B.) (3s.) AV Future Simple Future: īriṣyate Periphrastic Future: īritā Aorist RAo: airirat -iṣ-Ao: airiṣṭa Perfect īriré V. (erire RV.) īrāaṃ cakre Causative īráyati etc. V.+,-te etc. V.B. (īryate etc. B.+; īritá V.+; īryant M.; īrayádhyai RV.) Verbal Nouns 1Abs: īrṇá B.+ Derivatives īra E.+ īrya B. īrin E.+ īraṇa E.+ -īritṛ U. -īraka C. īryā C. -īraṇīya C. īrmá V.B. The form īryayati, doubtless false, is found once in ŚB. Meanings ī́rte v PPP īrṇá trans. set in motion, impel, further; intrans. stir, move, rise. Caus. īráyati, te, PPP īritá = S. tr ; also bring forth. raise (the voice), utter, proclaim, cite; P. be raised, uttered, called. ā (also Caus. ) procure, get, obtain, raise, utter. nyā appoint as (2A). ud trans. cause to rise, draw out of (Ab); intrans. stir, move, rise. Caus. = ud trans., also throw, hurl, shoot (lit. & fig.), raise, utter, speak; show, betray; further, strengthen, elevate; rouse up, impel, excite. P. be hurled, raised, excited; be proclaimed or taught, pass for (N). abhyud Caus. simple, further, excite; utter, speak. samud Caus. drive out, hurl, cast, raise, utter, proclaim (PPP samudīrita). pra stir, move, come forth; rise, sound. Caus. drive on, send forth; push on, press urge; turn, direct; emit, utter, pronounce. vi (also Caus. ) split, divide. sam put together, shape, create, produce. Caus. the same, also rouse up, impel, revive, instruct with (I). Cf. udīrṇa, samudīrṇa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_iir_sy.html"> √ īrṣy    √ īrṣy, “be jealous” Present I. ī́rṣyati etc. B.S Verbal Nouns PPP: īrṣyita C Derivatives īrṣyā́ AV.+ īrṣyin C. īrṣyú AV.+ īrṣyitavya C. īrṣyaka C. īrṣyālu C. Evidently a secondary root, but of doubtful origin (BR., from irasy). Not seldom written without the y in later works. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_iiz.html"> √ īś    √ īś, “be master” Present I. īśata V.B.U II. īṣṭe ī́cate etc. (2s ī́kṣe RV., ī́śe RV.S.; ī́śe 3s. V.B., īśite U.; īśidhve AV.) V.+ Future Simple Future: īśiṣyati U.,-te B Periphrastic Future: īśitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aiśiṣṭa Perfect ī́śire ? RV. īśāṃ cakre Verbal Nouns PPP: īśita U Derivatives ī́ś B. īśā́ AV.+ īśana U. īśitṛ U.+ īśvará AV.+ īśá B.+ īśin U.+ īśitavya C. -īśu V.+ Meanings ī́ṣṭe 1 v (ī́śe) be master, own, possess, reign, rule (G or A); dispose of, claim at (G); have power or be able to (Inf in tum or tos, L, or A). Cf. ríśāna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ii_s.html"> √ īṣ, eṣ    √ īṣ, eṣ, “move” Present I. ī́ṣate etc. V.B.,-ti etc. V.B.U. éṣati etc. AV Future Simple Future: īṣiṣyate Periphrastic Future: īṣitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aiṣiṣṭa Perfect īṣé RV. (aíyes plpf. RV1.) īṣāṃ cakre Verbal Nouns -īṣita V.B Derivatives īṣā́ ? RV. eṣá RV.-eṣṭi C. eṣṭṛ́ B.S. Doubtless ultimately one with √ 1 iṣ , √ 2 iṣ Meanings ríṣati & ríṣate v move, hasten, flee, retire, deviate from (Ab); leave, abandon (A); ī́ṣant assaulting, hurting. apa withdraw from (Ab). ā (mostly Ā) hasten towards; approach with prayers, beseech, assail, attack; strive after, covet. vi stretch (intrans.). Cf. údīṣita, sámīṣita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_iih.html"> √ īh    √ īh, “be eager” Present I. ī́hate etc. B.+,-ti E.+ Future Simple Future: īhiṣyate Periphrastic Future: īhitā Aorist RAo: aijihat -iṣ-Ao: aihiṣṭa Perfect īhāṃ cakre Causative īhaya- Desiderative ījihiṣa- Verbal Nouns PPP: īhita E.+; Inf: īhitum C Derivatives -īha C. īhā E.+ -īhana E. ehá AV. -ehas V.+ Meanings ríhate v (ríhati), PPP īhita (q.v.) be eager endeavour, strive after, wish for (A); have a mind or intend to (Inf). sam = S. Cf. samīhita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_u.html"> √ u    √ u, “proclaim” Present I. avate II. uve RV1 V. unoti RV1 Future Simple Future: oṣyate Periphrastic Future: otā Aorist -s-Ao: auṣṭa Perfect ūve Causative āvaya- Desiderative ūṣiṣa- Extremely doubtful root; uvé is possibly interjection (Bö.); vyùnoti is perhaps for víyunote; and the PPP óta, put here by BR., doubtless belongs to √ vā “weave”. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_uk_s.html"> √ 1 ukṣ    √ 1 ukṣ, “sprinkle” Present VI. ukṣáti etc. V.+,-te etc. V.+ Passive ukṣyate etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: ukṣiṣyati etc. B.S Periphrastic Future: ukṣitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aukṣiṣam etc. B Perfect ukṣāṃ cakāra Causative ukṣayati etc. S.+ Verbal Nouns ukṣitá V.+; -úkṣya B.+ Derivatives -ukṣ RV. úkṣaṇa AV.+ -ukṣitavya B.C. uṣṭṛ́ RV1. -ukṣa B.S. ukṣaṇīya JB. úṣṭṛ B.S. úṣṭra V.+ ukṣán V.+ Whether ukṣán and uṣṭṛ́ etc. belong here, is very doubtful. Meanings ukṣáti ukṣáte v PPP ukṣitá 1 sprinkle, besprinkle; drip drop (Ā intrans.). anu , abhi , ava , ā besprinkle. pari sprinkle round. pra sprinkle before one's self, consecrate, sacrifice, kill. saṃpra besprinkle, Ā refl. vi shed, Ā besprinkle. sam besprinkle (l. & f.). pour out. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_uk_s.html"> √ 2 ukṣ, vakṣ    √ 2 ukṣ, vakṣ, “grow” See √ vakṣ, ukṣ 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_uc.html"> √ uc    √ uc, “be pleased” Present IV. ucyati etc. V.B Future Simple Future: uciṣyati Periphrastic Future: ucitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aucīt Perfect uvócitha uvóca, ūciṣé RV Verbal Nouns PPP: ucitá V.+ 1Abs: ocitvā Derivatives -óka RV. okyà RV. ókas V.+ okivā́ṃs RV1.-ócana V. -ocara AV. Meanings úcyati v PPP ucitá (q.v.) be pleased or wont, like. ni delight in (A or L). sam be fond of (I). Cf. samucita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_uch.html"> √ uch    √ uch See √ 1 vas 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ujh.html"> √ ujh    √ ujh, “forsake” Present VI. ujhati etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: ujhiṣyati Periphrastic Future: ujhitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aujhīt C Perfect ujhāṃ cakāra C Verbal Nouns PPP: ujhita E.+; Inf: ujhitum C.; 2Abs: -ujhya C Derivatives -ujha S.+ ujhana C. ujhiti PB. A secondary root, coming from ud + √ hā (ujjahāmi etc.). Meanings ujjhati v PPP ujjhita (q.v.) forsake, leave, give up, avoid, escape. pra and sam = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_u_jch.html"> √ uñch    √ uñch, “glean” Present VI. ? uñchati etc. S.+ Future Simple Future: uñchiṣyati Periphrastic Future: uñchitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: auñchīt Perfect uñchāṃ cakāra Causative uñchaya- Desiderative uñcichiṣa- Verbal Nouns Inf: uñchitum C.; 2Abs: -uñchya C Derivatives uñcha S.+ uñchana C. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ud.html"> √ ud, und    √ ud, und, “wet” Present VI. undati etc. B.S VII. unátti undánti etc. V.B.S., undáte (3p.) AV Passive udyate RV Future Simple Future: undiṣyati Periphrastic Future: unditā Aorist RAo: aundidat -iṣ-Ao: aundīt Perfect ūdus AV. undāṃ cakāra Causative undaya- Desiderative undidiṣa- Verbal Nouns PPP: utta B., unna S.C.; 2Abs: -údya B.S Derivatives úd RV. udani- RV. -udra V.+ ódatī RV. udaká V.+ -uditṛ C. útsa V.+ odaná V.+ udán , uda V.+ údman B. úndana B.+ ódman B. Meanings und unátti 2 v & undati (also Ā), PPP utta & unna spring (water), bubble up, wet, bathe. anu , abhi & upa sprinkle, wet. ni immerse. vi spring or bubble forth, also = sam sprinkle, wet. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ubj.html"> √ ubj    √ ubj, “force” Present VI. ubjáti etc. V.B.S Future Simple Future: ubjiṣyati Periphrastic Future: ubjitā Aorist RAo: aubjijat -iṣ-Ao: aubjīt Perfect ubjāṃ cakāra Causative ubjaya- Desiderative ubjijiṣa- Verbal Nouns PPP: ubjitá AV.B.; 2Abs: -ubjya JB Derivatives -udga ? B.+ ubja RV. ? B.+-ubji- PB. Meanings ubjáti v force, subdue. ni press down, overthrow. nis let loose. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ubh.html"> √ ubh, umbh    √ ubh, umbh, “confine” Present VI. umbhata (2p.) AV., aumbhat MS.; ubhati VII. unap RV., aumbhan TS IX. aubhāt ubhnā́s RV Future Simple Future: ubhiṣyati, umbhiṣyati Periphrastic Future: ubhitā, umbhitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aubhīt, aumbhīt Perfect uvobha , umbhāṃ cakāra Verbal Nouns PPP: ubdhá RV.B., umbhita C.; 2Abs: -ubhya S Derivatives -úmbhana TS. Meanings umbháti ubhnā́ti unápti v PPP ubdhá, umbhita confine, unite, couple. ni keep down. sam keep together, cover, shut up. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_u_s.html"> √ 1 uṣ    √ 1 uṣ, “shine”, See √ 1 vas . 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_u_s.html"> √ 2 uṣ    √ 2 uṣ, “burn” Present I. ósati etc. V.+ IX. uṣṇán, uṣṇánt RV1 Passive uṣyate etc. C Future Simple Future: oṣiṣyati Periphrastic Future: oṣitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: auṣīt etc. B.S Perfect uvoṣa ŚB. oṣāṃ cakāra Causative oṣaya- Desiderative oṣiṣiṣa- Verbal Nouns PPP: uṣṭa B.S.; 1Abs: oṣitvā; 2Abs: -oṣya TS.;-uṣas K.; óṣam ŚB Derivatives úṣa ? RV. uṣná V.+ -uṣyá ŚB. oṣá ,-óṣa V.+ uṣā C. -uṣṇi TA. ūṣmán V.+ -óṣas RV. uṣman E.+ oṣiṣṭha B. Apparently a differentiated form of √ 1 vas, which see. Meanings óṣati & uṣṇā́ti 1 v burn, consume, destroy, punish. ud expel by heat. ni burn down. prati & sam burn. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_uur_nu.html"> √ 1 ūrṇu    √ 1 ūrṇu See √ 1 vṛ . 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_uuh.html"> √ 1 ūh    √ 1 ūh, “remove” Present I. ū́hati V.+,-te V.+ Passive uhyate B.+, ūhyate C Aorist √-Ao: uhyāt ŚB.; ohi C. RAo: aujihat -iṣ-Ao: auhīt B Perfect ūhāṃ cakāra Causative ūhayati C Verbal Nouns PPP: ūḍha B.+, ūhita C.; Inf: ūhitum E.+, oḍhum E.+,-ūhitavaí B.; 2Abs: -ūhya B, +,-úhya B.+;-óham RV.,-ū́ham MS Derivatives ūha AV.+ ūhyà B.+ ūhanīya S.+ ūḍhi C. -ūhaka C. ūhana S.+ ūhitavya C. -oha RV. -oghas? RV. Doubtless a differentiated form of √ vah from which in some forms and meanings it is hardly to be separated. Meanings (uh) ū́hati ūhate v PPP ūḍha & ūhita 1 shift, change. adhi put on; raise above (L). apa push off, remove, destroy; avoid, shun, give up. vyapa dispel, remove, destroy. abhi overlay, cover. ava push down. ud push upwards, bring forth. abhyud push on, push further. vyud push asunder, move away, sweep out. upa push near, insert, produce. samupa bring near, offer. nis push out, pull out, remove. pari heap or pile round, surround, fortify. prati push back, strip off, doff, remove; keep off, detain; reject, refuse; outstrip, surpass, excel; disturb, interrupt. vi push asunder, separate; divide, arrange (esp. in battle-array). prativi arrange in return. sam bring together, gather, collect. parisam sweep together. Cf. udvyūḍha, upoḍha, nivryūḍha, vyūḍha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_uuh.html"> √ 2 ūh    √ 2 ūh, “consider” Present I. óhate etc. V ūhati C.,-te E. ohiṣe (1s.) RV1 II. óhate (3p.) óhāna ohāná RV Future Simple Future: ūhiṣyate Periphrastic Future: ūhitā Aorist RAo: aujihat -iṣ-Ao: auhiṣṭa V Perfect ūhé etc. V. ūhāṃ cakre Causative ūhayati etc. E Desiderative ūjihiṣa- Verbal Nouns Inf: ūhitum c.; 2Abs:-ūhya C Derivatives ūha E.+ ūhana C. ūhitavya C. óhas RV. ūhya C. ūhanīya A. óha-? RV. óhasāna RV. Probably “bear in mind”, and so originally identical with √ 1 ūh and √ vah Meanings ohate ūhati ohate ūhate 2 v mind, mark, watch, wait or lurk for (A or L); conceive, understand; be regarded as, pass for (N). api conceive, comprehend, guess. abhi wait or lurk for (A), also = prec. ni mind, notice. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root__r.html"> √ ṛ, ṛch    √ ṛ, ṛch, “go, send” Present II. árti TS III. íyarti etc. (iyárṣi) V.B V. ṛṇóti etc. ṛṇve etc. V. ṛṇváti etc. RV VI. ṛcháti etc. V.+,-te etc. ŚB.E.; archati etc. U.E rante ranta RV., rántī ? SV IX. ṛṇāti Passive aryate Future Simple Future: ariṣyati B Periphrastic Future: artā Aorist √-Ao: ārta ārata etc. (aryāt TS., arīta RV.; arāṇá RV.) V.B Th Ao: ā́rat etc. V.B. (aranta arāmahi V.) -s-Ao: ārṣīt Perfect āra (ā́ritha) ārús etc. V.+; ānarchat M1. arāṃ cakāra Causative arpáyati etc. V.+,-te C. (arpipam AV.: arpayitā E.; arpitá árpita V.+;-árpya V.+; arpyate C.) Desiderative aririṣa- Intensive álarti etc. RV. arāryate etc Verbal Nouns PPP: ṛtá V.+, arṇa C.; ártos B.; 1Abs: -ṛtvā́ AV.B.U.; 2Abs: -ṛ́tya AV.;-ā́ram RV Deriv.: ará , ára V.+ árṇa V.+ ā́rya V.+ rátha V.+ aryá , árya V.B.S. árṇas RV. iras- RV. -arpaka C. áraṇa V.+ ártha V.+ íriṇa V.+ -arpya C. aráṇi V.+ -arman,árma V.+ írya V. árpaṇa V.+ aratí RV. árvan ,-arva V.+ -ṛchā U.+ arpaṇīya C. aráru V.B. árvant V.B. ṛtí , ṛ́ti V.+ -arpitṛ E.+ arí V.+ ārá V.+ ṛtú V.+ -arpayitṛ́ ŚB. aritṛ́ RV. -ārin B. -ṛtha V. -arpayitavya C. arítra ,áritra V.+ ā́ruka TA. ṛṇá V.+ Meanings íyarti ṛṇóti ṛṇuté ṛṇváti ṛccháti ṛccháte arcchati árti v pp ṛtá (q.v.) move (trans.), raise, excite; move (intrans.), rise, hasten, meet with, get at, reach, attain. Caus. arpáyati hurl, throw, pierce, send, put, place, fasten or fix in, turn, direct (eyes or mind); offer, deliver, give back, restore. anu Ā rise after (A). apa open, unlock. abhi hasten towards, approach, assail. ā put in, insert, get, procure, reach, fall into (A), afflict, distress. ud rise, raise. Caus. make to rise or thrive. upa approach, assist; go against, offend, transgress. ni put down, set in; succumb, perish. nis put asunder, dissolve; be deprived of (Ab or G). pra go forth, advance, also = Caus. set in motion, stir up. prati insert. Caus. throw against, fasten, fix, put on; deliver, give back, restore. vi open (trans. & intrans.). sam put together, get done; come together, meet (I), run together to (A or L). Caus. hurl at (A) strike, hit; put on, insert, fasten; deliver, restore. Cf. ā́rta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root__rc.html"> √ ṛc    √ ṛc See √ arc . 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1__rj.html"> √ ṛj, ṛñj, arj    √ ṛj, ṛñj, arj, “direct, stretch, attain” Present I. árjati B.U.C IV. ṛ́jyant, ṛjyate RV. ṛñjase (1s.) ṛñjasāná RV VI. ṛñjáti -áte etc. RV. AA VII. ṛñjate (3p.) RV Passive ṛiyate Future Simple Future: arjiṣyati Periphrastic Future: arjitā Aorist RAo: ārjijat -iṣ-Ao: ārjiṣṭa Perfect ānarjus ānṛjús AV1. ? Causative arjayati -te etc. S.E.+ Desiderative arjijiṣa- Verbal Nouns ṛñjáse RV1 Derivatives arjaka C. ṛjipyá RV. ṛ́jīyas V. -arjya C. ṛjíśvan RV. ṛjú V.+ arjana E.+ ṛjīpín RV. ráji RV. arjanīya C. ṛjīṣá RV. rájiṣṭha RV.B. -arjayitṛ C. ṛjūnas RV. rajīyas JB. -ṛṅga RV. rāji AV.+ It seems impossible to divide these forms (generally distributed to two different roots) from one another. The root has three well-marked stages of development: ṛj or ṛñj in RV., arj in Brāh., and arjaya in the later language. Compare also √ rāj probably a derivative from it. With it is related, further, the anomalously formed stem irajya (irajyáti -teetc. RV., and irajyú RV.), “direct, rule”. Meanings ṛj : ṛñjáti ṛñjáte ṛ́jyati ṛ́jyate 1 v stretch out (intrans.), strive after, long for. abhi grasp, snatch. ā Ā strive after, long for. ni reach, attain. pra strive towards. sam strive together. Cf. irajy, yáti & ṛñjasāná. árj : árjati 2 v reach, get, obtain. Caus. arjayati, arjayate = S. ati get over, admit or remove. anu & ava dismiss. upa admit; Caus. get, acquire. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2__rj.html"> √ 2 ṛj    √ 2 ṛj, “shine” Inferable from the Derivatives árjuna V.+ -ṛjīká V. ṛ́jīti RV. ṛjrá RV. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root__rt.html"> √ ṛt, art    √ ṛt, art, “pursue” Future Simple Future: artiṣye AV1 Aorist -iṣ-Ao: artiḍhvam PB1 Derivatives artaná VS1. -artitṛ V1. ártuka ŚB1. A very doubtful root; ánvartiṣye and anvartitṛ́ apparent contractions for anu-vart-; and Bö. amends artiḍhvam to arthi- (but ??). But artana and artuka seem to show that the thing had assumed the value of a root. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root__rd.html"> √ ṛd, ard    √ ṛd, ard, “stir, dissolve” Present I. árdati etc. AV.+ VI. ṛdantu ā́rdan RV VII. ṛṇatti Future Simple Future: ardiṣyati Periphrastic Future: arditā Aorist RAo: ārdidat -iṣ-Ao: ārdīt Perfect ānarda Causative ardáyati etc. (ārdayīt ardyate ardita) V.+ Desiderative ardidiṣa- Verbal Nouns arṇṇa ? ŚB Derivatives -ardaka C.-ardin C. ardana E.+ Of perplexing variety of meanings. Meanings ṛdati ṛ́rdati v dissolve (intrans.), pass away; stir (trans.), trouble, vex, afflict, hurt, destroy, torment. Caus. ardáyati, PPP ardita = S. trans. abhi vex, afflict. vi pass away; Caus. destroy, annihilate. sam Caus. wound. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root__rdh.html"> √ ṛdh    √ ṛdh, “thrive” Present IV. ṛdhyate -ti V.+ (pass ?.) V. ṛdhnóti etc. V.+ VII. ṛṇádhat ṛndhyām ṛndhánt V Passive ṛdhyate etc. V.+, ṛdhyant M Future Simple Future: ardhiṣyate ŚB Periphrastic Future: ardhitā JB Aorist √-Ao: ā́rdhma B.S., ṛdhā́the RV., ṛdhyā́m etc. V.B.S., ṛdhyā́sam etc. AV.B.S., ṛdhīmáhi RV., ṛdhánt RV., ā́rdhi B Th Ao: ṛdhema AV.ŚB RAo: ārdidhat -iṣ-Ao: ārdhīt ārdhiṣṭa MS Perfect ānṛdhús AV., ānṛdhe RV.ŚB Causative ardháyati etc. AV.+ Desiderative ī́rtsati etc. (aírtsīt etc.) AV.ŚB. ardidhiṣa- Verbal Nouns PPP: ṛddha AV.+ 1Abs: ṛddhvā, ardhitvā Derivatives árdha ? V.+ -ardhi RV. -ṛ́dha RV. ṛdhnuka AGS. ardhá ? V.+ árdhuka B.S. ṛ́dhat , ṛ́dhak? V.B. -īrtsā AV. árdhya RV. -ṛdh V.S. ṛ́ddhi AV.+ -ardhayitṛ U.S. Compare roots √ vṛdh and √ rādh . Meanings ṛdhnóti ṛdhyate ṛdhyati v PPP ṛddha (q.v.) thrive, succeed, prosper; make prosperous, further, promote, accomplish. Caus. ardháyati gratify. anu fulfil, execute. vi be deprived of (I). Caus. exclude from, deprive of (I). sam thrive, prosper, be accomplished. Caus. make succeed, fulfil, furnish with (I). Cf. vyṭṛddha, sámṛddha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root__rz.html"> √ ṛś(?)    √ ṛś(?), “harm” Perhaps to be inferred from the Derivatives -arśa RV. árśas VS.+ ṛ́kṣa V.+ ṛkṣī́kā AV.B. -arśani RV. arśasāná RV. -ṛkṣara V. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root__r_s.html"> √ ṛṣ    √ ṛṣ, “rush, push” Present I. árṣati etc. (arṣase AV.) V.B VI. ṛṣáti etc. V.B.S Future Simple Future: arṣiṣyati Periphrastic Future: arṣitā Aorist etc -iṣ-Ao: ārṣīt Perfect ānarṣat TA Causative arṣaya- Desiderative arṣiṣiṣa- Verbal Nouns ṛṣṭa V.B. arṣitvā Derivatives -arṣa B. -árṣu RV. ṛṣabhá V.+ ṛṣṭí V.+ -árṣaṇa B. arṣṭṛ́ B. ṛ́ṣi V.+ ṛṣvá V.B. arṣaṇī́ AV. ṛṣú RV. Hardly calls for the usual division into two roots. Some of the derivatives doubtful. Meanings árṣati 1 v flow, glide. anu flow after (A). abhi flow or let flow towards (A). pari flow or let flow round (A). vi run through (A). sam meet with (I), come together to (A). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ej.html"> √ ej, īj    √ ej, īj, “stir” Present I. ījate, ī́jamāna RV.; éjati etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: ejiṣyati Periphrastic Future: ejitā Aorist RAo: aijijat Perfect ejāṃ cakāra Causative ejayati ŚB.,-te C Desiderative ejijiṣa- Derivatives ejáthu AV. 2Abs: -ejaya V.+ Meanings éjati v stir, move, tremble; Caus. ejayati, ejayate move (trans.). apa drive away, chase. ud move, rise. sam the same. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_edh.html"> √ edh    √ edh, “thrive” Present I. édhate etc. V.+, -ti etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: edhiṣyate Periphrastic Future: edhitā Aorist RAo: aididhat -iṣ-Ao: edhiṣīyá etc. AV.B Perfect edhire C. edhā́ṃ cakrire ŚB., edhām babhūvire C Causative edhayati etc. S.+ Desiderative edidhiṣa- (in d.) Verbal Nouns PPP: edhita E.+; Inf: édhitum B.+ Derivatives -edha ? B.S. edhatú V.B.-edhana R. edhas S.E. edidhiṣu VS. Perhaps related with √ ṛdh . Meanings édhate v (édhati), PPP edhita thrive, prosper, grow up, get strong, great, or happy. Caus. edhayati make thrive or prosper, strengthen, honour, celebrate. sam = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_katth.html"> √ katth    √ katth, “boast” Present I. katthate etc. E.+,-ti etc. E Future Simple Future: katthiṣyate Periphrastic Future: katthitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: akatthiṣṭá Perfect cakatthe Causative katthayati E Verbal Nouns PPP: katthita E.+; Inf: katthitum E Derivatives -katthā E. katthaka C.-katthin E.+ katthana E.+ katthitavya C. A secondary prakritized root, but of unclear derivation. Meanings katthate (katthati) v boast, praise, flatter; abuse, blame. vi boast or brag of (I), praise, extol; degrade, humble (also Caus. ). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kath.html"> √ kath    √ kath, “talk” √ katth √ kath √ kad Present X. kathayati (-te) C. Aorist RAo: acakathat, acíkathat Meanings kathayati (kathayate ) v PPP kathita (q.v.) talk, converse with (I saha ); relate, report, denounce, declare, explain, state. P. be called, pass for (N). pari name. pra announce, report. vi talk idly, chatter. sam = S. Copyright © 2005 Lennart Warnemyr 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kad.html"> √ kad    √ kad, “destroy” Only in the deriv. kadana E.+, and in cakāda kadanam R., where cakāda is a misreading for cakāra. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kan.html"> √ kan, kā    √ kan, kā, “be pleased, enjoy” Present IV. kā́yamāna RV1 Aorist -iṣ-Ao: akāniṣam kā́niṣas RV Perfect cākana cākánas etc. cākanyhāt cākandhi etc. cā̆kánanta cākán RV.; caké cakāná V.B.S Derivatives kanā́ RV. kaniṣṭá V.B. kanī́na V.+ kanyā́ V.+ kanaka ? E.+ kániṣṭha B.+ kánīyas V.+ -kāti RV. -kāyyá RV. Doubtless the same with the following root, √ kam The stem cākán, on account of its accent, rather parfect than intensive. Meanings (only PPP kā́yamāna, Ao akāniṣam, & Pf or intens-stem cākan or cakān) be glad, be satisfied with, enjoy (A, L, G, or I); be liked, please, (w. G); love, wish, desire (A). ā be pleased with (L); strive after, long for. Cf. saṃcakāná. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kam.html"> √ kam    √ kam, “love” Future Simple Future: kamiṣyate etc. B Periphrastic Future: kamitā B Aorist RAo: acakamata acīkamata etc. B -iṣ-Ao: kamiṣīṣṭa Perfect cakamé etc. V.+ Causative kāmáyate etc. V.+,-ti etc. E Desiderative cikamiṣa- Intensive caṅkam- Verbal Nouns PPP: kāṃta E.+; 1Abs: kāṃtvā, kamitvā; -kamas B.;-kā́mam ŚB Derivatives kám ? V.+ kamitṛ C. kā́mya V.+ kā́muka B.+ kama-? V. kamra C. -kāmyā́ AV.+ kāṃti E.+ kamana C. kā́ma V.+ -kāman RV1. kāmayitavya C. kamanīya C. kāmín V.+ kāmana S.+ Doubtless the same with the preceding √ kan, kā . Meanings (without Pr), PPP kānta (q.v.) wish, desire, love. Caus. kāmáyate (ti) the same; kāmaṃ kāmayamāna having a wish. anu & abhi wish, desire. ni lust after, long for (A). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kamp.html"> √ kamp    √ kamp, “tremble” Present I. kampate etc. U.+,-ti etc. E Future Simple Future: kampiṣyate Periphrastic Future: kampitā Aorist RAo: acakampat -iṣ-Ao: akampiṣṭa Perfect cakampe etc. E Causative kampayati etc. B.+,-te etc. U.+ (kampyate C.) Desiderative cikampiṣa- Intensive caṅkamp- Verbal Nouns PPP: kampita E.+ kapita; Inf: kampitum E,-tos B.; 2Abs: -kampya S.+ Derivatives kampa E.+ kampin E.+ kampanā E.+ kapanā́ ? RV. -kampā E.+ kampya E.+ -kampanīya C. kapí ? V.+ -kampaka E.+ kampana E.+ kampra S.+ képi ? RV. Meanings kampate (kampati) v PPP kampita (q.v.) tremble, shake. Caus. kampayati, te make tremble or shake, agitate. anu sympathize with, commiserate (L or A); Caus. the same (w. A). abhi & ā = S. ud tremble, swing upwards. Caus. shake up, agitate. pra tremble, quiver, shake, become loose. Caus. make tremble, swing, agitate. vi tremble, stir, move, cease from (Ab) Caus. make tremble. sam = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kal.html"> √ kal    √ kal, “drive, produce” Present etc I. kalate III. cakale, etc Causative kālayati etc. S.+,-te etc. B.+ (kālyate etc. S.+) kalayati etc. E.+,-ti etc. C Derivatives kalā́ ? B.+ -kalya C. -kalanīya C. -lālaka C. -kalikā C. kalana S.+ -kalayitṛ C. -kālana S.+ Divided by BR. and Bö. into two roots: 2 kal (kālay), “drive”; and 1 kal (kalay), “drive etc. etc.” Meanings kalayati (kalayate) & kālayati v PPP kalita (q.v.) drive, impel; carry, bear; do, make, cause, produce, utter; observe, notice; try, examine; suppose, think, regard as (2A). ā shake, agitate, cast, fling; seize, tie, fasten; observe, notice; try, etc. = S. ud drive out, let loose. upa drive home. nis drive out, chase away. pari follow, pursue, seize, devour; consider or regard as. pra drive out, impel, pursue. sam drive away, put to flight; join, combine, be of opinion. Cf. utkalita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ka_s.html"> √ kaṣ    √ kaṣ, “scratch” Present I. kaṣati etc. AV.+,-te etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: kaṣiṣyati TS Periphrastic Future: kaṣitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: akā̆ṣīt Perfect cakāṣa Verbal Nouns PPP: kaṣita C.;-kāṣam S.+ Derivatives kaṣa E.+ kaṣaṇa C.-kāṣa B.+-kāṣin C. Meanings kaṣati kaṣate v rub, scratch (Ā scratch one's self or being scratched), hurt, destroy. apa scratch off. ud rub in, dye. ni rub in or scrape off. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kas.html"> √ kas    √ kas, “open” Present I. kasati etc. AV.C Future Simple Future: kasiṣyati Periphrastic Future: kasitā Aorist RAo: acīkasat C Perfect cakase C Causative kāsayati etc. C. (kāsyate C.) Desiderative cikasiṣa- Intensive canīkas- Verbal Nouns PPP: kasta V.B.S., kasita S.+ Derivatives kasanā ? C. -kasti TS. -kāsa E.+ -kāsin S.+ -kāsanīya C. -kasuka AV.+ -kasvara C. -kāsaka C. -kāsana C. Meanings kasati v PPP kasta w. ud gape, open (intrans.). nis Caus. niṣkāsayati drive away. pra Caus. (the same*), cause to expand or bloom. vi burst, expand, spread, bloom, blossom, shine, beam. Caus. cause to blow or shine. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kaa.html"> √ kā    √ kā See √ kan . 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kaa_gk_s.html"> √ kāṅkṣ    √ kāṅkṣ “desire” Present I. kāṅkṣati -te etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: kāṅkṣiṣyati Periphrastic Future: kāṅkṣitā Aorist RAo: acakāṅkṣat -iṣ-Ao: akāṅkṣīt Perfect cakāṅkṣa E.+ Causative kāṅkṣayate E Desiderative cikāṅkṣiṣa- Intensive cākāṅkṣya- Verbal Nouns PPP: kāṅkṣita E.+ Derivatives -kāṅkṣa C. kāṅkṣin E.+ -kāṅkṣaṇa C. kāṅkṣā E.+ -kāṅkṣya C. kāṅkṣaṇīya C. -kāṅkṣitavya C. Perhaps a desiderative formation from √ kan or √ kam . Meanings kāṅkṣati kāṅkṣate v desire, long for, strive after, expect (A), wait (absol.). anu Ā & abhi wish for, strive after (A). ā the same + long for (G), turn to (A) require as a complement (g.). pratyā Ā expect, watch. samā, pra , & prati desire, long for. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kaaz.html"> √ kāś    √ kāś, “appear, make a show” Present I. kāśate etc. B.+,-ti etc. E Future Simple Future: kāśiṣyate Periphrastic Future: kāśitā Aorist RAo: acakāśat -iṣ-Ao: akāśiṣṭa Perfect cakāśe etc. E.+ kāśāṃ cakre Causative kāśayati AV.+,-te U.+ (kāśyate E.) Desiderative cikāśiṣa- Intensive cākaśīti etc. V.B.U., cākaśyáte etc. B.S Verbal Nouns PPP: kāśita E.; 2Abs: -kā́śya B Derivatives kā́śa V.+ -kāśin E.+ -kāśanīya C. -kāśaka E.+ -kāśya C. -caṅkaśa AV. -kāśana E.+ -kāśayitavya C. Meanings kāśate (kāśati) v PPP kāśita be visible, appear, shine, be brilliant or pleasant. I. cā́kaśīti & cākaśyáte shine bright; see clearly, survey. abhi I. shine bright upon, illumine; look on, survey. ava be visible, lie open. nis C niṣkāśayati See √ kas . pra be visible, shine, radiate, appear, become clear or manifest. Caus. prakāśayati (te) make visible, cause to appear, show, unveil, explain, declare as (A). saṃpra & Caus. the same. vi appear. Caus. display, spread; illuminate, irradiate. l. PfP vicā́kaśat shining, beaming; beholding, perceiving. sam appear, behold. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kaas.html"> √ kās    √ kās, “cough” Present I. kāsate etc. C.,-ti C Future Simple Future: kāsiṣyate Periphrastic Future: kāsitā Aorist RAo: acakāsat -iṣ-Ao: akāsiṣṭa Perfect kāsāṃ cakre Causative kāsaya- Desiderative cikāsiṣa- Intensive cākās- Derivatives kā́s AV. kāsá AV.C. kāsā AV. kā́sikā AV.-kāsana C. Verb-forms only in the medical literature, and probably denominative, from √ kā́s or kāsá. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ku.html"> √ ku    √ ku See √ kū 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kuc.html"> √ kuc, kuñc    √ kuc, kuñc, “shrink, curl” Present I. kuñcate etc. C VI. kucati etc. S1.C Passive kucyate C Future Simple Future: kociṣyati kuñciṣyati Periphrastic Future: kocitā kuñcitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: akocīt, akuñcīt Perfect cukoca C. cukuñca Causative kuñcayati etc. E.+; kocayati etc. E.+ Desiderative cukuñciṣa- Intensive cokucya- Verbal Nouns PPP: kucita E.+, kuñcita E.+ Derivatives kuca E.+ kuñcana C. -kocaka C. -kucana C. kuñci C. -kocin C. -kuñcaka C. koca E.+ -kocana E.+ Given by the grammarians as two distinct roots, and not without some justification. Meanings kuñc , kucati, kuñcate, PPP kuñcita v (q.v.) & kucita shrink, curl, contract, draw in (intrans.) Caus. kuñcayati. sam P = S. + close, shut (intrans.). Caus. saṃkocayati contract, draw in (trans), close up, lessen, diminish. Cf. ākuñcita, vikuñcita, saṃkucita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ku_jj.html"> √ kuñj    √ kuñj, “rustle” Present I. kuñjati C A single occurrences, in the Harṣacarita. If not a false reading, is probably an artificial word. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ku_t_t.html"> √ kuṭṭ    √ kuṭṭ, “divide, crush” Causative kuṭṭayati etc. C. (kuṭṭita C.,-kuṭṭya E.+) Derivatives -kuṭṭa E.+-kuṭṭaka C. kuṭṭana C. Perhaps a prakritized form of √ 1 kṛt . The forms avakuṭya and prakuṭya (BR. √ 2 kuṭ ) are only the usual and permitted abbreviations of-kuṭṭya. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ku_n_th.html"> √ kuṇṭh    √ kuṇṭh, “dull” Doubtless only a denominative from kuṇṭha E.+, “dull”. The participle kuṇṭhita C., and the derivatives kuṇṭhaka E.+,-kuṇṭhana E.+, occur. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kuth.html"> √ kuth    √ kuth, “stink” Causative kothayati etc. C Verbal Nouns PPP: kuthita C Derivatives kotha C. -kothaka B. Except the n. pr. nikothaka, found only in Suśruta: no proper root. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kup.html"> √ kup    √ kup, “be angry” Present IV. kupyati etc. E.+,-te etc. E Future Simple Future: kopiṣyati Periphrastic Future: kopitā Aorist Th Ao: akupat RAo: acūkupat -iṣ-Ao: kopiṣṭhās E Perfect cukopa etc. U1. E Causative kopáyati etc. RV. ŚB. E.+-te E. (cukopayiṣa- in d.) Desiderative cukupiṣa- . cukopiṣa- Intensive cokup- Verbal Nouns PPP: kupita RV1. E.+ (kupta C1. ?) Derivatives kupá B.S. kupāyú AV. ? kopin E.+ -kopitṛ E. kupana ? C. -kupya E. kopya E. kopayiṣṇu E. kúpaya RV. kopa E.+ kopana E.+ cukopavisu E. Meanings kupyati kupyate v PPP kupita become moved or agitated, boil up, be angry with (D or G). Caus. kopáyati, te excite, agitate, make angry. pari become greatly moved, be very angry. Caus. excite vehemently, make very angry. pra = S., Caus. = S. Caus. sam become angry. Caus. boil up; make angry, excite. Cf. prákupita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ku_s.html"> √ kuṣ    √ kuṣ, “tear” Present VI. kuṣati etc. C IX. kuṣṇāti etc. C Future Simple Future: koṣiṣyati kokṣyati Periphrastic Future: koṣitā koṣṭā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: akoṣīt -sa- Ao: akukṣat (cf. IS) Perfect cukoṣa Causative koṣaya- Desiderative cukuṣiṣa- cukoṣiṣa- Intensive cokuṣ- Verbal Nouns kuṣita C.; -kúṣya MS Derivatives koṣá ( ?n. pr.) ŚB. -koṣaṇa S.C. The occurrence in MS. hardly a genuine one. Meanings kuṣṇāti & kuṣati v PPP kuṣita pinch, tear, gnaw, knead. nis the same. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kuu.html"> √ kū    √ kū, “design” Present II. kauti C VI. kuvate ŚB2 Verbal Nouns PPP:-kūta AV.+; -kā́vam TS Derivatives -kūti V.+ kaví V.+ kávīyas SV. Used only with ā, except in niṣkā́vam, the belonging of which is doubtful (as is also that of kaví). RV. hasa-kava, kavatnú, kavārí, “stingy”, of questionable relationship. The grammarians set up roots 1 ku, 2 ku or kū, “shout”, giving them a full set of forms; and Nir. once uses their intens. kokūyate. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kuuj.html"> √ kūj    √ kūj, “hum” Present I. kū́jati etc. AV.+,-te etc. E Future Simple Future: kūjiṣyati Periphrastic Future: kūjitā Aorist √-Ao: akūji C Perfect cukūja -je etc. C Causative kūjaya- Desiderative cukūjiṣa- Intensive cokūj- Verbal Nouns PPP: kūjita E.+; 1Abs: kūjitvā C Derivatives kūja E.+ kūjana E.+ kūjitavya E. Meanings kūjati kūjate v make inarticulate sounds. cry, sing (of a bird), coo, caw, hum, moan, groan, etc. anu follow in crying etc. abhi , ā , ud , vi , sam = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kuu_d.html"> √ kūḍ, kūl    √ kūḍ, kūl, “burn” Causative kūḍayati etc. RV1. AB1.+, kūlayati etc. S.+ (PPP: kūlita C., 2Abs:-kūḍya S.C.) Meanings kūḍayati v (kūḍalayati) singe, scorch. upa roast. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kuu_n.html"> √ kūṇ    √ kūṇ, “shrink” Present I. kūṇati C1 Causative kūṇayati etc. C Meanings kūṇati v PPP kūṇita contract, close (intrans.). ni & vi = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kuurd.html"> √ kūrd    √ kūrd, “leap, exult” Present I. kūrdati -te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: kūrdiṣyate Periphrastic Future: kūrditā Aorist etc -iṣ-Ao: akūrdiṣṭa Perfect cukūrda etc. C.-de Verbal Nouns PPP: kūrdita C Derivatives kūrda S. kūrdana C.-kroda ? TS.-krodin ? MS. Compare √ gūrd , which is doubtless the same with this. Meanings kūrdati kūrdate v leap, jump. ud jump up. pra jump forward. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_k_r.html"> √ 1 kṛ (skṛ)    √ 1 kṛ (skṛ), “make” Present I. karanti etc. RV. kurmi E. kṛṣe (1s.) RV1 II. kárṣi AV1., kṛthás kṛtha kṛṣé RV V. kṛṇóti kṛṇuté etc. V.B.S VIII. karóti kuruté etc. RV3.AV.+ Passive kriyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: kariṣyati etc. V.+,-te etc. B.C. (akariṣyat etc. B.+) Periphrastic Future: kartā S.+ Aorist √-Ao: ákaram ádar ákran etc. akri ákṛta ákrata etc. V.B.S. (kárati -te etc. V.B.S., kriyāma RV., kriyāsam -āsma V.B.S., kṛdhí etc. V.+, kṛṣvá etc. RV., kránt krāṇá RV.; kránta RV.; akat ŚB.); ákāri V.+ Th Ao: ákarat etc. AV.B.S RAo: acīkarat C -s-Ao: akārṣīt etc. B.+, akṛṣi etc. B.C Perfect cakā́ra cakré etc. (cakártha cakṛṣé etc.) V.+ (cakriyās acakrat etc. acakriran RV.) Causative kārayati -te etc. B.+ (kāryate etc. B.; cikārayiṣa- in d.) Intensive karikṛ- carikṛ- V.B Desiderative cíkīrṣati etc. AV.+,-te etc. S.+ (acikīrṣīs ŚB.; cikīrṣayati C.) Verbal Nouns PPP: kṛtá V.+; Inf: kártum AV.+,-tave V.B.,-tavaí B.S.,-tos V.B.S.; 1Abs: kṛtvā́ AV.+,-tvī́ V.B.,-tvā́ya B.; 2Abs: -kṛ́tya V.+;-kā́ram B.+ Derivatives kará V.+ kártṛ RV. kāruka B.+ -kṛtha RV. karaṇá RV. kartṛ́ V.+ -kūrmi,-in RV. -kra RV. káraṇa V.+ kártra AV. -kṛt V.+ krátu V.+ karaṇīya B.+ kárman V.+ -kṛ́tya n. V.+ kriyā KŚS.E.+ -karaṇi? E. kárvara V. -kṛtya a. V.+ cákri RV. káras RV. -kāra V.+ kṛtyā́ V.+ -karikra B. káriṣṭha RV. kāraka E.+ kṛ́ti V.+ -cikīrṣ C. -kariṣṇu S.+ kārin AV.+ kṛ́tu (-tvas ) V.+ cikīrṣā E.+ karúṇa V.B. kāryá AV.+ kṛ́tvya RV. cikīrṣu E.+ kártva V. kāraṇa S.+ kṛtnú V. kārayitṛ B.E. kartavyà B.+ -kāraṇīya C. kṛtríma V.+ kārayitavya E.+ kāru E.+ kṛ́tvan V. cikārayiṣu C. kṛ́tvarī AV. -ciṣkārayiṣu E. The root-form skṛ is found especially after sam and pari; but also the aor. nír askṛta RV., and PPP upaskṛta E.+ In V. occur only saṃskṛta and pariṣkṛta RV.AV., and pariṣkṛṇvánti and-vánt RV. (against sám akṛṇvan etc. RV.). But from B. on, forms with sk after sam are frequent, almost to the exclusion of those with simple k; even such as sam askurvata, saṃ caskāra, saṃ skariṣyanti, saṃskārayām āsa, saṃciṣkārayiṣu. Of the derivatives, there are found with saṃ only: skaraṇa S.+, skartavya C., skartṛ E.+, skāraka E.+, skārya E.+, skṛti B.+; also skriyā with saṃ C. and pari C.; skāra with saṃ S.+, pari E.+, and upa C.; and skara with apa C., upa E.+, pari E., and vi ( ?) E.+; finally, ā́skra RV., which is doubtful. Meanings (skṛ), kṛṇóti, kṛṇuté, karóti, kurute (karati & karti), PPP kṛtá (q.v.) make, do, cause or produce anything in or on one's self or others; absol. act, work; bring or help to (D); get or procure for (G), Ā for one's self; make or begin something (A, esp. kim) with something (I); make something (A) of something (I or Ab); make (into), render 2A or A & Adj or Adv in ī, ū – With the A of an abstrans. kṛ answers to a verb of kindred mng, e.g. w. praveśam = enter, w. maraṇam die, w. rājyam reign; esp. in the periphr. Pf, e.g. vidāṃ cakāra he knew. We often use a more special verb, e.g. perform or offer (yajñam), prepare or till (kṣetram), fix (samayam), wait (kṣaṇam), utter (vācam or śabdam), exert (vīryam), show, betray, feel (kṛpām, bhāvam, sneham), enjoy (sukham), marry (dārān), violate, dishonour (kanyām) etc ; put, set in or on (pāṇau, skandhe), take to (hṛdi); ponder, deliberate (cetasi, manasi, hṛdaye), turn, direct (manas, w. L), call, name (nāmnā) etc. Note also dvidhā kṛ divide into two, bhasmasāt reduce to ashes, tṛṇavat value like straw. For other phrases cf. the corr. Adj or Adv Caus. kārayate cause to act or do (2A or A of th. & I of pers.), have something put in (L), also = S. Des cíkīrṣati, the wish to act or do. Int karikrati (3 pl.) do repeatedly. adhi put before or over, place at the head, appoint to (L); make a thing the chief matter or main point; be entitled to (P w. L, Ā w. A or Inf). anu do afterwards, imitate, equal (A or G). apa put off, remove; injure, offend, do wrong (A, L or G). abhi do in behalf of (A); effect, make. ā bring or call near; bring about, perform, prepare; serve a god (G), sacrifice. Caus. call near; ask for (2A). apā keep off, remove, pay (a debt); reject, desist. udā expel, select. upā bring near, fetch; grant, present; acquire, get; invite, prepare, undertake, begin (r.). nirā separate, select; push, away, keep off, reject, destroy; refuse, contradict. vyā divide, separate from (I), analyse, explain. samā bring together, collect, unite; make ready, prepare. is (=nis) arrange, make ready, prepare. upa bring near, impart, grant, offer, render a service (G or L of pers.); further, support; w. skṛ Ā prepare, cultivate (land), adorn. enchase; think of, care for (A or *G); deform, corrupt. pratyupa return a service. tiras put aside, remove, cover, conceal; cut out, supplant, surpass; contemn, despise, blame, abuse. ni bring down, humiliate. vini wrong, injure, offend. nis bring forth from (Ab); drive away (also w. skṛ), dispel, exclude; accomplish, arrange, settle, prepare, bring together; restore, requite. pari prepare (food); w. skṛ make ready, fit out, adorn. puras put before or at the head, place in front, introduce, appoint to (L); show, betray. pra perform, effect, cause, make, render (2A); take, marry; appoint to (L); undo, destroy, kill; violate, deflower; Ā induce, move, cause to do; direct or turn (manas, buddhim) upon (D L). resolve; gain, acquire, effect; put before, mention. vipra hurt, wrong, injure, disappoint (caus. the same*). prati do against, return, repay, revenge (A of th., G, D, L of pers.); counteract, withstand (P of th. and G of pers.); restore, requite, repay. Des wish to requite or revenge (A of th., A or L of pers.). vi make different, change, alter, divide. detail, specify; deform, spoil, destroy; develop, produce; Ā (P.) become different, alter, become hostile, unkind, or faithless (w. G or L); contend, fight. sam (kṛ & skṛ) put together, join, compose, prepare, arrange; consecrate, invest, initiate, marry; refine, embellish, adorn. abhisam (skṛ) arrange, perform. Ā render (2A); consecrate, dedicate. upasam (skṛ) prepare, adorn. pratisam restore, repair. Cf. adhikṛta, adhikṛtya, upaskṛta, nikṛta, pariṣkṛta, puraskṛta, puraskṛtya, prakṛta, víkṛta, saṃskṛta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_k_r.html"> √ 2 kṛ, kir    √ 2 kṛ, kir, “scatter” Present VI. kiráti etc. V.+,-te etc. V.+ Passive kīryáte etc. B.+ (kīryet E.) Future Simple Future: kariṣyati etc. E. karīṣyati Periphrastic Future: karī̆tā Aorist √-Ao: kīrāt C -s-Ao: akīrṣata PB -iṣ-Ao: kāriṣat RV Perfect cakāra cakre E. cakarus Causative kārayati , kīrayet E Intensive cākar- , cekīrya- Desiderative cikariṣa- Verbal Nouns kīrṇa B.+; -kīrya S.+ Derivatives kara V. ? B.+ -kāra? S.+ -kira C. -kīrya C. -karaka E. -kāraka C. kiráṇa V.+ -kula? E.+ -karitṛ B. -kir C. -kiri B. One or two late forms occur with prefixed s: apaskiramāṇa, praticaskare; others are authorized by the grammarians; in derivatives, viṣkira S.+ Meanings (skṛ), kiráti, kiráte, PPP kīrṇa pour out, cast forth, scatter, strew, cover, fill. anu scatter, strew; cover, fill. abhi sprinkle, cover, fill. ava pour down, scatter, spread, spend (semen); cast off, reject; sprinkle, bestrew, cover, fill. samava bestrew, cover entirely. ā scatter or bestow abundantly, cover over, fill. samā scatter over, cover. ud whirl up (dust); excavate, engrave. upa scatter or throw down, besprinkle, bestrew. vini scatter, disperse; throw away, abandon. pari scatter or strew about, surround. pra scatter forth, throw down; spring forth, issue, rise. vi throw asunder or about, cast, hurl, scatter, disperse, dissolve, split, rend. sam pour out, bestow richly, cover, fill; mix together, confound. Cf. ávakīrna, ākīrṇa, utkīrṇa, prakīrṇa, vikīrṇa, viprakīrṇa, vyākīrṇa, saṃkīrṇa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_3_k_r.html"> √ 3 kṛ    √ 3 kṛ, “commemorate” Present cakránt ? RV Aorist -s-Ao: akārṣam AV -iṣ-Ao: akāriṣam ákārīt RV Intensive carkarmi carkṛdhi etc. carkirāma -ran cárkṛṣe (3s.) RV. AV1 Derivatives kārá RV. kārú V. kīrtí V.+ carkṛtí RV. kārín RV. kīrí ,-ín RV. -keru RV. carkṛ́tya V. Cakránt is anomalous and altogether questionable. Meanings I.-st. carkṛ 2 (3 sgl. Ā cárkṛṣe w. P & pass. mg.) commemorate, mention, extol (G). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_k_rt.html"> √ 1 kṛt    √ 1 kṛt, “cut” Present I. kartati etc. E VI. kṛntáti etc. V.+,-te etc. B.E Passive kṛtyáte etc. AV.+ Future Simple Future: kartayati AV.; kartiṣyati C Periphrastic Future: kartitā Aorist Th Ao: ákṛtas RV. (kṛtant- RV.) RAo: acīkṛtas TB. acakartat -iṣ-Ao: kartīs B Perfect cakarta etc. (cakartitha, cakartus) V.+, cakartire E Causative kartayati etc. S.+, kṛntayati LŚS Intensive carīkṛt- Desiderative cikartiṣa- (in d.) cikṛtsa- Verbal Nouns PPP: kṛttá V.+; 1Abs: -kṛ́tya V.+;-kártam ŚB Derivatives kartá V.+ -kartin C. kṛ́tā RV. kṛntana S.+ gárta ? B.+ karttavya E. kṛtí RV. kṛntátra V.B. kartya C. -karttṛ E.+ kṛ́tti ? V.+ cikartiṣā C. kartana V.+ kartarī̆ C. -kṛnta B. cikartiṣu C. Saṃskṛtatrá V1. is doubtless not referable to this root. Meanings kṛntáti kṛntáte 1 v (kartati), PPP kṛttá cut, cut off, cleave, split, divide, destroy. Caus. kartayati (kṛntayati) the same. apa & api cut off. ava cut off, destroy. Caus. cause to be gashed. ud cut out or off, carve, tear asunder, destroy. ni cut or hew down, cut or tear off; Ā cut one's self (e.g. the nails). Caus. cause to be cut. pari cut round, clip, cut off, exclude from (Ab). pra cut off or asunder. vi the same, tear to pieces, lacerate, destroy. Caus. the same. sam cut etc. (together). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_k_rt.html"> √ 2 kṛt    √ 2 kṛt, “spin” Present VII. kṛnátti etc. V.B.S. Causative kartita kartya C. Derivatives karttṛ E. Meanings kṛṇátti 2 v twist the thread, spin. Caus. kṛtayati weave. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_k_rp.html"> √ kṛp    √ kṛp, “lament” Present I. kṛpate etc. V. (kálpant ? AV.) Perfect cākṛpánta RV. Aorist √-Ao: akṛpran C -iṣ-Ao: akrapiṣṭa RV Causative kṛpáyati (kṛpayánt RV.) -te etc. JB. Derivatives kṛpá E.+ kṛpáṇa V.+ kṛpáṇá AV.+ Meanings kṛpate mourn, long for (A). anu S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_k_rz.html"> √ kṛś    √ kṛś, “be lean” Present IV. kṛ́śyati ŚB Future Simple Future: karśiṣyati Periphrastic Future: karśitā Aorist ThAo: akṛśat Perfect cakárśa AV Causative karśáyati etc. V.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: kṛśita AB. 1Abs: kṛśitvā, karśitvā Derivatives karśana V.+ kṛśá V.+ kráśīyas C. Meanings kṛ́śyati v PPP kṛśita become or be lean or feeble. Caus. karśayati, PPP karśita (often confounded with the Caus. of kṛṣ) make lean, keep short of food, diminish, attenuate, vex, torment. anu , ava , pra , vi afflict, vex. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_k_r_s.html"> √ kṛṣ    √ kṛṣ, “drag, plough” Present I. kárṣate etc. V.+-te etc. B.+ VI. kṛṣáti -te etc. V.+ Passive kṛṣyáte etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: krakṣyánt S., krakṣye B., karkṣyati karṣiṣyánt B Periphrastic Future: karṣṭā, kraṣṭā Aorist RAo: acīkṛṣam RV. acakarṣat -s-Ao: akārkṣīt, akrākṣīt -sa- Ao: akṛkṣat etc. B. (akṛkṣathās ŚB.) Perfect cakarṣa etc. (cakarṣatus) B.+ Causative karṣayati etc. E.+ Intensive cárkṛsati etc. V.B. carīkṛṣ- Desiderative cikṛkṣa- Verbal Nouns PPP: kṛṣṭá AV.+; Inf: kraṣṭum E.+; 1Abs: kṛṣṭvā́ B.+; 2Abs: -kṛṣya S.+ Derivatives karṣa S.+ karṣū́ B.+ kā́rṣi ,-ṣín B. kṛṣya S.+ karṣaka E.+ karṣaṇa E.+ kā́rṣman RV. kṛṣṭí V.+ karṣin ,-ṣí B.+ karṣaṇīya C. kṛṣí V.+ kraṣṭavya C. -kraṣṭṛ C. It does not seem worth while to divide this root, evidently one, into two nearly related ones, as is often done. Meanings kárṣati kárṣate v (kṛṣáti, kṛṣáte), PPP kṛṣṭá (q.v.) drag, draw; pull, tear, bend (a bow); draw furrows, plough (only kṛ́ṣati); draw to one's self, get possession of, overpower. Caus. karṣayati tug, pull, tear, extract; affict, vex (cf. kṛś Caus. ). I. cárkṛṣati plough. ati draw beyond. anu draw after one's self; attract from the preceding, supply (g.); quote. apa draw away, take off; reject, remove; bend (a bow); detract, debase, dishonour. vyapa draw away, take off, doff; reject, remove, abandon. ava draw or take off, remove, drag down. ā draw on, attract; bend (a bow); drag away; take off, extract, remove from (Ab). apā turn away, avert from (Ab). vyā draw to one's self; draw off, remove, avert. samā draw near; extract from (Ab). ud draw out or up, take off; bend (a bow); raise (fig.); rise, be superior. ni draw down. saṃni P. come near, come in contact with (I). nis draw out, extract; tear in pieces, rend asunder. pari draw about, conduct (army); vex afflict; think over, ponder. pra draw forth, conduct (an army); vex, afflict. vipra draw away, remove. saṃpra the same. vi draw asunder, tear in pieces; draw towards one's self (arrow), bend (bow), turn up (foam), drag about, pull; conduct (army); extract, deprive, withhold. sama draw together, contract; drag away, carry off. Cf. apakṛṣṭa, avakṛṣṭa, utkṛṣṭa, nikṛṣṭa, prakṛṣṭa, vikṛṣṭa, viprakṛṣṭa, saṃnikṛṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_k_rp.html"> √ kṛp    √ kṛp, “lament” Present I. kṛpate etc. V. (kálpant ? AV.) Perfect cākṛpánta RV. Aorist √-Ao: akṛpran C -iṣ-Ao: akrapiṣṭa RV Causative kṛpáyati (kṛpayánt RV.) -te etc. JB. Derivatives kṛpá E.+ kṛpáṇa V.+ kṛpáṇá AV.+ Meanings kṛpate mourn, long for (A). anu S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_knuu.html"> √ knū    √ knū, “wet” Present IV. knūyate Future Simple Future: knūyiṣyati Periphrastic Future: knūyitā Aorist aknūyīt Perfect cuknūye Causative knopayati (-knopam C.) Verbal Nouns -knū́yam ŚB Derivatives -knopana C. Meanings (*knūyate), only Caus. knopayati (abhi) wet, moisten. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_krak_s.html"> √ krakṣ    √ krakṣ, “crash” Present I. krákṣamāna RV1 Derivatives -krakṣa RV1. -krakṣin RV1. Apparently an onomatopoetic root. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_krath.html"> √ krath    √ krath, “be jubilant” Present I. krathati etc Causative krātháyati TB1 Derivatives kratha E. krathana E. krātha E.-krāthin E. krāthana C. A very doubtful group of derivatives, in meaning and connection. Meanings (*krathati), only Caus. krātháyati exult; *hurt. injure (G). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_krand.html"> √ krand, kland    √ krand, kland, “cry out” Present I. krándati etc. V.+,-te etc. E. klandate C1 Future Simple Future: krandiṣyati Periphrastic Future: kranditā Aorist Th Ao: kradas RV RAo: acikradat etc. V.B -s-Ao: ákrān V.B -iṣ-Ao: akrandīt C Perfect cakranda C., cakradé RV. (cakradat etc. RV.) Causative krandáyati etc. V.+ Desiderative cikrandiṣa- Intensive kánikrand- , kánikrad-, kanikradyá- V.B. cākrand- Verbal Nouns PPP: krandita C.; Inf: kranditum C Derivatives kránda V.+ klandá AV. krandanú RV. -krandin C. krándana V.+ krándas V. krándya V.B. -krandanīya C. kanikradá B. Meanings krándati krándate v roar, neigh, creak, click, cry, lament. Caus. krandáyati make roar, neigh, etc., also = S. I. kánikrantti, kanikrantte, esp. PPP kánikrat, kánikradat & kanikradyámāna = S. abhi shout or roar at, call to (also Caus. & Int). ava roar (also Caus. ). ā call to, invoke, cry, lament. Caus. the same; also cause to cry or lament. pra call aloud. vi lament. sam cry together with (I). Cf. ākrandita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kram.html"> √ kram    √ kram, “stride” Present I. krā́matietc. krámateetc. V.+ (kramati etc. RV. ? E.+, krāmate etc. U.E.) IV. krāmyati Passive kramyate etc. S.+ Future Simple Future: kraṃsyáti -te AV.B.E.; kramiṣyati -te B.+ (akramiṣyat U.) Periphrastic Future: kramitā, kraṃtā Aorist √-Ao: akran ákramus etc. RV Th Ao: akramat -man AV.B RAo: acikramat -s-Ao: akraṃsta -sata etc. V.B.S. (kraṃsate RV.) -iṣ-Ao: ákramīt etc. V.B.U., krámiṣṭa (3s.) RV. (akramīm RV., akrāmīt ŚB.) Perfect cakrā́ma cakramús etc., cakramé etc. V.+ (cákramanta RV.) Causative kramayati etc. B.+; krāmayati etc. B.+ (krāmyate C.) Desiderative cikramiṣati etc. B.U. cikraṃsa- Intensive caṅkram- V.+, caṅkramyáte B.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: krāṃtá AV.+; Inf: krámitum B.+,-tos B., krāṃtum E.+; 1Abs: kramitvā E.+, krāṃtvā́ B.+ kraṃtvā; 2Abs: -krámya V.+;-kráme RV.;-krā́mam AV.+ Deriv.: kráma V.+ -kramaṇīya E.+ -krāmya C. -krāṃtṛ E. -kramin E.+ -kramitavya E. -krāmaṇa C. caṅkrama AV.+ kramya C. -krāma B. -krā́muka B. caṅkramaṇa S.+ krámaṇa V.+ -krāmin AV.B. -krāṃti B.+ -krāmayitavya C. The aor. akran is by some referred to √ krand . Meanings krā́mati krámate v (kramati, krāmate), PPP krāntá (mostly – ṃ & w. P mg). stride, step, walk, go or come to (A or L); go over, pass, ascend, approach (sex.); surpass, pervade, fill, accomplish; Ā proceed well, succeed. Caus. kramayati (krāmayati) cause to stride. I. caṅkramate, caṅkramyáte & caṅkramīti step to and fro, wander, walk, pass. ati step beyond, cross, pass, excel, overcome, pass by, neglect, transgress (abs. or w. A); part or escape from, lose, be deprived of (Ab). Caus. let pass, take no notice of (A). abhyati step beyond or across, pass, excel, overcome, overstep, neglect, transgress. vyati & samati the same, adhi ascend, mount up to (A) anu go on or along, follow; go through, enumerate. apa go or pass away; withdraw or fly from (Ab). abhi step near, approach, attack, overwhelm; enter, begin, undertake. samabhi come near, approach. ava go away, fly; tread upon, overwhelm (A). ā approach, visit, enter, tread upon (A or L); cling to, grasp, attack, overpower, take hold or possession of (A); undertake, begin (Inf); ascend, mount (mostly Ā). adhyā attack, seize, occupy. samā the same + tread upon, overpower, take hold or possession of (A). ud go up or out, depart; escape, fly or withdraw from (Ab or A); pass by, neglect. vyud go asunder, part, go away; overstep, transgress, disregard. upa come near, approach, enter (A or L); go against, attack; treat, deal with (A); (mostly Ā) undertake, begin, be about to (A, D, or Inf). samupa come near; undertake, begin (Ā w. Inf). ni enter, step, tread down. nis go out of (Ab), depart, fly, escape. Caus. cause to step out, expel, lead or take away. abhinis, upanis, & vinis go out, come forth from (Ab). parā step forward, advance, exert one's self, excel. pari walk about (esp. on the stage), circumambulate, walk through, visit; overtake, overcome. pra step forth, set out, go to (A), go across, pass; Ā deal with (L); Ā (P) proceed to, undertake, begin (A, artham, or Inf). saṃpra Ā proceed to, begin (A or Inf). prati & anuprati come back. vi go asunder, part, separate; walk through, bestride; move on, advance, proceed, exert one's self; content, fight against (A). anuvi Ā step after. nirvi step out. sam come together, meet, encounter; go to, enter (A), pass from (Ab) to (L), go through or across, come near, walk along. Caus. cause to pass, transport, deliver; lead to (2A), cast upon (A of th. and L of pers.). anusam follow after (A), also = upasam step towards, come or pass to (A). Cf. adhyākrānta, ākrānta, niṣkrānta, vikrānta, saṃkrānta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_krii.html"> √ krī    √ krī, “buy” Present IX. krīṇā́ti krīṇīte etc. V.+ Passive krīyate etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: kreṣyati -te etc. B.S Periphrastic Future: kretā Aorist akraiṣīt , akreṣṭa Perfect cikrāya S. cikriye Causative krāpayati , acikrapat Desiderative cikrīṣate C Intensive cekrī- Verbal Nouns PPP: krītá V.+; Inf: kretum E.+; 1Abs: krītvā́ AV.+; 2Abs: -krī́ya B.+ Derivatives krayá AV.+ krayya B.+ -krāyaka E.+ kretavya E.+ -krayaka E. kráyaṇa B.+ -krī AV.+ kretṛ E.+ -krayin E.+ krayaṇīya S. -krīti B. kreya E.+ Meanings krīṇā́ti & krīṇīté v PPP krītá (q.v.) buy, purchase (w. I of price & A or G of pers.). apa = S. abhi buy for a certain purpose. ava Ā purchase, hire. ā & upa buy. nis buy off or ransom from (Ab); Ā (~ ātmānam) buy off one's self. pari purchase, get by exchange; hire, obtain (*w. D or I of price). vi exchange or sell for (I). sam = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_krii_d.html"> √ krīḍ    √ krīḍ, “play” Present I. krī́ḍati -te etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: krīḍiṣyati C Periphrastic Future: kriḍitā Aorist RAo: acikrīḍat -iṣ-Ao: akrīḍīt Perfect cikrīḍa -ḍe etc. B.+ Causative krīḍayati etc. S.+ (krīḍāpayati R.) Desiderative cikrīḍiṣa-. (in d.) Intensive cekrīḍ- Verbal Nouns PPP: krīḍita E.+; Inf: krīḍitum C.; 2Abs: -krīḍya E Derivatives krīḍá V.+ krīḍín V.+ krīḍí RV.B. cikrīḍiṣā C. krīḍā́ B.+ krīḍana E.+ krīḍitṛ C. cikrīḍiṣu C. krīḍú RV. Meanings krī́ḍati v (krī́ḍati) & krīḍate, PPP krīḍita (q.v.) play, sport, amuse one's self with (I of th. & I ~ saha, sārdham, or samam of pers.). Caus. krīḍayati cause to play. ā & samā = S. pari play about pra begin to play, also = S. vi & sam = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kru.html"> √ kru    √ kru, “be rough or raw” Such a root appears to be assumable for the derivatives kravaṇá RV. kravís, -vi V. kraviṣṇú V. kravyá V.+-kru RV. krūrá AV.+ 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_krudh.html"> √ krudh    √ krudh, “be angry” Present IV. krúdhyati etc. AV.+,-te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: krotsyati Periphrastic Future: kroddhā Aorist Th Ao: krudhat etc. AV RAo: ácukrudhat etc. RV Perfect cukrodha cukrudhus etc. B.+ Causative krodháyati etc. AV.+ (krodhyate M.) Desiderative cukrutsa- Intensive cokrudh- Verbal Nouns PPP: kruddhá V.+; Inf: kroddhum E.; 1Abs: kruddhvā S Derivatives krudh C. krúdhmí RV. kródha AV.+ krodhana E.+ krodhanīya E. Meanings krádhyati 1 v (krudhyate), PPP kruddhá be angry with (D, G, or L; PPP also w. upari or prati). Caus. krodháyati make angry, irritate. abhi be angry with (A). prati be angry with (A) in return. sam & abhisam be angry. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kruz.html"> √ kruś    √ kruś, “cry out” Present I. króśati etc. V.+,-te etc. RV.E Passive kruśyate E Future Simple Future: krokṣyati Periphrastic Future: kroṣṭā Aorist -sa- Ao: akrukṣat etc. V.B Perfect cukrośa etc. E. cukruśe Causative krośya E.+ Desiderative cukrukṣa- Intensive cokruś- Verbal Nouns PPP: kruṣṭa B.+; Inf: kroṣṭum E.; 2Abs: -kruśya E.+ Derivatives -krośa V.+ -krośin C. klóśa RV. kroṣṭu C. -krośaka B.+ -krośya S. krośaná V.+ kroṣṭṛ́ V.+ -krośayitṛ C. Meanings króśati króśate v PPP kruṣṭa (w. P & Ps. mg) cry out, shout, croak, lament; call to (A). anu shout at (A); Caus. show sympathy (lit. follow in lamenting). abhi call or cry at (A), lament, mourn. ā call aloud, scold at, revile, defame; challenge, emulate. ud cry out, call to (A). upa show anger or defiance. pra raise a cry, call at (A). vi the same. sam cry out together, shout angrily at (A). Cf. apakruṣṭa, ākruṣṭa, upakruṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kruu_d.html"> √ krūḍ    √ krūḍ, “thicken”, ( ?) Causative akrūḍayat , krūḍyamāna, cukrūḍāyati B All in a single passage of the Kāṭhaka. Possible derivative, kroḍá AV.+ 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_klath.html"> √ klath    √ klath, “turn” ( ?) Present I. kláthan B A single occurrence, in VS.; no derivatives. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kland.html"> √ kland    √ kland See √ krand. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_klam.html"> √ klam    √ klam, “be weary” Present IV. klāmyati C Future Simple Future: klamiṣyati Periphrastic Future: klamitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aklamīt Perfect caklāma , caklame C Causative klāmayati C Verbal Nouns PPP: klāṃtá E.+ Derivatives klama E.+ klāṃti C. Compare √ śram. Meanings klāmyati v PPP klānta (q.v.) be weary or languid. Caus. klāmayati tire, exhaust. pari be extremely tired or exhausted. vi Ā languish, despond. Cf. atiklāmita, viklānta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_klav.html"> √ klav    √ klav, “stammer” Verbal Nouns klavita C Probably artificial and false, inferred from viklava E.+, viklavita C. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_klid.html"> √ klid    √ klid, “be wet” Present I. klindant C1 IV. klidyati -te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: klediṣyati kletsyati Periphrastic Future: kleditā klettā Aorist √-Ao: aklidat RAo: aciklidat Perfect cikleda Causative kledayati etc. S.+ Desiderative ciklediṣa- , ciklidiṣa-, ciklitsa- Intensive ceklid- Verbal Nouns PPP: klinna S.+ 1Abs: kliditvā, klittvā Derivatives -klíndu AV. -kledin C. kledana C. kleda E.+ -kledya E. -klediyas AV. Meanings klidyati v PPP klinna (q.v.) be or become wet. Caus. kledayati wet, moisten, soil. Cf. klindant, parikninna, viklinna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kliz.html"> √ kliś    √ kliś, “distress” Present IV. kliśyate etc. E.+,-ti etc. E.+ IX. kliśnāti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: kleśiṣyati klekṣyati Periphrastic Future: kleśitā kleṣṭā Aorist etc RAo: acikliśat -iṣ-Ao: akleśīt -sa- Ao: aklikṣat Ao/Ps/3/sg: akleśi Precative: kliśyāt Perfect cikleśa etc. C Causative kleśayati etc. E.+ Desiderative cikleśiṣa- , cikliśiṣa-, ciklidṣa- Intensive cekliś- Verbal Nouns PPP: kliṣṭa E.+ kliśita; Inf: kleṣtum E.; 1Abs: kliśitvā, kliṣṭvā; 2Abs: -klíśya ŚB.+ Derivatives kleśa U.+ -kleśaka C. kleśin C. kleśana C. kleṣṭṛ E. Meanings kliśnāti v (kliśyati, kliśyate) PPP kliṣṭa (q.v.) torment, trouble, molest; P. kliśyate (ti) be distressed, suffer. Caus. kleśayati = S. trans. ati (kliśyati) have or give too much pains.* sam press together, sqash; trouble, molest. Cf. parikliṣṭa, vikliṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kva_n.html"> √ kvaṇ    √ kvaṇ, “sound” Present I. kvaṇati C Future Simple Future: kvaṇiṣyati Periphrastic Future: kvaṇitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: akvāṇīt Perfect cakvāṇa Causative kvaṇayati etc. C Verbal Nouns kvaṇita C Derivatives -kvaṇana C. Meanings kvaṇati v PPP kvaṇita (q.v.) sound, hum, tinkle. ud = S.* 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kvath.html"> √ kvath    √ kvath, “boil” Present I. kvathati -te etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: kvathiṣyati Periphrastic Future: kvathitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: akvathīt Perfect cakvātha Causative kvāthayati etc. S.+ (kvāthyate etc. E.+) Verbal Nouns kvathita C Derivatives kvatha C. kvathana C. kvātha C. kvāthayitavya C. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_k_sad.html"> √ kṣad    √ kṣad, “divide” Present I. kṣádate etc. V.B Perfect cakṣadé etc. RV Derivatives kṣattṛ́ V.-kṣad RV. kṣádman RV. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_k_san.html"> √ kṣan    √ kṣan, “wound” Present VIII. kṣaṇóti kṣaṇuté etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: kṣaṇiṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: kṣaṇitā Aorist √-Ao: akṣata -iṣ-Ao: kṣaṇiṣṭās AV. akṣaṇīt Perfect cakṣāṇa cakṣaṇe Causative kṣāṇaya- Desiderative cikṣaṇiṣa- Intensive caṅkṣaṇ- Verbal Nouns kṣata V.+; kṣaṇítos ŚB Derivatives kṣaṇana C. kṣati E.+ Meanings kṣaṇóti v PPP kṣata (q.v.) hurt, harm, wound, break; Ā kṣaṇuté refl. & intrans. Cf. parikṣata, vikṣata. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_k_sap.html"> √ kṣap    √ kṣap, “be abstinent” Present I. kṣapati E.+, kṣápate V.S Verbal Nouns kṣapitum C Derivatives kṣapaṇa E.+ The words kṣáp V., kṣapā́ V.+ do not appear to be connected with this root. Meanings kṣapati 1 v & kṣápate do penance, be abstinent. sam the same. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_k_sam.html"> √ kṣam    √ kṣam, “endure” Present I. kṣámate etc. V.+,-ti etc. E.+ (kṣā́mat AV. ?) IV. kṣamyate etc. E.+ kṣāmyati Passive kṣamyate E.+ Future Simple Future: kṣaṃsyati etc. E., kṣamiṣyati B.+ Periphrastic Future: kṣaṃtā, kṣamitā Aorist Th Ao: akṣamat RAo: acikṣamat -s-Ao: akṣaṃsta -iṣ-Ao: akṣamiṣṭa Perfect cakṣame etc. B.+ (cakṣamīthās RV.) Causative kṣamayati etc. E.+ (kṣāmaye M., kṣamāpaya-. C.) Desiderative cikṣaṃsa- , cikṣamiṣa- Intensive caṅkṣam- Verbal Nouns PPP: kṣāṃta E.+, kṣamita E.; Inf: kṣaṃtum E.+ Derivatives kṣám , kṣā́ V. kṣamaṇīya E. kṣaṃtṛ E. kṣāṃti E.+ kṣamá AV.+ kṣaṃtavya E.+ kṣāmya E. kṣmā́ V.+ kṣamā E.+ kṣamitavya E. kṣā́man V. cākṣmá ? RV. kṣā́mi SV. kṣamāpaṇa C1. Meanings kṣámate 1 v (kṣamati & kṣamyate), PPP kṣānta (q.v.) be patient or quiet, endure, suffer, bear, pardon, forgive (G or D of pers. & A of th., PPP also kṣamita); be able to (Inf). Caus. kṣamayati, te ask pardon for (2A); endure, put up with (A). abhi be gracious, pardon. sam suffer, put up with (A). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_k_sar.html"> √ kṣar    √ kṣar, “flow” Present I. kṣárati etc. V.+,-te etc. E Future Simple Future: kṣariṣyati Periphrastic Future: kṣaritā Aorist ákṣār (3s.) RV Perfect cakṣāra C Causative kṣārayati etc. B.+ Desiderative cikṣariṣa- Intensive cākṣar- Verbal Nouns PPP: kṣarita B.; kṣáradhyai RV Derivatives kṣara V.+ kṣaraṇa C. kṣāraṇa C. kṣīrá ? V.+ Meanings kṣárati v (kṣárate) flow, glide, melt away, perish; flow with, abound in (A). Caus. kṣārayati cause to flow, dismiss. abhi flow through (A); overflow. anu flow upon or into (A) abhi the same, flow about. ā Caus. cause to flow near, sprinkle, soil; defame, accuse. upa flow near. prati flow around or towards. pra stream forth. vi flow asunder, pour down. sam flow together. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_k_sal.html"> √ kṣal    √ kṣal, “wash” Causative kṣālayati etc. B.+ (kṣālāpayīta S.) Derivatives kṣāla E.+ -kṣālaka E.+-kṣālya C.-kṣālana S.+ Doubtless the same with the preceding root, √ kṣar. Meanings kṣālayati v wash, cleanse. pra & abhiprā = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_k_saa.html"> √ kṣā    √ kṣā, “burn” Present IV. kṣā́yati etc. B.S Causative kṣā́páyati etc. AV.B.S Verbal Nouns PPP: kṣāṇa ? B.S Derivatives -kṣā́ṇa B. kṣātí RV. kṣāma B.+ kṣāra E.+ Meanings kṣā́yati v PPP kṣāṇa 1 burn, set on fire. Caus. kṣāpáyati burn, scorch. pra burn (intrans.). sam burn (trans.). Cf. avakṣā́ṇa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_k_si.html"> √ 1 kṣi    √ 1 kṣi, “possess” Present I. kṣáyati etc. V II. kṣéti etc. V.B. (kṣyánt TS., kṣiyánt V.) VI. kṣiyáti etc. AV.B Future Simple Future: kṣeṣyánt RV Aorist -s-Ao: kṣeṣat RV Perfect cikṣāya Causative kṣayáya RV., kṣepayat RV Derivatives kṣáya V. kṣayaṇá VS. -kṣit V.+ -kṣetṛ RV. kṣā́ ? V. kṣatrá ? V.+ kṣití V.+ kṣétra V.+ -kṣas? RV. kṣéma V.+ Meanings kṣéti kṣiyáti kṣáyati 1 v abide, dwell, inhabit; rule, be master of (G). Caus. kṣayáyati & kṣepayati pacify. adhi dwell in, rest on, spread over (A or L). ā dwell in, inhabit, be or become possessed of (A), exist. upa dwell in or near, remain with, rest or depend on (A), pari dwell about (A). prati settle at (A). sam dwell together with (I). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_k_si.html"> √ 2 kṣi, kṣī    √ 2 kṣi, kṣī, “destroy” Present I. kṣayati E II. kṣidhí SV1 IV. kṣī́yate etc. V.B V. kṣiṇoti etc. AV.+ IX. kṣiṇā́ti etc. V.B Passive kṣīyáte V.+ Future Simple Future: akṣeṣyata (3s.) ŚB.; kṣayiṣyāmi R Periphrastic Future: kṣetā Aorist √-Ao: kṣīyat; kṣāyi B.S -s-Ao: kṣeṣṭhās kṣeṣṭa AV.B.S.U Perfect cikṣāya Causative kṣayayati etc. E.+; kṣapayati etc. E.+ Desiderative cikṣīṣati B Intensive cekṣi- Verbal Nouns PPP: kṣitá V.+, kṣīna AV.+;-kṣetos B.; 1Abs: kṣītvā; 2Abs: -kṣī́ya ŚB Derivatives kṣaya E.+ -kṣayaṇa AV.B.S. kṣeṣṇú B. -kṣapayitṛ C. kṣayin E.+ kṣayiṣṇu U.C. kṣapaṇa E.+ kṣapayiṣṇu C. kṣayya B.+ -kṣit B. kṣapitavya C. kṣayayitavya E. kṣíti AV.+ Meanings kṣiṇāti kṣiṇóti 2 v (kṣayati), PPP kṣitá & kṣīṇá (q.v.) destroy, injure, exhaust; P. kṣīyáte (kṣī́yate) be exhausted, perish, cease, wane (moon). Caus. kṣayayati & kṣapayati, te = S. tr; w. kālam etc. pass, spend. apa & upa P. = S. P. pari destroy; P. suffer loss, become poor. pra , sam P & P. = S. Cf. parikṣīṇa, prákṣīṇa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_k_sip.html"> √ kṣip    √ kṣip, “throw” Present VI. kṣipáti etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ Passive kṣipyate E.+ (-yant M.) Future Simple Future: kṣepsyati etc. E.+,-te E Periphrastic Future: kṣeptā Aorist √-Ao: kṣipyāt; akṣepi RAo: cikṣipat etc. V -s-Ao: akṣaipsīt, akṣipta Perfect cikṣepa etc. U.E.+, cikṣipe E Causative kṣepayati etc. E.+ Desiderative cikṣipsa- (in d.) Intensive cekṣip- Verbal Nouns PPP: kṣiptá V.+, kṣipita S.; Inf: kṣeptum E.+,-tos B.; 1Abs: kṣiptvā C.; 2 Abs: -kṣipya E.+; -kṣepam E Derivatives kṣíp RV. kṣipti C. kṣepya C. kṣeptavya E.+ -kṣipa C. kṣiprá V.+ kṣepan B. kṣeptṛ E.+ kṣípā RV. kṣepa E.+ kṣepaṇa S.+ kṣepnú RV. kṣipaní RV. kṣepaka E.+ kṣépiṣṭha B. -cikṣipsu C. kṣipaṇú RV. -kṣepin C. kṣépīyas B.+ Meanings kṣipáti kṣipáte v PPP kṣiptá 1 (q.v.) throw, cast, send; put, place, direct, turn (esp. the eye or mind); hit, hurt; abuse, scold; throw down, cast off, reject; destroy, annihilate; pass, spend (time). Caus. kṣepayati cause to (be) cast, make to descend through (I) into (L). adhi bespatter, insult, abuse. apa cast off, take away, remove. abhi strike at (A). ava throw down, throw into (L) hurl at (D); take off. ā throw at (L or D), put in (L); strike, hit; draw near, attract; take away, withdraw, cast off; insult, revile. vyā stretch out (the hand), open (the mouth); strike, attract (the mind). samā throw together, pile up; shake, hurl; take away, tear off, expel, destroy; insult, revile. ud throw, set or take up, life, raise; extract from (Ab); cast off, get rid of (A). samud throw up, lift; loosen, deliver of (Ab); annihilate, destroy. upa throw at, hurl against (L); strike, hit, esp. w. words, i.e. either insult, mock, revile, or intimate, insinuate, allege, allude to (A). ni throw down, place, put, apply; deposit, grant, deliver, entrust, appoint (2A or A of pers. & L of th.); leave, abandon, give up. upani put down. vini throw or put down, commit, entrust. pari throw beyond, put or lay round, surround, encircle, place or put in (L). pra throw far, set before; fling at, put in (L); let down. prati hurt, harm, reject, despise. vi throw asunder, scatter, dispel, distribute; extend, stretch out; let loose (the bow-string), shoot off (the bow); *handle, manage. pravi toss, harass. sam throw together, heap up; compress, contract, abbreviate, diminish. Cf. ākṣipta, vikṣipta, saṃkṣipta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_k_su.html"> √ kṣu    √ kṣu, “sneeze” Present II. kṣauti kṣuvánti etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: kṣaviṣyati Periphrastic Future: kṣavitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: akṣāvīt Perfect cukṣāva etc. B., cukṣuve C Desiderative cukṣūṣati JB. caus. cukṣāvayiṣati Verbal Nouns PPP: kṣuta E.+; 1Abs: kṣutvā B.+ Derivatives kṣava AV. kṣavathu C. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_k_sud.html"> √ kṣud    √ kṣud, “crush” Present I. kṣódati -te RV VII. kṣuṇatti kṣuntte Future Simple Future: kṣotsyati, -te Periphrastic Future: kṣottā Aorist Th Ao: akṣudat -siṣ-Ao: akṣautsīt akṣutta Perfect cukṣudus E Causative kṣodayati etc. RV.C Verbal Nouns PPP: kṣuṇṇa E.+; 2Abs: -kṣudya C Derivatives kṣudrá V.+ kṣoda E.+ kṣódas RV. kṣódiṣṭha B. kṣodya E. kṣodīyas B.+ Meanings kṣódati v PPP kṣuṇa (q.v.) pound, shatter, shake, stamp upon, dash to pieces. Caus. kṣodáyati shake, crush. ava , pra , vi , sam = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_k_sudh.html"> √ kṣudh    √ kṣudh, “be hungry” Present IV. kṣúdhyati etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: kṣotsyati Periphrastic Future: kṣoddhā Aorist Th Ao: kṣudhat AV Perfect cukṣodha Verbal Nouns PPP: kṣudhita U.+ 1Abs: kṣudhitvā Derivatives kṣúdh V.+ kṣudhā E.+-kṣudhya AV. kṣudhi C. kṣódhuka B.S. Meanings kṣúdhyati v PPP kṣudhita 1 be hungry. vi = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_k_sup.html"> √ kṣup    √ kṣup, “be startled” ( ?) Present VI. akṣupat R1. (Th Ao?) Derivatives kṣupa E.+ kṣúmpa RV. Not a genuine root. The only verbal form in a single punning etymology. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_k_subh.html"> √ kṣubh    √ kṣubh, “quake” Present I. kṣobhate U1 IV. kṣubhyati -te etc. E.+ V. kṣubhnuyus JB IX. kṣubhnāti Perfect cukṣobha C., cukṣubhe AV.+ Aorist Th Ao: akṣubhat RAo: acukṣubhat -iṣ-Ao: akṣobhīt -bhiṣṭa Ao/Ps/3/sg: akṣobhi Precative: kṣubhyāt Future Simple Future: kṣobhiṣyati, -te Periphrastic Future: kṣobhitā Verbal Nouns PPP: kṣubdha B.+, kṣubhita E.+;-kṣobdhos ŚB. Inf: kṣobhitum; 1Abs: kṣubdhvā, kṣubhitvā Intensive cokṣubh- Desiderative cukṣubhiṣa- , cukṣobhiṣa- Causative kṣobhayati -te E.+ (kṣobhyate E.+, cukṣobhayiṣa- in d.) Derivatives kṣúbh RV. kṣobha B.+ -kṣobhin C. kṣóbhaṇa V.+ kṣubhā E.+ kṣobhaka C. kṣobhya E.+ kṣobhayitṛ C. cukṣobhayiṣu E. Meanings kṣubhyatí kṣubhyate 1 v (kṣobhate), PPP kṣubdha or kṣubhita tremble, shake, be agitated. Caus. kṣobhayati (te) agitate, impel, set in motion. pra vi & sam = S. Cf. prakṣóbdhos. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_k_s_nu.html"> √ kṣṇu    √ kṣṇu, “whet” Present II. kṣṇaumi RV., kṣṇauti S., kṣṇuvāná AV Perfect cukṣṇāva Aorist -iṣ-Ao: akṣṇāvīt Future Simple Future: kṣṇaviṣyati Periphrastic Future: kṣṇavitā Verbal Nouns PPP: kṣṇutá B.; 2Abs: -kṣṇutya B Derivatives -kṣṇut B.S. kṣṇótra RV. Meanings kṣṇóti v whet, sharpen. ava rub to pieces, crush. sam Ā = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_k_smaa.html"> √ kṣmā    √ kṣmā, “tremble” Present IV. kṣmāyate Perfect cakṣmāye Causative kṣmāpayati C No genuine root. The single example in Nirukta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_k_svi_d.html"> √ kṣviḍ    √ kṣviḍ, “hum” Present I. kṣveḍati etc. E.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: kṣveḍita E.+ Causative kṣveḍayati E Derivatives kṣveḍa E.+ kṣveḍana E.+ A later form of the root next following, √ kṣvid. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_k_svid.html"> √ kṣvid    √ kṣvid, “hum” Present I. kṣvedati etc. B Verbal Nouns PPP: kṣviṇṇa C.;-kṣvídas B Apparently onomatopoetic. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_k_svel.html"> √ kṣvel    √ kṣvel, “play” Present I. kṣvelati etc. R Verbal Nouns PPP: kṣvelita E.+ Derivatives kṣvelana C. kṣveli C. Meanings kṣvelati v leap, jump; play. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_khac.html"> √ khac    √ khac, “show through ? Present I. khacati etc. C Verbal Nouns PPP: khacita E.+ Meanings khacati v PPP khacant glimmering, shining, & khacita q.v. Cf. utkhacita & parikhacita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kha_jj.html"> √ khañj    √ khañj, “limp” Present I. khañjati etc. C Perfect cakhañja Derivatives khañja C. khañjana C. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_khad.html"> √ khad    √ khad, “be hard” Present VI.-khadánt ? ŚB Perfect cakhāda Derivatives khadā S. khadirá V.+ Very doubtful root, the occurrence in ŚB. perhaps a false reading. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_khan.html"> √ khan, khā    √ khan, khā, “dig” Present I. khánati -te etc. V.+ Passive khāyate etc. B.+, khanyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: khaniṣyati etc. B.+ Periphrastic Future: khanitā Aorist √-Ao: khanyāt, khāyāt RAo: acīkhanat -s-Ao: khān B -iṣ-Ao: akhā̆nīt, akhaniṣṭa Perfect cakhā́na cakhnus etc. AV.+ cakhne Causative khānayati etc. S.+ (khanaya-. E. ?) Desiderative cikhaniṣa- Intensive caṅkhan- , cākhā- Verbal Nouns PPP: khātá V.+; Inf: khánitum B.+; 1Abs: khanitvā C., khātvā B.+,-tvī́ B.; 2Abs: -khāya B.+;-khānam S Derivatives khá V.+ khanana C. khanítra V.+ khānya S. khā V.+ khananīya C. khara V.+ khāni C. khaná AV. khaní AV.+ khátṛ C. -khu V.+ khanaka E. khanitṛ́ V.+ khānaka C. -kheya C. Meanings khánati khánate v PPP khāta dig, dig up, delve, bury. Caus. khānayati. abhi turn up (the soil). ud root up, extract, exterminate, destroy. prod & samud the same. ni bury, inter; dig up, root up; infix, pierce. nis dig out. pari dig round, dig up. pra eradicate, overturn. vi dig up. Cf. antarnikhāta, utkhāta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_kharj.html"> √ kharj    √ kharj, “creak” Present I. kharjati S Derivatives khargálā V.+ kharjū́ra B.+ 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_khall.html"> √ khall    √ khall, “be relaxed” Present I. khallate C Verbal Nouns khallita C Derivatives khalla C. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_khaa.html"> √ khā    √ khā See √ khan. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_khaad.html"> √ khād    √ khād, “chew” Present I. khā́dati etc. V.+ Passive khādyate C Future Simple Future: khādiṣyate E.-ti Periphrastic Future: khāditā Aorist RAo: acakhādat -iṣ-Ao: akhādīt Perfect cakhā́da etc. V.+ Causative khādayati etc. E.+ Desiderative cikhādiṣati E.+ Intensive cākhād- Verbal Nouns khāditá B.+; khāditvā B.U Derivatives khādá V.+ khādya E.+ khā́das- RV. cikhādiṣu E.+ khādaka S.+ khādana E.+ khāditavya C. khādin E.+ khādanīya C. khāditṛ C. Meanings khā́dati v (khādate) chew, bite, eat, devour, consume, destroy. Caus. khādayati also = S. pra & sam chew, eat, devour. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_khid.html"> √ khid    √ khid, “tear” Present IV. ? see Ps VI. khidáti etc. V.+ VII. khintte Passive khidyate etc. E.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: khetsyati Periphrastic Future: khettā Aorist RAo: acīkhidat -siṣ-Ao: akhaitsīt Perfect cikheda Causative khedayati -te E.+ Desiderative cikhitsa- Intensive cekhid- Verbal Nouns PPP: khinna E.+; 2Abs: -khídya B.S.;-khídam AV Derivatives -khida B. khidvāṃs RV. khedin C. kheditavya E. khidrá RV. khédā̆ V.+ khedana C. khedayitavya C. Meanings khidáti v PPP khinna (q.v.) depress (fig.); P. khidyate (ti) be depressed, languish, suffer pain. Caus. khedayati, te depress, afflict, vex. ā snatch. ud pull out. ni press down. nis cut off, remove. pari P. = S. P. pra push away. vi tear asunder. sam press together; pull out, snatch away. Cf. parikhinna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_khud.html"> √ khud    √ khud, “to have sexual intercourse” Present VI. khudáti etc. V Intensive canīkhudat S. (kánīkhunat TB.) Derivatives khódana AV. Meanings To sport wantonly or amorously RV. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_khel.html"> √ khel    √ khel, “stagger” Present I. khelati etc. E.+ Causative khelayati etc. C Verbal Nouns PPP: khelita C Derivatives khelá V.+ khelana C. kheli C. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_khyaa.html"> √ khyā    √ khyā, “see” Present II. khyāsi khyāti khyāhi khyāta E.+ Passive khyāyate etc. B.+ (khyāyiṣyate B.) Future Simple Future: khyāsyáti etc. B.+,-te E.+ Periphrastic Future: khyātā Aorist √-Ao: akhyāyi; khyāyāt, khyeyāt Th Ao: ákhyat etc. V.B.S., akhyata etc. V.B -s-Ao: khyeṣam B.S. khyāsīṣṭa Perfect cakhyau cakhyus etc. V.+ Causative khyāpayati -te etc. B.+ (acikhyapat; khyāpyate etc. C.; cikhyāpayiṣa- in d. C.) Desiderative cikhyāsita C Intensive cākhyā- Verbal Nouns PPP: khyātá AV.+; Inf: khyā́tum B.+; 2Abs: -khyā́ya V.+;-khyaí V.B.;-khyā́- yam B Derivatives -khya B.+ -khyātṛ V.+ -khyeya AV.+ khyāpana E.+ -khyā V.+ khyā́na B.+ khyāpaka C. khyāpanīya C. khyāti B.+ -khyāyaka E.+ khyāpin C. -cikhyāsu C. -khyātavya E.+ -khyāyin S.+ khyāpya E. cikhyāpayiṣā C. Meanings (khyāti), PPP khyāta (q.v.) see, appear; P. khyāyate be called or known; Caus. khyāpayati, PPP khyāta (q.v.) see, appear; P. khyāyate be called or known; Caus. khyāpayate make known, proclaim; show, betray; praise, celebrate. ati survey, overlook, neglect, abandon. anu behold, view. antar descry, find out. abhi behold, look at; favour, protect. Caus. make known. ava look down, behold. ā behold, view; count, enumerate; show, declare, announce, tell, narrate; name, designate as (2A). Caus. make known, tell; Ā have told to one's self. pratyā name singly; turn away, repulse, reject, refute, deny, forbid; outvie, excel, sur pass. vyā explain, illustrate; announce, proclaim, tell, call, name. samā enumerate, communicate, declare as (iti). pari look around, behold, consider; overlook, neglect. pra behold, see; announce, tell; P. be visible or known. prati behold, see. vi look about, look at, see, perceive; shine forth, beam; illuminate, make visible, show. Caus. make visible or known, proclaim, tell, confess. abhivi look at, behold. sam appear together with, belong to (I); count together, reckon up, estimate. parisam reckon up completely, enumerate, calculate. Cf. abhikhyāta, abhivikhyāta, prakhyāta, pravikhyāta, vikhyāta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_gach.html"> √ gach    √ gach See √ gam. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_gad.html"> √ gad    √ gad, “say” Present I. gadati etc. S.+ Passive gadyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: gadiṣyate E Periphrastic Future: gaditā Aorist √-Ao: agādi C -iṣ-Ao: agā̆dīt Perfect jagāda jagade etc. E.+ Causative gādayati S Desiderative jigadi- ṣati E Intensive jāgadyate C Verbal Nouns PPP: gadita E.+; Inf: gaditum C.; 2Abs: -gadya S Derivatives gada B.+ gadana B.+ -gādin C. gadgada C. gadya E.+ gadi C. -gādya C. ví gada in AV. ( V. 22. 6) is doubtless a vocative, vígada. Meanings gadati v (gadate), PPP gadita speak, pronounce, recite, tell (A of pers. & th.), enumerate, name, call. ni = S; P. be called, pass as (N). praṇi teach, assert. vini speak to, address (A); P. be called. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_gadh.html"> √ gadh    √ gadh, “attach” ( ?) Verbal Nouns PPP:-gadhita RV2 Derivatives gádhya RV. A root of doubtful meaning and relations. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_gabh.html"> √ gabh    √ gabh See √ gāh. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_gam.html"> √ gam, gach    √ gam, gach, “go” Present I. gácchati etc. V.+,-te etc. V.+. gámanti RV.,-ntu V II. gathá RV1 Passive gamyáte etc. AV.+ Future Simple Future: gamiṣyati etc. AV.+,-te etc. E. (agamiṣyat U.) Periphrastic Future: gaṃtā́ etc. B.+ Aorist √-Ao: ágamam ágan ágman etc. ágata áganmahi agmata etc. V.B.S. (gámat etc. V.B., gamāmahai RV.; gamyā́t etc. V.B.S., gmīya B.; gahi gantu etc. V.B.S.; gmánt V.); agāmi RV., agami C Th Ao: agamat etc. B.+ (gamét etc. V.B.S., gamemahi V.S.) RAo: ajīgamat etc. V.B -s-Ao: agaṃsi agaṃsmahi etc. S.+ (agasmahi etc. V.B.) gaṃsīṣṭa, gasīṣṭa -iṣ-Ao: gamiṣṭam RV., gmiṣīya VS Perfect jagā́ma (jagántha jagamitha) jagmús etc. jagmé etc. V.+ (jaganma RV.; jaganvā́ṇs V.+, jagmivāṇs B.+; jagamyātam etc. RV.; ájagan etc. ajagmiran V.) Causative gamáyati etc. V.+,-te etc. S.+ (gāmaya RV1.) Desiderative jígamiṣati -te etc. B.+, jigāṃsati etc. AV.+,-te etc. S.+ Intensive gánīgam- V.B., jaṅgam- (in d.), jāgam- AV. ? Verbal Nouns PPP: gatá V.+; Inf: gáṃtum B.+,-tave V.B.,-tavaí V.,-tos V.B.; 1Abs: gatvā́ AV.+,-tvā́ya V.B.,-tvī́ RV.; 2Abs: -gátya V.+,-gamya U.S.+; gámadhyai RV.,-dhye TS.;-gámas MS Derivatives gacha C. gamiṣṇú B. -gátvan RV. gamayitṛ B.+ -gama V.+ -gat V. gatvara C. gamayitavya B.C. gamaka C. gáti V.+ -gāmin E.+ jágat V.+ -gamin C. -gaṃtva S. -gāmuka B.+ jágmi RV. gamya U.+ gaṃtavyà B.+ gmā́ RV. jigatnú V. gámana V.+ gáṃtṛ V.+ -gman RV. jañgama U.+ gamanīya E.+ -gatha V.B. jmā́ RV. jaṅgamana C. gámiṣṭha V.S. gatnú AV. jmán V. -jigamiṣu C. jigāṃsu C. -jigamiṣā C. Meanings gácchati gácchate gámati gánti v PPP (– ṃ w. P & pass. mg.) gatá (q.v.) go, move; go or come to, get at, fall into or upon, undergo, incur, reach, acquire (A ~ prati, L, or D); approach sex. (A); move on, wander; keep on (with a PPP); approach mentally, perceive (~ manasā), guess, understand (P. be understood or meant); go away, pass, set out, depart, die. – With the A of an abstrans. often = become or be w. Adj or PPP, as harṣaṃ gacchati he becomes glad, upālambhanaṃ gacchati he is censured (cf. i2). Caus. gamáyati, te cause to go or come, lead or bring towards (A, D, or L); put a person into a condition (2A); grant, impart (G of pers. & A of th.); cause to go away i.e. send forth; pass, spend; overcome; *cause a person (A) through some other (I) to go; make understood, explain; convey the idea of (A), mean, denote. Des jígamiṣati & jígāṃsati wish to go, be going. 1. gánīganti approach, visit. – accha, acchā go to, meet with. ati pass away, pass over (A). adhi get at, meet with, obtain, acquire; commence, undertake, accomplish; approach (sex.), take to wife, marry; find out, invent, discover; perceive, learn, study, read. samadhi come near, get at, obtain, acquire; learn, study, read. anu go after, follow, accompany (also Caus. ); seek, look for; approach, arrive, visit, enter; observe, obey, imitate, answer to; go out, be extinguished, die. samanu go after, follow; penetrate, pervade. antar step between, exclude from (Ab). apa go away, depart, cease, disappear. vyapa the same. api go into, join, approach (sex.); get, obtain. abhi come near, approach, visit; go after, follow; find, meet; approach (sex.); undertake, take to (A), get, acquire; perceive, understand, learn (also Caus. ). ava come down, descend; come to, approach, visit; fall into, incur; get, obtain; undergo, undertake; learn from (Ab), perceive, guess, understand; be of opinion, know; take for, consider as (2A). Caus. bring near, procure; cause to know, make acquainted with, teach (2A or G of pers. & A of th.). ā go near, approach, come to (A or L), come back (~ punar); meet with (I); reach, obtain, get at, undergo, incur; befall, betide. Caus. bring near, convey; procure, ascertain (A), learn from (Ab). Des wish to come to (A). I. approach repeatedly (A). adhyā meet with, encounter, find. anvā go after or along. abhyā come near, approach, visit; fall into, incur. upā & samupā the same. nyā come down to (A). paryā go or come round. pratyā come back, return from (Ab) to (A); return to life, revive, recover. samā come together, associate, meet, encounter (I ~ saha or sārdham); come near, approach, come to (A or L), come back; meet with, find. ud go up, rise, shoot up, grow; come forth, extend, spread. apod, Des apojjigāṃsati wish to withdraw from, to avoid (Ab). abhyud rise, go out to meet (A), extend, spread; agree, consent to (A). pratyud come forth again; go out to meet or to face (A); set out, depart. upa come near, approach, visit; go against, attack; meet, encounter, approach (sex.), undertake; undergo incur; reach, befall, happen. abhyupa come near, go to, join, get at; reach, obtain; admit, consent to (A). samupa come near, go to, undergo, incur. ni settle down, approach (also sex.), get at, incur, undergo. upani & saṃni meet with, encounter. nis go out, depart, proceed from (Ab), appear; go away, disappear; get rid of (Ab); reach, get, fall into (nidrām fall asleep). vinis go out, depart, set off, cease, vanish; get rid of (Ab). parā go away, depart. pari walk about, circumambulate surround, inclose, pervade, spread. pra set out, start, advance, proceed; go to, get at (A). práti go to meet, come back, return. vi go asunder, go away, pass, cease, vanish. Caus. pass, spend (time). sam (mostly Ā) meet, encounter, join, approach (sex.); harmonize, agree; be fit, answer, correspond. Caus. bring together, join with (I); lead to (A), bestow on (L). abhisam & upasam meet with, come (together) to (A). Cf. anugata, antargata, abhyāgata, ā́gata, udgata, upagata, parigata, vigata, saṃgata. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_garj.html"> √ garj    √ garj, “roar” Present I. garjati etc. E.+,-te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: garjiṣyati Periphrastic Future: garjitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: agarjīt Perfect jagarja etc. E.+ Verbal Nouns garjita E.+; garjitvā E.;-garjya C Derivatives garja C. -garjin C. garjana E.+ garji C. Meanings garjati v (garjate) roar, growl, hum, rave, thunder, chatter (of birds); brag, boast. anu roar or rave after. abhi roar at (A), shout. pra begin to roar or thunder. prati roar against, answer with roars, shout at (A); oppose, resist; emulate or vie with (G or I). vi roar, shout. sam shout together (anyónyam). Cf. abhigarjita, udgarjita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_gard.html"> √ gard    √ gard, “exult” (?) Present I. agardat PB Derivatives gárda TS. Perhaps the same with √ gūrd. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_garh.html"> √ garh    √ garh, “chide” Present I. garhate etc. RV.S.E.+,-ti etc. E.+ Passive garhyate etc. C Future Simple Future: garhiṣyate Periphrastic Future: garhitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: agarhiṣṭa Perfect jagarha -he etc. E.+ Causative garhayati -te etc. U.+ Desiderative jigarhiṣa- Intensive jāgarh- Verbal Nouns PPP: garhita S.+; Inf: garhitum E.; 2Abs: -garhya C Derivatives garhā E.+ garhya S. ? + garhaṇa E.+ garhitavya E. garhin E.+ garhaṇīya E. Meanings garhate v (garhati), garhayate (ti), PPP garhita (q.v.) chide, blame, censure, reproach, complain to (D) of (A). *ni (garhate) find fault with (D). vi reproach, blame, abuse, revile. Cf. vigarhita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_gal.html"> √ gal    √ gal, “drop” Present I. galati etc. C Aorist -iṣ-Ao: agālīt Perfect jagāla Causative gālayati etc. C Intensive galgalīti VS., galgalyate C Verbal Nouns PPP: galita E.+ Derivatives galana C. gālana C. Meanings galati v PPP galita (q.v.) drip, drop, fall, vanish, pass away. Caus. gālayati cause to drop, liquify, melt, filter, wring out. ava & ā drop down. pra the same. vi be dissolved or melted, fall down, pass away, perish. pravi stream forth, cease, vanish. (sam come forth, break out, rise.*) Cf. nirgalita, parigalita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_galbh.html"> √ galbh    √ galbh, “dare” Present I. galbhate etc. C Perfect jagalbhe C Derivatives -galbha B.+ With pra, and doubtless in reality a denominative of pragalbhá. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_gaa.html"> √ 1 gā    √ 1 gā, “go” Present I. jígāti etc. V.B II. gāte Passive gīyate Future Simple Future: gāsyate, (adhy-) agīṣyata Periphrastic Future: gātā Aorist √-Ao: ágāt águs etc. V.+ (gāni gātá etc. V.; agan 3p. C.) agāyi RAo: (adhy-) agīṣṭa ágīṣata etc. B.+ agāsta; geṣam -ṣma AV.B.S Perfect jagāyat RV.1, (adhi-) jage etc. E.+ Causative gāpayati , ajīgapat Desiderative jigīṣati etc. SV1.C1. jigāsa- Intensive jegīya- Verbal Nouns gā́tave RV1 Derivatives -gā V.+ gā́tra V.+ -gāya V. gáṅgā ? V.+ -ga V.+ -gāna RV. -gū? B. gātú V.B. -gāman RV. geṣṇa ? U. Meanings jígāti 1 v go, move, come, approach, repair to (A or L); follow, persecute; undergo, incur, obtain. – accha go or come. ati step beyond, cross; surpass, overcome, escape; leave unnoticed, neglect; pass away, perish, die. adhi fall into, obtain; think of, resolve on (A); remember, attend to (G or A); study (mostly Ā), learn from (Ab). anu go after, follow, go along; undergo, incur. antar go between (A); separate, exclude from (Ab). apa go away; keep or cease from (Ab). api enter, mix with (A). abhi come near, approach, get at, obtain. ava go away, be lost; go to, join (A). ā & abhyā come near. approach, get at; befall, visit (A). upā come near, approach, come to (A). paryā turn round (intrans.); carry on, be engaged in (A). ud rise. upa go to, get at (A). nis go out, go away or come forth from (Ab). pari go about, surround, pervade, enter, befall, visit; disregard, avoid. pra come forth, proceed; move towards (A); go away, withdraw from (Ab). apapra go away, cease, desist. vi the same. sam meet; go to (A). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_gaa.html"> √ 2 gā, gai    √ 2 gā, gai “sing” Present I. gāti KB1., gānti M. gāyiṣe (1s.) RV1 IV. gā́yati etc. V.+,-te etc. V.+ Passive gīyáte etc. V.+ (gīyant M.) Future Simple Future: gāsyati etc. B.+ (agāsyat etc. B.U.) Periphrastic Future: gātā Aorist √-Ao: geyāti; agāyi -s-Ao: gāsi (1s.) RV -siṣ-Ao: agāsīt -siṣus etc. V.B.U. (gāsiṣat RV.) Perfect jagān etc. B.+, jage etc. C Causative gāpayati etc. B.+,-te B. ajīgapat; gāyayeyus UB Desiderative jigāsati etc. B Intensive jegīyate etc. E.+ jāgā- Verbal Nouns PPP: gītá V.+; Inf: gātum B.+; 1Abs: gītvā B.+; 2Abs: -gāya AB.,-gī́ya ŚB.C Derivatives -gā V.+ gāyatrá V.+ gātṛ V.+ gīti S.+ -ga AV.+ gāyana S.+ gāthá V.+ gī́tha AV.+ -gāya C. -gā́yas RV. gā́thā V.+ geya B.+ gāyaka E.+ gāyú RV. gāna U.S.+ -geṣṇa AB. -gāyin C. gātavya C. -gāman RV. -jigītha,-ta B.U. -gāpana S. Meanings gā́yati (gā́yate) & gāti v PPP gītá 2 (q.v.) sing, chant, recite, praise, proclaim; P. also be called, have the name of (N). Caus. gāpayati. Int jegīyate (w. P & pass. mg.). – accha call with a song. anu sing after or to (A), praise, celebrate. abhi sing or call to (A), fill or praise with song. ā sing to (A), gain by singing. ud intonate, begin to sing, chant, recite, fill with song. upa sing to or before (D, L, A), praise, celebrate, fill with song. ni accompany with song, sing, proclaim. pra begin to sing; praise, celebrate; sound, resound. abhipra begin to celebrate. vi decry, blame. sam sing together. Cf. anugīta, udgīta, upagīta, vigīta, saṃgīta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_gaah.html"> √ gāh    √ gāh, “plunge” Present I. gā́hate etc. V.+,-ti etc. E Passive gāhyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: gāhiṣyate E.+ Periphrastic Future: gāḍhā, gāhitā Aorist RAo: ajīgahat -s-Ao: agāḍha -iṣ-Ao: agāhiṣṭa Perfect jagāha C. (jigāhīre s1.) Causative gāhayati etc. C Desiderative jigāhiṣa- , jighākṣa- Intensive jáṅgahe V. jāgāh- Verbal Nouns PPP: gāḍha S.+, gāhita E.+; Inf: gāhitum E.; 2Abs: -gāhya S.+ Derivatives -gáha RV. gāhá V.+ gámbhan B. gabhvara C. gáhana RV.E. -gāhin C. gambhára RV. gādhá V.+ gah- ,gaṃhmán B. -gāhya E.+ gámbhiṣtha B. gādhana C. gáhvara AV.+ gāhana S.+ gabhīrá V.+ gāhanīya C. gambhīrá V.+ The connection of these derivatives is probable, but not beyond question. Meanings gā́hate (gā́hati) v PPP gāḍhá (q.v.) dive or enter into (A). ati emerge from, overcome (A). abhi penetrate into (A). ava or va plunge or enter into, be absorbed in (L or A). ud emerge, rise. upa enter. pra penetrate, pervade. vi dive into, bathe in, enter, penetrate (A or L); get, attain (A); w. kakṣām be equal to (G). Cf. avagāḍha, udgāḍha, parigāḍha, pragāḍha, vagāḍha, vigāḍha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_gir.html"> √ gir, gil    √ gir, gil See √ 2 gṛ. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_gu.html"> √ gu    √ gu, “sound” Present I. gavate Future Simple Future: goṣyate Periphrastic Future: gotā; guta Aorist -iṣ-Ao: agoṣṭa Perfect juguve Intensive jóguve jóguvāna V.B Derivatives -gut ? RV. jogū́ RV. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_gu_jj.html"> √ guñj    √ guñj, “hum” Present I. guñjati etc. C Future Simple Future: guñjiṣyati Periphrastic Future: guñjitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aguñjīt Perfect juguñja Verbal Nouns PPP: guñjita C Derivatives guñja C. -guñjin C. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_gu_n_th.html"> √ guṇṭh    √ guṇṭh, “cover up” Causative guṇthayati etc. C. (guṇṭhita E.+,-guṇṭhya S.+) Derivatives guṇṭhana C. Probably a denominative formation. Meanings guṇṭhayati v PPP guṇṭhita veil, conceal, hide, cover. ava , samava, ā & pari = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_gup.html"> √ gup    √ gup, “protect” Present I. gopant ? C1 Passive gupyate etc. B Future Simple Future: gopsyati etc. AV.+ gopiṣyati Periphrastic Future: goptā, gopitā Aorist RAo: ajūgupat etc. B.S. (ajugupa- B.) -s-Ao: agaupsīt -iṣ-Ao: agopīt Perfect jugopa jugupus etc. V.+ Causative gopayati etc. E.+,-te etc. E. (gopyate E.) Desiderative jugupsate etc. B.+,-ti etc. E.+, jugupiṣa- (in d.) jugopiṣa- Intensive jogup- Verbal Nouns PPP: gupitá V., guptá AV.+; Inf: goptum B., gopitum C Derivatives -gup E.+ gopya E.+ goptavya E. jugupsā E.+ -gupya B. gópana AV.+ goptṛ́ AV.+ jugupsu S.+ gúpti AV.+ -gopanīya C. gópiṣṭha B. jugupiṣu E. Perhaps ultimately a denominative from gopā́, but assuming the aspect of a root even in the Veda. Meanings PPP gupitá & guptá 1 (q.v.) keep, protect, guard from (Ab) Des jugupsate (ti) beware of, shun, detest; PPP jugupsita detested, abominable, or *detesting (w. Ab). prati beware of (Ab). vi Des fly from, be afraid of (Ab). Cf. adhigupta, anugupta, abhigupta, saṃgupta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_guph.html"> √ guph, gumph    √ guph, gumph, “twine” Present I. gumphati etc. C Causative gumphayati etc. C Verbal Nouns gumphita , guphita C Derivatives gumpha C. -gumphaka C. gumphana C. Meanings gumphati & gumphayati v PPP gumphita string together, wreathe, wind. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_gur.html"> √ gur    √ gur, “greet” Present VI. guráte etc. V.+,-ti etc. C Future Simple Future: guriṣyate Periphrastic Future: guritā Aorist √-Ao: gūrta RV -iṣ-Ao: aguriṣṭa Perfect jugure jugurat -ryās -ryā́t RV Causative gūraya- (in d.) Intensive járgurāṇa RV Verbal Nouns PPP: gūrtá V.+, gūrṇa S.+; 2Abs: -gū́rya V.+,-gurya C Derivatives -gur B.S. gūraṇa C. -goraṇa C. jugurváṇi RV. -guraṇa C. gūrtí RV. -gūrayitṛ C. Doubtless a secondary form of √ 1 gṛ. Meanings (guráte) v (only – ṃ), PPP gūrtá (q.v.) & gūrṇa (– ṃ) *lift up. apa reject, revile, threaten. ava threaten. ā approve, agree. ud lift up, raise. Cf. udgūrṇa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_gulph.html"> √ gulph    √ gulph, “bunch” Causative gulphayeyus S1., gulphita S Derivatives gulphá AV.+ A very doubtful case. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_guh.html"> √ guh    √ guh, “hide” Present I. gū́hati -te etc. V.+ Passive guhyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: gūhiṣyati -te, ghokṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: gūhitā, goḍhā Aorist √-Ao: agūhi Th Ao: guhas guhant- guhámāna RV RAo: ajūguhat -s-Ao: agūḍha -iṣ-Ao: agūhīt, agūhiṣṭa -sa- Ao: aghukṣat etc. V.B. aghukṣata Perfect jugūha C., juguhe jugūhire E Causative gūhayati etc. S.+ Desiderative jugukṣati RV. jughukṣa- Intensive joguh- Verbal Nouns PPP: gūḍhá V.+; Inf: gūhitum E.+; 1Abs: gūhitvā, gūḍhvā, gūḍhvī́ RV.; 2Abs: -guhya E.+,-gūhya ? E Derivatives gúh RV. gúhya V.+ gūhitavya E. góha V.B.S. guha E.+ -gūha C. -gūhitṛ C. -gohana RV. gúhā V.+ gūhana S.+ -gohya RV.S. Meanings gū́hati gū́hate v PPP gūḍhá 1 (q.v.) hide, cover, keep secret. apa hide, put away. ava cover, conceal; embrace. ud pierce or twist through. upa cover, hide, embrace. ni & vini cover, conceal, keep secret. Cf. upagūḍha, nigūḍha, vigūḍha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_guurd.html"> √ gūrd    √ gūrd, “exult” ( ?) Present I. agūrdan JB Derivatives gūrda B.+ Compare roots √ kūrd, √ gard and √ gūrdh. See J.A.O.S., vol. xi., p. cxlvii. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_guurdh.html"> √ gūrdh    √ gūrdh, “exalt” (?) Causative gūrdhaya RV1 Perhaps the same with the preceding, √ gūrd. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_g_r.html"> √ 1 gṛ    √ 1 gṛ, “sing” MMW calls this root: gṝ. Present VI. (sam-)girate etc. C.,-ti C. gṛṇīṣé (1s.) V IX. gṛṇā́ti gṛṇīté etc. V.+ (gṛṇé 3s. V., gṛṇáta 2p. AV.) Future Simple Future: gariṣyati Periphrastic Future: garī̆tā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: agārīt Precative: gīryāt Perfect jagára TA Derivatives -gara AV.+ -garitṛ B.S. gír V.+ -gīrya B.S. -garaṇa C. -gira C. gṛṇádhyai AA. Compare roots √ gur and √ 2 jṛ. Meanings gṛṇā́ti gṛṇīté 1 v (also w. pass. mg), girate, girati (only w. sam) sing, invoke, call, praise, proclaim, relate. anu join in praising; answer, agree (*D); repeat. abhi chime in with (A); salute praise, approve, accept. ā approve, praise, pratyā answer, respond. upa invoke, call to (A). pra proclaim, extol, celebrate. prati invoke, welcome (A); answer, respond (D); assent, agree (*D). sam chime in, agree, assent, promise, acknowledge, affirm. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_g_r.html"> √ 2 gṛ, gir, gil    √ 2 gṛ, gir, gil, “swallow” Present VI. giráti etc. AV.+,-te etc. E.+ (gírāmi AV1.); gilati etc. B.+ IX. gṛṇā́ti etc. AV.S Passive gīryate etc. E Future Simple Future: gariṣyati B.C. garīṣyati Periphrastic Future: garī̆tā Aorist √-Ao: (or Th Ao) garat -ran V. RAo: ajīgar RV1. ? -s-Ao: agīrṣṭa -iṣ-Ao: gārīt RV Precative: gīryāt Perfect jagāra V.+ Causative girayati C. gārayati Desiderative jigariṣa- Intensive járgurāṇa RV., jalgulas RV. jāgṛjegilya- Verbal Nouns PPP: gīrṇá V.+, gilita C.; Inf: giritum C.; 2Abs: -gī́rya AV.+ Derivatives gará AV.+ -gāra E.+ -gila AV.+ gárgara ? V.+ gala E.+ -gārin E.+ -giraṇa C. -jīgarta? B.+ -garaṇa C. -gir V.B.S. gilana C. jígarti RV. garas ? B.S. -gira AV. -gra,-gri RV. Meanings giráti 2 gírati, girate, gilati (gṛṇā́ti), PPP gīrṇá swallow, devour. ava swallow down. ud spit out, pour out, discharge, eject, burst out with (A). ni swallow down, devour, suppress. nis spit out. sam devour. Cf. udgīrṇa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_3_g_r.html"> √ 3 gṛ, jāgṛ    √ 3 gṛ, jāgṛ, “wake” Aorist RAo: ájīgar RV.; jigṛtám -tá RV Intensive jāgarti jā́grati etc. V.+ (jāgarāsi etc., jāgṛyāt etc., jāgṛhí etc.; jā́grat; ájāgar; jāgā́ra etc. Causative jāgaráyati etc. Simple Future: jāgariṣyáti -te Periphrastic Future: jāgaritá.) Irreg., as √ jāgṛ : Present II. jāgṛmi M. VI. jāgrati, -te etc. S.E., jāgarati M. -iṣ-Ao: jāgarīt, Ao/Ps/3/sg: ajāgāri, Precative: jāgaryāt, Perfect: jajāgāra E.+, jāgarām āsa C. Derivatives jāgara B.+ jāgaraṇá B.+ jāgarū́ka RV.C. jāgṛtavya E. jāgaraka C. jāgariṣṇu C. jāgartavya E. jā́gṛvi V.+ Meanings I. jāgarti 3 (jāgarati, jāgrati) II. jāgarti 3 (jāgarati, jāgrate) be awake, wake up, wake or be watchful, have a care for (D), rule over (L ~ adhi). Caus. jāgaráyati wake (trans.), rouse, excite, animate. pra keep watch, wait for (G), wake (trans.). prati watch near or over (A). Cf. jāgṛvás. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_g_rdh.html"> √ gṛdh    √ gṛdh, “be greedy” Present IV. gṛ́dhyati etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: gardhiṣyati B Periphrastic Future: gardhitā Aorist Th Ao: ágṛdhat etc. V.B.U Perfect jagṛdhus B.C. (jāgṛdhús RV.) Causative gardhayati Desiderative jigardhiṣa- Intensive jarīgṛdh- Verbal Nouns PPP: gṛddha E.+; 1Abs: gṛddhvā C. gṛdhitvā Derivatives gṛ́tsa ? V.B. gṛdhna E. gṛ́dhya AV. gṛ́dhra V.+ gardha C. gṛdhnú V.+ gṛdhyā E. gardhin V.+ gṛdhyin E. Meanings gṛ́dhyati v PPP gṛddha (q.v.) be eager or greedy, speed, hasten, strive after, long or wish for (A or L). anu & prati strive after, covet (L). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_gai.html"> √ gai,    √ gai,“sing” See √ 2 gā. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_grath.html"> √ grath, granth    √ grath, granth, “tie” Present I. granthati, grathati VII. gṛṇatti ? AV IX. grathnā́ti etc. B.+ Passive grathyati C Future Simple Future: granthiṣyati B Periphrastic Future: granthitā Aorist RAo: ajagranthat -iṣ-Ao: agranthīt Precative: grathyāt Perfect jagrantha jagranthus grethus Causative granthayate E., grathayati C Desiderative jigranthiṣa- Intensive jāgranth- , jāgrathya- Verbal Nouns PPP: grathitá V.+; 1Abs: granthitvā, grathitvā; 2Abs: -grathya B.+;-grantham B Derivatives grathín RV. grathana C. grathna S. granthana S.+ grathya C. grathanīya C. grantha B.+ granthí V.+ grathitavya C. granthín RV. Meanings granth grathnā́ti v PPP grathitá tie or string together, arrange, compose, write. ud tie up, fasten, wind; also = Caus. udgrathayati unbind, loosen. vi & sam bind together, connect. Cf. ságrathita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_grabh.html"> √ grabh, grah    √ grabh, grah, “seize” Present I. gṛhṇati etc. E.,-te U. gṛhīthās E.,-ītá MS.C.,-īṣva B., agṛhītām E IX. gṛbhṇā́ti gṛbhṇīté etc. V.B.; gṛhṇā́ti gṛhṇīté etc. (gṛhāṇá) V.+ Passive gṛhyáte etc. AV.+ Future Simple Future: grahīṣyati -te B.+ (agrahīṣyat etc. B.+, agrahaiṣyat B.U.; gṛhīṣyati, grahiṣyati E.) Periphrastic Future: grahītā E Aorist √-Ao: agabham V.B., agṛbhran RV.; grabhat AB., gṛbhāṇá MS. gṛhyāt; agrāhi Th Ao ? gṛhe (3s.) MS., gṛhate (3p.) gṛhāmahi RV RAo: ajigrabhat MS. ajīgṛbham K., ajigrahat C -s-Ao: aghṛkṣata -iṣ-Ao: agrabhīt agrabhīṣus etc. agrabhīṣaṭa etc. V.B. (agrabhīm TS.); agrahīt etc. agrahīṣṭa etc. AV.+ (agrahaiṣam AB.) Perfect jagrā́bha jagṛbhus jagṛbhré etc. V. (jagṛbhma jagṛbhyāt V., jagṛbhriré RV.; ajagrabham etc. V.B.S.U.); jagrā́ha jagṛhus jagṛhe etc. V.+ (jagṛhmá SV.; jagrāhatus M.) Causative gṛbháyant RV.; grāhayati -te B.+ (grāhyate etc. C.) Desiderative jighṛkṣati -te etc. B.+, jigrahīṣa- KB. (ajagrabhaiṣan ? AB.) Intensive jāgrah- , jarīgṛhya- Verbal Nouns PPP: gṛbhītá V.B., gṛhītá AV.+; Inf: gráhītum B.+,-tavai B.,-tos B.; 1Abs: gṛbhītvā́ AV., gṛhītvā́ AV.+; 2Abs: -gṛ́bhya V.,-gṛ́hya V.+;-grábhe RV., gṛbhé RV.,-graham JB.; gṛhaye K.;-grā́ham B.+ Derivatives grábha RV. -grahiṣṇu S. grāhyà V.+ gṛ́bhi V. gráha V.+ grahītavya B.+ grā́hi V. gṛhú RV. -grahin E. grábhītṛ AV.B. grā́huka B. -gṛhīti B.+ gárbha V.+ grahītṛ AV.+ gṛ́bh V.B. jighṛkṣā E.+ grábhaṇa V.S. grābhá V.B.S. -gṛh C. jighṛkṣu E.+ gráhaṇa AV.+ grāha AV.+ gṛbhá RV. grahaṇīya E. grāhaka E.+ gṛhá V.+ -gráhi B.+ grāhin E.+ gṛ́hya AV.+ grāhayitavya C. Compare √ glah. There seems to be no good reason why the root should not be given as gṛbh, gṛh. Meanings grah , gṛbhṇā́ti, gṛbhṇīté, gṛhlā́ti, gṛhlīté v (gṛhlati, gṛbhṇā́ti, gṛbhṇīté, gṛhlā́ti, gṛhlīté gṛhlate), PPP gṛbhītá & gṛhītá (q.v.) grasp, seize, catch; take (in various mgs, e.g.) gather, pluck, collect, take up or draw (a fluid); take away, rob, occupy, buy, chose, marry, esp. w. pāṇiṃ or pāṇau take (by) the hand (A); accept, receive; assume, use, put on or in; undertake, undergo, begin; gain over, win; get, acquire, keep, hold; take into the mouth, mention, name; take in with the mind, perceive, observe, understand, learn; admit, approve, obey, follow; take for, consider as (2A); ger. gṛhya having taken i.e. accompanied by, furnished with, with (A); P. gṛhyate be meant by (I). Caus. grāháyati cause to grasp, seize, take etc. (pāṇiṃ the hand, see above); cause to choose or marry (2A), cause a person (A) to be occupied with (I), make learn, teach (2A). Des jighṛkṣati, te be about to seize or take, strive to perceive or understand. anu follow in taking etc., accept, admit, approve, support, uphold; favour (āsanam the seat = deign to sit down), oblige, make happy, esp. anugṛhīto ’smi I am happy or satisfied = thanks for (I). apa take away, tear off. abhi seize, catch, take hold of, take up, put together, put on, set (a blossom or fruit), accept, receive. ava let loose; stop, keep from (Ab); separate, divide (G); perceive, notice, feel. ā grasp, seize, draw tight (the reins); take in, learn. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_gras.html"> √ gras    √ gras, “devour” Present I. grasati etc. E.+, grásate V.B Passive grasyate etc. E Future Simple Future: grasiṣyati -te etc. E.+ Periphrastic Future: grasitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: agrasīt C Perfect jagrasāná jagrasīta RV Causative grāsayati etc. B.S Desiderative jigrasiṣa- Intensive jāgras- Verbal Nouns PPP: grasitá RV., grasta E.+; 1Abs: grasitvā́ B.;-grāsam C Derivatives grasya E. grásiṣṭa V.B. grasti C. grāsa S.+ grasana C. grasiṣṇu E. grastṛ C. -grāsaka C. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_glap.html"> √ glap    √ glap See √ glā. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_glah.html"> √ glah    √ glah, “gamble” Present I. glahate etc. E Future Simple Future: aglahīṣyat E Periphrastic Future: glahitā, glāḍhā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aglahīṣṭa Perfect jaglahe Derivatives gláha AV.+ gláhā AV. gláhana AV. Doubtless from √ grah. Meanings glahate v play with dice. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_glaa.html"> √ glā    √ glā, “be weary” Present II. glāti E IV. glā́yati etc. AV.+,-te etc. S.E Future Simple Future: glāsyati Periphrastic Future: glātā Aorist √-Ao: glāyāt, gleyāt -s-Ao: glāsīṣṭa -siṣ-Ao: (or -s-Ao: ) glāsīs E Perfect jaglau Causative glāpáyati etc. V.+; glapayati etc. E.+,-te E. ajiglapat (glapet M1.) Desiderative jiglāsa- Intensive jāglā- Verbal Nouns PPP: glāná B.+ (glānta M.) Derivatives -glā? GB. glāvín VS. -glā́pana B. glāni E.+ glāsnu S.+ glapana C. Meanings glā́yati v (glāyate & glāti), PPP glāná (q.v.) be loth, displeased, averse to (L or I); be wearied, exhausted, fade away. Caus. glāpáyati & glapayati; PPP glāpita wearied, faded, withered. pra fade, wither. Cf. pariglāna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_gha_t.html"> √ ghaṭ    √ ghaṭ, “strive” Present I. ghaṭate etc. E.+,-ti E.+ Future Simple Future: ghaṭiṣyate C Periphrastic Future: ghaṭitā Aorist R Ao : ajīghaṭat -iṣ-Ao : aghaṭiṣṭa Perfect jaghaṭe C Causative ghaṭayati etc.(ghaṭyate) E.+,-te C.; ghāṭayati etc. (ghāṭyate) E.+ Desiderative jighaṭiṣa- Intensive jāghaṭīti C Verbal Nouns PPP: ghaṭita C.; Inf: ghaṭitum C Derivatives ghaṭa E.+ ghaṭanā C. ghāṭin C. ghāṭi RV. ghaṭaka C. ghāṭa AV.+ ghāṭana C. ghaṭayitavya C. ghaṭana C. ghāṭaka C. ghāṭanīya E.+ Meanings ghaṭate (ghaṭati) v be eager or busy, work at, exert one's self for, strive after (L, D, or A); be accomplished, come round, succeed, be possible, fit, or suitable; meet, join (I). Caus. ghaṭayati (te), PPP ghaṭita bring together, unite, place upon (L), bring near, procure, cause, effect, produce, make, form. ud open (intrans.); Caus. uḍghāṭayati open (trans.), reveal. pra exert one's self, devote one's self to (L); commence, begin. vi go asunder, burst. Caus. vighaṭayati tear asunder, destroy, annihilate. sam come together, meet. Caus. saṃghaṭayati & saṃghāṭayati assemble, collect. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_gha_t_t.html"> √ ghaṭṭ    √ ghaṭṭ, “rub” Present I. ghaṭṭate Future Simple Future: ghaṭṭiṣyati Periphrastic Future: ghaṭṭitā M Perfect jaghaṭṭire R Causative ghaṭṭayati etc. E.+ (ghaṭṭyate C.) Verbal Nouns PPP: ghaṭṭita E.+ Derivatives ghaṭṭa E.+ -ghaṭṭin C. ghaṭṭana E.+ ghaṭṭitṛ E. Meanings ghaṭṭate v (only – ṃ) & Caus. ghaṭṭayati stroke, touch (also with words = mock), shake, set in motion. ava Caus. touch, stroke, rub; also = ud & upa Caus. stir about. pari Caus. rub or touch on all sides vi Caus. break asunder, burst open, stir about, shake, open. sam rub or crush to pieces, bruise. Caus. cause to rub against (I), stir about, touch, collect, meet. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ghar.html"> √ ghar    √ ghar See √ ghṛ. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ghas.html"> √ ghas    √ ghas, “eat” Present I. ghasati Future Simple Future: ghatsyati Periphrastic Future: ghastā Aorist √-Ao: ághas (2, 3s.) ákṣan etc. V.B.S. (aghat 3s. B.S., ághastām 2d., aghasta 2p. B.; ghásas -sat RV.S.; ghástām Imp. B.), gdha ? RV1 Th Ao: aghasat ? JB RAo: ajīghasat MS Perfect jaghā́sa jakṣus jakṣivā́ṃs etc. V.B. (jakṣīyā́t RV.) Desiderative jíghatsati etc. AV.+ Verbal Nouns -gdha- TS Derivatives kṣú V. ghasmara E.+ ghāsá AV.+ -gdhi B. ghasa AV.+ ghasra C. -ghāsin VS. jighatsā B.+ ghasana C. ghasvara C. -ghāsyá B. jighatsú AV.+ ghasí VS. ghāsí RV. Compare √ 1 jakṣ, which is a reduplicated form of this. The anomalous participle gdha occurs only in agdhā́d, and gdhi in ságdhi. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ghu_t.html"> √ ghuṭ    √ ghuṭ, “turn” (?) Present I. ghuṭati, ghoṭate Future Simple Future: ghoṭisyati, -te Periphrastic Future: ghuṭitā ghoṭitā Aorist Th Ao: aghuṭat -iṣ-Ao: aghoṭiṣṭa Perfect jughoṭa jughuṭe Verbal Nouns PPP: ghuṭita C., ghoṭita E.; 2Abs: -ghuṭya C Derivatives ghoṭa S. No proper root. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ghu_s.html"> √ ghuṣ    √ ghuṣ, “sound” Present I. ghóṣati -te etc. V.+ IV. ghuṣyant C1 Passive ghuṣyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: ghoṣiṣyati Periphrastic Future: ghoṣitā Aorist √-Ao: ghóṣi RV Th Ao: aghuṣat RAo: ajūghuṣat -iṣ-Ao: aghoṣīt Perfect jughoṣa JB Causative ghoṣáyati etc. V.+ (ghoṣyate C.) Desiderative jughuṣiṣa- , jughoṣiṣa- Intensive joghuṣ- Verbal Nouns PPP: ghuṣṭa E.+ ghuṣita; 2Abs: -ghúṣya RV.C Derivatives -ghuṣa AV. ghóṣa V.+ ghoṣaṇa E.+ ghóṣi RV. ghuṣya E. -ghoṣaka C. ghoṣaṇā C. ghoṣṭṛ B. ghoṣín AV.+ ghoṣaṇīya C. One or two RV. forms (including the anomalously accented ghóṣayas) are referred by BR. to a root √ 2 ghuṣ, “crush”; but hardly with sufficient reason. Meanings ghóṣati (ghóṣate) v PPP ghuṣṭa sound, cry, call out, proclaim. Caus. ghoṣáyati cause to sound etc., also = S. ava proclaim aloud, offer. ā listen to; also = Caus. cry aloud, proclaim. ud sound, cry aloud. Caus. proclaim. vi make noise, sound, proclaim. sam sound, fill with noise, proclaim, praise, offer. Cf. uḍghuṣṭa & parisaṃghuṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ghuur_n.html"> √ ghūrṇ    √ ghūrṇ, “waver” Present I. & VI. ghūrṇati -te E.+ Future Simple Future: ghūrṇiṣyati Periphrastic Future: ghūrṇitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aghūrṇīt Perfect jughūrṇa -ṇe E.+ Causative ghūrṇayati etc. (ghūrṇyate) C Verbal Nouns PPP: ghūrṇita E.+ Derivatives ghūrṇa S.+ ghūrṇana C. Meanings ghūrṇati ghūrṇate v PPP ghūrṇita move to and fro, tremble, shake, whirl. Caus. ghūrṇayati cause to move to and fro etc. ava, ā, pari, vi = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_gh_r.html"> √ ghṛ, ghar    √ ghṛ, ghar, “drip” Present I. gharati III. jígharti etc. V.B. (jigarti S1.) Passive ághriyata MS Future Simple Future: ghariṣyhati Periphrastic Future: ghartā Aorist -siṣ-Ao: aghārṣīt Perfect jaghāra Causative ghārayati etc. AV.+ (ghāryate S.) Verbal Nouns PPP: ghṛtá V.+;-ghāram GB Derivatives -ghāra B.S. -ghāraṇa S. gharmá V.+ ghṛṇā́ RV. -ghārin AV. jághri RV. ghṛṇá RV. ghṛ́ṇi V. gharmá etc. are referred to a second root ghṛ, “be hot”; but the two are probably ultimately identical. Meanings jígharti v PPP ghṛtá (q.v.) sprinkle, moisten. vyā Caus. the same. Cf. abhíghṛta, víghṛta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_gh_r_s.html"> √ ghṛṣ    √ ghṛṣ, “rub” Present I. gharṣati etc. E.+,-te etc. E Passive ghṛṣyate etc. C. (-ti etc. E.+ ) Future Simple Future: gharṣiṣyati Periphrastic Future: gharṣitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: agharṣīt Perfect jagharṣa C Causative PPP: gharṣita E Verbal Nouns PPP: ghṛṣṭa E.+; 1Abs: ghṛṣṭvā C.; 2Abs: -ghṛṣya S.+ Derivatives gharṣa E.+ gharṣaṇa E.+ ghṛ́ṣu RV. ghṛ́ṣvi RV. -gharṣin C. -ghṛṣṭi E. -ghṛ́ṣva TA. The relation to this root of the last three derivatives is doubtful. Meanings gharṣati v PPP ghṛṣṭa rub (Ā refl.), polish. crush, pound. Caus. gharṣayati rub, grind. ava rub off. ud the same, rub over, strike against. ni rub into, graze, chafe; try, examine. nis rub against (L) sam grind to pieces, crush, wound; contend, vie with (saha). Cf. vighṛṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ghraa.html"> √ ghrā    √ ghrā, “smell” Present I. jíghrati etc. V.+ ,-te etc. S.E II. ghrāti KB.E III. jíghrati (3p.) AV.MS., jighrāṇa E., jighratī C Passive ghrāyate C Future Simple Future: ghrāsyati Periphrastic Future: ghrārā Aorist √-Ao: aghrāt, ghrāyāt S. -siṣ-Ao: aghrāsīt Ao/Ps/3/sg: aghrāyi Precative: ghreyāt Perfect jaghrau C Causative ghrāpayati etc. B.+ ajighrapat -ghripat Desiderative jighrāsa- Intensive jāghrā- , jeghrīya- Verbal Nouns PPP: ghrātá B.+ ghrāṇa; 1Abs: ghrātvā, jighritvā C.; 2Abs: -ghrāya S.+,-jighrya S.+;-ghrā́yam B.S Derivatives -ghra S. ghrāti B.+ ghrātṛ́ B.+ -jighra AV.+ ghrā́ṇa B.+ ghrātavyà B.+ ghréya E.+ -jighraṇa S.+ -ghrāpaṇa S. Meanings jíghrati (jíghrate & ghrāti) v PPP ghrātá (– ṃ w. P & Ps mg) smell, sniff, kiss, perceive. ava smell, kiss. ā the same, touch, seize. samā & upa smell, touch with the mouth, kiss. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_cak.html"> √ cak    √ cak, “quake” Present I. cakanti C1 Verbal Nouns PPP: cakita C Meanings (cakati) v PPP cakita (q.v.) tremble, shake, be alarmed. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_cakaas.html"> √ cakās    √ cakās, “shine” Present II. cakāsti -sati etc. C. (cakāśat C., cakāśete ? E.) Aorist RAo: acacakāsam, acīcakāsam Perfect cakāsāṃ cakāra Causative cakāsayām āsatus C. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_cak_s.html"> √ cakṣ    √ cakṣ, “see” Present I. cakṣate -ṣante etc. RV.E.+, cakṣati etc. E II. cáṣṭe cákṣate etc. V.+, cakṣi cakṣus RV Passive cakṣyate etc. E.+ Perfect cacakṣé etc. B.+, cacákṣa RV. (acacakṣam RV.) Causative cakṣayati etc. V.B Verbal Nouns Inf: caṣṭum C.; 2Abs: -cákṣya V.+;-cákṣe RV.,-cákṣi V.; cákṣase V Derivatives -cakṣ RV. cákṣya V.B. cakṣáṇi RV. cákṣus V.+ -cakṣā ŚB. cákṣan AV. cákṣas V.B.S. -cakṣin AVP. cákṣaṇa V.+ cákṣu V.U. Meanings cáṣṭe cákṣate (cákṣati) v see, look at, perceive; consider as (2A); appear, become, visible; show, announce, declare, tell, say. anu look after or at; name, term. abhi behold, view, survey; see with favour, address; name, term. ava look down upon (A), behold, perceive. ā look at, inspect; proclaim, announce, relate, tell, speak to (A); signify, mean (A); name, term. pratyā refuse, reject; reply to, answer (A). vyā recite, explain. pari overlook, neglect, despise, condemn; name, term; speak to (A), answer. pra relate, tell; consider as, take for, call, name. saṃpra explain, suppose. prati see, perceive, behold, expect; cause to appear, show. vi appear, shine, see, behold, look at, observe; also = Caus. cause to appear, show, reveal; proclaim, announce, tell. sam view, behold, survey, examine, observe; enumerate, report; call, name, term. Cf. abhicáṣṭe, vicáṣṭe. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ca_jc.html"> √ cañc    √ cañc, “dance” Present I. cañcati C. A late and doubtless derivative root (perhaps from cañcala ?). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ca_t.html"> √ caṭ    √ caṭ, “go” (?) Present I. caṭati etc. C Perfect cacāṭa C Causative cāṭayati etc. C Verbal Nouns PPP: caṭita C Derivatives -cāṭa C.-cāṭana C.-cāṭanīya C. Also a late root, perhaps a form of √ cat; caṭaka E.+, caṭu C., cāṭu C. probably have nothing to do with it. Meanings caṭati v PPP caṭita happen, take place; arrive, get to or into (L). ud go away, disappear. Caus. uccāṭayati drive away, expel. vi break (intrans.). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_cat.html"> √ cat    √ cat, “hide”, ( ?) Present I. cátant RV Future Simple Future: catiṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: catitā Aorist RAo: acīcatam -te TA -iṣ-Ao: acatīt, acatiṣṭa Perfect cacāta cete Causative cātayati -te V.B Verbal Nouns PPP: cattá V Derivatives -cát RV. catín RV.-cā́tana V.-catnuka ? AB. The words cātaka C., catura C., cattra or cāttra C. probably do not belong to this root. Meanings only cátant & cattá hide one's self. Caus. cātáyati, only cátant & cattá hide one's self. Caus. cātáyate scare, drive away. nis , pra , & vi Caus. Ā the same. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_can.html"> √ can    √ can, “be pleased” Aorist -iṣ-Ao: caniṣṭám RV., cániṣṭhat ? RV. Derivatives cánas V.B. cániṣṭha RV. cā́ru V.+ Compare √ kan. The form cániṣṭhat is plainly corrupt. Meanings (only Ao caniṣṭám) delight in, enjoy. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_cand.html"> √ cand    √ cand See √ ścand. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_cam.html"> √ cam    √ cam, “sip” Present I. cā́mati B.+; camanti etc. C V. camnoti Future Simple Future: camiṣyati Periphrastic Future: camitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: acamīt Ao/Ps/3/sg: acāmi Perfect cacāma cemus E Causative cāmayati etc. B.+ (-camayya ŚGS1.) Desiderative cicamiṣa- Intensive cañcam- Verbal Nouns PPP: cāṃta S.+; 2Abs: -cámya B.+ Derivatives camaka ? n. pr. C. camana S.+ camū́ ? V.+ -cāma S.+ camasá V.+ -cāṃti C. Always with prep. ā, except in Nirukta. Meanings cā́mati & camati v sip, drink. ā sip, rinse the mouth, lick up, absorb, cause to disappear. Caus. ācamayati & ācāmayati cause to sip. Cf. ācānta, paryācānta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_car.html"> √ car    √ car, “move” Present I. cárati -te etc. V.+ Passive caryáte etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: cariṣyati etc. B.+,-te B. (acariṣyat M.) Periphrastic Future: caritā Aorist RAo: ácīcarat etc. AV.+ -s-Ao: acārṣam B.S -iṣ-Ao: acārīt etc. V.B.U.S. (cacārīt ? U. ) Perfect cacā́ra (cacartha C.) cerús etc. AV.+, cere C Causative cāráyati -te etc. B.+ (cāryate E.+) Desiderative cicariṣati etc. ŚB.; cicarṣati KB Intensive carcarīti etc. AV.B.; carcūryá- V.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: caritá V.+, cīrṇa U.+; Inf: cáritum B.+,-tave V.,-tavaí B.,-tos B.S., cartum E.+; 1Abs: caritvā́ B.+, cartvā M., cīrtvā M.; 2Abs: -cárya B.+; caráse RV.; carádhyai RV.;-cā́ram B Derivatives cara V.+ -caraṇīya C. carṣaṇí V.+ céru RV. carā́ RV. -caréṇya RV. cāra AV.+ cacará RV. cáraka B.+ caritavya B.+ cāraka E.+ cárcara RV.C. -cárya AV.+ cartavya E. cārin V.+ carācará V.B. -caryā S.+ -caritṛ U. -cāryá B.+ -cārayitavya C. carátha RV. carítra V.+ cāraṇa E.+ -cārayitṛ C. cáraṇa V.+ cariṣṇú B.+ cāraṇīya C. cicariṣu B. caráṇi RV. -cárṣaṇa? RV. -cāruka B. Compare √ cal. Meanings cárati (cárate) v PPP caritá (q.v.) & cīrṇa move, go, drive (w. I), walk, roam, wander through or along (A), pervade, explore (only PPP carita); behave, conduct one's self, act or deal with (I or L), be engaged or busy with (I), have sexual intercourse with (I); continue doing or being (PPP, Adj, ger., or Adv); exercise, perform, produce, cause, effect, do, make, render (2A); consume, eat, feed, pasture. – Caus. cāráyati cause to move, walk, roam, eat, pasture, approach sexually, set in motion, impel; cause to do (2A). Des cicariṣati or cicarṣati try to go, be willing to approach sex. (I). Int carcarīti or carcūryáte (w. P & Ps mg) move quickly or repeatedly, wander, roam (A or L). áccha move towards (A). ati escape, go past (A), transgress, also = seq. vyati commit offence against (A). adhi move on or over. anu move along or through, follow; move towards, strive after, endeavour to, keep or take to, behave, conduct one's self. Caus. cause to be pervaded or explored by (I). antar move between or within, be inside (A, L, or G). apa depart, also = seq. abhi act wrongly towards (A). vyabhi the same; Ā bewitch, practise sorcery. ava descend. ā come near, approach, enter, visit; use, employ, treat (like – vat), apply to (A); behave, conduct one's self; deal with, have intercourse with (I ~ saha), undertake, practise, perform, accomplish, effect, do, make. samā proceed, deal or converse with (I), perform etc. = prec. ud rise (l. & f.); emit, esp. the excrement, also = Caus. uccārayati utter, pronounce. abhyud rise over (A). prod cause to sound. vyud go forth in different directions; be unfaithful to (A), commit adultery with (I); perform, accomplish. upa come near, approach, wait on (A), attend, treat with (I), undertake, begin. nis & vinis go or come forth. parā go away, depart. pari walk about, circumambulate; wait upon, serve. Caus. be attended by (I). pra come forth, appear, succeed, thrive; go towards, arrive at, reach, visit; proceed, undertake, begin; be active or busy with (loc); perform, do. saṃpra begin to move, go on, take place, happen. vi go asunder, open, spread, be diffused; fall on, attack; walk about, roam, wander, go through, pervade; have intercourse with (I); go astray, fail, sin; practise, fulfil, do. Caus. cause to roam or go astray, corrupt, seduce; move to and fro (in the mind) i.e. deliberate, consider, reflect, ponder, examine, ascertain, state. pravi advance, proceed, go about, roam. sam come together, meet, approach, arrive, appear, reach to (ā); spread through, pervade; stay, remain; exercise, fulfil. Caus. make to meet, bring into contact, set in motion, cause to go. anusam go after or along, spread through, penetrate, also = seq. abhisam go towards, seek for. Cf. ācarita, ācaritavya, vicārita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_carc.html"> √ carc    √ carc, “repeat” Causative carcayati C., carcita E.+ Derivatives carcā C. carcaka C.-carci S. carcana C.-carcī C. Probably in reality a denominative of carcā, and this a frequentative formation, perhaps from √ car. Meanings Caus. carcayati, PPP carcita (q.v.) repeat, esp. by inserting iti. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_carv.html"> √ carv    √ carv, “chew” Present IV. carvati etc Passive carvyate etc. C Causative carvayati etc. C Verbal Nouns PPP: carvita C., cūrṇa S.+; Inf: carvitum C Derivatives carvya C. carvaṇa C. carvaṇā C. cūrṇi C. Meanings Caus. carvayati, PPP carvita chew, munch, sip, suck. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_cal.html"> √ cal    √ cal, “stir” Present I. calati etc. AV.+,-te etc. E Future Simple Future: caliṣyati E.+ Periphrastic Future: calitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: acālīt. Precative: calyāsam Perfect cacāla celus etc. E.+ Causative calayati etc. C.; cālayati S.+,-te R. (cālyate E.,-ti M.) Desiderative cicaliṣa- (in d.) Intensive calcalīti MS., cācalat AV Verbal Nouns PPP: calita E.+ ; Inf: calitum E.+ Derivatives cala E.+ -calī AV.+ -cālin C. -cācali RV. -calaka C. -calū B.S. cālya E.+ cañcala E.+ -calāka B.+ calitavya E. cālana E.+ calācalá V.E. calana E.+ cāla C. -cācala AV. cicaliṣu C. A later variation of √ car. Meanings calati (calate) v PPP calita (q.v.) get into motion, stir, budge; tremble, quiver, totter; set out, start, depart, pass away; walk, march; spread, be diffused; be troubled or disappointed; swerve, deviate, fall off from (Ab). Caus. calayati or cālayati set in motion, shake, push, disturb, agitate; expel or turn off from (Ab). ā , Caus. ācālayati set in motion, stir. ud get off from, leave (Ab); also = prod set out, depart. samud start up or set out together. pari Caus. move, stir, turn round. pra get in motion, shake, tremble; come forth, rise, start up; swerve or deviate from (Ab); proceed, advance, depart; be perplexed or troubled. Caus. set in motion, shake, stir. vi move to and fro, waver, totter, set out, start, fall off or down, depart, swerve or deviate from (Ab); be perplexed or disappointed. Caus. vicālayati set in motion, excite, turn from (Ab), shake, destroy. pravi get in motion, shake, tremble, swerve, deviate, leave from (Ab). sam move, shake, tremble, proceed, advance, start or set off from (Ab). Caus. saṃcālayati set in motion, cause to tremble, remove, push away from (Ab). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_caay.html"> √ cāy    √ cāy, “note, observe” Present I. cā́yati etc. B., cā́yamāna RV Passive cāyyate TS Future Simple Future: cāyiṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: cāyitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: acāyiṣam AV. acāyiṣṭa Perfect cikyus AA. cacāya -ye. -cāyāṃ cakrus JB Verbal Nouns PPP: citá B.; 1Abs: cāyitvā́ AV.;-cā́yya V.B.U Derivatives cāyanīya C. cāyitṛ C. cāyú RV.-citi B. A form, but an early specialized one, of √ 2 ci. The meanings “reverence, be in awe” are rare and secondary. Meanings cā́yati cā́yate v fear, worship, revere; notice, observe, discern. apa fear, revere. ni only ger. nicā́yya worship, observe, perceive. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_ci.html"> √ 1 ci    √ 1 ci, “gather” Present I. cayat cáyema RV II. ceti RV V. cinóti cinuté etc. V.+ cinvati (3s.) C Passive cīyáte etc. B.+ (-cīyant M.) Future Simple Future: ceṣyáti -te etc. B.+ Periphrastic Future: cetā etc. E Aorist √-Ao: acet citana ciyántu RV. ciyāt -s-Ao: acaiṣam etc. B. aceṣṭa -iṣ-Ao: cayiṣṭam RV Perfect cikā́ya etc. cikye -yire etc. V.+ cicāya cicetha, cicye Causative cāyayate C. cāpayati Desiderative cikīṣate etc. B.+; cicīṣati C Intensive ceci- Verbal Nouns PPP: citá V.+; Inf: cetum B.+,-tavai B.; 1Abs: citvā́ B.+, cayitvā E.; 2Abs: -cítya C.,-cīya M Derivatives kāya VS. ? E.+ -cayiṣṭha RV. cít B. cītí AV. caya S.+ -cāya B. cítya AV.B. cetavyà B. cáyana AV.+ -cāyin E.+ -cityā B.+ -cetṛ B. cayanīya C. -cāyyà B. cíti B.+ ceya S.E.+ cayitavyà MS. -cicīṣā C. See √ 2 ci. Meanings cinóṇi cinuté (ceti, cáyati, cinvati) v PPP citá 1 (q.v.) heap up, pile up, arrange, construct, build (esp. the sacrific. altar); collect, gather; cover, inlay, set with (I); P. cīyate increase, thrive, abound. Caus. cayayati & capayati, cāyayati & cāpayati. adhi heap or build upon (L). apa gather, collect; P. decrease, wane, get rid of (Ab). ava gather, pick off (*2A), take off (a garment). ā & samā collect, accumulate; lad, cover, furnish with (I). ud gather, collect, pick off. samud = prec., also connect, add. upa connect, join; heap up, accumlate, augment, strengthen, cover, furnish with (I); P. increase, grow, get strong. samupa heap up, collect; P. increase, grow. pari pile up, accumulate; P. increase, grow. pra gather, collect, accumulate, augment, strengthen; P. increase, become strong. vi pick out, select, segregate, sever, disperse, distribute. saṃvi select. sam pile up, arrange, prepare, gather, accumulate. Cf. apacita, ā́cita, upacita, nicita 1, paricita 1, pracita, samupacita, sácita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_ci.html"> √ 2 ci    √ 2 ci, “note, observe” Present I. cayate etc. V.B III. cikéṣi etc. V.B. (cikīhi AV., ciketu TS., cikéthe RV., cikitām AV., cíkyat V., acikayus B.) V. cinoti cinute E.+ Passive cīyate etc. C Future Simple Future: ceṣyati E Aorist √-Ao: ácet ácidhvam RV -s-Ao: aceṣṭa C Perfect cikāya etc. V.+ Desiderative cikīṣati -te etc. V.B.S Verbal Nouns PPP: citá V.+; Inf: cetum E.+; 2Abs: -citya E.+ Derivatives -caya V.+ -cāyin E.+ -cetavya E.+ -ceya E. -cayana C. -cít RV. cetṛ́ V.B. -cira RV. cāyaka C. citi B.+ Compare √ cāy, which appears to be an early specialized form of this root; cay ( BR. 3 ci) is another. The forms and derivatives of √ 2 ci are not everywhere well separable from those of √ 1 ci, and there is reason to suspect the two roots of being ultimately one; words with the prefixes nis and vi, specially, are probably best referred to √ 1 ci, with the meaning “take apart”, and so “resolve, decide”. Meanings cikéti , cinoti, cinute (cayate) observe, perceive, notice, seek for, search. anu remember. apa respect, honour. ni notice, observe. nis & vinis examine, consider, fix upon. pari search, examine, find out, discover. P. get acquainted. vi discern, distinguish, make clear, illustrate, examine, try, look for, strive after. pravi examine, try. sam deliberate, ponder. Cf. ápacita, abhiniścita, nicitá 2, niṃścita, paricita 2, viniścita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_cit.html"> √ cit    √ cit, “perceive, know, appear” Present I. cétati etc. cétante RV Future Simple Future: cetiṣyati Periphrastic Future: cetitā Aorist √-Ao: áceti céti RV., cité ? RV., citántī ? RV., cítāna V.B. (-cetāna RV.) RAo: acīcitat -s-Ao: acait RV -iṣ-Ao: acetīt Perfect cikéta cikitus etc. cikité -tré etc. V.B.S. (cíketa; cíketati etc. cíketat etc.; cikiddhi; aciket, acikitat, cikitas; cikitrire) ciceta Causative citáyati etc.-te etc. RV.; cetáyati etc. -te etc. V.+ Desiderative cíkitsati etc. V.+,-te E.+ (acikitsīs AV., cikitsyate etc. E.+ ) Intensive cékite etc.-tat RV.C Verbal Nouns PPP: cittá V.+; cité ? RV.; citáye VS. acíte RV Derivatives kéta V.+ cétya RV. cetyā́ RV. cikitsā B.+ ketana E.+ cétana V.+ cikít RV. cikitsaka B.+ ketú V.+ cetanā E.+ cíkiti SV. cikitsya E.+ cít V.+ cétas V.+ cikitú V. cikitsana E.+ citi C. cétiṣṭha V.B. cikitván RV. -cikitsanīya C. cítti V.+ cetú RV. cikitvít RV. cikitsú AV.+ cittí RV. -cetúna RV. -ciketas U. cetayitavya U.+ citrá V.+ céttṛ V.B. cikita S. cetayitṛ B.+ Compare roots √ 2 ci and √ cint. The grammarians give two separate roots, kit and cit, each with full sets of forms- which are not all reported here. Meanings cétati cétate v PPP cittá 1 (q.v.) perceive, observe, attend to (G or A), aim at, intend (D), strive after, desire (A), take care of (A); conceive, understand, know; intrans. appear, be conspicuous or known. Caus. cetáyati, te & citáyati make attentive, remind, instruct, teach; notice, put to mind, attend to; Ā (P) be conscious or sensible, think, reflect, conceive, understand, remember; appear, be conspicuous, shine. Des cikitsati (te) intend, aim at, care for; treat medically, heal. Int cékite appear, shine. ā attend to, call to mind, understand, know, find out, invent; intrans. appear, shine, excel. pra become visible, appear, also = Caus. perceive, understand, announce, proclaim. vi observe, discern conceive, know (also Caus. ); Ā be perceptible, appear. Des wish to discern, deliberate, doubt, hesitate. sam perceive (together), survey, notice; be unanimous, agree. Cf. cikitváṃs, cékitāna, vícitta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_cint.html"> √ cint    √ cint, “think” Causative cintayati etc. -te etc. B.+ acicintat cintyate etc. U.+ ; cintayita C. Derivatives cintā E.+ -cintin C. cintana E.+ -cintitṛ E. cintaka E.+ cintya U.+ cintanīya C. cintayitavya C. Perhaps the denominative of a nasalized derivative of √ cit. Meanings cintayati cintayate v PPP cintita (q.v.) think, reflect, consider, find out, invent; think of, care for (A, D, L, or ~ prati); w. neg. not care for, not mind. anu meditate, consider, call to mind. samanu & abhi consider, ponder upon (A). pari meditate, ponder, think of, find out. pra reflect, consider; invent. vi discern, observe, meditate, think of (A) or to (Inf), consider, regard, imagine, invent. sam think, meditate, consider. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_cud.html"> √ cud    √ cud, “impel” Present I. códati -te etc. V Aorist RAo: acūcudat E -iṣ-Ao: codīs RV Causative codáyati etc.-te etc. V.+ (codyate etc. S.+) Verbal Nouns PPP: cudita M Derivatives codá RV.C. -codin C. codanā S.+ códiṣṭha RV. códa RV. codya E.+ codanīya B. codayitavya C. codaka S.+ códana V.+ -codas RV. codayitṛ́ RV.C. coditṛ́ RV. Meanings códati códate v impel, incite, urge; Ā hasten, speed. Caus. codáyati (te) = S. + animate, accelerate, press; inspire, excite; turn, cast, direct; start (trans.), further, help on, bring or offer quickly; settle, fix. abhi Caus. incite, encourage, summon, invite, request, command; ask, inquire for (A). pari Caus. set in motion, impel, summon, request. pra push on, impel. Caus. the same + animate, inspire, inflame, summon, urge, request, command, etc. (v. abhi). sam Caus. set in motion, impel, excite, inflame, summon, request, solicit; speed, procure quickly. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_cup.html"> √ cup    √ cup, “stir” Present I. copati M1 Future Simple Future: copiṣyati Periphrastic Future: copitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: acopīt Perfect cucopa Verbal Nouns PPP: cupita C Derivatives -cumpuna ? V.B. Meanings copati v stir, move (intrans.). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_cumb.html"> √ cumb    √ cumb, “kiss” Present I. cumbati etc. E.+,-te C Passive cumbyate etc. C Future Simple Future: cumbiṣyati Periphrastic Future: cumbitā Aorist etc -iṣ-Ao: acumbīt Perfect cucumba etc. E.+ Causative cumbayitum C Desiderative cucumbiṣati C Verbal Nouns PPP: cumbita C.; Inf: cumbitum C.; 2Abs: -cumbya C Derivatives cumbā C. cumbaka C. cumbin C. cumbana C. Meanings cumbati cumbate v kiss, touch; Caus. cumbayati. vyati touch closely. pari = S. vi kiss. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_cur.html"> √ cur    √ cur, “steal” Aorist RAo: acūcurat C Causative corayati etc. E.+-te E.+ (coryate C.) Derivatives corá TA.+ coraka C. corayitavya C. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_culump.html"> √ culump    √ culump, “suck in” A single occurrence of a form from this bastard root, with ud, is referred to in Böhtlingk's Lexicon, as found in the Mahāvīracarita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_cuu_s.html"> √ cūṣ    √ cūṣ, “draw, suck” Present IV. cūṣati Passive cūṣyate C Future Simple Future: cūṣiṣyati Periphrastic Future: cūṣitā Aorist RAo: acucūṣat -iṣ-Ao: acūṣīt Perfect cucūṣa Causative cūṣayati C Derivatives cūṣin C. cūṣaṇa C. coṣa C. coṣaṇa C. cūṣya E.+ coṣya E.+ 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_c_rt.html"> √ cṛt    √ cṛt, “bind” Present I. cartati VI. cṛtáti etc. V.B.S Passive cṛtyáte B Future Simple Future: cartiṣyati, cartsyati Periphrastic Future: cartitā Aorist etc RAo: acīcṛtat, acacartat -iṣ-Ao: acartīt Perfect cacarta AV Causative cartayati Desiderative cicartiṣa- , cicṛtsa- Intensive carīcṛt- Verbal Nouns PPP: cṛttá V.S.; 2Abs: -cṛtya B.S.;-cṛ́tam AV Derivatives -cartya B.-cartana B.-cṛt V.+-cṛtya B. Meanings cṛtáti v PPP cṛttá (only – ṃ) w. ati fasten connect, attach. ava let loose. ā & upa fasten, tie, affix. ni insert. nis loosen, untie. pari wind round, tie together. vi untie, loosen, open, spread out. sam be joined to (I). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ce_s_t.html"> √ ceṣṭ    √ ceṣṭ, “stir” Present I. céṣṭati etc. AV.+,-te etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: ceṣṭiṣyati Periphrastic Future: ceṣṭitā Aorist RAo: aciceṣṭat acaceṣṭat -iṣ-Ao: aceṣṭīt Perfect ciceṣṭa etc. E Causative ceṣṭayati etc. B.+,-te etc. S.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: ceṣṭita E.+; Inf: ceṣṭitum E.+; 1Abs: ceṣṭtitvā́ B Derivatives -ciṣṭu? B. (á-) ceṣṭa C. ceṣṭana E.+ ceṣṭayitṛ E. ceṣṭā S.+ ceṣṭitavya E. Meanings céṣṭati céṣṭate v PPP ceṣṭita (q.v.) move the limbs, stir, exert one's self, be active or busy, be engaged in (A); act or behave towards (L); make, do, perform. Caus. ceṣṭayati, te set in motion, impel. ā make, perform. pari wallow, roam about. vi move the limbs, writhe, struggle, stir, be active or busy, act or behave towards (L), effect, produce. sam be restless, exert one's self, P Cf. viceṣṭita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_cyu.html"> √ cyu    √ cyu, “move, stir” Present I. cyávate etc. V.+,-ti etc. RV. ? E.+ Future Simple Future: cyoṣyate B Periphrastic Future: cyotā Aorist √-Ao: cyávāna ? RV RAo: acucyavat -van -vus V.B. (-vīt -vītana cucyavat -vīrata cucyuvīmáhi RV.) acicyavat -s-Ao: acyoṣṭa etc. V.B.U Perfect cucyuvé RV. (cicyuṣé RV.) Causative cyāváyati etc. V.+,-te etc. V.+ cicyāvayiṣa-, cucyāvayiṣa-; cyavayati PB1 Desiderative cucyūṣa- Intensive cocyu- Verbal Nouns PPP: cyutá V.+; Inf: cyavitum E., cyótos ŚB Derivatives -cyava V.+ -cyavīyas RV. -cyāvuka B. cyautná RV. cyávana V.+ cyāva E. -cyut V.+ cyāvayiṣṇú AV. -cyávas RV. cyāvana E.+ cyuti V.+ cyāvayitavya B. The RV. forms here grouped under the reduplicated aorist are of difficult and doubtful classification. Meanings cyávate (cyávati) v PPP cyutá move, stir, waver, shake; go away, escape, fall, flow, retire from, get rid or be deprived of (Ab), sink (l. & f.), decrease, wane, vanish. Caus. cyāváyati (cyavayati) set in motion, shake, agitate (Ā intrans.); cause to fall or drop, pour out, loosen; remove or expel from (Ab), deprive of (2A). ā Caus. cause to flow over, pour out. ud Caus. draw out, extrP pari get loose; fall, descend, swerve or part from, get rid of (Ab), sink down, decline. pra start, proceed; get off, flow out, pour down, descend, part from, get rid or be deprived of (Ab). Caus. move, shake, drive away, expel, drop down, divert from (Ab), cause to fall, ruin. anupra rush atter, follow (A). vi go or fall asunder; go away, fall off, part from (Ab) fail, be lost. Cf. pracyótos. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_cyut.html"> √ cyut    √ cyut, “drip” Present I. cyotati etc. S.C Future Simple Future: cyotiṣyati Periphrastic Future: cyotitā Aorist Th Ao: acyutat RAo: acucyutat -iṣ-Ao: acyotīt Perfect cucyota Causative cyotayati C Desiderative cucyotiṣa- , cucyutiṣa- Intensive cocyut- Only a blundering varia lectio for √ ścut, which see. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_chad.html"> √ chad    √ chad, “cover” Present I. chadati -te Causative chādáyati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ (chādyate etc. S.+ cichādayiṣa-.) Verbal Nouns PPP: channa B.+ Derivatives -chad V.+ chadi B.+ chala ? E.+ chādya C. chada S.+ chadís V.+ -chāda B.+ chādana S.+ -chadin C. chattra S.+ -chādaka C. chadana E.+ chadman S.+ -chādin C. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_chand.html"> √ chand, chad    √ chand, chad, “seem, please” Present I. chandati B.E II. chantsi -ntti RV Aorist RAo: acachadat C -s-Ao: achān -ntta -ntsus RV. (chantsat RV.) Perfect cachanda RV. (cachadyāt RV.) Causative chadáyati etc. V.B.; chandayati etc. B.+,-te etc. RV. (chandyate etc. E.+) Derivatives -chad RV. chandá RV. chándya RV. chándas V.+ chánda V.+ chandaka E.+ chandana C. chándu RV. Of very questionable relationship to √ chad “cover”, although the two are not separated by the Hindu grammarians. Meanings & chand chantti chandati chadáyati (chadáyate) 2 v seem, appear, pass for (N), please; Ā like, be pleased with (A or L). Caus. chandayati offer (w. A of pers. & I of th.); allure, strive to corrupt. upa Caus. = S. Caus. sam offer (= S. Caus. ). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_chaa.html"> √ chā    √ chā, “cut up” Present chyati etc. AV.B. chāyáti ? TB. chayet C Future Simple Future: chāsyati Periphrastic Future: chātā Aorist √-Ao: achāt -iṣ-Ao: achāsīt Perfect cachau Causative chāyayati B.U Desiderative cichāsa- Intensive cāchā- , cāchi- Verbal Nouns PPP: chāta S., chitá ŚB.C.; 1Abs: chayitvā C.; 2Abs: -chā́ya ŚB Derivatives chavī́-vi ? B.+ -chāna C. Meanings chāti v PPP chita (only – ṃ) & chāta (q.v.) cut off. ava flay, skin. ā the same, cut off. pra bleed, scarify. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_chid.html"> √ chid    √ chid, “cut off” Present VII. chinátti chindánti etc. V.+ ( chindeta C.; achinam M.) Passive chidyáte etc. V.+ (chidyati etc. E.) Future Simple Future: chetsyati -te etc. B.+ (achetsyat M.) Periphrastic Future: chettā Aorist √-Ao: chedma RV.; chidyāt; áchedi V.B.S Th Ao: achidat etc. AV.+ RAo: acichidas E -s-Ao: achaitsīt etc. B.+ (chetsīt etc. B.+), chitsi etc. AV.+ (chetsi etc. B.U.) Perfect cicheda cichide etc. B.+ Causative chedayati etc. S.+ Desiderative cichitsati -te JB Intensive cechid- Verbal Nouns PPP: chinná V.+; Inf: chettum B.+,-ttavaí B.S.; 1Abs: chittvā́ B.+; 2Abs: -chídya AV.+ Derivatives -chid V.+ -chitti B.+ -chedaka C. chedanīya C. chidā C. chidrá V.+ -chedin E.+ chettavya E.+ chidura C. cheda AV.+ chedya E.+ chettṛ B.+ chedana B.+ cichitsu E. Meanings chinátti chinte 1 v (chindati), PPP chinná (q.v.) cut, hew or tear off, chop, rend, split, pierce, separate, divide, interrupt, disturb, destroy. Caus. chedayati cause to cut etc., also = S. antar cut off, intercept. ava reject; P. be severed from (Ab). vyava cut off, split, sever from (Ab), interrupt. ā the same; take away, rob, remove, destroy; disregard, neglect. P. ud cut out or off, destroy, interrupt, impede, disturb; P. cease, fail. samud tear out, exterminate. pari cut on both sides, clip round, mow; limit on all sides, fix accurately, define, decide. pra tear, cut or hew off, split, pierce, snatch away, rob. vi tear or break asunder, separate, divide, disturb, interrupt, destroy, sam cut or hew off, split, pierce, destroy (a doubt), decide (a question). Cf. avacchinna, ucchinna, vicchinna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_chu_t.html"> √ chuṭ, chuḍ    √ chuṭ, chuḍ, “wrench” Causative choḍayati etc. C., choṭita C Derivatives choṭikā C. choṭana C. All very late and questionable forms. Meanings Caus. prachoḍayati stretch out. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_chur.html"> √ chur    √ chur, “scatter” Present churati etc Aorist -iṣ-Ao: achorīt etc Perfect cuchora etc Causative churayati etc. C., churita E.+; chorayati etc C Derivatives -churaṇa C. Meanings churayati v (chorayati), PPP churita bestrew, beset, inlay. ā PPP clothed. vi PPP = S. PPP 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ch_rd.html"> √ chṛd    √ chṛd, “spue, eject” Present I. chardati VII. chṛṇatti etc. B. chṛntte Future Simple Future: chardiṣyati -te, chartsyati -te Periphrastic Future: charditā Aorist √-Ao: achṛdat RAo: acachardat acichṛdat -iṣ-Ao: achārdīt achṛtta Perfect cacharda C.-de Causative chardayati -te etc. B.+ cichardayiṣa- Desiderative cichardiṣa- , cichṛtsa- Intensive carīchṛd- Verbal Nouns PPP: chṛṇṇá B. 1Abs: charditvā, chṛttvā Derivatives chardana S.+ chardi S.+ chardis C. chardayitavya C. chardanīya C. Meanings chṛṇatti v PPP chṛṇá pour out or upon, eject, spue, vomit. Caus. chardayati the same, make overflow. ā pour upon, fill. pra Caus. vomit, eject. vi Caus. cast off, abandon. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_jak_s.html"> √ 1 jakṣ    √ 1 jakṣ, “eat” Present I. jakṣati etc. U.C II. jakṣiti jagdhi C., ajakṣus KB., jakṣat (pp) U.C Future Simple Future: jakṣiṣyati Periphrastic Future: jakṣitā Aorist RAo: ajajakṣat -iṣ-Ao: ajakṣīt Perfect jajakṣa Causative jakṣaya- Desiderative jijakṣiṣa- Intensive jājakṣ- Verbal Nouns jagdhá V.+; jagdhum C.; jagdhvā́ AV.+, jagdhvā́ya RV Derivatives jágdhi B.+ A reduplicated form of √ ghas. The present forms found later only in the Bhāgavata-Purāṇa. Meanings jakṣiti 1 v (jakṣati), PPP jagdhá (q.v.) eat, consume. pra & vi = S. PPP 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_jak_s.html"> √ 2 jakṣ    √ 2 jakṣ, “laugh” Present II. jákṣat (pp) RV.ŚB A reduplicated form of √ has. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_jagh.html"> √ jagh    √ jagh, “eat, devour” Present V. jaghnuyāt ? C Found only in Vasiṣṭha (i.23); but Bühler appears to read jahnuyāt; he renders it “offend”. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_jan.html"> √ jan, jā    √ jan, jā, “give birth, be born” Present I. jánati -te etc. V.B II. já- niṣva RV.B III. jajanti IV. jā́yate etc. V.+,-ti etc. E.+ Passive janyate Future Simple Future: janiṣyati -te etc. V.+ (ajaniṣyata etc. B.), jāsyati etc. E Periphrastic Future: janitā́ B.+ Aorist √-Ao: ajan (3s.) S., ajñata (3p.) B.; ájani jáni V.B., jā́ni RV.; jājāt E.+ RAo: ájījanat -nata etc. V.+ -iṣ-Ao: ájaniṣṭa etc. V.+, jániṣṭām RV. (janiṣīya -ṣīṣṭa -ṣīmahi V.B.S.; janiṣeyam -ya K.; jániṣṭhat ? SV.) Perfect jajā́na jajñús etc. jajñé etc. V.+ (jajanús RV., jajánat B.) Causative janáyati -te etc. V.+ (jijanayiṣet ŚB.) Desiderative jíjaniṣate ŚB Intensive jañjan- , jājā- Verbal Nouns PPP: jātá V.+; jánitos V.B.S.; janitvī́ RV Derivatives gnā́ V.B.S. jánī̆ V.+ janitṛ V.+ jénya RV. -jana C. -janu,-nū́ AV.B. janítra V.+ jā́nuka B. jána V.+ janús V.B. jánman V.+ jájñi B. janaka E. jantú V.+ jániman V. jánayati B.S. jánya V.+ jántva RV. jániṣṭha ? V.B. janayitavya C. jánana V.+ jánitva V. -janiṣṇu B. janayitṛ B.+ jánas V.+ janitavyà AV. janiṣya E. janayiṣṇu E. -jijanayiṣitavyà ŚB. jā́ V.+ jā́tu ? V.+ jā́ni V.+ jāyā́ V.+ -ja V.+ jātū́ RV. -jā́man V. -jāyin E.+ jāti B.+ jātṛ AV. ? jāmā E. -jā́van RV. jā́na V.B.U. jāmí V.+ -jāvara B. Meanings jā́yate (jā́yati) v older jánati, jā́yate (ti), older jánate, PPP jātá (q.v.) be born or produced, grow, be born again, be by birth or nature, be destined for (A), become (N or *D); be, take place, happen, be possible or suitable; generate, beget with (L), bring forth, produce, cause, effect. The older Pr stem & Caus. janáyati, te have only the trans. mgs. adhi be born, become, be. anu be born later or after (A); take after, resemble (A). abhi be born or destined to (A), be born, become (N). ā be born. Caus. beget; cause to be born for (D), make prolific. ud beget, produce; be born, arise. upa be produced in addition, be born (again), appear, arise. Caus. procreate, cause, effect, attempt. samupa arise, appear, be born (again). Caus. produce, cause. pra be born (again) arise, propagate offspring through or in (I), bring forth, beget with (L or I). Caus. cause to propagate offspring or to be born, beget, generate. prati be born again. vi be born, arise, become, be changed into (N); propagate offspring, beget, bring forth. sam be born with (I), come forth, appear, take place, become, pass; bring forth. Caus. beget, bring forth, produce, generate, cause. Cf. anujāta, abhijāta, prajāta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_jap.html"> √ jap    √ jap, “whisper” Present I. jápati etc. B.+,-te etc. S.+ Passive japyate E Future Simple Future: japiṣyáti B Periphrastic Future: japitā Aorist RAo: ajījapat -iṣ-Ao: ajapīt GB. ajāpīt Perfect jajāpa jepus etc. E Causative jāpayati Desiderative jijapiṣa- Intensive jañjapyáte ŚB Verbal Nouns PPP: japita S.+, japta E.+; Inf: japitum E.; 1Abs: japitvā B.+, japtvā S.+ Derivatives japá B.+ japana E. jāpa E.+ jāpya E.+ japin C. japanīya C. jāpaka E.+ -jañjapa C. jápya B.+ japtavya E.+ jāpin C. jañjapūka C. Meanings jápati jápate v PPP japita & japta whisper, mutter, esp. prayers, invoke in a low voice. ā mutter into (karṇe). upa whisper to i.e. bring over secretly. sam whisper or talk about. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_jam.html"> √ jam    √ jam Present I. jamati Intensive jājamat M Artificially made forms, to frame a derivation for the name jamadagni. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_jambh.html"> √ jambh, jabh    √ jambh, jabh, “chew up, crush” Present I. jambhate, jabhate Aorist RAo: ajījabham AV. ajajambhat -iṣ-Ao: jambhiṣat RV Causative jambháyati etc. V.B Intensive jáñjabhāna AV.S.,-bhat S.; jañjabhyáte etc. B.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: jabdha AV.; Inf: jabhitum C Derivatives jámbha V.+ jámbhaka B.+ jabhya ? AV. jámbhana AV.+ jambhá AV.+ Meanings jambh v snap at (ápi), seize with the mouth. Caus. jambháyati crush, destroy. Int janjabhyate open the jaws, snap at; w. abhi the same. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_jar.html"> √ jar    √ jar, see √ jṛ. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_jalp.html"> √ jalp    √ jalp, “murmur, speak” Present I. jálpati etc. B.+,-te etc. C Passive jalpyate C Future Simple Future: jalpiṣyate Periphrastic Future: jalpitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: ajalpīt Perfect jajalpa etc. E. (jalpire C.) Verbal Nouns PPP: jalpita E.+ Derivatives jalpa E.+ jalpin E. -jalpana C. jalpitṛ E. jalpaka C. jalpya E. jálpi V. -jarjalpa? VS. Meanings jálpati v (jálpate), PPP jalpita (q.v.) murmur, chatter, talk; address, speak to (A or I ~ sārdham), speak of (A). abhi address, answer, talk over, suggest, advise. upa & pari chatter. pra speak, announce, proclaim. vi speak, utter. sam talk, speak. Cf. prajalpita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_jas.html"> √ jas    √ jas, “be exhausted” Present I. jásamāna RV (2p.) RV IV. jasyata Aorist RAo: ajījasata (2s.) ŚB. (jajastám RV.) Perfect jajāsa AV Causative jāsayati etc. B.+ (jāsyate E.) Derivatives jásu RV. jásuri RV.-jasra V.+ jásvan RV. Meanings jásate v be exhausted, languish. Caus. jāsayati exhaust, weaken. ud Caus. destroy (G or A). ni (jasyati) perish, disappear. Caus. exhaust. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_jah.html"> √ jah    √ jah, see √ hā. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_jaa.html"> √ jā    √ jā, see √ jan. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_ji.html"> √ 1 ji    √ 1 ji, “conquer” Present I. jáyati -te etc. V.+ II. jéṣi jitam RV Passive jīyate etc. E.+ (jīyeyam M.) Future Simple Future: jeṣyati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.; jayiṣyati JB.E.,-te E Periphrastic Future: jetā́ etc. B.E Aorist √-Ao: ajāyi, jīyāt jayyāt JUB.M RAo: ajījayat M -s-Ao: ajaiṣīt etc. V.+ (ajais -ait jeṣam jes jéṣma V.B.S., jéṣat etc. RV.), jeṣi TB. (ajaiṣṭa M.) -iṣ-Ao: ajayit TS., ajayiṣata (2p.) C Perfect jigā́ya etc. (jigetha RV.; jigīvā́ṃs V., jiginā́ṃs B.+) jigye etc. V.+-jayām āsa C Causative jāpayati etc. B.S. (ajījapata -jipata B.) Desiderative jígīṣati -te etc. V.+ Intensive jejīya- Verbal Nouns PPP: jitá V.+; Inf: jétum B.+,-tave B.; 1Abs: jitvā́ B.+; 2Abs: -jítya AV.+; jiṣé RV Derivatives jayá V.+ jíti V.+ jetṛ V.+ jāyú RV. jayin E.+ -jítvan V.B. jayitṛ B.E. jā́yuka MS. jayyà B. -jitvara C. jéman RV. jigyú RV. -jayana E.+ jina C. jemán B. jigīṣā́ V.+ jayús RV. jiṣṇú V.+ jeya E.+ -jigīṣin GB.E. -ji AV. jayiṣṇu U.E. jeṣá V.B.S. jigīṣú V.+ -jit V.+ jétva V.B. -jeṣin B. -jāpayitṛ B. -jityā B. jetavya E.+ jāyin B.+ Meanings jáyati jáyate v PPP jitá conquer, win, subdue, overcome, suppress, expel from (Ab), deprive of (2A); absol. vanquish (in a game or a suit of law), be victorious. jayati, tu (w. N), jitam 3 (w. I) = victorious is or be –, hail to – ! Caus. jāpayati cause to conquer or win (2A); salute with reverence*. Des jígīṣati wish to win, seek for prey. apa keep off, prevent. abhi win, conquer, obtain. ava win, gain, reconquer, vanquish, ward off. ā & ud conquer, win, subdue. nis gain, attain, subdue, conquer, overcome, sur pass. vinis the same. parā (mostly Ā) lose, be deprived of (A), succumb (Ab*); vanquish, overcome. pari , pra , prati win, conquer, vanquish. vi (mostly Ā) the same; surpass, excel; also = S. absol. Des (mostly Ā) wish to win or conquer, attack. sam win, conquer, obtain (together). Cf. párājita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_ji.html"> √ 2 ji, jinv    √ 2 ji, jinv, “quicken” Present I. jínvati etc. V.B.S.,-te RV V. jinóṣi RV.TS., ajinot JB., jinvé RV Future Simple Future: jinviṣyati AB Periphrastic Future: jinvitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: ajinvīt Perfect jijinváthus RV Verbal Nouns PPP: jinvitá AV Derivatives jīrá V.B.S. jīrí RV. -jinva RV. Meanings jínvati v (jínvate), jinóti be lively, hasten; put in motion, quicken, impel, refresh, further, favour, bring or help to (D); fill, satisfy. pra quicken, speed on, favour, help to (D). upapra urge on, impel. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_jiiv.html"> √ jīv    √ jīv, “live” Present I. jī́vati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ Passive jīvyáte etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: jīviṣyati etc. B.+ (ajīviṣyam U.),-te M Periphrastic Future: jīvitā Aorist √-Ao: jīvyā́sam -yāsma AV.B.S RAo: ajījivat, ajijīvat -iṣ-Ao: ajīvīt etc. AV.+ Perfect jijīva etc. B.+,-ve R Causative jīváyati etc. V.+ (jīvāpayati etc. E.+; jijīvayiṣa- in d.) Desiderative jijīviṣate B.+,-te C.; jújyūṣati etc. ŚB. (jijyūṣita AB.) Intensive jejīvya- Verbal Nouns PPP: jīvitá V.+; Inf: jī́vitum B.+,-tavaí AV.; 1Abs: jīvitvā JB.; 2Abs: -jīvya E.+; jīváse V.B.M1 Derivatives jīvá V.+ jīvya E.+ jīvás V.B.E. -jīvitṛ C. jīvaka S.+ jī́vana V.+ jīvā́tu V.+ jijīviṣā E. jīvin B.+ jīvanī́ya AV.+ jīvātṛ ( in d .) C. jijīviṣu E. jīvitavya C. -jijīvayiṣu E. Meanings jī́vati v (jī́vate), PPP jīvita (q.v.) live, revive (~ punar), subsist on (I). Imper. jīva (~ ciram) may you live (long)! Caus. jīvayati (te) make or keep alive, nourish, bring up; wish a pers. to live (by calling jīva). Des jijīviṣati (te) or jújyūṣati wish to live, seek a livelihood by (I). ati survive. anu live after i.e. like (A); live for, be devoted to (A); live on, subsist by (I). ā live on, make use of, enjoy (A). ud & pratyud revive; Caus. restore to life. upa subsist (~ vṛttim); live on, make use of, practise (A, G, or I); live under, depend on, serve (A). pratyupa Caus. restore to life. *vi revive. sam live (together), subsist on (I), revive. Caus. vivify, keep alive, nourish. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_jur.html"> √ jur, √ jṛ.    √ jur, √ jṛ. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ju_s.html"> √ juṣ    √ juṣ, “enjoy” Present II. jóṣi V VI. juṣáte etc. V.+-ti etc. RV.E.+ Future Simple Future: joṣiṣyate Periphrastic Future: joṣitā Aorist √-Ao: ajuṣran RV. (joṣati jóṣat jóṣā RV., joṣase AV.; juṣāṇá V.B.C.); juṣyāt C RAo: ajūjuṣat -iṣ-Ao: jóṣiṣat RV Perfect jujóṣa etc. V.+, jujuṣé etc. V.C. (jújoṣati etc. jújoṣat etc. RV.; jújoṣate RV., jujóṣate SV.; jujuṣṭana V.; ajujoṣam K. jujuṣan RV.) Causative joṣáyate etc. V.+,-ti E Desiderative jujuṣiṣa- , jujoṣiṣa- Intensive jojuṣ- Verbal Nouns PPP: júṣṭa V., juṣṭá V.+; juṣṭvī́ RV Derivatives -jus V.+ jóṣa V.+ -jóṣas V.B. joṣayitavya C. -juṣa B. jóṣya RV. joṣṭṛ V.B.S. jóṣayitṛ B. júṣṭi V. joṣaṇa B.+ Meanings juṣáte juṣáti v PPP júṣṭa 1 or juṣṭá (q.v.) be pleased or satisfied; be fond of, delight in, enjoy (A or G); like to, resolve upon (D or Inf, esp. in dhyai); prefer or choose (a cert. place), i.e. visit, inhabit. Caus. joṣayate (ti) like, love, approve of, choose. abhi like, visit, frequent. upa cheer, gladden. prati cherish, fondle; delight in, be pleased with (A). Caus. fondle, caress. Cf. prajuṣṭa, saṃjuṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_juu.html"> √ jū    √ jū, “be swift” Present I. jávate etc. RV.B IX. junā́ti etc. RV Aorist RAo: ajījavat Perfect jūjuvus -vat -vā́ṃs -vāná RV Causative jāvayati C. jijāvayiṣa- Verbal Nouns PPP: jūtá V., javita E.+;-jávam TS Derivatives javá V.+ jávana V.+ jáviṣṭha V.+ júvas RV. javín V.+ jávas V. jávīyas RV.B.U. jū́ V.B. jūtí V.B.U. Related with √ jīv, and perhaps with √ 2 ji jinv, javita is more probably denominative from java. Meanings jávate 1 & junā́ti v PPP jūtá press on, speed; impel, incite, promote, inspire; expel, drive, away. pra press on (trans. & intrans.). Cf. jūjuvás & jūjuvāná. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_juurv.html"> √ jūrv    √ jūrv, “consume” Present I. jū́rvati etc. V Aorist -iṣ-Ao: jūrvīt RV Doubtless a secondary formation (u- or eighth class) from √ jṛ jur. Meanings jū́rvati v singe, burn. ni burn down. sam = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_j_r.html"> √ 1 jṛ, jur    √ 1 jṛ, jur, “waste away” Present I. járati etc. jaranta RV. (járant V.+) IV. jī́ryati etc. AV.+,-te etc. B.+; jū́ryati etc. RV VI. juráti etc. RV Passive jīryate etc. C Future Simple Future: jarī̆ṣyati Periphrastic Future: jarī̆tā Aorist √-Ao: jīryāt Th Ao: ajarat RAo: ajījarat -iṣ-Ao: jāriṣus RV Perfect jajā́ra AV. jajarus, jerus; jujurvā́ṃs RV Causative jaráyati -te etc. V.+ (jāráyant RV.) Desiderative jijarī̆ṣa- , jijīrṣa Intensive jājṛ- , jejīrya- Verbal Nouns PPP:jīrṇá AV.+, jūrṇá RV. jarī̆tvā Derivatives jára V.+ járūtha ? RV. -jīrti C. jáguri RV. jarā́ V.+ jā́ra RV. jī́rṇi B. jarjara B.+ jaraṇá V.+ jāraṇa C. -jur RV. jarayitṛ C. jaraṇi RV. jírvi AV. -jurya V.B. -jarayu RV. jarás V.+ jívri ? RV. jū́rya RV. jarā́yu ? V.+ jarimán V.B. jūrṇí RV. jariṣṇu C. Compare √ jūrv and √ jvar Meanings járati v PPP jīrṇá 1 (q.v.) make or grow old; jī́ryati (te) grow old, age, decay, wither, waste away; be dissolved or digested. Caus. jaráyati (te) make old, wear out, digest. sam (jīryati) grow old (together). Cf. járant. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_j_r.html"> √ 2 jṛ    √ 2 jṛ, “sing” Present I. járate etc. V Verbal Nouns jarádhyai RV Derivatives jaráṇā ? RV. jarā́ RV. jaritṛ́ V.S. jū́rṇi ? RV. A secondary form of √ 1 gṛ. BR ascribe a few of the forms to a third √ jṛ (jar), “approach”. Meanings járate 2 v crackle, roar (fire); sound, call, invoke. prati call to, salute. sam sound. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_j_rmbh.html"> √ jṛmbh    √ jṛmbh, “gape” Present I. jṛ́mbhate etc. V.+,-ti etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: jṛmbhiṣyate Periphrastic Future: jṛmbhitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: ajṛmbhiṣṭa Perfect jajṛmbhe etc. E.+ Causative jṛmbhayati etc. C Intensive jarījṛmbhate C Verbal Nouns PPP: jṛmbhita E.+; 1Abs: jṛmbhitvā S Derivatives jṛmbha E.+ jṛmbhaka E.+ -jṛmbhin C. jṛmbhaṇa E.+ jṛmbhā C. Meanings jṛmbhate v (jṛmbhati), PPP jṛmbhita (q.v.) gape, yawn, open (of a flower), blossom; spread, extend; come forth, rise; be or feel at ease. Caus. jṛmbhayati cause to yawn. Int jarījṛmbhate extend far. ud & samud open wide, come forth, appear, arise. pari spread round. pra begin to yawn. vi yawn, gape, blossom, expand, break forth, appear; be or feel at ease. sam expand, break forth, appear. Cf. vijṛmbhita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_jeh.html"> √ jeh    √ jeh, “loll, pant” Present I. jéhamāna V Future Simple Future: jehiṣyate Periphrastic Future: jehitā Aorist RAo: ajijehat -iṣ-Ao: ajehiṣṭa Perfect jijehe Causative jehayati If , as seems probable, jihmá V.+belongs here, the root should be written √ jih. It is perhaps a secondary reduplicated formation from √ hā. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_j_jaa.html"> √ jñā    √ jñā, “know” Present I. jānati -te etc. U.E. jña (2s. impv.) C IX. jānā́ti -nīté etc. V.+ (jānīma jānithās M.) Passive jñāyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: jñāsyati -te etc. B.+ (ajñāsyat M.) Periphrastic Future: jñātā B Aorist √-Ao: ajñāyi V.+; jñeyā́s RV. jñāyāt -s-Ao: ájñāsam ajñāsthās AV.B., jñeṣam AV.B -siṣ-Ao: ajñāsiṣam etc. AV.+ Perfect jajñaú jajñé etc. V.+ Causative jñapayati etc. AV.+,-te U. (ajijñipat TS., ajijñapat etc. C. jñaptá B.+ jñapita, jñaptum E.+; jñapyáte ŚB. jñīpsa-) jñīpsyate C.; jñāpayati etc. B.+,-te etc. E.+ (jñāpyate etc. E.+, ajñāpiṣyat ? U.) Desiderative jijñāsate etc. AV.+,-ti etc. E.+ (jijñāsiṣi B., jijñāsyate etc. E.+) Intensive jājñā- Verbal Nouns PPP: jñātá V.+; Inf: jñā́tum B.+,-tos B.; 1Abs: jñātvā́ B.+; 2Abs: -jñā́ya B.+;-jñā́yam B Derivatives -jānaka ? E. jñātṛ́ V.+ -jñapya C. -jñāpayitavya C. -jñā V.+ jñātra B. -jñapana AV.B. jijñāsā B.+ jñá B.+ -jñāya V.B. jñapti C. jijñāsyà B.+ jñā́s RV. jñeya B.+ jñāpaka E.+ jijñāsana C. jñā́na V.+ -jajñi V.B. jñāpya E.+ -jijñāsenya B. jñātí V.+ jijñu E. jñāpana C. -jijñāsitavya U. jñātavya U.+ jñāpanīya C. jijñāsu E.+ Meanings jānā́ti jānīté 1 v (jānati, jānate), PPP jñātá know, be or get aware of (A, r. G), recognize, ascertain, investigate, acknowledge, approve, perceive, observe, notice (A), remember (G); consider or regard as, understand or suppose that – (2A), know how to (Inf); *Ā have to do with, deal with (G). With na know nothing of (A). Caus. jñāpayati, te & jñapayati, te, PPP jñaptá & jñāpita inform, teach; announce, notify; make a person acquainted with (2A); Ā beg, request (A). Des jijñāsate (ti) wish to know, try, examine; ascertain, suppose. Des Caus. jñīpsati wish to make a person acquainted with (2A); PPP jñīpsyamāna wished or intended to be informed. anu permit, grant, approve, forgive, pardon (G of pers.); empower, authorize to (D or ~ prati w. A); dismiss, bid farewell (A), be gracious or kind to (A). Caus. ask for permission or leave, take leave of (A). abhyanu & samanu the same. abhi perceive, notice, understand, know; acknowledge as, think that (2A), concede, grant; agree, approve. pratyabhi recognize again, notice, understand, come to one's self, recover one's consciousness. samabhi know, recognize. ava despise, sur pass. ā attend to, notice, hear, learn, understand. Caus. command, appoint a pers. (A) to (D or L). samā perceive, notice. Caus. bid, appo Int upa & samupa think out, invent. nis & vinis discern, find out. pari observe, understand, ascertain, know thoroughly, know as (2A). pra understand, distinguish, discern, be clever or wise, perceive, become aware of, find out. prati acknowledge, recognize, approve, consent, agree, promise (D, G, r. L of pers., A of th.); Ā state, affirm, answer; perceive, observe, become aware of. saṃprati consent to, promise. vi perceive, find out, observe, notice, hear from (G); consider as, understand or know that (2A); distinguish, discern, know thoroughly, become or be wise; vijñāyate it is well known or recognized (a rule, dogma, etc.); mā vijñāyi this (prec. N) is not to be understood (g.). Caus. make known, report, communicate, say that (2A); make one understand, apprise, teach; interrogate, beg, ask for (D, prati, artham, or nimittam*). abhivi become aware of, notice. sam Ā be of one mind, agree together, harmonize with (L, *I or *A), obey (D); direct, appoint (A), understand, know. Caus. cause to agree together, unite; appease, satisfy; make understood, make signs or hints to (anyo 'nyam), order, command. abhisam agree in (A), acknowledge. Cf. anujñāta, abhyanujñāta, parijñāta, prajānánt, prajñāta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_jyaa.html"> √ jyā, jī    √ jyā, jī, “overpower, injure” Present IV. jī́yate RV.ŚB IX. jinā́ti etc. V.B.S Passive jīyáte AV.MS Future Simple Future: jyāsyati -te B Periphrastic Future: jyātā Aorist √-Ao: jīyāt -siṣ-Ao: ajyāsiṣam etc. B Perfect jijyaú B Causative jyāpayati , ajijyapat Desiderative jíjyāsati etc. V.B Intensive jājyā- , jejīya- Verbal Nouns PPP: jītá AV. jīna; 1Abs: jītvā; 2Abs: -jyāya Derivatives -jīti V.B.S. jyā́na B. -jyeya B.U. jyā́yas V.+ jyā́ V.B. jyāní AV.B. -jyéya n. AV. jyeṣṭha V.+ -jya AV. -jyāya MS. jyāyuka JB. jyāyiṣṭha E.+ Related with √ ji. Meanings jinā́ti v PPP jitá 1 overpower, oppress, deprive of (2A), P. jīyáte (jī́yate), Des jíjyāsati adhi & pra overwhelm. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_jyut.html"> √ jyut    √ jyut, “shine” Present I. jyótati MS.,-te M. ? Causative jyotáya AV. (jyotyámāna ŚB.) Verbal Nouns 2 Abs: -jyótya B.S Derivatives jyuti E. jyotā VS. jyotaya ? AV. jyótis V.+ -jyotana S. jyótsnā B.+ A differentiated form of √ dyut. Meanings jyótati v (jyótate) shine; Caus. jyotáyati (~ ava) illuminate. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_jri.html"> √ jri    √ jri, “go” Present I. jrayati RV1 Future Simple Future: jreṣyati Periphrastic Future: jretā Aorist RAo: ajijrayat -iṣ-Ao: ajraiṣīt Precative: jrīyāt Perfect jijrāya Causative jrāyaya- Desiderative jijrīṣa- Intensive jejrī- Derivatives -jráya RV. jráyas RV. jrayasāná RV.-jri RV. Meanings jráyati v w. upa stretch out to (A). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_jvar.html"> √ jvar    √ jvar, “be hot” Present I. jvarati etc. U.+ Passive jvaryate C Future Simple Future: jvariṣyati E Periphrastic Future: jvaritā Aorist RAo: ajijvarat -iṣ-Ao: ajvārīt Perfect jajvāra Causative jvarayati etc. C Desiderative jijvariṣa- Intensive jājvarya- , jājūr- Derivatives jvara AV.+ -jvāra RV.C. Another form of √ jval, and apparently related with √ jṛ, √ jur and √ jūrv. Meanings jvarati v be hot or feverish. Caus. jvarayati make feverish. sam be grieved or sorry. anusam be sorry for (A), also = abhisam be grieved or envious. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_jval.html"> √ jval    √ jval, “burn, flame” Present I. jválati etc. B.+,-te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: jvaliṣyati B.+ Periphrastic Future: jvalitā Aorist RAo: ajijvalat -iṣ-Ao: ajvālīt B.U., ajvalīt C Perfect jajvāla etc. B.+ Causative jvalayati etc. B.+,-te GB.; jvālayati etc. S.+ (jvālyate B.+) Desiderative jijvaliṣa- Intensive jājvalīti C. (-lati -lant E.),-lyate E Verbal Nouns PPP: jvalita B.+; 2Abs: -jvalya S Derivatives jvala E.+ jvalitṛ C. jvālā E.+ -jvālana C. jvalana B.+ jvāla S.+ jvālin E.+ Compare √ jvar, of which this is another form. Meanings jválati v (jválate), PPP jvalita (q.v.) blaze, flame, burn, glow, shine. Caus. jvalayati & jvālayati set on fire, illuminate. Int jājvalīti & jājvalyate flame violently, be brilliant. abhi shine, Caus. = ava Caus. illuminate. ud blaze up, flame, shine; Caus. = S. Caus. pra flame up, shine forth; Caus. set on fire, kindle. abhipra & saṃpra flame up, catch fire prati blaze, burn. abhivi flame against or opposite to. sam blaze, flame; Caus. kindle, illuminate. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_jha_t.html"> √ jhaṭ    √ jhaṭ, “confuse” Only in ujjhaṭita, in a single doubtful occurrence ( C.). Given a full set of forms by the grammarians. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_jha_n.html"> √ jhaṇ    √ jhaṇ, “sound” A single occurrence, jhaṇati, in the Harṣacarita ( Bö.). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_jhar.html"> √ jhar    √ jhar, “fall” Present I. jharant C1. Derivatives jhara E.+ -jharaṇa C. A very questionable root. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root__ta_gk.html"> √ ṭaṅk    √ ṭaṅk, “cover” (?) Present I. ṭaṅkati, ṭaṭaṅka Aorist √-Ao: aṭaṅki C Causative ṭaṅkayati C Verbal Nouns PPP: ṭaṅkita C Derivatives ṭaṅka E.+ Most probably a denominative of ṭaṅka, rather. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root__tal.html"> √ ṭal    √ ṭal, “be confused” Present I. ṭalati C. A single late occurrence, doubtless artificial. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root__tiik.html"> √ ṭīk    √ ṭīk, “trip” Present I. ṭīkate C. A single late and doubtless artificial occurrence. Bö. gives also uṭṭīkita, but without statement of authority. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root__tup.html"> √ ṭup    √ ṭup, “swell” Bö. suggests such a root as origin of (ā-) ṭopa E.+. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root__dam.html"> √ ḍam    √ ḍam, “sound” A single doubtful (onomatopoetic ?) occurrence, ḍamant C. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root__damb.html"> √ ḍamb    √ ḍamb, “mock” Present I. ḍambate ? C Causative ḍambayati etc. C. (ḍambyate C.) Derivatives -ḍamba C. -ḍambaka C. -ḍambin C. -ḍambya C. -ḍambana C. All forms only with prefix vi. Meanings viḍambayati v PPP viḍambita imitate, equal (A); mock, cheat, deceive. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root__dii.html"> √ ḍī    √ ḍī, “fly” Present I. ḍayate C. ? IV. ḍīyate C. ? Passive ḍīyate C Future Simple Future: ḍayiṣyate Periphrastic Future: ḍayitā Aorist RAo: aḍīḍayat -iṣ-Ao: aḍayiṣṭa Perfect ḍiḍye Causative ḍāyayati C Desiderative ḍiḍayiṣa- Intensive ḍeḍī- Verbal Nouns PPP: ḍīna E.+; 2Abs: -ḍīya C Derivatives -ḍayana C. -ḍīyana E. ḍītara ?ŚB -ḍī̆yāna C. A later form of √ 1 dī, and rare, except in ḍīna. Meanings ḍayate ḍīyate v PPP ḍīna fly, move through the air. ud fly up, Caus. uḍḍāpayati scare. prod fly up and away. pra fly up. Cf. uḍḍīna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root__dval.html"> √ ḍval    √ ḍval, “mix” Causative ḍvālayati etc. C. Derivatives -ḍvālana C. Only used by one scholiast; no proper root. Meanings Caus. ḍvālayati w. ā mix. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root__dhauk.html"> √ ḍhauk    √ ḍhauk, “approach” Present I. ḍhaukate etc. C Future Simple Future: ḍhaukiṣyate Periphrastic Future: ḍhaukitā Aorist RAo: aḍuḍhaukat -iṣ-Ao: aḍhaukiṣṭa Perfect ḍuḍhauke C Causative ḍhaukayati etc. C Desiderative ḍuḍhaukiṣa- Intensive ḍoḍhauk- Verbal Nouns PPP: ḍhaukita E.+ Derivatives ḍhaukana C. Meanings ḍhaukate v approach (A). Caus. ḍhaukayati cause to approach, bring near to (G). upa Caus. present, offer. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ta_ms.html"> √ taṃs, tas    √ taṃs, tas, “shake” Present I. taṃsati -te Aorist Th Ao: átasat AV.B RAo: átataṃsatam RV Perfect tatasré RV Causative taṃsayati VS.,-te RV. (taṃsayádhyai RV.) Intensive tantasaíte RV. tantasyate Derivatives -taṃsa B.+ taṃsu ? E.+ tásara V.B. -tantasā́yya RV. -taṃsana C. -tasti? B.+ títau ? RV.S.+ Meanings tas v pour out (fig.); Caus. taṃsayati shake. abhi shake out of, rob. pari Caus. shake, stir. vi the same. Cf. avataṃsay. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tak.html"> √ tak    √ tak, “rush” Present I. takati II. takti atakta RV Future Simple Future: takiṣyati Periphrastic Future: takitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: atā̆kīt Perfect tatāka Verbal Nouns PPP: taktá RV.;-táṅkam AV Derivatives -takana C. tákavāna RV. takvá RV. -tákvarī AV., táku RV. -takri? RV. tákvan V.B. Probably not to be separated from √ tac, which with prefix ā has won a special meaning. Meanings takti v PPP taktá rush, fly. nis Ā rush on, attack (A). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tak_s.html"> √ takṣ    √ takṣ, “fashion” Present I. tákṣati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ II. tāṣṭi AB., tákṣati (3p.) etc. RV V. takṣṇuvánti etc. B.S Passive takṣya- Future Simple Future: takṣiṣyati, takṣyati Periphrastic Future: takṣitā, taṣṭā Aorist RAo: atatakṣat -iṣ-Ao: atakṣiṣus RV. (takṣiṣat S.) Perfect tatákṣa etc. V.+ (takṣathus takṣus V.B.), tatakṣé etc. V.B Causative takṣaya- Desiderative titakṣiṣa- , titakṣa- Intensive tātakṣ- Verbal Nouns PPP: taṣṭá V.+; 2Abs: -takṣya C Derivatives takṣa S.+ tákṣya RV. takṣaṇa S.+ taṣṭi C. takṣaká AV.+ tákṣan V.+ táṣṭṛ RV. Meanings tákṣati tákṣate takṣṇoti & tāṣṭi v PPP taṣṭá hew, cut, work, fashion, make, invent. anu procure, get. apa split or cut off. ā produce, procure. ud fashion out of (Ab). nis shape or form. pra fashion, make. vi = apa . sam = S. (~ together). Cf. vítaṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ta_jc.html"> √ tañc, tac    √ tañc, tac, “coagulate” Present VII. tanákti etc. B.S Future Simple Future: taṅkṣyati tañciṣyati Periphrastic Future: taṅktā tañcitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: atāṅkṣīt, atañcīt Perfect tataṅka Causative tañcaya- Desiderative titaṅkṣa- , titañciṣa- Intensive tātañc- , tātacya- Verbal Nouns PPP: takta ; 1Abs: taktvā, tañcitvā; 2Abs: -tácya B Derivatives -taṅka E.+ -táñcana B.S. takmán AV. takra E.+ -taṅkyà B.S. See √ tak. Only used with ā. Meanings tanákti v contrP ā coagulate. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ta_t.html"> √ taṭ    √ taṭ, “clatter” A single form, taṭati, in Adbh.Brāh., doubtless an onomatopoetic formation. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ta_d.html"> √ taḍ    √ taḍ, “beat” Present II. tāḍhi ? RV1 Aorist RAo: atītaḍat Perfect tatāḍa C Causative tāḍayati etc. E.+ (tāḍyate E.+) Derivatives taḍít V.+ tāḍaka E.+ tāḍya E.+ tāḍanīya C. tā́ḍa AV.+ -tāḍin C. tāḍana E.+ tāḍayitṛ C. Meanings Caus. tāḍayati beat, strike, hurt, hit. abhi & ā Caus. the same. pari strike, pelt. vi pound, crush; Caus. pelt, wound, strike against (L). sam beat, strike, hit. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_tan.html"> √ 1 tan, tā    √ 1 tan, tā, “stretch” Present VIII. tanóti tanuté etc. V.+ Passive tāyáte etc. V.+, tanyate etc. C Future Simple Future: taṃsyáte B. taniṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: tanitā, tāyitā C Aorist √-Ao: atan RV., átata etc. (atathās atnata) V.B.; atāyi B Th Ao: atanat etc. RV RAo: atītanat -s-Ao: atāṃsīt B. (atān V.), atasi ataṃsmahi B -iṣ-Ao: atānīt MS. atanīt, ataniṣṭa Perfect tatā́na etc. V.+ (tatántha V.B. tenitha), tenus etc. E.+ (tatánat etc. tatananta tatanyus RV.); tené etc. AV.+ (tatane RV., tatne etc. V., tate RV.) Causative tānayati AV.C Desiderative titāṃsa- , titaniṣa- Intensive tantan- Verbal Nouns PPP: tatá V.+; Inf: tantum B.; 1Abs: tatvā B., tatvā́ya B. tanitvā; 2Abs: -tátya B.+,-tāya C Derivatives tán V. tániman B.+ tantí V.+ -tā RV. tána RV. tániṣṭha B.S. -tati B.+ tā́na V.+ tanā́ AV. tánīyas B. tántu V.+ -tānaka C. tánaya V.+ tanú V.+ tanitṛ C. -tānuka ? C. tánas RV. tanū́ V.+ tántra V.+ -tāyitṛ C. -táni V.+ tanus E. -tatnī̆ AV.B. tatanúṣṭi RV. -tatnu AV. tena ? C. titāṃsu C. Compare √ tāy. Meanings tanóti tanuté v PPP tatá 1 (q.v.) extend, stretch, spread (intrans. & trans.); last, continue; protract, prolong, lengthen; spin out, weave (l. & f.); prepare, arrange, direct, accomplish, perform, compose, make. P. tāyáte be extended, increase, grow. adhi string (the bow), cover. anu extend along (intrans.), continue; carry on, maintain. abhi extend or reach over (acc); spread out, unfold, place in front. ava sink down; overspread, cover; loosen, let off (esp. the bow-string). ā spread over, penetrate, cover (esp. with light); expand, diffuse, stretch (a bow); bring forth, produce, effect, show, betray. anvā stretch or reach over; spread (trans. & intrans.). vyā diffuse, produce, effect. samā the same, stretch (esp. the bow). pari stretch around, surround, envelop. pra spread, extend (trans. & intrans.); cause, produce; show, betray. vi spread over, cover, fill, stretch out (a cord, web, etc.) string (a bow); diffuse, extend; prepare, arrange, sacrifice; produce, effect; make, render (2A). sam join one's self with, hold together; cover, fill; connect, continue, protract; effect, accomplish; exhibit, evince. anusam add, join, annex; spread, expand; carry on, prosecute. Cf. ā́tata, pravitata, vítata, sátata. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_tan.html"> √ 2 tan    √ 2 tan, “roar” Present IV. tanyati RV Derivatives tanyatā́ RV. tanyatú V. tanyú RV. tanayitnú RV. Appears to be an abbreviated form of √ stan. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tand.html"> √ tand    √ tand, “be weary” Present I. tandate RV1. (tandrat ? RV1.) Derivatives tandra V.+ tandri E.+ tandrī́ AV.+ Meanings tandate v relax, give way. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tap.html"> √ tap    √ tap, “heat” Present I. tápati -te etc. V.+ IV. tápyati etc. B.+,-te etc. B.+ Passive tapyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: tapsyáti etc. B.+ (atapsyat M.),-te etc. E.; tapiṣyati etc. E Periphrastic Future: taptā E Aorist √-Ao: tapāná SV.; átāpi V.B RAo: atītapat E.,-pe RV. (tītapāsi AV.) -s-Ao: atāpsīt etc. V.B.S., atapthās ? AV Perfect tatā́pa tepé etc. V.+ (tatápate RV.) Causative tāpáyati etc.-te etc. AV.+ (tāpyate B.E.; Periphrastic Future: tāpitā E.) Desiderative titapsa- Intensive tātapyate etc. E.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: taptá V.+, tapita C.; Inf: taptum E.+, táptos ŚB.; 1Abs: taptvā B.+; 2Abs: -tápya V.+ Derivatives -tap RV.S. tápu RV. tápiṣṭha V. -tāpin B.+ tapa V.+ tápus V. tapiṣṇu E. -tāpya B. tapya E. tápuṣī̆ V.B. tapīyas C. tāpana E.+ tápana V.+ tapti C. tapyatú V.B. -tāpitṛ ? E. tapaná ,-nī́ V.B. taptavya E. tāpa AV.+ tāpayitṛ C. tápas V.+ taptṛ E. tāpaka C. tāpayiṣṇú RV. Meanings tápati v (tápate), PPP taptá (q.v.) be warm or hot, burn (I), shine; castigate one's self, do penance, suffer; heat, burn (trans.), distress, pain, torment. P. tapyáte (also tápyate, ti) has only the intrans. mgs. Caus. tāpayati, te make hot, consume by heat, listress, pain, castigate (one's self). ati make warm or hot, trouble, distress. anu heat, pain; P. suffer pain, repent, long for (A). pratyanu & samnu P. repent. abhi make hot, shine upon, pain, ache; P. suffer pain. ā glow, shine, heat; P. suffer pain, w. tapas castigate one's self. abhyā heat, pain, torment. ud the same. upa make hot, vex, hurt; also = P. suffer, pain, get unwell (P also impers. w. G or A of pers.). nis (niṣ) heat, singe. pari burn all round, set on fire, kindle; also = P. feel pain, suffer, do penance (~ tapas). Caus. pain, afflict. pra P give out heat, burn, shine (l. & f.); shine upon, warm, heat, singe, roast, pain, torment; also = P. feel pain, suffer, castigate one's self. Caus. heat, warm, illumine, kindle; pain, distress. prati give out heat towards, make hot or warm. vi give out strong heat, burn; pervade, penetrate. sam heat, burn, pain, torment (also Caus. ); suffer pain, repent. P. be distressed, grieve, do penance. abhisam vex, distress. Cf. úttapta, upatapta, pratapant, pratapta, saṃtapta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tam.html"> √ tam    √ tam, “faint” Present IV. tā́myati etc. B.+,-te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: tamiṣyati Periphrastic Future: tamitā Aorist √-Ao: atā̆mi Th Ao: tamat etc. RV.B.S Perfect tatāma B Causative tamáyati etc. B.S Verbal Nouns PPP: tāṃtá B.+; támitos B.S Derivatives tamaka C. tamī C. tāṃti C. tāma C. tamana S. támiṣīci V. -tameru VS. -tāmaka C. támas V.+ támisra V.+ tamrá RV. tāmī S. tāmrá AV.+ Meanings tā́myati v (tā́myate), PPP tāntá become dark, dull, or stiff; faint away, be exhausted, lauguish, perish (also impers. w. A of subj.). ā , ud & sam languish, be perplexed. pra be out of breath, be exhausted, languish. Cf. ávatānta, nitānta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tark.html"> √ tark    √ tark, “think” Causative tarkáyati -te etc. E.+ (tarkyate etc. E.+) Derivatives tarka S.+ tarkaka E. -tarkyà B.+ tarkaṇīya E. tarkā E. tarkin C. tarkaṇa E.+ tarkuka ? E. Probably a denominative formation. Meanings tarkayati v (tarkayate) suppose, conjecture, guess, reflect, regard as (2A), think of (A), think to (Inf). pari ponder, think over, consider as (2A). vi suppose, conjecture, reflect on (A), ascertain. sam regard as (2A). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tarj.html"> √ tarj    √ tarj, “threaten” Present I. tarjati etc. E.+,-te E Future Simple Future: tarjiṣyati Periphrastic Future: tarjitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: atarjīt Perfect tatarja Causative tarjayati etc. E.+,-te E. (tarjyate etc. E.) Verbal Nouns PPP: tarjita E.+; 2Abs: -tarjya E Derivatives tarjaka C. tarjana E.+ tarjanā E.+ Meanings tarjati v (tarjate), PPP tarjita (q.v.) threaten, menace, abuse, revile. Caus. tarjayati, te = S. + deride, mock; frighten, terrify. abhi & vi Caus. scold, revile. pari Caus. threaten. sam Caus. = S.Caus. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tas.html"> √ tas    √ tas, see √ taṃs. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_taa.html"> √ tā    √ tā, see √ 1 tan. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_taay.html"> √ tāy    √ tāy, “stretch” Present I. tāyate Passive tāyyámāna VS Future Simple Future: tāyiṣyate Periphrastic Future: tāyitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: atāyiṣṭa Ao/Ps/3/sg: atāyi Perfect tatāye tāyāṃ cakre ? JB Very questionable forms. The JB. manuscript reads (iii. 177) anusaṃtāyāyāṃ cakre. Belongs probably in some way to √ 1 tan, tā. The Bhāgavata-Purāna has once tāyitā (periph. fut.), which is given above under √ 1 tan, tā. Meanings tāyate v (cf. √ 1 tan) w. vi & sam expand. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_taav.html"> √ tāv    √ tāv Present I. tā́vati AV Probably a false reading. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ti.html"> √ ti    √ ti, “crush” Present V. tinoti C1 A single occurrence, and most probably a false reading. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tij.html"> √ tij    √ tij, “be sharp” Present I. téjate etc. RV.ŚB Perfect ? titigdhi B.S Causative tejayati etc. E.+ Desiderative títikṣate etc. V.+,-ti etc. E.+ (titikṣmahe M.) Intensive tétikte etc. V.B Verbal Nouns PPP: tiktá V.+ Derivatives -tikti RV. tīkṣṇá V.+ téjana V.+ téjīyas RV.C. tigitá RV. tegá ? VS. téjas V.+ titikṣā E.+ tigmá V.+ teja C. téjiṣṭha V.B.S. titikṣú AV.+ Meanings téjate v PPP tiktá (q.v.) be or make sharp. Caus. tejayati sharpen, incite. Des títikṣate (ti) wish to be sharp or firm against, i.e. endure, bear (A). I. tétikte = S. trans. & intrans. ud & sam Caus. incite, impel. Cf. nítikta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tim.html"> √ tim    √ tim, “be quiet” Present IV. timyant C1. tīmyati Perfect titema Intensive tetimya- Verbal Nouns PPP: timita R Derivatives timi ? E.+ timira ? E.+ Apparently related with √ tam; the participle, with that of √ stim. Meanings timyati v PPP timita become quiet (or “damp”). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tir.html"> √ tir    √ tir see √ tṛ. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_til.html"> √ til    √ til Accepted by BR. in VS. xxiii. 24 prátilāmi (TS.TB. prásulāmi); but an unintelligible and probably false reading. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tu.html"> √ tu    √ tu, “be strong” Present II. tavīti RV. tauti Perfect tūtāva RV. (tūtos -ot RV.) Intensive távītuat RV Derivatives tavā-? RV. tavás V. távyas RV. tuví- V.VS. távya RV. taviṣá V. tīvrá V.+ túvis- V.B. tavyà TS. táviṣī RV. túmra ? RV. tū́ya V. távas V.B.S. távīyas V. turá V.+ tūtumá ? RV. Meanings tavīti 1 v be strong. ud & sam (1. távītvat) effect, bring about. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tuc.html"> √ tuc    √ tuc, “impel, generate” A root or root-form (see √ tuj ) inferable from the following Derivatives túc RV. -túka? RV. toká V.+ tókman ,-ma V.+ 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tuj.html"> √ tuj    √ tuj, “urge, thrust” Present I. tojati túñjamāna RV VI. tujánt tujete RV VII. tuñjánti tuñjáte (3p). etc. RV Passive tujyáte etc. RV Future Simple Future: tojiṣyati Periphrastic Future: tojitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: atojīt Perfect tūtujāná (and tū́tujāna) tutujyāt RV. tutoja Causative tujáyant etc. V Verbal Nouns tujáse RV.,-túje RV., tujáye ? V Derivatives túj V.C. túji RV. túgra RV. tuṅga ? E.+ tújya RV. tuñjá RV. túgvan RV. tūtuji RV. This and the preceding are probably two forms of the same root. For the connection of meaning, compare the roots √ su, √ sū. Meanings tujáti tujáte 1 v (tuñjáti & tuñjáte 3 pl.) push on, impel, stir up; press out, emit, promote, further; Ā dash together or wave to and fro, hasten, rush on; P. be vexed or angry. Caus. tujáyati hasten, run. Cf. ātúje, tūtujāna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tud.html"> √ tud    √ tud, “push, thrust” Present VI. tudáti etc. V.+,-te E VII. ? tundāná AV., tundate RV. ( tudāyáti AV.) Passive tudyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: totsyati -te Periphrastic Future: tottā Aorist RAo: atūtudat -iṣ-Ao: atautsīt atutta Perfect tutóda V.+ tutude Causative todayati etc. E.+ (todyate E.+) Desiderative tututsa- Intensive totudyate S Verbal Nouns PPP: tunná V.+; 1Abs: tuttvā; 2Abs: -tudya E Derivatives -tud S.E.C. tunda ? C. -todin V.+ todana C. -tuda AV.+ todá V.+ todya C. tóttra B.+ Meanings tudáti v (tudáte), PPP tunná strike, push, prick; pound, crush, Caus. todayati goad, prick. ā goad, urge on. ni pierce, penetrate. pra strike at, prick at; Caus. urge, impel. vi pierce, strike, tear. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tur.html"> √ tur    √ tur see √ tṛ. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_turv.html"> √ turv, tūrv    √ turv, tūrv, “overcome” Present I. tū́rvati etc. RV.B Derivatives turvá RV. turván RV. turvī́ti RV. tū́rvi RV. turváṇi RV. A speciallized form of √ tṛ, tur, to which the derivatives might in part with equal propriety be referred. Meanings tū́rvati v overpower. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tul.html"> √ tul    √ tul, “lift, weigh” Present I. tolati Causative tolayati etc. E.+ (tolyate C.); tulayati etc. E.+,-te etc. E.+ Derivatives tula C. tulya S.+ tolaka C. tolana E.+ tulā́ B.+ tulana C. tolya C. Meanings tolayati & tulayati tulayate v PPP tulita lift up, weigh, examine, compare; equal, match, resemble. ā lift up. ud raise, weigh. sam weigh against each ofter. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tuz.html"> √ tuś    √ tuś, “drip” Present I. tośate etc. V. (tośé RV.) Causative tośaya RV Derivatives tośá RV. -tóśana RV. tośás RV. BR. refer two or three of the forms to a root 2 tuś= tuṣ. Meanings tośate 1 v drip (intrans.). ni drip down (trans. & intrans.); Caus. grant, distribute. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tu_s.html"> √ tuṣ    √ tuṣ, “be content” Present IV. tuṣyati etc. S.+,-te C Future Simple Future: tokṣyati Periphrastic Future: toṣṭā Aorist Th Ao: atuṣat RAo: atūtuṣat Perfect tutoṣa etc. E.+ Causative toṣayati etc. JB.+ (toṣyate C.); tuṣáyantī RV Desiderative tutukṣa- Intensive totuṣ- Verbal Nouns PPP: tuṣṭa E.+; Inf: toṣṭum E.; 2Abs: -tuṣya C Derivatives tuṣṭi E.+ -toṣaka C. toṣaṇa E.+ toṣayitavya E. tūṣṇī́m ? V.+ toṣin E.+ toṣaṇīya E.+ toṣayitṛ C. toṣa E.+ toṣya E. toṣṭavya C. Meanings tuṣyati v (tuṣyate), PPP tuṣṭa become quiet, be satisfied or pleased with, delight in (G, D, I, L, or A w. prati); also = Caus. toṣayati, te (tuṣáyati) satisfy. upa Caus. satisfy. pari be delighted or charmed, be happy. Caus. satisfy completely, please much. sam be calm, content, or happy. Caus. gratify, rejoice, comfort. Cf. parituṣṭa, saṃtuṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tuurv.html"> √ tūrv    √ tūrv see √ turv. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_t_r.html"> √ tṛ, tir, tur    √ tṛ, tir, tur, “pass” Present I. tárati etc. V.+,-te etc. V.+ III. titarti etc. RV.C. tutorti. IV. tī́ryatī ? AV.; tūrya RV1. táruṣema -ṣante -ṣanta RV VI. tiráti -te etc. V.B.S.; turáti -te etc. V.B. VIII. tarute RV1. 2 ? turyā́ma RV. Passive tīryate ? E Future Simple Future: tariṣyati etc. S.+,-te etc. E.+ tarīṣyati Periphrastic Future: tarī̆tā Aorist √-Ao: atāri V.B. tīryāt RAo: atītaras AV -s-Ao: atārṣīt etc. S.+ -iṣ-Ao: átārīt etc. V.B.S. (átārima RV.; tāriṣat etc. V.B.S.; tāriṣīmahi RV.) Perfect tatāra V.+ (tatarúṣas RV.), terus E.+, tatare C.; titirus titirvā́ṃs RV.; tuturyā́t -yāma RV Causative tāráyati etc. AV.+,-te etc. S.+ (tāryateetc. E.+); turáyant V.,-yante RV Desiderative titīrṣati etc. B.+,-te etc. E., tū́tūrṣati RV. titarī̆ṣa- Intensive tartṛ- RV., táritṛ- RV., tártur- RV. tātṛ- Verbal Nouns PPP: tīrṇá V.+, tūrtá ŚB., tūrṇa S.+; Inf: tartum E.+, taritum E.+, tarītum E.+; 1Abs: tīrtvā́ AV.U.; 2Abs: -tīrya E.+,-tū́rya RV.;-tíram -tíre RV.; tarádhyai RV.; tarīṣáṇi RV Derivatives tára V.+ táras V.+ tartavya E. tārá AV.+ tarín ? AV. tarás SV. taritavya S.+ tāraka E.+ tárya RV. tárīyas RV. -tárītu ? V.B. tārin RV.E.+ tarī̆ E.+ táru ? RV. -tarītṛ V. tāryà AV.E.+ táraṇa V.+ táruṇa ? V.+ tarutṛ V. tāraṇa E.+ taraṇīya E.+ tárus RV. tárutra RV. -tāraṇīya C. taráṇi V.+ táruṣa V. -taritra ? E. -tārayitṛ B. -taratha ? C. tárūṣas RV. -tárman RV. -tira AV.B. tirás ? V.+ tī́ra B.+ titīrṣā C. tīrthá V.+ titīrṣu E.+ túr RV.B. turas- RV. -tūrti V.B. táturi V.B.S. túra V.+ turí RV. tū́rṇi V.B. -tartura RV. turáṇa RV. turyā́ TS. -tū́rya V.B.S. tuturváṇi RV. toraṇa ? E.+ Compare roots √ tur (oftener given as a separate root), √ turv, √ tvar, and √ trā. Meanings tárati tárate tiráti tiráte turáti turáte titarti tarute v PPP tīrṇá (w. P & pass. mg) cross over, get through, overcome, subdue, escape; float, swim, rush on; be saved, survive; Ā emulate, content, also = Caus. tāráyati, te lead or help over (A), bring to (A or D), further, save. Des titīrṣati, te wish to pass over or to arrive at (A). I. tartarīti, tarītarti, PPP tárītrat get through, be victorious or fortunate. ati & vyati cross, pass, overcome. abhi overtake, get up to (A). ava come down, descend (esp. from heaven to earth, mahīm), alight; betake one's self from (Ab) to (A); take place, happen; overcome, surpass. Caus. make descend, lead or bring (down) from (Ab) to (A or L); remove, take off, avert from (Ab); introduce, establish. ā pass, cross, overcome; enlarge, increase. ud the same + come up from (Ab), esp. out of the water (~ jalāt), escape, be saved from (Ab). Caus. cause to come out, vomit up, take off; lead or fetch over, save from (Ab), deliver, rescue. abhyud cross, pass, get through unto (D). samud = ud. ni overthrow, humiliate. nis come forth from, get out of (Ab); pass, finish, accomplish; overcome, master Caus. save, deliver; overcome, vanquish. pra take to the water, cross over; start on, advance, increase, grow; lead on, further, strengthen, promote, prolong (esp. āyus the life); Ā live on. Caus. extend, lengthen; cheat, deceive; lead astray, seduce to (D or L). vipra Caus. cheat, deceive. vi cross through, traverse; further, promote, prolong; remove from (Ab); destroy, frustrate; grant, bestow, give, offer; perform, cause, effect. sam cross over, pass through (l. & f.), escape, be saved; also = Caus. bring over, save. Cf. avatīrṇa, uttīrṇa, nistīrṇa, vitīrṇa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_t_rd.html"> √ tṛd    √ tṛd, “split, bore” Present I. tardati VII. tṛṇátti etc. V.B.U., tṛntte ŚB. (atṛṇam KBU.) Future Simple Future: tardiṣyati -te, tartsyati -te Periphrastic Future: tarditā Aorist √-Ao: tárdas RV., tṛdyus S RAo: atatardat, atītṛdat -iṣ-Ao: atardīt Perfect tatárda etc. V.C. (tatárditha RV.), tatṛdāná RV Causative tardayati S Desiderative títṛtsati etc. V.B.-te; titardisati -te Intensive tarītṛd- Verbal Nouns PPP: tṛṇṇá B.S.U.; 2Abs: -tṛ́dya B.S.;-tṛ́das V Derivatives tardá AV.+ -tardi? E. -tṛd RV. tṛdilá RV. tradá RV. tárdman AV.B.S. -tṛtti B. tṛ́tsu ? RV. tardana V.+ tṛ́ṇman ? AV. Meanings tṛṇátti tṛntte v PPP tṛṇá split, bore, open, let free. anu bore after i.e. for (water), make flow. abhi split, open, release; win, acquire. ā split, pierce, separate. vi pierce, cleave, open, break through, excavate. sam hollow out, connect by a hole, fasten, together. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_t_rp.html"> √ tṛp    √ tṛp, “be pleased” Present I. tarpanti E IV. tṛ́pyati etc. AV.+,-te etc. E.+ V. tṛpṇoti etc. V.B. (tṛpnoti etc. C.) VI. tṛmpáti etc. V.B.S Future Simple Future: atrapsyat B. tarpsyati, tarpiṣyati Periphrastic Future: tarpitā, tarptā, traptā Aorist √-Ao: tṛpyāsma TS Th Ao: átṛpat etc. V.B. (tṛpánt RV.) RAo: atītṛpat etc.-panta AV.+ atatarpat -s-Ao: atārpsīt, atrāpsīt -iṣ-Ao: atarpīt Perfect tatarpa etc. E. (tātṛpus -pāṇá V.) Causative tarpáyati etc. V.+,-te etc. V.+ (tarpyate etc. E.; titarpayiṣati B.S.) Desiderative títṛpsati V. titarpiṣa- Intensive tarītṛp- Verbal Nouns PPP: tṛptá AV.+ Derivatives -tarpaka C. tárpaṇa AV.+ -tṛpa RV.C. tṛprá ? V.B.S. -tarpya E. tarpaṇīya U. tṛpála RV. -tṛpsu TA. tálpa ? AV.+ -tṛp RV. tṛ́pti V.B. tā́trpi RV. tṛptí RV. tarpayitavyà B. Some accept a √ 2 tṛp “steal” for asutṛ́p V.C. and paśutṛ́p RV. Meanings tṛ́pyati v (tṛ́pyate), tṛpṇóti (tṛpnoti), tṛmpáti (tarpati), PPP taptá satiate one's self, be satisfied or content with (G, I or – ṃ); enjoy (Ab). Caus. tarpáyati, te satisfy, please, nourish; Ā refl. abhi Caus. satiate, refresh. ā be satiated or satisfied; Caus. satiate. pari Caus. satiate or refresh thoroughly. pra Caus. satiate, fill. vi be satiated or pleased. sam be satiated or satisfied with (G). Caus. satiate, refresh, gladden. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_t_r_s.html"> √ tṛṣ    √ tṛṣ, “be thirsty” Present IV. tṛ́ṣyati etc. V.B Future Simple Future: tarṣiṣyati Periphrastic Future: tarṣitā Aorist Th Ao: tṛṣat etc. AV.B., tṛṣāṇá RV RAo: atītṛṣāma etc. V.B Perfect tātṛṣús -ṣāṇá tatṛṣāṇá RV Causative tarṣáyati etc. B. (tarṣita E.+) Verbal Nouns PPP: tṛṣitá V.+, tṛṣṭá ? adj. V.; 1Abs: tṛṣitvā, tarṣitvā Derivatives tarṣa E.+ tarṣaṇa C. tṛṣ E.+ tṛṣú RV. tarṣyā́- RV. tarṣula E. tṛṣā C. tṛ́ṣṇā V.+ tṛṣyā́ V. tṛṣṇáj RV. Meanings tṛ́ṣyati v PPP tṛṣitá 1 be thirsty, be greedy, desire. Caus. tarṣáyati cause to thirst. vi thirst, languish. Caus. cause to languish. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_t_rh.html"> √ tṛh    √ tṛh, “crush” Present VI. tṛhati, tṛṃhati VII. tṛṇeḍhi tṛṇéḍhu tṛṃhanti etc. V.B. tṛṇehmi Passive tṛhyáte etc. AV Future Simple Future: tarhiṣyati, tarkṣyati Periphrastic Future: tarhitā, tarḍhā Aorist √-Ao: tṛhyāt; atarhi Th Ao: atṛham AV RAo: atatarhat, atītṛhat -iṣ-Ao: atarhīt -sa- Ao: atṛkṣat Perfect tatarha AV Causative tarhaya- Desiderative titarhiṣa- , titṛkṣa- Intensive tarītṛh- Verbal Nouns PPP: tṛḍhá RV.; 1Abs: tṛḍhvā́ AV. tarhitvā; -tárham AV Derivatives tárhaṇa V. Meanings tṛṇeḍhi v PPP tṛḍhá crush, bruise, dash to pieces. vi = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tyaj.html"> √ tyaj    √ tyaj, “forsake” Present I. tyajati etc. S.+,-te etc. E.+ Passive tyajyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: tyakṣyati -te etc. E., tyajiṣyati -te etc. E.+ Periphrastic Future: tyaktā Aorist √-Ao: tyajyāt; atyāji RAo: atityajat -s-Ao: atyākṣīt etc. E.+ Perfect tatyāja tatyaje etc. E.+ (tityā́ja RV., tityagdhi ? K.) Causative tyājayati etc. E.+ (tyājyate C.) Desiderative tityakṣa- C Intensive tātyaj- Verbal Nouns PPP: tyaktá B.+, tyajita C.; Inf: tyaktu- E.; 1Abs: tyaktvā E.+; 2Abs: -tyájya B.+ Derivatives -tyaj V.+ tyajana AVP. tyaktavya E.+ tyājaka C. -tyaja E.+ tyájas RV. tyaktṛ E.+ tyājya E.+ tyajya E.+ tyajás V. tyāgá V.+ -tyājana C. tyāgin E.+ Meanings tyajati 1 v (te), PPP tyaktá (tyajita) leave, abandon, let alone, spare, avoid, shun, dismiss, shoot off, cast away, put off, get rid of (also P. tyajyate w. I); disregard, neglect, renounce, give up; w. tanum, jīvitam, prāṇān = set aside or risk body or life, also = die. Caus. tyājayati cause to leave or abandon, deprive of (2A), expel, turn out (bahis). abhi quit. samabhi give up, renounce, risk (jīvitam). pari leave, abandon, expel, reject, put off, give up, disregard, neglect, set aside, risk (cf. S.). sam leave, abandon, reject, shun, avoid, withdraw from (A), deliver, give up, etc. (= pari). Caus. deprive of (2A). Cf. tyaktkā, nítyakta, parityakta, parityajya, saṃtyajya, saṃtyakta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_trap.html"> √ trap    √ trap, “be abashed” Present I. trapate etc. E.+,-ti etc. E Future Simple Future: trapsyate trapiṣyate Periphrastic Future: traptā trapitā Aorist √-Ao: atrapta -iṣ-Ao: atrapiṣṭa Perfect trepe Causative trapayati etc. C. trāpayati Desiderative titrapsa- , titrapiṣa- Intensive tātrap- Derivatives tṛprá ? V.B.S. trapa E.+ -trapaṇa C. trápu ? AV.+ trapā E.+ -trapaṇīya C. Meanings trapate v (trapati) become perplexed or ashamed. Caus. trapayati make perplexed or ashamed. apa & vyapa turn perplexed away. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tras.html"> √ tras    √ tras, “be terrified” Present I. trásati etc. V.+,-te etc. E IV. trasyati etc. E.+,-te etc. C Future Simple Future: trasiṣyati E Periphrastic Future: trasitā Aorist RAo: atitrasan AV -iṣ-Ao: trāsīs ŚB. atrasīt Perfect tatrāsa tatrasus etc. E.+, tresus E.+ (treṣus M1.), tatrasire E Causative trāsayati etc. AV.+,-te etc. E. (trāsyate E.) Desiderative titrasiṣa- Intensive tātrasyate JB Verbal Nouns PPP: trastá B.+;-trasas K Derivatives trasa V.+ trasara C. trāsa AV.+ trāsana E.+ trasana S. trasnu B.+ trāsaka C. trāsanīya C. trāsin E. -trāsuka B. Meanings trásati (trásate) & trasyati (trasyate) v PPP trastá tremble, quake, be afraid of (Ab, G, or I). Caus. trāsayati (te) shake, agitate, frighten, scare. apa start back, flee. ud Caus. frighten, rouse up. samud Caus. frighten, terrify. nis flee. parā Caus. frighten away. pra flee in terror. Caus. affright, scare. vi & sam tremble, fear; Caus. terrify, frighten. Cf. uttrasta, paritrasta, samutrasta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_traa.html"> √ trā    √ trā, “rescue” Present II. trā́sva trā́dhvam RV., trāti trāhi etc. E.+ IV. trā́yate etc. V.+ Passive trāyate etc. C Future Simple Future: trāsyate etc. B.+,-ti E Periphrastic Future: trātā Aorist -s-Ao: atrāsmahi ŚB. (atrāsatām ŚB., trāsate trā́sāthe -sīthām RV.) Perfect tatré V.B Verbal Nouns PPP: trāta B.+ trāṇa; Inf: trātum E.+; 1Abs: trātvā C Derivatives trā́ V.+ trāṇa U.+ trātṛ́ V.+ trā́man V.+ -tra V.+ trātavya E.+ trātra RV.C. -trā́van? AV. trayayā́yya RV. A secondary root, from √ tṛ. Meanings trā́yate trā́te (trā́ti) v PPP trāta 1 (q.v.) protect shelter, rescue from (Ab or G). pari & sam = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tru_t.html"> √ truṭ    √ truṭ, “come to pieces” Present IV. truṭyati etc. C. (truḍyeyus C.) VI. truṭati etc. C Perfect tutroṭa C Causative troṭayati etc. C Verbal Nouns truṭita C Derivatives truṭi E.+ troṭaka C. Probably a denominative formation from truṭi. Meanings truṭati & truṭyati v (truḍyati), PPP truṭita burst, break (intrans.), fall asunder. Caus. troṭayati tear, break, cut, divide. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tvak_s.html"> √ tvakṣ    √ tvakṣ, “fashion” Present I. tvakṣati II. tvakṣāṇá RV1 Future Simple Future: tvakṣiṣyati Periphrastic Future: tvakṣitā tvaṣṭā Aorist -s-Ao: atvakṣīt Perfect tatvakṣa Derivatives -tvákṣaṇa RV. tvákṣas RV. tvákṣīyas RV. tvaṣṭi C. tváṣṭṛ V.+ Compare √ takṣ. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tva_gg.html"> √ tvaṅg    √ tvaṅg, “leap” Present I. tvaṅgati etc. C Late and probably artificial. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tvac.html"> √ tvac    √ tvac, “cover” Such a root is assumed by come for tvác V.+ “skin”, and ātúc RV. “dimness”. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tvar.html"> √ tvar    √ tvar, “hasten” Present I. tvárate etc. B.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: tvariṣyate Periphrastic Future: tvaritā Aorist RAo: atitvarat E. atatvarat -iṣ-Ao: atvariṣṭa Perfect tatvare E.+ Causative tvaráyati etc. AV.+,-te etc. E. (tvaryate E.); tvāraya- C Desiderative titvariṣa- Intensive tātvarya- , totur- Verbal Nouns tvarita E.+ Derivatives tvara C. tvarā S.+ tvaraṇá AV. tvaraṇīya E. A secondary root-form √ tṛ, tur under which are here placed the derivatives with tūr- (tūrti, tūrṇa.). Meanings tvárate (tvárati) v PPP tvarita, tūrtá & tūrṇa (q.v.) hurry, hasten to (D, L, or inf). Caus. tvaráyati (te, tvarayatitarām) quicken, accelerate; snatch away. ati hasten very much. pari hasten about. pra & sam hasten, speed. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tvi_s.html"> √ tviṣ    √ tviṣ, “be stirred up” Present I. tveṣati -te II. atviṣus RV IV. tviṣyant C1 VI. atviṣanta RV Future Simple Future: tvekṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: tveṣṭā Aorist etc RAo: atitviṣat -s-Ao: atvikṣat -kṣata Perfect titviṣé etc. RV. (átitviṣanta RV.) titviṣus Causative tveṣaya- Desiderative titvikṣa- Intensive tetviṣ- Verbal Nouns PPP: tviṣitá RV.; tviṣé RV Derivatives tvíṣ V.+ tvíṣi V.B.S. tveṣín RV. tveṣátha RV. tviṣā C. tveṣá V.B. tveṣyà RV. tveṣás RV. Meanings PPP tviṣitá stir, move (trans. & intrans.); glitter, sparkle. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_tsar.html"> √ tsar    √ tsar, “approach stealthily” Present I. tsárati etc. V.B.S Future Simple Future: tsariṣyati Periphrastic Future: tsaritā Aorist -s-Ao: atsār RV -iṣ-Ao: atsāriṣam ŚB Perfect tatsāra RV Verbal Nouns -tsárya ŚB Derivatives tsarā C. tsáru V.+-tsāra V.+ tsārín V.B. Meanings tsárati v creep, sneak, steal upon. abhi & upa = S. ava sneak away. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_da_mz.html"> √ daṃś, daś    √ daṃś, daś, “bite” Present I. dáśati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ daṃśati C1 Passive daśyate etc. E Future Simple Future: daśiṣyati E. daṅkṣyati Periphrastic Future: daṃṣṭā Aorist RAo: adadaṃśat -s-Ao: adāṅkṣīt Precative: daśyāt Perfect dadaṃśus E. (dadaśvā́ṃs RV.) Causative daṃśayati etc. S.+ (daṃśita adj. E.+) Desiderative didaṅkṣa- Intensive dándaśāna RV. (dandaśayitvā C.) Verbal Nouns PPP: daṣṭá AV.+; 1Abs: daṃṣṭvā B.; 2Abs: -daśya E Derivatives daṃśa AV.+ daṃśana E.+ dáṃṣṭrā̆ V.+ daśā ? B.+ daṃśaka C. dáṃśuka B. dáṃśman AV.S. daśana E.+ -daṃśin AV. daṃṣṭṛ́ AV. daṅkṣṇú B. Meanings dáśati v (dáśate & daṃśati), PPP daṣṭá r. daṃśita (q.v.) bite. Caus. daṃśayati cause a pers. (A) to be bitten by (I). nis , pari & vi bite through. sam bite, seize with the teeth, press together. Cf. saṃdaṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_da_ms.html"> √ daṃs    √ daṃs, “be wondrous” Causative daṃsáyas RV1. Derivatives -dáṃsa RV. dáṃsas V.B. dáṃsu RV. dasmá V. daṃsánā̆ RV.S. dáṃsiṣṭha RV. dasmánt RV. dasrá V. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dak_s.html"> √ dakṣ    √ dakṣ, “be able” Present I. dákṣate etc. V.B.,-ti RV Future Simple Future: dakṣiṣyate B Periphrastic Future: dakṣitā Aorist RAo: adadakṣat B -iṣ-Ao: adakṣiṣṭa Perfect dadakṣe B Causative dakṣayati etc. B Derivatives dákṣa V.+ dákṣas V. dakṣā́yya RV. dákṣiṇa V.+ Meanings dákṣati dákṣate v P satisfy, please (D); Ā be able or strong. Caus. dakṣáyati make able or strong. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dagh.html"> √ dagh    √ dagh, “reach to” Present V. daghnuyāt B Future Simple Future: daghiṣyante JUB Aorist √-Ao: dhak dhaktam daghma daghyās RV Th Ao ? daghat B Verbal Nouns -dághas B.,-dághos ŚB Derivatives -dagh S.-daghna V.+-daghvan V.B. Meanings daghnoti v reach, attain. ati reach beyond, pass. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dad.html"> √ dad    √ dad see √ 1 dā. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dadh.html"> √ dadh    √ dadh see √ 1 dhā. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dan.html"> √ dan    √ dan, “straighten” (?) Present dán dánas RV. Very doubtful forms. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dabh.html"> √ dabh, dambh    √ dabh, dambh, “harm” Present I. dábhati etc. V.B V. dabhnoti etc. V.B Passive dabhyate RV Future Simple Future: dambhiṣyati Periphrastic Future: dambhitā Aorist √-Ao: dabhús RV RAo: adadambhat -iṣ-Ao: adambhīt. dambhiṣak S Perfect dadā́bha debhus RV.; dadámbha AV. (dadabhanta RV.) Causative dambháyati etc. V.B Desiderative dípsati etc. V.B.; dhīpsati JB. dhipsa-, didambhiṣa- Intensive dādambh- , dādabh- Verbal Nouns dabdhá V.; dabdhum B.; dambhitvā, dabdhvā; -dábhe RV Derivatives dábha V. dabdhi B.S. dābhya V.+ dambhin E.+ dábhya RV. -dabhna? AV. dambha E.+ -dámbhana V.+ dabhī́ti RV. dabhrá V.+ dambhaka C. dipsú V. dābha V.B. Meanings dambh , dábhati, dabhnoti, PPP dabdhá v harm, injure, deceive, beguile. P. suffer damage or loss. Caus. dambháyati, dábhati, dabhnoti, PPP dabdhá harm, injure, deceive, beguile. P. suffer damage or loss. Caus. dambháyate ward off, strike down. Des dípsati wish to hurt or destroy. ā hurt, injure. upa Caus. destroy, annihilate. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dam.html"> √ dam    √ dam, “control” Present IV. dā́myati ŚB Aorist -iṣ-Ao: adamīt Causative damáyati etc. V.+ Verbal Nouns dāṃtá B.+; dāṃtvā, damitvā E.;-damya E. ? Derivatives dám V.+ damaka E.+ -damatra S.+ damitṛ́ RV. dáma V.+ damin E. damana V.+ damayitṛ E. damá B. -damya E. Meanings dā́myati v PPP dāntá 1 (q.v.) be or make tame; conquer, master, control. Caus. damáyati = S. trans. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_day.html"> √ day    √ day, “share” Present I. dáyate etc. V.+, dayāmasi AV Future Simple Future: dayiṣyate Periphrastic Future: dayitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: adayiṣṭa Perfect dayām āsa C Causative dayayet C Intensive dandayya- , dādayya- Verbal Nouns dayita E.+ Derivatives dayā́ V.+ dayitnu S. A secondary form of √ 2 dā “divide”, from which it is hardly worth separating. Meanings dáyate (dáyati) v PPP dayita (q.v.) divide, allot (A or *G); possess, partake; sympathize with, love (A or G); repent. ava & nirava satisfy. vi divide, distribute; separate, destroy, be liberal with (I), i.e. impart. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_daridraa.html"> √ daridrā    √ daridrā see √ 1 drā. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dal.html"> √ dal    √ dal, “burst” Present I. dalati etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: daliṣyati -te etc. C. (adaliṣyat C.) Aorist -iṣ-Ao: adalīt C. adālīt Perfect dadāla Causative dalayati etc. C.; dālayati etc. E.+ (dalyate C., dālyate C.) Verbal Nouns dalita E.+ Derivatives dala E.+ -dāla B.+ dālana C. dāli C. dalana C. -dālaka B.+ -dālya C. dalayitṛ C. A secondary root-form from √ 1 dṛ. Meanings dalati v PPP dalita (q.v.) burst, split, open (intrans.). Caus. dālayati & dalayati cause to burst, divide, tear or drive asunder. ava burst or fly open. ud Caus. split, cleave, tear up. vi burst or fly open; tear asunder, split. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_das.html"> √ das, dās    √ das, dās, “waste” Present I. dā́sati etc. V.B.S IV. dásyati etc. V.B.S Future Simple Future: dasiṣyati, dāsiṣyati Periphrastic Future: dasitā, dāsitā Aorist Th Ao: dasat etc. V.B.S. (dásamāna ? RV.) -iṣ-Ao: dāsīt RV Perfect dadasvā́ṃs RV. dadāsa Causative dasaye TS.,-yanta RV.; dāsayati etc. AV.B Verbal Nouns dasta B.+ Derivatives dása RV. -dasvant AV. dāsá V.+ dāsanu B. -dasya V.S. dásyu V.+ -dāsin S.+ -dāsuka B. Usually classed as two roots, das and dās; dā́sati etc. only with abhi. Meanings dásyati v PPP dasta suffer want, languish. Caus. dasayate exhaust, consume. apa , upa , pra & vi be exhausted, be wanting, fail. dā́sati v w. abhi bear ill-will towards, try to harm, persecute. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dah.html"> √ dah    √ dah, “burn” Present I. dáhati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ II. dhákṣi RV IV. dahyati E Passive dahyáte etc. AV.+,-ti etc. S.+ Future Simple Future: dhakṣyáti etc. V.+,-te etc. S.+ (dhakṣyet adhakṣyam M.); dahiṣyati E.+ Periphrastic Future: dagdhā Aorist √-Ao: dahyāt M. ? RAo: adīdahat C -s-Ao: adhākṣīt etc. V.+ (adhāk V.B.S., dhákṣant dákṣant RV.) Perfect dadā́ha etc. B.+, dehe C Causative dāhayati etc. E.+ (dāhyate U.) Desiderative didhakṣati etc. E.+,-te etc. E.; dhī́kṣate ŚB Intensive dandahīti etc. C., dandahyate etc. C Verbal Nouns PPP: dagdhá V.+; Inf: dágdhum B.+,-dhos B.; 1Abs: dagdhvā́ V.+; 2Abs: -dáhya B.+;-dáhas B.;-dāham C Derivatives dah V.S. dakṣī RV. -dāgha AV. dāhana E. dahati E. dákṣu RV. dāha AV.+ dā́huka B.S. dáhana AV.+ dhákṣu RV. dāhaka C. didhakṣā E.+ -dagdhavya E. dakṣús RV. dāhin S.+ didhakṣu E.+ dagdhṛ V.+ dāhya E.+ Meanings dáhatí (dáhate) v PPP dagdhá (q.v.) burn, inflame (l. & f.), consume, destroy. P. dahyáte (ti) be burnt, burn (intrans.), suffer, pine. Caus. dāhayati (cause to) burn. Des didhakṣate be about to burn or destroy. Int dandahīti & dandagdhi burn completely (trans.); dandahyate the same (trans. & intrans.). ati burn over, dry up. anu burn over again, burn thoroughly. upa kindle. ni burn down, P. intrans. nis & vinis burn out, destroy by fire. pari burn round (trans.); P. burn, glow. pra burn, consume, destroy. prati burn against. vi burn out, damage or consume by fire; P. be burnt or inflamed, glow. sam P burn or destroy (together); P. be burnt or tortured. Cf. vídagdha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_daa.html"> √ 1 dā, dad    √ 1 dā, dad, “give” Present I. dádati -te etc. V.+ (dadīyam U., dadāyant U.) II. dā́ti dātu RV.; admi E.+ III. dádāti dátte etc. V.+ (dehí V.+, daddhí V.) IV. dāyamāna M Passive dīyáte etc. V.+; dadyámāna RV Future Simple Future: dāsyáti etc. AV.+ (adāsyat M.),-te etc. B.+; dadiṣye K Periphrastic Future: dātā́ etc. B.E. daditā Aorist √-Ao: ádāt etc. V.+, deyām RV.; adi MS., adithās adita adimahi B., dīṣva B.; dāyi V.B. adādi Th Ao: ā́dat etc. V.B RAo: adīdadat -s-Ao: adiṣi adiṣata V.B.C. (dāsat dā́sathas RV.; deṣam deṣma B.S.) dāsīṣṭa -iṣ-Ao: adadiṣṭa SV Perfect dadaú dadé etc. V.+ (dadātha dadrire RV.; dadivā́ṃs dadāvā́ṃs AV., dadvā́ṃs RV.) dadade Causative dāpayati etc. AV.+ adīdapat Desiderative dítsati etc. V.+,-te etc. C.; dídāsant RV., didāsitha B.S. didadiṣa- Intensive dādā- , dedīya-, dādad- Verbal Nouns PPP:-dāta RV., dattá V.+,-tta V.+,-dita E.+ dadita; Inf: dā́tum V.+-tave V.,-tavaí RV.,-tos V.B.; 1Abs: dattvā́ AV.+,-tvā́ya RV.; 2Abs: -dā́ya V.+,-dádya AV.;-dā́m B.,-daí RV.; dāváne RV.;-dā́yam B.+ Derivatives dā́ ,-da V.+ dāyá V.+ -di JB.+ dadí V. dā́ti V. dāyaka E.+ díya RV. ditsā C. -tti V.B. dāyin AV.+ déṣṭha RV. ditsú V.+ dātavya B.+ -dā́van V.S. deṣṇá V.+ diditsu M. dātṛ V.+ dāván RV. -dád AV. dāpin C. dātrá ? V.B. dā́nu ? V. -dada C. -dāpya S.C. dā́na V.+ -déya n V.B. datti C. -dāpana S. dāná ? RV. déya gdve. V.+ dátra ? V. dāpanīya C. dā́man RV.E. -dās ? V.+ dāda E. dāpayitavya C. dāmán RV. -das V.B. daditṛ́ VS. -dāpayitṛ B. Meanings dádāti dátte dádati dádate (dā́ti) (dadmi) v PPP dattá 1 (q.v.) give, grant, bestow, impart (w. A or partit. G of th., G or L of pers.), give in marriage (bhāryām), give back, restore (punar); pay (ṛṇam); open *(dvāram); deliver up, hand over (~ haste); make over, surrender; concede, allow, permit; give away, sell (I of price); offer, sacrifice; communicate, teach, pronounce; put in or on, turn to (L); w. pāvakam set fire to (L); w. agnīn burn (D); do, make, cause, perform, bring about. Ā receive, carry, bear, keep, guard from (Ab). Caus. dāpayati cause to give, grant, etc. (1 or 2A), make pay (2A), demand from (Ab); put in or on (L).* Des ditsati, te, dídāsati wish or be ready to give. anu concede, yield, remit, grant, admit. abhi give. ā Ā (P) accept, receive, conceive (garbham); take, grasp, seize, rob; take or separate from (Ab); take along with one's self, carry off; put on, don; take = eat, gnaw (daśanais); perceive, comprehend, mark; keep, retain (in the memory); undertake, begin. apā Ā take off. abhyā Ā (P) appropriate, put on, take up (vākyam). upā Ā accept, receive, acquire, appropriate, take, seize, choose, employ, mention; undertake, begin. samupā Ā obtain, get, take, rob, put on, employ. pratyā Ā receive or take oack, recall, repeat. vyā Ā (~ mukham) open the mouth, gape. samā P give, restore; Ā take (together), seize, grasp, gather, collect; comprehend, understand, observe, take to heart; undertake, begin. ud add, grant, give. parā deliver, surrender, give up; exchange for (D), barter. pari surrender, deliver up; intrust, deposit with or in (D, L, or G); grant, bestow. pra P (Ā) give up, deliver, present, offer, give in marriage (bhāryām); pay, discharge (a debt), restore, sell (w. I of price); teach, communicate, impart; grant, permit; put in set (fire) to (L). saṃpra give up, deliver, concede, grant, impart, teach, communicate. prati restore, return, give. vi distribute. sam give (together), grant, concede; Ā P. meet together. Cf. ātta ādā́ya, udātta, upātta, upādāya, párītta, prátta, vyātta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_daa.html"> √ 2 dā    √ 2 dā, “divide, share” Present I. dā́ti etc. V.B.S VI. ? dyáti etc. AV.B.S Passive dīyate etc. AV.+ Future Simple Future: dāsyati S Periphrastic Future: dātā Aorist √-Ao: adāt, deyāt; adimahi B. (adīm- VS.K.) -s-Ao: diṣīya RV Perfect dadire B Causative dāpayīta S Desiderative ditsa- , didāsa-, dīdāṃsa- Intensive dādā- , dedi- Verbal Nouns PPP: diná V.B., dita C., dāta, -tta B.+; 2Abs: -dāya B.+,-ditya ? C Derivatives -tti B. dā́tṛ RV.C. -dā́na AV.B.S. dāyá ? RV. dā́tu RV. dā́tra RV. -dānīya B.S. díti ? RV. -dātavya C. dāná ? RV. dā́nu V. -deya C. A form of this root is √ day, given above separately. Meanings dā́ti dyáti v PPP diná 3 & dita cut, mow. ava cut off, divide (esp. the sacrif. cake). nis distribute, among (2A). samava cut in pieces and collect them. ā , vi & sam cut up, bruise, crush. Cf. ávatta, samávatta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_3_daa.html"> √ 3 dā, di    √ 3 dā, di, “bind” Present II ? dīṣva VS VI ? dyati etc. V.B Aorist -iṣ-Ao: adiṣi AV. ? Verbal Nouns dita V.+; -dāya S.+ Derivatives -dātṛ RV.C. dā́man V.+ -dāya C. díti ? V.+ -dā́na V.+ dāmán RV. -di AV. dīná ? V.+ Not recognized by the native grammarians as separate from the preceding, and of somewhat doubtful character. Meanings dyáti v PPP dita 4 (only – ṃ) bind. ā & ni tie, fetter. vi loosen. sam bind together, fasten, tie. Cf. nídita, sádita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_4_daa.html"> √ 4 dā    √ 4 dā, “clear” Present IV ? dāyamāna C1 Passive dāya- Future Simple Future: dāsyati Periphrastic Future: dātā Aorist -s-Ao: adāsīt; Precative: dāyāt Perfect dadau Causative dāpaya- Desiderative didāsa- Intensive dādā- Verbal Nouns PPP: dāta TA.E.+ Derivatives -dāna C. Only with ava; certainly no separate root, and probably a speciallzation of meaning of the participle of √ 2 dā. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_daaz.html"> √ dāś    √ dāś, “make offering” Present I. dā́śati etc. V II. dāṣṭi RV V. dāśnóti RV Future Simple Future: dāśiṣyati Periphrastic Future: dāśitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: adāśīt Perfect dadā́śa etc. V. (dádāśati -śas -śat RV.; dadāśvā́ṃs RV.B., dāśvā́ṃs V., dāśivā́ṃs SV.) Causative adāśayat ŚB1 Desiderative didāśiṣa- Intensive dādāś- Derivatives dā́ś V. -dā́śa AV.+ dāśú V. dā́śuri V. Meanings dā́śati dāṣṭi & dāśnóti 1 v make offering, sacrifice, grant, bestow, dedicate, serve a god (D) with (I), be pious or religious. Caus. dāśayati offer. Cf. dāśvás. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_daas.html"> √ dās    √ dās see √ das. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_div.html"> √ div    √ div, “play” see √ 1 dīv. No root √ div “shine” exists as such in the language, except fo far as it may be inferable from the noun dív or dyú V.+, divít RV., and the (in that case, secondary) root dyut. With all these the root dīv “play” has nothing to do. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_diz.html"> √ diś    √ diś, “point” Present III. (Pf ?) dídeśati dídeṣṭu etc. didiṣṭa RV IV. diśyati M1 VI. diśáti etc. V.+,-te etc. RV.E.+ Passive diśyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: dekṣyati etc. S.+,-te C Periphrastic Future: deṣṭā Aorist RAo: adīdiśat -s-Ao: adikṣi ádiṣṭa RV -sa- Ao: adikṣat ŚB.C Perfect didéśa etc. AV.+, didiśe C Causative deśayati etc. E.+,-te C Desiderative didikṣati C Intensive dédiśat etc. dédiṣṭe etc. RV., dediśyate AV.VS Verbal Nouns PPP: diṣṭá V.+; Inf: deṣṭum E.+; 2Abs: -díśya B.+;-díśe RV Derivatives díś V.+ deśaka C. -déśana B.+ deṣṭṛ V.+ diṣṭi V.+ deśin S.+ deśanā C. deṣṭrá RV. deśá AV.+ deśya AV.+ deṣṭavya E.+ -didikṣā C. -didikṣu C. Meanings dídeṣṭi diśáti dídeṣṭi diśáte v PPP diṣṭá 1 (q.v.) point out, show, produce (a witness); assign, grant, bestow; order, command, bid (Inf). Caus. deśayati, te show, assign, direct, bid. Int dédiṣṭe exhibit, show, bid, order or direct urgently; dediśyate show or prove one's self. ati assign, transfer, extend to (G). anu point at (A), direct, bid, assign. samanu assign. apa the same; indicate, state, denounce; feign, pretend. vyapa designate, name; feign, pretend. ā aim at, menace, challenge (A), assign, announce, teach, designate, term; foretell, prophesy of a pers. (A, P. w. N); direct, order, appoint to (L, D, Inf, or artham). Caus. indicate, show. upā assign, give in marriage to (G); announce, tell. pratyā direct, order, recommend; invite, summon; reject, despise; vanquish, surpass. vyā assign or distribute (separately); explain, indicate, teach; direct, order, appoint to (L, D, or ~ prati); foretell, prophesy of a pers. (A, P. w. N). samā assign, impart, communicate (D or G); teach, designate, name (2A); direct, appoint to (D, Inf, or artham), also = Caus. order, command (absol.). ud stretch out towards (A); indicate, explain, teach, designate as, mean by (2A), predict or prophesy of (A); point out i.e. propose or offer as (2A). samud mention, enumerate; designate, name (2A). upa point to (A), show; indicate, explain, mention, speak of (A); advise, recommend; inform, instruct, teach (2A); command, rule over (A). pratyupa teach in return (2A). samupa point to (A), teach, show (2A). nis point to (A), assign, destine, designate, name, regard as, take for (2A); mention, proclaim, predict; advise, suggest (2A). abhinis name, designate (2A); settle, determine. vinis assign, destine for (L); indicate, proclaim; designate, name (2A); resolve, determine; appoint to, charge with (L). pari indicate, state. pra the same + announce, proclaim, direct, order; assign, grant, impart. saṃpra indicate, designate, state. sam assign, destine for; direct, instruct, order; appoint to, charge with (2A). pratisam give a pers. (A) a commission (in return) to (G); direct, command. Cf. uddiśya, nirādiṣṭa, samuddiśya. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dih.html"> √ dih    √ dih, “smear” Present II. degdhi dihanti ádihan etc. V.+ (déhat RV.) digdhe Passive dihyate etc. C Future Simple Future: dhekṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: degdhā Aorist √-Ao: adehi RAo: adīdihat -s-Ao: adigdha -sa- Ao: adhikṣus JB. adhi- kṣat -ṣata Perfect didihe E. dideha Causative dehayati -te E.+ Desiderative didhikṣa- Intensive dedih- Verbal Nouns PPP: digdhá AV.+; 2Abs: -dihya S.+ Derivatives -dih V.S. -degha B. dehī́ RV. -dehya C. deha B.+ dehikā C. dehalī S.+ Meanings dégdhi v PPP digdhá (q.v.) anoint, smear. abhi wreath, also = S. ava , pari , pra = S. sam the same; Ā P. be doubtful or dubious; P. also be confounded with (I). Caus. confound, perplex, Ā be uncertain. Cf. ādigdha, upadigdha, nídigdha, saṃdigdha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_dii.html"> √ 1 dī    √ 1 dī, “fly” Present IV. dī́yati etc. RV., dī́yase SV Intensive dédīyitavaí ŚB Represented later by √ ḍī. From it may possibly come didyú V.B. Meanings dī́yati dī́yate 1 v fly. nis fly away. pari fly about. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_dii.html"> √ 2 dī, dīdī    √ 2 dī, dīdī, “shine” Present dīdyati (3p.) etc. ádīdet etc. dīdye etc. V.B.S. (dī́dayat RV., dīdāyat dīdayante AV., dīdihí V.B.S., didīhí RV.; dīdyāsam B.S.) Perfect dīdā́ya V.B.S. (dīdaya ŚB.S., dīdétha dīdiyus RV.; dīdivā́ṃs V.B.; dīdáyasi etc. dīdáyat etc. V.B.; dīdidāya ? AŚS.; dīdidāsi dīdyasva S Derivatives -dīti RV.-dīditi RV. dī́di- RV. dī́divi RV. dīdhiti S.+ Compare √ dīp. Some confusion of forms is made between dīdī and dīdhī. Meanings 3 pl. dīdyati intrans. shine, gleam, be bright or visible, please; trans. bestow by shining (D or L of pers., A of th.). abhi bestow by shining. ā shine upon. ni = S. trans. pra shine forth. sam shine together, also = S. trans. Cf. dī́dyat, dī́dyāna, dīdivás. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_diik_s.html"> √ dīkṣ    √ dīkṣ, “be consecrated” Present I. dīkṣate etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: dīkṣiṣyáte etc. B.+ Periphrastic Future: dīkṣitā Aorist RAo: adidīkṣas B -iṣ-Ao: adīkṣiṣṭa etc. B Perfect didīkṣé etc. B., didīkṣus PB.C Causative dīkṣayati etc. B.+,-te E. (dīkṣāpaya E.) Desiderative didīkṣiṣate etc. B Verbal Nouns PPP: dīkṣitá AV.+; 1Abs: dīkṣitvā́ B.U.; 2Abs: -dīkṣya S Derivatives dīkṣā́ AV.+ dīkṣaka C. (n. pr.) dīkṣaṇa S.+ dīkṣayitṛ B. BR. suggest a derivation from √ dakṣ. Meanings dī́kṣate v PPP dīkṣitá (q.v.) be consecrated. Caus. dīkṣáyati, te consecrate. Des didīkṣiṣate wish to be consecrated. abhi = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_diidhii.html"> √ dīdhī    √ dīdhī see √ dhī. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_diip.html"> √ dīp    √ dīp, “shine” Present IV. dī́pyate etc. AV.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: dīpiṣyate Periphrastic Future: dīpitā Aorist √-Ao: adīpi RAo: adidīpat etc. RV.C.; adīdipat etc. B.E -iṣ-Ao: adīpiṣṭa Perfect didīpe C Causative dīpáyati etc. V.+,-te etc. S.E. (dīpyáte TB.E.) Desiderative didīpiṣa- Intensive dedīpyate etc. E.+ (-yantīm E.) Verbal Nouns PPP: dīpta U.+ Derivatives dīpa U.S.+ dīpaka E.+ dīpana S.+ dī́pti B.+ dīpin C. dīpra C. Probably related with √ 2 dī. Meanings dī́pyate dīpyáte (dīpyati), PPP dīpta (q.v.) blaze, flame, shine, be brilliant (l. & f.). Caus. dīpáyati, te kindle, inflame, illuminate; excite, raise. Int dedīpyate blaze brightly, be radiant. ā Caus. inflame, kindle. ud flame up, burn; Caus. = S. Caus. upa Caus. kindle, set fire to (A). pra flame forth. burn. Caus. kindle, inflame, rouse. vi blaze, flame; Caus. kindle, illuminate. sam flame; Caus. inflame, excite. Cf. atidīpta, ādīptapradīpta, sádīpta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_diiv.html"> √ dīv    √ dīv, “play” Present IV. dī́vyati etc. V.+,-te etc. B.+ (divyati etc. M. ?) Future Simple Future: deviṣyati etc. E.+ (adeviṣyat M.) Periphrastic Future: devitā Aorist RAo: adīdivat -iṣ-Ao: adevīt etc. E Perfect didéva AV Causative devayati etc. C Desiderative dideviṣa- , dudyūṣa-; dudyūṣaya- Intensive dedīv- Verbal Nouns PPP: dyūtá AV.+ dyūna; Inf: devitum E.+; 1Abs: devitvā, dyūtvā; 2Abs: -dī́vya RV Derivatives dī́v , dyū́ V. dīvitṛ ? devin AV.+ devitṛ E.+ -dī́van V. -deva B. devitavya E. -dyūtyà RV. dīvana C. dévana V.+ Proper form, dīū; and it has nothing to do with the so-called root div “shine”, which is diu. Meanings dīvyati dīvyate v PPP dyūtá 1 (q.v.) play at dice (akṣais or *akṣān), gamble with (I) for (A, I, D, or *G). sport, joke; trifle with, mock, rally (A). Caus. devayati cause to play. ati play higher; put to stake. prati play against (A); *put to stake (G or A). vi play for (A), joke, sport. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_diiv.html"> √ 2 dīv (dev)    √ 2 dīv (dev), “lament” Present I. devati E.+-te Future Simple Future: deviṣyate Periphrastic Future: devitā Aorist Th Ao: adidevat -iṣ-Ao: adeviṣṭa Perfect dideva Causative devayati etc. E.+,-te E.+ Verbal Nouns dyūna B.+; devitum E Derivatives -deva E.-devaka C.-devin E.-devana C. Only with pari (unless in ādyūna); hence perhaps a peculiar specialization of meaning of √ 1 dīv (paridyūna “played out” ?). At any rate, rather dīv than div, on account of the long ū in dyūna. Meanings devati devate v PPP dyūna 2 (q.v.) lament, be distressed. pari (P & Ā) the same; Caus. paridevayati, te lament, deplore. Cf. ādyūna, paridevita, páridyūna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_du.html"> √ du, dū    √ du, dū, “burn” Present V. dunóti etc. AV.+ dunvasva M Passive dūyate etc. U.S.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: doṣyati Periphrastic Future: dotā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: adauṣīt Precative: dūyāt Perfect dudāva Causative dāvayati C Desiderative dudūṣa- Intensive dodu- Verbal Nouns PPP: dūná AV.+, duta AA. ? C1 Derivatives dava C. davathu C. dāvá AV.+ dūyana C. -davyà B.S. davathu C. -dāvyà AV.B. doman AV. For the form daviṣāṇi RV., BR. assume a √ 2 du = √ 1 dīv “play”. Meanings dunóti (dunvate) v PPP dūná 1 q.v. (& duta) burn, grieve (trans. & intrans.); P. dūyate (ti) only intrans. Caus. dāvayati = S. trans. abhi burn (trans.). ā Ā grieve, be afflicted. pari burn violently (intrans.), be distressed. pra burn (intrans.), vex, afflict. vi burn, destroy; Ā be distressed. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dudh.html"> √ dudh    √ dudh, “stir up” Present dódhat V Verbal Nouns PPP: dúdhita RV Derivatives dúdhi RV. dudhrá RV. dodhaka ? C. Probably a reduplicated form of √ dhū. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dul.html"> √ dul    √ dul, “raise” Causative dolayati etc. C Derivatives dulā́ ? TS. dola E.+ Doubtless another form of √ tul; as verb, denominative of dola. Meanings dolayati v PPP lita raise, swing. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_du_s.html"> √ duṣ    √ duṣ, “spoil” Present IV. duṣyati etc. B.+,-te etc. E.+ (dūṣyant C1.) Future Simple Future: dokṣyati Periphrastic Future: doṣṭā Aorist Th Ao: duṣat B RAo: adūduṣat etc. V -iṣ-Ao: doṣiṣtam ŚB Perfect dudoṣa Causative dūṣayati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ (dūṣyate etc. E.+) doṣayati Desiderative dudukṣa- Intensive doduṣ- Verbal Nouns PPP: duṣṭa S.+ Derivatives dus- V.+ dūṣin E.+ doṣa U.S.+ doṣya MS. dúṣṭi AV.C. dūṣya E.+ doṣā́ V.+ doṣás AV. dūṣa E.+ dū́ṣaṇa AV.+ doṣin C. -dūṣayitṛ C. dūṣaka E.+ dū́ṣi AV. Meanings duṣyati (duṣyate) v PPP duṣṭa 2 (q.v.) be or become bad, corrupted, defiled, impure; sin be guilty. Caus. duṣayati q.v. pra get worse, be spoiled or contaminated, do amiss, sin against (prati). vi act improperly, commit a sin. sam be polluted. Cf. praduṣṭa, vipraduṣṭa, saṃduṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_duh.html"> √ duh    √ duh, “milk, derive” Present II. dógdhi duhánti etc. V.+, dugdhé duháte etc. V.+ (duhé 3s. V.B., duhaté RV., duhrate -hré V.B.; dúhāna V., duhāná dúghāna RV.; duhā́m 3s. V.B., duhrā́m duhratām 3p. AV., dhuṅgdhvam AŚS.; dohat dóhate etc. RV.; duhīyát -yán RV.; duhús RV., áduhan B.,-hran AV.B.) IV. duhyati etc. C.,-te M VI. duhet etc. E.+, aduhat V.B.E.+ Passive duhyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: dhokṣyate C Periphrastic Future: dogdhā Aorist √-Ao: adohi RAo: adūduhat etc. C -s-Ao: adugdha, ádhukṣata (3p.) RV., dhukṣīmáhi B -sa- Ao: ádhukṣat -ṣata etc. V.+ (dhukṣásva adukṣat etc. dukṣata RV.) Perfect dudóha duduhé etc. V.+ (dudóhitha V.+, duduhré V.B.,-hrire V.; dudūhus C.) Causative doháyati etc. B.+,-te S. (dohyáte B.) Desiderative dudhukṣati C. (dúdukṣati RV.) Intensive doduh- Verbal Nouns PPP: dugdhá V.+; Inf: dogdhum E., dógdhos B.; 1Abs: dugdhvā B.+; duhádhyai RV.; doháse RV.; 2Abs: -doham C Derivatives -duh V.+ dóha V.+ dóhana B.+ dogdhavya B.E. -dugh S. dógha RV. dohána RV. dogdhṛ́ AV.+ -duha E. -dohaka C. dóhas V.B.S. dogdhra S. dúgha V. -dohin E. dohás RV. dudhukṣu E. duhitṛ́ V.+ dohya C. Meanings dógdhi dugdhé 1 v (duháti, duháte, dóhati, dóhate, duhyati, duhyate), PPP dugdhá (q.v.) milk, i.g. extract, derive, draw the good out of (2A); yield, grant, bestow (mostly Ā). Caus. doháyati, te cause to milk, also = S. milk, extrP Des dúdukṣati & dudhukṣati with to milk. nis P Ā milk out, extrP vipra P suck out. vi Ā milk out, empty. sam P Ā milk or suck (together); Ā yield or grant together. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_duu.html"> √ dū    √ dū see √ du. Another root dū seems inferable from the Derivatives dáviṣṭha V. dávīyas V.B. dūtá V.+ dūrá V.+ dū́r ? ŚB. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_d_r.html"> √ 1 dṛ    √ 1 dṛ, “pierce, split” Present II. dárṣi adar dárt RV IX. dṛnīyā́t ŚB Passive dīryáte etc. B.+, dīryati etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: darī̆ṣyati Periphrastic Future: darī̆tā Aorist √-Ao: dīryāt C Th Ao: adarat RAo: adīdarat etc. E.+ adadarat -s-Ao: darṣase dárṣat darṣate darṣiṣṭa RV -iṣ-Ao: adārīt Perfect dadā́ra etc. V.+ (dadṛvā́ṃs RV.) dadaritha dadaratus dadratus, dadre S.+ Causative dārayati etc. B.+,-te etc. C. (dāryate etc. E.+); daráyati etc. RV.C Desiderative didarī̆ṣa- ,didīrṣa- Intensive dárdṛ- RV.TS. (dardirat adardirus RV.); dādṛhí RV. dedīrya- Verbal Nouns PPP: dīrṇá B.+, dṛta R.; 2Abs: -dī́rya B.+;-dāram C Derivatives dara V.+ dartnú RV. dāraṇa E.+ dṛ́ti V.+ daraṇa S.+ darmán RV.S. -dāri E.+ dṛván ? VS. -daraṇīya C. darmá RV. dārú RV. drá ? AV. -dari RV.C. dāra AV.+ dāruṇá ? B.+ -driya RV. dárīman RV. -dāraka E.+ -dir ŚB. dadru C. dartṛ RV. dārin V.+ durá ? RV. -dardira RV. Compare √ dal. Meanings dṛṇā́ti 1 v (dárṣi), PPP dīrṇá burst, break asunder, split open (trans. & intrans.); P. dīryáte (ti) the same (intrans.). Caus. daráyati & dārayati (te) = S. trans. + drive asunder, disperse, scatter. Int. (dardṛ- & dādṛ-) = S. trans. ava S. & Caus. split, break, burst asunder (trans.); P. the same (intrans.). ā split, go asunder; also = Int. rend, break, open, make accessible. nis S. & Caus. rend, split, cleave. pari Ā rend on all sides, P. peel or drop off on all sides (skin). pra break, tear; P. split, open, burst asunder (intrans.). vi split, tear, rend asunder, open; P. burst, go asunder; Caus. rend or saw in pieces, break through, open, drive asunder, chase away; Int. split, open (trans.). Cf. avadīrṇa, páridīrṇa, vidīrṇa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_d_r.html"> √ 2 dṛ    √ 2 dṛ, “heed” Passive driyáte etc. B.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: dariṣyate Periphrastic Future: dartā Aorist √-Ao: adṛthās etc. B RAo: adīdarat -s-Ao: dṛḍhvam B Perfect dadre Causative dāraya- Desiderative didariṣa- Intensive dardṛ- , dedrīya- Verbal Nouns PPP: dṛta , E.+; 2Abs: -dṛ́tya B.+ Derivatives -dara U.? C. -daraṇa S.+ -dartavya C. -duri RV. -darin C. -daraṇīya C. -dāra V.B.S. -dṛtya B. Only with prefix ā, and with passive present-system, suggesting a specialization from √ 1 dṛ. Meanings driyáte v w. ā , ādriyate (ti), PPP ādṛta 2 (q.v.) regard, respect, mind (w. A or Inf); also w. pass. mg. – atyā have much regard or consideration. pratyā be regardful towards (A). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_d_rp.html"> √ dṛp    √ dṛp, “rave” Present I. darpati S IV. dṛpyati etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: drapsyati ŚB., darpiṣyati JB Periphrastic Future: draptā, darptā, darpitā Aorist Th Ao: adṛpat B -s-Ao: adrāpsīt, adārpsīt -iṣ-Ao: adarpīt Perfect dadarpa Causative darpayati etc. E.+ Verbal Nouns dṛpta V.+, dṛpita RV Derivatives darpa E.+ darpaka C. darpin C. darpaṇa E.+-dṛpti RV. Meanings dṛpyati (darpati) v PPP dṛpta rave, be foolish, insolent, or proud. Caus. darpayati, PPP darpita make mad, foolish, etc. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_d_rbh.html"> √ dṛbh    √ dṛbh, “bunch” Present I. dṛbhmas ? B VI. dṛbháti etc. B Causative darbhita C Verbal Nouns dṛbdha B.+ Derivatives darbhá V.+ dṛ́bhīka ? RV. dṛbdhi ? darbhaṇa S. ? Meanings dṛbháti v bunch, make into tufts, string together, connect. sam connect, compose, write. Cf. saṃdṛbdha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_d_rz.html"> √ dṛś    √ dṛś, “see” Present IV. paśyati etc., see. √ 1 paś. Passive dṛśyáte etc. V.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: drakṣyáti etc. B.+,-te etc. E.+ Periphrastic Future: draṣṭā etc. E Aorist √-Ao: adarśam etc. B.+ (adarśma TS., aḍśma JB., adarśus B.; adarśas -śat B.S.; darśati etc. V., dárśat etc. V.B.), ádṛśan V.B. (adṛśram dṛśāná dṛ́śāna RV.), ádarśi dárśi V Th Ao: dṛśan V., ádṛśàn B., dṛśéyam etc. V.B RAo: adīdṛśat etc. B.+ adadarśat -s-Ao: adrākṣīt etc. B.+ (ádrāk B.), adṛkṣata RV. (dṛ́kṣase RV.) drakṣīran -sa- Ao: dṛkṣam K Perfect dadárśa dadṛśé etc. V.+ (dádṛśe dádṛśre dádṛśāna RV., dadṛśrām AV.,-śrire TB., dadṛśivāṃs U., darśivāṃs E.+) dadarśitha dadraṣṭha Causative darśáyati etc. AV.+,-te etc. S.+ (didarśayiṣa- S.+) Desiderative dídṛkṣate etc. V.+,-ti E Intensive darīdṛśyate C. dardṛś- Verbal Nouns PPP: dṛṣṭá V.+; Inf: dráṣṭum AV.+; 1Abs: dṛṣṭvā́ AV.+,-ṭvā́ya RV.; 2Abs: -dṛ́śya V.+; dṛśé V.B.; dṛśáye V.;-darśam C Derivatives dárśa V.+ darśanī́ya B.+ dṛśīkú B.S. draṣṭṛ́ AV.+ darśá AV.+ dṛ́ś V.+ dṛśénya RV. -dreśya U. darśaka E.+ -dṛ́śa V.+ dṛ́ṣṭi V.+ didṛkṣā E.+ -darśin E.+ dṛ́śya V.+ -dṛśna TS. didṛ́kṣu V.+ dárśya RV. dṛśatí RV. -dṛśvan. C. didṛkṣéya RV. darśatá V.B. dṛśí V.+ -dṛkṣa B.+ didṛkṣénya V.B. dárśana V.+ dṛśīka V. draṣṭavyà B.+ darśayitṛ E.+ Meanings (Pr, cf. √ paś), PPP dṛṣṭá (q.v.) see, behold, know by (I); see with the mind, notice, observe, try, examine; find out, invent (esp. a sacred song). P. Ā dṛśyáte (ti) be seen or visible, appear or be regarded as, pass for (N); be found, occur. Caus. darśáyati cause a pers. (A, G, D, or *I) to see (A), show, w. ātmānam one's self, i.e. appear, pretend to be; produce, point out, make known as or prove to be (2A); – PPP darśitam (impers.) appearance has been made by (I).* Des dídṛkṣate (ti) desire or like to see. anu look at (A), behold, see (manasā with the mind); P. Ā be seen, appear; Caus. cause to see, teach, show (2A). abhi behold, see; P. be seen, appear; Caus. cause to see, show, betray. ā Ā appear; Caus. show. ud Caus. PPP uddarśitam = darśitam (v.S.). upa look on, notice, observe; P.Ā be visible, appear; Caus. cause to see, show, explain; exhibit, pretend, feign. ni Caus. cause to see, show, point out, explain, teach, proclaim. pari see = visit; behold, notice, know, understand, find out; P. be visible, appear; Caus. show, explain. pra P. Ā be visible, appear; Caus. make visible, show, point out, make known or clear, explain, teach. saṃpra behold; P. be seen, appear; Caus. cause to see, show, ātmānam pretend to be (Adv in vat), point out etc. = prec. prati behold, notice; P. Ā be seen or visible, appear as (N); Caus. cause to see, show. vi P. Ā be clearly visible, come forth, appear; Caus. = prec. sam P Ā behold, observe; P. Ā be seen or appear (together), resemble; Caus. cause to see, make manifest, show; w. ātmānam etc. = saṃpra Caus. Cf. abhyuddṛṣṭa, uddṛṣṭa, saṃdṛṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_d_rh.html"> √ dṛh, dṛṃh    √ dṛh, dṛṃh, “make firm” Present I. dṛ́ṃhati etc. -te etc. V.B darhati IV. dṛ́hya dṛ́hyasva RV VI. dṛṃhántam AV., dṛṃhéthe RV Future Simple Future: darhiṣyati, dṛṃhiṣyati Periphrastic Future: darhitā, dṛṃhitā Aorist RAo: adadarhat, adīdṛhat -iṣ-Ao: adṛṃhīt etc. B. adarhīt Perfect dadarha , dadṛṃha dādṛhāṃá adadṛhanta RV Causative darhaya- ; dṛṃhayati etc. V.S Desiderative didarhiṣa- , didṛṃhyiṣa- Intensive darīdṛh- , dardṛh-; darīdṛṃh-, dardṛṃh- Verbal Nouns PPP: dṛḍhá V.+ Derivatives dṛh B.+ -dṛṃha AV. dṛṃhitṛ́ . V.B. dṛ́ṃhaṇa AV.B.S. drahyát ? RV. Divided by the Hindu grammarians into two roots, dṛṃh “fix”, and dṛh “grow”, from the latter of which are then derived dīrghá V.+ and the related words drā́ghīyas V.B.S., drā́ghiṣṭha RV., drāghmán V.B., drāghimán B. (drāghuyā́ TS.). Meanings (dṛṃh) dṛṃheti v PPP dṛḍhá (q.v.) make or be firm; Ā dṛ́hate or dṛ́hyati, te only intrans. Caus. dṛṃhayati, PPP dṛṃhitá (q.v.) make firm, fortify, fix; m. hold fast, be firm. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dev.html"> √ dev    √ dev see √ 2 dīv. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dyu.html"> √ dyu    √ dyu, “attack” Sāyaṇa has once pra dyauti, apparently an artificial formation, on the authority of the occurrence of a root √ dyu in the Dhātupāṭha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dyut.html"> √ dyut    √ dyut, “shine” Present I. dyótate etc. V.+,-te etc. E Future Simple Future: dyotiṣyati B Periphrastic Future: dyotitā Aorist √-Ao: dyutant- dyutāná V.B., dyútāna RV Th Ao: adyutat etc. B.+ RAo: ádidyutat etc. V.B -s-Ao: ádyaut dyaut V.B -iṣ-Ao: adyotiṣṭa Perfect didyute etc. V.+, didyóta AV., didyutus TS Causative dyotayati etc. V.+ (dyotyate C.); dyutayanta RV Desiderative didyutiṣa- , didyotiṣa- Intensive dávidyut- V.B. dedyut- Verbal Nouns PPP: dyuttá AV.ŚB. dyutita; 1Abs: dyutitvā, dyotitvā; 2Abs: -dyutya AB Derivatives dyút V.+ dyota AV.+ dyótana V.+ -dyótman RV. -dyuta E. dyotaka C. dyotaná RV. didyút V.B. dyuti E.+ dyotin C. dyotaní V. -dyotayitavya C. dyotya C. dyotis C. Compare √ jyut and √ div. BR. set off a few of the forms to a √ 2 dyut “break”. Meanings dyótate (dyótati) v PPP dyuttá 1 shine, beam, twinkle, glitter. Caus. dyotayati, PPP dyotita make brilliant, illuminate, make clear or manifest. Int dávidyutati (3 pl.) shine bright. abhi Caus. illuminate, irradiate. ud shine forth; Caus. illuminate; Int. shine intensely. pra begin to shine; Caus. irradiate. vi beam, glitter, shine forth (impers. vídyotate it lightens), also = Caus. illumine, irradiate. sam shine together, emulate in shining. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dram.html"> √ dram    √ dram, “run” Present dramati Future Simple Future: dramiṣyati Periphrastic Future: dramitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: adramīt Perfect dadrāma Causative dramayati Desiderative didramiṣa- Intensive dandramyate U Apparently another form of √ 1 drā. Meanings Int dandramyate run about, roam. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_draa.html"> √ 1 drā    √ 1 drā, “run” Present II. drāhi drā́tu drāntu V Future Simple Future: drāsyati Periphrastic Future: drātā Aorist √-Ao: drāyāt, dreyāt -s-Ao: drāsat RV -siṣ-Ao: adrāsīt Perfect dadrus etc. V.C., dadrāṇá RV Causative drāpayati ŚB. (adidrapat dídrāpayiṣati ŚB.) Desiderative didrāsa- Intensive dáridrāti etc. TS.C. dādrā- Verbal Nouns PPP: drāṇa U.+ Derivatives drá ? AV. drāk ? C. drāpi ? B. dáridra B.+ Compare roots √ dram and √ dru. The intensive stem daridrā is rekoned by the Hindu grammarians as a root, and artificially furnished with a set of verb-forms and primary derivatives. Meanings drā́ti 1 v run, hasten; Caus. drāpayati; Int. dáridrāti run about, be in need. apa run away. abhi overtake. vi run asunder or away, disappear. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_draa.html"> √ 2 drā    √ 2 drā, “sleep” Present II. drāti etc. B.+ IV. drāyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: drāsyáti B Aorist -s-Ao: (or -siṣ-Ao:) adrāsīt B Perfect dadrau C Desiderative didrāsati C Verbal Nouns PPP: drāṇa AV.B.+, drita ? C Derivatives -drā V.+-didrāsu C. Meanings drāti drāyate 2 v sleep. ava fall asleep. ni go to sleep, sleep. Cf. nidrāṇa & nidrita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_draa_d.html"> √ drāḍ    √ drāḍ, “split” A single doubtful occurrence, uddrāḍayan C. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dru.html"> √ dru    √ dru, “run” Present I. drávati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: droṣyati B Periphrastic Future: drotā Aorist √-Ao: drūyāt; adrāvi RAo: adudruvat B.+ (adudrot dudrávat RV.) adudravat, adidravat Perfect dudrāva etc. B.+ dudrotha, dudruma, dudruve etc. E Causative drāváyati etc. V.+,-te etc. E. (drāvyate E.); dravayanta RV Desiderative dudrūṣa- Intensive dodru- (dodrāva TS.) Verbal Nouns PPP: drutá B.+; Inf: drotum C.; 1Abs: drutvā́ B.; 2Abs: -drútya B.+ Derivatives dravá V.+ draví RV. -drāva VS. -dru V.+ dravya ? U.S.+ dravitṛ́ RV. -drāvin S.+ druti C. drávaṇa B.+ dravitnú V. -drāvya E. drāvayitnú RV. dravará RV. dráviṇa etc. ? V.+ drāvaṇa E.+ Meanings drávati 1 v, PPP drutá (q.v.) run, hasten, flee; become fluid, melt (l. & f.). Caus. drāváyati (te). ati run past (A). adhi run towards, mount, leap upon, cover. anu run after, follow, pursue; run through i.e. recite quickly. apa run away. abhi run near, hasten towards, attack, assail; visit, befall. ā run near, approach. samā run (together) towards or against (A). ud run up or out. upa & samupa rush at (A); attack, visit, befall. nis run out or away. pari run about. pra hasten, on, rush at (A); run away, flee, escape. vipra run asunder, also = saṃpra run away, flee. vi run asunder or away, flee. Caus. drive away, chase, put to flight. sam run together. Cf. vidruta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_druh.html"> √ druh    √ druh, “be hostile” Present IV. drúhyati etc. B.+,-te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: dhrokṣyati MS. drohiṣyati Periphrastic Future: drogdhā, droḍhā, drohitā Aorist √-Ao: druhyāt; adrohi Th Ao: druhas -han V.E RAo: adudruhat -s-Ao: drogdhās M -sa- Ao: adrukṣas B Perfect dudróha etc. V.B. (dudróhitha AV.), dudruhe C Causative drohaya- Desiderative dudrukṣat K. dudrohiṣa-, dudruhiṣa-, dudhrukṣa- Intensive dodruh- Verbal Nouns PPP: drugdhá V.+ drūḍha; drogdhavai K.; 1Abs: drugdhvā, drohitvā, druhitvā; 2Abs: -drúhya MS.E Derivatives drúh V.+ druhyú RV. drógha V. drogdhavyà B.+ druhya C. druhiṇa C. droha V.+ drogdhṛ E.+ druhú AV. drúhvan V. drohin E.+ dudhrukṣu C. Meanings drúhyati 1 v (te), PPP drugdhá (q.v.) be hostile, hurt, offend, strive to harm (D, G, L, or A); *emulate, vie. abhi hurt, injure, plot against (A, D, or L) commit (A); PPP w. P & PS mg. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_druu.html"> √ drū    √ drū, “hurl” (?) Present IX. drūṇāti MS., drūṇāná RV Only two occurrences, of which that in MS. does not appear connectible with √ dru. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dvar.html"> √ dvar    √ dvar ? Such a root perhaps to be recognized in dvará RV., dvarín RV.,-dvaras ? RV., and in dvā́r or dúr V.+ “door”. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dvi_s.html"> √ dviṣ    √ dviṣ, “hate” Present II. dvéṣṭi dviṣánti etc. V.+, dviṣṭe dviṣáte etc. AV.+ VI. dviṣati etc. M., dviṣate etc. S.U.+ Future Simple Future: dvekṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: dveṣṭā Aorist √-Ao: adveṣi RAo: adidviṣat -sa- Ao: dvikṣat dvikṣata (2s.) AV Perfect didveṣa ŚB. didviṣe Causative dveṣayati C Desiderative didvikṣa- Intensive dedviṣ- Verbal Nouns PPP: dviṣṭa V.+; Inf: dveṣṭum E., dvéṣṭos ŚB Derivatives dvíṣ V.+ -dviṣṭi C. dveṣin E.+ dveṣaṇīya C. dviṣa C. dvéṣa V.+ dvéṣya AV.+ dvéṣas V.B. -dviṣeṇya RV. -dveṣaka E. dvéṣaṇa V.+ dveṣṭṛ E.+ Meanings dvéṣṭi dviṣṭé 1 v (dviṣati & dviṣate), PPP dviṣṭa (q.v.) hate, be hostile or a rival (w. A, r. D or G). pra dislike, hate, show enmity against (A). vi PĀ the same; Ā also hate each other mutually, be hostile towards one another. Cf. dviṣánt, vidviṣant, vidviṣāṇa, vidviṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dhan.html"> √ dhan    √ dhan, “run” Present I. dhanati III. dadhanti Perfect dadhánat dadhanyus dadhanvā́ṃs RV Causative dhanáyan -yante -yanta RV Derivatives dhániṣṭha RV. Compare roots √ dhanv, √ dhav, √ dhāv, √ dhū. Meanings (dadhanti) set in motion. Caus. dhanáyati, dhanáyate = S., Ā also = be quick, run. pra spring forth, flow. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dhanv.html"> √ dhanv    √ dhanv, “run” Present I. dhánvati etc. V.B. (dhaniva SV.) Aorist -iṣ-Ao: ádhanviṣus V.B Perfect dadhanvé -viré RV Derivatives dhánutṛ RV. Seems to be a secondary root-form, from the preceding. Its v has value as u in half the RV. cases (in the present-system). Meanings dhánvati v (dhánvate) run, speed (intrans. & trans.); swing or bend (the bow). – accha, anu & abhi run towards or near. pra run (asunder), dissolve, perish. sam Ā run near or together with (I). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dham.html"> √ dham, dhmā    √ dham, dhmā, “blow” Present I. dhámati etc. V.+,-te etc. U.E II. dhmānt C Passive dhamyate etc. V.+,-ti E.; dhmāyáte etc. B.+,-ti etc. ŚB.E.+ Future Simple Future: dhamiṣyati etc. E.+ dhmāsyati Periphrastic Future: dhmātā Aorist √-Ao: dhmāyat dhmeyāt; adhmāyi -siṣ-Ao: admāsīt C Perfect dadhmau etc. dadhmire E Causative dhmāpayati etc. E.+ (dhmāpyate E.) adidhmapat Desiderative didhmāsa- Intensive dādhmāyate C. dedhmīya- Verbal Nouns dhamitá RV., dhmātá V.+;-dhmā́ya B.+ Derivatives -dhama AV.+ dhamitra C. -dhmānīya C. dhmāpana C. -dhamana C. -dhmā̆ B.+ dhmātavya C. dhamáni V.+ dhmā́na AV.+ dhmātṛ RV. Meanings (dhmā), dhámati (te), PPP dhamitá & dhmātá blow, exhale; kindle (fire by blowing), melt (ore). anu blow upon. apa blow off. abhi blow at, terrify by blowing. ā inflate, blow, sound, proclaim aloud; P. be inflated or puffed up. upā & samupā blow, sound. ud exhale, breathe out, proclaim. upa blow at (A). nis & parā blow away. pra blow forth, blow away i.e. terrify by blowing, blow at (A); Ā proclaim aloud. Caus. blow into (a conchshell), sound. vi blow i.e. drive asunder, scatter, disperse, destroy. sam blow or melt together; proclaim aloud. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dhav.html"> √ dhav    √ dhav, “flow” Present I. dhavate etc. RV Derivatives dhávīyas RV. Meanings dhavate v run, flow. ava flow down, descend. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_dhaa.html"> √ 1 dhā, dadh    √ 1 dhā, dadh, “put” Present I. dádhati -te etc. V.+ II. dhāti RV3 III. dádhāti dhatté etc. V.+ IV. dhāyeta MU., adhāvata M Passive dhīyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: dhāsyati -te etc. B.+ (adhāsyat C.) Periphrastic Future: dhātā etc. B Aorist √-Ao: áhāt adhus etc. V.+ (adhītām RV.; dheyām -yus -yāsus RV.; dhā́tu etc. V.; dhetana RV.TB.), adhithās adhita etc. V.+ (ahita hita AV.TA.; adhīmahi dhīmahi dhīmahe V.B.; dhāmahe RV.; dhiṣe dhire dhéthe dhaithe RV.; dhiṣvá RV.); ádhāyi dhā́yi V.+ Th Ao: adhat SV., dhat RV -s-Ao: dhāsus dhāsathas -tha V., adhiṣi -ṣata B.+ (dhiṣīya B.S., dheṣīya MS.) -iṣ-Ao ? dhāyīs RV Perfect dadhaú dadhé etc. V.+ (dadhā́tha V., dadhidhvé -iṣvá -idhvam RV., dadhre RV.) Causative dhāpayati etc. V.+ dhāpayīta S. (dhāpyate C.) Desiderative dhítsati etc. V.+,-te etc. V.+ (dhitsyate C.); dídhiṣate etc. -te etc. RV. adhitsiṣam AA. (dídhiṣāṇa RV.) Intensive dedhīyate Verbal Nouns PPP: hitá V.+,-dhita V.C.; Inf: dhā́tum B.+,-tave V.B.,-tavaí AV.,-tos V.B.,-dhitum C.; 1Abs: dhitvā́ B. hitvā; 2Abs: -dhā́ya AV.+;-dhā́m AV.; dhiyádhyai RV.;-dhāyam Derivatives -dhā̆ V.+ dhāya S. -dhi V.+ -dadhus MS. -dhā́na V.+ -dhāyaka C. -dhiti V.B.S. dadhiṣú AV. dhānā́ ? V.+ -dhāyin C. -hiti V.+ didhiṣú V.+ -dhānīya C. dhāyyà B.S. dheya B.+ didhiṣā́yya RV. dhā́tu V.+ dhā́yu RV. -dhéya n V.+ -dhitsā E.+ -dhātavya B.+ dhāsí RV. dhéṣṭha V.B. -dhitsu S.+ dhātṛ V.+ -dhas V.+ -dadha B.S. -dhāpana S. dhā́man V.+ dádhi V.B. -dhāpayitavya C. Meanings dádhāti dhatté; dádhati dádhāti dhatté dádhate 1 (dhāti, dhāyate) v PPP hitá (q.v.) & dhita (only – ṃ) put, set, lay; put upon, bring to, direct towards (L or D), fix (esp. the mind) upon, think of (L or D); resolve, determine to (D, L, A w. ~ prati, or Inf); establish, constitute, appoint (2A); create, produce, cause, do, make; hold, keep, wear, bear, maintain; Ā take to one's self, receive, obtain, get, win, conceive (gárbham); w. ókam & cánas enjoy, delight in (L or D); assume, incur, show, betray (Ā & P). Caus. dhāpayati (only – ṃ). Des dídhiṣati, the wish to give; Ā wish to win or get, w. avadyam bid defiance (G); dhítsati wish to put or place upon (L). adhi P set upon (esp. the fire); bestow on (D or L), grant, impart; Ā acquire, get, exhibit. anu put on additionally; induce to (D). vyanu unfold, exhibit. antar PĀ put into (L) or between, separate, exclude; hide, conceal, cover; P receive or contain within; keep from (Ab), withhold; P. be covered or hidden, disappear. apa P take or drive away. api or pi put in (L); offer or present to (D), bestow on (L); cover, shut up, hide, conceal; P. be hidden, become invisible, disappear in (L). abhi put on or to, surround or cover with (I), give up to (D), deliver; practice, apply, commit; name, designate; tell (2A); P. be called. pratyabhi draw back, reabsorb; answer, consent. ava put down or in, immerse (in water), shut up or enclose in (L); be immersed in (L), be attentive. Caus. cause to be laid in. vyava put asunder, place between, separate, interrupt; P. be separated or interrupted. ā put on (esp. wood on the fire), lay, set, place in or on, direct towards, fix upon (L or D), lay down, deposit; impart, grant, bestow, offer (D, L, or G of pers.), bring to (D), employ at (L); produce, cause, effect; Ā seize, take, receive, conceive (gárbham), appropriate to one's self. atyā place above, extol. adhyā place upon. anvā put on (esp. wood), i.e. set up or kindle (the fire). abhyā the same. upā put on, place upon (L); Ā seize, take. nirā take out or away. paryā lay about, surround. vyā P. be divided, be separated from (Ab); be uncomfortable or ill. samā put on (wood), set up or kindle (fire); lay, set, place on or in (L), turn or fix (the eyes or mind) upon (L), collect or concentrate the mind (ātmānam); impose, adjust, apply; unite, keep together, reconcile, restore, settle, arrange, cause, produce. Ā put on (a garment), conceive (of women), accept, appropriate to one's self, manifest, betray, devote one's self entirely to (A); establish, state, concede, agree. upasamā = anvā + put a thing in its place. pratisamā adjust (the arrow), put in order, restore. udā shut up, erect; cast away, expose. upa put on or in, w. adhastāt under; put on the fire, put (the horse) to the yoke, put to mind (hṛdi); lie down upon (A), (g.) precede immediately (only P.); commit to (D), impart, teach; add, join; use, employ. tiras set aside, remove, drive back, overwhelm; hide, conceal. Ā be hidden from (Ab), vanish, disappear. ni lay down, take off, put, set, place in or on (L ~ antár or antar – ṃ), put before one (D), turn (the eyes) to (L), set the mind i.e. resolve upon (D); deposit, keep, guard; appoint, commit, entrust; keep down, suppress, remove, finish. With kriyām take pains with (L); w. bhūmau or avaṭe bury; w. maulau esteem highly; w. manasi or hṛdaye reflect, ponder; w. máno mánasi consent (lit. put mind to mind). Caus. cause to deposit or to put in (L). adhini lay upon, bestow, impart. apani put aside, remove, drive away. abhini lay on, impose; approach, touch. upani place near, put before (D); lay down, bury (a treasure); deposit, commit, entrust (L); bring about, effect. praṇi lay down, prostrate (the body); put on or in (L); touch, approach with (I), turn or fix (eyes or mind) on (L); be intent upon or attentive to (A); stretch forth, send out (esp. spics, carān), explore, search; find out to be (2A) pratini put instead, substitute; order, command. vini lay apart, distribute, take off or down; put in, fix on, appoint to (L). saṃni lay down (together) in or at (L); place near or aside; keep, preserve, heap up, collect; Ā appoint, assign; w. dṛṣṭim fix on (L), w. hṛdayam concentrate, collect; Ā P. be near or present. Caus. bring near, fetch. nis find out. pari PĀ lay or set around, put on, don (vāsas etc.); surround, clothe, dress; P conclude the recitation (r.). Caus. cause to put on (2A), surround or clothe with (I). vipari change, esp. clothes (vāsas). puras Ā (P) put before, place in front or at the head, prefer, choose, be intent on or eager for (A); appoint (esp. to priestly functions); commit, entrust to (D or G). pra present, offer; set forward, send out (spies). prati put instead, replace; adjust (the arrow), take aim; put to the lips, set the foot upon (L), stride out; present, offer, restore; Ā commence, begin. vi distribute, divide; impart, procure, grant; appoint, arrange, settle; destine, design; exhibit, show, betray; find out, produce, found, form, cause, effect, make (in various mgs & w. various nouns = √ 1 kṛ q.v.); make, render (2A); lay, place, put, fix in or on (L); set forward or send out (spies). Des (dhitsati, te) wish to impart, fix, settle, find out, procure, make or render (2A); intend or purpose i.g. anuvi Ā appoint or regulate (in due order); cause or effect (after another), bring about, perform; P. be regulated according to, i.e. obey, follow (A or G). prativi arrange, prepare, make ready; counteract, take measures against (L). saṃvi Ā dispose, arrange; settle, direct, order, appoint; hold up, carry on, manage, employ, use; make or render (2A). sam put together, connect, compose, unite; close, collect (lit. & fig.); repair, restore; lay down, put in or on (L, esp. śaram dhanuṣi, also absol. = aim, shoot); impart, grant, bestow (together) on (L); Ā bring together, unite; make peace or agree with (I, r. A); stand out against (A), rival, vie. P. be united with = get possessed of (I); be held or contained in (L). anusam add, connect; follow (lit.* & fig.), observe, explore, ascertain. abhisam snap at (L), unite or join, esp. the arrow with the bow (I); bring about, beget; aim at (D or L), purpose, intend (A or D); call to mind, ponder; consent, agree about (A); win over, take in, cheat, deceive. upasam add, increase; join or connect with (I); aim at, keep in view; cheat, deceive. pratisam put together (again), readjust; Ā put on (esp. the arrow on the bow), restore, return. Cf. atyāhita, antárhita, ápihita, abhíhita, ávahita, ā́hita, úddhita, upasaṃhita, upahita, upādhā́ya, upā́hita, tirohita, níhita, párihita, purohita, praṇihita, vinihita, vihita, vyavahita, vyā́hita, sáhita, saṃnihita, samā́hita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_dhaa.html"> √ 2 dhā    √ 2 dhā, “suck” Present IV ? dháyati etc. V.+ Passive dhīyate Future Simple Future: dhāsyati E Periphrastic Future: dhātā Aorist √-Ao: adhāt AV. dheyāt RAo: adadhat -siṣ-Ao: adhāsīt Perfect dadhús RV Causative dhāpayate etc. RV.,-ti ŚB. adīdhapat Desiderative dhitsa- Intensive dādhā- , dādhī-, dedhīya- Verbal Nouns PPP: dhītá V.B.; dhā́tave V.; 1Abs: dhītvā́ ŚB.; 2Abs: -dhī́ya ŚB.-dhāya Derivatives -dhā V.+ -dhāyin C. dhārú AV. dhénā V. -dhaya B.+ dhā́yas V. dhāsí RV.S. dhenú V.+ dhā́tu RV.S. dhāyú RV. dhāsyú AV. dadhán , dádhi V.+ Related with √ dhi. The connection of some of the derivatives by no means beyond question. Meanings dháyati v PPP dhītá 3 suck, drink, imbibe. Caus. dhāpáyate suckle, nourish. upa Caus. Ā = S.Caus. nis suck out. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_dhaav.html"> √ 1 dhāv    √ 1 dhāv, “run” Present I. dhā́vati etc. -te etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: dhāviṣyati C.-te Periphrastic Future: dhāvitā Aorist √-Ao: dhāvyāsam RAo: adadhāvat RV. adīdhavat -iṣ-Ao: adāvīt B. adhāviṣṭa Perfect dadhāva -ve Causative dhāváyati etc. V.+ Desiderative didhāviṣa- Intensive dādhāvya- Verbal Nouns PPP: dhāvita E.+; 1Abs: dhāvitvā C.; 2Abs: -dhāvya C Derivatives dhāvaka E. dhāvin C. dhāvana E.+ dhāvitṛ E. dhā́rā ? V.+ Compare roots √ dhan, √ dhanv, √ dhav. It is reckoned by the grammarians as filling up the defective conjugation of √ sṛ. Meanings dhā́vati 1 v (te) run, stream, pour, ride, swim, glide; hasten, rush, run after or against (A). Caus. dhāváyati cause to run, impel; ride or drive (w. I of the vehicle); jump, dance. ati run over or past (A). anu run after, through, towards, against (A); succour, assist (A). apa run away, depart (from a previous statement), prevaricate (j.). api run into (A). abhi run towards or against, attack or succour (A). ava run or drop down from (Ab). ā run or flow towards (L), come near, return; run against (A). upa run near, approach, hasten towards, resort to (A); Ā run, glide. nis stream or spring forth, run out, escape from (Ab). pari run or flow about or through (mṛgayām go hunting), run near or after (A). pra run forth or away, hasten, rush on, resort to (A), penetrate. prati run back; rush against, assail (A). vi run away or through, be scattered or lost in (L). anuvi run after in different directions. sam run together, rush against, assail (A). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_dhaav.html"> √ 2 dhāv    √ 2 dhāv, “rinse” Present I. dhā́vati etc. -te etc. V.+ Passive dhāvyate C Aorist -iṣ-Ao: adhāviṣṭa (3s.) RV Perfect dadhāva dadhāvire C Causative dhāvayati etc.-te etc. B.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: dhautá SV.+; 1Abs: dhautvā ? C.; 2Abs: -dhāvya S Derivatives dhāva C. -dhāvin C. dhautí RV. dhā́rā ? V.+ dhāvaka E. dhā́vana B.+ Perhaps rather related with √ dhū than with √ 1 dhāv. Meanings dhā́vati dhā́vate v PPP dautá 2 (q.v.) rinse, wash, cleanse, purify; Ā also refl. C dhāváyati wash. ā knead, press out, cleanse (esp. the Soma-stems). ni Ā rub or anoint one's self; rub one's self against i.e. cling to (L). pra rub off, Caus. wash. vi wash or cleanse off. sam Ā run or wash one's self. Cf. nirdauta, vidauta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dhi.html"> √ dhi, dhinv    √ dhi, dhinv, “nourish Present V. dhinoti dhinvanti etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: dhinviṣyati Periphrastic Future: dhinvitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: adhinvīt PB Perfect didhinva Perhaps only another form of √ 2 dhā, with causative value. Some of the derivatives given under √ 2 dhā might be put as properly here. Meanings dhinoti 1 v nourish, refresh, gladden. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dhii.html"> √ dhī, dīdhī    √ dhī, dīdhī, “think” Present II. dhīmahi B.+ III ? dīdhayas dī́dhayan dīdhyat etc. dī́dhyat adīdhet etc. dī́dhye dīdhyāthām dīdhīthām dī́dhyāna adīdhīta etc. V.B Perfect dīdhaya -dhima (-mas SV.) -dhiyus -dhyus dīdhire V.B Desiderative ? dhī́ṣamāṇa RV1 Intensive dedhyat TS Verbal Nouns PPP: dhītá V.+ Derivatives dhī́ V.+ dhī́ra V.+ dhiyasāná RV. -dīdhayu RV. dhītí V.B. dhī́van RV. dī́dhiti V.+ Compare √ dhyā. The form dhīmahi belongs here only as thus used later, with a false apprehension of its proper meaning. Meanings dī́dhye ádīpdet v PPP dhītá (q.v.) appear, seem (P); perceive, look at (A); think, consider (manasā), desire. anu observe, think over. abhi think of, consider. ā attend to, care for (G), make up one's mind. ud look up to (A). prati hope, expect. vi hesitate, be irresolute. Cf. dī́dhyat & dī́dhyāna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dhuk_s.html"> √ dhukṣ    √ dhukṣ, “kindle” Present I. dhukṣate E1 Future Simple Future: dhukṣiṣyate Periphrastic Future: dhukṣitā Aorist RAo: adudhukṣat -iṣ-Ao: adhukṣiṣṭa Perfect dudhukṣe Causative dhukṣayati etc. E.+ (dhukṣyate C.) Desiderative dudhukṣiṣa- Intensive dodhukṣ- Derivatives -dhukṣaṇa E.+ Occurring only with the prefix sam. Meanings dhukṣate v only w. sam S. & Caus. saṃdhukṣayati kindle. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dhuu.html"> √ dhū, dhu    √ dhū, dhu, “shake” Present II. dhuváte (3p.) ŚB., dhuvāná TS V. dhūnóti dhūnuté etc. V.+; dhunoti dhunute etc. JB.S.+ VI. dhuvati etc. AV.B. (dhūvet K.) IX. dhunīyāt dhunāna dhūnāna C. dhunet ? M1 Passive dhūyáte etc. AV.+ (dhūyant M.) Future Simple Future: dhaviṣyati B.S.,-te B. dhoṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: dhavitā, dhotā Aorist -s-Ao: adhūṣṭa -ṣata RV.S. adoṣṭa -iṣ-Ao: adhāvīt adhuvīt, adhaviṣṭa Perfect dudhāva etc. E.+, dudhuve AV. (dudhuvīta dūdhot RV.) Causative dhūnayati -te etc. E.+ dhāvayati Desiderative dudhūṣa- Intensive dodhavīti etc. V.E., dodhūyate etc. E.+ (dodhūyat Part. E.+); davidhu- RV. (davidhāva RV.) Verbal Nouns PPP: dhūtá V.+, dhuta E.+ dhūna; Inf: dhavitum; 1Abs: dhūtvā B.U.; 2Abs: -dhū́ya AV.+ Derivatives -dhu V. -dhāva B. dhuvaka JB. -dhuti C. -dhava RV. dhavitavyà ŚB. dhúvana B.S. dhúni ? V.B. -dhavana B.S. dhavítra B.S. dhū́ti RV. dhūnana E.+ Compare √ 2 dhāv. Meanings dhūnóti dhūnuté dhunoti dhunute v (dhūváti, dhuváti, dhunāti, dhunīte), PPP dhūtá & dhuta shake, toss, agitate; shake off a thing from (2A), cast away, remove; fan, kindle (fire); intrans. struggle, resist. Int dodhavīti & dodhūyate shake violently, flourish, swing, fan; intrans. move to and fro, totter, rush on. apa shake off. abhi shake, fan. ava shake or throw down, shake off from (Ab) upon (L), reject; move to and fro, toss. vyava shake off, reject, renounce. ā & vyā shake, toss, stir. ud rouse up, stir, lift, swing, fan, kindle, move, excite; throw off, reject. samud shake up, raise, stir, toss. nis shake out or off, drive away, remove, expel; swing, brandish. vinis shake off, drive asunder, reject; move to and fro, toss. pra move onward (trans.), blow away or out. Int shake or blow out (the beard). vi shake, toss, swing (Ā also refl.), fan, kindle, drive asunder or away, remove, destroy; Ā shake off (1 or 2A), give up, renounce. sam shake towards i.e. bestow on (D); Ā raff up together. Cf. ávadhūta, ādhūta, uddhūta, nirdhūta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dhuurv.html"> √ dhūrv    √ dhūrv, “injure” Present I. dhū́rvati etc. V.B Future Simple Future: dhūrviṣyati Periphrastic Future: dhūrvitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: adhūrvīt ŚB Perfect dudhūrva Verbal Nouns Inf: dhū́rvitum ŚB A secondary root-form from √ dhvṛ dhur. Meanings dhū́rvati v injure, damage. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dh_r.html"> √ dhṛ    √ dhṛ, “hold” Present I. dhareran AŚS1.; adhāram R1 Passive dhriyáte etc. V.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: dhariṣyati etc. E.+,-te etc. AV.+ Periphrastic Future: dhartā C Aorist √-Ao: dhṛthās AV.; adhāri C RAo: ádīdharat etc. V.B.S. (dīdhar, didhṛtam -tá RV.),-rata (3s.) ŚB -s-Ao: adhārṣīt Perfect dadhāra etc. (dadhartha) JB.E.+; dādhā́ra V.B. (dādhártha RV.TA.); dadhré etc. V.+ Causative dhāráyati -te etc. V.+ (dhāryáte E.+; didhārayiṣa- S.C.) Desiderative didhīrṣa- (in d.) didhariṣate Intensive dardharṣi adardhar RV.; dādharti dādhrati dādhartu B. (dadhartu ? AVP.; dādhārayati JB.) Verbal Nouns PPP: dhṛtá V.+; Inf: dhartum C.-tavai KB.; 1Abs: dhṛtvā́ B.+; 2Abs: -dhṛtya E.; dhartári RV.;-dhāram S Derivatives dhára V.+ dharmán RV. -dhāri C. dhruvás RV. dháraṇa AV.+ dhárman V.+ dhīra E.+ dhruví V.B. -dharaṇīya C. dhárma AV.+ dhúr V.+ dā́dhṛvi RV. dharaṇi E.+ dhariman C. dhura E.+ dṛdhrá ? RV. dharúṇa V.B. dhárīman RV. -dhṛt V.+ didhīrṣā C. -dhártu RV. dhárīyas B.S. -dhṛk E.+ -didhīrṣu C. -dhárītu RV. -dhā́ra V.+ dhṛ́ti V.+ -dhāraya V.+ dhartṛ́ V.B. dhā́raka B.+ -dhṛtvan B. dhārayú RV. dhartrá B.S. dhārin U.S.+ -dhra V.+ dhārayitavya U.+ dháritṛ B.+ dhārya E.+ -dhri ? V.+ dhārayitṛ B.+ dharṇasí V.B. dhā́raṇa V.+ dhruvá V.+ dhārayiṣṇu C. dharṇí RV. -dhāraṇīya C. -didhārayiṣā C. Meanings (dharati, dharate), PPP dhṛtá (q.v.); Caus. dhārayate), PPP dhṛtá (q.v.); Caus. dhārayati, te = S. hold, bear, carry on, keep down, suppress, keep back i.e. own to (D or G); withstand, resist; uphold, maintain, preserve, support, wear, use, possess; turn the mind or set the heart on (L or D), be determined to (Inf). With garbham become or be pregnant; w. daṇḍam or damam inflict punishment on (L); w. vratám observe a vow; w. mūrdhnā (dhni) or śirasā (si) honour highly; w. tulayā weigh, measure; manasā bear in mind, remember; ātmānam, prāṇān, śarīram, etc. live on, survive. P. dhriyate (ti) be held, borne, etc., mostly = P intrans. Int dárdharti & dādharti hold fast; establish, fix. adhi bring upon. carry over to, communicate (L). abhi maintain, uphold, withstand. ava settle, establish, state, assume as certain, consider as (2A or A & N w. iti); learn, hear, understand, perceive, observe, ponder. ā uphold, preserve, keep (esp. in the memory), put on or to (L). P. ādhriyate be (contained) in (L). ud draw out, elevate, raise, further. samud maintain, support. upa bear, support, take for, consider as (2A); learn, hear, perceive, observe, think over. ni lay down in, bring to (L); appoint, render (2A). nis take out, set off, ascertain, decide. pra keep in mind, think over, ponder; w. manas set the mind on (D), determine; w. daṇḍam = S. saṃpra commit, entrust to (D); w. buddhim & L = prec. w. manas & D, manasā = S; make up the mind, resolve, settle. vi hold, bear; keep asunder, separate, distribute, arrange; keep from (Ab), withhold, suppress; support, preserve, guard; w. manas set the mind upon (L). sam keep together, bear, support, maintain; keep in mind, remember; keep back, withhold, resist; hold, wear, possess; w. manas = prec. Cf. vídhṛta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dh_r_s.html"> √ dhṛṣ    √ dhṛṣ, “dare” Present I. dhárṣati etc. VS.B II ? dhṛṣánt RV., dhṛṣāṇá AV V. dhṛṣṇóti etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: dharṣiṣyati Periphrastic Future: dharṣitā Aorist Th Ao: adhṛṣas ŚB. (dhṛṣámāṇa ? RV.) RAo: adīdhṛṣat, adadharṣat -iṣ-Ao: adharṣiṣus TA Perfect dadhárṣa etc. V.B. (dādhṛṣus AV.; dadhárṣat -ṣati dadharṣīt RV.; dadhṛṣate dádhṛṣanta AV Causative dharṣayati etc. B.+ Desiderative didharṣiṣa- Intensive darīdhṛṣ- Verbal Nouns PPP: dhṛṣṭá V.+, dhṛṣitá V.; 2Abs: -dhṛṣya B.+;-dhṛ́ṣe V.B.,-dhṛ́ṣas RV Derivatives dhárṣa V.+ dharṣaṇa E.+ dhṛ́ṣṭi B.+ dadhṛṣá RV. -dharṣin C. -dhṛṣ V. dhṛṣya V.+ dadhṛṣváṇi RV. -dharṣyà AV. dhṛṣáj RV. -dharṣayitavya C. Meanings dhṛṣṇóti dhárṣati v PPP dhṛṣitá & dhṛṣṭá q.v. be bold, dare or venture to (Inf), defy (A). Caus. dharṣayati, PPP dharṣita attack, injure, violate; Ā overwhelm. apa overwhelm, conquer. abhi S. & Caus. the same. ā venture against, attack. Caus. injure, offend. pra venture against, assail, injure, harass. Caus. the same + violate (a woman), destroy, lay waste. saṃpra Caus. assail, defy. prati hold out against, withstand. vi Caus. venture against, injure, harass, also = seq. sam Caus. violate (a woman), destroy. Cf. ādhṛ́ṣe & dhṛṣánt. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dhmaa.html"> √ dhmā    √ dhmā see √ dham. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dhyaa.html"> √ dhyā    √ dhyā, “think” Present II. dhyāti etc. B.+ (dhyāyāt B.S.) IV. dhyā́yati etc. B.+,-te etc. E.+ (dhyāyīta U.) Passive dhyāyate C Future Simple Future: dhyāsyati E Periphrastic Future: dhyātā JUB Aorist -s-Ao: dhyāsus M -siṣ-Ao: ádhyāsiṣam ŚB Perfect dadhyau etc. B.+ Causative dhyāpayati Desiderative didhyāsate ŚB Intensive dādhyā- Verbal Nouns PPP: dhyāta B.+; 1Abs: dhyātvā B.+; 2Abs: -dhyāya E.+; dhyāyam C Derivatives dhyā́ V.+ dhyāna U.+ dhyātṛ C. -didhyāsana C. -dhyāyin B.+ dhyātavya C. dhyeya E.+ -didhyāsitavyà B. -didhyāsu C. Compare √ dhī, of which this is a later secondary form. Meanings dhyā́yati 1 v (te, dhyāti), PPP dhyāta think of (A), reflect, meditate, ponder (manasā or si etc.). Des didhyāsate. anu = S. + regret, remember. samanu muse, ponder. apa think ill of (A), bewitch by evil thoughts. abhi set the mind on (A or L); intend, wish, desire; take for (2A); absol. meditate, ponder. ava despise, curse. ni perceive, notice; also = Des nididhyāsate be thoughtful or attentive. nis ponder on, think over, consider (regard, contemplate, observe closely or intently*). pra meditate upon, reflect, consider, find out. sam reflect, ponder. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dhraj.html"> √ dhraj, dhrāj    √ dhraj, dhrāj, “sweep” Present I. dhrájati etc. RV.; dhrā́jamāna MS Aorist -iṣ-Ao: dhrājiṣīya MS Derivatives -dhrajati RV. dhrájas RV. dhrā́j MS. dhrā́ji V.B. dhráji- RV. dhrājá MS. dhrājí MS. Meanings dhrájati v sweep, glide (of the wind, birds, etc.). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dhva_ms.html"> √ dhvaṃs, dhvas    √ dhvaṃs, dhvas, “scatter” Present I. dhvaṃsati -te etc. B.+ Passive dhvasyate C.,-ti GB Future Simple Future: dhvaṃsiṣyate Periphrastic Future: dhvaṃsitā Aorist Th Ao: dhvasán RV RAo: adadhvaṃsat -iṣ-Ao: advaṃsiṣṭa Perfect dadhvaṃsus U., dadhvaṃsire E.; dadhvasé V.B Causative dhvaṃsáyati etc. B.+,-te etc. JB.; dhvasáyati etc. RV Desiderative didhvaṃsiṣa- Intensive danīdhvaṃs- -dhvasya- Verbal Nouns dhvasta B.+;-dhvasya E.+ Derivatives -dhvasa E.+ dhvasánti n.pr . RV. dhvasmán RV. dhvaṃsin E.+ dhvasán n.pr . ŚB. dhvasirá RV. dhvasrá RV.B. dhváṃsana B.+ dhvasáni V. dhvasti C. dhvaṃsá RV.+ dhvaṃsi S. -dhvaṃsaka C. Meanings dhvaṃsati dhvaṃsate v PPP dhvasta (q.v.) sink down, fall to dust, perish (also P. dhvasyate); be gone (only imper.). Caus. dhvaṃsáyati, PPP dhvaṃsita strew, fell, destroy, violate (a. woman). dhvasáyati spatter, sparkle. apa be gone (only imper.). ava Ā be scattered or dispersed. ni Caus. (dhvasayati) scatter, destroy. vini be gone (only imper.). pra Ā flow away, subside (water); fall to dust, perish vi Ā (P) be scattered, crumble down. Caus. (dhvaṃsayati) crush, waste, destroy. Cf. apadhvasta, ādhvasta, upadhvastá, paridhvasta, vidhvasta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dhvan.html"> √ dhvan    √ dhvan, “sound” Present I. dhvanati etc. C Future Simple Future: dhvaniṣyati Periphrastic Future: dhvanitā Aorist RAo: adidhvanat adadhvanat -iṣ-Ao: ádhvanīt RV Perfect dadhvanus C Causative dhvanayati B. (dhvanayīt RV.); adhvānayat RV. (dhvānita C.) Intensive dandhvan- (in d.) Verbal Nouns PPP: dhvanita C., dhvāntá B.+ Derivatives dhvana TA. dhvaní AV.C. dhvāna S.+ dandhvana E. dhvanyà RV. dhvanana S.+ dhúni ? V.B. The RV. forms are set off by BR., perhaps rightly, to a separate √ dhvan “cover”, to which then dhvāntá RV.E.+ “dark” is also referred. Meanings dhvanati v PPP dhvanita 2 (q.v.) sound; Caus. dhvanayati or dhvānayati cause to sound. abhi & pra = S. Cf. apadhvānta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_dhv_r.html"> √ dhvṛ, dhur, dhru    √ dhvṛ, dhur, dhru, “injure” Present I. dhvárati etc. B Future Simple Future: dhvariṣyati Periphrastic Future: dhvartā Aorist -s-Ao: adhvārṣīt, ádhūrṣata (3p.) RV. dhvṛṣīṣṭa -iṣ-Ao: dhvariṣīṣṭa Perfect dadhvāra Causative dhvārayati Desiderative dúdhūrṣati etc. AV.ŚB Intensive dādhvarya- Verbal Nouns PPP: dhūrta E.+, dhruta TB.; dhū́rvane RV Derivatives dhúr ŚB.MS. -dhru ? RV. dhvarā́ MS. -dhvartavya TS. dhūrtí RV.MS. -dhrut RV. dhvarás RV. -dhvṛt RV. -dhoraṇa ? C. dhrúti RV. Compare √ dhūrv, which is a secondary form (u-class) of this root. Meanings dhvárati v bend, cause to fall, ruin. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_na_mz.html"> √ naṃś    √ naṃś see √ 2 naś. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_nak_s.html"> √ nakṣ    √ nakṣ, “attain” Present I. nákṣati -te etc. V.B Future Simple Future: nakṣiṣyati Periphrastic Future: nakṣitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: anakṣīt Perfect nanakṣús -kṣé RV Derivatives nákṣatra ? V.+ nakṣya RV. A secondary form of √ 2 naś. Compare also inakṣ, under √ 2 naś. Meanings nákṣati nákṣate v get at, obtain. abhi = S. ava overtake. pari get round. pra come near. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_na_t.html"> √ naṭ    √ naṭ, “dance, play” Present I. naṭati C Causative nāṭayati etc. C Derivatives naṭa E.+ naṭana C. nāṭa C. nāṭin C. naṭanīya C. nāṭaka C. nāṭayitavya C. A prakritized formation from √ nṛt. Meanings naṭati v dance, play. Caus. nāṭayati perform, represent (d.). ud play a trick (w. G). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_nad.html"> √ nad    √ nad, “sound” Present I. nádati etc. AV.+,-te etc. E.+ Passive nadyate E Future Simple Future: nadiṣyati Periphrastic Future: naditā Aorist Th Ao: anīnadat -iṣ-Ao: anā̆dīt Perfect nanāda nedus E.+, nedire E Causative nadáyati -te etc. RV.E.; nādayati -te etc. E.+ (nādyate E.+) Desiderative ninadiṣa- Intensive nā́nadati (3p.) etc. V.E., nānadyate etc. JB.E Verbal Nouns PPP: nadita C.; 2Abs: -nadya E.+ Derivatives nadá V.+ -nadathu U. nādá V.+ -nadana E. nadī́ ? V.+ nadanú RV. nādín AV.+ nānada B.S. -nadin E. nadanimán AV. nādi S. Compare the next root (√ nand). Meanings nádati v (nádate) sound, roar, cry, hum (svanam, śabdam, etc.). Caus. nadáyati or nādayati, te, PPP nādita (q.v.) make resound. I. nā́nadati (3. pl.) sound violently, howl, neigh. anu & abhi sound towards (A); Caus. (also vyanu) make resound, fill with noise. ud & samud sound, howl. roar, cry. upa Caus. make resound. ni sound, cry out, shriek; Caus. = prec. Caus. pra (ṇadati) begin to cry or roar. prati sound back, answer with a cry or howl. vi sound, cry, roar (ravam, svanam, etc.), also = Caus. make resound, fill with noise. sam sound, roar, cry out. Caus. = prec. Caus. , abs. cry aloud. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_nand.html"> √ nand    √ nand, “rejoice” Present I. nándati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ Passive nandyate etc. C Future Simple Future: nandiṣyate E.-ti Periphrastic Future: nanditā Aorist RAo: ananandat -iṣ-Ao: anandīt Perfect nanandus etc. E.+ Causative nandayati -te etc. U.+ Desiderative ninandiṣa- Intensive nānand- Verbal Nouns PPP: nandita E.+; 2Abs: -nandya E.+ Derivatives nánda V.+ nándana RV.+ nandáthu B.+ nánāndṛ ? V. nandaka E.+ -nandanīya C. nāndaná SV.U. -nandayitavya U.+ nandin AV.+ nándi B.+ nāndī́ RV.E.+ -nandayitṛ C. -nandya C. nanditṛ E. nānduka C. Doubtless the same with the preceding root (√ nad). Meanings nandati v (nandate) rejoice, be satisfied with (I, r. Ab) Caus. nandayati gladden. abhi please; be pleased with, delight in (A), greet, take leave of (A), accept, approve; w. na reject, decline. pratyabhi greet (in return). samabhi congratulate. ā rejoice; Caus. gladden, make happy, bless. prati greet joyfully or in return, bid farewell (A), speak kindly or humbly to (A); accept, approve; w. na decline, refuse. Caus. gladden, make happy. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_nabh.html"> √ nabh    √ nabh, “burst” Present I. nábhate etc. V IV. nabhyati IX. nabhnāti Perfect nanābha nebhe Causative anabhayan AB.; nambhaya TS.S Derivatives nábh RV. nabhanyà RV. nabhāka RV.B. nā́bh RV. nabhanú ,-ū́ RV. nábhas V.+ nábhya V.B.S. nā́bhi V.+ The connection of part of the derivatives with this root is quite questionable. Meanings nábhate v burst (trans. & intrans.). Caus. tear open, rend asunder. ud Caus. = S. Caus. pra burst, split (intrans.). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_nam.html"> √ nam    √ nam, “bend, bow” Present I. námati -te etc. V.+ (namāna R.) Passive namyate U.+ Future Simple Future: naṃsyati B., namiṣyati C Periphrastic Future: naṃtā Aorist RAo: anīnamat etc. RV.C -s-Ao: anān K., anaṃsata (3p.) B. (naṃsai náṃsante RV.) -siṣ-Ao: anaṃsīt C Perfect nemus C. (nānāma nanámas RV.), neme RV. (nanāmire M.) Causative namayati etc. V.+,-te C.; nāmayati etc. U.S. (nāmyate etc. E.+,-ti etc. C.) Desiderative ninaṃsa- (in d.) Intensive nánnamīti etc. V.B. (nannamus B.),-māna (námnate anamnata RV.); nannamyate S Verbal Nouns PPP: natá V.+; Inf: naṃtum C., namitum C.; 1Abs: natvā C.; 2Abs: -nátya B.,-namya E.+;-námam -náme RV Derivatives -nam AV. námī ? RV. -nāma E.+ nemí V.+ náma RV. ? E.+ nati AV.+ -nāmaka C. -nannama RV. namana C. náṃtva RV. nāmin V.+ -ninaṃsu C. namanīya C. naṃtṛ C. nāmya E.+ namayitavya C. námas V.+ namrá V.+ nāmana C. -namayitṛ C. namasāná V. -nāmuka B. namayiṣṇu RV. Meanings námati námate v PPP natá (q.v.) bend, bow (mostly intrans.), yield or submit to (D or G, r. A); aim at (G) with (I). Caus. namayati or (mostly – ṃ) nāmayati (nāmyati) cause to bend, curve; w. cāpam or dhanus bend a bow; cerebralize (g.). Int. nannamīti bend (intrans.), bow very low. ati hold aside. anu incline to (D). abhi bow or incline to (D). ava bend down (intrans.), bow; Caus. the same (trans.), w. dhanujyām bend the bow. ā (intrans.) bend, stoop, bow before (A); trans. bend down, overthrow, subdue. Caus. = prec. trans., w. dhanus bend a bow. ud rise, ascend (lit. & fig.), also = Caus. raise, lift, erect. samud rise; Caus. = prec. Caus. upa come or repair to, befall, occur, come into the mind (w. A, later also w. D or G of pers.), approach or wait upon (A) with (I). Caus. bring near, offer or present to (G). ni bend (trans. & intrans.), bow to (A), humble one's self, submit. pari (intrans.) bend aside, stoop; change, develop, ripen, fade, be accomplished. Caus. ripen, bring to an end, pass (time). pra bend or bow before (D, G, L, or A). Caus. bow (trans.); make a person (A) bend before (D). abhipra bend or bow before (D or A), prati incline towards (A). vi bow, bend (intrans.); Caus. the same trans. sam bow, bend, humble one's self, submit to (D, G, or A); Ā yield or conform one's self to, obey (D); make straight or right. arrange, prepare (PĀ). Caus. bend down, make sink, change, arrange, prepare, accomplish. Cf. ápanata, abhyunnata (add.), avanata, ā́nata, unnatá, úpanata, nirṇata, pariṇata, praṇata, pronnata, vinata, sánata samabhyunnata, samunnata. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_nard.html"> √ nard    √ nard, “bellow” Present I. nardati etc. B.+,-te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: nardiṣyati Periphrastic Future: narditā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: anardīt Perfect nanarda E Causative -nardayati GB Intensive nānardyamāna C Verbal Nouns PPP: nardita E.+;-nardam E Derivatives -narda S.+ -nardin U. nardana C. Meanings nardati v (nardate), PPP nardita bellow, roar, scream, sound. abhi roar to (A). prati roar or scream against (A); roar after (food etc.). vi roar out, cry, thunder. sam roar. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_naz.html"> √ 1 naś    √ 1 naś, “be lost” Present I. náśati -te etc. V.E.+ IV. náśyati etc. V.+,-te etc. E Future Simple Future: naśiṣyati AV.+; naṅkṣyati -te etc. E.+ (anaṅkṣyata M) Periphrastic Future: naśitā E. naṃṣṭā Aorist Th Ao: anaśat E.+ RAo: aneśat etc. V.B.; anīnaśat etc. V.+ (nīnaśus E.) Perfect nanāśa V.E., neśus B.+ Causative nāśáyati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ (nāśayádhyai RV.; nināśayiṣa- C.) Desiderative ninaśiṣa- , ninaṅkṣa- Intensive nānaś- Verbal Nouns PPP: naṣṭá V.+; Inf: naṣṭum, naṃṣṭum; 1Abs: naṣṭvā, naṃṣṭvā Derivatives -naś RV.B. naṣṭi B.+ nāśin B.+ nāṣṭrā́ AV.B. -naṃśin V.S. naśvara C. nāśya E.+ nāśayitṛ́ VS. naśana B.+ nāśa B.+ nā́śana AV.+ naṃśuka K. nāśaka E.+ nāśuka TS. The forms from the stem naśa are perhaps to be classed as of RAo. Meanings náśyati 1 v (náśyati 1 (te) & náśate) & náśati (te), PPP naṣṭá (q.v.) be lost or missing, vanish, disappear, wane, perish, fly, escape, be gone. Caus. nāśáyati (te), PPP nāśita make disappear, expel, destroy, violate, deflower; lose, also from memory, i.e. forget. apa be gone. ava wane, disappear. nis Caus. expel, drive away. pra (ṇaśyati) be lost, disappear, run away. vipra be lost, vanish, have no effect or result. saṃpra disappear, cease. vi be lost, vanish, perish, have no effect or success; be deprived of (Ab). Caus. make disappear, destroy, annihilate, kill. anuvi disappear or perish after (A). Cf. pranaṣṭa, vinaṣṭa, vipranaṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_naz.html"> √ 2 naś, naṃś    √ 2 naś, naṃś, “attain” Present I. náśati -te etc. V Aorist √-Ao: ā́naṭ V.B. (naṭ V.; anaṣṭām nak nakṣi impv. náṃśi naśimahi RV.) Desiderative ínakṣati etc. RV Verbal Nouns -náśe RV.VS Derivatives náṃśa RV. -náṃśana RV. -náśa V. -nā́śa RV.S. The form ā́naṭ is by some referred to √ 1 aś. Compare √ nakṣ. Meanings (naṃś), náśati, náśate attain, get, meet with (L); reach, befall. Des ínakṣati q.v. – accha come near. abhi , ud , pari , pra , vi & sam reach, attain. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_nas.html"> √ nas    √ nas, “unite” Present I. násate etc. RV Aorist √-Ao: nasīmahi RV Meanings násate 1 v meet, encounter; copulate (man and wife). sam meet, join with (I). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_nah.html"> √ nah    √ nah, “tie” Present I. nahet M IV. náhyati -te etc. V.+ (nahyus AB.) Passive nahyate C Future Simple Future: natsyati -te Periphrastic Future: naddhā Aorist RAo: anīnahat -iṣ-Ao: anātsīt anaddha Perfect nanāha (nanaddha nehitha) nehe Causative nāhayati etc. S.+ Desiderative ninatsa- Intensive nānah- Verbal Nouns PPP: naddhá V.+; 1Abs: naddhvā; 2Abs: -náhya B.+ Derivatives -nah (nádh) V.+ náhus V.+ nāha AV.+ -nāhana C. náhana V.+ -naddhi B. -nāhya B.S. -nāhuka ? AB. náhas ? C. -naddhavya E.+ Meanings náhyati v (nahati), PPP naddhá (q.v.) tie, bind on; Ā put on, esp. armour, arm one's self. Caus. nāhayati cause to tie together. apa unbind, loosen. api or pi tie on, fasten, bind under, cover, obstruct. ava bind on, put over, cover. ā bind on; Ā be stopped up. ud push off, remove; break forth, rise from (Ab). upa tie up, bind together. pari tie round, gird, encircle. sam tie together, bind over, fasten; gird, clothe, arm (Ā refl.); PĀ put on, make ready or prepare to (Inf). Cf. ápinaddha, ānaddha, unnaddha, nínaddha, pariṇaddha, vínaddha, sánaddha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_naath.html"> √ nāth, nādh    √ nāth, nādh, “seek aid” Present I. nāthate etc. B.+,-ti etc. E.+; nā́dhamāna V Passive nāthyate C Future Simple Future: nāthiṣyati, nādhiṣyate Periphrastic Future: nāthitā, nādhitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: anāthīt, anādhiṣṭa Perfect nanātha , nanādhe Verbal Nouns PPP: nāthitá B.+, nādhitá RV.; Inf: nāthitum C.; 2Abs: -nāthya C Derivatives nāthá V.+ -nādha B. nā́dhas RV. Meanings nāth : nā́thate v (nā́thati), PPP nāthitá (q.v.) seek aid; beg or ask for (G or *D of th. or 2A). Caus. nāthayati cause to ask. anu & upa P ask. nādh : = nāth, only nā́dhamāna seeking aid, supplex, & nādhitá = nāthitá a. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ni_ms.html"> √ niṃs    √ niṃs, “kiss” Present II. níṃsate niṃsata níṃsāna RV Future Simple Future: niṃsiṣyate Periphrastic Future: niṃsitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aniṃsiṣṭa Perfect niniṃse Derivatives -niṃsin C. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_nik_s.html"> √ nikṣ    √ nikṣ, “pierce” Present I. míkṣati etc. AV Future Simple Future: nikṣiṣyati Periphrastic Future: nikṣitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: anikṣīt Perfect ninikṣa Verbal Nouns -níkṣe V Derivatives -nikṣaṇa C. nī́kṣaṇa ? RV. nékṣaṇa AV.S. Is perhaps a desiderative formation from √ 1 naś. Meanings níkṣati v pierce. vi = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_nij.html"> √ nij    √ nij, “wash” Present II. ? nije C., nijāná RV III. ninikta (2p.) RV Passive nijyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: nekṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: nektā Aorist Th Ao: anijam -jan AV.S RAo: anīnijat -s-Ao: anaikṣīt nikṣi AV Perfect nineja , ninije Causative nejayati etc. B.+ Desiderative ninikṣa- Intensive nénekti nenikté etc. V.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: niktá V.+; 1Abs: niktvā́ B.+; 2Abs: -níjya B.+;-níje RV Derivatives -nij V.S. -neka S.C. -neja C. néjana V.+ -nikti C. -nega B.S. nejaka C. -nektṛ S. . -nejya PB The intensive is regarded by the grammarians as the present-stem of this root. Meanings PPP niktá (q.v.), I. nénekti, nenikté wash, cleanse, purify; Ā refl. ava = S; Caus. avanejayati cause to wash off. abhyava PĀ wash, cleanse; Caus. = prec. Caus. nis P wash off, cleanse; Ā wash, dress, or adorn one's self. pra wash off, cleanse. vi wipe off. Cf. nirṇikta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_nind.html"> √ nind, nid    √ nind, nid, “revile” Present I. níndati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ Passive nidyáte RV.; nindyate C Future Simple Future: nindiṣyati Periphrastic Future: ninditā E Aorist √-Ao: nindyāt U., nidāná RV -iṣ-Ao: ánindiṣus RV.S. (níndiṣat AV.) Perfect nininda E.+ (nindima ninidús RV.) Desiderative nínitsati RV.,-te S Verbal Nouns PPP: ninditá V.+; 2Abs: -nindya E Derivatives níd RV. nindā́ AV.+ níndya V.+ ninditṛ́ RV. nídā RV. nindaka E.+ nindana C. ninitsú RV. -nedya RV. nindin C. nindanīya C. Meanings nind , níndati v (níndate), PPP nindita (q.v.) revile, abuse, blame, despise; ridicule, mock, sur pass. Des nínitsati be willing to revile. prati & vi revile, censure, reproach. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_nii.html"> √ nī    √ nī, “lead” Present I. náyati -te etc. V.+ II. néṣi V.S., nethá RV., ánītām RV III ? ninīthás ninīyāt RV., ninetu MS Passive nīyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: neṣyati etc. AV.+,-te etc. B.+ (aneṣyathās M.); nayiṣyati etc. JB.E.+ (anayiṣyat JB.), -te etc. R Periphrastic Future: netā E., nayitā E Aorist √-Ao: anāyi RAo: anīnayat -s-Ao: anaiṣīt etc. V.+ (nais anait B.S.; neṣati etc. RV., néṣat V.B., neṣa AV.), aneṣṭa etc. V.B -iṣ-Ao: anayīt AV., anayīṣṭa (2p.) S. anāyiṣata (Ps) C Perfect ninā́ya ninyus etc. V.+ (ninétha RV., nīnima TS.), ninye B.+-nayām āsa M.,-nayāṃ cakre R Causative nāyayati etc. E.+,-te R Desiderative nínīṣati etc. V.+,-te etc. U.S.+ Intensive nenīyáte etc. V.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: nītá V.+; Inf: nétum B.+,-tavaí B.S.,-tos B.S., nayitum B.+; 1Abs: nītvā́ B.+, nayitvā E.+; 2Abs: -nī́ya AV.+; neṣáni RV.;-nāyam JB Derivatives -nī V.+ -nāyya C. netrá AV.+ néṣa RV. naya V.+ -nāyana C. nīthá V.+ néṣṭṛ V.+ -nayin E.+ nīti V.+ nī́thā V. -nenī RV. nayana U.S.+ netavya E.+ neman- ? RV. ninīṣā E.+ nāyá RV.C. nayitavya E.+ -nī́ya B. ninīṣu E.+ nāyaka E.+ netṛ V.+ neya S.+ -ninīṣeṇya B. -nāyin E. -nayitṛ E. náyiṣṭha RV. Meanings náyati náyate v PPP nītá 1 lead, guide, conduct, direct (l. & f.); carry away, remove; draw near, attract; bring to or into (A, esp. of an abstrans., prati, D, or L); Ā (P) lead home, i.e. marry (a wife); pass or spend (time); make out, ascertain, settle. – With ágram take the lead, head (G); w. daṇḍam bear the rod, i.e. inflict punishment; w. an Adv in sāt reduce to or change into, e.g. bhasmasāt; w. śūdratām make a person (A) a Śūdra; samatām make equal; w. duḥkham make unhappy. pain; w. pritoṣam gratify; w. kṣayam destroy (cf. ī & gam). Caus. nāyayati cause a pers. or th. to be led or carried away by (I) to (A). Des nínīṣati, te be willing to lead etc., to carry off, to bring into (A); to find out or ascertain. I. nenīyáte lead away as a captive, have power of (A). – accha lead near or towards (A). ati lead over or beyond (A); I. bring forward. anu bring near or towards (A); try to win, conciliate; ask, request. pratyanu conciliate, deprecate, ask pardon for (A). apa lead or take away, put off, remove. vyapa the same. abhi lead near or towards (A); fetch, procure; represent, act, perform (d.). ava lead down, push or put into (A or L); pour down, off, or over. abhyava lead down or pour into (A). vyava pour out singly. samava lead or pour together, mix, unite. ā lead or bring near, fetch, cause; lead or bring towards or into (A, w. kśam subject, subdue), lead or bring back (punar); pour in, mix; offer, sacrifice. udā lead up or out (esp. out of the water). upā lead or bring near, draw towards (A); get or cause to (G of pers. & A of th.); lead away, carry off. paryā lead round or near. pratyā lead or bring back, recover; pour to, fill up by pouring in. samā conduct together, gather, collect; lay together (the hands); conduct towards, unite with (I saha); pour together, mix; lead or bring near; carry away, lead home; offer, sacrifice. ud lead upwards, bring up, erect; lead out, deliver, rescue; draw out (water), fill up by drawing; lead off (vadhāṃya to death); find out, investigate, infer. samud lift up, raise (lit. & fig.), investigate, ascertain; pay off (a debt). upa lead near, bring to, present, offer, communicate; carry off, lead away, take to one's self, receive (esp. as a pupil); bring or put into a state or condition, ātmānam betake or expose one's self to (A or L*); bring about, cause, produce. Caus. cause a person (A) to be received as a pupil. samupa draw near, admit, lead to (A), present, offer; lead away, take to one's self; bring about, cause. ni lead to (D or L), cause to (D Inf); bend, incline; pour out or in; offer, sacrifice; perform, accomplish. nis lead or take away; find out, settle, decide. parā lead away or back. pari lead or carry round, esp. lead a bride round the fire, i.e. marry; lead away, carry off, lead near, bring to (A); find out, explore. Caus. pariṇayayati & pariṇāyayati marry a man (A) with a woman (A). pra bring forwards, lead further, promote; convey (r.); conduct or take to (Ā to one's self), present, offer; bring or reduce to (a state); employ, inflict (punishment); state, decide, teach, compose, promulgate; perform, accomplish; show, betray (esp. one's feelings), love, desire. saṃpra bring together, collect, raise (taxes); employ, inflict (punishment); compose, promulgate. prati lead back or towards, put together, mix. vi lead or drive away, remove; spend, pass (time); mix, stir up (Soma etc.); part (the hair); spread, extend; train, discipline, teach, instruct; cause or induce to (D Inf); perform, accomplish. sam lead together, gather, collect, unite; mix together, stir up (r.); bring near, fetch, get, procure; present with (I); give back, restore, return. Cf. apanīta, abhinīta, abhivinīta, nirṇīta, pariṇīta, práṇīta, vinīta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_nii_d.html"> √ nīḍ    √ nīḍ, “nest” May be mentioned on account of nīḍá V.+ and nīḍí RV. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_nu.html"> √ 1 nu, nū    √ 1 nu, nū, “praise” Present I. návate -ti etc. V II. nauti nuvánti etc. V.+ (anāvan RV.) VI. nuvati Passive nūyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: naviṣyati, nuviṣyati Periphrastic Future: navitā, nuvitā Aorist RAo: anūnavat ánūnot etc. RV -s-Ao: anauṣīt, ánūṣi etc. V.B -iṣ-Ao: anāvīt anuvīt, anaviṣṭa RV Perfect nunāva C Causative nāvayati (nunāvayiṣa-.) Desiderative nunūṣa- Intensive nónavīti nonumas etc. V., nonuvanta RV. (nónāva nonuvus RV.); návīnot RV Verbal Nouns PPP: nuta C. nūta; Inf: navitum, nuvitum; 2Abs: -nutya S.;-nāvam B Derivatives -nava B.+ navana C. nāvá RV. nonuva C. návya RV. náviṣṭi RV. nuti C. Meanings nauti nuváti návate návati v PPP nuta 2 roar, sound, exult, praise. I. nónavīti, návīnot howl, thunder. – accha call or shout to (A). anu I. cheer after (A). abhi hail, shout to (A). ā Ā sound, scream; I. sound through (A). pra roar, sound, howl, hum, utter (esp. the syllable oṃ). abhipra shout to, hail (A). sam sound or roar together. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_nu.html"> √ 2 nu    √ 2 nu, “move” Present I. návate etc. RV II. nauti S Causative nāvayati etc. B Verbal Nouns nūta ? PB Meanings návate 3 v (nauti) move (trans & intrans.); Caus. nāvayati move from a place, remove. apa P lay, by. abhi & ava Ā turn to (A). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_nud.html"> √ nud    √ nud, “push” Present VI. nudáti -te etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: notsyati E.,-te B.E Periphrastic Future: nottā Aorist √-Ao: nudyāt E.+ RAo: anūnudat -s-Ao: anautsīt, ánutta etc. V.B -iṣ-Ao: nudiṣṭhās AV Perfect nunoda C., nunude etc. V.+ Causative nodayati etc. U.+ (nodyate E.+) Desiderative nunutsa- (in d.) Intensive anonudyanta B Verbal Nouns PPP: nuttá V.+, nunna SV.E.+, nudita M.; 2Abs: -nudya S.+;-núde RV.,-nudas K.,-nódam V Derivatives -nud V.+ noda V.+ nodya C. -nunutsu C. -nuda E.+ -nodaka C. nodana C. -nodayitavya C. nutti B.+ -nodin C. -nottavya B. Meanings nudáti nudáte v PPP nuttá 1 & nunna push, thrust; impel, incite; expel, drive away, remove, reject. Caus. nodayati impel. I. nonudyate drive away repeatedly, chase. apa , vyapa, apā & vyapā push or drive away, chase, remove. nis push out, expel, remove, reject. parā push away, chase, remove. pra push or drive away, chase; impel, incite. prati push back, repel, avert. vi drive asunder or away; strike, wound. Caus. drive away, pass or spend (time); divert, amuse; delight in, enjoy (I). sam press or bring together. Caus. bring near, fetch; impel, incite. upasam = prec. S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_n_r.html"> √ nṛ    √ nṛ, “sport” To be recoginized with probability in the Derivatives narúṇa TA. naríṣṭa AV.VS. nariṣyant E.+ narmá VS. narman E.+ also in sūnára V.B. and sūnṛ- (sūnṛ́tā V.+). Compare also √ nṛt. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_n_rt.html"> √ nṛt    √ nṛt, “dance” Present IV. nṛ́tyati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ Passive nṛtyate C Future Simple Future: nartiṣyati C. nartsyati Periphrastic Future: nartitā Aorist √-Ao: nṛtus RV. (Pf. ?) Th Ao: nṛtámāna ? RV RAo: anīnṛtat, ananartat -iṣ-Ao: anartiṣus V Perfect nanarta nanṛtus E.+ Causative nartáyati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ Desiderative ninartiṣa- (in d.) ninṛtsa- Intensive narīnartti etc. C., narīnṛtyate C.-ti ? C Verbal Nouns PPP: nṛttá AV.+; Inf: nartitum C., narttum C.; 1Abs: nartitvā C.; 2Abs: -nartam B Derivatives nṛ́t AV. -nartin VS. nṛtú RV. nartayitṛ E. nṛtya U.+ nartana S.+ nṛtū́ RV. ninartiṣā C. -narta E.+ nṛ́ti ? AV. -nṛtti B. nartaka E.+ nṛtí V. nartitavya C. Compare roots √ naṭ and √ nṛ. Meanings nṛ́tyati (nṛ́tyate) v PPP nṛttá 1 dance; play, act, represent (d.). Caus. nartáyati (te) cause to dance or to move to and fro. I. narinartti, narīnartti, narīnṛtyati, nṛ́tyati (te), PPP nṛttá 1 dance; play, act, represent (d.). Caus. nartáyati (te) cause to dance or to move to and fro. I. narinartti, narīnartti, narīnṛtyate (cause to) dance about or to and fro. anu dance after or before (A). ā dance or hasten near. Caus. cause to dance or move gently. upa dance before (A). pari dance about (A). pra dance (forwards), begin to dance. sam dance together. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ned.html"> √ ned    √ ned, “flow” Present I. nédati etc. B.,-te U Future Simple Future: nediṣyati, -te Periphrastic Future: neditā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: anedīt, -diṣṭa Perfect nineda , ninede ninide Derivatives -neda MS. Meanings nédati 1 v w. ati overflow. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_pac.html"> √ pac    √ pac, “cook” Present I. pácati -te etc. V.+ (pacāna M.) IV. pácyate etc. RV.ŚB Passive pacyáte etc. V.+,-ti M Future Simple Future: pakṣyati -te etc. B.+ (apakṣyat C.) Periphrastic Future: paktā́ B Aorist √-Ao: pacyāt; apāci RAo: apīpacat -s-Ao: apākṣīt, apakta pákṣat RV Perfect papā́ca pecus etc. V.B. papaktha, pecitha, pece pecire etc. V.+ (ápeciran AV.) Causative pācayati -te etc. B.+ (pācyate E.) Desiderative pipakṣa- Intensive pāpacyate etc. C Verbal Nouns (pakvá;) páktave AV.B.; 1Abs: paktvā́ AV.E Derivatives pac ? C. paktí RV. pakthín RV. pācaka E.+ -paca B.+ pákti VS.+ pakvá V.+ -pācin C. -pacya AV. paktavya E. pacelima C. pācya U. pácana V.+ paktṛ́ AV.+ pāka V.+ pācana C. pacatá V.B. paktrima C. pākin C. -pācayitṛ C. pacatyà RV. pakthá RV.B. pākya U.S.+ Meanings pácati pácate v cook, bake, boil, roast, burn (bricks), digest; mature, ripen, develop (trans., pácyate intrans.); P. pacyáte be cooked etc., also intrans. = pácyate. Caus. pācayati, te cook or cause to cook (trans.), bring to maturity or perfection. pari P. be cooked or roasted, grow mature (lit. & fig.), bear results. vi cook thoroughly; P. be cooked or digested, ripen i.e. have results (of an action). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_paj.html"> √ paj    √ paj, “start”( ?) Present I. pā́paje RV1 Derivatives pajrá V.S. pā́jas V.B. The connection of form and meaning among these words is altogether questionable. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_pa_t.html"> √ paṭ    √ paṭ, “tear” Present I. paṭati C1 Causative pāṭayati etc. U.+,-te etc. E. (pāṭyate c.) Derivatives pāṭa E.+ pāṭaka B.+ -pāṭin C. pāṭana E.+ pāṭya C. pāṭanīya C. Meanings paṭati v split, burst, open (intrans.). Caus. pāṭayati cause to split etc., break asunder, rend, tear, cut off, hurt, injure. ava Caus. split, tear asunder, open. ud & samud Caus. the same + expel, remove, dethrone. vi split, tear, rend, divide, root out, remove, drive away. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_pa_th.html"> √ paṭh    √ paṭh, “read” Present I. paṭhati etc. TA.+,-te etc. E.+ Passive paṭhyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: paṭhiṣyati Periphrastic Future: paṭhitā Aorist RAo: apīpaṭhat -iṣ-Ao: apā̆ṭhīt Perfect papāṭha C Causative pāṭhayati etc. C. (pāṭhyate C.) Desiderative pipaṭhiṣa- Intensive pāpaṭhīti etc. C., pāpaṭhyate C Verbal Nouns PPP: paṭhita S.+; 1Abs: paṭhitvā C Derivatives paṭhaka E. paṭhitavya C. pāṭha S.+ pāṭhya E.+ paṭhana C. paṭhiti C. pāṭhaka E.+ pāṭhana C. paṭhanīya C. pāṭhin E.+ Meanings paṭhati (paṭhate) v read aloud, recite, rehearse; teach, mention; repeat to one's self, study, learn from (Ab). Caus. pāṭhayati teach to talk or read, teach i.g. (2A); read, peruse. Int pāpaṭhīti & pāpaṭhyate recite often, read or study diligently. anu speak after, repeat. pari enumerate, name, mention. pra recite aloud; Caus. teach, explain. vi & sam read, peruse. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_pa_n.html"> √ paṇ    √ paṇ, “bargain” Present I. paṇate etc. B.+,-ti etc. E.+ Passive paṇyate etc. E Future Simple Future: paṇiṣyate Periphrastic Future: paṇitā Aorist RAo: apīpaṇat -iṣ-Ao: apaṇiṣṭa Perfect peṇe Causative paṇayati etc. C. pāṇayati Desiderative pipaṇiṣa- Intensive pampaṇ- Verbal Nouns PPP: paṇita E.; 1Abs: paṇitvā S Derivatives paṇa AV.+ páṇana B.+ paṇāyya B. -pāṇa AV. -paṇin C. paṇí V.+ vaṇíj ? V.+ pāṇí ? V.+ páṇya B.+ paṇitṛ C. paṇayitṛ C. Meanings páṇate (páṇati) v PPP paṇita (q.v.) bargain, barter, buy; bet, wage, stake, risk, play for (G); win a thing (I) from (A) at play. vi sell; bet, stake (G). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_pat.html"> √ 1 pat    √ 1 pat, “fly, fall” Present I. pátati etc. B.+,-te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: patiṣyáti etc. AV.+,-te E. (apatiṣyat B.+) Periphrastic Future: patitā M Aorist √-Ao: apāti B RAo: apaptat etc. V.B.S.; apīpatat etc. V Perfect papā́ta petús etc. V.+ (paptima paptús paptivā́ṃs RV.; papatyāt AV.) Causative pātáyati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ (pātyate etc. E.+); patáyati etc. V.B.S.,-te RV Desiderative pipatiṣati etc. AV. ŚB.; pitsa- (in d.) Intensive pā́patīti etc. RV. panīpat- Verbal Nouns PPP: patitá AV.+; Inf: pátitum B.; 1Abs: patitvā́ AV.B.; 2Abs: -pátya B.+;-pā́tam B.+ Derivatives -pat RV. pátman V.B. pāta AV.+ -paptani RV. pata- V.+ -patya B. pātaka S.+ patāpata S. pátana V.+ pátvan V.B.S. pātin AV.+ pīpatiṣu E.+ -ptu ? MS. patará RV. pātya E.+ -pitsu C. patāka S.+ patáru RV. pātana S.+ patayālú AV.C -patitavya C. pátiṣṭha V.B. pātanīya C. patayiṣṇú V. páttra V.+ -patiṣṇu B.+ pā́tuka B.+ pātayitṛ C. pátatra V.C. patīyas B. Meanings pátati (pátate) v PPP patitá (q.v.) fly, soar, rush; come down, descend, fall or sink (lit. & fig. adhas), lose caste, rank, or position; fall or light upon (L); incur or get into (L); come to pass, happen. Caus. pātáyati, pátati (te), PPP patitá (q.v.) fly, soar, rush; come down, descend, fall or sink (lit. & fig. adhas), lose caste, rank, or position; fall or light upon (L); incur or get into (L); come to pass, happen. Caus. pātáyate (& patayati q.v.) cause to fly or fall, pour out or shed (water, tears, etc.); hurl, cast, throw; put, turn, direct to, impose or inflict upon (L); throw down, fell, ruin, cut off or asunder, divide (dvedhā́); Ā rush on, hasten. Des pipatiṣati & pitsati being about to fly or to fall in. – accha fly towards (A). ati fly or fall beyond or past. anu fly to, through, or after; go after, follow, pursue. antar fly into (L). abhi fly or hasten near, go towards or against; fall down or upon, come into (A). Caus. throw on (D or L); throw down, kill. samabhi rush upon (A). ava fly, jump, fall down or upon (A). ā fly or hasten near, fall into or upon (A or L); happen, occur, fall to one's (G) share. Caus. throw or cut down, let fall, shed (tears). abhyā hasten near, rush upon (A). samā fly or hasten near, rush upon (A); come to, obtain; have sexual intercourse with (saha). ud fly or spring up, come forth, rise, start, set out, escape. Caus. cause to fly up, lift, raise. abhyud fly or jump up. Caus. cause to fly up to (A). samud fly or spring up (together) etc. = ud S. upa fly near, hasten towards (A or L). ni fly down, alight, descend, fall or rush upon (A or L), get or fall into (L), tumble down, throw one's self down (pādayos); happen, occur (w. G = come into the mind*), fall to the share of (L), fall into ruin, be lost or in vain. Caus. cause to fall, let fall, drop, throw down; put in, turn upon (L); fell, destroy, kill; put down, establish (g.). praṇi throw one's self down, bow to (A, D, or L). Caus. cause to fall down or bow. vini fly, fall, rush, descend upon or into (L); attack, assail. Caus. throw down, cut off or split (the head), inflict (punishment); destroy, ruin, kill. saṃni fly, fall, or descend upon (L); assemble, meet, encounter; come together with (I saha). Caus. throw down, shoot off; collect, unite, bring together. nis & vinis fly or rush out, come forth, depart, retreat, escape. parā fly away or past, fall out or down, depart, escape, retreat, stay away, fail; fly along, hasten; come near, arrive. pari fly or run about, round, or to and fro; leap down from (Ab), rush or fall upon (L). Caus. cause to fall down, shoot off, throw into. pra fly forth or along, hasten to (L); fall down, rush upon, come into (L). Caus. cause to flee, pursue. vi fly along or through; split, burst asunder (intrans.). Caus. cause to fly away, shoot off; rend asunder, throw down, destroy, kill. sam fly or rush together; meet, encounter (of friends & foes); hasten on or towards (A), come to, arrive at (A or L); fall down upon, get into (L), happen, pass, occur. Caus. hurl upon, throw down into (L). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_pat.html"> √ 2 pat    √ 2 pat, “rule” Present IV. pátyate etc. V.B Doubtless only a denominative of páti. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_path.html"> √ path    √ path, “go” (?) Present I. páthati etc. S Future Simple Future: pathiṣyati Periphrastic Future: pathitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: apathīt Perfect papātha Causative pāthayati B.S Derivatives páth pathí pánthan V.+ pánthā V. pánthan- B. pā́thas V.+ pā́this B. No real root; the present forms doubtless bad readings for patati etc.; the causative a denominative of the stem path. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_pad.html"> √ pad    √ pad, “go” Present II. ? padyām R1., patsva M1 IV. pádyate etc. V.+,-ti etc. AB.E Future Simple Future: patsyati etc. B.+ (patsyantu C.),-te etc. U.+ Periphrastic Future: pattā Aorist √-Ao: apadi ŚB. (3s. pass. ?) apadmahi etc. VS.-dran RV. (padāti -dāt V.; padīṣṭá V.); ápādi pā́di V.+ RAo: apīpadat AV.B -s-Ao: apatsi etc. V.B.U. (patthās AV.) Perfect papāda pedus etc. V.+, pede etc. B.+ Causative pādáyati etc. V.+,-te etc. AV.+ (pādyate etc. B.+; pipādayiṣati B.+) Desiderative pitsati B.,-te C Intensive panīpadyate C Verbal Nouns PPP: panná AV.+; Inf: páttum B.+,-tave RV.,-tos B.; 2Abs: -pádya V.+;-pádas V.B.;-pā́dam B.+ Derivatives -pad V.+ pattí AV.+ -pādin C. -pitsā C. pā́d V.+ -pattavya E.+ -pā́dya B.+ -pitsu C. padá V.+ -pattṛ C. -pādana E.+ -patsu C. -padana B.U.S. -padva ? C. -pādanīya C. -pādayitavya C. padanī́ya B.+ -pāda B.+ pādú ? RV.MS. -pādayitṛ C. -pádi RV1. -pādaka E.+ pā́duka B.C. -pipādayiṣā C. -pipādayiṣu C. Meanings pádyate (pádyati) v PPP panná 1 (q.v.) fall, drop, fall out, sink down, perish; (mostly – ṃ) go, step, tread; go to (A). Caus. pādáyati, pádyate (ti), PPP panná 1 (q.v.) fall, drop, fall out, sink down, perish; (mostly – ṃ) go, step, tread; go to (A). Caus. pādáyate bring to fall. ati go beyond (A); transgress, neglect (also Caus. ). anu go after, follow, betake one's self to or into; get at, befall. apa escape. api enter. abhi approach, appear, betake one's self to or into, meet with (A, r. L); catch, seize, overpower, master, undertake, accept. ava fall down or out; lose, be deprived or fall short of (Ab). ā come near, approach, enter; get into, meet with (A), esp. get in trouble, meet with an accident; happen, occur, be; evamāpadyate so is it. Caus. cause to go or enter, bring to or into (A), esp. bring to fall, ruin, destroy; bring near, procure, occasion; get, obtain. abhyā get into (A). pratyā come back, return. vyā perish, be lost; Caus. destroy, kill. samā attack, assail; get into (A); occur, appear. ud come forth or out of (Ab), be born, happen, occur, appear, arise, begin. Caus. P (Ā) procreate, beget with (L), cause, effect, produce, bring forth; grow (plants or animals), spill (blood), kindle (fire). vyud originate (scil. from a root), have an etymology (g.). Caus. produce, cause; derive, trace back to a root (g.). samud come forth, be born of (L), happen, occur, present one's self. Caus. bring forth, effect, cause, produce. upa fall upon, attack; come near, approach (esp. for aid or instruction); get to or into (A or L), fall to the lot of (G); happen, occur, take place, appear as (N), turn to (D); be fit or right. Caus. bring about, cause, effect, arrange, prepare; make or appoint (2A); present or furnish with (2A or A of pers. & I of th.); give (also in marriage), offer, procure, bestow on (A of th. & D, r. L of pers.); find out, ascertain, prove. abhyupa approach, ask for help (A); endow or furnish with (I). ni lie down, rest; lie with (A); Caus. lay down, fell, destroy. anuni & upani (A) lie with. nis come forth, spring up, arise, ripen, be accomplished. Caus. P (Ā) bring about, make ripe, prepare, accomplish, settle, decide. abhinis come to, enter (A), come forth, appear. pra come or resort to (A), visit, enter, get, obtain, meet with (A), undertake, begin; happen, take place, become, be; assent, agree. anupra enter after (A), follow, obey. abhipra approach, enter, undertake, begin; get at, resort to (A). saṃpra enter (together), repair or resort to (A); be accomplished or brought about. prati step to, enter upon, resort to, get at or into, meet with (A), undertake, begin; happen, take place; perform, accomplish, make = reddere (2A), do anything to, behave towards (L, G, or A); find out, learn, understand, think, judge (w. anyathā falsely); accede, yield, consent, confess, promise, answer (uttaram). Caus. lead or bring to (A); get, procure; give (also in marriage) to, present, bestow on (2A or A of th. & L, D, or G of pers.); cause, effect, produce; make clear, explain, teach, show. viprati go hither and thither, be perplexed or uncertain, waver. saṃprati go to, get at (A); obtain, recover; consent, agree, acknowledge; take for (2A). vi fall asunder, go amiss, fail, perish, die. Caus. destroy, kill. sam fall to, devolve upon (L or G); turn out well, succeed, prosper; come together, meet with, get at (A or I); arise, be born, become (N or D = turn out to be, be changed into). Caus. P (Ā) procure, furnish, present, provide (A of th. & D or G of pers. or A of pers. & I of th.); bring about, accomplish, make ready, prepare, transform, make into (2A), get, obtain; agree, consent. abhisam be changed into, become like (A); get at, obtain (A or L). Caus. make into or like (A). upasam come to, arrive at (A). Caus. bring near, procure. Cf. avapanna, āpanna, utpanna, upapanna, upasaṃpanna, niṣpanna, pratipanna, pratyutpanna, pratyupapanna, prapanna, vipanna, vipratipanna, vyutpanna, samutpanna, sápanna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_pan.html"> √ pan    √ pan, “admire” Present I. pánanta RV Passive panyáte RV Aorist -iṣ-Ao: paniṣṭa (3s.) RV Perfect papana papné RV Causative panáyati -te etc. RV Intensive pánipnat V.B Verbal Nouns PPP: panitá RV Derivatives pana- RV. panas- RV. paniṣṭama SV. pányas RV. pánya RV.K. panú RV. pániṣṭi SV. -panyā RV. panā́yya RV.AB. panitṛ́ RV. pániṣṭha V.B. -panyu RV. pánīyas V. panayā́yya RV. The words paṇya S., paṇā́yya ŚB. seem to belong in meaning to this root. Meanings pánate v PPP panitá be wonderful; admire, praise, commend. Caus. panáyati, te = S. tr ; Ā also rejoice at, be glad of (A or G). ā admire, praise. vi P. pride one's self. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_pard.html"> √ pard    √ pard, “fart” Present I. pardate C1 Derivatives parda , pardin pardana Meanings pardate v fart, to break wind downwards 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_paz.html"> √ 1 paś, spaś    √ 1 paś, spaś, “see” Present IV. páśyati -te etc. V.+ Aorist √-Ao: áspaṣṭa (Pr. ?) RV. apaspaśat Perfect paspaśé etc. V Causative spāśayate etc. V.B.,-ti S Verbal Nouns PPP: spaṣṭa V.+ Derivatives páś ? RV. paśyin C. -paśyana C. spaśa B.+ paśya V.+ paśyata AV. spáś V.B. -spā́śana AV. paspaśā C. The stem paśya is regarded as supplying the deficient present of √ dṛś. Meanings only Pr páśyati, only Pr páśyate 1 (cf. √ spaś & √ dṛś) see, behold, perceive, look, look on, try, examine, ponder; regard or consider as, take for (2A or A & Adv in vat), see with the spiritual eye (of seers and poets), find out, invent. ati look beyond. anu look at, behold, discover, regard or consider as etc. = S. ava look at, observe. ud look up, foresee, expect, behold, perceive. pari look over, survey, descry, discover, learn, understand, know as (2A). pra look forward, foresee, view, behold, know, recognize, take for (2A). prati look at, behold, experience, learn. vi see in different places or in detail, discern, distinguish; perceive, observe, know, understand. abhivi behold, perceive. sam see (together or at the same time), look over, survey, observe, consider, try, examine, perceive, behold, know, understand; Ā look at each other, be together. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_paz.html"> √ 2 paś    √ 2 paś, “bind” Regarded as inferable from paśú V.+, pā́śa V.+. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_paa.html"> √ 1 pā    √ 1 pā, “drink” Present I. píbati -te etc. V.+ II. pānti RV1., pāthás AV1 III. pipatu K., pipīte pipate pipīya apipīta B., pipāná RV., pípāna AV Passive pīyáte etc. AV.+ Future Simple Future: pāsyati -te etc. B.+ Periphrastic Future: pātā Aorist √-Ao: apāt etc. V.+ (pāhí pātám pātá pā́nt V.); peyās (3s.) RV.; ápāyi RV RAo: apīpyat -s-Ao: pāsta AV Perfect papaú etc. V.+ (papātha RV., papīyāt RV.), pape etc. V Causative pāyáyati etc. V.+,-te C. (pāyyate S.; pipāyayiṣet K.) Desiderative pipāsati etc. V.+; pípīṣati etc. RV. (√ 1 pī ?) Intensive pepīyate etc. U.C. pāpā- Verbal Nouns PPP: pītá V.+; Inf: pātum C., pā́tave V.B.,-tavai B.S.,-tos KB.; 1Abs: pītvā́ V.B.S.,-tvī́ RV.;-pā́ya AV.S., 2Abs: -pīya E.+;-paí ? RV.; píbadhyai RV. pāyam Derivatives -pā̆ V.+ pā́nta RV. pitú ? V.B. -piba AV.C. pā́na V.+ -pāyaka E. pītí V.B.S. papí RV. pānīya E.+ -pāyin B.+ -pītha V.+ pipāsā́ B.+ pātavya B.+ -pā́yya RV.C. -péya V.+ pipāsu E.+ pātṛ V.+ pāyána V.+ pipīṣu RV. pā́tra V.+ -pā́van V.B. pāyayitavyà MS. Compare √ 3 pā. Meanings píbati píbate (pāti) v PPP pītá 1 (with pass., r. with P mg), drink, imbibe, swallow, draw in, enjoy. Caus. pāyáyati, PPP pāyitá give to drink (2A). Des pipāsati (pípīṣati) wish to drink, be thirsty. Int pepīyate drink greedily or repeatedly (also w. pass. mg). ā drink up, drink out of (Ab) or at (A); imbibe, absorb, draw in, enjoy. ni drink in, imbibe, absorb. pari drink before and after (A), drink or draw up. pra begin to drink, drink in, sip. vi drink up, drink largely, drink out of (Ab). sam P & Ā drink in together. Cf. pipāsant & pipāsita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_paa.html"> √ 2 pā    √ 2 pā, “protect” Present II. pā́ti etc. V.+ (pāná RV1.) Passive pāyate Future Simple Future: pāsyati Periphrastic Future: pātā Aorist -s-Ao: pāsati etc. RV -siṣ-Ao: apāsīt C Perfect papau Causative pālayati Desiderative pipāsa- Intensive pāpā- Verbal Nouns pāta ; pātum E Derivatives -pā̆ V.+ pātṛ́ V.C. pāla V.+ pitṛ́ ? V.+ -pā́na AV.+ pā́tra ? RV1. -pā́van V.B. -pīti RV. pātavya C. pāyú V. páti ? V.+ -pītha V. -pā́yya RV. -pī́thya RV. Meanings pā́ti 3 v (PPP pāná) protect, watch, shelter from or defend against (Ab); rule, govern; keep, observe. abhi guard, observe. ni protect, shelter from (Ab), watch, observe, keep. nis protect from (Ab). pari protect on all sides, observe, keep, maintain. pra protect or shelter from (Ab). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_3_paa.html"> √ 3 pā    √ 3 pā, “rise against” BR. refer to such a root certain forms from the reduplicated middle stem pipī with prefix ud. Since, however, such forms occur with the unquestionable meaning “drink”, and, on the other hand, forms from ut-piba ( ŚB.) with the meaning given to √ 3 pā, it seems probable that we have here only a curiously specialized use of ud+√ 1 pā. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_paay.html"> √ pāy    √ pāy, “to void excrement” Present I. pāyate ? U Derivatives pāyú B.+ A single very doubtful occurrence (see BR.). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_pi.html"> √ pi, pī    √ pi, pī, “swell, fatten” Present I. páyate RV II ? píyāna RV III ? pīpihí V.B., pipyatam etc. pīpáyat etc. pīpaya ápīpet etc. (-payat -pema -pyan) pīpáyanta pī́pyāna RV V. pinvánt -vatī́ AV., pinvire pinvāná RV., pinvāte apinvātām JB Perfect pīpā́ya etc. (pīpetha pipyathus -yus pīpivā́ṃs pipyúṣ-) pipye ? (pīpyāná) RV Verbal Nouns pīná AV.+ Derivatives -paya ? RV. -pit RV. pī́va AV. pīvara E.+ páyas V.+ pitú V.B. pī́van V.+ pī́vas V.B. -pyasa ? AV. pīyū́ṣa V.+ pīvāṃs M. pī́viṣṭha ŚB. The roots pinv and pyā (given for convenience separately) are extensions of this. The classification of the reduplicated forms is difficult and questionable. Meanings (pi) páyate (pīpeti) v PPP pīná 1 & pīpivás (q.v.) swell, be exuberant, overflow; cause to swell or overflow, fill, bless. abhi swell, be exuberant. ā & pra swell or cause to swell. Cf. ā́pīta 2 & ā́pīna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_pinv.html"> √ pinv    √ pinv, “fatten” Present I. pínvati -te etc. V.B.S Future Simple Future: pinviṣyati Periphrastic Future: pinvitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: apinvīt Perfect pipinváthus RV Causative pinvayati ŚB Verbal Nouns pinvitá ŚB Derivatives -pinva RV. pínvana B.S. A secondary root-form, from Pr-stem V. pinu of √ pi, pī, from which stem a few regular forms are also made in the older language. Meanings pínvati pínvate v cause to swell or stream; fill, moisten; pour forth, discharge; intrans. swell, overflow. Caus. pinváyati = S. trans. pra = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_pibd.html"> √ pibd    √ pibd, “be firm”(?) Present I. píbdamāna V.B Derivatives pibdaná V. Meanings only PPP píbdamāna being firm or compact. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_piz.html"> √ piś    √ piś, “adorn” Present VI. piṃśáti -te etc. V.B Passive piśyáte AV Future Simple Future: peśiṣyati Periphrastic Future: peśitā Aorist √-Ao: piśāná RV RAo: apīpiśat -iṣ-Ao: apeśīt Perfect pipéśa pipiśus pipiśé -śre V Causative peśaya- Desiderative pipiśiṣa- pipeśiṣa- Intensive pépiśat -śāna V.B Verbal Nouns PPP: piṣṭá V.B., piśitá AV.+ Derivatives píś V. piśācá V.+ peśa V.+ péśas V.+ piśá V. piśā́ci RV. peśī B.+ peśitṛ́ VS. piśánga V.+ píśuna ? V.+ péśana V. Meanings piśáti piśáte v PPP piśitá 1 & piṣṭá (q.v.) cut up, carve (esp. meat), arrange, prepare, adorn, shape, form; Ā also refl. adorn one's self, be brilliant or beautiful. abhi & ā adorn, embellish. Cf. pepiśát, pépiśāna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_pi_s.html"> √ piṣ    √ piṣ, “crush” Present VI. piṃṣá AV. ?, apiṃṣat M.; piṣeyam piṣantī apiṣan E., ápīṣan AV VII. pináṣṭi piṃṣánti etc. V.+ (piṇák RV.), piṃṣe M Passive piṣyáte etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: pekṣyati U Periphrastic Future: peṣṭā Aorist √-Ao ? apiṣṭām (3d.) C1 RAo: apīpiṣat E -sa- Ao: apikṣan ŚB. apikṣātām Perfect pipéṣa pipiṣe etc. V.+ Causative peṣayati etc. S.+ Desiderative pipikṣa- Intensive pepiṣ- Verbal Nouns PPP: piṣṭá V.+; Inf: péṣṭum B.+,-ṭavaí B.; piṣṭvā́ B.; 2Abs: -piṣya S.+;-péṣam B.+ Derivatives peṣa E.+ peṣya C. péṣaṇa B.+ péṣṭra ? AV. peṣaka C. péṣī RV. peṣṭṛ C. pípiṣvant ? RV. Doubtless we are to read apiṃṣṭām for apiṣṭām (Bhāg. Pur.). Meanings pináṣṭi (piṃṣati) v PPP piṃṣṭá (q.v.) grind, pound, crush, destroy. Caus. peṣayati = S. nis & vinis pound, crush, rub (the hands). pra crush or grind down. prati rub or beat against (together), pound, crush. vi beat asunder, pelt with (I). sam pound, squeeze, crush or grind down. Cf. utpiṣṭa, prápiṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_pis.html"> √ pis    √ pis, “stretch” (?) Present IV. pisyati ŚB Perfect pipisus ŚB Derivatives pésuka ŚB. Meanings písyati v stretch. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_pii.html"> √ 1 pī    √ 1 pī see √ pi. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_pii.html"> √ 2 pī    √ 2 pī see √ pīy. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_pii_d.html"> √ pīḍ    √ pīḍ, “press” Perfect pipīḍé RV Causative pīḍayati etc. AV.+,-te E. (pīḍyate etc. B.+;-pīḍam C.) Derivatives -pīḍa E.+ -pīḍaka C. pīḍanīya E. -pīlana C. pīḍā S.+ -pīḍin C. pīḍayitavya E. pipīla ? AV.+ pīḍana U.+ Meanings pīḍáyati (pīḍáyate) v PPP pīḍita (q.v.) press, squeeze, oppress, suppress, vex, harass, pain, beleaguer (a city), eclipse (sun or moon). abhi press against, tread upon, press, squeeze, vex, pain, beleaguer. ava press down, vex, harass. ā press out, vex, plague. ud press upwards or out of. upa press, suppress, vex, pain. ni press against or together, plague, annoy. nis press out or together. pari press together, compress, plague or torment greatly. pra press, squeeze, pain. sam press together, pain, torment. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_piiy.html"> √ pīy    √ pīy, “abuse” Present I. pī́yati etc. V.B Derivatives píyāru V. pī́yaka AV. pīyatnú RV. pīyú V.B. Meanings pī́yati v abuse, blame. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_pu_t.html"> √ puṭ    √ puṭ, “scale” Present VI. puṭati C Passive puṭyete C Future Simple Future: poṭiṣyati Periphrastic Future: poṭitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: apoṭīt Perfect pupoṭa Causative puṭayati , poṭayati Verbal Nouns puṭita ? C Derivatives puṭa B.+ puṭana C. -poṭa C. -poṭana C. -puṭaka C. -poṭaka C. A late and bastard root, probably denominative of puṭa. Meanings puṭati v to fold or cover. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_puth.html"> √ puth    √ puth, “crush” Present puthyati Future Simple Future: pothiṣyati Periphrastic Future: pothitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: apothīt Perfect pupotha Causative pothayati etc. E.+,-te E.+ Derivatives potha E. pothaka E. Meanings Caus. pothayati (te) crush, destroy. ava , ni , vi = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_pu_s.html"> √ puṣ    √ puṣ, “thrive” Present I. poṣati C1 IV. púṣyati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ IX. puṣṇāti etc. E.+ Passive puṣyate etc. C Future Simple Future: poṣiṣyati, pokṣyati Periphrastic Future: paṣitā, poṣṭā Aorist √-Ao: puṣyāsam -sma B.,-yāt C. apoṣi Th Ao: apuṣat (puṣeyam -ema V.B.S., puṣa S.) RAo: apūpuṣat -iṣ-Ao: apoṣīt Perfect pupóṣa etc. V.+ (pupuṣyās RV.) Causative poṣayati etc. V.+ Desiderative pupoṣiṣa- , pupuṣiṣa-, pupukṣa- Intensive popuṣ- Verbal Nouns puṣṭá V.+; puṣyáse RV Derivatives -puṣ RV.C. pūṣa C. póṣa V.+ -poṣas RV. puṣya V.+ pūṣán V.+ poṣaka E.+ poṣuka B. púṣka- V.+ pūṣaṇá RV.E. poṣin RV.C. poṣṭṛ E.+ púṣpa V.+ pūṣaryà RV. póṣya V.+ poṣitṛ C. puṣṭí V. poṣaṇa E.+ poṣayitnú RV. púṣṭi AV.+ poṣaṇīya C. poṣayiṣṇú AV. Meanings púpyāta v (púpyāte, pupṇāti & poṣati), PPP puṣṭá (q.v.) intrans. thrive, bloom, grow, prosper; trans. cause to thrive etc; cherish, foster, develop, unfold, display, possess, enjoy. Caus. poṣayati cherish, foster, rear, bring up, cause to be nourished by (I). uda (utpuṣṇāti) nourish, make fat. upa = S.* Cf. paripuṣṭa, vipuṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_puu.html"> √ pū    √ pū, “cleanse” Present I. pávate etc. V.B.S. (pávamāna V.+), pava RV1., pavant C1. punīṣé (1s.) RV1 IX. punā́ti punīté etc. V.+ (punāhí SV., punaté RV.) Passive pūyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: paviṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: pavitā Aorist RAo: apīpavat -iṣ-Ao: apāviṣus RV., apaviṣṭa etc. RV.MS Perfect pupuvus B.S.,-ve etc. B. (apupot RV.MS.) Causative paváyati etc. B.S.,-te AA.; pāvayati etc. B.+,-te E. (pāvyate etc. C.) Desiderative pupūṣati C1, pipaviṣa- Intensive popu- Verbal Nouns PPP: pūtá V.+ pavita, pūna; Inf: pavitum JB.; 1Abs: pavitvā, pūtvā́ AV., pūtvī́ RV.;-pū́ya B.S.;-pāvam S Derivatives -pū V.B. pávyā RV. potṛ V.+ -pāva V.+ -pu AV. pávana V.+ potrá V.+ pāvaká V.+ -pvā ? V. pū́ti B.+ pavītṛ́ RV. pāvana E.+ pava C. pūtríma AV. pavitṛ́ AV.+ -puna E.+ pavā́ RV. pavítra V.+ pavayitṛ́ B. Meanings punā́ti punīté pávate 1 v (ti), PPP pūtá (q.v.) cleanse, purify, make clear or bright, sift, discern; contrive, invent, compose; Ā also clear itself, flow clear; grow or be pure (lit. & fig.). Caus. paváyati or pāváyati purify. ati purify, strain over or through (A); Ā pass through (the body). abhi Ā clear itself, flow clear towards or for (A). ā Ā flow clear towards (A) or in (L), bestow by flowing (also P). ud cleanse, purify. nis winnow. parā clear off. pari strain, filter, purify; Ā flow off clear. vi cleanse thoroughly. sam cleanse, purify; Caus. the same. Cf. nípūta, paripūta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_puuj.html"> √ pūj    √ pūj, “reverence” Present I. apūjan ? M1 Aorist apūpujat Perfect pupūjire M1 Causative pūjayati etc. S.+,-te etc. E. (pūjyate etc. E.+) Derivatives pūjā S.+ pūja E.+ pūjana RV.E.+ pūjayitṛ E. pūjaka E.+ pūjanīya E.+ pūjayitavya C. Meanings pūjayati pūjayate v PPP pūjita (q.v.) reverence, worship, honour, present with (I); respect, regard. abhi receive or greet reverentially, honour or present with (I), praise, celebrate. pari esteem highly. pra honour, praise, esteem, present with (I). prati honour (in turn), salute respectfully, esteem, present with (I), praise, extol. sam do honour to, salute respectfully, praise, celebrate, esteem, present with (I). Cf. abhipūjita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_puuy.html"> √ pūy    √ pūy, “stink” Present I. pū́yati etc. B.S.-te Passive popūy- Future Simple Future: pūyiṣyate Periphrastic Future: pūyitā Aorist RAo: apūpuyat -iṣ-Ao: apūyiṣṭa Perfect pupūte Causative pūyaya- Desiderative pupūyiṣa- Intensive popū- Verbal Nouns pūta , pūyita (Caus. ?) ŚB Derivatives pū́ya B.+ pū́ti AV.+ Meanings pū́yati v become foul or putrid, stink. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_puur.html"> √ pūr    √ pūr see √ 1 pṛ. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_p_r.html"> √ 1 pṛ, pṛṇ, pūr    √ 1 pṛ, pṛṇ, pūr, “fill” Present III. píparti píprati etc. V.C. (ápiprata 3s. RV.; pipīpṛhi C1.) IV. pū́ryamāṇa RV1 V. pṛṇuyāt S1 VI. pṛṇáti -te etc. V.B IX. pṛṇā́ti etc. V.B.S Passive pūryáte etc. B.+,-ti etc. E. (or pres. 4.) Future Simple Future: parī̆ṣyati Periphrastic Future: parī̆tā Aorist √-Ao: pūrdhí RV.; apūri C.; priyāsam AV. pūryāt RAo: apūpuram ŚB. (pūpurantu RV.); pīparat RV1 -iṣ-Ao: apārīt, pūriṣṭhās TA Perfect pupūre -rire C. (pupūryās RV.); papāra, paparus paprus papṛvā́ṃs ? MS Causative pārayati ; pūráyati etc. AV.+,-te etc. E.+ (pūryate etc. E.+) Desiderative piparī̆ṣa- , pupūrṣa- Intensive pāpṛ- , popūr- Verbal Nouns PPP: pūrṇá V.+, pṛta S1. pūrita; Inf: pūritum R.; 1Abs: pūrtvā; 2Abs: -pūrya E.+;-puras K.; pṛṇádhyai RV.; -pūram S Derivatives púr V. párīṇas RV. pūraka E.+ pápri RV. -paraṇa C. párīman RV. -pūrin E. pápuri RV. párus V.+ páreman SV. -pū́rya B.E. púpuri SV. párvan V.+ púrīṣa ? V.+ pū́raṇa B.+ púraya ? RV. purú V.+ pūrtí V.+ pūraṇīya C. pūrayitṛ E. pūra E.+ -pṛṇa V.B.S. pūrayitavya C. See also √ prā, which is a secondary form of this root. Meanings píparti pṛṇā́ti pṛṇáti v PPP pūrtá 1 & pūrṇá (q.v.) fill, make full; sate, nourish, refresh; give abundantly, lavish (D of pers. & A of th.), present with (A of pers. & I of th.), fulfil, accomplish. Ā & P. pūryáte (pū́ryate & pūryati) fill or sate one's self, become full of (I). Caus. pūráyati, te make full, complete, fulfil, accomplish; fill, cover, present with (I). abhi make full; Ā P. become full, be filled with (G); Caus. fill, complete, load, cover, present abundantly with (I), increase, augment, fulfil, accomplish. ā fill, sate; make full, complete, fulfil, accomplish; Ā P. be or become full, increase, be rich in (I); Caus. fill wholly, cover with (I). ni put down, pour out (r.). pari Ā P. be filled, become full or complete by (I); Caus. fill, make full, accomplish. pra fill, make up, complete, accomplish; Ā P. refl. ; Caus. = S. prati bestow in return; Caus. fill, satiate, satisfy, accomplish. sam Ā P. be or become filled; Caus. fill, make full, fulfil, accomplish. Cf. abhipūrṇa, ā́pūrṇa, paripūrṇa, pṛṇánt, pratipūrṇa, saṃpūrṇa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_p_r.html"> √ 2 pṛ    √ 2 pṛ, “pass” Present I. para VS1. ? II. párṣi RV III. píparti píprati etc. V.B.S.C. (pīpṛhi S1.C1.) Aorist RAo: ápīparat etc. V.B. (pī́parat V.B., pīpárat RV1.) -s-Ao: párṣati etc. RV., párṣat V.B., parṣa V -iṣ-Ao: pāriṣat RV Causative pāráyati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ (pāryate C.) Verbal Nouns parṣáṇi RV Derivatives -páraṇa V. parṣáṇi RV. pā́raṇa V.+ pípru ? V. partṛ́ RV. párṣiṣṭha RV. pāraṇīya E.+ -pāraya RV. parṣá ? RV. pārá V.+ perú V. pārayitṛ́ B. -parṣin ? ŚB. -pārin AB. pápri V. pārayiṣṇú V.+ The aorist stem parṣ has almost won the value of a secondary root. Meanings píparti 2 v pass (trans.), bring across or to (A), rescue, save from (Ab); protect, further, promote. Caus. pāráyati (te) the same + come through, overcome; resist, keep one's ground; be capable of or able to (Inf). ati lead over, bring across (A); pass (trans.), go through (A). Caus. lead over, pass (trans.); Ā rescue, deliver from (Ab). nis draw or help out of (Ab), escape; Caus. = S. sam Caus. bring over; finish, perform. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_3_p_r.html"> √ 3 pṛ    √ 3 pṛ, “be busy” Present V. pṛṇoti C1., pṛṇvāṇa C1 Passive priyate E.+ Causative pārayati etc. C Verbal Nouns PPP: pṛta B.+ Derivatives -pra ? RV. -pāra E.+ Only with ā and (especially) vyā; hence in all probability a specialized use of √ 1 pṛ or √ 2 pṛ (√ 1 pṛ “be filled up or occupied”, or √ 2 pṛ with vi-ā, “made to pass to and fro, kept in motion”). Meanings pṛṇoti v PPP pṛtā (only – ṃ) ā be busy or active; w. vyā (priyate or pṛṇute) be busy or occupied with (artham). Caus. vyāpārayati set to work, employ in or at (L, I, or artham). Cf. āpṛta (add.), vyāpṛta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_p_rc.html"> √ pṛc    √ pṛc, “mix” Present I. pṛñca pṛ́ñcatī AV III. pipṛgdhi V.B., pipṛkta RV VII. pṛṇákti pṛñcánti etc. V.B., pṛṅkté etc. V.B Passive pṛcyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: parciṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: parcitā Aorist √-Ao: párcas RV., pṛcīya etc. RV.S., pṛcāná RV -s-Ao: aprāk AV., apṛkṣi -kta etc. V.B.S -iṣ-Ao: aparcīt, aparciṣṭa Perfect papṛcus E. (papṛcāsi RV.,-cyāt etc. V.), papṛcāná RV Causative parcaya- Desiderative piparciṣa- Intensive parīpṛc- Verbal Nouns PPP: pṛktá V.+,-pṛgṇa ? RV1.; -pṛ́ce RV.,-pṛ́cas V.B.S Derivatives -pṛc V.B. parka AV.+ pṛ́kṣ ? RV. prakṣá ? V.AA. -párcana V. pṛkṣá ? RV. Meanings pṛṇákti pṛṅkté 1 v etc., PPP pṛktá (q.v.) mix, mingle, unite or combine with (I, r. L); fill, satiate; bestow richly, lavish upon (L); augment, increase. ā mix or unite with (I); fill, satiate (Ā refl.); pervade, penetrate. upa add to (L), increase, augment; approach, esp. for sexual intercourse. vi bring asunder, separate from (I); scatter, disperse, fill, satiate. sam PĀ mix, mingle, join, touch; fill, endow, present with (I). Cf. anupṛkta, sápṛkta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_p_r_n.html"> √ pṛṇ    √ pṛṇ see √ 1 pṛ. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_p_rt.html"> √ pṛt    √ pṛt, “fight” Inferable from the derivatives pṛ́t RV., pṛ́tanā̆ V.+ 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_p_rz.html"> √ pṛś, pṛṣ    √ pṛś, pṛṣ (?) Under this heading may be grouped a number of words of doubtful relations, in part perhaps connected with √ spṛś: pṛ́śana RV. pṛ́śni V.+ pṛṣṭá V.B. párśu V.+ pṛśanī́ RV. pṛ́ṣant V.+ pṛṣṭí V.B. párśāna V. pṛṣatá B.+ pṛṣṭhá V.+ 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_pyaa.html"> √ pyā    √ pyā, “fill up” Present IV. pyā́yate etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: pyāsyate, pyāyiṣyate Periphrastic Future: pyātā, pyāyitā Aorist √-Ao: apyāyi -iṣ-Ao: pyāyiṣīmahi S -siṣ-Ao: pyāsiṣīmahi AV.B.S Perfect pipye ? RV. papye Causative pyāyáyati etc. AV.+,-te etc. C. (pyāyayiṣṭhās U.; pyāyyáte etc. B.+) Verbal Nouns PPP: pyāta TS. pyāna Derivatives -pyāya C. -pyāyya E. -pyā́yana B.+ -pyāyayitṛ B. -pyāyin C. Is a secondary root-form from √ pi, pī. Meanings pyā́yate v swell, overflow. ā swell, become full of or rich in (I); make full, enlarge, strengthen. Caus. āpyāyáyati, te cause to swell, make full, esp. pour water upon the Soma; nourish, refresh; excite, rouse. samā swell, grow, increase; Caus. nourish, strengthen, vivify. pra swell, Caus. make swell. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_prach.html"> √ prach    √ prach, “ask” Present VI. pṛcháti -te etc. V.+ Passive pṛchyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: prakṣyati etc. B.+ (aprakṣyat B.U.) Periphrastic Future: praṣṭā Aorist RAo: apaprachat -s-Ao: áprākṣīt etc. V.+ (áprāṭ RV.), apraṣṭa C. (pṛkṣase ? RV.) Perfect papracha paprachus B.+ Causative prachaya- Desiderative pipṛchiṣa- (in d.) Intensive parīpṛch- Verbal Nouns PPP: pṛṣṭá V.+; Inf: práṣṭum V.+; 1Abs: pṛṣṭvā E.+; 2Abs: -pṛchya E.+;-pṛ́cham -che RV Derivatives -pṛch RV. pṛchaka B.+ praṣṭṛ U.+ pipṛchiṣu C. prāch- E.+ pṛ́chya RV.C. praśná V.+ papṛkṣéṇya RV. pṛchā C. praṣṭavya E.+ -pṛaśnya B. pipṛkṣu C. prāś AV. The RV. form papṛkṣé is also referred hither by BR. Meanings pṛccháti (pṛccháte) v PPP pṛṣṭá (q.v.) ask, question, inquire, w. A of pers. or (&) th; seek, request, entreat; P. pṛcchayate be asked after (A, r. D, L, arthe, adhikṛtya, or hetos). With na not care for (A). anu ask, ask some one after (2A). ā Ā (P) bid farewell to (A), invoke (a god), ask, inquire. upā & samā bid farewell. pari ask, question, interrogate a person (A) about (A prati , r. L or G). prati ask, interrogate a person about (2A). vi ask, inquire, ascertain. sam Ā consult, converse or talk with (Ab), absol. with each other; ask, question, inquire (2A). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_prath.html"> √ prath    √ prath, “spread” Present I. práthate etc. -ti etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: prathiṣyate Periphrastic Future: prathitā Aorist √-Ao: prathāná RV RAo: (pqerf. ?) papráthat etc.-thanta RV -iṣ-Ao: aprathiṣṭa etc. RV Perfect paprathé etc. V.+,-thatus C Causative pratháyati etc. V.+,-te etc. V. (práthayi TS.S.) Verbal Nouns PPP: prathita E.+ Derivatives -pṛth ? RV. pṛ́thī̆ V.B. práthana B.+ práthiṣṭha V.B. pṛthá B.+ pṛthú V.+ práthas V.B. práthīyas B.S. pṛ́thak V.+ pṛthivī́ V.+ prathu E.+ prathasnu ? TB. pṛ́thavāna RV. prathā C. prathimán RV.C. prathayitṛ C. Meanings práthate v PPP prathita (q.v.) spread, extend (intrans., r. prathati trans.); become larger or wider, increase, grow; appear, arise; become famous or celebrated. Caus. pratháyati trans. (Ā intrans. or refl.) spread, broaden, extend, augment; proclaim, celebrate, disclose, show, manifest. anu Ā (intrans.) spread along (A). abhi Ā (intrans.) stretch before or against; Caus. (trans.) spread about (A), divulge. ā Caus. (trans.) spread, expand. prati Ā (intrans.) spread round or over. vi P spread, expand; Ā (intrans.) stretch, increase, be large or wide. Caus. spread, extend, disclose, unfold, manifest. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_praa.html"> √ prā    √ prā, “fill” Present II. prā́si RV Aorist √-Ao: aprāt etc. V.B.; aprāyi AV -s-Ao: aprās (3s.) RV.B Perfect papraú . etc. V. (paprā́tha RV.; paprā RV.), papre etc. V Verbal Nouns PPP: prātá RV Derivatives -prā RV.-pra AV.B.S.-prā́ṇa (api-) RV.-prā́van RV. A secondary root-form, from √ 1 pṛ. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_prii.html"> √ prī    √ prī, “please” Present IV. (or Ps.) prīyate etc. U.+,-ti etc. E.+ (priyanti R1.) IX. prīṇā́ti -nīté etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: preṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: pretā Aorist √-Ao: prīyāt C -s-Ao: apraiṣīt etc. B. (préṣat RV.) apreṣṭa Perfect pipriyé -yāṇá RV.; apipres etc. B.S. (pipráyat etc.-áyasva piprīhí RV.) Causative prīṇayati etc. S.+ Desiderative píprīṣati RV Intensive peprī- Verbal Nouns PPP: prītá V.+; 1Abs: prītvā́ ŚB Derivatives -prī V.B.S. prīti S.+ premán V.+ piprīṣā E.+ priyá V.+ pretṛ́ RV.S. préyas V.+ piprīṣu E.+ práyas V.B. preṇí V. préṣṭha V.+ prīṇana E.+ prīṇayatṛ C. The so-called causative is, of course, a denominative, apparently of a Part. prīṇa, not occurring independently. Meanings prīṇā́ti prīṇīté prīyate 1 v (ti), PPP prītá (q.v.) P please gladden, rejoice, propitiate; also = Ā be glad or cheerful, delight in, be content or pleased with, be fond of (G, I, L, or Ab). Caus. prīṇayati = S.A ; Des príprīṣati wish to please or propitiate. ā P please, satisfy, gladden, propitiate. Ā be glad, rejoice. sam (prīyate) be glad or cheerful, delight in (L or Ab). Cf. āprīta, páriprīta, saṃprīta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_pru.html"> √ pru    √ pru, “flow” Present I. právate etc. RV.B.S Aorist -s-Ao: proṣṭhās S Perfect pupruve etc. B Verbal Nouns prutá RV Derivatives pravá RV. pravaṇá ? V.+ -prut V.B. A side-form to the much more common √ plu. Meanings právate v flow, spring up. ati jump away. apa jump down. abhi jump near. ud jump up or forth. ni sputter about. Cf. vípruta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_pruth.html"> √ pruth    √ pruth, “snort” Present I. próthati etc. V.B.,-amāna RV Future Simple Future: prothiṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: prothitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aprothīt, -thiṣṭa Perfect puprotha , -othe Causative prothayitvā S Intensive pópruthat RV Verbal Nouns -prúthya RV., prothya S Derivatives protha B.+ prothátha RV. Meanings próthati v snort. pra = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_pru_s.html"> √ pruṣ    √ pruṣ, “sprinkle” Present IV. ápruṣyat ŚB V. pruṣṇuvánti -ṇávat -ṇute RV VI. pruṣa RV.,-ṣánt ? AV IX. pruṣṇánt B Future Simple Future: proṣiṣyánt TS Periphrastic Future: proṣitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aproṣīt Perfect puproṣa Verbal Nouns pruṣitá RV Derivatives -pruṣ V.+ -prūṣ TS. pruṣvā AV.B. pṛ́ṣvā ? TS. Compare √ pluṣ. Meanings pruṣṇóti pruṣṇute v (pruṣyati), PPP pruṣitá sprinkle, wet, moisten. abhi Ā sprinkle anything on one's self. pari sprinkle about. vi drip off or down. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_plii.html"> √ plī    √ plī (?) The isolated form vi plīyante occurs at SVB. iii 9. 1. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_plu.html"> √ plu    √ plu, “float” Present I. plávate etc. V.+,-ti etc. B.+ II ? pluvīta S., apluvan E Future Simple Future: ploṣyati -te etc. B Aorist RAo: apuplavat, ápiplavam ŚB -s-Ao: aploṣṭa etc. B Perfect pupluve B.+,-vus E.+ Causative plāvayati etc. B.+,-te etc. E.+ (plāvyate C.); plavayati C1 Desiderative puplūṣa- Intensive poplūyate etc. B.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: plutá AV.+; 2Abs: -plutya U.S.+,-plū́ya ŚB.K Derivatives plavá V.+ plavana S.+ plāva B.+ plāvya E.+ plavaka E. plavitṛ E. -plāvaka C. plāvana B.+ -plavin C. pluti S.+ plāvin B.+ plāvayitṛ E. Compare √ pru. Meanings plávate v (plávati), PPP plutá (q.v.) float, swim, bathe, sail; vibrate, hover, soar, fly; blow (wind), pass away (time); spring, jump, dance. Caus. plāvayati, te make float or swim, inundate, overflow, cover with (I), bathe, cleanse, wash away, remove. Int poplūyate swim about. abhi sail or move towards (A), spring or hasten near, attack, visit. samabhi inundate, submerge, attack, visit. ava immerse; jump down or off. ā bathe, plunge, or wash (trans. & intrans.); overflow, inundate, cover; jump near, over, up, or off. Caus. = S. trans.; Ā also bathe (intrans.). upanyā swim near or towards (A). samā bathe (intrans.); overflow, cover thoroughly. ud spring up, emerge, rise. upa swim on the surface, float upon, hover towards, overflow, cover, veil, eclipse, attack, assail. pari swim about, bathe; flood, inundate; soar about, fly through; spring about, move restlessly, waver, go astray. pra go to sea (A); Caus. cause to float away, wash or flood with water. vi go asunder, be dispersed, fall into disorder, go astray, be ruined, perish. Caus. make swim; flood, inundate; spread abroad, divulge; ruin, destroy. sam flow together, gather, contract (intrans.); fluctuate, waver (mind). Caus. gather, contract (trans.), flood, inundate. Cf. abhiparipluta (add.), abhipluta, āpluta, upapluta, prápluta, vipluta, saṃpluta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_plu_s.html"> √ pluṣ    √ pluṣ, “burn Present I. ploṣati C1. pluṣyati, pluṣṇāti Passive pluṣyate C Future Simple Future: ploṣiṣyati Periphrastic Future: ploṣitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aploṣīt Perfect puploṣa Verbal Nouns PPP: pluṣṭa E.+ Derivatives plúṣi V.B. ploṣa C. ploṣin C. ploṣaṇa C. Compare √ pruṣ. Meanings ploṣati v PPP pluṣṭa burn, singe. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_psaa.html"> √ psā    √ psā, “devour” Present II. psā́ti etc. AV.B Passive apsīyata JB Future Simple Future: psāsyati Periphrastic Future: psātā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: apsāsīt Perfect papsau ; psāyāt Causative psāpaya- Desiderative pipsāsa- Intensive pāpsā- Verbal Nouns psātá B.;-psā́ya B Derivatives psānīya C. Doubtless a secondary root-form, from √ bhas. Meanings psā́ti v PPP psāta chew, devour. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_phakk.html"> √ phakk    √ phakk, “swell” (?) Present I. phakkant C1 Passive phakkyate Future Simple Future: phakkiṣyati Periphrastic Future: phakkitā Aorist RAo: apaphakkat -iṣ-Ao: aphakkīt Perfect paphakka Causative phakkaya- Desiderative piphakkiṣa- Intensive pāphakk- The single occurrence doubtless artificial. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_pha_n.html"> √ phaṇ    √ phaṇ, “spring” Present I. phaṇati C Future Simple Future: phaṇiṣyati Periphrastic Future: phaṇitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aphaṇīt aphāṇīt Perfect paphāṇa paphaṇus Causative phāṇayati etc. RV.LŚS. phaṇayati Desiderative piphaṇiṣa- Intensive pánīphaṇat RV., pamphaṇat S Derivatives phaṇá B.+ phāṇṭa B.+ phéna ? V.+ Meanings phaṇati v spring. Caus. phāṇayati cause to spring or run. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_phar.html"> √ phar    √ phar, “scatter” (?) Intensive parpharat RV1. Derivatives -pharvī V.B. phárvara RV. phā́riva RV. parpharī́ka RV. All the derivatives of doubtful meaning and connection. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_phal.html"> √ 1 phal    √ 1 phal, “brust” Present I. phalati etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: phaliṣyati Periphrastic Future: phalitā Aorist RAo: apīphalat -iṣ-Ao: aphālīt Perfect paphāla E. phelus Causative phālayati etc. E Desiderative piphaliṣa- Intensive pamphul- Verbal Nouns PPP: phalita E.+ Derivatives phálaka B.+ phalin C. phā́la V.+ phulla E.+ See √ 2 phal. The Part. phullant M1. is doubtless a denominative formation from phulla. Meanings phalati v PPP phulla 1 (q.v.) burst, split (intrans.). ud burst out, rush forth. Caus. utphālayati tear open, open wide (eyes). prati rebound, be reflected. vi & sam burst or split asunder. Cf. utphulla, praphulla, protphulla, samutphulla, saṃphulla. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_phal.html"> √ 2 phal    √ 2 phal, “fruit” Present I. phalati etc. E.+,-te E Future Simple Future: phaliṣyati etc. E.+ Perfect phelire C Verbal Nouns PPP: phalita E.+ Derivatives phála V.+ phalitavya E. Doubtless in reality a denominative of phála, which from √ 1 phal. Meanings phalati phalate v PPP phalita 2 (q.v.) fruit, bear fruit, have results or consequences, be fulfilled. prati & vi bear fruit, ripen, be accomplished. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ba_mh.html"> √ baṃh    √ baṃh, “make firm” Present I. paṃhate Future Simple Future: baṃhiṣyate Periphrastic Future: baṃhitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: abaṃhiṣṭa Perfect papaṃhe Causative baṃhayate etc. B Verbal Nouns bāḍha V.+ Derivatives bahala C. bahú . V.+ báṃhiṣṭha V.+ bāhú ? V.+ báṃhīyas MS. Meanings PPP bāḍha (q.v.), Caus. baṃhayate make firm, strengthen, increase. sam C = S. Caus. Cf. ávabāḍha, níbālha (add.). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bandh.html"> √ bandh    √ bandh, “bind” Present I. abandhat C.,-dhata (3s.) E., abadhnanta E IX. badhnā́ti etc. V.+ (badhāna AV.+, bandhāna E., badhnīhi C.),-nīté etc. V.B.S Passive badyáte etc. V.+,-ti C Future Simple Future: bhantsyati etc. B.S., bandhiṣyati -te E.+ Periphrastic Future: banddhā Aorist RAo: ababandhat -iṣ-Ao: abhāntsīt. Precative: badhyāt Perfect babándha AV.+, bedhús AV., babandhus E.+; bedhé -dhiré etc. AV. babandhe Causative bandhayati etc. B.+ Desiderative bibhantsa- Intensive bābandh- , bābadhya- Verbal Nouns PPP: baddhá V.+; Inf: banddhum E.+, baddhum ? E., bandhitum E.; 1Abs: baddhvā́ AV.+,-dhvā́ya B.; 2Abs: -bádhya B.+;-bádhe AV.;-bandham C Derivatives bandhá V.+ bándhana V.+ -baddhavya C. badhirá V.+ bandhaka E.+ bandhanīya E.+ -banddhṛ C. bandhayitṛ C. bandhin E.+ bándhu V.+ banddhra AV. bandhya E.+ -bándhuka B. Meanings badhnā́ti badhnīté v (bandhati), PPP baddhá (q.v.) bind, tie, attach, fix, fasten put on (mostly Ā); bind (a victim for the gods), i.e. sacrifice; bind together, join, construct, compose; effect, produce, perform, make, get, show, manifest, betray; obstruct, stop, close, dam up (~ setunā); catch, take or keep prisoner; direct, turn (the eyes or mind) upon (L or Inf). Caus. bandhayati cause to be bound, caught, constructed, dammed up, etc. anu tie to, attach (l. & f.), join, connect; stick to, adhere, follow, (*equal, resemble); adduce, cause, effect; show, betray; hold together, last; insist upon, be urgent with (A). P. be tied to etc., be added as indicatory letter (g.). ava tie to, attach. ā bind or tie on, join, unite, bring together; begin, enter into (conversation). ud tie up, hang. upa bind, fetter. ni bind on, fasten, tie to (L); fetter, chain (l. & f.); join, unite; build, construct; close up, stop, restrict; fix, put or turn upon (L); compose, write down; betray, manifest. pari bind or put on, tie round (Ā), surround, obstruct, stop. pra tie, fasten, fetter. prati tie to, fasten; enchase, set in (L); join, connect; fix, direct; shut out, keep off, exclude; stop, interrupt. sam bind together, connect, attach; P. be bound together, be connected with i.e. belong to (I). abhisam connect with, mean by. P. be connected with, belong to, be to be supplied. Cf. anubaddha (add.), avabaddha, ābaddha, udbaddha, upanibaddha, nibaddha, nirbaddha (add.), pratibaddha, prabaddha, saṃbaddha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bal.html"> √ bal    √ bal, “whirl” (?) Intensive balbalīti ŚB1. It is not probable that this solitary verb-form has anything to do with the common derivatives (from a √ bal “be strong”): bála V.+, bálīyas AV.+, báliṣṭha B.+, baliman U., bālá ? S.+ 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_baadh.html"> √ bādh    √ bādh, “oppress” Present I. bā́dhate etc. V.+,-ti etc. E.+ Passive bādhyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: bādhiṣyati C.,-te E Periphrastic Future: bādhitā Aorist RAo: ababādhat -iṣ-Ao: bādhiṣṭa V. (bādhithās TA.); bādhiṣṭām TA Perfect babādhé V.+,-dha ? M Causative bādhayati etc. AV.+ Desiderative bībhatsate etc. V.+; bibādhiṣate ŚB.C Intensive bābadhe bā́badhāna, badbadhé -dhāná RV.B Verbal Nouns PPP: bādhitá V.+; Inf: bādhitum E.; 2Abs: -bā́dhya RV.; bā́dhe RV Derivatives bādh RV. -bādhin B.C. bādhanīya C. bibhatsa S.+ bādhá , -ā V.+ bādhyà B.+ -bā́dhas RV. bibhatsā́ B. bādhaka E.+ bādhana E.+ bādhitavya E.+ bibhatsú V.+ bādhitṛ E.+ bādhayitṛ C. Compare √ vadh, badh. The reference of bībhatsa- to this root is not beyond question. Meanings bā́dhate v (bā́dhati), PPP bādhitá oppress, torment, beset, hurt, injure, remove, annul. Caus. bādhayati oppress, vex, pain, fight. Des bībhatsate feel aversion or loathing (Ab). Int bābadhe or baddhadhé press heavily, confine, hem in. ati afflict or distress hard (A or G). apa drive away, remove (also Caus. ). Des have a loathing for (Ab). abhi press hard, pain, vex, obstruct. ava keep off. ā press against, torment, distress. ud break forth. ni press down, hem in, beset. nis keep off. pari keep off, exclude or prevent from (Ab or G), protect from (Ab); vex, harass, pain. pra press forwards, urge on, further; drive back, repel, torment, afflict, molest, injure, abolish, undo. prati drive back, ward off, hem in, disturb, afflict. vi press or drive asunder, repel, afflict, pain, hurt, injure. sam press together, oppress, afflict, torment. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_budh.html"> √ budh    √ budh, “know, wake” Present I. bódhati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ IV. búdhyate etc. V.+,-ti etc. E.+ Passive budhyate c Future Simple Future: bhotsyati B.,-te E Periphrastic Future: boddhā Aorist √-Ao: bodhi (impv.) RV.; abudhran -ram RV., budhāná RV.; ábodhi V.+ Th Ao: budhánta RV., budhéma AV. ? RAo: abūbudhat V -s-Ao: ábhutsi etc. V.B., abuddha C. bhutsīṣṭa -iṣ-Ao: bódhiṣat RV., abodhiṣata C Perfect bubudhé etc. V.+, bubodha E. (búbodhati etc. bubodhas RV.) Causative bodháyati etc. V.+,-te B. (bodhyate E., bubodhayiṣa- in d.) Desiderative bubhutsati -te etc. C. bubodhiṣa- Intensive bobudhīti etc. B.C Verbal Nouns PPP: buddhá V.+; Inf: boddhum E.+; 1Abs: buddhvā C.; 2Abs: -budhya B.+;-búdhe B., budhí RV Derivatives -budh V.B. bodhin E.+ buddhi S.+ bodhayitavya C. budha B.+ bodhya E.+ boddhavya U.+ bodhayitṛ́ RV.C. -budhya RV. bódhana V.+ bodhitavya C. bodhayiṣṇu E. búdhan- TB. bodhanīya E.+ boddhṛ E.+ bubodhayiṣu E.+ bodhá V.+ bodhi E.+ bubhutsā C. bibodhayiṣu R1. bodhaka E.+ bodhít- RV. bubhutsu E.+ Meanings bódhati v (bódhate), búdhyate (ti), PPP buddhá (q.v.) wake, awake (intrans., r. trans.); watch, notice, heed (A or G); perceive, learn, know, understand, regard or know as, take for (2A), present with (A of pers. & I of th.). Caus. bodháyati awaken, revive, restore to consciousness, cause to notice, attend, or understand; remind of, teach (2A). Des bubhutsate wish to know or learn. Int bobudhīti have knowledge of (A). anu awake, watch, notice, perceive, think of, consider. Caus. remind of, teach, inform. ava awake; perceive, learn, understand. Caus. awaken, remind, inform, explain. samava perceive, learn. ā attend to (A). ud Ā awake. ni (bodhati) attend to, learn or hear from (G, r. sakāśāt), understand, know. pra (budhyate) wake up, be awake, watch; expand, blossom; (bodhati) know, understand. Caus. awaken, cause to expand or blossom, make sensible of, admonish, persuade; teach, instruct (2A). prati awake, expand, blossom, notice, perceive. Caus. awaken, admonish, remind, inform, teach. vi awake; perceive, learn. Caus. awaken, make conscious, bring to reason. sam awake, watch, perceive, notice. Caus. awaken (lit. & fig.), make attentive to or aware of, exhort, admonish, teach (2A). Cf. udbuddha, prátibuddha, prabuddha, vibuddha, saṃbuddha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bul.html"> √ bul    √ bul, “submerge” Causative bolayati C. The single occurrence in a commentary is doubtless artificial. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_b_r_mh.html"> √ bṛṃh, vṛṃh    √ bṛṃh, vṛṃh, “roar” see √ vṛṃh. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_b_rh.html"> √ 1 bṛh    √ 1 bṛh, “make big or strong” Present I. bṛṃhati -te etc. ŚB VI. bṛhati etc. AV.B Perfect babarha AV., babṛhāṃá RV Causative barhaya V.; bṛṃhayati etc. (or vṛṃh-) E.+, -te E Intensive bárbṛhat barbṛhi RV Verbal Nouns PPP: bṛḍha ŚB., vṛḍha ŚB.C Derivatives bṛh- V.+ bṛhánt V.+ bráhman V.+ bṛṃhaṇa E.+ -barha S.+ -bárhas V.B. brahmán V.+ bṛṃhaṇīya C. -bárhaṇa V.+ bárhiṣṭha V.+ -bṛṃhin C. bṛṃhayitavya C. barháṃā RV. barhís ? V.+ Compare the following root √ 2 bṛh, vṛh. Meanings bṛháti 2 v (only bṛhánt q.v.) & bṛṃhati, bṛṃhate; Caus. bṛṃháyati, te, PPP bṛṃhita (q.v.) make great or big, strengthen, augment, further. abhi Caus. strengthen, increase, augment. upa the same; Int (barbṛhi) press or embrace close. samupa Caus. strengthen, supply, complete. pari P Ā enclose, encircle, make tight or firm, strengthen, fortify. Caus. strengthen, augment. sam join firmly together. Caus. saṃvarhayati join together, attach (D); saṃbṛṃhayati strengthen, encourage. Cf. upabṛṃhita, paribṛḍha, parivṛḍha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_b_rh.html"> √ 2 bṛh, vṛh    √ 2 bṛh, vṛh, “tear” See √ vṛh. The relations of the two root bṛh, and the connection of some of their derivatives, are not wholly clear. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bruu.html"> √ brū    √ brū, “say” Present II. brávīti bruvánti etc. brūté bruváte etc. V.+ (brūmi R., bravīhi E.+, abrūvan U., abravat ? M. bravīthās -īta U.) VI. abruvam U.E., bruvadhvam M., bruvamāṃa C Aorist √-Ao: brūyāsta M1 Derivatives -brava V. -bruva AV.+ Meanings brávīti brūté v say, tell (A of th. & G, D, L of pers; or 2A), speak to (A, r. G); name, call (2A), speak of (A prati or adhikṛtya); answer (punar); announce, foretell; Ā (P) call one's self or profess one's self to be (N, r. + iti). – acchā Ā call near. ati abuse, revile. adhi encourage, console, comfort (D), speak in favour of or intercede for (D). anu pronounce, recite; teach, rehearse to (D), address reverentially (D), invite a person (D) to (G); say, speak; take for, recognize; Ā repeat, learn by heart. apa speak off, i.e. conjure, charm with words; console a person (Ab) for the loss of (A). ā Ā converse. ud renounce, give up (A or G). upa Ā (P) speak to (A), beg for (D, r. A), invoke, persuade. nis pronounce (clearly and singly), explain. pra tell forth, proclaim, announce, teach, praise, relate, betray, call, describe as (2A). prati speak back, answer; Ā return (an attack etc.). vi speak out, utter, state, explain, answer a question; declare falsely; contradict, disagree; Ā dispute, contend. sam PĀ talk together, converse; Ā consent, agree, say anything to (2A). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_blii.html"> √ blī    √ blī see √ vlī. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhak_s.html"> √ bhakṣ    √ bhakṣ, “partake of, eat” Present I. bhakṣati -te etc. E.+ Aorist √-Ao: abhakṣi C RAo: ababhakṣat ŚB Causative bhakṣáyati etc. V.+,-te etc. B.+ (bhakṣyáte etc. B.+; bibhakṣayiṣati S.+) Desiderative bibhakṣiṣati E. ? Verbal Nouns Inf: bhakṣitum E.+;-bhakṣam S Derivatives bhakṣá V.+ bhakṣya E.+ bhakṣitavya C. bhakṣayitṛ E.+ bhakṣaka C. bhákṣaṇa V.+ bhakṣitṛ E. bhakṣayitavya B.+ bhakṣin S.+ bhakṣanīya B.C. bhakṣiván B.S. bibhakṣayiṣā C. bibhakṣayiṣu E.+ Secondary root-form, from √ bhaj (as denominative of bhakṣá); the non-“causative” forms only sporadic. Meanings bhakṣati bhakṣate v older bhakṣáyati, bhakṣáyate, PPP bhakṣitá (q.v.) partake of, enjoy, eat, drink, devour, consume, waste, destroy. Caus. bhakṣáyati *cause a pers. (I or A) to eat (A); cf. also S. Des bibhakṣiṣati & bibhakṣayiṣati wish to eat or devour. pari enjoy or drink (esp. what belongs to another), eat, feed on. sam enjoy or devour (together). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhaj.html"> √ bhaj    √ bhaj, “divide, share” Present I. phájati -te etc. V.+ II. bhakṣi RV Passive bhajyáte etc. AV.+ Future Simple Future: bhakṣyati -te etc. B. (abhakṣyan M.); bhajiṣyati -te etc. E.+ Periphrastic Future: bhaktā Aorist RAo: abībhajus ŚB -s-Ao: abhākṣīt etc. V.+ (abhāk V.B., bhakṣat RV.), ábhakṣi -kta etc. V.+ (bhakṣīṣṭa etc. V.B.S.,-ṣīta SV.) Perfect babhā́ja bhejus etc. V.+ (babhakṭha ŚB. bhejitha), bhejé -jiré etc. V.+ Causative bhājayati etc. V.+,-te C. (bhājyáte etc. AV.B.) Desiderative bibhakṣa- ; bhikṣa- (see √ bhikṣ) Intensive bābhaj- Verbal Nouns PPP: bhaktá V.+; Inf: bhaktum B.+, bhajitum E.; 1Abs: bhaktvā́ AV.+,-tvā́ya RV.; 2Abs: -bhajya B.+;-bhā́jam (inf.) B Derivatives bhāj V.+ bhajanīya E.+ bhāgá V.+ bhājaka C. bhága V.+ bhajenya C. bhāgin B.+ bhājin U.+ bhajin C. bhaktí V.+ -bhāgya S. bhājya C. -bhajya C. bhajitavya E. bhāgīyas C. bhā́jana B.+ bhajana C. bhaktṛ RV. -bhāja S. bhājayú RV. Compare the derivative root-forms √ bhakṣ and √ bhikṣ; compare also √ bhañj. Meanings bhájati bhájate v PPP bhaktá (q.v.) deal out, apportion, dispense, distribute (w. G or D of pers.), share, divide (Ā among each other); Ā grant, bestow, endow, furnish with (I); Ā (P) receive as a portion, partake of, enjoy, prefer, choose, take or go to, pursue, practise, belong or be attached to, revere, honour, worship, love, court. Caus. bhājáyati deal out, distribute, divide; make a pers. (A) share in (G). apa give a pers. (G or D) a share of (G); content, satisfy; divide, distribute. ā P (Ā) deal out, give a pers. (A) a share in (L). anvā Ā make a person share in (L) after or along with others. nis exclude from (Ab), content or satisfy with (I); Caus. disinherit. pari divide. prati fall again to the share of (A). vi part asunder, divide, distribute (2A, A of th. & D or L of pers., or A of pers. & I of th.); Ā also share among each other or with (I). pravi divide, distribute. saṃvi sever, sunder; divide with (I saha, D, or G); give a share, present with (I). sam distribute, divide, share, present with a gift, endow. Cf. anvābhakta (add.), ā́bhakta, pravibhakta, vibhakta, saṃbhakta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bha_jj.html"> √ bhañj    √ bhañj, “break” Present VII. bhanákti etc. V.+ (abhanas AV.) Passive bhajyáte etc. AV.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: bhaṅkṣyati E Periphrastic Future: bhaṅktā M Aorist √-Ao: abhāji c. abhañji; bhajyāt RAo: ababhañjat -s-Ao: abhāṅkṣīt etc. E.+ Perfect babhañja etc. V.+,-jire C Causative bhañjaya- Desiderative bibhañkṣa- Intensive bambhañj- , bambhajya- Verbal Nouns PPP: bhagna S.+; 1Abs: bhaṅktvā E.+, bhaktvā E.; 2Abs: -bhajya E.+;-bhañjam C Derivatives bhaṅgá V.+ bhaṅgi C. bhañjana AV.+ bhaṅktṛ C. bhaṅgin RV.C. bhañjaka C. -bhañjanu RV. bhaṅgurá V.+ Meanings bhanákti v PPP bhagna (q.v.) break, bend, curve; scatter, disperse; defeat, conquer; frustrate, disappoint, destroy, annihilate; P. bhajyate with intrans. mg. (Caus. bhañjayati w. śūle pierce with a pale*). abhi break, destroy. ava break down (trans.). nis break asunder, split. pra break, destroy; rout, defeat (an army). vi break to pieces; scatter, distribute; frustrate, disappo Int sam break, crush. Cf. paribhagna, saṃbhagna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bha_t.html"> √ bhaṭ    √ bhaṭ, “hire” The so-called root (bhāṭayati etc. C.) is only a denomivative of bhaṭa E.+ doubtless a prakritized form of bhṛta. Meanings bhāṭayati v hire. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bha_n.html"> √ bhaṇ    √ bhaṇ, “speak” Present I. bhaṇati etc. JB.C Passive phaṇyate C Future Simple Future: bhaṇiṣyati Periphrastic Future: bhaṇitā Aorist √-Ao: abhāṇi C RAo: abībhaṇat, ababhāṇat -iṣ-Ao: abhāṇīt Perfect babhāṇa C. babhaṇitha Causative bhāṇayati Desiderative bibhaṇiṣa- (in d.) Verbal Nouns PPP: bhaṇita C.; 1Abs: bhaṇitvā C Derivatives -bhaṇa C. bhaṇana C. bhaṇiti C. bhāṇaka C. bhaṇanīya C. bhāṇa C. bibhaṇiṣu C. A later form of √ bhan. Meanings bhaṇati v PPP bhaṇita (q.v.) speak, say, relate; call, name (2A). Caus. bhāṇayati (bhaṇāpayati) cause to speak. prati answer, reply. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhan.html"> √ bhan    √ bhan, “speak” Present I. bhánati etc. -nanta RV Probably related with √ bhā. Compare √ bhaṇ, the later form. Meanings bhánati v speak, tell. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhand.html"> √ bhand    √ bhand, “be bright” Present I. bhándate etc. RV Causative bhandayati Derivatives bhandána V.B. bhándiṣṭha V.S. bhadrá V.+ Meanings bhándate v be bright, shine; resound, praise. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bharts.html"> √ bharts    √ bharts, “revile” Present I. bhartsati etc. AV. ? KB.E Causative bhartsayati etc. E.+,-te C1. (bhartsyate etc. E.+) Derivatives bhartsana E.+ The form bhartsyā́mi AV. is certainly a false reading. Meanings bhartsati & bhartsayati bhartsayate v PPP bhartsita (q.v.) threaten, revile, mock, deride. abhi , ava , nis , pari , sam = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bharv.html"> √ bharv    √ bharv, “devour” Present I. bhárvati etc. RV. Derivatives -bharva ? RV. bhārvará ? RV. Meanings bhárvati v munch, devour. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhal.html"> √ bhal    √ bhal, “perceive” Present I. bhalate etc Causative bhālayati -te etc. U.C Meanings nibhālayati nibhālayate v look at, behold, perceive; (nis the same*). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bha_s.html"> √ bhaṣ    √ bhaṣ, “bark” Present I. bhaṣati etc. E.+,-te etc. E Future Simple Future: bhaṣiṣyati Periphrastic Future: bhaṣitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: abhāṣīt Perfect babhāṣa Verbal Nouns Inf: bhaṣitum E Derivatives bhaṣá VS. bhaṣaka C. bhaṣaṇa C. -bhāṣ ? AB. Meanings bhaṣati bhaṣate v bark. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhas.html"> √ bhas    √ bhas, “devour” Present I ? bhásat bhasáthas RV III. bábhasti bápsati etc. V.B. (babhasat RV., babdhām C1.) Verbal Nouns PPP: bhasita C Derivatives bhas C. bhástrā ? B.+ -psu RV. babhasa U. -bhasa ? E. bhásman V.+ Compare the derived root √ psā. The nouns bhasád V.B.S., bháṃsas V. hardly belong here. Meanings bábhasti bápsati v PPP bhasita 1 (q.v.) chew, devour, consume. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhaa.html"> √ bhā    √ bhā, “shine” Present II. bhāti etc. V.+ Passive bhāyate Future Simple Future: bhāsyáti B.+ Periphrastic Future: bhātā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: abhāsīt. Precative: bhāyāt Perfect babhau etc. E.+ Causative bhāpaya- , abībhapat Desiderative bibhāsa- Intensive bābhā- Verbal Nouns PPP: bhāta U.+ Derivatives bhā́ V.+ bhāna E.+ bhānú V.+ -bhā́van-varī V.+ bha S.+ bhāti C. bhā́ma V. bhā́s V.+ Compare roots √ bhan and √ bhās. Meanings bhā́ti v PPP bhāta 1 be bright, shine, be splendid or beautiful, please (A w. prati or pratibhāti w. A); show one's self, appear; look or be like (N iva or Adv in vat), pass for (N). ati shine bright or brighter than (A). anu shine after (A). abhi shine forth, appear. ava shine down or upon. ā shine upon, illumine; shine forth, appear, look or be like (iva, yathā or Adv in vat). ud shine out, become manifest. nis & vinis shine forth. pra shine forth, begin to be bright (as the night), appear or be like (N iva). prati shine upon, illumine; become manifest, offer or present one's self, come into the mind, occur to (A or G); appear to (G or A prati), look or be like, resemble (= S.); seem fit, please. saṃprati appear, come into the mind, occur. vi shine forth, shine far and wide, begin to be bright (night), be brilliant, make a show, catch the eye, appear, arise, look or be like (= S.); shine upon, illumine. sam shine out, become manifest, arise, appear as (N iva or yathā). Cf. ābhāta, nirbhāta, prabhāta, vibhāta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhaam.html"> √ bhām    √ bhām, “be angry” Present I. bhāmate Future Simple Future: bhāmiṣyate Periphrastic Future: bhāmitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: abhāmiṣṭa Perfect babhāme Causative bhāmaya- Intensive bābhāmya- Verbal Nouns PPP: bhāmitá RV.TS Derivatives bhā́ma V.B. In reality, the solitary form bhāmitá is doubtless quasi-Part from bhā́ma (√ bhā). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhaa_s.html"> √ bhāṣ    √ bhāṣ, “speak” Present I. bhāṣate etc. B.+,-ti etc. E.+ Passive bhāṣyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: bhāṣiṣyate C Periphrastic Future: bhāṣitā Aorist √-Ao: abhāṣi RAo: ababhāṣat, abībhaṣat -iṣ-Ao: abhāṣiṣi C Perfect babhāṣe etc. B.+ Causative bhāṣayati etc. E.+,-te etc. B.E Desiderative bibhāṣiṣa- Intensive bābhāṣ- Verbal Nouns PPP: bhāṣita E.+; Inf: bhāṣitum U.+, bhāṣṭum E.; 1Abs: bhāṣitvā E.; 2Abs: -bhāṣya E.+ Derivatives -bhāṣ AB. bhāṣaka C. bhāṣaṇa E.+ bhāṣitavya E. -bhāṣa E.+ bhāṣin E. -bhāṣaṇīya C. bhā́ṣitṛ B.+ bhāṣā S.+ bhāṣya S.+ Related with roots √ bhā, √ bhās, √ bhan. Meanings bhāṣate v (bhāṣati), PPP bhāṣita (q.v.) speak, talk, say, tell (A of pers. & th.); name, call (2A). Caus. bhāṣayati, te cause to speak; tell, say. anu call after or to (A), speak to or about (A); pronounce, confess. apa abuse, revile. abhi speak, say, tell (A of th. or- &- pers.), proclaim, confess. ā speak to, address (A), converse with (saha); say, tell (1 or 2A); name, call; exclaim, promise. vyā & samā address, speak to, communicate. pari speak to, admonish, remind, pronounce, explain, teach. pra speak out, name, proclaim, communicate, expound, explain, converse with (A). prati speak back, answer (A of pers. or th.); relate, communicate. vi revile, abuse; P. admit an alternative, be optional (g.). sam talk to, converse with (I saha), address, salute, persuade. Caus. = S. Cf. vibhāṣita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhaas.html"> √ bhās    √ bhās, “shine” Present I. bhā́sati etc. AV.+,-te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: bhāsiṣyate Periphrastic Future: bhāsitā Aorist RAo: ababhāsat abībhasat -iṣ-Ao: abhāsiṣṭa Perfect babhāse etc. E.+ Causative bhāsayati etc. U.+,-te E. (bhāsyate C.) Desiderative bibhāsiṣa- Intensive bābhās- Verbal Nouns PPP: bhāsita C Derivatives bhās E.+ bhāsaka C. -bhāsana E.+ bhāsura E. bhāsá B.+ bhāsin E.+ bhā́sas RV. bhāsvará B.+ bhāsya C. Doubtless a secondary root-form from √ bhā, perhaps through the noun bhā́s. Compare also √ bhāṣ. Meanings bhā́sati bhā́sate v PPP bhāsitá 2 (q.v.) shine, be bright, appear as or like (N or I), become clear or obvious, be imagined or conceived. Caus. bhāsayati, te make shine, illuminate, cause to appear as (I), show, manifest. ava Ā shine, light, become manifest, appear as (I or Adv in vat). Caus. shine upon, illumine. ā Ā appear as (iva). ud shine forth, make a show, catch the eye. Caus. illumine (Ā), illustrate, embellish. samud shine with (I). nis Caus. illumine. pari Ā appear, look like (iva). Caus. beautify, adorn. pra shine, be bright, appear like (iva). Caus. illumine, illustrate. prati Ā shine forth, become manifest, appear like (N) or as (I of an intrans.), be brilliant, make a show. Caus. show, manifest. vi shine, be bright. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhik_s.html"> √ bhikṣ    √ bhikṣ, “beg” Present I. bhíkṣate etc. V.+, ti etc. E Future Simple Future: bhikṣiṣye E Periphrastic Future: bhikṣitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: abhikṣiṣṭa Perfect bibhikṣe B.U Causative bhikṣayati C Verbal Nouns PPP: bhikṣita E.+; Inf: bhikṣitum E.; 1Abs: bhikṣitvā U.C Derivatives bhikṣā́ V.+ bhikṣaṇa S.+ bhikṣitavyà ŚB. bhikṣu C. bhikṣin E. bhikṣuka S.+ A desiderative formation from √ bhaj. Meanings bhíkṣate v (bhíkṣati) wish for (A or G); request, beg (1 or 2A), esp. go begging for food. Caus. bhikṣayati cause to beg. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhid.html"> √ bhid    √ bhid, “split” Present VII. bhinátti bhindánti etc. V.+, bhintte C., bhindāná RV Passive bhidyáte etc. B.+,-ti etc. E Future Simple Future: bhetsyati etc. S.+,-áte etc. B.+ (abhetsyat U.) Periphrastic Future: bhettā Aorist √-Ao: ábhedam -et etc. RV. (bhét bhédati bhidánt RV., bhidyús ? MS.); abhedi B.E Th Ao: abhidat bhideyam AV RAo: abībidhat -s-Ao: abhaitsīt, bhitthās TS. bhitsīṣṭa Perfect bibhéda bibhidús V.+, bibhide C Causative bhedayati etc. E.+,-te E. (bibhedayiṣa- in d.), bhidāpaya- (in d.) Desiderative bíbhitsati etc. RV.E Intensive bebhid- Verbal Nouns PPP: bhinná V.+; Inf: bhettum B.+, bhéttavaí B.S; 1Abs: bhittvā́ V.+; 2Abs: -bhídya V.+ Derivatives bhíd V.+ bhedaka S.+ bhindú V.B. bhettṛ́ V.+ -bhida E.+ bhedin B.+ bhidura C. bibhitsā E.+ bhidā C. bhedya E.+ bhitta ? C. bibhitsu E.+ bhídya V.+ bhedana S.+ bhittí B. bibhedayiṣu E. bhedá V.+ bhedanīya E. bhettavya E.+ bhidāpana C. Meanings bhinátti 1 v (bhintte), PPP bhinná (q.v.) split, cleave, cut asunder, break in twain, destroy, annihilate; pierce, open, expand; loose, extricate; interrupt, disturb, trouble; disclose, betray; divide, separate, part; change, alter; distinguish, discriminate. P. bhidyáte (ti) be split etc., mostly intrans. burst, open, expand, blossom, get loose or free; separate or keep aloof from (I); change, alter, differ from (Ab). Caus. bhedayati, te split, break, destroy, divide, disunite, seduce. Des bíbhitsati wish to break or destroy. ava cleave asunder, pierce. ud break through (disclose, betray*); P. burst open, become manifest nis split or tear asunder, pierce, hurt, wound, loose, unveil, discover; P. split, burst, open (intrans.). pari P. be split, broken, changed, disfigured. pra split forth, tear asunder, open, pierce, divide. prati pierce, penetrate; disclose, betray; reproach, censure. vi split or break asunder, pierce, destroy, divide, disunite, change, alter. Caus. alienate, estrange from (Ab). sam cleave, split, break, pierce, hurt, wound, interrupt, give up; combine, mingle, join, associate with (A). anusam & upasam bring together, mingle, mix. Cf. udbhinna, nirbhinna, prodbhinna (add.), vibhinna, saṃbhinna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhi_saj.html"> √ bhiṣaj    √ bhiṣaj, “heal” Present II. bhiṣakti RV. VII ? abhiṣṇak RV. Derivatives bhiṣáj V.+ bheṣajá V.+ The use of bhiṣaj as a verbal root in RV. is very abnormal. The denominative bhiṣayáti etc. V.B., from the noun bhiṣáj, is quite common. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhii.html"> √ bhī, bhīṣ    √ bhī, bhīṣ, “fear” Present I. bibhyati -yanti etc. E.+ bháyate etc. V III. bibhéti bíbhyati etc. V.+ (bibhitas etc. bibhiyāt C.) Passive bhīyate Future Simple Future: abheṣyat ŚB Periphrastic Future: bhetā Aorist √-Ao: bhes B.S., bhema RV., bhiyāná RV. abhāyi RAo: bībhayat ábībhayanta RV -s-Ao: ábhaiṣīt etc. V.+ (bhais B.+) Perfect bibhāya bibhyus etc. V.+ (bībhāya AB.AA.), bibhye E. bibhayā́ṃ cakāra B Causative bhāyayati etc. C. (-bhāyya B.); bhīṣayate etc. B.+,-ti etc. E.+ (bībhiṣas TS.,-ṣathās RV.; bhyiṣayant C.) Desiderative bibhīṣa- Intensive bebhī- Verbal Nouns PPP: bhītá V.+; Inf: bhetum E.; 2Abs: -bhīya C.; bhiyáse RV Derivatives bhī́ V.+ bhiyásāna AV. bheya E. bhīṣā E.+ bhayá V.+ bhīti C. bhīrú V.+ bhīṣaka E.+ bhayya B. bhetavya E.+ -bhīla E. bhī́ṣaṇa V.+ bhiyás V. bhīmá V.+ bhī́s V.B.U. bhīṣmá B.+ The “causative” stem is, of course, a denominative from a derivative noun. Compare √ bhyas. Meanings bháyate bibhéti 1 v (bibhyati), PPP bhītá (q.v.) fear, be afraid of (Ab or G, r. I or A); fear for, be anxious about (Ab). Caus. bhīṣáyate (ti) & bhāyayati frighten, terrify. ni C put in fright. vi take fright. Cf. prabhīta, vibhīta, saṃbhīta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_bhuj.html"> √ 1 bhuj    √ 1 bhuj, “bend” Present VI. bhujáti etc. V.+ Passive bhujyate C Future Simple Future: bhokṣyati Periphrastic Future: bhoktā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: abhaukṣīt Perfect bubhoja ábubhojīs RV Verbal Nouns bhugna S.+; -bhujya S.+ Derivatives -bhuj AV. bhogá V.+ bhují RV. bhujyú V.B. bhuja E.+ bhujmán ? RV. Meanings bhujáti v PPP bhugna 1 (q.v.) bend, turn, make crooked. ava & ā bend in. ni bend down. nis & vinis bend aside, turn away. pari encompass, embrace. pra bend, fold. Cf. ābhugna, vyābhugna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_bhuj.html"> √ 2 bhuj    √ 2 bhuj, “enjoy” Present I ? bhuñjati etc. U.+,-te etc. E VII. bhuṅkté bhuñjáte etc. V.+ (-jaté RV.), bhunákti bhuñjanti etc. V.+ (bhuñjīyāt. etc. S.+, bhuñjītam E.) Passive bhújyate etc. B.+,-ti M. ? Future Simple Future: bhokṣyate etc. S.+,-ti etc. E.+ Periphrastic Future: bhoktā R Aorist √-Ao: bhojam, bhójate RV. Th Ao: bhujema RV RAo: abūbhujat, -jata -s-Ao: abhaukṣīt, abhukta -siṣ-Ao ? bhukṣiṣīya B.S Precative: bhujyāt; Ao/Ps/3/sg: abhoji Perfect bubhujé etc. V.+ (-jmáhe -jriré RV.), bubhujus E.+ Causative bhojayati etc. AV.+, te C.; bhuñjāpayati C Desiderative bubhukṣate etc. E.+, t1i E Intensive bobhujīti C.,-jyate C Verbal Nouns PPP: bhukta E.+; Inf: bhoktum E.+; 1Abs: bhuktvā B.+, bhuṅktvā C.; bhójase RV.; bhújam bhujé RV Derivatives bhúj V.+ bhóga V.+ bhují RV. bhujiṣyà AV.+ -bhoj- RV. bhogin B.+ -bhogi RV. -bhujiṣṭha ? AV. bhojá V.+ bhógya AV.+ -bhogaya RV. bubhukṣā E.+ bhojaka E.+ bhójana V.+ bhukti S.+ bubhukṣu C. bhojin . S.+ bhojanīya B.+ bhoktavya S.+ bhojayitavya E.+ bhojyà V.+ bhójas V.+ bhoktṛ U.+ bhojayitṛ C. The word bhuṅkṣita R1. is perhaps an irregular formation from this root. Meanings bhunákti bhuṅkté 2 v (bhuñjati, te), PPP bhukta (q.v.) enjoy (in older lang. w. I, later mostly w. A), esp. food (i.e. eat, feed on, ~ A), but also the earth, a country or town (i.e. rule), a woman (i.e. love carnally), etc; experience, endure, atone for (A) at the hands of (G); be of use to, serve (A). Caus. bhojayati (te) cause to enjoy or eat, feed (A of pers. & A or I of th.). Des bubhukṣate (ti) wish to eat, be hungry. bobhujīti 1 enjoy. anu reap the fruit of (A), partake of, enjoy. abhi be of service to (A). upa enjoy (also carnally), eat, consume, use, possess, partake of, live on, reap the fruit of (A); be of use or service to (A). pari eat before another or leave another without food (A); eat, devour, use, employ. sam eat together, keep a common meal, enjoy (also carnally). Caus. cause to eat, feed with (I). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhur.html"> √ bhur    √ bhur, “quiver” Present VI. bhurántu -ránta -rámāṇa RV Intensive járbhurīti -rat -rāṇa RV Derivatives bhuraṇa V. bhurváṇi RV. bhū́rṇi V. bhuríj ? V.+ Doubtless a specialized root-form from √ bhṛ; al the forms and derivatives such as might come from √ bhṛ: cf. √ tṛ. Meanings bhurati bhurate v quiver, jerk, struggle, stir, flash. Int járbhurīti = S. pari Int = S. Int sam Int rush along. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhuraj.html"> √ bhuraj    √ bhuraj The single form bhurajanta RV1. is regarded as coming from √ bhṛjj “roast”. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhuu.html"> √ bhū    √ bhū, “be” Present I. bhávati etc. V.+,-te etc. B.+ Passive bhūyate etc. E.+,-ti U Future Simple Future: bhaviṣyáti etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ (abhaviṣyat etc. U.+, bhaviṣyadhvam E.) Periphrastic Future: bhavitā́ B.U.E Aorist √-Ao: ábhūt -ūvan etc. V.+ (bhūyā́sam -sma etc. V.+,-tāma V.B.U.; bodhí V.B., bhū́tu etc. V.); abhāvi C Th Ao ? ábhuvat etc. V. (bhúvat etc. V.B., bhuvāni RV.) RAo: abūbhuvas AV. abībhavat -iṣ-Ao: bhaviṣāt ? AB. abhaviṣṭa, bhaviṣīṣṭa Perfect babhū́va etc. V.+ (babhū́tha -ū́vitha V.B.; babhūyās -yā́t babhūtu RV.) Causative bhāvayati etc. AV.+,-te C. (bhāvitum R.; bhāvyate etc. E.+, bibhāvayiṣati B.) Desiderative búbhūṣati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ Intensive bobhavīti etc. V.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: bhūtá V.+; Inf: bhávitum B.+,-tos B.; 1Abs: bhūtvā́ V.+,-tvī́ RV.; 2Abs: -bhū́ya V.+; bhuvé -bhúve V.,-bhvè RV.; bhūṣáṇi RV.;-bhū́yam B.,-bhávam ŚB Derivatives bhū́ V.+ bhúvana V.+ bhū́yas V.+ bhāvyá V.+ -bhu V.+ -bhavas B. bhávīyas RV. bhāvana E.+ -bhva V. bhúvas B.+ bhū́yiṣṭha V.+ bhāvanīya E.+ bhúva B.+ bhū́ti V.+ -bhaviṣṭha RV. bhā́vuka B.+ bhava V.+ bhūtí RV. bhū́ri V.+ bubhūṣā B.+ bhavá AV.+ bhávītva RV. -bhū́varī V.B. bubhūṣaka E. bhavaka C. bhavitavyà B.+ bhūṣṇu B.+ bubhūṣitavya JB. -bhavin C. bhavitṛ E.+ bhaviṣṇú B.+ bubhūṣu S.+ bhávya V.+ bhavítra V. -bhū́ya AV.+ bhāvayitavya B.+ -bhvan V. bhū́man V.S. bhāva U.S.+ bhāvayitṛ B.+ bhavana E.+ bhūmán V.+ bhāvaka E.+ bhāvayú RV. bhavanīya C. bhū́mī̆ V.+ bhāvin E.+ Meanings bhávati 1 v (bhávate), PPP bhūtá (q.v.) become, be (N or Adv in ī or ū), rise, appear, happen, occur; exist, live (w. na cease to be, perish, die), stay, abide; be possible or suitable; befall, fall to the lot of, belong to (G, r. D or L); serve for, tend or conduce to (D of th.), devote one's self to, be occupied with (L); get something i.e. thrive, prosper, be lucky (idám); turn out well, succeed. bhavet may be, granted; bhavatu good, possible, enough of this. Caus. bhāvayati, te, PPP bhāvita (q.v.) bring into existence or being, produce, effect, cause; cherish, further, refresh, comfort; practise, exercise; get possessed of, obtain; show, manifest, call to mind, imagine, consider, know, take for (2A); convince, convict, state, establish; mingle, mix, saturate, steep. Des búbhūṣati (te) wish to become or be, to rise or thrive, endeavour at (A); like, prefer, honour, esteem. Int bobhavīti be repeatedly, use to be. ati be or become in a high degree; excel, overcome (A). anu be after, come up with, attain, equal; embrace, comprehend, include; help, serve, further; enjoy, feel, experience, suffer; perceive, hear, learn. samanu enjoy, experience. antar be within, penetrate. apa be absent or wanting. abhi be against, surpass, overcome, oppress, harass, humiliate; turn to, approach or present with (I). ā be present or at hand; exist, live on; come forth, spring from (Ab). anvā follow, imitate. abhyā occur, happen. ud come forth, arise, grow, increase, be sufficient or equal. Caus. bring forth, produce, develop, display. samud spring forth, arise, increase. upa approach, assist. tiras be absent or lost, disappear, vanish. Caus. cause to disappear, dispel. nis be off, move on. parā perish, be lost, succumb, yield; overcome, conquer, harm, hurt, injure. Caus. overthrow, destroy. pari surround, encompass, comprehend, include; attend, manage, take care of (A); surpass, overcome, vanquish; hurt, injure, despise, disgrace; mock, scoff. pra come forth, spring up, arise, appear, happen, occur, spread, expand, increase, grow; be numerous or strong, prevail, rule over, dispose of (G, L, or D); be equal to or a match for (D), be able to or capable of (Inf); be of use, profit, avail (D). Caus. augment, increase, strengthen, nourish, further. prati equal (A). Caus. observe, learn, know. bi expand, develop, arise, appear; suffice for, be equal to, attain, pervade, fill (D or A), be able to (Inf). Caus. cause to expand or develop, open, show, manifest; separate, divide; discern, discover, perceive, know, recognize or acknowledge as, take for (2A), deliberate, ponder, fancy, imagine, suppose, establish, prove, convict, convince. P. be considered as, pass for, appear, seem (N). sam come or be together, assemble, meet, be united with (I saha or L), have sexual intercourse with (I saha or sārdham & A); be held or contained in (L); originate, be produced or engendered, be born, spring from (Ab), happen, occur, exist, become, be, fall to a person's (L or G) share or lot, be possible, be able to or capable of (Inf). Caus. bring together, produce, accomplish, make that-(PPP); go to meet, betake one's self to, salute, honour, gratify or present with (I); combine, think, judge (anyathā falsely); imagine, suppose, give a person (L) credit for (A), consider as, take for (2A) P. be possible. abhisam attain, get possessed of, participate in (A). Cf. antarbhūta, ūdbhūta, prábhūta, samudbhūta, saṃbhūta, saṃbhūya. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhuu_s.html"> √ bhūṣ    √ bhūṣ, “attend upon, adorn” Present I. bhū́ṣati etc. V.B1 Future Simple Future: bhūṣiṣyati Periphrastic Future: bhūṣitā Aorist RAo: abubhūṣat -iṣ-Ao: abhūṣīt Perfect bubhūṣa Causative bhūṣayati etc. E.+,-te etc. E.+ Derivatives bhūṣā E.+ bhūṣaṇa E.+ -bhūṣéṇya RV. bhūṣayitavya E.+ bhūṣya C. bhūṣitavya JB. A secondary root-form, from √ bhū. The Vedic forms are devided by BR. between two roots: √ 1 bhūṣ, “be, move” etc., √ 2 bhūṣ, “attend upon” etc. Meanings bhū́ṣati v be busy for, endeavour at, attend upon (D). Caus. bhūṣayati (te), PPP bhūṣita adorn, embellish (Ā refl.). ā observe, maintain; conform one's self to (L). upa consider, regard, follow (A). pari serve, attend upon (A); honour, obey, follow. Caus. adorn. prati make ready, prepare; wait on, serve, honour, obey. vi Caus. adorn. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bh_r.html"> √ bhṛ    √ bhṛ, “bear” Present I. bíbhramāṇa RV1. bhárati -te etc. V.+ II. bharti RV2 III. bíbharti bíbhrati etc. V.B., bibhárti etc. RV1. +, bibhṛṣva bibhrāṇa C Passive bhriyate etc. V.+,-ti E Future Simple Future: bhariṣyáti etc. V.+ (ábhariṣyat RV.) Periphrastic Future: bhartā́ ŚB Aorist √-Ao: bhartám bhṛtám B., abhṛta C.; bhriyāsam -yāt B.; abhāri V.B RAo: bībharas E -s-Ao: abhārṣīt etc. V.B. (abhār V.B.; abhāriṣam AV.; bharṣat RV.) Perfect babhāra etc. B.+ (babhrima C.), babhre -rāṇá RV.; jabhā́ra etc. V.B.,-bhre etc. V. (jabhartha -bhárat ajabhartana RV.) bibharām babhūva C Causative bhārayati E Desiderative bubhūrṣati etc. B.+ bibhariṣa- Intensive jarbhṛtás RV., bháribhrati etc. RV., barībharti C Verbal Nouns PPP: bhṛtá V.+; Inf: bhártum V.+,-tave V.,-tavaí V.; 2Abs: -bhṛ́tya V.+; bháradhyai RV Derivatives -bhra ? V.+ bhartṛ V.+ bhārá V.+ -bhṛtra RV. bhára V.+ bhrā́tṛ ? V.+ bhārin B.+ -bhṛ́tvan V. -bhala ? AV.S. bharítra RV. bhāryà AV.+ bhṛthá V.+ bháraṇa V.+ -bhárṇas RV. -bhṛt V.+ -babhra B. bharaṇīya E.+ bhárman RV.C. bhṛtí V.+ babhrí V. bharas V.B. bhárīman RV. bhṛ́ti ŚB1. jarbhári RV. -bhári RV.C. bhā́rman RV. bhṛ́tya gdve . B.+ bámbhāri ? B. bharu C. bhariṣá ? RV. bhṛ́tya n . AV. bubhūrṣā S. bharatá V.+ bhrūṇá V.+ bhṛtyā́ V. bubhūrṣu C. bhartavyà V.+ bhṛtenya AV. Meanings bíbharti v (bibhárti), bhárati, bhárate (bharti), PPP bhṛtá bear (in all mgs), hold, carry, wear, keep (also in memory), contain, possess, have, maintain, support, nourish; hire, pay; convey, transport (Ā move on rapidly), take away (Ā for one's self, obtain, win); procure, offer, present, bestow; experience, undergo (w. ājñām obey); raise (the voice or a sound, Ā refl.); fill, load. Des búbhūrṣati wish to keep or maintain. bháribhrat 1, barībharti bear hither and thither or repeatedly. apa carry off, take away. ava bear down, ward off; thrust or push in, introduce; imprint, impress; sever, cut off. ā bring near, procure, cause, produce; fill. paryā bring near from (Ab). samā bring together or near. ud take out, select; deliver from (Ab); lift up, hold high. upa bring near, procure, get. nis take out of (Ab). pari PĀ bring; Ā spread (trans. & intrans. w. A). pra bring forward or near, place before, make ready; offer, present; stretch out, hurl, cast; bring in, introduce; Ā flash, vibrate, rush on, fly along. abhipra hurl, shoot; Ā = prati present, offer. vi take asunder, spread out, diffuse; Ā place here and there, distribute. sam bring together, collect, concentrate, compose, make ready, arrange, prepare, pay back, restore; nourish, foster. Cf. ābhṛta, níbhṛta, saṃbhṛta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bh_rjj.html"> √ bhṛjj    √ bhṛjj, “roast” Present IV. bhṛjyéyus ? B VI. bhṛjjáti etc. V.+-te Passive bhṛjjyate C.,-ti E Future Simple Future: bhrakṣyati -te, bharkṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: bhraṣṭā bharṣṭā Aorist RAo: ababharjjat ababhrajjat -iṣ-Ao: abhrākṣīt abhārkṣīt, abhraṣṭa abharṣṭa Perfect babharjja -je, babhrajja -je Causative bhrajjayati ; bharjjayati etc. C Desiderative bibhrakṣa- bibharkṣa, bibhrajjiṣa- bibharjjiṣa- Intensive barībhṛjjya- Verbal Nouns PPP: bhṛṣṭa S.+; 1Abs: bhṛṣṭvā C Derivatives bharjjana S.+ bhṛjjana B. bhráṣṭra B. bhrāṣṭra C. Meanings bhṛjjáti v PPP bhṛṣṭa roast, parch (esp. grain). Caus. bharjayati = S. ava , pari , sam the same. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhyas.html"> √ bhyas    √ bhyas, “fear” Present I. ábhyasetām RV., bhyásāt SV Future Simple Future: bhyasiṣyati Periphrastic Future: bhyasitā Aorist RAo: abibhyasat -iṣ-Ao: abhyasiṣṭa Perfect babhyase Causative bhyāsaya- Desiderative bibhyasiṣa- Intensive bābhyas- Derivatives -bhyasa AV. A derivative root-form, from √ bhī (through bhiyas?). Meanings bhyásate v fear, tremble at (Ab). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhra_mz.html"> √ bhraṃś, bhraś    √ bhraṃś, bhraś, “fall” Present I. bhráṃśate etc. B.+,-ti AV1. ? IV. bhraśyate etc. S.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: bhraṃśiṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: bhraṃśitā Aorist Th Ao: bhraśat V.B RAo: ababhraṃśat -iṣ-Ao: abhraṃśiṣṭa Perfect babhraṃśa -aśus, babhraṃśe Causative bhraṃśayati etc. E.+ (bhraṃśyate etc. S.+); bhrāśáyan RV Desiderative bibhraṃśiṣa- Intensive bābhraśya- , banībhraśya-, banībhraṃś- Verbal Nouns PPP: bhraṣṭá AV.+,-bhṛṣta V Derivatives bhraṃśa B.+ bhráṃśana AV.+ -bhráṃśuka B. bhrā́śya RV. bhraṃśin B.+ bhraṃśathu C. Meanings bhráśate bhraśyate v (ti), PPP bhraṣṭá (q.v.) fall, drop, bounce against (L) or from (Ab); sink, decline, decay, disappear, be gone or lost; be deprived of, lose (Ab). Caus. bhraṃśayati cause to fall, throw down, drop (trans.); precipitate, overthrow, cause to be lost, deprive of (Ab). pra fall down, disappear, vanish, be deprived of. Caus. bring to fall, deprive of (Ab). vi fail, have no success in (L); turn away from, abandon (Ab). Caus. cut or break off, fell, ruin, destroy; deprive of (Ab). sam fall down. Cf. apabhraṣṭa, paribhraṣṭa, prabhraṣṭa, vibhraṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhram.html"> √ bhram    √ bhram, “wander” Present I. bhramati etc. ŚB1. ? B.+, -te etc. E.+ IV. bhrāmyati etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: bhramiṣyati C Periphrastic Future: bhramitā Aorist √-Ao: bhramyāt S.; abhrāmi E RAo: abibhramat E -iṣ-Ao: abhramīt Perfect babhrāma babhramus etc. E.+, bhrematus -mus C Causative bhrāmayati etc. E.+,-te C. (bhrāmyate U.+); bhramayati etc. S.+ (bhramyate C.) Desiderative bibhramiṣa- Intensive bambhramīti etc. C.,-myate etc. C Verbal Nouns PPP: bhrāṃta E.+; Inf: bhramitum C., bhrāṃtum C.; 1Abs: bhramitvā E., bhrāṃtvā C.; 2Abs: bhramya C.,-bhrāmya C.;-bhrāmam C Derivatives bhṛmá V. bhramá V.+ bhrami C. bhrāmaka C. bhṛmí RV. -bhramin C. bhrāṃti C. bhrāmin C. bhṛ́mi RV. bhramaṇa E.+ bhrāma C. bhrāmaṇa C. bhṛ́ṅga ? AV.+ bhramaṇīya C. Meanings bhramati v (bhramate), bhrāmyati, PPP bhrānta (q.v.) roam, wander, stroll; go through, perambulate (A); fly about, flutter; move round, rotate; stagger about, waver, go astray, be perplexed or mistaken. Caus. bhramayati & bhrāmayati (te) cause to roam etc., whirl round, swing, roll; cause to err, perplex, embarrass, confuse; PPP bhramita falsely taken for or confounded with (– ṃ)*. bambhramīti 1 & bambhraṃmyate wander about or through, the latter also w. pass. mg. ud start up, rise. Caus. whirl around, swing, rouse, agitate, trouble, disturb. pari wander about, roam, turn round. Caus. move to and fro, shake, stir. pra roam, wander through, permeate. vi wander about or through, move to and fro (trans. & intrans.), stagger, tumble, waver, be perplexed or agitated. sam wander, rove, be perplexed or bewildered. Cf. udbhrānta, vibhrānta, saṃbhrānta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhraaj.html"> √ bhrāj    √ bhrāj, “shine” Present I. bhrā́jate etc. V.+,-ti etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: bhrājiṣyate E Periphrastic Future: bhrājitā Aorist √-Ao: abhrāṭ RV.; bhrājyāsam AV.; abhrāji RV RAo: ababhrājat, abibhrajat -iṣ-Ao: abhrājiṣṭa Perfect babhrāja -ājatus E.+ babhrāje, bhreje Causative bhrājayati etc. E.+ Desiderative bibhrājiṣa- Intensive bābhrāj- Derivatives bhrā́j V.+ bhrājaka C. bhrajas ? AV.B. -bhrāṣṭi RV. -bhraj ? V. bhrājin C. bhárgas V.+ bhṛṣṭí ? V.B.S. bhárga B.+ bhrājana C. bhrājí MS. bhrā́jiṣṭha B.C. bhrājá V.+ bhrā́jas V.B.S. bhrājis- B.E. bhrājiṣṇu E.+ bhṛ́gu ? V.+ Meanings bhrā́jate bhrā́jati 1 v shine, flash, beam. – Caus. bhrājayati make shine, irradiate. pari shine all around. pra , vi , sam = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhrii.html"> √ bhrī    √ bhrī, “consume” Present IX. bhrīṇanti RV1 Future Simple Future: bhreṣyati Periphrastic Future: bhretā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: abhraiṣīt Perfect bibhrāya Causative bhrāyaya- Desiderative bibhrīṣa- Intensive bebhrī- Meanings bhrīṇā́ti v hurt. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_bhre_s.html"> √ bhreṣ    √ bhreṣ, “totter” Present I. bhreṣati B.,-te RV Perfect bibhreṣa -ṣe Derivatives bhréṣa B.+ Doubtless related with √ bhraṃś. Meanings bhreṣati bhreṣate v totter, go astray. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ma_mh.html"> √ maṃh, mah    √ maṃh, mah, “be great, be liberal, bestow” Present I. máṃhate etc. V.B. mahe RV.M.,-heta -hema RV Future Simple Future: maṃhiṣyate mahiṣyati Periphrastic Future: maṃhitā mahitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: amaṃhista, amahīt Perfect māmahé -hāná V.B. (māmahanta etc. māmáhas RV.) mamāha, mamaṃhe Causative maṃháyam etc. RV.; maháyati etc. V.+,-te etc. V.B Verbal Nouns PPP: mahitá B.+; 1Abs: mahitvā E.; mahé V.B.; maháye RV Derivatives maghá V.+ makhá ? V.+ mahana C. mahmán AV. maṃhánā RV. majmán ? V. mahanīya E. máhis- RV. maṃhanīya C. máh V.+ mahánt V.+ mahiṣá V.+ máṃhīyas RV. maha n . E.+ mahás V.+ mahiṣṭha C. máṃhiṣṭha V.B.S. mahá V.+ máhas V.+ mahīyas B.+ makṣú ? RV. mahā́ V.+ máhi V.+ mahayya U. maṅkṣu ? C. mahya ? E. mahín RV. mahā́yya RV. maṃhayú RV. mahán V. mahimán V.+ mahayā́yya RV. Generally devided into two (related) roots, but the forms and meanings are not separable with distinctness. Meanings maṃh : máṃhate maṃháyati v grant, bestow, w. vi distribute. mah : mahate mahayati mahate mahayate v PPP mahita 1 (q.v.) P (Ā) gladden; delight, exalt, refresh, excite, impel; esteem highly, honour; Ā be glad, rejoice at (I or A); grant, bestow. sam stir up, excite; honour, celebrate. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_majj.html"> √ majj    √ majj, “sink” Present I. májjati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ (majjāna C.) Future Simple Future: maṅkṣyati etc. B.+,-te B.; majjiṣyati E Periphrastic Future: maṅktā Aorist √-Ao: majjyāt ŚB.; amajji C RAo: amamajjat -s-Ao: amāṅkṣīt -iṣ-Ao: majjīs M Perfect mamajja E.+ Causative majjayati etc. B.+,-te etc. E.+ Desiderative mimaṅkṣa- (in d.) Intensive māmaṅkti , māmajjyate Verbal Nouns PPP: magna U.S.+; Inf: majjitum E.+ maṅktum; 1Abs: maṅktvā, maktvā; 2Abs: -májjya AV.+ Derivatives majján ? V.+ majjūka C. madgú ? B.+ mimaṅkṣu C. majjana S.+ maṅktavya C. -majra ? RV. majjayitṛ́ B. Meanings májjati v (májjate), PPP magna (q.v.) sink (in water), dive, bathe, be submerged or drowned, be ruined, perish. Caus. majjáyati (te) = S. trans. or P ud emerge or plunge. Caus. cause to emerge or come up. upa sink, dive. ni sink down, plunge or penetrate into (L); disappear, perish; cause to sink or fall. Caus. cause to dive, drown. saṃni sink down, fall. nis sink; overflow. pra & vi plunge, rush into (A or L). Cf. āmagna, unmagna, nimagna, saṃmagna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ma_jc.html"> √ mañc    √ mañc, “purify” (?) Present I. mañcate Future Simple Future: mañciṣyate Periphrastic Future: mañcitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: amañciṣṭa Perfect mamañce Verbal Nouns 2 Abs:-mañcya C1 Derivatives mañca ? E.+ -mañcana C. Doubtless artificial. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ma_n.html"> √ maṇ    √ maṇ, “sound” Assumed for the quasi-Part. maṇita, occurring once or twice in late Sanskrit. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ma_n_t.html"> √ maṇṭ    √ maṇṭ, ? Causative maṇṭáyet TB1. Probably a false reading. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ma_n_d.html"> √ maṇḍ    √ maṇḍ, “deck” Present I. maṇḍati -te Causative maṇḍayati etc. E.+,-te E Derivatives maṇḍa U.+ maṇḍana E.+ maṇḍitṛ C. Meanings maṇḍayati v PPP maṇḍita deck, adorn, embellish, glorify. pari & prati = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_math.html"> √ math, manth    √ math, manth, “shake” Present I. mánthati etc. V.+,-te V.B.; máthati etc. AV.E.+,-te etc. E.+ IX. mathnā́ti etc. V.+,-nīte etc. B. (mathnadhvam M.) Passive mathyáte etc. V.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: mathiṣyati -te etc. B.+; manthiṣyati B.S Periphrastic Future: mathitā E Aorist RAo: amīmathat, amamanthat -iṣ-Ao: mathīt etc. V., amathiṣata JB.; ámanthiṣṭām RV Perfect mamā́tha AV.+, mamathus C., methus methire B.; mamantha -nthus E.+ Causative māthayati etc. E.; manthayati etc. S.+; mathayati etc. C Desiderative mimathiṣa- , mimanthiṣa- Intensive māmath- , mammath-, māmanth- Verbal Nouns PPP: mathitá V.+; Inf: mathitum E.+,-tos B., mánthitavaí MS.; 1Abs: mathitvā́ B.+ manthitvā; 2Abs: -máthya B.+,-manthya E. ?;-mātham C Derivatives math V.+ mathí RV. -māthin E.+ -manthanī B.S. -matha E.+ -máthi V. manthá V.+ manthitavyà MS.S. -mathyà B. -mathitṛ S. mánthā V. mánthitṛ AV.B. máthya B.+ mathná RV. manthaka C. manthu ? C. mathan C. mathrá RV. mánthya B.S. manthāna E.+ mathana U.+ mātha B.+ -mánthana V.+ manmatha E.+ Meanings manth mathnā́ti mathnīte máthati 1 v (te), mánthati, te, PPP mathitá stir, whirl (w. agním excite fire by attrition), churn, produce by churning; shake, agitate, confuse, crush, grind, oppress, afflict, destroy, annihilate. Caus. manthayati cause (milk) to be churned. abhi twirl, turn round, w. agním produce fire by attrition. ā churn (the sea), shake, agitate. ud shake up, excite, disturb, mix, mingle; strike, hurt, cut off, tear or root out, destroy, kill. upa stir up, mix, mingle. nis elicit by attrition out of (2 acc), shake or tear out of (Ab), wipe off; stir about, agitate, excite, hurt, harass, crush, pound, break in pieces, destroy. pra stir about, churn (the sea), tear away, cut out or off, harass, annoy, hurt, injure, lay waste, devastate, destroy. Caus. pramāthayati handle roughly, harass, kill. vi Ā tear away, rend asunder, crush down; P rout, disperse, perplex, bewilder. sam pound, crush. Cf. unmathya. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_mad.html"> √ mad, mand    √ mad, mand, “be exhilarated, exhilarate” Present I. mádati etc. V.B.S.C1.,-te etc. AV.B.; mándati -te etc. V.B II. mátsi -sva V III. mamatsi etc. (mamáttu etc., mamádat etc., ámamadus) V IV. mā́dyati etc. B.+,-te E Passive madyámāna RV Future Simple Future: madiṣyati, mandiṣyate Periphrastic Future: maditā, manditā Aorist √-Ao: mandús -dāná RV RAo: ámīmadat etc.-danta V.B.U -s-Ao: amatsus RV., amatta etc. V.B.S. (mátsati etc. mátsat RV.) -iṣ-Ao: amādiṣus etc. V.+ (mādithās M.); ámandīt etc. mándiṣṭa etc. (mandiṣīmahi) V.B Perfect mamā́da V.B. (māmadant ? S.); mamanda etc. RV. (mamandat amamandus RV.) Causative madáyati etc. AV.+,-te C.; mādayati -te V.+; mandáyati etc. RV. (mādayádhyai mandayádhyai RV.) Desiderative mimadiṣa- Intensive māmad- Verbal Nouns PPP: mattá RV.+, maditá (caus.?) V.+; maditos B.; mandádhyai RV Derivatives -mā̆d V.B. -madvara E.+ -mā́dya V. -manda S. máda V.+ mádiṣṭha V.B. mā́dana V.+ mandín RV. madín V.B. madiṣṇu B.+ -mā́duka B. mandána V.B. mádya V.+ matsará V.+ medín ? V.+ mandí RV. madana V.+ mátsya ? V.+ madāmada U. mandāra V.+ -maditavya U. maderú ? RV. madayitṛ C. mandú RV. madirá RV. -mā́da V.+ mādayitṛ C. mandrá V.+ madrá ? B.+ mādaka C. mādayitnú RV. mándiṣṭha RV. mádvan RV. -mādin E.+ mādayiṣṇú V. mandasāná V. mandayú RV. mandayitṛ C. Might well enough be divided into two different though related roots, of kindred meaning. BR. refer a few of the forms to a root √ 2 mad “delay”. Meanings manda , mádati, mádate, mándati, mándate, mamátti, mā́dyati, PPP mattá v (q.v.) bubble, undulate, boil, be agitated or (pleasantly) excited; rejoice at, revel in (I, G, or L, r. A), be mad or drunk with (I); gladden, delight, exhilarate, intoxicate. Caus. madáyati, te, mādayati, te & mandayati, te P (Ā) = S. trans. ; Ā the same refl. anu shout or hail to, acclaim (A). abhi be glad or gladden. ud be excited or out of one's senses; gladden, exhilarate. Caus. excite, confuse, madden. upa rouse, encourage. pra rejoice, exult, be careless about (Ab) not attend to, take it easy. abhipra gladden, exhilarate; perplex, confound. vi be perplexed or confused; confound, embarrass, disturb. sam rejoice together at (I). Cf. abhimatta, āmatta (add.), únmatta, pramatta, vimatta, saṃmatta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_man.html"> √ man    √ man, “think” Present III. mamandhi -nyāt ámaman RV IV. mányate etc. V.+,-ti etc. U.+ (manyā́sai ? ŚB.) VIII. manuté etc. V.+ (manvaté 3p. RV.) Passive manyate C Future Simple Future: maṃsyate etc. B.+ (-syeran M.),-ti E.; maniṣye V.B Periphrastic Future: mantā, manitā Aorist √-Ao: amata RV., ámanmahi V.B. (mánāmahe etc. mananta manāná RV.) RAo: amīmanat -s-Ao: amaṃsta etc. V.+ (máṃsate etc. V.B.; maṃsīṣṭá etc. -sīrata V.; masīya RV.; māṃsta AV.TA.,-stām TA., mandhvam KB.) -iṣ-Ao: amaniṣṭa Perfect mene etc. B.+ (mamnā́the -ā́te RV.) Causative mānayati etc. AV.+,-te etc. E.+ (mānyate E.+; mimānayiṣa- in d.) Desiderative mīmāṃsate etc. AV.+,-ti etc. B.U. (amīmāṃsiṣṭhās ŚB.; mīmāṃsyáte AV.+) mimaṃsa, mimaniṣa- Intensive manman- Verbal Nouns PPP: matá V.+ manita; Inf: mantum E.+, mántave RV.,-tavaí V.B.,-tos B.; 1Abs: matvā́ U.+ manitvā; 2Abs: -matya B.+,-manya E.+ Derivatives -mana ? TS. matí V.+ -māti V.B. -manya V.+ manā́ RV. mántu V. māna V.+ -manyaka C. mánas V.+ mantavyà B.+ -mānaka C. mīmāṃsā́ B.+ manīṣā́ V.+ manotṛ RV. mānin U.+ mīmāṃsaka C. mánu V.+ mantṛ́ B.+ mānya E.+ mīmāṃsya U.S.+ manú V. mántra V.+ mānana E.+ -mimānayiṣu E. mánus V.B. mánman V.B.S. mānanīya E.+ mānayitṛ E.+ manána RV. manyú V.+ -mā́nuka B. mānayitavya E.+ mananā́ RV. múni ? V.+ mananīya C. Compare √ mnā. BR. and Gr. refer, perhaps with reason, the reduplicated present forms to another root, meaning “delay” (√ 2 mad, mand BR.; √ 2 man Gr.). Meanings mányate mányati manuté v PPP matá (q.v.) think, believe, imagine; consider as or take for (2A, A & D, or A & Adv in vat), also refl. consider one's self as, pass for, appear as (N iva); think fit or right, approve of (A); think of, meditate on (as in prayer), intend or wish for, remember, mention, declare (A, r. G); find out, invent; perceive, observe, know, understand, comprehend (G or A). With bahu esteem, honour, w. laghu disesteem, despise, w. sādhu (iti) approve, commend, w. tṛṇāya (cf. above) value at a straw, esteem lightly, w. na think nothing of, disregard; manye methinks-(often inserted parenthetically). Caus. mānayati (te), PPP mānita honour, esteem. Des mīmāṃsate (ti) consider, examine, call in question. ati value lightly, slighten; be proud or conceited. anu assent, approve, like; acknowledge as (2A); grant, impart; allow, permit; indulge, forgive; w. na have no patience with, dislike. Caus. ask (A) for permission, take leave of (A), beg for (A); honour, regard, consider. ava disregard, despise. abhi put one's mind upon, wish for (A), love, like; have (evil) intentions against (A), threaten, menace, hurt, injure, kill; think, suppose, take for or consider as (2A, P. 2 N). ava despise, treat contemptuously, disregard. abhyava the same. pari overlook, neglect, forget. prati answer, return, oppose (2A). Caus. honour, applaud, regard, consider, deign to accept. vi distinguish. Caus. disgrace, disregard, slighten. sam think, suppose, take for (2A); intend, purpose; esteem, honour. Caus. honour, revere. Cf. ánumata, abhimata, vimata, saṃmata. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_mah.html"> √ mah    √ mah see √ maṃh. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_maa.html"> √ 1 mā    √ 1 mā, “measure” Present II. māti etc. V.+, māsva RV., mīmahe C III. mímīte mimate etc. V.+, mimīmas E., mimīyāt etc. mimātu mimīhí etc. V. (mimet KB.) IV. māyate Passive mīyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: māsyati -te Periphrastic Future: mātā Aorist √-Ao: meyāt; amāyi V.+ -s-Ao: ámāsi AV. (mā́sātai AV.) māsīṣṭa -siṣ-Ao: amāsīt Perfect mamé mamiré etc. V.+, mamau etc. RV.C Causative māpayati -te etc. U.S.+ (amīmapat Desiderative mitsati C Intensive māmā- , memīya- Verbal Nouns PPP: mitá V.+; Inf: mātum B.+, mitum C.; 1Abs: mitvā́ V.+, mītvā S.; 2Abs: -mā́ya V.+;-mé -maí RV Derivatives mā́ V.+ -mātavya C. māyā́ V.+ -mitsā C. mā́na V.+ mā́tṛ V.+ māyú V. māpaka C. māná ? RV. mātṛ́ ? V.+ mā́s ,-mas V.+ -māpya C. miti U.+ mā́trā V.+ méya AV.+ -māpana E. Meanings mímīte 2 v (mamāti & māti), PPP mitá (q.v.) measure, mete, compare with (I); measure across i.e. pass through, traverse; measure out = apportion, give, grant; help a pers. (A) to (D); prepare, arrange, form, make, create, develop, display (also refl.) show, manifest; conclude, infer; intrans. (Pr māti) correspond in measure, find room in (L); w. na be beside one's self with (I). Caus. māpayati, te cause to be measured or built, build, erect. anu be inferior in measure, be not equal to (D) in (A); form after i.e. recreate in thought, conclude or infer from (Ab). upa apportion, grant; compare with (I). nis measure ont; fashion or make out of (Ab or I), construct, build, form, make, create, compose, produce, show, betray. abhinis produce, create, make, compose. vinis the same; fashion out of (Ab or I). pari measure around; limit, measure through, complete. pra measure, tax, estimate; frame, create, make, arrange; conceive, understand. vi measure out, pass through, count over, arrange, settle. sam measure, make equal to or compare with (I), apportion, distribute, grant, bestow. Cf. anumita, upamita (add.), nírmita, párimita, pratimita, pramita, sáṃmita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_maa.html"> √ 2 mā    √ 2 mā, “exchange” Present I. mayet M., mayante RV Passive mīyate C Future Simple Future: māsyate, mātā Aorist -s-Ao: amāsta Perfect mame Intensive etc. as √ 1 mā. Verbal Nouns 2 Abs:-mítya AV. ?-māya Derivatives -maya S.+ -mātavya C. Doubtless a specialization of √ 1 mā in connection with certain prepositions. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_3_maa.html"> √ 3 mā    √ 3 mā, “bellow” Present III. mímāti V. (mimeti SV., mimanti RV.; mimīyāt K.) Aorist RAo ? ámīmet V. (mīmayat RV.) Perfect mimāya V.B Intensive mémyat RV Verbal Nouns mā́tavaí . V Derivatives māyú V.+ mayú ? B. mayū́ra ? V.+ Apparently an onomatopoetic root. Meanings mímāti 4 v bellow, roar, low; w. anu & ā bellow etc. towards (A). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_maarg.html"> √ mārg    √ mārg, “chase” Present I. mārgati -te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: mārgiṣyati E Periphrastic Future: mārgitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: amārgīt Perfect mamārga Causative mārgayati etc. E.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: mārgita E.+; Inf: mārgitum E.; 1Abs: mārgitvā E Derivatives mārga E.+ mārgin E. mārgaṇa E.+ mārgitavya E.+ Really a denominative formation from mārga “track”. Meanings mārgati mārgate v (mārgayati), PPP mārgita track, hunt, (cf. seq.), seek for, strive after, ask, request (2A) pari = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_mi.html"> √1 mi    √1 mi, “fix” Present V. minóti etc. V.+, minute S Passive mīyate V Future Simple Future: meṣyant ? AB. māsyati -te Periphrastic Future: mātā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: amāsīt, amāsta -siṣ-Ao: māsīṣṭa. Precative: meyāt; Ao/Ps/3/sg: amāyi Perfect mimāya mimyús RV. mimye Causative māpayati Desiderative mitsati -te Intensive memi- Verbal Nouns PPP: mitá V.B.S.U.;-mitya AV. ? AB.-māya Derivatives maya ? E.+ mít V. -méka ? V.B. métṛ RV. -mayana B. mití V. Doubtless a form of √ 1 mā, with which it agrees also in meaning in later Sanskrit. Meanings minóti minute v PPP mitá 1 (q.v.) fix, establish, build, erect, measure, observe, perceive. ud set up, erect. ni dig in, fix, build, construct. pra erect, build; perceive, understand. vi fix, set up, build. sam fix or set up together. Cf. vímita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_mi.html"> √ 2 mi    √ 2 mi, “damage” see √ mī. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_mik_s.html"> √ mikṣ (miś)    √ mikṣ (miś), “mix” Present I. mímikṣati etc. V.B.S III. mimikṣvá RV Perfect mimikṣáthus etc.-ṣé -ṣire RV Causative mekṣayati B.S Derivatives miśrá V.+ -miśla V.B. -míkṣā V.B.S. mékṣaṇa B.S. mimikṣú RV. Seems a desiderative formation to a simpler √ miś; referred by the grammarians (and Gr.) to √ mih. Meanings mímikṣati 1 v mix, stir up; prepare. Caus. mekṣayati stir up, mix with (I). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_migh.html"> √ migh    √ migh see √ mih. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_mith.html"> √ mith    √ mith, “alternate, altercate” Present I. methati etc. V.B.S., methete RV VI ? mithatī́ RV Perfect mimetha RV Verbal Nouns PPP: mithita RV.; 1Abs: mithitvā C Derivatives mithatí RV. míthu V.B. míthus B. -méthaka ŚB. mithás V.+ mithuná V.+ mithyā́ B.+ -méthana S. Meanings méthati méthate v (& mithati) meet together, either associate, pair; or (more commonly) altercate, wrangle, reproach (A); Ā contest with each other. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_mid.html"> √ mid, mind    √ mid, mind see √ med. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_mil.html"> √ mil    √ mil, “combine” Present VI. milati etc. C Future Simple Future: miliṣyati B.+ Aorist -iṣ-Ao: amelīt, ameliṣṭa Perfect mimilus C Causative melayati etc. C.; melāpaya- (in d.) Verbal Nouns PPP: milita C.; 1Abs: militvā C.; 2Abs: -milya C Derivatives milana C. mela C. melana C. melāpaka C. melaka C. melāpana ? C. Meanings milati v PPP milita (q.v.) meet, assemble, join (I saha, G, or L), mix, combine; occur, happen. Caus. melayati bring together with (G), assemble (trans.). sam come together, be present, get into possession of (G). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_mi_s.html"> √ miṣ    √ miṣ, “wink” Present VI. miṣáti etc. V.+,-te E Future Simple Future: meṣiṣyati (miṣyanti ? R.) Periphrastic Future: meṣitā Aorist RAo: amīmiṣat U -iṣ-Ao: ameṣīt Perfect mimeṣa C Verbal Nouns PPP: miṣita C.; 2Abs: -miṣya C.;-míṣas RV.;-meṣam E Derivatives -miṣ V.+ -meṣa V.+ -meṣaṇa C. -memiṣa B. miṣa V.+ 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_mih.html"> √ mih    √ mih, “urinate” Present I. méhati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ méghamāna RV2 Future Simple Future: mekṣyáti etc. AV.B.S Periphrastic Future: meḍhā Aorist RAo: amīmihat -sa- Ao: amikṣat ŚB Perfect mimeha Causative mehayati etc. RV.C Desiderative mimikṣa-. see √ mikṣ. Intensive mémihat ŚB Verbal Nouns PPP: mīḍha V.+; mihé RV Derivatives míh RV. meha B.+ méhana V.+ méḍhra AV.+ -míhya ŚB. -mehin C. -mehanīya S. meṇḍhra ? C. meghá V.+ mehánā RV. mehatnú RV. mīḍhá ? V.+ mīḍhvā́ṃs ? V.+ Compare √ mikṣ. Meanings méhati 1 v (te), PPP mīḍhá (q.v.) make water; wet, sprinkle. Caus. mehayati cause to make water. abhi urine upon (A). ava make water upon or towards (A). ni = S. pari wet by urining upon. pra = S. prati make water in the direction of (A). Cf. mīḍhváṃs. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_mii.html"> √ mī, mi    √ mī, mi, “damage” Present III. mimītas ? RV.,-īyāt ? V.B IV. mī́yate etc. RV.B.+ V. minoti etc. RV1.C1 IX. minā́ti etc. V.B., aminanta mināná RV. (minat -nan RV., minīt AV.); mīnāti ŚB. mīnīte Passive mīyáte etc. ŚB.MS Future Simple Future: meṣyase PB. māsyati, -te Periphrastic Future: mātā Aorist -s-Ao: amāsta, māsīṣṭa; meṣṭa etc. AV.B.S -siṣ-Ao: amāsīt Precative: mīyāt Ao/Ps/3/sg: ámāyi B Perfect mimāya etc. RV., mimye C. (mīmaya AV.) mamau, mame Causative māpayati etc. E.+ amīmapat Desiderative mitsa- Intensive mémyāna RV Verbal Nouns PPP: mīta V.+; métos B.; 1Abs: mītvā; 2Abs: -mīya, -māya; míyam -míye RV Derivatives -mi- ? RV. -mīya B. -māyu B. -mātavya E. -mī RV. -mayu AV. mā́yuka AV.B. -māpana E.+ -maya B.+ -mīti C. -māpayitṛ C. Meanings minā́ti v (minoti) damage, lessen, diminish; fail, transgress; frustrate, annul; Ā P. mīyáte, mī́yate perish, be lost. Caus. māpayati only with pra (q.v.) ā disturb, remove, annul, change, alter (Ā intrans., refl., or recipr.). ud Ā disappear. pra frustrate, annul, destroy, annihilate; change, alter; transgress, neglect, miss, forget; outstrip, sur pass. P. Ā perish, die. Caus. destroy, kill; cause to be killed by (I). Cf. pramīta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_miil.html"> √ mīl    √ mīl, “wink” Present I. mīlati etc. B.+,-te S Passive mīlyate C Future Simple Future: mīliṣyati Periphrastic Future: mīlitā Aorist RAo: amimīlat C. amīmilat -iṣ-Ao: amīlīt Perfect mimīla C Causative mīlayati B.+,-te E Desiderative mimīliṣa- Intensive memīl- Verbal Nouns PPP: mīlita B.+; 2Abs: -mī́lya V.+ Derivatives -mīla S.+ mīlaka C. -mīlin AV.C. mīlana E.+ Meanings mīlati v PPP mīlita (q.v.) close the eyes, wink (also = mil). Caus. mīlayati close, shut. ā & vyā Caus. close (the eyes). ud open, expand, (trans. & intrans.); come forth, appear. Caus. open, expand, manifest. prod & samud = ud (also Caus. ). ni shut the eyes, wink; close, contract (intrans.); disappear, vanish. Caus. shut or cause to shut. sam close the eyes; close up, contract (intrans.). Caus. close, shut. Cf. unmīlita, nimīlita, saṃmīlita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_miiv.html"> √ mīv, mū    √ mīv, mū, “push” Present I. mī́vati etc. AV.B Verbal Nouns mīvitá B.,-mūta V.S.;-mī́vya B Derivatives -mu ? C1. mūrá RV1. -maviṣṇu ? RV1. -móta ? AV1. Meanings mīvati v PPP mūta (q.v.) & mīvita push, move. ā push aside, wrench open (door). pra push towards. prati push back, shut to. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_muc.html"> √ muc, mokṣ    √ muc, mokṣ, “release” Present VI. muñcáti etc. V.+,-te etc. V.+; mucánti etc. mucasva etc. (Th Ao?) RV.TA Passive mucyáte etc. AV.+, múcyase etc. V.,-ti etc. U.E+ Future Simple Future: mokṣyati -te etc. B.+ Periphrastic Future: moktā Aorist √-Ao: ámok AV. (mogdhí TA.); mucīṣṭa RV. Th Ao: ámucat etc. V RAo: amūmucat C -s-Ao: amauk etc. B. (mokṣīs C.), ámukṣi etc. V.; mukṣīya V.B Ao/Ps/3/sg: ámoci V.+ Perfect mumóca mumucé etc. V.+ (mumoktu etc. V.B., mumócat etc. múmocati mumucas amumuktam RV.) Causative mocayati -te etc. E.+ (mocyate C.; mumocayiṣa- C.) Desiderative múmukṣati -te etc. V.+; mókṣate etc. B.+ Intensive momuc- Verbal Nouns PPP: muktá AV.+; Inf: moktum B.+; 1Abs: muktvā́ B.; 2Abs: -múcya V.+; mókam B Derivatives -muc V.+ mocya E.+ mucyu GB. mumucu E.+ -mucī AV. mócana V.+ -mukṣā MS. mumukṣā E.+ -muca E.+ mocanīya B.+ mokṣa B.+ mumukṣú V.+ moka ,-kī V.+ -muci E. mokṣaka E.+ mocayitṛ C. -mokya AV. -mucu E.+ mokṣin E.+ mocayitavya C. moca E.+ múkti AV.+ mokṣya C. mumocayiṣu E. mocaka C. moktavya E.+ mokṣaṇa E.+ mokṣayitavya C. -mocin C. moktṛ B.+ mokṣanīya E. mokṣayitṛ E. mumokṣayiṣu E. The desiderative formation mokṣ has nearly the same right to be treated as a separate root that √ bhakṣ has. Meanings muñcáti muñcáte 1 v & mucáti, mucáte, PPP muktá, ger. mukttā́ (q.v.) release, deliver from (Ab or tas) unloose, open; let go, set free, relinquish, abandon, forsake, quit, put off, lay aside, give up, grant, bestow; discharge, shed; emit, utter; send forth, shoot, throw, hurl against (L, D, G, or A w. prati). P.Ā mucyate (múcyate, mucyati) be released from, get rid of, escape (Ab & I, r. G), be deprived of, want (I); be liberated from sin or mundane existence. Caus. mocayati, te release, deliver or redeem from (Ab, r. I), set free, let loose; unbind, open etc., cause to give up or discharge (2A). Des mumukṣati, te P be about to give up or send forth, Ā (also mókṣate) wish to be liberated from (Ab). esp. desire final liberation. ati P. avoid, escape (A). abhi let loose, emit, stream forth; throw, hurl, shoot off. ava loose, release, unyoke, unharness; take off, doff. ā put on (a garment); let loose, emit, hurl, throw, cast. ud free or save from (Ab); unfasten, loosen, open; take off, doff; leave, relinquish; give back, restore; send forth, emit, throw, hurl. Caus. deliver from (Ab), loosen, untie (the hair), take off. upa put on, don. nis loosen, untie, free from (Ab). P. cast the skin (of a snake), be stripped or deprived of (I). vinis abandon, give up; P. be delivered from (I). pari free from (Ab), loose, unbind, take off, abandon, give up, send forth, emit. P. get rid of (Ab, G, or I), be liberated from worldly ties. pra et go release from (Ab), loosen, untie, shake off scare away, abandon, give up, emit, discharge, shed; hurl, shoot off. P. get rid of (Ab or I); become loose, fall off (fruit); leave off, cease. vipra free, deliver, loosen, unfasten, take off. P. be liberated from (Ab), escape. prati fasten on (L), put on, dress a person (D, L, or G); with (A). Ā dress one's self, assume (a form etc.); set free, release, dismiss, give up, abandon, return, restore (a debt). P. get rid of (Ab). Caus. rescue, save. vi loosen, unharness, take off (clothes); abandon, quit, give up, avoid, loose, w. na not rest or leave off; forgive, pardon; emit, pour forth, utter; hurl, cast, shoot off, take, assume (a shape). Ā (also P) unharness, put up, stop; (also P.) get loose, fall off; P. be freed or escape from, be deprived of, lose (Ab, Adv in tas, or I). Caus. unloose, unharness, liberate from (Ab), ward off. pravi dismiss, let loose, give up. sam pourforth, shed (tears). Caus. liberate. Cf. átimukta, āmukta, unmukta, nirmukta, vinirmukta, vipramukta, vimukta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_mu_t.html"> √ muṭ    √ muṭ, “break” Present I. moṭate C1 Causative moṭayati C1 Derivatives moṭaka C. -moṭin C. moṭana C. Meanings moṭate v w. ud break or pluck off. Caus. moṭayati (prati) strangle, smother, kill. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_mud.html"> √ mud    √ mud, “be merry” Present I. módate etc. V.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: modiṣye E Periphrastic Future: moditā Aorist √-Ao: mudīmahi RV RAo: amūmudat -iṣ-Ao: modiṣīṣṭhās AV Perfect mumóda V.+, mumude etc. E.+ Causative modayati -te etc. B.+ (mumodayiṣati ŚB.) Desiderative mumudiṣa- , mumodiṣa- Intensive momud- Verbal Nouns PPP: mudita E.+;-modam C Derivatives múd V.+ móda V.+ modana E.+ mudrá V. -muda AV.+ modaka E.+ modanīya U.+ mudira ? C. mudā E.+ modin AV.+ -mudvin ? C. Meanings modate 1 v (modati), PPP mudita (q.v.) be glad or merry, rejoice at, have pleasure in (L or I). Caus. modayati (te) gladden. anu rejoice after, with, or at (A of pers. & th.); agree to, approve of, applaud, permit. Caus. gladden; approve of etc. = S. pra become or be joyful, exult. Caus. gladden. prati meet or welcome with joy, rejoice at (A, r. G). Caus. delight, exhilarate. Cf. pramudita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_mu_s.html"> √ muṣ    √ muṣ, “steal” Present I. móṣatha RV1 VI. muṣati etc. E IX. muṣṇāti etc. V.+ (muṣāṇa C.) Passive muṣyate etc. C.,-yant E Future Simple Future: moṣiṣyati Periphrastic Future: moṣitā Aorist √-Ao: amoṣi C RAo: amūmuṣat -iṣ-Ao: moṣīs amoṣiṣus V.B Perfect mumoṣa C Causative moṣaya-; muṣayant ? C Desiderative mumuṣiṣa- Intensive momuṣ- Verbal Nouns PPP: muṣitá V.+, muṣṭa C.; 1Abs: muṣitvā C.; 2Abs: -múṣya V.+; muṣé RV Derivatives -muṣ V.+ mū̆ṣaka C. muṣṭí ? V.+ -moṣin B.+ mū́s RV. -múṣi B. moṣa B.+ moṣya C. mūṣa E.+ muṣīván RV. -moṣaka E. moṣaṇa S.C. Meanings muṣṇā́ti 1 v (móṣati, muṣati), PPP muṣitá (q.v.) rob, steal, plunder, rob or bereave of (2A); carry off, ravish (lit. & fig.); surpass, excel. abhi rob of (2A). ava , ā & nis take away, carry off. pari rob of (2A). pra rob, take away. withdraw. vi & sam rob, carry off. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_muh.html"> √ muh    √ muh, “be crazed” Present IV. múhyati etc. V.+,-te etc. U.+ Future Simple Future: mohiṣyáti B. mokṣyati Periphrastic Future: mohitā, mogdhā, moḍhā Aorist Th Ao: amuhat etc. B RAo: amūmuhat etc. AV.B Perfect mumoha etc. B.+, mumuhe E Causative moháyati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ (mohyate C.) Desiderative mumohiṣa- , mumuhiṣa-, mumukṣa- Intensive momuhat S., momuhyate E Verbal Nouns PPP: mugdhá V.+, mūḍha AV.S.U.+; muhé RV.;-móham B Derivatives -muh AV.B. mudhā ? E.+ -mohaka E. móhuka B. múhu V.B. mógha V.B. mohin E.+ momughá B. múhus V.+ móha AV.+ mohana E.+ mohayitṛ E. Meanings múhyati v (múhyate), PPP mugdhá & mūḍhá (q.v.) be confused or faint; ert, lose one's senses; fail, not turn out well. Caus. moháyati, te confuse, bewilder, disarrange, cause to rr or fail. Int momuhyate be in great confusion. ati = S. Int anu become perplexed after (A). vyā Ā become perplexed; Caus. perplex, bewilder, confuse pari err, go astray (fig.). Caus. make confused, throw into disorder. pra become perplexed or embarrassed, lose consciousness, faint vi & sam the same; Caus. stupefy, deprive of consciousness, cause to err or fail. Cf. atimugdha, atimūḍha, unmugdha (add.), parimūḍha, pramugdha, pramūḍha, vimugdha, vimūḍha, vyāmūḍha, saṃmugdha, saṃmūḍha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_muu.html"> √ mū    √ mū see √ mīv. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_muurch.html"> √ mūrch, mūr    √ mūrch, mūr, “thicken” Present I. mūrchati etc. AV.+ Future Simple Future: mūrchiṣyati Periphrastic Future: mūrchitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: amūrchīt Perfect mumūrcha E.+ Causative mūrchayati B.+,-te E Verbal Nouns PPP: mūrchita E.+, mūrtá B.+ 1Abs: mūrtvā Derivatives mūrá ? V.B. mūrkhá B.+ mūrchā E.+ mūrchana E.+ mū́rti B.+ Meanings mūrchati v PPP mūrtá & mūrchita (q.v.) become rigid, coagulate, thicken, increase, grow, sound loudly; become torpid or senseless, faint away, swoon. Caus. mūrchayati (te) cause to thicken; form, shape, strengthen, augment, excite, rouse. sam thicken, coagulate, become firm or solid, sound loudly. Caus. stupefy, stun. Cf. vimūrchita, saṃmūrchita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_m_r.html"> √ 1 mṛ    √ 1 mṛ, “die” Present I. maranti etc. márate etc. RV. (mara C1.) Passive mriyáte etc. V.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: mariṣyati etc. AV.+,-te E Periphrastic Future: martā Aorist √-Ao: amṛta etc. V.B.S.; murīya V RAo: amīmarat etc. B.C -s-Ao: mṛṣīṣṭa Perfect mamā́ra mamrus etc. V.+, mamre etc. C Causative māráyati etc. AV.+,-te E. (māryate etc. E.+; mimārayiṣa- in d.) Desiderative mumūrṣati etc. S.+ Intensive marīmarti C. marmṛ-, memrīya- Verbal Nouns PPP: mṛtá V.+; Inf: martum E.+,-tave AVP.; 2Abs: mṛtvā́ B.+;-māram E Derivatives mara V.+ marā́yu V.B. márman ? V.+ mā́ruka B.S. maraka C. márta ,-tya V.+ māra V.+ -mamri AV. maraṇa B.+ mṛti C. māraka C. múrmura ? B.+ maru ? B.+ martavya E.+ mārin B.+ mumūrṣā E.+ -mura ? AV. mṛtyú V.+ mā́raṇa B.+ mumūrṣu B.+ mimārayiṣu C. The following root (√ 2 mṛ, mṛṇ, “crush”) is doubtless the same with this. Meanings marati márate v also P. mriyáte 1 (ti), PPP mṛtá (q.v.) die, depart from life. Caus. māráyati (te) kill, slay, put to death. Des mumūrṣati wish or be about to die. Int maṃrīmarti suffer the pangs of death. anu die after (A), follow in death. abhi affect or soil by dying. pari die around (A). Cf. pramṛta & mamṛvás. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_m_r.html"> √ 2 mṛ, mṛṇ    √ 2 mṛ, mṛṇ, “crush” Present VI. mṛṇáti etc. V.B IX. mṛṇīhí etc. V Passive mūryáte ŚB Aorist √-Ao: mṛṇyus K RAo: ámīmṛṇan AV -iṣ-Ao: amārīt Perfect mumurat ? RV Verbal Nouns PPP: mūrṇá AV.B Derivatives múr RV. mura ? E.+ -marītṛ RV. malímlu ? B. -múri RV. -mṛṇa V.B. Hardly to be separated from the preceding root, √ 1 mṛ. Meanings mṛṇā́ti v PPP mūrṇa 2 crush, destroy. upa P. (mūryáte) be destroyed. ni , pra & vi = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_m_rk_s.html"> √ mṛkṣ    √ mṛkṣ, “stroke” Present I. mrakṣanti C VI. mṛkṣā RV Perfect mimṛkṣus RV Causative mrakṣaya- C., mṛkṣayati E Derivatives mṛkṣá RV. mṛkṣín RV. -mrakṣa RV. mrakṣaṇa C. Doubtless a secondary root-form from √ mṛj. Meanings mṛkṣáti mrakṣati v stroke, rub, smear. Caus. mrakṣayati, PPP mrakṣita = seq. abhi S. & Caus. smear, anoint ni rub on, touch (L) 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_m_rc.html"> √ mṛc    √ mṛc, “injure” Present IV. mṛcyati ? JB Aorist -s-Ao: mṛkṣīṣta RV Causative marcáyati etc. V.B.S Verbal Nouns mṛktá RV.AA Derivatives mṛ́c RV. marká RV. márka B.S. mṛcaya AB. Meanings PPP mṛktá; Caus. marcáyati 1 injure, hurt. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_m_rch.html"> √ mṛch    √ mṛch, “perish” Present I. mṛchante U. Very likely a false reading; if not, a secondary root, from √ 1 mṛ. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_m_rj.html"> √ mṛj    √ mṛj, “wipe” Present I. mārjati -te etc. E.+ II. mā́rṣṭi mṛjánti mārjanti etc. V.+, mṛṣṭé mṛjate etc. V.+ (mārjīta S.) VI. mṛjati -te etc. AV1.S.C VII. mṛñjata (3p.) RV., mṛṇajāni GB., mṛñjyāt ŚB Passive mṛjyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: mrakṣyate B., mārkṣyate B.S. mārjiṣyati Periphrastic Future: mraṣṭā JB. mārṣṭā, mārjitā Aorist RAo: amīmṛjanta B. amamārjat -s-Ao: amārkṣīt etc. B -iṣ-Ao: amārjīt etc. B -sa- Ao: amṛkṣat etc. V.B.S., amṛkṣata etc. RV.B Ao/Ps/3/sg: amārji Perfect mamā́rja mamṛjus etc. V.+ (mamārjus E., māmṛjus RV.), mamṛje AV. (māmṛjé -jīta RV.) Causative marjayati -te etc. V.; mārjayati -te etc. B.+ (mārjyate C.) Desiderative mimārjiṣa- , mimṛkṣa- Intensive marmṛjmá -janta etc. RV.,-jyáte etc. V.B.S. (marmṛjāná RV.), marīmṛjyate B Verbal Nouns PPP: mṛṣṭá V.+, mṛjita C., mārjita (caus.?) S.+; Inf: marṣṭum C., mārṣṭum C., mārjitum E.+; 1Abs: mṛṣṭvā́ AV.S., mārjitvā B.; 2Abs: -mṛ́jya AV.+,-mārjya C.;-mṛ́jas B Derivatives -mṛja C. -mārjaka E.+ mārjāra E.+ mārṣṭavya C. mṛjā E.+ mā́rjana V.+ mārjālyà RV. -mṛgra RV. márjya RV. -mārjanīya E. mṛ́ṣṭi B.+ -mṛ́gvan AV. -mārga AV.+ -mā́rguka B. mārṣṭi C. marmṛjénya RV. Compare √ mṛkṣ. Meanings mā́rṣṭi mṛṣṭé v (mṛjáti, mṛjáte, mārjati, mārjate), marjáyati, te & mārjáyati, te, PPP mṛṣṭá (q.v.), mṛjita & mārjita (q.v.) wipe, clean, polish, rub, stroke, adorn (Ā also refl.); wipe off, remove, destroy, get rid of (A); (also Ā) wipe off (a guilt, i.e. throw it) upon (L); Ā take away, carry off, win. Int marmṛjyáte, marīmṛjyate, etc. wipe or clean repeatedly, Ā one's self. anu wipe down, smooth, purify. apa wipe off, remove, throw upon (L). ava stroke down wards, wipe away. ā wipe off, clean, purify. ud stroke upwards; wipe off, clean, adorn; Ā refl., also carry off, win. upa stroke, wipe, polish. ni rub in or upon (L), rub or wipe off (Ā refl.), lead to, bestow on (L); Ā take for one's self, carry off. nis wipe off, destroy. pari wipe all round, rub, stroke, polish, clean, purify; wipe away, remove, destroy, get rid of (A). pra wipe, polish, clean, stroke; wipe off, remove, destroy, frustrate. vi wipe off, rub dry, clean, purify, embellish, adorn (tanvṛm refl.), stroke, smear, anoint sam rub off, sweep clean, strain, filter, purify, stroke; wipe off, remove, destroy. Cf. unmṛṣṭa, parimṛṣṭa, pramṛṣṭa, saṃmṛṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_m_r_d.html"> √ mṛḍ    √ mṛḍ, “be gracious Present VI. mṛḍáti etc. V.B.S.,-ase B IX. mṛḍnāti Future Simple Future: marḍiṣyati Periphrastic Future: marḍitā Aorist RAo: amīmṛḍat amamarḍat -iṣ-Ao: amarḍīt Perfect mamarḍa (mamṛḍyus RV.) Causative mṛḍáyati etc. V.B.C.,-te C Desiderative mimarḍiṣa- Intensive marīmṛḍ- Derivatives mṛḍa B.+ mṛḍīká V.+ marḍitṛ́ RV. -mṛḍaya B. mṛḍana C. mṛḍitṛ́ AV. mṛḍayā́ku RV. mṛdya C. Meanings mṛḍati v (mṛḷáti), te & mṛḍayati (mṛḷáyati), te be gracious, forgive (D of pers. & A of th.); treat graciously, make happy. abhi forgive. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_m_r_n.html"> √ mṛṇ    √ mṛṇ see √ 2 mṛ. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_m_rd.html"> √ mṛd, mrad    √ mṛd, mrad, “rub, crush” Present I. mardati -te etc. E.+ mrada RV.,-date MS IX. mṛdnāti etc. S.+, mṛdnīta S Passive mṛdyáte etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: mradiṣyati mardiṣyate JB Aorist √-Ao: mṛdyāsam B.S RAo: amīmṛdat E. amamardat -iṣ-Ao: amardīt Perfect mamarda mamṛdus E.+ (mamardus M.), mamṛde E Causative mardayati etc. E.+,-te E. (mardyate C.; mimardayiṣa- in d.); mradayati TS Desiderative mimardiṣati E Intensive marmarttu RV. marīmṛd- Verbal Nouns PPP: mṛditá AV.; Inf: marditum E.+,-tos B.; 1Abs: mṛditvā C.; 2Abs: -mṛ́dya B.+;-mradé B.;-mardam C Derivatives mṛ́d V.+ mardin E.+ mṛ́ttikā B.+ mṛdú AV.+ -mṛda S. márdana B.+ marditavya E. mṛtsnā B.+ marda E.+ mardanīya C. -marditṛ E. mimardiṣu E. mardaka C. -mradas V.B.S. mradīyas B. mimardayiṣu E. Meanings mṛdnāti mardati mṛdnāti mardate 1 v (mradati, mradate) PPP mṛditá, rub, squeeze, crush, smash; wipe off, destroy. Caus. mardayati, te press or rub hard, pound, crush, grind down, destroy, harass, afflict, also cause to be rubbed etc. abhi crush, smash, destroy, lay waste. ava the same. ud rub in, mix with (instr). ni smash, destroy, rub or strip off. pari trample down, squash, wear away, wipe off. pra crush down, bruise, pound, destroy, ravage. vi & sam the same. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_m_rdh.html"> √ mṛdh    √ mṛdh, “neglect” Present I. márdhati etc. RV VI. mṛdhāti RV.S., -asva S Aorist √-Ao: mṛdhyās RV Th Ao: mṛdhas S -iṣ-Ao: mardhīs etc. RV.B. (márdhiṣat RV.) Verbal Nouns mṛddhá MS Derivatives mṛ́dh V.B. mṛdha V.+ mṛ́dhas RV. mṛdhrá RV. mardhuka JB. Meanings márdhati v PPP mṛddhá 1 (q.v.) neglect, forsake, contemn, despise. pari slacken, relent, cease. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_m_rz.html"> √ mṛś    √ mṛś, “touch, feel” Present VI. mṛśáti etc. V.+,-te etc. V.+ Passive mṛśyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: markṣyati mrakṣyati Periphrastic Future: marṣṭā mraṣṭā Aorist -s-Ao: amārkṣīt amrākṣīt mṛkṣīṣṭa ? RV -sa- Ao: ámṛkṣat etc. V.B Perfect mamarśa mamṛśus E.+ (māmṛśús RV.), mamṛśe B.+ Causative marśayati etc. B.+ Intensive mármrśat etc. V.B., marīmṛśya- B Verbal Nouns PPP: mṛṣṭá V.+, mṛśita C.; Inf: marṣṭum E.+; 2Abs: -mṛ́śya V.+;-mṛ́śe V.B.;-márśam B.S Derivatives -mṛśa B.+ marśa B.+ -marśin U.+ marīmṛśá AV. -mṛśya B.+ -marśaka E. márśana V.+ Meanings mṛśáti mṛśáte v PPP mṛṣṭá & mṛśita touch, stroke, grasp, take hold of (lit. & fig.); think of, consider. anu grasp, seize, take into consideration. abhi touch, feel, bring into contact with (I). ava touch, grope, consider. ā touch, feel, enjoy, consider, examine. parā touch, seize, grasp, violate (a woman); point to, mean, P. be meant. pari touch, grope, seize, examine, try, consider. pra touch, feel, vi touch, feel, stroke, try, examine, find out. Caus. consider, reflect upon. sam take hold of, seize, touch. Cf. āmṛṣṭa, 2 parimṛṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_m_r_s.html"> √ mṛṣ    √ mṛṣ, “not heed” Present I. marṣati -te IV. mṛ́syate etc. V.+,-ti etc. E.+ Passive mṛṣyate E Future Simple Future: marṣiṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: marṣitā Aorist √-Ao: mṛṣṭhās RV Th Ao: amṛṣan M., mṛṣat S. (-ṣant ? C.),-ṣanta RV RAo: mīmṛṣas V. amamarṣat -iṣ-Ao: amarṣīt, marṣiṣṭhās RV Perfect mamárṣa RV.E., mamṛṣe E Causative marṣayati etc. E.+,-te etc. E.+ Intensive māmṛṣat S Verbal Nouns PPP: mṛṣita ; 1Abs: mṛṣitvā, marṣitvā; 2Abs: -mṛṣya E.;-mṛ́ṣe RV Derivatives -mṛ́ṣā V.+ -márṣa V.+ marṣaṇa E.+ -marṣi E. -mṛṣya RV. marṣin E.+ marṣaṇīya E.+ Meanings mṛ́ṣyate v (mṛ́ṣyati) not heed, forget, suffer, bear, put up with (A). Caus. marṣayati, te make forget (A); suffer, endure, bear, forgive, pardon; w. na not let alone, molest, disturb. api forget, neglect. ā (also Caus. ) bear patiently. upa Caus. the same. pra forget, neglect (A or D). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_med.html"> √ med (mid)    √ med (mid), “be fat” Present IV. médyati etc. V.B VI. medátām RV Passive midyate Future Simple Future: mediṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: meditā Aorist Th Ao: amidat -iṣ-Ao: amediṣṭa Perfect mimeda , mimide Causative mindayati ; medáyati etc. V.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: minna , 1Abs: miditvā meditvā Derivatives médana RV. medín V.+ médas V.+ medurá B.+ medya C. Meanings mádyati v (medáte) be fat. Caus. medáyati make fat. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_mod_s.html"> √ modṣ    √ modṣ see √ muc. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_mnaa.html"> √ mnā    √ mnā, “note” Present I. manati etc. S.+,-te S II. mnāyus C1 Passive mnāyate C Future Simple Future: mnāsyati Periphrastic Future: mnātā Aorist √-Ao: mnāyāt, mneyāt -siṣ-Ao: amnāsiṣus C Perfect mamnau Causative mnāpaya- , amimnapat Desiderative mimnāsa- Intensive māmnā- Verbal Nouns PPP: mnāta S.+ Derivatives -mnāna S.+ -mnātavya C. -mnāya S.+ Only with prefix ā: a secondary root-form from √ man- to which, indeed, the forms from stem mana- more properly belong. Meanings manati v w. ā mention, repeat, regard as, take for (A). samā the same. Cf. āmnāta (add.), samāmnāta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_myak_s.html"> √ myakṣ    √ myakṣ, “be situated” (?) Present I. myakṣa RV Aorist √-Ao: amyak RV. Ao/Ps/3/sg: amyakṣi RV Perfect mimyákṣa mimikṣús -kṣire RV Meanings myákṣati v be fixed in, rest on (L); be present. apa keep off. ā be present in or on (L). ni hold; Ā be present in (L). parā be beside. sam keep together. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_mrad.html"> √ mrad    √ mrad see √ mṛd. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_mrit.html"> √ mrit, mlit    √ mrit, mlit, “dissolve” Present IV ? mṛityét -yeyus ŚB Verbal Nouns -mletya S Derivatives -mretuka PB. Perhaps related with √ mṛd. Meanings mrityáti (vi) v dissolve, decay. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_mruc.html"> √ mruc, mluc, mlup    √ mruc, mluc, mlup, “set” Present I. mrócati etc. AV.B.; mlócati etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: mrociṣyati, mlociṣyati Periphrastic Future: mrocitā, mlocitā Aorist Th Ao: amrucat JB -iṣ-Ao: amrocīt, amlocīt Perfect mumloca ŚB.U Intensive malimlucāmahe S Verbal Nouns PPP: mrukta B.+, mlukta RV., mlupta B.S.;-mrúcas RV Derivatives -mruc V.B. -mrocana C. -mrukti B. malimlucá AV.+ mroká AV. -mlocana C. -mlukti C. malimluc S. -mloca E.+ -mloci C. Meanings mrócati v w. ni set (of the sun), w. abhi ni set upon (A). Cf. abhinimrukta (add.). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_mre_d.html"> √ mreḍ    √ mreḍ, “gratify” (?) Present I. mreḍeran U1 Causative mreḍayati etc. E.+ (mrelayati S.) Derivatives -mreḍa C. Meanings mreḍayati v PPP mreḍita (q.v.) gratify, to be mad. ā repeat, PPP reiterated, repeated, (in Gr.) reduplication, reiteration, the second word in a reiteration upani to make happy, gladden 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_mlaa.html"> √ mlā    √ mlā, “relax” Present II. mlānti E IV. mlā́yati etc. B.+,-te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: amlāsyatām B.,-yetām U Periphrastic Future: mlātā Aorist √-Ao: mlāyāt, mleyāt -siṣ-Ao ? mlāsīs E Perfect mamlau etc. E.+ Causative mlāpáyati AV.+ ; mlapayati C Verbal Nouns PPP: mlātá RV., mlāna B.+ Derivatives -mlāni C. -mlāyin C. -mlāpana C. mlāpin C. Meanings mlā́yati mlā́yate (mlāti) v PPP mlātá & mlāna (q.v.) relax, languish, wither, fade, decay. Caus. mlāpáyati cause to wither or langish, weaken. pari , pra , vi = S. Cf. āmlāna & parimlāna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_mluc.html"> √ mluc    √ mluc see √ mruc. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_mlup.html"> √ mlup    √ mlup see √ mruc. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_mlech.html"> √ mlech    √ mlech, “speak barbarously” Present I. mlechati etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: mlechiṣyati Periphrastic Future: mlechitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: amlechīt Perfect mimlecha Verbal Nouns PPP: mlechita , mliṣṭa Derivatives mlechá B.+ Meanings mlechati to speak indistinctly (like a foreigner or barbarian who does not speak Sanskrit) 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_yak_s.html"> √ yakṣ    √ yakṣ, “press on” (?) Present I. yákṣati etc. RV1.R1.,-te RV1 Verbal Nouns -yákṣe RV2 Derivatives yakṣá V.+ yákṣya RV. yákṣu RV. yákṣma V.+ yakṣín RV. yakṣman E.+ The character fo the root and the connection of its derivatives are very doubtful. Meanings yákṣati yákṣate v w. pra press on, strive after (A), overtake. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_yach.html"> √ yach    √ yach see √ yam. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_yaj.html"> √ yaj    √ yaj, “offer” Present I. yájati -te etc. V.+ II. yákṣi V.B.S., yákṣva RV. yajase (1s.) RV1 Passive ijyate etc. E.+,-yant E Future Simple Future: yakṣyati etc. B.+,-áte etc. V.+ Periphrastic Future: yaṣṭā́ B Aorist RAo: ayīyajat etc. B -s-Ao: ayākṣīt etc. V.B.S. (ayās RV., ayāṭ V.B.S.; yákṣat V.B.S., yakṣatas -ṣatām RV.), ayaṣṭa etc. V.B.S. (yakṣate etc. V.B.; yakṣīya MS.) Precative: ijyāt Perfect iyāja etc. E.+, ījé etc. V.+, yejé AV. ? Causative yājayati etc. B.+,-te E Desiderative yiyakṣati -te E.; íyakṣati etc. V.,-te etc. V.B Intensive yāyaj- (in d.) Verbal Nouns PPP: iṣṭá V.+; Inf: yáṣṭum B.+,-ṭave V.B., ījitum M.; 1Abs: iṣṭvā́ AV.+; 2Abs: -ijya; yájadhyai V., yajádhyai TS.; -yā́jam AV Derivatives -ij V.+ yajás RV. yajñá V.+ -yājin B.+ yā̆j V.+ -yaji RV. yájyu V. yājya B.+ yája B. yájus V.+ yájīyas V. yājyā̀ B.+ yajā S. yajatá V. yájiṣṭha V. yājana S.+ yajin B.+ íṣṭi V.+ yájvan V.+ yājanīya C. -yájya RV. yajati S.+ yajvin E.+ -yā́juka B. -yajyā V.B.S. yaṣṭavyà B.+ yajiṣṇu E. yāyajū́ka B.+ ijya C. yaṣṭṛ V.+ -yāga E.+ yiyakṣu E.+ ijyā S.+ yájatra V.B. -yāja V.+ yājayitavyà B. yájana AV.+ yajátha V. yājaka E.+ yājayitṛ C. Appears to be related with roots √ yam and √ yach and √ yat, and to mean originally “reach out, extend”. Meanings yájati yájate v PPP iṣṭá 1 (q.v.) worship, esp. with sacrifices or oblations, consecrate, hallow, offer, sacrifice (P mostly on account of another, Ā on one's own account or by the help of another). Caus. yājayati te sacrifice (as priest) for (A) with (I), cause a person. (A) to sacrifice with (A or I) by means of a priest (I). Des yiyakṣati, te wish to sacrifice. anu worship afterwards with (I). apa drive away, Ā purchase by a sacrifice. api sacrifice (A of the god or the oblation). ava avert, drive away, or satisfy by a sacrifice. ā consecrate, hallow, worship, win by a sacrifice (for men from the gods, Ā also for one's self). pari get or procure by a sacrifice; worship or sacrifice before or after another. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_yat.html"> √ yat    √ yat, “stretch” Present I. yátate etc. V.+,-ti etc. V.+ Passive yatyate C Future Simple Future: yatiṣyate etc. B.+,-ti etc. E.+ Aorist √-Ao: yátāna, yatāná RV RAo: ayīyatat -iṣ-Ao: ayatiṣṭa B Perfect yete etc. V.B.U Causative yātáyati -te etc. V.+ (yātyate etc. B.+) Desiderative yiyatiṣa- Intensive yāyat- Verbal Nouns PPP: yatta V.+, yatita E.; Inf: yatitum E.; 2Abs: -yátya B Derivatives -yā̆t V.+ yátti MS. -yātaka E.+ yatúna RV. -yátana AV.+ -yattavya E. -yātya S.+ yayā́ti ? V.+ yatanīya C. yatitavya E.+ yātanā̆ E.+ yáti V.+ yatna E.+ Meanings yátati yátate v PPP yattá (q.v.) & yatita P join, connect, unite; P (Ā) associate one's self with, rival with (I); Ā join one's self with, meet (as friends or foes); Ā (P) try to join, strive after, endeavour at, be devoted to or intent upon (L, D, A prati, or Inf); Abs. exert one's self, take pains, be cautious or careful. Caus. yātáyati, te P put in order, arrange, join, connect (Ā refl.), remind (G) of (A); requite with reward or punishment (also Ā). adhi Ā fasten, stick or put on. ā arrive, enter, stay or abide in (L), strive after (D). anvā Caus. P connect, unite, cause to join or partake of (L or A). upa Ā befall. ni Ā get at (L). nis Caus. carry off, lead away; fetch out of, get, procure, give back, restore, requite. pratinis Caus. give back, restore. pari surround. pra make effort, take pains, strive after, endeavour at (L, D, A, or Inf). prati thwart, oppose; retaliate, requite. vi Caus. arrange; do penance; vex, harass. sam P join, connect; Ā intrans. join with (I), assemble, meet together, encounter. Cf. anvā́yatta (sic!), ā́yatta, samāyatta, sáyatta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_yabh.html"> √ yabh    √ yabh, “fuck” Present I. yábhati etc. AV.B Future Simple Future: yapsyáti etc. B.S Aorist -siṣ-Ao: ayāpsīt Perfect yayābha Desiderative yiyapsate etc. S Verbal Nouns Inf: yabdhum C., yabhitum C Derivatives -yabhya AV. yābha C. Meanings yábhati to have sexual intercourse. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_yam.html"> √ yam, yach    √ yam, yach, “reach” Present I. yáchati -te etc. V.+ yamati -te etc. E.+ II. yáṃsi RV.; yamiti ? JB Passive yamyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: yaṃsyáti B., yamiṣyati C Periphrastic Future: yaṃtā Aorist √-Ao: áyamus etc. RV. (yámati yámat etc. V., yamate. etc. V.; yamyās 3s. yamīmahi RV.; yaṃdhí etc. RV.); áyāmi V.B RAo: ayīyamat -s-Ao: áyāṃsam etc. V.B. (áyān RV.; yaṃsat etc. V.B.S., yaṃsatas RV.), áyaṃsta etc. V.B. (ayāṃsi AV., yaṃsate RV.) -iṣ-Ao: yámiṣṭa (3s.) RV -siṣ-Ao: ayaṃsiṣam Perfect yayāma yemús etc. V.B. (yayaṃtha RV.; yamátus -mus RV.), yeme etc. V.+ Causative yāmáyati etc. V.E.+; yamayati etc. B.+,-te E Desiderative yiyaṃsati B Intensive yaṃyamīti RV Verbal Nouns PPP: yatá V.+; Inf: yáṃtum B.+,-tave RV., yamitum C., yámitavaí RV.; 1Abs: yatvā S., yamitvā C.; 2Abs: -yátya AV.B.,-yamya S.+;-yámam V.B Derivatives yáma V.+ yáti V.+ yamúnā V.+ -yāmin B.+ yamá ? V.+ -yáṃtu RV. -yamīyas RV. -yāmana C. -yamaka C. yaṃtavyà B.+ yámiṣṭha RV. -yaṃsénya RV. yamin B.+ yaṃtúr RV. yamasāná RV. -yachana E. -yamya E.+ yaṃtṛ V.+ yā́ma V.+ yaṣṭí ? B.+ yámana B.+ yaṃtrá V.+ yāmaka B.+ Compare √ yaj and √ yat. Meanings yácchati yácchate v (yamati, yamate), PPP yatá (q.v.) hold, hold up, lift, raise, erect, sustain, support; hold back, restrain, check, stop; hold out, offer, grant, furnish, give (D or L of pers. & A of th., or A of pers. & I of th.); stretch, extend, show; Ā rest on (L), stretch or extend with (I); hold out, persevere, be obedient or faithful to (D). Caus. yamáyati (te) hold back, restrain, control, bring in order. adhi erect, raise towards (L), extend over (D). anu direct, turn, arrange, Ā conform one's self to, follow (A). antar restrain, check (inwardly). ā hold out, stretch, extend, lengthen, bend (a bow), put on or draw back (an arrow), throw (a lance), abs. take aim; stop, check, restrain, draw near, bring. abhyā draw, extend, protract; aim at (A). nirā stretch out. vyā tear asunder, stretch out, extend; Ā (P) struggle or contend about (L). Caus. (vyāyāmya) take exercise, samā draw together, contract, pull, stretch. uda lift up, raise (lit. & fig.); hold forth, offer, present; shake up, stir, agitate; check, restrain, stop; P Ā strive, prepare for, endeavour at (D or artham). prod raise, uplift. samud the same, check, curb, restrain. upa take hold of, seize; offer, present; take to wife, marry. ni hold, restrain, stop (Ā intrans.); fasten, lie to, bind up (the hair); take, assume; offer, present; govern, control, limit; fix, establish. Caus. restrain, curb; fasten, tie to (L), suppress, limit. vini & saṃni hold, restrain, suppress. pra stretch, hold out, offer, give; produce, cause; pronounce, utter; restore, pay back, return. pratipra offer in turn, give back, restore. saṃpra offer or present (together), grant, bestow, give in marriage; return, restore. vi hold asunder, stretch out, extend. sam hold together, draw tight (reins), restrain, curb, check, control, govern, bind together or up, attach, fasten, fetter; suppress, omit, annul, destroy. Caus. bind, fetter, bind up, arrange (hair); check, curb, subdue. Cf. abhyudyata (add.), ā́yata, udyata, níyata, práyata, prodyata, víyata, vyāyata, sáyata. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_yas.html"> √ yas, yeṣ    √ yas, yeṣ, “be heated” Present I. yéṣati etc. V.B. yasati III. yayastu RV IV. yásyati etc. AV.+ Future Simple Future: yasiṣyati Periphrastic Future: yasitā Aorist Th Ao: ayasat C RAo: ayīyasat -iṣ-Ao: ayāsīt Perfect yayāsa Causative yāsayati etc. E.+-te. (yāsyate E.) Desiderative yiyasiṣa- Intensive yāyas- Verbal Nouns PPP: yastá V.+, yasita B.C. yasitvā, yastvā Derivatives yās V.B.S. -yāsaka C. -yā́sya V.+ yaska ? B.+ -yāsa B.+ -yāsin C. -yāsana C. Meanings yásyati yayasti v PPP yastá be hot or eager, exert one's self. ā = S., Caus. āyāsayati strain, stretch, tire, vex, harass (w. ātmānam refl.*). pra commence to boil up or be agitated, be hot or eager. Cf. āyasta (add.), práyasta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_yah.html"> √ yah    √ yah Such a root, of questionable meaning, is assumable for the Derivatives yahú RV. yahvá V. yahvánt RV. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_yaa.html"> √ yā    √ yā, “go” Present II. yā́ti etc. V.+ (ayus B.+ ayān; yāmaki = yāmi KB.), yāmahe E1 Passive yāyate E Future Simple Future: yāsyati etc. AV.+,-te etc. E.+ Periphrastic Future: yātā E.+ Aorist -s-Ao: ayāsam etc. V. (yā́sat V.B.; yeṣam RV.) -siṣ-Ao: ayāsiṣam etc. V.+ (yāsiṣat RV.; yāsisīṣṭhās V.B.) Perfect yayaú etc. V.+ (yayā́tha V.), yaye C Causative yāpáyati etc. B.+ ayīyapat Desiderative yiyāsati etc. E.+ Intensive īyāyate ? U., yāyā- (in d.) Verbal Nouns PPP: yātá V.+; Inf: yātum E.+, yā́tve V.,-vaí B.; 1Abs: yātvā́ B.S.; 2Abs: -yā́ya B.+;-yaí V.B.;-yāyam S Derivatives -yā V.B. yātṛ V.+ yāyin B.+ yāyāvará B.+ yā́na V.+ -yātra E.+ yā́van V.B. yiyāsā C. yú ? V.B. yātrā E.+ yéṣṭha RV. yiyāsu E.+ -yāti U.+ -yātha RV. yayí ,-ī́ RV. -yāpa C. yātú ? V.+ yā́ma V.+ -yayin RV. yāpaka C. yātavya E.+ yā́man V.B.S. -yíyu RV. yāpya B.+ yayu V.B. yāpana S.+ Doubtless a secondary form of √ 1 i, ī, ay. Meanings yā́ti (yā́te) v PPP yātá 1 (– ṃ mostly w. P mg) go, travel, march, set out, depart, fly, escape, pass, vanish, perish; go off, speed, succeed; proceed, act, behave; go to (A, L, or D), reach, attain to a condition (A of an abstrans., cf. gam), go to a woman, have sexual intercourse with (A), approach with a request, ask for (2A); make out, learn, understand. With ākhyām be called (N + iti), w. khaṇḍaśas or dalaśas fall to pieces, w. śatadhā fall into a hundred pieces; kva tadyātam how is it with it ? yātu let it go, no matter. Caus. yāpáyati make or bid go (to *A), dismiss, send out, drive away, pass, spend. Des yiyāsati wish or be about to go etc. accha approach, arrive. ati pass by, overtake, omit. anu go to (A), go after, follow (esp. in death), obey, imitate, equal, reach, attain. apa go away, depart, retreat, flee, cease, desist. pratyapa retreat, fly back. vyapa go away, set out, flee. abhi approach, go to or against; take to, partake of (A). ava come down, descend from (ā́ w. Ab); go away, depart; avert, remove. ā approach, arrive, come from (Ab) to or into (A, r. L), get at, enter into, partake of (A); appear to (G), befall (A). atyā pass by (A). abhyā come near or to (A). upā, abhyupā, samupā the same. pratyā return, come back to (A), go to meet or against (A). samā come near (together), arrive; assemble, meet, come out of or from (Ab) to (A or L); pass away; get into a state or condition (A). ud rise, go forth or out, depart from (Ab). pratyud rise and go to meet or against (A). upa come near, arrive, visit, approach (A, also L of place); enter (A), meet, encounter, undergo (A); occur to, fall to one's share (A). abhyupa come to, get at, go against (A). pratyupa return, come back to or into (A prati or L). samupa come near (together), go or resort to (A). ni come down to or upon (A), run over (with a carriage), get into (A). nis go or come out of (Ab) to or into (A); pass away, vanish. Caus. cause to go away, expel from (Ab). abhinis & vinis go out, depart from (Ab). pari go round, circumambulate, surround, keep, guard; go through, pervade; pass by, avoid; flow off (Soma). pra go forth, set out, go towards (A accha or prati, & L) or against (A); walk, run, ride, drive, flow, etc; vanish, pass away, die; get into, partake of (A); proceed, act, behave. anupra set out after (A), follow. abhipra approach (A), set out, leave for (A), attack, assail. pratipra come near or back. saṃpra set out (together), walk or flow towards (A prati). prati come near or back to (A prati); go against (A); comply with, gratify (A). vi pass or cut through, go or turn away. sam go or come together, meet, encounter (as friends or foes), approach, arrive, get into a state or condition. anusam go to and fro, go to, visit. abhisam go to or against (A). pratisam go against, attack. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_yaac.html"> √ yāc    √ yāc, “ask” Present I. yā́cati -te etc. V.+ Passive yācyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: yāciṣyati B.S.-te E Periphrastic Future: yācitā Aorist √-Ao: yācyāt RAo: ayayācat -iṣ-Ao: ayācīt etc. V.E. (yāciṣat RV.), ayāciṣṭa B. (yāciṣāmahe RV.) Perfect yayāca yayāce B.+ Causative yācáyati -te AV.+ Desiderative yiyāciṣa- Intensive yāyāc- Verbal Nouns PPP: yācitá AV.+; Inf: yā́citum AV.+; 1Abs: yācitvā B.+; 2Abs: -yā́cya B.+ Derivatives yācaka E.+ yācana E.+ yācitavya E.+ yācñā́ B.+ yācin C. yācanā E.+ yācitṛ E.+ yācñyá AV.B. yācya E.+ yācanīya E.+ yāciṣṇu E.+ Meanings yā́cati yā́cate v PPP yācita ask, beg, request (A or Ab, r. G of pers; A prati of th., also artham or arthe & D of an abstrans.); woo, ask a girl (A) from (Ab, r. A); offer a thing (A) to (D). Caus. yācayati cause to ask or sue; ask a thing (A) for (arthe). anu ask, entreat. abhi ask, request (2A); ask (a girl) in marriage from (A). ā & upa ask, implore. nis beg off from (2A or A of th. & I of pers.). pra ask, beg (2A). saṃpra & sam the same. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_yaad.html"> √ yād    √ yād, “unite” (?) Present I. yā́damāna RV. Derivatives yā́das B.+ yā́dura RV. Meanings only yā́damāna closely connected with (I). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_yu.html"> √ 1 yu    √ 1 yu, “unite” Present II. yaúti yuvati etc. AV.B.S., yuté yuvate etc. V.B VI. yuváti -te etc. V.B IX. yunāti -nīte Passive yūyate Future Simple Future: yaviṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: yuvitā́ ŚB. yavitā Aorist √-Ao: yūyāt; ayāvi RAo: ayīyavat -iṣ-Ao: yā́viṣṭam ? RV. ayaviṣṭa Perfect yuyāva yuyuvé RV Causative yāvayati , yiyāvayiṣati Desiderative yúyūṣati RV. yiyaviṣa- Intensive yóyuvat AV., yóyuve etc. RV Verbal Nouns PPP: yutá V.+; 2Abs: -yū́ya V.+,-yutya S Derivatives yú B.+ yuti C. yūna S. yós ? V.+ -yava RV. -yūti ? V.+ yóni ? V.+ yóṣaṇā etc. ? V.+ yávana AV.+ yotra E. yúvan ? V.+ -yāva E.+ -yuvana S.+ yūthá ? V.+ yáviṣṭha V.+ -yāvana C. -yut V.B. yavīyas S.+ yāvayitṛ C. Compare √ yuj and √ 2 yu; from the latter, in combination with prefixes, the forms and derivatives fo this root are not always separable with certainty. Meanings yaúti yuté yuváti yuváté v PPP yutá 1 (q.v.) fasten, hold fast, bind, harness, join, unite, draw towards one's self, attract get possession of. Des yúyūṣati wish to attract or hold fast. ā draw onwards or towards, seize, occupy, get, procure, mix, mingle. paryā & samā mix, stir up. ni tie on, fasten; procure, bestow; take to one's self, appropriate. pra stir up, mix; disturb, destroy. sam take to one's self, consume; put together, join, connect; share with, bestow on (I). Cf. abhiyuta, āyuta, níyuta, sáṃyuta, samāyuta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_yu.html"> √ 2 yu, yuch    √ 2 yu, yuch, “separate” Present I. yúchati etc. V III. yuyóti etc. V.B., yuyudhvám etc. V.B VI. áyuvanta etc. V.B.S Aorist √-Ao: yuyāt B., yūyātām (3d.) B. (yūyās 3s. V.), yavanta RV.; áyāvi B RAo: yūyot RV -s-Ao: ayauṣīt etc. V.B. (yaus RV., yoṣati etc. V., yóṣat RV.; yoṣam etc. B.S., yūṣam AV.), yoṣṭhās B.S -iṣ-Ao: yā́vīs RV Causative yāváyati etc. V.; yavayati etc. V.B Intensive yóyuvat etc. V.B. (yoyāva MS.) Verbal Nouns yutá RV.; yótave -tavaí -tos RV.;-yāvam AV.B Derivatives yáva AV.C. -yuti RV.C. -yutvan RV. -yā́vana AV. -yávana MS. -yotṛ RV. -yā́van AV. yū́yuvi RV. -yut V.B. Compare √ 1 yu. Meanings yuyóti yúcchati yuyóti yúcchate v PPP yuta 3 trans. repel, keep or ward off, separate, protect from (Ab); intrans. keep apart, be or remain separate. Caus. yaváyati or yāváyati = S. trans. Int part. yóyuvat yield, give way. apa remove, avert from (Ab or D). nis keep off, repel. pra remove; keep away (intrans.), be indolent or heedless. vi part (trans. & intrans.); separate or be separated from, deprive or be deprived of (I); scatter, disperse, open. Cf. víyuta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_yuj.html"> √ yuj    √ yuj, “join” Present II. yujé V., yujmahe yujata (3p.) RV., yukṣvá V VI ? yuñjati -te etc. U.E.+ VII. yunákti yuṅkté etc. V.+ (yunaṅkṣi ? C., yuñjīyāt R.) Passive yujyáte etc. V.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: yokṣyati etc. B.+,-te etc. AV.+ Periphrastic Future: yoktā́ B Aorist √-Ao: áyuji etc. V.B. (yojate yujāná RV.), yojam yója yujyā́tām etc. RV.); áyoji V.C Th Ao: ? yujanta RV., ayujat -janta C RAo: ayūyujat etc. E.+ -s-Ao: ayokṣīt S., ayaukṣīt ayukṣi etc. V.+ (ayuṅkṣmahi C.) Perfect yuyója yuyujé etc. V.+ (yuyujma -jré V.; niniyoja AB.; yuyójate RV.) Causative yojayati etc. E.+,-te etc. E.+ (yojyate etc. C.) Desiderative yuyukṣati etc. E.+ Intensive yoyuj- Verbal Nouns PPP: yuktá V.+; Inf: yoktum B.+; 1Abs: yuktvā́ V.+,-tvā́ya V.B.; 2Abs: -yujya E.+; yujé RV Derivatives yúj V.+ yóga V.+ yójana V.+ yugma S.+ -yuja V.S. yógya AV.+ yojanīya C. yugmán B. yújya V.B. yogyā́ RV. yukti V.+ -yúgvan V.B.S. yugá V.+ yogin S.+ yoktavyà B.+ yuyukṣu C. yugya E.+ yojaka E.+ yoktṛ́ B.+ yojayitavya C. -yuṅga B. yojya E.+ yóktra V.+ yojayitṛ S.C. yuñjaka E.+ yojitṛ C. Meanings yunákti yuṅktá yujáte 1 v & yuñjati, yuñjate PPP yuktá (q.v.) yoke, harness (of waggon and steed); make ready, fit out, prepare, arrange, set to work (P. refl.); apply, use, fasten or fix on put or place (dhuri at the head lit. at the hill), turn or direct (esp. the mind) upon (L); (yogam) be intent on, meditate (also Ā); appoint, institute; bid, order, enjoin; unite, connect, join with (I); P. Ā cling to, adhere, marry; P present or furnish with (A of pers. & I of th., or L G of pers. & A of th.); Ā become possessed of (A); P. the same (I saha) or fall to one's (G) share or lot, be fit or suitable for (L, G or I), be proper or right. Caus. yojayati te yoke, harness, fit out, array; use, employ, undertake, begin; appoint to or charge with (L), fasten, fix (esp. the mind) or place on (L); unite, connect, furnish, endow with (I). Des yuyukṣati wish to lay on or to appoint anu strive to overtake, pursue; ask, question (A of pers. or & th.). abhi P appoint to, charge with (L); P (Ā) prepare or get ready for (A or Inf); Ā (P) yoke, harness, put to; attack, march against; P. be sued for or be accused of (A). Caus. furnish with, make a pers. (A) share in (I). pratyabhi attack or accuse in return. ā harness, put to (L); Ā fasten, put on, place in (L). Caus. fix upon (L), put together. samā arrange, prepare; join, bring together with (I). ud make one's self ready, set to work; set off, be gone. Caus. urge on, impel, also = samud Caus. incite or animate to (D). upa Ā (P) yoke, harness, put to (L); use, employ, appropriate, enjoy; consume, eat. P. be applied, be useful, necessary, requisite, or qualified for (L, D of th., G of pers.). ni Ā (P) fasten or put to (L, dhuri = S.); join, put together; bind or attach to, fix or turn upon (L or D); put (a task) upon, commission, elect (2A), appoint to, charge with (A of pers. & L or D of th; or L of pers. & A of th.); use, employ. Caus. harness, put to (L); tie on, fasten, set (jewels); direct, impel, exhort or constrain to (D, A w. prati, L, or artham), appoint to (L), choose for, elect (2A); commit or entrust to (L); set, lay, fix; place in or upon, take into or to (L); employ, set to work; furnish with, cause to partake of (I). vini Ā (P) loosen, untie, unharness, shoot of – at (L), appoint to, destine for (L, D or artham); place, fix (the mind) upon; use, employ; eat, consume. Caus. appoint to, charge with (L, arthāya or artham); commit to (L), present, offer to (D), use, employ. saṃni place in or on (L); commission, appoint, employ. Caus. the same, charge with (= vini Caus. ); urge on, impel; destine, assign. pra Ā (P) harness, put to (L), prepare (I) for (D), join with (I), set in motion, hurl, cast shut off-at (L or D), turn or fix upon (L), utter, pronounce, show, manifest; animate, impel, bid, direct to (D or L), elect, choose for (2A), bring to or into (A), place at or upon (L), add; use, employ; effect, produce; arrange, execute, perform (d.). P. be fit or suitable. c. hurl, cast; bring forth, utter, show, betray; fix, concentrate (the mind); direct, instruct, appoint to (L), commit to (D), begin, undertake; represent, perform; use, employ; exact (interest). anupra Ā add after (Ab); pursue, overtake; follow. vipra sever from (I); Caus. deprive or rid of (I). saṃpra yoke, harness, set in motion, let loose; execute. perform (music). P. be joined or added; partake or be guilty of (I). Caus. fit out make ready; join or connect with (I); bring forth, use, employ. vi detach or sever from (I); PĀ liberate from or deprive of (I, r. Ab); ĀP. relax, yield, give way. Caus. separate, rid or deprive of (Ab or I). sam P put together, join, unite, bind, fetter; endow or furnish with (I), fix (the mind) upon (L). Caus. yoke, harness; fit out. equip (an army), lay on, shoot off (an arrow), turn or fix (the mind) on (L) appoint (to a commission), intrust or commit to (G); perform, accomplish; add to (L), put together, join, etc. = S. Cf. abhiyukta, āyukta, udyukta, upayukta, niyukta, niryukta (add.), prayukta, viprayukta, viyukta, visaṃyukta, saṃyukta, saṃprayukta, samāyukta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_yudh.html"> √ yudh    √ yudh, “fight” Present I. yodhati etc. AV.PB II. yótsi RV IV. yúdhyate etc. V.+,-ti etc. V.+ Passive yudhyate C Future Simple Future: yotsyati -te etc. B.+ Periphrastic Future: yoddhā E Aorist √-Ao: yódhi, yodhat, yodhāná RV., yudhāna ? C RAo: yūyudhas M -s-Ao: yotsīs E., ayuddha C., yutsmahi AV -iṣ-Ao: ayodhīt etc. V. (yodhiṣat RV.) Perfect yuyódha yuyudhé etc. V.+ Causative yodhayati etc. V.+,-te etc. E. (yodhyate E.) Desiderative yúyutsati -te etc. V.+ Intensive yoyudh- yavīyudh- (in d.) Verbal Nouns PPP: yuddhá V.+; Inf: yoddhum E.;-yuddhvī RV.;-yudhya E.; yudham JB., yudhé RV.; yudháye RV Derivatives yúdh V.+ yudhmá RV. yodhana E.+ yúyudhi RV. -yudha V.+ yúdhvan RV. yodhanīya C. yū́yudhi RV. yudhi- AV. yodhá V.+ yodhuka JB. yavīyúdh RV. -yudhya RV. yodhaka E. yódhīyas RV. yuyutsā E. yudhénya V. yodhin E.+ yoddhavya E.+ -yutsā ? C. yódhya V.+ yoddhṛ V.+ yuyutsu E.+ Meanings yúdhyate yúdhyati yodhati v PPP yuddhá 1 (q.v.) fight, combat, contend with (I saha or samam) for or about (L); fight (trans. w. A), vanquish. Caus. yodháyati, yúdhyate, yúdhyati, yodhati, PPP yuddhá 1 (q.v.) fight, combat, contend with (I saha or samam) for or about (L); fight (trans. w. A), vanquish. Caus. yodháyate cause to fight, fight (trans.), defend. Des yúyutsati, te wish to fight with (I or A). abhi fight (A or I), vanquish, win by fighting. ā fight (trans.). ud rise against (D). ni fight with (saha or sākam). pra (begin to) fight, attack (A). Caus. cause to open the fight. maṃpra (begin to) fight. prati fight against, vanquish, be a match for (A). Caus. the same. sam fight together, fight with (A or I sārdham). Cf. prayuddha, pratiyuddha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_yup.html"> √ yup    √ yup, “obstruct” Present IV. yupyati Future Simple Future: yopiṣyati Periphrastic Future: yopitā Aorist Th Ao: ayupat RAo: ayūyupan etc. B Perfect yuyópa yuyopimá V Causative yopáyati etc. V.B.S Intensive yoyupyáte etc. B.S Verbal Nouns PPP: yupitá AV.B.S Derivatives yū́pa V.+ -yópana V.+ yoyupana C1. Meanings only pf. yuyópa & PPP yupitá obstruct, thwart, hurt. Caus. yopáyati efface, destroy. Int yoyupyáte make smooth or straight (hair). sam Caus. efface, smooth. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ye_s.html"> √ yeṣ    √ yeṣ see √ yas. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ra_mh.html"> √ raṃh    √ raṃh, “hasten” Present I. ráṃhate etc. RV.,-ti RV Future Simple Future: raṃhiṣyati Periphrastic Future: raṃhitā Aorist RAo: araraṃhat -iṣ-Ao: araṃhīt Perfect rārahāṇá RV.B. raraṃha Causative raṃháyati -te etc. RV Verbal Nouns PPP: raṃhita S Derivatives -raṃha E. raṅghas C. ṛhánt ? RV. rághīyas B. ráṃhya RV. rahas ? C. raghú V.+ lághīyas AV.+ ráṃhas V.+ ráṃhi V.B. laghú AV.+ laghiṣṭha JB. Compare √ rah. Meanings ráhate ráhati v PPP raṃhita Ā run, hasten, P make run or hasten. Caus. raṃháyati, ráhate, ráhati, PPP raṃhita Ā run, hasten, P make run or hasten. Caus. raṃháyate = S. Cf. rārahāṇá. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_rak_s.html"> √ rakṣ    √ rakṣ, “protect” Present I. rákṣati -te etc. V.+ Passive rakṣyate etc. U.+ Future Simple Future: arakṣiṣyas M., rakṣye ? R1 Periphrastic Future: rakṣitā E.C Aorist √-Ao: rakṣyāt RAo: ararakṣat -s-Ao: arakṣīt etc. AV.+ (rakṣiṣat etc. RV.), arākṣīt etc. B.S. (arāṭ ? MS.) Perfect rarákṣa etc. V.+ (rārakṣāṇá RV.) Causative rakṣayati etc. C.,-te B Desiderative rirakṣiṣati etc. E Intensive rārakṣ- Verbal Nouns PPP: rakṣitá V.+; Inf: rakṣitum E.+; 2Abs: -rakṣya C Derivatives rakṣa B.+ rakṣya E.+ rákṣas V.+ rirakṣā C. rakṣā E.+ rákṣaṇa V.+ rakṣás V.B. rirakṣu C. rakṣaka C. rakṣaṇā C. -rákṣi V.B. rirakṣiṣā C. rakṣin S.+ rakṣaṇīya E.+ rakṣitavya E.+ rirakṣiṣu E.+ rakṣitṛ́ V.+ The relation of rakṣas “demon” to this root is questionable. But rakṣīs AV1. is too weak evidence on which to accept a √ 2 rakṣ “harm”. Meanings rákṣati rákṣate v PPP rakṣitá protect, guard, keep, save from (Ab), take care of (A); beware of, prevent (A). Caus. rakṣayati protect from (Ab), save. Des rirakṣati wish to protect from (Ab). anu guard or protect (by following). abhi & samabhi keep, protect. ā protect, guard from (Ab). pari keep, guard, watch, protect, save from (Ab), take care of, maintain, observe. pra preserve, rescue or deliver from (Ab). prati keep, observe. vi the same. sam guard, watch, keep, maintain, take care of, defend, save. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ra_gg.html"> √ raṅg    √ raṅg, “rock” Present I. raṅgant C1. Doubtless artificial. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_rac.html"> √ rac    √ rac, “procuce” Future Simple Future: raciṣyati C. ? Aorist √-Ao: araci C RAo: arīracat C Causative racayati etc. E.+ (racyate C.) Derivatives racana E.+ -rañca C. -rañci C. racayitṛ C. -racanā C. -rañcya C. Meanings raṅgati v move hither and thither, rock. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_raj.html"> √ 1 raj    √ 1 raj, “direct” see √ ṛj. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_raj.html"> √ 2 raj, rañj    √ 2 raj, rañj, “color” Present I. rañjati etc. ? E.+ rajati -te IV. rajyati -te etc. AV1.E.+ Passive rajyate C Future Simple Future: raṅkṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: raṅktā Aorist RAo: arīrajat ararañjat -iṣ-Ao: arāṅkṣīt araṅkta, raṅkṣīṣta Precative: rajyāt Perfect rarañja rarañje Causative rajayati AV.; rañjayati etc. E.+,-te E Desiderative riraṅkṣa- Intensive rā́rajīti V Verbal Nouns PPP: raktá B.+; 1Abs: raktvā, raṅktvā; 2Abs: -rajya C Derivatives raṅga E.+ rañjana E.+ rajanīya E. rakti C. rañjaka E.+ rañjanīya C. rájas ? V.+ rāga U.+ -rañjya C. rajana AV.+ rají ? RV. -rāgin E.+ rajaka E.+ rajanī̆ E. rajatá V.+ rajayitṛ́ VS. The forms with nasal belong to the later language. Meanings rañj , rajyati, rajyata, PPP raktá v (q.v.) be coloured or red, be exited or agitated, be affected with a strong feeling, esp. be delighted with, fond of, be in love with or have pleasure in (L). Caus. rañjayati (rajayati), PPP rañjita colour, redden; brighten, illumine; rejoice, delight, please, satisfy. anu be coloured or reddened after, take the tinge of, be delighted with, feel affection towards (A or L). Caus. colour after or according to (I); brighten, exalt, gratify, win, conciliate. apa lose colour; Caus. estrange, alienate (A). abhi be charmed or delighted with (I). upa eclipse, cast a shade upon (L). vi lose colour, become cold or indifferent towards (Ab or L). sam be coloured or reddened. Caus. colour, redden, rejoice, gratify. Cf. anurakta, aparaktra, uparakta, virakta, saṃrakta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ra_jch.html"> √ rañch    √ rañch, “mark” Only in (ni-) -rañchana C.: Compare √ lāñch. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ra_t.html"> √ raṭ    √ raṭ, “howl” Present I. raṭati etc. C Future Simple Future: raṭiṣyati Periphrastic Future: raṭitā Aorist RAo: arīraṭat -iṣ-Ao: arāṭīt Perfect rarāṭa reṭus Intensive rāraṭīti etc. E.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: raṭita C Derivatives raṭana C. -raṭi C. Meanings raṭati v PPP raṭita (q.v.) howl, yell, cry, roar. Int rāraṭīti scream aloud, croak. ā = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ra_nv.html"> √ raṇv    √ raṇv, “delight” Present I. raṇva etc. TS Verbal Nouns raṇvitá RV A secondary formation from √ ran, apparently through raṇvá. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_rad.html"> √ rad    √ rad, “dig” Present I. rádati etc. V.B.,-te AV II. ratsi RV Future Simple Future: radiṣyati Periphrastic Future: raditā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: arā̆dīt Perfect rarā́da RV. redus Verbal Nouns PPP: raditá AV.B Derivatives rada RV.C. radana C. Meanings rádati rádate v PPP raditá scratch, gnaw, rend, dig open (a way), guide, lead into a course (a river), convey or bring to (D). pra scratch, dig. vi separate, open. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_radh.html"> √ radh, randh    √ radh, randh, “be or make subject” Present II. randdhi RV1 IV. rádhyati etc. AV.B Future Simple Future: radhiṣyati, ratsyati Periphrastic Future: radhitā, raddhā Aorist Th Ao: radham etc. V RAo: rīradhas etc. RV. (rīradhā 1s. RV.) ararandhat -iṣ-Ao: randhīs RV Perfect rarandha rarandhima redhma rāradhús RV1 Causative randháyati etc. V.+ Desiderative riradhiṣa- , riratsa- Intensive rāranddhi ? RV. rāradh- Verbal Nouns PPP: raddhá RV.; Inf: radhitum Derivatives randhana RV.C. ránddhi RV. rándhra ? RV.+ radhrá RV. Meanings randh rádhyati v PPP raddhá be or make subject to (D); harass, pain. Caus. randháyati (te) = S. trans. Int (rārandhí) subdue. ni give into the power of (D). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_ran.html"> √ 1 ran    √ 1 ran, “take pleasure” Present I. ráṇati etc. RV.,-anta RV IV. ráṇyati etc. RV. (raṇyáthas RV1.) Future Simple Future: raṇiṣyati Periphrastic Future: raṇitā Aorist RAo: arīraṇat, ararāṇat -iṣ-Ao: arāṇiṣus RV. (ráṇiṣṭana RV.) Perfect rāraṇa RV. (rāráṇas etc. rārán rārandhí etc. arāraṇus RV.B.) Causative raṇáyati etc. V.,-anta RV. rāṇayati Desiderative riraṇiṣa- Intensive raṃraṇ- Derivatives rán RV. ráṇya V. ránti ? V. ráṇitṛ RV. ráṇa V.+ raṇyà AV. rántya V. raṇvá V. ráṇvan RV. Compare √ ram. Meanings ráṇati ráṇate & raṇyati 1 v be pleased, rejoice, take pleasure in (L, r. A). Caus. raṇáyati, te delight a pers. with (I) or in (L), or = S. (w. L). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_ran.html"> √ 2 ran    √ 2 ran, “ring” Present I. raṇati etc. C Causative raṇayati C Verbal Nouns raṇita C Derivatives -raṇana C. A late and probably artificial formation. Meanings raṇati v PPP raṇita 2 (q.v.) ring, sound, tinkle. Caus. raṇayati make ring etc. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_rap.html"> √ rap    √ rap, “chatter” Present I. rápati etc. V.B Intensive rā́rapīti etc. V Derivatives -rāp RV. -rāpin AV. A variant of √ lap, which compare. Meanings rápati v chatter, whisper; Int rārapīti = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_rapz.html"> √ rapś    √ rapś, “be full” Present I. rapśate etc. V., rapśant- RV Perfect rarapśe RV Derivatives -rapśa RV. -rapśin V.B. Meanings rapśate v (S. only in seq.) be full. pra reach beyond (Ab). vi be overfull, have plenty of (G or I). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_raph.html"> √ raph    √ raph Perhaps to be seen in raphitá RV1 “miserable” (?): compare √ riph. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_rabh.html"> √ rabh, rambh    √ rabh, rambh, “take hold” Present I. rábhate etc. V.+,-ti etc. S.+; rambhati -te E.+ Passive rabhyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: rapsyate etc. E.+,-ti E Periphrastic Future: rabdhā Aorist √-Ao: arambhi C RAo: ararambhat -s-Ao: árabdha RV Perfect rebhé etc. V.+ (rārabhe RV.), rarabhmá RV Causative rambhayati etc. B.+,-te B Desiderative ripsate etc. B.C Intensive rārabh- , rārambh- Verbal Nouns PPP: rabdhá V.+; Inf: rabdhum E.; 2Abs: -rábhya V.+;-rábham RV.,-rábhe V.B Derivatives rabha E. rábhi V.+ rábhiṣṭha V.B. rambhín V.+ -rábhya B.+ -rabhin V.S. rábhīyas B.S. -rámbhana V.+ rábhas V.+ -rabdhi C. rábhyas RV. -rambhanīya B.S. rabhasāná RV. -rabdhavya E. rambhá V.+ -ripsu C. rabdhṛ C. rambhaka C. Compare √ labh, which is the same in another phonetic form. Meanings rambh , rábhate, rábhati (rambhti, te), PPP rabdha v (– ṃ w. P & pass. mg) take hold, seize, embrace. Caus. rambhayami & Des ripsate (only – ṃ). anu grasp, seize. ā take hold upon, touch, seize, lean or stay upon (A), reach to, attain; undertake, begin to (A or Inf). anvā take hold of from behind, hold on to (A). samanvā take hold of each other or together. abhyā grasp, touch, get at, undertake, begin. prā & samā the same. pari & saṃpari embrace (together). sam take hold of (each other), seize upon, partake of, enjoy (I); Ā P. be excited or agitated. abhisam grasp, hold fast. Cf. ā́rabdha (sic!), ārabhya, prārabdha, sárabdha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ram.html"> √ ram    √ ram, “be or make content” Present I. rámate -ti etc. V.+ IX. ramṇāti etc. V.B Passive ramyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: raṃsyate etc. B.+,-ti B Periphrastic Future: raṃtā Aorist √-Ao: rántī ? SV RAo: árīramat etc. RV -s-Ao: araṃsīt C., áraṃsta etc. V. raṃsīṣṭhās -siṣ-Ao: raṃsiṣam SV Perfect rarāma reṃus etc. B.+, reme etc. B.+ Causative ramayati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+; rāmayati etc. V.+ (riramayiṣa- in d.) Desiderative riraṃsa- (in d.) Intensive raṃram- Verbal Nouns PPP: ratá B.+; Inf: raṃtum E.+,-tos B., ramitum E.; 1Abs: ratvā́ B., raṃtvā C.; 2Abs: -ramya S.+-ratya; -ramam S Derivatives rama E.+ ráti B.+ raṃtavya C. rāmaṇa E. ramyà B.+ ráṃti AV.+ ráṃtṛ RV. raṃsu- ? RV. ramaṇa B.+ ramáti AV.B. rā́trī ? V.+ riraṃsā E.+ ramaṇīya U.+ rámati AV.B. rā́ma V.+ riraṃsu C. -rāmin RV. riramayiṣu C. Compare √ 1 ran, from which one or two of the derivatives here given may perhaps come, at least in part. Compare also √ lam. Meanings rámate rámati ramṇāti v PPP rate (q.v.) trans. stop, fix, settle; gladden, delight, enjoy (esp. carnally); intrans. stop, rest, stay gladly with (L or D); delight in, be pleased with or to (L, I, or Inf); be happy or content; dally or have sexual intercourse with (I samam, saha, sākam, or sārdham). Caus. ramáyati or rāmáyati = S. trans. anu P stop (intrans.), stay; Ā find pleasure or delight. abhi Ā stop, stay; delight in, be satisfied or pleased with (L or I saha). upāva Ā feel comfortable. ā P stop, cease; take delight in (L), enjoy carnally (I samam). upā P (Ā) rest, repose, desist from (Ab). vyupā & samā the same. upa P stop (trans.); PĀ stop (intrans.), rest, stay repose; cease from, renounce, resign (Ab). vyupa P Ā come to rest, cease, desist from (Ab). ni Ā go to rest, cease, end. Caus. nirāmayati stop, check, restrain. pari P take pleasure in, rejoice at (Ab). vi P (Ā) stop, cease, pause, rest; desist from (Ab), renounce, resign (Ab or absol.). Caus. viramayati or virāmayati bring to rest or to an end. Cf. anurata, uparata (add.), nirata (to be placed after nirañjana), virata. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ramb.html"> √ ramb    √ ramb, “hang down” Present I. rámbate etc. RV. Derivatives -rambaṇa B.U. Compare √ lamb, from which the verb-forms and derivatives mostly come. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_rambh.html"> √ rambh    √ rambh, “roar” Present I. rambhati -te etc. C. The isolated occurrences probably artificial. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_raz.html"> √ raś    √ raś Such a root inferable from the derivatives: raśanā́ V.+ raśmán RV. raśmí V.+ rāśí V.+ Meanings rasati rasate v PPP rasita 1 (q.v.) roar, howl, cry, sound. abhi neigh to (A). ā & vi roar, scream. Cf. anurasita, ārasita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ras.html"> √ ras    √ ras, “roar” Present I. rasati -te etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: rasiṣyati Periphrastic Future: rasitā Aorist RAo: arīrasat -iṣ-Ao: arā̆sīt Perfect rarāsa resus etc. E.+ Causative rāsaya- Desiderative rirasiṣa- Intensive rāras- Verbal Nouns rasita C Derivatives rasana C. rasitṛ C. Compare √ 1 rās. The root √ 2 ras “taste” is only a denominative of rasa. Meanings rasati rasate v PPP rasita 1 (q.v.) roar, howl, cry, sound. abhi neigh to (A). ā & vi roar, scream. Cf. anurasita, ārasita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_rah.html"> √ rah    √ rah, “desert” Present I. rahati Future Simple Future: rahiṣyati Periphrastic Future: rahitā Aorist RAo: arīrahat -iṣ-Ao: arahīt Perfect rarāha rehus Causative rahayati etc. S.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: rahita E.+; Inf: rahitum E Derivatives raha RV.+ rahaṇa C. rahas E.+ ráhū- ? RV. -rahin C. rahasya , -yu B.+ Meanings rahati v PPP rahita (q.v.) leave, desert, abandon. Caus. rahayati = S. or cause to leave etc. vi Caus. abandon, desert. Cf. virahita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_raa.html"> √ 1 rā, rās    √ 1 rā, rās, “give” Present I. rā́sate etc. V.B.S II. rā́si RV., rāti C., rāté B., rā́sva V.B.S III. rirīhi RV., rarāsva AV., raridhvam etc. (rárate 3s., rárāṇa) V Future Simple Future: rāsyati Periphrastic Future: rātā C Aorist -s-Ao: árāsma etc. V.B. (rā́sat etc. V.B.); rāsāthām rāsīya RV Perfect rarimá -ivā́ṃs RV., raré etc. RV Verbal Nouns PPP: rātá V.+; rātave C Derivatives -rā C. rayí ? V.+ rākā́ ? V.+ rárāvan RV. raí or rā́ ? V.+ rayiṣṭha B. rāti V.+ -ráru V.B. -rāya V. rátna ? V.+ rā́van V.B. The present-stem rāsa is plainly an extension of the aorist-stem rās. Meanings rā́ti rāté v PPP rātá 1 (q.v.) give, grant, bestow. sam = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_raa.html"> √ 2 rā    √ 2 rā, “bark” Present IV. rā́yati etc. V.B Future Simple Future: rāsyati Periphrastic Future: rātā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: arāsīt Perfect rarau Derivatives -rā́van ? V.S. Meanings rā́yati v bark, bark at. abhi bark at. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_raaj.html"> √ rāj    √ rāj, “be kingly” Present I. rā́jati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ II. rā́ṣṭi rā́ṭ RV Future Simple Future: rājiṣyati Periphrastic Future: rājitā Aorist √-Ao: rājyāsam S RAo: ararājat -iṣ-Ao: arājiṣus RV. arājiṣṭa Perfect rarāja rejus etc. E.+, rarājatus M., reje etc. E.+ rarāje Causative rājayati etc. B.+,-te etc. AV.E Desiderative rirājiṣa- Intensive rārāj- Verbal Nouns rājáse RV Derivatives rā́j V.+ rā́jan V.+ rājaná B.+ rā́ṣṭrī V.B.S. -rāja V.+ rāján RV. -rājin RV.B. rāṣṭrá V.+ Is most probably an old denominative of rā́j “ruler”, from √ ṛj, raj, which see. The anomalous stem irajyá- (see ib.) is related with it. Meanings rā́jati rā́jate rā́ṣṭi 1 v reign, rule, direct, be master of (G); shine, glitter, be illustrious or eminent, distinguish one's self, appear as (iva). Caus. rājayati, te rule, govern. anu imitate. nis Caus. cause to shine or glitter. pari shine all around. vi = S. +excel, surpass (Ab). ativi shine very bright. anuvi follow (A). sam reign, rule (G). Cf. irajy. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_raadh.html"> √ rādh    √ rādh, “succeed” Present V. rādhnoti etc. B.+ IV. rā́dhyate etc. AV.+,-ti etc. S.+ Passive rādhyate C Future Simple Future: rātsyati etc. AV.B.S Periphrastic Future: rāddhā Aorist √-Ao: arādham B. (rādhati -dhat etc. RV.,-dhās ŚB.); rādhyāsam -sma AV.B.S.; árādhi V.B.U RAo: arīradhat etc. B.C -s-Ao: arātsīt etc. AV.B.S -iṣ-Ao: rādhiṣi etc. AV.B.U Perfect rarā́dha etc. V.B Causative rādhayati etc. AV.+ (rādhyate E.; riradhayiṣati B.) Desiderative rirātsa- . ritsa- Intensive rārādh- Verbal Nouns PPP: rāddhá AV.+; 1Abs: rāddhvā́ B.; 2Abs: -rādhya B Derivatives rā́dha V.+ rā́dhana AV.+ -rādhi AV. -rādhayitṛ C. -rādhin E. -rādhanīya C. rā́ddhi AV.B.S. -rādhayiṣṇu E. rā́dhya V.+ rā́dhas V.+ -rāddhṛ C. The form iradhanta RV1., with the Inf. irádhyai (for iradhádhyai) RV1, appears to belong to this root. Meanings rāghnoti rā́dhyate rā́dhyati v PPP rāddhá (q.v.) succeed, prosper (of pers. & th.); be happy, have luck with (I); partake of, get at or to (D or L); *prophesy to (rādhyati w. D); accomplish, bring about; win over, gratify, conciliate. Caus. rādháyati bring about, satisfy. apa miss (the mark), fail; be at fault, offend, sin against (L of th. or G of pers.). abhi Caus. satisfy, content. ava fail, make a fault. ā Caus. make happy, satisfy, conciliate, try to win, honour, serve (A); gain, partake of (A). upā serve (A). samā Caus. = ā Caus. prati counteract, oppose (A). vi be deprived of (I); hurt, injure, offend. sam Caus. agree about or upon (L); satisfy, content. Cf. áparāddha, abhirāddha, iradh. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_raas.html"> √ 1 rās    √ 1 rās, “roar” Present I. rāsati -te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: rāsiṣyate Periphrastic Future: rāsitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: arāsiṣṭa Perfect rarāse C Intensive rārāsyate E Derivatives rāsa ? C. rā́sabha ? B.+ Compare √ ras and √ 2 rā. Meanings rāsati rāsate v roar, howl. Int rārāsyate cry aloud, lament. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_raas.html"> √ 2 rās    √ 2 rās see √ 1 rā. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ri.html"> √ ri, rī    √ ri, rī, “flow” Present IV. rī́yate V.B V. ariṇvan MS VI. riyati IX. riṇā́ti riṇīte etc. V.B.S Passive reri- Future Simple Future: reṣyati Periphrastic Future: retā Aorist RAo: arīrayat -iṣ-Ao: araiṣīt Perfect rirāya Causative repaya- arīripat Desiderative rāyaya- Intensive rirīṣa- Derivatives -raya E. rít RV. rītí V.+ rétas V.+ reṇú V.+ Compare √ lī. Meanings rī , riṇā́ti, riṇīte, rīyate, PPP rīṇa v P let loose, sever from (Ab); cause to run or stream, emit, grant, bestow; Ā flow, run, dissolve. anu Ā flow after (A). ā P cause to run; Ā run. ni loosen, unveil, tear asunder, destroy. nis sever from (Ab). vi hew asunder, cleave. sam put together, restore. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_rikh.html"> √ rikh    √ rikh, “scratch” Present VI. rikha RV1 Derivatives rekhā E. The usual form of this root is √ likh, which see. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ri_jkh.html"> √ riñkh, riñg    √ riñkh, riñg, “creep” Present I. riṅkhati etc. C.; riṅgati -te etc. C Perfect etc. ririṅkha , ririṅga etc.etc Causative riṅgayati C Derivatives riṅkhaṇa C. riṅgin C. riṅgi C. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ric.html"> √ ric    √ ric, “leave” Present IV ? rícyate etc. TS.,-ti E VII. riṇákti etc. V.B. riṅkte Passive ricyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: rekṣyate B Periphrastic Future: rektā Aorist √-Ao: riktam ? RV.; areci V.B.S Th Ao: aricat C RAo: arīricat etc. B.S -s-Ao: ā́raik RV., arikṣi etc. V.B Perfect riréca riricé etc. V.B. (riricyāt etc. V., ririkvā́ṃs RV., arirecīt RV.) Causative recayati etc. B.+ Desiderative ririkṣa- Intensive reric- Verbal Nouns PPP: riktá V.+ ríkta Derivatives -teka V.+ -recya C. -riñca E.+ -rikti JB. -rekin C. récana V.+ -riñcya C. rikthá V.+ reca B.+ -recanīya C. -riñci E.+ rékṇas RV. recaka E.+ réku RV. -ríkvan RV. The accent rícyate is quotable only from TS., and ricyáte only from ŚB. Meanings riṇákti v PPP riktá (q.v.) leave, clear (a room), let go, let free; deliver up, part with, sell; leave behind, supplant. P.Ā ricyáte, rícyate be emptied, be deprived of or freed from (I), be destroyed, perish. Caus. recayati make empty, give up, abandon; emit breath (mārutam). ati ĀP. leave behind, reach beyond, surpass, predominate over (A or Ab). Caus. cause to preponderate, overdo. abhyati ĀP. be left in favour or for the sake of (A). vyati P. reach beyond, surpass, excel, differ from (A or Ab). ā cede, yield (D of pers. & A of th.). ud & pra ĀP. reach beyond, exceed, preponderate over (Ab). vi ĀP. the same, be emptied or purged. Caus. empty, purge. Cf. átirikta, údrikta, virikta, vyatirikta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_rip.html"> √ rip    √ rip, “smear” Present riripús RV Verbal Nouns riptá RV Derivatives ríp V. répas V. ripú V.+ riprá V. Compare the other form of the root, √ lip, to which most of the formation belongs. Meanings only PPP riptá 1 smear, stick, cleave to; cheat, impose upon (only riripús). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_riph.html"> √ riph    √ riph, “snarl” Present I. rephant B VI. riphant -atī́ AV.B.S Passive riphyate S Perfect etc. rirepha etc.etc Verbal Nouns PPP: riphitá B.+ Derivatives repha S.+ Meanings ripháti rephati v PPP riphita snarl. ava the same. ā snore. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ribh.html"> √ ribh    √ ribh, “sing” Present I. rébhati etc. V.B.C1. ? Passive ribhyate RV Future Simple Future: rebhiṣyati Periphrastic Future: rebhitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: arebhīt Perfect rirébha RV Derivatives rebhá V.+ rebhin C. Meanings rébhati v crackle, creak, murmur, chatter, talk, sing, shout, praise. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_riz.html"> √ riś    √ riś, “tear” Present VI. riśánt riśáte etc. RV Verbal Nouns riṣṭá V.U Derivatives riśā́ AV. See the other form, √ liś, from which the forms mostly come. Meanings riśáti v PPP riṣṭá (q.v.) tear, pull, bite off, crop. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ri_s.html"> √ riṣ    √ riṣ, “be hurt” Present I. reṣat réṣāt V IV. ríṣyati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: reṣiṣati Periphrastic Future: reṣitā, reṣṭā Aorist √-Ao: rīḍhvam TA Th Ao: ariṣan etc. V.B.S. (riṣātha etc. RV., ríṣant rī́ṣant ? RV.) RAo: rīriṣat etc. V.+ (rīriṣīṣṭa RV.C., ririṣīṣṭa ririṣes RV.) -iṣ-Ao: areṣīt Perfect rireṣa Causative reṣáyati etc. V.+ (riṣayádhyai RV.) Desiderative rírikṣati etc. RV. ririṣiṣa-, rireṣiṣa- Intensive reriṣ- Verbal Nouns PPP: riṣṭá V.+; riṣé riṣés RV Derivatives ríṣ V. reṣa B.C. reṣaṇá V. reṣmán AV.B. réṣ ? B. -reṣin S. ríṣṭi V.B.S. ririkṣu RV. -riṣa AV. riṣaṇa- RV. riṣīka ? C. Meanings ríṣyati ríṣyate réṣati v PPP riṣṭá 1 (cf. riś) be hurt, receive harm, suffer wrong, fail, perish; harm, injure. Caus. reṣáyati = S. trans., Ā = S. refl. or intrans. Des rírikṣati wish to harm. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_rih.html"> √ rih    √ rih, “lick” Present II. réḍhi rihánti etc. V.B., rihaté RV., rihāṇá V., ríhāṇa VS., rehāṇā S Perfect ririhvā́ṃs RV Intensive rérihat -hāṇa etc. V.B., rerihyáte etc. V.B Verbal Nouns rīḍha RV Derivatives -réhaṇa AV. rerihá AV. The other verb-forms and derivatives made from √ lih, which see. Meanings réḍhi v PPP rīḍha lick, caress, kiss. Int rerihyáte, PPP rerihat & rérihāṇa lick repeatedly, kiss. ā lick, gnaw at (A). pari & prati the same. sam lick together. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_rii.html"> √ rī    √ rī see √ ri. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_ru.html"> √ 1 ru    √ 1 ru, “cry” Present I. ravati -te etc. JB.+ II. rauti ravīti ruvanti etc. B.+ (rūyāt S., ravāṇa ? S.) VI. ruváti etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: raviṣyati Periphrastic Future: ravitā rotā Aorist √-Ao: rūyāt RAo: arūruvat C. arīravat -iṣ-Ao: árāvīt etc. RV Perfect rurāva E., ruruvire B Causative rāvayati etc. S.+ Desiderative rurūṣa- Intensive róravīti etc. V.+, róruvāṇa B.; rorūyate etc. E.+,-ti E Verbal Nouns PPP: rutá AV.+; Inf: rotum C Derivatives ráva V.+ -rávas V.+ ruvátha B. rāva E.+ ravaṇa C. ravitṛ B. rúma ? RV. rāvin E.+ ruvaṇa- RV. ravátha V.B.S. rāvaṇa E.+ rā́van B. Meanings rauti ruváti ravati ravate v PPP rutá 1 (q.v.) roar, howl, shriek, croak, sound, thunder. Caus. rāvayati cause to roar or cry, fill with cries. Int. roravīti, rorūyate, ti roar or cry out loudly. abhi & ā roar etc. (at or against). pra roar or cry aloud. vi roar, yelp, shout, creak, rattle, tinkle; cry or call at. Caus. cry aloud, make resound. Cf. abhiruta, viruta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_ru.html"> √ 2 ru    √ 2 ru, “break” Present I. rávat B II. rudhí AV. ? Aorist -iṣ-Ao: rāviṣam etc. V.B Intensive róruvat RV Verbal Nouns PPP: rutá V.B Derivatives ravitṛ B. -rāvin B. A very few sporadic occurrences, and not unquestionable. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ruc.html"> √ ruc    √ ruc, “shine” Present I. rócate etc. V.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: rociṣyate E Periphrastic Future: rocitā Aorist √-Ao: rucīya TA., rucāná RV.; Th Ao: arucat C RAo: árūrucat RV.,-cata (3s.) etc. B -s-Ao: arukta TA -iṣ-Ao: arociṣṭa etc. B.+ (rociṣīya B., ruciṣīya AV.) Ao/Ps/3/sg: aroci RV Perfect ruroca rurucé etc. V.+ (rurukvā́ṃs rurucyās rurucanta RV.) Causative rocáyati etc. V.+,-te etc. B.+ (rocyate E.); rucayanta RV Desiderative ruruciṣate ? AA. rurociṣa- Intensive rórucāna RV Verbal Nouns PPP: rucitá B.+; Inf: rocitum E.; rucé V Derivatives rúc V.+ rocaka E.+ rúci AV.+ rucira E.+ rucí MS. rucá B. -rocin C. roci C. rukṣá RV. rucā E. roká V.+ rocís V.+ ruciṣya C. rucaka E.+ róka RV. rócuka MS. rociṣṇú B.+ rucya C. -rokin V.B. rukmá V.+ -ruśa ? RV. rocá AV.+ rocaná V.+ rúkmant V.B. rúśant ? V. -rocas B. Meanings rócate (rócati) v PPP rucitá 1 (q.v.) shine, be bright, make a show, appear beautiful or good, please (D or G); delight in (A), long for (D). Caus. rocáyati, rócate (ti), PPP rucitá 1 (q.v.) shine, be bright, make a show, appear beautiful or good, please (D or G); delight in (A), long for (D). Caus. rocáyate P Cause to shine, illuminate, make bright or pleasant; cause a person (A) to like or long for (D); PĀ take delight in, approve, like (A or Inf); choose (2A); intend, purpose; be agreeable, please (also P.). ati shine over or outshine (A). abhi shine, be brilliant or splendid, please (D). Caus. P content or satisfy with (I), entertain, amuse; PĀ take delight in, have a taste for, like (A or Inf). ud Ā shine forth. upa Ā approach with brightness. pra shine forth, be brilliant or clear, please. Caus. P make shine, illumine, make agreeable or pleasant, commend, approve, like. prati Ā please (A). vi Ā shine forth, glitter, be bright or radiant, become visible, appear like (N), excel, outshine (A), appear good, please (G). Caus. P make shine, illumine; take delight in (A). sam Ā shine (together or in emulation). Caus. P take delight in, approve of, resolve upon (A); choose for (2A). Cf. abhirucita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ruj.html"> √ ruj    √ ruj, “break” Present II ? rukte B VI. rujáti etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ Passive rujyate E Future Simple Future: rokṣyati Periphrastic Future: roktā Aorist √-Ao: rok VS., ruk MS RAo: arūrujat C -s-Ao: araukṣīt Perfect rurója rurujus etc. V.+ (rurójitha RV.) Causative rojayati Desiderative rurukṣa- (in d.) Intensive roruj- Verbal Nouns PPP: rugná V.+; 1Abs: ruktvā́ B.; 2Abs: -rújya B.+;-rúje RV Derivatives ruj V.+ róga V.+ -rujana C. -rujatnu RV. rujá V.+ logá V.B. -rogaṇa AV. rurukṣáṇi RV. rujā E.+ rujā́nā RV. Meanings rujáti v PPP rugṇá 1 (q.v.) break, crush down, destroy; pain, afflict. Caus. rojayati give one a blow upon (L). ava break off. ā break open or asunder, tear out, lacerate, dislimb. pra break to pieces. vi & sam break, crush, rend. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ru_th.html"> √ ruṭh    √ ruṭh, “torment” Present I. roṭhamāna R1. Compare √ luṭh. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_rud.html"> √ rud    √ rud, “weep” Present I. rodati -te etc. S.+ II. roditi rudanti etc. V.+ (rudimas rudihi C., arodīt B.+) VI. rudati -te etc. S.+ Passive rudyate C Future Simple Future: rodiṣyati C Periphrastic Future: roditā Aorist Th Ao: árudat etc. AV.U RAo: arūrudat -iṣ-Ao ? araudiṣīt C Perfect ruroda rurudus etc. E., rurude E Causative rodáyati etc. V.+ Desiderative rurudiṣa- (in d.) Intensive rorudat E., rorudyate etc. E.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: rudita E.+; Inf: roditum C.; 1Abs: ruditvā E.+, roditvā E.; 2Abs: -rudya C Derivatives -rud AV. rodana E.+ ródas etc. ? V.+ -roruda AV. -ruda ? C. rudana C. roditavya E.+ rurudiṣu C. róda AV.U. rudrá ? V.+ rurudiṣā C. Meanings roditi rudati roditi rudate rodati rodate v PPP rudita (q.v.) cry, weep, lament. Caus. rodáyati cause to weep or lament. Int rorudyate weep very much. anu weep after or for (A). pra burst into tears, begin to weep or lament; cry aloud; weep with (A). vi weep or cry aloud, sob. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_rudh.html"> √ 1 rudh    √ 1 rudh, “grow” Present I. ródhati ródhat RV VI. rudhánt ? RV1 Derivatives -rudh V.+ -rodha AV.+ -ródhana V.B. Appears to be another form of √ ruh. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_rudh.html"> √ 2 rudh    √ 2 rudh, “obstruct” Present I. rodhati E II. rudhmas AV VI ? rundhati -te etc. B.+ VII. ruṇáddhi rundhanti runddhé rundhate etc. V.+ Passive rudhyáte etc. V.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: rotsyati -te etc. B.+ Periphrastic Future: roddhā Aorist √-Ao: arodham RV., arudhma MS. (rudhánt ? RV.) Th Ao: arudhat etc. V.+ RAo: arūrudhat -s-Ao: arautsīt etc. B.+ (araut AV., rotsīs U.), arutsi aruddha etc. B.U. (arautsi AB.) Precative: rudhyāt C. Ao/Ps/3/sg: arodhi Perfect rurodha rurudhe etc. V.+ (rurodhitha RV., rurundhatus E.) Causative rodhayati -te etc. E.+ (rodhyate E.); rundhayati E Desiderative rurutsate etc. B.,-ti E. (-syamāna ? B.S.) Intensive rorudhas E Verbal Nouns PPP: ruddhá V.+; Inf: roddhum E.+,-dhos B., rodhitum E.; 1Abs: ruddhvā E.+; 2Abs: -rúdhya V.+,-rundhya E.;-rúdham AV.B.,-rúndham B.;-ródham B Derivatives -rudh V.+ rodhaka . E.+ ródhana V.+ -ruddhi B. -rudha RV. rodhin S.+ rodhanā́ RV. roddhavya E.+ ródha V.+ rodhya E.+ ródhas V.+ roddhṛ B.+ -ródhuka B. rurutsu C. Meanings ruṇáddhi runddhé (rundhati) (ruṇáddhi) (runddhé) (rundhate) (rodhati) v PPP ruddha 2 obstruct, hold back, keep off, hinder, suppress, shut up, close, stop or fill up, besiege, invest, cover, veil. Caus. rodhayati, te hold back, stop, cause to be confined or besieged by (2A or A & I). anu obstruct (a way), hem in, surround; fetter, master, govern; follow immediately (A); mostly P. rudhyate (ti) cleave or cling to, be devoted to, intent upon, engaged in (A); conform one's self to, have a regard for (A). apa keep or ward off, remove, expel or exclude from (Ab). ava hold back, keep away from (2A), hold fast, confine in, shut up (L, r. A); obstruct, hinder; surround, besiege; cover, veil; remove, expel from (Ab); cling or be devoted to (A). Ā hold, contain; get, attain. samava shut up, confine; get, attain; P. be contained in (L). ā shut up, confine, invest, surround, besiege; ward off, expel drive away. upa the same, drive in (cattle); keep back, retain; molest, pain, harass, trouble, disturb, prevent; menace, compromise; cover, veil. ni hold back or fast, stop, overtake, check, restrain, obstruct, hinder, shut up, confine. saṃni hold back or fast, shut up, confine, check, restrain, suppress; stuff, fill. pari shutup, confine, keep back. pra hold back, obstruct, hinder. prati hold back, resist, disturb, trouble, shut up, confine; veil, cover. vi hinder, obstruct, restrain, suppress, surround, besiege, confine, shut up; Ā be opposed by (I); P. virudhyate (ti) be opposed or contrary to (I); disagree, contend or fight with (I saha, G, L, or prati). Caus. render hostile, disunite, exasperate. sam drive in (cattle), confine, keep prisoner, invest, besiege, hold back, stop, detain, hold fast, fetter, withhold, refuse; veil, cover. Cf. ávaruddha (add.), uparuddha, niruddha, viruddha, saṃruddha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_rup.html"> √ rup    √ rup, “break, pain” Present IV. rúpyati etc. B Future Simple Future: ropiṣyati Periphrastic Future: ropitā Aorist Th Ao: arupat RAo: arūrupat etc. AV.B Perfect ruropa Causative ropayati B Verbal Nouns PPP: rupita RV Derivatives ropaṇá AV. rópi AV. rópuṣī RV. Probably the same with √ lup, though differentiated from it in meaning. Meanings rúpyati 1 v have racking pain in the belly. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ru_s.html"> √ ruṣ    √ ruṣ, “be vexed” Present I. roṣati RV.B IV. ruṣyati -te etc. E.+ VI. ruṣati etc. S.+ Future Simple Future: roṣiṣyati Periphrastic Future: roṣitā roṣṭā Aorist Th Ao: aruṣat RAo: arūruṣat -iṣ-Ao: aroṣīt Perfect ruroṣa Causative roṣayati -te etc. E.+ (roṣyate E.+) Desiderative ruruṣiṣa- , ruroṣiṣa- Intensive roruṣ- Verbal Nouns PPP: ruṣita E.+, ruṣṭa E.+; ruṣya E Derivatives ruṣ E.+ roṣa E.+ roṣaṇa E.+ roṣin C. Occasionally written ruś; and part of the AV. forms of rúśant are referred here by BR. Meanings roṣati ruṣyati roṣati ruṣyate ruṣati ruṣate v PPP ruṣita 1 & ruṣṭa (q.v.) be vexed, be cross or angry. Caus. roṣayati, te vex, annoy, irritate. Cf. abhiruṣita, āroṣita, viruṣṭa, saṃruṣita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ruh.html"> √ ruh    √ ruh, “ascend” Present I. róhati -te etc. V.+ VI. ruhati -te etc. E.+ Passive ruhyate E Future Simple Future: rokṣyáti B.+,-te E., rohiṣye E Periphrastic Future: roḍhā Aorist Th Ao: aruhat. etc. V.+ (ruheyam etc. ruha rúhāṇa V.B.S.) -sa- Ao: árukṣat etc. V.B.S Perfect ruroha ruruhús etc. V.+ (ruróhitha AV.), ruruhe etc. C Causative roháyati etc. V.+,-te etc. B.+; ropayati etc. B.+,-te E. (ropyate E.+, aropi C.) Desiderative rurukṣati etc. V.+ Intensive roruh- Verbal Nouns PPP: rūḍhá V.+; Inf: róḍhum B.+, rohitum E.; 1Abs: rūḍhvā́ AV.; 2Abs: -rúhya AV.+,-rūhya AB.;-rúham RV.; róhiṣyai TS.;-róham B Derivatives rúh V.+ róhaṇa V.+ -roḍhavya E.+ ropin E.+ -ruha E.+ rohaṇīya S.+ -roḍhṛ C. ropya E.+ róha AV.+ róhas RV.S. -rurukṣu E.+ ropaṇa E.+ rohaka E.+ -róhuka B. ropa E.+ ropaṇīya C. rohin B.+ rūḍhi B.+ ropaka E.+ ropayitṛ E.+ -rohyà B. Meanings róhati róhate & (ruhati) (ruhate) v PPP rūḍhá 1 (q.v.) rise, mount up, climb, spring up, grow, develop, thrive; grow together, i.e. cicatrize, heal. Caus. roheyati & ropayati, te raise up, erect, place on, fix, fasten, commit, intrust; grow (trans., i.e.) plant, sow; heal, cure (cf. S.). ati rise beyond (A), grow higher. adhi ascend, mount (A, r. L), w. tulām be a match for (I); rise into, get at, obtain (paramá koṭim) the highest degree). Caus. raise above, place or fix upon (L or A); put in, appoint to (L), intrust, commit to (L), bend (a bow). anu ascend, Ā grow up or together. api & samapi grow together. abhi & samabhi mount, ascend, rise to (together). ava descend from (Ab) upon (A), tread on (L), enter. Caus. descend (trans.) or take down from (Ab); set, plant (trees); deprive of (Ab), decrease, diminish, destroy. ā mount, ascend climb; rise to (A or L), bestride, enter (also = inire, kakṣām = tulām, cf. sub adhi), spring forth, develop, increase; get to, arrive at, reach, attain. Caus. cause to mount, ascend, or enter (A, w. tulām = saṃśayatulām expose to danger, compromise, w. pattram commit to paper, write down); set, plant; string (a bow); raise, promote; place in or upon, appoint to (L or A); cause, produce, show, betray. atyā exceed all limits. adhyā mount, ascend, enter; rise into the air. Caus. cause to ascend (2A), promote or appoint to (L); falsely suppose or transfer to (L), exaggerate. anvā rise after (A), mount, ascend, enter, bestride. abhyā mount, ascend, rise to or above. upā mount, ascend, approach, get at (A). samā ascend or rise to or upon (A or L), approach (as friend or foe), enter upon, engage in (A, w. tulām cf. sub adhi). Caus. cause to mount or ascend (2A or A & L), load or place upon; raise, erect, promote, exalt; put in (L or A), deposit (the sacred fire), string (a bow), entrust, commit, transfer, attribute to (L); show, manifest. upa grow together; Caus. cause to grow together, heal. pra grow forth, sprout; grow together, cicatrize or heal; increase, thrive. Caus. plant, fix on or in (L). prati grow or sprout again; Caus. plant again, restore. vi grow out, germinate. Caus. cause to grow, plant, cause to cicatrize, heal; expel, remove from (Ab). sam grow, esp. grow together, cicatrize, heal; grow forth, germinate, appear. Caus. cause to grow etc., plant, sow = propagate (ātmānam refl.). Cf. atyārūḍha (add.), adhirūḍha, abhyā́rūḍha, ávarūḍha, ārūḍha, uparūḍha, nirūḍha, prarūḍha, virūḍha, saṃrūḍha, samārūḍha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ruu_s.html"> √ rūṣ    √ rūṣ, “strew” Present etc. rūṣati etc.etc Causative rūṣayati ; roṣayati etc. C Verbal Nouns PPP: rūṣita E.+ ruṃṣita C Derivatives rūṣaṇa C. rūkṣá ? V.+ Meanings PPP rūṣita covered or smeared with, cleaving to (– ṃ). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_rej.html"> √ rej    √ rej, “tremble” Present I. rejati -te etc. V.B Causative rejáyati etc. RV Meanings réjati réjate v P shake (trans.); Ā shake (intrans.), tremble. Caus. rejáyati = S. trans. pra Ā tremble; Caus. shake (trans.). sam Ā tremble. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_re_d.html"> √ reḍ    √ reḍ, “deceive” (?) Present I.-reḍant B.S. Only in the phrase áreḍatā mánasā. Of wholly doubtful character. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_rebh.html"> √ rebh    √ rebh see √ ribh. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_lak_s.html"> √ lakṣ    √ lakṣ, “mark” Present I. lakṣate C.,-ti E Causative lakṣayati-te etc. E.+ (-lakṣita B.+,-lakṣya S.+; lakṣyate E.+) Derivatives lakṣá V.+ lakṣya U.+ lakṣaṇīya C. lakṣmī́ V.+ lakṣaka C. lakṣaṇa B.+ lákṣman V.+ -lakṣayitavya E. Really a denominative formation from lakṣá, but having attained the position and value of a secondary root. Meanings lakṣate lakṣati v mark, notice; cf. lakṣay. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_lag.html"> √ lag    √ lag, “attach” Present I. lagati etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: lagiṣyati etc. C Periphrastic Future: lagitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: alagīt Perfect lalāga Causative lā̆gayati C Verbal Nouns PPP: lagna B1.? E.+; 1Abs: lagitvā C.; 2Abs: -lagya C Derivatives -lagana C. laganīya C. liṅga ŚB.U.+ The lateness of this root is strongly opposed to the derivation from it of lakṣá etc. Meanings lagati v PPP lagna (q.v.) attach or fasten one's self to (L), cling to, adhere, approach, near, follow immediately, happen, occur, pass away. ava abide, stay, tarry. ā cling to, adhere. vi cling or stick to (L). Cf. anulagna, avalagna, ālagna, parilagna*, pratilagna* (add.), vilagna, saṃlagna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_la_ggh.html"> √ laṅgh    √ laṅgh, “leap” Present I. laṅghati -te C Future Simple Future: laṅghiṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: laṅghitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: alaṅghīt, alaṅghiṣṭa Perfect lalaṅgha -ghe Causative laṅghayati etc. E.+ (laṅghita S.+; laṅghyate C.) Derivatives laṅghaka C. -laṅghin C. laṅghya E.+ laṅghana S.+ laṅghanīya C. Doubtless related with √ raṃh. Meanings laṅghati laṅghate v leap; mostly Caus. laṅghayati (te), PPP laṅghita spring over, go beyond (A); travel over (adhvānam); mount, ascend, enter; get off, escape; overstep, transgress; violate, offend; excel, surpass, outstrip. ati Caus. transgress. abhi Caus. leap or step over, transgress, offend. ud Caus. the same + pass by, escape; pass or travel over (way). vi Caus. leap over, pass by; transgress, violate; neglect, omit; surpass, excel; wrong, offend. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_lajj.html"> √ lajj    √ lajj, “be ashamed” Present VI. lajjate etc. B1.E.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: lajjiṣyate Periphrastic Future: lajjitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: alajjiṣṭa Perfect lalajjire C Causative lajjayati etc. C Desiderative lilajjiṣa- Intensive lālajj- Verbal Nouns PPP: lajjita C.; Inf: lajjitum E Derivatives lajjā E.+ Meanings lajjate (lajjati) v PPP lajjita (q.v.) be abashed or embarrassed, be ashamed of (I or G) or to (Inf). Caus. lajjayati make ashamed, confound. vi & sam = S. Cf. vilajjita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_la_d.html"> √ laḍ    √ laḍ “move about” Present I. laḍati C1 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_lap.html"> √ lap    √ lap, “prate” Present I. lapati etc. AV.E.+,-te etc. E IV. lapyant M Passive lapyate C Future Simple Future: lapiṣyati etc. B.+ Periphrastic Future: lapitā Aorist RAo: alīlapat, alalāpat -iṣ-Ao: alāpīt Perfect lalāpa lepus E.+ Causative lāpayati etc. AV.+,-te etc. B.U Desiderative lilapiṣa- Intensive lā́lapīti etc. AV.B.; lālapyate etc. E.+,-ti E Verbal Nouns PPP: lapitá AV.+, lapta E.; Inf: lapitum C., laptum E.; 2Abs: -lapya E.+ Derivatives -lap AV. lapana C. -lapitavya C. -lāpin E.+ -lapya C. lapanīya C. -lāpa AV.+ -lāpya C. -lapti C. -lāpaka E.+ lāpana E.+ Compare the other root-form, √ rap. Meanings lapāta (lapāte) v PPP lapitá (q.v.) chatter, prate, talk, lament. Caus. lāpayati cause to talk. Int lā́lapīti chatter senselessly, prattle, lālapyate (ti) wail, lament. apa deny, refuse, conceal. abhi talk, speak of; name, call. ā address, speak to (A), converse with (samam or saha), say, tell (2A). Caus. cause to speak, engage in conversation, question. ud Caus. = prec. Caus. or caress. samud raise the voice; (wail, lament*). pra prattle, chatter, talk, lament. Caus. compel to speak. vi wail, moan, chatter, talk confusedly or at random. sam converse, Caus. address. Cf. ālapita, pralapita, vilapita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_labh.html"> √ labh    √ labh, “take” Present I. labhate etc. AV.+,-ti etc. AV. ? E.+; lambhate etc. E Passive labhyáte etc. B.+,-ti C Future Simple Future: lapsyate etc. B.+,-ti etc. B.+; labhiṣyati C Periphrastic Future: labdhā E Aorist √-Ao: alambhi RAo: alalambhat -s-Ao: alabdha alapsata B.; lapsīya S Perfect lalābha C., lebhé etc. V.+ Causative lambhayati etc. B.+,-te B Desiderative lípsate etc. AV.+,-ti etc. E.+; līpsate etc. B.S. (lipsyáte ŚB.) Intensive lālabh- , lālambh- Verbal Nouns PPP: labdha V.+; labdhvā́ AV.+;-lábhya B.+;-lámbham B.S Derivatives -labha S.+ labhana C. lambha B.+ lambhuka B.U. labhya B.+ -labhanīya C. lambhaka B.+ lipsā AVP.E.+ lābha B.+ labdhi E.+ -lambhin E.+ lipsu E.+ -lābhaka RV. labdhavya U.+ -lambhyà B.S. lipsitavya E. lābhin C. labdhṛ B.+ lambhana S.+ līpsitavya B. lambhanīya U.+ Compare the other root-form, √ rabh. Meanings lábhate (labhati & lambhate) v PPP labdha (q.v.) catch, seize; meet with, find; obtain, get, receive; be capable of or able to, succeed in (D or Inf); possess, have, enjoy; perceive, know, learn, understand. P. be caught etc., be allowed or permitted; result, follow. Caus. lambhayati cause to take or receive (2A or A of pers. & I of th.); get, obtain, find out, learn. Des lípsate (ti) wish to catch or obtain. anu catch or seize from behind. abhi seize, touch, get, attain. Des wish to catch or seize. ā catch, seize, touch, take hold of (esp. the sacrificial animal to kill it); undertake, begin; gain, acquire, get, attain. Caus. cause to seize, touch, or begin. Des wish to touch or kill. anvā seize or touch (from behind); hold or stick to (A). upā touch, also = Caus. reproach, blame. samā take hold of, seize, touch, get, obtain, rub over, anoint upa catch, meet with, find, obtain (P. fall to one's share), recover; conceive (garbham); perceive, learn, ascertain, understand, know as (2A). Caus. let have or know. pratyupa receive back, recover. samupa get, obtain; learn, understand. pra seize; take hold of, get, obtain, also = Caus. take in, dupe, fool, mock. vipra = prec. Caus. prati receive back, recover, get, obtain; get it i.e. be punished; perceive, learn, understand, know as (2A); wait for, expect. vi take asunder or away; get, procure; cede, surrender, yield. Caus. let a pers. have a th. (2A). sam wrestle or struggle with (I), take hold of one another; obtain, receive. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_lam.html"> √ lam    √ lam, “take pleasure” Present lalāma C1. Derivatives lamaka ? S. Sporadic variation of √ ram. Meanings only lalāma, enjoy (sexually). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_lamb.html"> √ lamb    √ lamb, “hang down” Present I. lambate etc. B.+,-ti etc. E.+ Passive lambyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: lambiṣyati E., alambiṣyata C Periphrastic Future: lambitā Aorist RAo: alalambat -iṣ-Ao: alambiṣṭa Perfect lalambe etc. E.+ Causative lambayati etc. E.+,-te C. (lambyate etc. E.+) Verbal Nouns PPP: lambita E.+; Inf: lambitum E.+; 2Abs: -lambya E.+ Derivatives lamba B.+ lambin B.+ lambana E.+ -lambitavya C. lambaka C. -lambya C. -lambuka B. Compare the other root-form, √ ramb. Meanings lambate (lambati) v PPP lambita (q.v.) hang down, sink; hang upon, cling to (L, w. raśmiṣu let free); stay behind, tarry, lag, linger. Caus. laṃmbayati hang up, suspend; w. karam put the hand to (D). ava hang down, descend, sink, sit down; hang, lean, rest, depend or rely upon, belong to (A, r. L or I); take hold of, seize, uphold, maintain; take to, affect, pursue (A); linger, tarry. Caus. hang or let down, suspend on (L); seize, take hold of, support, uphold; load upon, impose. ā hang down; hang or lean, depend or rest upon, hold or stick to (A, r. L); seize, take; support, maintain; take to, affect, pursue assume, show, exhibit. vyā hang down (from all sides), descend. samā cling to, lean or rely upon (A); take hold of, seize, assume; apply or devote one's self to (A). Caus. suspend on (L). ud Caus. hang, suspend. pari lag, loiter. pra hang down. prati Caus. hang, tie up. vi hang (on both sides) on (A or L); sink, descend; lag, loiter. Caus. suspend on (L); detain, delay, lag or loiter. pravi Caus. hang, suspend. Cf. avalambita, ālambita, ullambita (add.), pralambita (add.), vilambita, vilambya, samullambita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_lal.html"> √ lal    √ lal, “sport” Present I. lalati -te etc. E.+ Causative lālayati etc. E.+,-te C. (lālyate C.); lalayati etc. C Verbal Nouns PPP: lalita E.+ Derivatives lalana E.+ lālaka C. lālana C. lālayitavya E.+ -lāla C. -lālya C. lālanīya E.+ lālin C. Meanings lalani (lalate) v PPP lalita (q.v.) sport, dally, play, coruscate. Caus. lālayati cause to sport etc., caress, fondle, cherish, love. (ā play, sport). upa & sam Caus. = S. Caus. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_la_s.html"> √ laṣ    √ laṣ, “desire” Present I. laṣati -te etc. E.+ IV. laṣyati -te Future Simple Future: laṣiṣyati C.-te Periphrastic Future: laṣitā Aorist RAo: alīlaṣat -iṣ-Ao: alā̆ṣīt, alaṣiṣṭa Perfect lalāṣa leṣus C. leṣe Causative lāṣaya- Desiderative lilaṣiṣa- Intensive lālaṣ- Verbal Nouns PPP: laṣitá E.+ Derivatives -laṣya C. -laṣaṇīya C. -lāṣa C. -lāṣin C. -lāṣaka E.+ -lāṣuka C. Hardly occurs, in verb-forms of derivatives, except with abhi. Meanings laṣati (laṣate & laṣyati) v PPP laṣita desire, long for, strive after (A). abhi , samabhi, ā & pari = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_las.html"> √ las    √ las, “be lively” Present I. lasati etc. E.+,-te etc. C Future Simple Future: lasiṣyati Periphrastic Future: lasitā Aorist RAo: alīlasat -iṣ-Ao: alasīt Perfect lalāsa C Causative lāsayati etc. E.+ (lāsyate C.) Verbal Nouns lasita E.+ Derivatives -las C. -lasana C. lāsa E.+ -lāsin E.+ -lasa B.+ lāsana E.+ lāsaka E.+ lāsya E.+ lālasa E.+ In meaning, lālasa belongs distinctly to √ laṣ, and the two roots are very possibly one in origin; alasa is the only pre-epic form. Meanings lasati v PPP lasita gleam, glance; sound forth; appear, rise (only lasant & lasamāna), sport, play. Caus. lāsayati (cause or teach to) dance. ud = S. Caus. cause to gleam etc; cause, produce i.g. pratyud shine, appear. prod shine or sound forth, move hither and thither. samud shine or sound forth, appear. vi shine, glitter, appear, arise, sound forth, sport, play, move hither and thither, coruscate. Cf. ullasita, vilasita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_laa.html"> √ lā    √ lā, “grasp” Present II. lāti C Future Simple Future: lāsyati Periphrastic Future: lātā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: alāsīt Perfect lalau Verbal Nouns 1 Abs: lātvā C A few sporadic occurrences, probably artificial. Meanings lāti v grasp, seize, take; ger. lātvā having taken, i.e. with. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_laa_jch.html"> √ lāñch    √ lāñch, “mark” Only in lāñchita C. and lāñchana C.; perhaps connected with √ lakṣ. Meanings Caus. lāñchayati, PPP lāñchita mark, distinguish. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_likh.html"> √ likh    √ likh, “scratch” Present VI. likháti etc. AV.+,-te B.S Passive likhyate etc. S.+ Future Simple Future: likhiṣyati C. lekhiṣyati Periphrastic Future: lekhitā Aorist √-Ao: alekhi RAo: alīlikhat JB -iṣ-Ao: lekhīs B.S Perfect lilékha etc. B.+ Causative lekhayati etc. S.+; likhāpayati C Desiderative lilikhiṣa- , lilekhiṣa- Verbal Nouns PPP: likhitá AV.+ ; Inf: lekhitum, likhitum; 1Abs: lekhitvā, likhitvā C.; 2Abs: -líkhya B.+ Derivatives likhya C. lekha S.+ lekhaka E.+ lekhana S.+ likhana C. lékhā B.+ lekhin E.+ lekhanīya C. lekhya E.+ likhitṛ C. Compare the other root-form, √ rikh. Meanings likhati (likhate) v PPP likhitá (q.v.) scratch, furrow, slit, peck at (A); draw a line, write, write down, delineate, sketch, paint Caus. lekhayati cause to scratch etc; also = S. write, paint abhi = S., (hṛdayena) ponder upon*; Caus. cause to write or paint ā scratch, touch, cut in, write, delineate, paint; ponder upon (A*). samā the same. ud furrow, scratch, scrape, cut in, inscribe, write down; cut out, chisel, form; smooth, polish. prod scratch, furrow. samud the same, touch (the sky); write down, register, record. pari draw a furrow or a line around, enclose in a circle. pra scratch, furrow; sketch, delineate, write; PĀ scrape together; Ā comb one's self. prati write in return, answer. vi scratch, tear open, scrape, rub against, touch (the sky); scratch or cut in, write, delineate, paint sam scratch, engrave, inscribe, touch (a musical instrument) i.e. play. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_lip.html"> √ lip, limp    √ lip, limp, “smear” Present VI. limpáti etc. AV.+,-te etc. S.+ Passive lipyate etc. B.+,-ti E Future Simple Future: lepsyati -te Periphrastic Future: leptā Aorist √-Ao: alepi C Th Ao: alipat C. alipata RAo: alīlipat -s-Ao: alipta C., alipsata RV Perfect lilepa lilipus B.+ Causative lepayati etc. E.+; limpayati S Desiderative lilipsa- Intensive lelip- Verbal Nouns PPP: lipta AV.+; 2Abs: -lípya B.+ Derivatives lepa U.S.+ lepin E.+ lepana S.+ -limpa AV.B. lepaka C. lepya C. lipi E.+ limpi C1. lipti C. Compare the other root-form, √ rip. Meanings limpáti limpáte v PPP liptá (q.v.) smear, stain, soil (lit. & fig.), besmear with (I) or smear a th. (A) over or on a th., stick on to (L); P. lipyate cleave or stick to (intrans.). Caus. lepayati & limpayati = S. trans. anu smear, anoint with (I); Ā refl. ava the same; P. be haughty or arrogant. ā smear, anoint with (I); Caus. the same. upa the same. ni smear; cause to disappear; Ā disappear, become invisible. pra , vi , sam smear, anoint; Caus. the same. Cf. avalipta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_liz.html"> √ liś    √ liś, “tear” Present IV. liśyate VI. liśáte etc. B. (liśāna JB.) Future Simple Future: lekṣyate Periphrastic Future: leṣṭā Aorist RAo: alīliśat -iṣ-Ao: aleśiṣi B -sa- Ao: alikṣata Perfect liliśire B Causative leśaya- Desiderative lilikṣa- Intensive leliś- Verbal Nouns PPP: liṣṭá B.S Derivatives (ku-)liśa ? V.+ leśa B.+ leṣṭu E.+ Compare the other root-form, √ riś. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_lih.html"> √ lih    √ lih, “lick” Present II. leḍhi etc. B.+, līḍhe etc. E.+ VI. lihati etc. E.+ Passive lihyate E Future Simple Future: lekṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: leḍhā Aorist RAo: alīlihat -s-Ao: alīḍha -sa- Ao: alīkṣat S.-kṣata Ao/Ps/3/sg: alehi Perfect lileha , lilihe Causative leháyati etc. B.+ Desiderative lilikṣa- Intensive lelihat etc. E.+, lelihāna E.+, -hita JB., lelihyate etc. E.+,-hyant C Verbal Nouns PPP: līḍha E.+; 2Abs: -lihya S. leham S Derivatives -lih C. leha C. -lehin E.+ lehana S.+ -liha C. -lehaka E. lehya E.+ leliha E.+ Compare the other root-form, √ rih. Meanings leḍhi līḍhe lihati v PPP līḍha 1 lick, lick up, lick at (L), lick away i.e. destroy. Caus. leháyati cause to lick. Int lelihyate etc. (PPP lelihāna) lick frequently, play with the tongue. ava , ā , ud lick, touch (with mouth or beak). upa Ā enjoy by licking. nis lick off, sip. pari lick at (A); Int lick frequently. vi the same. sam & parisam lick at, enjoy. Cf. ālīḍha, ullīḍha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_lii.html"> √ 1 lī    √ 1 lī, “cling” Present I. láyate etc. V.B. (ni-) lāyata B IV. lī́yate AV. ? B.+,-ti etc. U.C IX. lināti Future Simple Future: leṣyati, lāsyati Periphrastic Future: letā, lātā Aorist -s-Ao: aleṣṭa ŚB. alaiṣīt -siṣ-Ao: alāsīt Perfect lilye etc. B.+, lilyus B.+ (ni-)layāṃ cakre ŚB. lalau Causative lāpayati etc. B.+ (lāpyate C.); lāyayati etc. C Desiderative lilīṣa- Intensive lelī- Verbal Nouns PPP: līna AV.+; Inf: letum C.; 2Abs: -līya E.+,-lā́ya B.S.;-lā́yam AV.B Derivatives láya B.+ -līyana C. -lāyya ? RV. -lāpya C. láyana AV.+ lā́ya ? RV. -lāyana C. -lā́pana B.+ layú ? MS. -lā́yaka VS. -leya ? C. -lāpayitavya C. Compare √ ri, rī. Meanings lī́yate lī́yati (láyate 1 v only w. ni), PPP līna (q.v.) cling, adhere, stick, light or sit upon (of birds & insects); stoop, cower; slip into, disappear. Caus. lāpayati & lāyayati-> sub vi. abhi cling to (A). ava settle down, cower, hide. vyava stoop, cower. ā cling or adhere to (L), sit down upon or in, stoop, cower, hide. ni cleave or stick to (A), lie or settle down upon (L); layate (also apani) hide, disappear from (Ab). saṃni settle down, alight; hide or disappear in (L). pra hide one's self; dissolve, be absorbed in (L); disappear, perish, die. saṃpra vanish, be dissolved or absorbed in (L). prati disappear. vi cling or stick to, cower upon (L); settle down, alight; conceal one's self, disappear, be dissolved, melt. Caus. (lāpayati & lāyayati) cause to disappear, dissolve, melt (trans.). pravi perish, disappear. sam cling or stick close to (A), find room in (L); hide, be concealed; stoop, cower, contrP Cf. abhilīna, avalīna (add.), ālīna, nílīna (add.), pralīna, vilīna, saṃlīna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_lii.html"> √ 2 lī    √ 2 lī, “be unsteady” Intensive lelā́yati B.U.S., alelāyat B., alelet B., lelāyántī leláyatas B.; lelāyate etc. U., alelīyata B.; leláya ? ŚB., lelā́ya MS., lelāyat JB Derivatives lelā́ ŚB. ? JB. Perhaps intensive of the preceding (√ 1 lī). The variety of form and accent is quite anomalous. Meanings only Int lelā́yati, lelā́yate 2 be unsteady, waver, tremble. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_lu_jc.html"> √ luñc    √ luñc, “tear” Present I. luñcati Future Simple Future: luñciṣyati Periphrastic Future: luñcitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aluñcīt Perfect luluñcus E.,-ñce C Verbal Nouns PPP: luñcita C.; 1Abs: luñcitvā C. lucitvā; 2Abs: -luñcya E Derivatives luk ? C. -luñca VS. -luñcaka C. -luñcana E.+ Meanings luñcati v PPP luñcita pluck, tear; peel, husk. ava & vi tear off or out. Cf. ulluñcita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_lu_th.html"> √ 1 luṭh    √ 1 luṭh, “roll” Present VI. luṭhati -te etc. C Future Simple Future: loṭhiṣyati Periphrastic Future: loṭhitā Aorist RAo: alūluṭhat aluloṭhat -iṣ-Ao: aloṭhīt aloṭhiṣṭa Perfect luloṭha C Causative loṭhayati C Intensive loluṭhīti C Verbal Nouns PPP: luṭhita C Derivatives loṭhana ? C. Meanings luṭhati luṭhate v PPP luṭita 1 roll, move to and fro (intrans.), stir up, agitate. Caus. loṭhayati = S. Des luluṭhiṣate be about to roll. Int loluṭhīti wallow (of a drunkard). ud , pari , pra & vi = S. intrans. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_lu_th.html"> √ 2 luṭh, luṇṭh    √ 2 luṭh, luṇṭh, “rob” Present I. luṇṭhati E1 Future Simple Future: luṇṭhiṣyati C Causative loṭhayati etc. C.; luṇṭhayati etc. C. (luṇṭhyate C.) Verbal Nouns PPP: luṇṭhitum C Derivatives -luṇṭhā C. luṇṭhaka C. luṇṭhana E1.C. luṇṭhi C. Meanings luṇṭh luṇṭhati 2 v = prec. S. tr ; Caus. luṇṭhayati & loṭhayati, PPP luṇṭhita rob, steal, plunder. nis & vi = S. Caus. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_lu_d.html"> √ luḍ    √ luḍ, “stir up” Present etc I. loḍati etc.etc Causative loḍayati etc. E.+; loḍita -loḍya S.+ (loḍyate etc. E.+) Derivatives -loḍana E.+ -loḍayitṛ C. Compare √ lul. A form or two from √ luṇṭh appear to have the meaning of √ luḍ. Meanings Caus. loḍayati stir up, agitate. ava rummage, investigate. ā stir up, agitate, trouble, disturb, rummage, work one's way through (A). samā mix together, mingle with (I), stir up etc. = prec. nis investigate thoroughly. vipra, prati , vi & sam stir up, trouble, disturb, confuse. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_lup.html"> √ lup    √ lup, “break” Present VI. lumpáti etc. AV.+,-te etc. S.+ Passive lupyáte etc. AV.+ (lúpyate TS.), -ti S Future Simple Future: lopsyati -te Periphrastic Future: loptā Aorist √-Ao: lopi S Th Ao: alupat RAo: alūlupat E. alulopat -s-Ao: alupta; lopsīya U Perfect lulopa etc. B.+, lulupe E Causative lopayati -te etc. JB.E+ (lopyate C.) Desiderative lulupsa- , lulopiṣa- Intensive lolupatpyate etc. U.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: lupta AV.+; Inf: loptum C.; 1Abs: luptvā S.+; 2Abs: -lupya AV.+;-lúmpam MS.,-lopam S.C Derivatives lup C. lopaka E.+ lopana E.+ -lumpaka E.+ -lupya C. lopin E.+ -lupti B. -lumpana E. lopa B.+ lopya C. loptṛ E. lolupa E.+ loptra E.+ Compare the other root-form, √ rup. lolupa belongs in meaning to √ lubh. Meanings lumpáti (lumpáte) v PPP lupta 1 (q.v.) break, harm, injure, attack, rub, plunder, consume, throw away, suppress, destroy, cause to disappear. P. lupyáte (lúpyate, lumpáti (lumpáte), PPP lupta 1 (q.v.) break, harm, injure, attack, rub, plunder, consume, throw away, suppress, destroy, cause to disappear. P. lupyáte (lúpyati) be broken or harmed etc ; be suppressed or elided, disappear (g.). Caus. lopayati, te omit, neglect, infringe, violate; divert from (Ab). Int lolupyate etc. confuse, disturb. apa pluck off, sever; P. fall off. ava strip off, snatch away; seize, attack; suppress, destroy. ā pull out, sever; P. be troubled or disturbed. vyā break, destroy. uda & samud take out, pick up. pari take away, remove, destroy. pra pluck out, rob, deprive of (tas). vipra take away, rob; trouble, disturb. vi tear or break in pieces, pull out or up, take away, rob, plunder, destroy, ruin; P. Ā decay, perish, disappear, be gone or missing. sam pluck, pull, snatch away; Caus. ruin, destroy. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_lubh.html"> √ lubh    √ lubh, “be lustful” Present I. lobhase C1 IV. lúbhyati etc. AV.+ VI. lubhati Future Simple Future: lobhiṣyati Periphrastic Future: lobdhā, lobhitā Aorist Th Ao: alubhat RAo: alūlubhat JB -iṣ-Ao: alobhīt Perfect lulubhe S.+ lulobha Causative lobháyati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ (lobhyate E.+; lulobhayiṣati AB.) Desiderative lulubhiṣa- , lulobhiṣa- Intensive lolubhyate C Verbal Nouns PPP: lubdha B.+, lubhita S.; Inf: lobdhum E Derivatives lobha E.+ lobhin E.+ lobhana S.+ lobhanīya E.+ -lobhaka C. -lobhya C. Meanings lúbhyati v PPP lubdha (q.v.) go astray, be lustful or covetous, Desire eagerly, long for (L or D); attract, allure. Caus. lobhayati confuse, disturb, trouble, derange; allure. Int. lolubhyate be very greedy of (L). anu Caus. long for (A). abhi Caus. entice, allure. ā get into confusion. upa Caus. allure, seduce. pari S. & Caus. the same. pra Ā go astray, be lustful, lust after (saha); also = Caus. allure, entice, seduce. vipra, saṃpra & prati Caus. = prec. Caus. vi fall into disorder or confusion; Caus. lead astray, perplex, confuse, seduce, divert, amuse. sam be confounded; Caus. confound, disarrange, tempt, allure, seduce. Cf. parilubdha (add.). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_lul.html"> √ lul    √ lul, “be lively” Present I. lolati, te etc. C Causative lolayati etc. E.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: lulita E.+ Derivatives lola E.+ lolana C. The same with √ luḍ. Meanings lolati v PPP lulita (q.v.) move hither and thither, roll, wallow; disappear. Caus. lolayati set in motion, agitate, confound. Cf. abhilulita, ālulita, vilulita, saṃlulita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_luu.html"> √ lū    √ lū, “cut” Present V. lunoti etc. B.S IX. lunā́ti etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: laviṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: lavitā Aorist RAo: alīlavat -vata -iṣ-Ao: alāvīt alaviṣṭa; Ao/Ps/3/sg: alāvi Perfect lulāva C Causative lāvaya- Desiderative lulūṣa- Intensive lolū- Verbal Nouns PPP: lūna B.+; 1Abs: lutvā S.;-lāvam C Derivatives láva B.+ -lavya C. lavana S.+ lāva C. lāvaka C. lāvitavya C. Meanings lunoti & lunā́ti lunīte v PPP lūna (q.v.) cut, sever, mow, pluck, hew down, tear asunder, pierce, destroy. ava cut off. ā tear or pluck off. nyā, vyā, nis , pari , pra , vipra, vi cut or hew off. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_lok.html"> √ lok    √ lok, “look” Present I. lokate etc. B1.C Future Simple Future: lokiṣyate Periphrastic Future: lokitā Aorist RAo: alukokat -iṣ-Ao: alokiṣṭa Ao/Ps/3/sg: aloki C Perfect luloke C Causative lokayati etc. E.+,-te etc. E.+ (lokyate etc. C.) Verbal Nouns Inf: lokitum C Derivatives -loka E.+ -lokin S.+ -lokana C. -lokayitṛ C. -lokaka C.+ -lokya E.+ -lokanīya E.+ -lokayitavya C. Doubtless from √ ruc, through a noun loka: compare also √ loc. Meanings lokate v mostly lokayati (te) look, look at, view, contemplate; perceive, know. abhi view, contemplate. ava & samava look, look at, contemplate, see, mark, perceive. ā & samā look at, behold, consider, regard, examine, investigate, perceive, learn, know as (2A). pari look around. (pra consider*). vi look at, regard, try, examine, study; perceive, see, discover, look over or beyond (A). pravi look at, observe, behold, see, consider. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_loc.html"> √ loc    √ loc, “see, consider” Present I. locate Future Simple Future: lociṣyate Periphrastic Future: locitā Aorist RAo: alulocat -iṣ-Ao: alociṣṭa Perfect luloce C1 Causative locayati -te etc. E.+ Desiderative lulociṣa- Intensive loloc- Derivatives -loca C. -locya C. locana E.+ -locanīya C. -locaka C. The same root with the preceding. Meanings (only – ṃ) locate & Caus. locayati, (only – ) locate & Caus. locayate w. ā consider, reflect; Caus. the same, r. cause to appear or be seen; PPP ālocita (n. also impers.). anvā, paryā, samā & nis Caus. call to mind, imagine, consider, reflect, deliberate. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vak.html"> √ vak    √ vak see √ vañc. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vak_s.html"> √ vakṣ, ukṣ    √ vakṣ, ukṣ, “increase” Present I & VI. úkṣant ukṣámāṇa aúkṣat RV Future Simple Future: vakṣiṣyati Periphrastic Future: vakṣitā Aorist RAo ? vavákṣat SV -iṣ-Ao: aúkṣīs RV Perfect vavákṣa vavakṣé etc. (vavákṣitha) V Causative ukṣayanta RV.; vakṣayam RV Verbal Nouns PPP: ukṣitá RV Derivatives vákṣaṇa RV. vakṣáṇā ? V. vakṣáṇi RV. vakṣátha RV. vákṣas ? V.+ Meanings (cf. √ 2 ukṣ), Caus. vakṣayati cause to grow or increase, strengthen. ati excel, be superior to (A). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vac.html"> √ vac    √ vac, “speak” Present II. vacmi vakṣi vakti E.+ III. vívakti etc. V Passive ucyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: vakṣyáti etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ (avakṣyat etc. B.U.) Periphrastic Future: vaktā́ B.+ Aorist Th Ao: avocat -cata etc. V.+ (vócati -te etc. V.+; vacāti etc. V.B.S., vocét -ceta etc. V.B., vocatu etc. V.; vocant C.; avoci C.) RAo: avīvacat Precative: ucyāsam B. Ao/Ps/3/sg: avāci V.B Perfect uvā́ca ūcús etc. V.+ (uváktha AV.), ūcé etc. V.+ (vavāca vivakvā́ṃs RV., vavakṣé RV.) Causative vācayati etc. B.+,-te etc. S. (vācyate C.) Desiderative vivakṣati -te etc. B.+ (vivakṣyate C.) Intensive ávāvacīt RV Verbal Nouns PPP: uktá V.+; Inf: váktum B.+,-tave RV.,-tos B.; 1Abs: uktvā B.+; 2Abs: -úcya B.+; vā́ce RV Derivatives vā́c V.+ vácana V.+ ukti V.+ vagnú V.B. -vaca E.+ vacaná RV. vakti U1. vákman ? RV. -úcya B.S. vacanīya S.+ váktva RV. vákmya ? RV. vāká V.+ vācana V.+ vaktavyà B.+ vagvaná RV. -vākin U1. -vācanīya C. vaktṛ V.+ vagvanú RV. vākyà V.+ vácas V.+ vaktra E.+ vivakṣā E.+ vācaka E.+ -vā́cas V. ukthá V.+ vivakṣu AV.+ vācin C. -vā́ku AV.+ ucátha RV. vācayitṛ C. vā́cya V.+ vācayitavya S. The aorist-stem voca is treated quite as a secondary root-form. Meanings vívakti vakti v PPP uktá (q.v.) say, speak, tell (2A or D G of pers. & A of th.); name, call (2A, Ā refl. 2 N); reproach, censure, blame (A); w. punar repeat or reply. P. ucyáte be called, pass for (N). Caus. vācayati, te cause to say, speak etc. (2A); read, recite; agree, promise. Des vivakṣati, (te), PPP vivakṣita wish to say, speak, etc; P. be meant or in question. accha call near, salute, invite. adhi speak in favour of, intercede for (D). anu recite (prayers etc.) for (G or D), teach, communicate; Ā say after (the teacher) i.e. learn, study. Caus. cause to recite; read. abhyanu say with regard to something; describe in words. abhi = prec., also i.g. say, tell (2A). ā address, invoke. upa exhort, impel. nis speak out, explain, derive (g.); speak off i.e. drive away with words. pra tell forth, proclaim, praise, mention, teach, communicate to (D or G); declare to be, name (2A); betray, denounce, deliver, surrender. paripra scold, reproach. pratipra indicate, denounce. saṃpra declare (together), announce, indicate. prati announce, commend (Ā); answer, return (2A); refute. vi announce, proclaim, explain, decide; Ā contend for, quarrel about (L). sam proclaim, communicate; say (together) to (A prati ); Ā converse, talk together. Cf. ánukta, anūcāná, nirukta, prátyukta (sic!), prokta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vaj.html"> √ vaj    √ vaj, “be strong” Present etc I. vajati etc.etc Causative vājáyati etc. V.B.S. (vājayánt RV.; vājayádhyai RV.) Derivatives vā́ja V.+ ójas V.+ ójīyas V.B. ugrá V.+ -vājana S. oja- RV. ojmán V. vájra V.+ ójiṣṭha V.B. The verbal forms are really denominative, from vāja. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_va_jc.html"> √ vañc    √ vañc, “move crookedly” Present I. váñcati V.B.S., -te C1 Passive vacyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: vañciṣyati Periphrastic Future: vañcitā Aorist RAo: avavañcat -iṣ-Ao: avañcīt vacyāt Perfect vavañca vāvakre RV Causative vañcayati etc. U.+-te etc. E.+ (vañcyate E.+) Desiderative vivañciṣa- Intensive vanīvañc- avāvacīt ? RV Verbal Nouns 1 Abs: vañcitvā vacitvā vaktvā Derivatives vañcaka E.+ vaṅkú RV. vakrá AV.+ vañcayitṛ C. vañcana V.+ váṅkri V.+ vákva RV. vañcayitavya E.+ vañcanīya E.+ vákvan RV. It is hardly necessary to assume a different root-form vak for a part of these forms, since they are all such as sometimes show a guttural in place of a palatal of the root. Meanings váñcati v totter, go crookedly, sneak; P. vacyáte move to and fro (lit. & fig.), rock, roll, hurry along. Caus. vañcayati, te, PPP vañcita (q.v.) mislead, deceive, cheat of (I or Ab), escape. – accha roll or move towards (A). abhi Caus. deceive, cheat. ā P. roll or spring forth. upa Caus. & nis Ā deceive, cheat. pari sneak about; Caus. cheat. pra Caus. escape. sam totter. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_va_n_t.html"> √ vaṇṭ    √ vaṇṭ, “divide” Present etc I. vaṇṭati etc.etc Passive vaṇṭyate C The single occurrence is doubtless artificial. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vat.html"> √ vat    √ vat, “apprehend” Present I. vatema vátantas RV Aorist RAo: avīvatan V Causative vātáyati etc. RV Derivatives -vāta ? RV. Only with api. Meanings vátati v only w. api apprehend, understand; Caus. vātáyati reveal, inspire (devotion). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vad.html"> √ vad    √ vad, “speak” Present I. vádati -te etc. V.+ (vādata -deyus E.; udeyam AV.) Passive udyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: vadiṣyáti etc. AV.+,-te B Aorist RAo: avīvadat -iṣ-Ao: avādīt etc. V.+ (vā́diṣas AV., vadiṣma AB.), vadiṣṭhās B. (avādiran AV.) Precative: udyāsam etc. B.S. Ao/Ps/3/sg: avādi C Perfect ūdimá ūdus V.B., ūde etc. B.U Causative vādayati-te etc. B.+ (vādyate B.+,-ti E.) Desiderative vivadiṣati etc. B.S Intensive vā́vadīti etc. V.B.,-dyáte etc. B Verbal Nouns PPP: uditá V.+, vadita E.+; Inf: vaditum B.+, váditos B.S.; 1Abs: uditvā S.; 2Abs: -udya B.+;-úde ? AV Derivatives -vada V.+ vā́dya AV.+ vaditṛ B.+ vadmán RV. -vadya V.+ vádana B.+ vāditra U.S.+ -vadāvada B. -udya AV.+ vādana S.+ vadiṣu S. vadāvadin S. vāda V.+ -vādanīya S.+ -vadiṣṇu S. -vādayitṛ B.+ vādaka E.+ vaditavyà B.+ vadiṣṭha B. vavādiṣu C. vādin V.+ vāditavya E. vāduka B. Compare √ vand. Meanings vádati vádate v PPP uditá (q.v.) P speak, raise the voice (vācam), sing, sound (ucaís or bṛhát loud); speak or say to, relate, communicate, proclaim, announce (A abhi, G or L of pers. & A of th.), tell, teach, (2A); counsel, advice, foretell, predict; designate as, name, call (2A). Ā speak or say to (A); talk over, discuss; dispute or quarrel about, lay a claim to (L). Caus. vādáyati, te cause to speak or sound, esp. a musical instrument, play on (A or L), absol. make music; speak, recite. Des vivadiṣati wish to speak or say. Int vā́vadīti or vāvadyáte speak or sound loudly. accha P salute, invite. ati P speak louder or better, oversound, overspeak, defeat in disputing. anu repeat (words), imitate. ava revile, abuse, disapprove of; Caus. the same. abhi speak to, salute; say with regard to, mean by a word etc., express, utter, declare to be, call (2A). Caus. address, salute; *Ā greet a pers. (A) by means of another (A or I); make resound i.e. play on (A). pratyabhi P greet in return (also Caus. Ā). ava depreciate by words. vyava resume speaking. ā speak to, address, announce, proclaim. ud raise the voice, speak out. Caus. call or sound. pratyud Caus. make resound. nis & parā speak off, remove. pari express one's self about (A), esp. censure, blame. pra speak forth, say, proclaim, announce; raise the voice, utter sounds (of birds & beasts); suppose, state; declare to be, call (2A). Caus. make sound, play on a musical instrument. prati speak to (A), answer, return, repeat. vi Ā (P) contradict, dispute or quarrel with (I, r. A) about (L); Caus. commence an action or law-suit. sam P Ā say together; converse with (I) about (L); accord, agree; (be all right*); declare to be, call (2A). Caus. make speak or sound, cause to converse, cause a conversation about (L); consent, agree; describe accurately. visam break an agreement; Caus. not stick to, neglect, miss. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vadh.html"> √ vadh, badh    √ vadh, badh, “slay” Present I ? vadha ? vadheyam AV., vadhet VS Passive vadhyate etc. E.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: vadhiṣyati -te etc. E. + Aorist -iṣ-Ao: ávadhīt etc. V.+ (avadhīm vádhīm V.B.; vádhiṣas RV., badhīs TA.) vadhiṣṭhās; vadhiṣiṣṭa Precative: badhyāsam -sus AV.B.S., vadhyāt B. Ao/Ps/3/sg: avadhi C Causative vadhayati etc. E Derivatives vadhá , ba- V.+ vadhánā RV. -vadhyā E.+ vadhasná RV. vádhaka AV.+ vádhatra RV. -vadhra RV. vadhasnú V. vádhya , bá- AV.+ vádhar RV. vádhri ? V.+ Meanings (vadhati) P. vadhyate (ji) v strike, slay, kill, destroy. Caus. vadhayati = S. apa cut off, cleave; drive away. abhi & samabhi smite upon (A). ā crush down, dash to pieces. ud tear out or in pieces. upa strike on (A), slay, kill. ni fix or fasten in (L); knock down, kill. nis frustrate, annihilate. parā cleave, tear asunder. pra beat. vi destroy. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_van.html"> √ van, vā    √ van, vā, “win” Present I. vánati -te etc. V VI. vanā́ti vanéma V.B VIII. vanóti vanuté etc. V.B.S Future Simple Future: vaniṣyate S Periphrastic Future: vanitā Aorist √-Ao: vanta ? RV., váṃsva RV -s-Ao: váṃsat etc. RV., váṃsi (1s.) vaṃsate V.B., vaṃsīmahi vasīmahi RV -iṣ-Ao: vaniṣat AV., vaniṣanta TS. (vanuṣanta RV.), vaniṣīṣṭa RV -siṣ-Ao: vaṃsiṣīya ? AV Perfect vāvā́na vavanmá etc. vavné (vāvántha vāvánse vavandhí) RV Causative vānayantu AV Desiderative vívāsati -te etc. V Intensive vanīvan- (in d.) Verbal Nouns -vāta V.B., vanita E.+;-vantave RV Derivatives -van ? B.S. -vánana V. vanús RV. -vānyà B.S. vana V.U. vanánā RV. vantṛ́ RV. vāmá ? V.+ vanín RV. vananīya C. vánitṛ RV. vánīvan RV. -ványa B. vánas RV. vániṣṭha RV. vāvā́ta V.+ vanád ? RV. vaní V.B. vánīyas RV. vāvā́tṛ RV. vanú RV. vanayitṛ C. Meanings (vā) vanóti vanuté vánati (vanáti) vanótivanuté vánati (vanáte v PPP vāta 1 (– ṃ) & vanita (cf. vanitā) like, love; wish, desire, aim at; get, obtain, acquire, win, conquer, dispose of, possess, enjoy. Caus. vānayati & Des vívāsati, te (only – ṃ). abhi wish for, long or strive after. ā the same, Des wish to win or attract, entice, allure. abhyā Des approach (as an enemy). upa Des seek to win. pra win, conquer. sam Caus. make well-disposed. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vand.html"> √ vand    √ vand, “greet” Present I. vándate etc. V.+,-ti E Passive vandyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: vandiṣyate Periphrastic Future: vanditā Aorist √-Ao: vandi RV -iṣ-Ao: vandiṣīmáhi RV Perfect vavanda etc. V.B.,-dé etc. V.+ Causative vandayati etc. E Desiderative vivandiṣa- (in d.) Verbal Nouns PPP: vanditá RV.+; Inf: vanditum E.+; 1Abs: vanditvā E.+; 2Abs: -vandya E.+; vandádhyai RV Derivatives -vanda V. vandin C. vandanīya E.+ vanditavya E.+ vándya V.+ vándana V.+ vandā́ru V.+ vanditṛ V.B. vivandiṣu C. Doubtless the same with √ vad. Meanings vándate (vándati) v praise, honour, salute reverentially. Caus. vandayati the same. abhi = S., pari praise, extol. pra praise aloud or begin to praise. prati & sam honour, salute reverentially. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_vap.html"> √ 1 vap    √ 1 vap, “strew” Present I. vápati -te etc. V.+ (upet S.) Passive upyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: vapayáti etc. B.S.; vapiṣyati etc. E.+ Periphrastic Future: vaptā Aorist √-Ao: vāpi B RAo: avīvapat -s-Ao: avāpsīt etc. B.+ avapta Precative: upyāt Perfect uvāpa ūpús etc. V.+ (vavāpa E.), ūpe etc. RV Causative vāpayati etc. B.+ Desiderative vivapsa- Intensive vāvap- Verbal Nouns PPP: uptá V.+, upita E1., vapta E1.; 1Abs: uptvā E.+; 2Abs: -úpya V.+ Derivatives vapá B. -vāpaka E. vapanīya C. vaptavya C. vapā́ V.B.S. -vāpin C. vāpana C. vaptṛ E.+ -úpya B. vāpya B.+ vāpī E.+ vapra S.+ vāpa B.+ vápana AV.+ upti C. -vapiṣṭha B. -vāpayitṛ B. Compare the following root (√ 2 vap). Meanings vápati vápate v PPP uptá 2 (q.v.) strew, scatter, esp. seed, sow; throw or cast (dice etc.). Caus. vāpayati sow, plant. anu bestrew; scatter, disperse. apa disperse, destroy. api & abhi bestrew, cover. ā strew or throw upon, mix, mingle, pour out. Caus. mix, add, arrange, comb (the hair). ud draw out, dig up, raise; cast away. upa heap up, bestrew, inter, cover. ni heap up, raise, sow upon (L); throw down, cast (dice). nis throw or draw out, deal out (from a larger mass), distribute; present an oblation to a god, offer. Caus. scatter, sow, deal out. parā throw aside, remove. pari bestrew with (I). pra scatter, pour out, throw upon or in (L), bestrew. prati infix, insert; stick or set with (I); join, add. sam pour in, mingle. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_vap.html"> √ 2 vap    √ 2 vap, “shear” Present I. vapati -te etc. V.B.S Causative vāpayati etc. S.,-yīta S Verbal Nouns PPP: upta S.; 1Abs: uptvā S.; 2Abs: -upya S Derivatives vápana B.+ vāpa C. vāpana S.+ váptṛ V.B.S. Doubtless the same with the preceding root: √ 1 vap “scatter off from one”. Meanings vápati vápate v PPP upta 1 shear, shave (hair or beard, Ā refl.), trim (nails); shear fig. = crop off, graze. Caus. vāpayati, te cause to shear or to be shorn (Ā refl.). pari shear around. pra shear off. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vam.html"> √ vam    √ vam, “vomit” Present I. vamati etc. E.+ II. vámiti vamanti etc. V.+ (avamīt V.B., avamat B.+) Future Simple Future: vamiṣyati Periphrastic Future: vamitā Aorist RAo: avīvamat -s-Ao: avān KB -iṣ-Ao: avamīt Ao/Ps/3/sg: avāmi Perfect vavāma E.+, vemus C. vavamus (uvāma ŚB.) Causative vāmayati etc. C.; vamayati etc. C Desiderative vivamiṣa- Intensive vaṃvam- Verbal Nouns PPP: vāṃtá B.+; 1Abs: vamitvā C Derivatives vami C. vamana C. vamitavya C. vamrá ? V.B. vāmin B.+ vāmanīya C. vamathu C. Meanings vámiti & vamati v PPP vānta (q.v.) vomit, spit out, give forth (vácas repent). Caus. vāmayati & vamayati cause to vomit. abhi spit at. ud & nis spit out, eject. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_val.html"> √ val    √ val, “turn” Present I. valati -te etc. C Future Simple Future: valiṣyati Periphrastic Future: valitā Aorist RAo: avīvalat -iṣ-Ao: avaliṣṭa Perfect vavale C Causative valayati C Verbal Nouns PPP: valitá C.; valitvā C Derivatives valana C. vali ? E.+ valaya E.+ Evidently a secondary root-form, probably from √ 1 vṛ, through some derivative. Meanings valati valate v PPP valitá (q.v.) turn (intrans.), return; break forth, appear. Caus. valayati or vālayati cause to turn or roll. vi turn away. Cf. saṃvalita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_valg.html"> √ valg    √ valg, “spring” Present I. válgati etc. AV.+,-te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: valgiṣyati Periphrastic Future: valgitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: avalgīt Perfect vavalga etc. E Causative valgayati S Verbal Nouns valgita E.+ Derivatives valgā E.+ -valgin C. valgana C. valgú V.+ Meanings válgati válgate v PPP valgita (q.v.) spring, jump (esp. with joy). abhi spring near or towards, boil up (water). ( ava leap, bound*.) ā move quickly, jump, spring. vyā gallop, leap, move hither and thither. pra & vi leap, spring. sam begin to undulate or boil up. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_valh.html"> √ valh    √ valh, “challenge” Present I. valhati -te etc. B.S Verbal Nouns valhita C.;-valhya B. Derivatives -valha B.S. -valhaka B.S. Meanings válhati válhate v challenge. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vaz.html"> √ vaś    √ vaś, “be eager” Present I. váśanti ávaśat RV., vaśa -śet AV. ? II. váṣṭi uśánti etc. V.+ (śmasi RV., vaṣṭa SV.) III. vavákṣi vivaṣṭi RV., vivaṣṭu SV VI. uśámāna RV1 Passive uśyate Future etc Simple Future: vaśiṣyati Periphrastic Future: vaśitā; uśita Aorist RAo: avīvaśat -iṣ-Ao: vaśīs E. avāśīt Precative: uśyāt Perfect vāvaśús -śe -śāná RV. uvāśa ūśus Causative vaśayati C.; vāśitā́ ? AV.+ Desiderative vivaśiṣa- Intensive vāvaś- Derivatives váśa V.+ uśánā ,-nas V.+ vaśí B. váṣṭi RV. uśá- ? RV. uśénya RV. uśī- ? V.+ vaśitṛ C. uśíj V.B.S. váśīyas ? AV. Meanings váṣṭi vivaṣṭi vaváṣṭi váśati v be eager, will, desire, long for, order, command; aver, declare to be (2A). Caus. vaśayati subdue. abhi rule over, command; strive after, Ā long for (A). Cf. uśánt, uśámāna (add.), vāvaśāná. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_vas.html"> √ 1 vas, uṣ, uch    √ 1 vas, uṣ, uch, “shine” Present II. vaste ? ŚB1 VI. ucháti etc. V.B.S Future Simple Future: avatsyat ŚB Aorist √-Ao: avasran RV -s-Ao: avāt ? AV Perfect uvā́sa ūṣús etc. V.B Causative vāsáyati etc. V.B Verbal Nouns PPP: uṣṭá V.+, uṣita S.E.; vástave RV.;-úṣi V.B Derivatives úṣ V.B. -uṣṭi V.+ vásīyas B.S. -vāsa AV.S. uṣā́ RV. vástu V.B. vásyas V.B.U. -vāsana C. -ūṣa E.+ vastṛ́ RV. usrá V.+ vāsará RV. uṣar- , usṛ́ RV. vásu V.+ úsri RV. vivásvan RV. uṣás V.+ vásiṣṭha V.+ vivasvant V.+ Meanings uccháti v PPP uṣṭá 2 (– ṃ) shine, light up, dawn; bring or drive away (dūré) by shining. Caus. vāsayati cause to shine. apa = S. + dūré, extinguish. vi shine abroad, light up. Caus. cause to dawn or grow bright. Cf. vyúṣṭa, vyuṣita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_vas.html"> √ 2 vas    √ 2 vas, “clothe” Present II. váste vásate vásāna etc. V.+ (vásiṣva RV., uṣāṇá RV1., vaddhvam S.) VI. uṣámāṇa RV1 Future Simple Future: vasiṣyate; vatsyati C1 Periphrastic Future: vasitā Aorist RAo: avīvasat -iṣ-Ao: avasiṣṭa etc. RV Perfect vavase C., vāvase -sāná RV Causative vāsáyati etc. V.+,-te RV. (vāsyate E.) Desiderative vivasiṣa- Intensive vāvas- Verbal Nouns PPP: vasita E.; Inf: vasitum E.+; 1Abs: vasitvā C.; 2Abs: -vasya E Derivatives -vas C. vāsin B.+ vasantá ? V.+ vástra V.+ vasa- RV. vásana V.+ vasitavya E. vásman RV. vásya B.S. vā́sana AV.+ vasitṛ C. -vāsa V.+ vā́sas V.+ vastṛ S. Meanings váste 3 v put on, don, enter, assume (an appearance). Caus. clothe, dress in, cover with (I), Ā refl. adhi put on. anu clothe, cover (Ā refl.), surround, protect. abhi cover one's self with (A). Caus. clothe or cover with (I). ni put on (over another garment). pari , pra , prati don. vi change clothes, also = Caus. put on, don. sam dress one's self in (I). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_3_vas.html"> √ 3 vas    √ 3 vas, “dwell” Present I. vásati etc. V.+,-te etc. B.+ Passive uṣyate C Future Simple Future: vatsyati etc. B.+,-te etc. E.+; vasiṣyati etc. E Periphrastic Future: vastā Aorist √-Ao: vásāna ? V.B.S. RAo: avīvasat MS -s-Ao: avātsīt etc. AV.+ (avāksam AB., avāstam U.) Precative: uṣyāt Ao/Ps/3/sg: avāsi Perfect uvāsa ūṣus etc. V.+;-vāsāṃ cakre U Causative vāsáyati etc. V.+,-te etc. AV.+ (vāsyáte etc. B.+,-yant E.;-vā́sas TA.) Desiderative vivatsati ŚB Intensive vāvas- Verbal Nouns PPP: uṣita S.+, uṣṭa E., vasita C.; Inf: vastum E.+,-tavai S., vasitum C.; 1Abs: uṣitvā́ B.+, uṣṭvā E.+; 2Abs: -úṣya B.+;-vāsam C Derivatives vás RV. vāsin AV.+ vāsas U. vā́stu V.+ -vasa E.+ vā́sya B.+ -vasu ? V. vástṛ B. -uṣaka C. vásana V.+ vasatí V.+ -vasatha V.B.S. -uṣya V.+ -uṣaṇa C. vastu E.+ vásman RV. vāsá V.+ vāsana S.+ vastavyà B.+ vāsayitavya E. -vāsaka E.+ -vāsanīya E.+ uṣitavya C. vāsayitṛ E.+ A few vas-forms, occurring in RV. in questionable connection, are referred in BR. to a root √ 4 vas “aim”. The causative forms ascribed by BR. to a root √ 5 vas “cut off” are also doubtless peculiar technical specializations from √ 3 vas. Meanings vásati vásate v PPP uṣita4 q.v. (& uṣṭa) stay in a place, esp. over night (rātrim), dwell, live, rest on (eye) or in (L); w. dūratas keep away; w. sukham be at ease or comfortable. Caus. vāsáyati, te cause to stay (over night), lodge; confine in (L), stop, detain, keep, support. adhi settle upon, occupy, inhabit. anu remove to a place after another person (A); dwell, inhabit; pass, spend (time). ā settle or enter upon (A), dwell or live in (L); cohabit with (A); w. gurostalpam commit adultery with the teacher's wife. Caus. harbour, lodge; take up one's abode in (A); stop, stay, esp. over night. adhyā choose as abode, inhabit (A), dwell or live in (L) enter upon, attend to (A). samā stop, stay (esp. over night); settle in, inhabit (A). Caus. make a halt, settle down. ud Caus. remove from its place (esp. the fire from the altar agnim), sever, cut off (a head), root out (trees), ravage, lay waste. upa abide, stay, wait, esp. with eating i.e. fast; enter upon, attend to (A). Caus. cause to stay (over night) or fast. ni dwell (of men & beasts), live in (L), inhabit, occupy, keep; incur, undergo; have sexual intercourse with (A). Caus. cause to stay, receive in one's house, lodge; make inhabitable, populate; inhabit. saṃni live with (I) in (L). nis finish (w. vāsam); Caus. expel from home, banish, send away, dismiss. pari stay (over night), live with (I); Caus. keep over night. pra set out, go abroad (for a night); depart, disappear, be gone; stay or dwell in (L); also = Caus. banish, exile. vipra go or be abroad. Caus. banish, remove. prati (stay over night*); have one's dwelling. vi change one's abode, go away from (Ab); pass, spend (time) Caus. drive away (from home or land), banish, exile, dismiss. sam dwell together, live with (I saha or A), cohabit with (A); stay or live in (L); pass, spend (A of time). Caus. cause to live together, bring together with (I saha), give shelter, harbour. Cf. adhyuṣita, abhyuṣita, upoṣita, paryuṣita, proṣita, viproṣita, vyuṣita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vah.html"> √ vah    √ vah, “carry” Present I. váhati -te etc. V.+ II. vákṣi voḍham -ḍhā́m uhīta vákṣva voḍhvam ūḍvam úhāna V.B Passive uhyáte etc. V.+,-yant E.+ Future Simple Future: vakṣyáti etc. AV.+,-te E.; vahiṣyati etc. E.+ Periphrastic Future: voḍhā́ B Aorist RAo: avīvahat -s-Ao: ávākṣīt etc. V.B.S. (ávāṭ vāṭ V.B.S., vákṣat etc. V.B.S., vákṣati etc. V.) avakṣi Precative: uhyāt S Ao/Ps/3/sg: avāhi C. Perfect uvāha ūhús etc. V.+, ūhé etc. V. (vavāha vavāhatus E.+) Causative vāhayati etc. B.+,-te etc. E.+ (vāhyate etc. E.+) Desiderative vivakṣa- Intensive vāvahīti C., vanīvāhyáte etc. B.S Verbal Nouns PPP: ūḍhá V.+, voḍha ? E1.; Inf: vóḍhum V.+,-ḍhave V.B.S.,-ḍhavaí B.; ūḍhvā́ B.; 2Abs: -úhya AV.+; vā́he RV.; váhadhyai RV Derivatives -vā̆h V.+ vāhya S.+ voḍhavya E.+ váhīyas V.B. váha AV.+ vahana S.+ -vāhitavya E. váhni V.+ vahín B.S. vā́hana V.+ voḍhṛ V.+ -váhman RV. vahyá V.S. vāhanīya C. vāhitṛ E. vákṣas ? V. ogha U.+ vahát RV. -vahitṛ U. vakṣáṇa ? V. aughá B. vāghát ? RV. vahitra C. vakṣī́ ? RV. vāhá V.+ vā́has V.B.S. váhiṣṭha V. vā́vahi RV. vāhaka E.+ ūḍhi B.+ vā́hiṣṭha V.B. vivadhá ? B.+ vāhín AV.+ vahatú V.B. -vāhayitṛ C. Compare root √ 1 ūh, √ 2 ūh. Meanings váhati váhate v PPP ūḍhá 1 (q.v.) conduct, carry (esp. the oblation), draw (waggon), guide (the horses); bring near, procure, cause, effect; offer, present (a sacrifice); carry off, rob; take to wife, marry; bear, support, feel, suffer; indulge, pardon; wear, have; undergo, incur; pass. spend; intrans. travel, go (in or by any vehicle), drive, ride, run, swim, flow, blow (wind), pass away (time); P. uhyáta be conducted etc., be borne along, move, go in or by (I). Caus. vāhayati, te cause to conduct, draw, or carry; guide, drive (cf. S.), ride on (A); step upon or travel over (a way); set to work, use, apply; take in, deceive. Int vanīvāhyáte carry hither and thither. ati carry over or across, pass by; spend (time). Caus. transport, transpose, let pass i.e. spend (time), escape (a foe etc.). anu carry along. apa carry or drive away (also Caus. ); take off, remove, give up. abhi convey near or towards, bring. ā the same, also bear (fig.), lead home i.e. take to wife; carry or drive away; intrans. flow. Caus. call near, invite (esp. gods to a sacrifice). anvā & abhyā bring hither or to. udā & samudā lead away, esp. lead out a bride from her father's house, i.e. marry. samā bring hither or to (together), assemble; Ā meet. ud & samud lead up or away; raise, elevate; draw out, extract; marry (cf. udā); lead or bring to, offer, present; bear, carry (lit. & fig.); have, possess, enjoy; endure, suffer; manifest, betray. ud Caus. (cause to) marry. upa lead or bring near, get, procure, cause, effect; betray into (A). samupa carry along, let flow; P. approach, begin, rise. ni lead down or towards (D or L); bear, support. nis lead out, extract, save from (Ab); carry off, remove; bring about, effect; succeed (of pers. & th.). Caus. pass, spend (time); bring about, perform, accomplish. parā lead or take to (D). pari lead about, esp. the bride or the wedding procession, i.e. wed; intrans. flow about. pra trans. carry onward or along, lead or bring to (A); intrans. be borne along, flow, blow. Caus. set in motion, send away, dismiss. prati conduct towards or near. vi lead away, marry (cf. udā), form a matrimonial alliance with (I); Ā get married, celebrate a wedding. Caus. give in marriage or marry. sam carry (together), conduct, lead, draw, drag, bear along; P. ride on (I). Caus. bring together, assemble, collect; drive (carriage etc.), guide, conduct, lead, take to wife; carry the hand along the body, stroke. Cf. apoḍha, udūḍha, upoḍha, óḍha, vyūḍha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_vaa.html"> √ 1 vā    √ 1 vā, “blow” Present II. vā́ti etc. V.+ IV. vā́yati etc. V.+,-te etc. E Future Simple Future: vāsyati etc. C Aorist -siṣ-Ao ? avāsīt B Perfect vavau etc. B.+ Causative vāpáyati etc. V.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: vāta S., vāna C.; Inf: vātum C Derivatives -vā AV.B. vā́ta V.+ -vāpaka C. -vāpayitṛ C. -vāna E.+ vāyú V.+ -vāpana C. -vāpayitavya C. -vāyyà AV. The forms from pres.-stem vāya have mostly the sense “be blown or ex-hausted”, and are generally referred to a different root, √ 2 vā. The two, however, seem evidently only two sides of the same original root, nor are the forms capable of being clearly devided between them. Meanings vā́ti vā́yati vā́ti vā́yate v PPP vātá 3 & vāna (– ṃ) blow, blow near or towards (trans. & intrans.), spread (intrans. of odours), smell. anu blow towards or after (A), inflame, rouse. abhi & ā blow towards or hither. ava blow down. upa cease to blow, be extinguished. nis blow, also = prec. Caus. nirvāpayati extinguish, allay, refresh, delight. parā blow away. pra blow, be exhaled or spread (odour). vi blow asunder or through. sam blow. Cf. nirvāṇa, pravātá. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_vaa.html"> √ 2 vā, vi, u    √ 2 vā, vi, u, “weave” Present IV. váyati etc. V.+,-te etc. B.+ Passive ūyate etc. B.S Future Simple Future: vayiṣyáti RV.-te; vāsyati Periphrastic Future: vātā Aorist -s-Ao: avāsta, vāsīṣṭa -siṣ-Ao: avāsīt Precative: ūyāt Perfect ūvus RV. vavau etc., uvāya ūyus etc Causative vāyaya- Desiderative vivāsa- Intensive vāvā- Verbal Nouns PPP: utá V.+, ūta S.; Inf: ótum RV., ótave RV., ótavaí V., vā́tave AV Derivatives -vāya RV.C. vāna S.+ ótu V.B. veṇī ? S.+ vāyaka C. vayúna ? V.+ -vātavya C. vema E. -vayana B.S. ūti ? C. vayitṛ B. véman B.+ Meanings váyati váyate v PPP utá 2 or ūta weave, interweave, plait, fig. = compose (hymns etc.). ā weave or lay in, interweave; also = samā Ā string upon (L). ud bind up, suspend. pari interweave; tie round, fetter, ensnare. pra weave or tie to (L). vi plait, twist, weave. sam weave together, interweave, inlay or adorn with (I). Cf. óta, prota, vyúta, vyūta, samutá. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_3_vaa.html"> √ 3 vā (in vivāsa-)    √ 3 vā (in vivāsa-) see √ van. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vaa_jch.html"> √ vāñch    √ vāñch, “desire” Present I. vāñchati etc. V.+ Passive vāñchyate etc. C Future Simple Future: vāñchiṣyati Periphrastic Future: vāñchitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: avāñchīt Perfect vavāñcha Causative vāñchayati E Verbal Nouns PPP: vāñchita E.+ Derivatives vāñchā C. Meanings vā́ñchati v PPP vāñchita (q.v.) desire, wish. abhi , samabhi, sam & abhisam = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vaaz.html"> √ vāś    √ vāś, “bellow” Present I. vā́śati etc. RV.E.+,-te etc. E.+ IV. vā́śyate etc. AV.+,-ti E Passive vāśyate C Future vāśiṣyate, vāśitā Aorist RAo: avīvaśat etc. ávīvaśanta RV. avavāśat -iṣ-Ao: avāśiṣṭhās B Perfect vavāśe etc. V.+ (vāvaśre -śāná avāvaśītam ávāvaśanta etc. RV.) Causative vāśayati etc. V.S Desiderative vivāśiṣa- Intensive vā́vaśat RV.; vāvāśyate E Verbal Nouns PPP: vāśita E.+; 1Abs: vāśitvā C.; 2Abs: -vāśya C Derivatives vaśā́ ? V.+ vāśaka C. -vāśya S. vāśrá V.+ vāśá V.S. vāśin E.+ vāśana C. Meanings vā́śati vā́śate vā́śyate vā́śati vā́śate vā́śyati v PPP vāśita (q.v.) bleat, low, roar, cry (of birds). Caus. vāśayati, te cause to bleat etc; Ā sound loudly. Int vāvaśyate howl, croak, sound loudly. anu & pratyanu low after or in return. abhi bleat or bellow at (A). prati the same. sam (also Int) bleak etc. (together). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vaah.html"> √ vāh    √ vāh, “press” Present I. vāhate etc. C Future Simple Future: vāhiṣyate Periphrastic Future: vāhitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: avāhiṣṭa Perfect vavāhe Causative vāhayati C Meanings vāhate 2 v press, urge. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_vic.html"> √ 1 vic    √ 1 vic, “sift” Present III. vivekṣi RV1 VII. vinákti etc. V.+ Passive vicyáte etc. AV.+ Future Simple Future: vekṣyati C Periphrastic Future: vektā Aorist RAo: avīvicat -iṣ-Ao: avaikṣīt Perfect viveca ? AV. (vivikvā́ṃs RV.) Causative vecayati etc. C Intensive vevekti S Verbal Nouns PPP: vikta B.+; Inf: vektum E.; 2Abs: -vicya S.+;-vecam S Derivatives -veka U.+ -vecaka C. -vikti B.+ -vektṛ C. -vekin C. -vecana E.+ -vektavya C. vívici V.B.S. -vekya C. Meanings vinákti v (vivekti), PPP vikta separate, esp. grain from chaff by winnowing, i.g. sift, sever from (Ab), try, examine. apa sever, separate (= S.). vi separate by tossing or blowing, i.g. sift; sever from (Ab); examine, try, distinguish, decide (a question). Caus. vivecayati = pravi separate, try, examine Cf. pravivikta, vivikta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_vic.html"> √ 2 vic    √ 2 vic see √ vyac. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vij.html"> √ vij    √ vij, “tremble” Present I. vejate E VI. vijáte etc. V.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: vijiṣyati E., vejiṣyati C Periphrastic Future: vijitā Aorist √-Ao (or -s-Ao?). vikthās V.B., cikta RV RAo: vīvijas RV -iṣ-Ao: avijiṣṭa Perfect vivije etc. V.+ Causative vejayati etc. B.+,-te E Desiderative vivijiṣa- Intensive vevijyáte RV., vévijāna RV Verbal Nouns PPP: vikta RV., vigna E.+ Inf: vijitum Derivatives víj RV. -vejaka C. -vejana C. vevijá RV. véga V.+ -vejin C. vigrá ? RV. vijitavya C. Meanings vijáte 1 v (ti & vejate), PPP vigna (vikta) dart up or back (intrans.), tremble, flee from (Ab). Caus. vejayati dart (trans.), frighten, agitate; strengthen, increase. Int vévijyate start up at (D), flee from (Ab). ud start up, take a fright, be afraid of (Ab, G, or I); get tired of or disgusted with, desist from (Ab). Caus. terrify, frighten, vex, annoy, harass. samud start for fear, take fright. pra rush away. vi Caus. frighten. sam start up, run away, fall asunder. Cf. āvigna, udvigna, právikta, vivigna, saṃvigna, samāvigna, samudvigna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_vid.html"> √ 1 vid    √ 1 vid, “know” Present I. veda E., vedate U II. vetti vidánti etc. V.+, vidmahe B.+ (avidus B.,-dan C.; vidāṃ karotu etc. C.) VI. vidáti -te etc. AV.U.E.+; vindati -te etc. E.+ Passive vidyate C Future Simple Future: vediṣyati -te etc. B.U. (avediṣyat U.); vetsyati -te etc. E.+ Periphrastic Future: veditā́ ŚB., vettā E Aorist RAo: avīvidat -s-Ao: avait ? C -iṣ-Ao: avedīt etc. B.+ vidām akran B Ao/Ps/3/sg: avedi Perfect véda vidús etc. V.+, vidre RV.; viveda etc. C. vidā́ṃ cakāra etc. B.U.S Causative vedáyate-ti etc. V.+ (vedyate etc. E.+; vivedayiṣa- in d.) Desiderative vividiṣati etc. B.+, vivitsati etc. C Intensive vevid- Verbal Nouns PPP: viditá AV.+; Inf: véditum B.+,-tos B., vettum E.; 1Abs: viditvā́ B.+ Derivatives víd V.+ vedana B.+ veditavyà B.+ vivitsā E.+ -vida B.+ vedanīya E.+ vidátha V.B. vivitsu E.+ véda V.+ -vedi B. vidyā́ V.+ vividiṣā C. vedaka E.+ vidú(s ?) RV. vidmán V. vividiṣu C. vedin B.+ vitti C. vidura E.+ vedayitṛ C. védya V.+ vettṛ U.+ vidván AV. vivedayiṣu E. vedyā́ RV.C. véditṛ V.+ vidvalá V. See √ 2 vid. Meanings vetti 1 v (veda), PPP viditá or vitta (q.v.) know, understand, learn, perceive, experience, feel; think or be mindful of (A or G), know how to (Inf); believe, suppose, know or recognize as, declare to be, take for, call, name (2A or A & N w. iti). Caus. vedáyate, ti make known, announce, report; inform of, teach (2A); take for, learn or know – to be (2A); perceive, notice, experience, feel. Des vividiṣati wish to know, inquire after (A). anu know thoroughly (lit. along). ā know well or exactly. Caus. address, invite, announce, proclaim, prescribe, inform; offer, present. ni Caus. cause to know, announce, report, communicate to (D, G, or L); name, call (2A), offer, present, surrender (ātmānam refl.). vini & saṃni Caus. make known, announce, report, offer, present, surrender. pari know very well. pra know. Caus. make known, announce, relate. prati understand, know. Caus. make known, announce, tell; acquaint with (2A); offer, entrust, commit. vi discern, know. sam know or understand (together); consent, agree. Caus. cause to know, inform, instruct; make known, communicate. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_vid.html"> √ 2 vid    √ 2 vid, “find” Present II. vitté etc. V.B. (vidé 3s. V.B., vidré V.B., vidām3s. AV.B., vidāná V.B., vídāna V.); vindate (3p. E., vindyāt ? C VI. vindáti -te etc. V.+ Passive vidyáte etc. V.+,-ti etc. E Future Simple Future: vetsyati -te etc. B.+ vediṣayti Periphrastic Future: vettā Aorist Th Ao: ávidat -data etc. V.B.S. (vidā́si etc. vidā́t etc. vidét -deta etc. V.B.S., videṣṭa AV.) RAo: avīvidat -s-Ao: avitsi V.B Ao/Ps/3/sg: avedi védi RV Perfect vivéda vividus etc. V.+ (vivéditha RV., vividat RV.), vividé etc. V.B.S Causative vedayati etc. E Desiderative vivitsati etc. B.+ Intensive vévidat -dāna etc. RV Verbal Nouns PPP: vittá V.+, vinna AV.+; Inf: vettum E., véttave AV.,-tavai ? TB.,-tos JB.; 1Abs: vittvā́ AV.B.; 2Abs: -vídya B.+; vidé RV Derivatives -vid V.+ vedya B.+ vitti AV.+ vidā́yya RV. -vídya V. védana V.+ -vettavya C. -vinda B.+ -véda V.+ -vedanīya C. -vettṛ E.+ -vindu V.B. -vedaka C. védas V.+ védiṣṭha RV. -vindaka C. -vedin C. véduka B. védīyas RV. -vivitsu ? E. Doubtless originally the same with the preceding root, √ 1 vid. In some of their meanings, the two are so close together as hardly to be separable; and there are instances, from the Veda down, of exchanges of form between them. Meanings vindáti vindáte 3 v (vitté), PPP vittá & vinna (q.v.) find, meet with, get, obtain; visit, befall; have, possess; find out for, procure (D); look for, turn to (A); Ā (P) take to wife (bhāryām), find a husband, marry; bring forth (sutam). P.Ā be found, be there (impers.), exist. vidyáte (ti) there is (esp. w. na), yáthā vidé as it is, i.e. as usual or as well as possible. Des vivitsati wish to find. Int vévidat, vévidāna be present. adhi supersede, supplant. anu find (after), get, obtain, take hold of; Ā bhāryām take to wife. P. be found, exist. abhi find, find out, know. ā get hold of, get at, acquire, incur, undergo. P. be, exist. nis divide from (Ab); Ā get rid of (G), take off (A); P. become depressed or dispirited, get weary of or disgusted with (Ab, I, r. A). pari P. be married with the younger brother before the elder has married. sam Ā find, get hold of, acquire, win. P. be found, be there (esp. w. na), exist, belong to (G). Cf. adhivinna, ánuvitta, nirviṇa, parivitta, parivinna, vidāna, saṃvidāná. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_vidh.html"> √ 1 vidh    √ 1 vidh, “worship” Present VI. vidháti etc. V.B.U.C.,-te etc. RV Derivatives vedhás V.+ Meanings vidháti 1 v (te) serve a god (D); worship, honour with (I); offer, consecrate (A); be gracious or friendly (of a god). upa worship, do homage. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_vidh.html"> √ 2 vidh    √ 2 vidh see √ vyadh. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vindh.html"> √ vindh    √ vindh, “lack” Present VI. vindháte etc. RV Derivatives vidhú V.+ vidháva V.+ vidhura E.+ A body of forms of not unquestionable connection. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vip.html"> √ vip, vep    √ vip, vep, “tremble” Present I. vépate etc. V.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: vepiṣyate Periphrastic Future: vepitā Aorist √-Ao: vipāná RV RAo: avīvipat etc. RV -iṣ-Ao: avepiṣṭa etc. B.S Perfect vivipre RV., vepus ? C. vivepe Causative vepáyati etc. V.+; vipáyanti RV Derivatives víp V. vépa V.+ vepaná V.+ vepáthu AV.+ vipana- ? RV. -vepin C. vépas RV. vépiṣṭha RV. vipas- V.+ vípra V.+ Meanings vépate 1 v (ti) tremble, quake, vibrate; Caus. vepayati shake, agitate. ud tremble, take fright. Caus. frighten. pari tremble. pra the same. Caus. shake, agitate. vi tremble, throb. sam tremble, quake. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_viz.html"> √ viś    √ viś, “enter” Present VI. viśáti -te etc. V.+ Passive viśyate etc. C Future Simple Future: vekṣyati etc. B.+,-te etc. E Periphrastic Future: veṣṭā M Aorist √-Ao: áviśran RV. RAo: avīviśat C -s-Ao: ávikṣmahi etc. RV -iṣ-Ao: veśīt RV -sa- Ao: avikṣat -ṣan B.C. avikṣata Precative: viśyāt Ao/Ps/3/sg: aceśi C Perfect vivéśa viviśe etc. V.+ (vivéśitha RV., viveśus RV., viveśatus C.,-viśivā́ṃs AV., viviśyās V., áviveśīs RV.) Causative veśáyati etc. V.+,-te etc. AV.+ (veśayte etc. S.+) Desiderative vivikṣati etc. E.+ Intensive veviś- Verbal Nouns PPP: viṣṭá V.+; Inf: veṣṭum E.+,-ṭavai B.; 2Abs: -víśya AV.+; víśam RV Derivatives víś V.+ -veśaka C. véśana V.+ veṣṭavya E.+ -viśa B.+ veśin S.+ -veśanīya C. -veṣṭṛ C. veśá V.+ veśyà V.+ veśanta V.B. véśman V.+ veśī́ RV. viśana E.+ veśás AV. vivikṣu E.+ -viṣṭi S. -veśayitavya C. Meanings viśáti viśáte v PPP viṣṭá 1 (q.v.) enter, go in or into, sit or settle down on (A or L); go home or to rest, set (of the sun); get into a condition, undertake, begin (A); deal with (I), fall to the lot of, occur or happen to (A). Caus. veśáyati cause to enter (A) or sit down upon (L). Des vivikṣati wish to enter (A). anu follow, enter (acc); follow a person (A) into (A). ā enter, pervade, settle down on or among (A, r. L); inire (A); approach, get at, take possession of (A); get into a state or condition (A). Caus. cause to enter, put into (L, r. A), turn or set upon, entrust or commit to (L). anvā enter, take possession of (A); follow, conform one's self to (A). abhyā enter, penetrate (A or L). upā the same, get into; visit, befall (A). prā come to (A); Caus. lead in, introduce. samā enter, penetrate, pervade (A), sit or settle down on (L or A); visit, befall (A); get into a condition (A); devote one's self to (A). Caus. lead or put into (A), turn upon (L), commit, entrust (L). upa approach (A); stop, sit or settle down, set (sun); cohabit (I); attend or apply one's self to (A). Caus. cause to sit down on, put in (L). upopa sit down beside each other or at a person's (A) side. paryupa sit around. samupa sit down or be seated (together). ni Ā (P) enter, penetrate, pervade (A or L); bite (of a leech); sit or settle down on (L), resort, turn, or attend to (A or L); establish one's self i.e. marry (man); stop, make a halt, come to rest, cease. Caus. cause to enter, cause to sit or settle down on (L); bring to rest; cause (a man) to marry, draw up or encamp (an army); lead, bring, put, transfer into (L); build, found, populate, make inhabitable (town etc.), throw or hurl upon, fix in, put on, turn or direct to (L), don (clothes); appoint to (L), confer upon (L). With citre paint, w. pattre write down, w. citte or hṛdaye call to mind. abhini Ā (P) enter or penetrate into, insist or be bent upon (A); belong to (L). Caus. lead into, turn or direct to, place or fix upon (L). upani Caus. encamp (an army), found (a city). pariṇi settle down around. vini put, place, fix, turn (L), appoint to, set about (L). saṃni Caus. lead into (a house), lodge, set or lay down, draw up (an army); place, put, fix in or on, hurl upon (L); build, found; appoint to (L), load or confer upon (L). nis enter (A or L, gṛheṣu become a householder, marry); pay back, restore; enjoy, delight in (A). pra enter, get into (A or L); pierce, penetrate; reach, attain (A), enjoy carnally (A); attend to, be bent upon (A, r. L); enter, make one's appearance (d.). Caus. cause to enter, lead in, introduce (L or A); lead home, marry; lay down, place, put etc. in (L or A); appoint, install; initiate into (A); write down. anupra enter (after another), get into or among (A, r. L), resort to (A). saṃpra enter, go in, inire, take to, deal with (A). Caus. cause to enter, bring or lead into (A). sam come near, approach; join (A or I); enter, go into (A, r. L), settle down, go to rest; lie or sleep with (I saha, D, or A), lie on or in (L). Caus. cause to lie down, set, place, put etc. on or in, bring into or to (L). anusam go to rest after (A). abhisam assemble around (A). Cf. anupraviṣṭa, abhiniviṣṭa, abhiviṣṭa, āviṣṭa, upaviṣṭa, nirviṣṭa, níviṣṭa, práviṣṭa, viniviṣṭa, saṃniviṣṭa, samāviṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vi_s.html"> √ viṣ    √ viṣ, “be active” Present I. véṣati etc. RV.E III. viveṣṭi etc. RV. (vivés víveṣas etc. RV.) Passive viṣyate B.+ Future Simple Future: vekṣyati -te etc. B.+ Periphrastic Future: veṣṭā Aorist √-Ao ? viḍḍhí AV.B.S Th Ao: aviṣat -iṣ-Ao: veṣiṣas RV -sa- Ao: avikṣat Perfect viveṣa viviṣus RV. (aviveṣīs RV.) Causative veṣayati etc. E.+ Desiderative vivikṣa- (in d.) Intensive véveṣṭi etc. V.B., véviṣāṇa RV., veviṣyate JUB Verbal Nouns PPP: viṣṭá V.+; viṣṭvī́ RV.; 2Abs: -víṣya AV.B.;-víṣe RV Derivatives -viṣ ? RV. veṣá AV.+ véṣaṇa V.+ -veṣṭavya C. víṣa V.+ -veṣaka E.+ veṣáṇa RV. -veṣṭṛ AV.+ viṣá ? V.+ -veṣin C. viṣaya ? E.+ víṣṇu ? V.+ -veṣya AV.B.S. viṣṭí V.+ -vivikṣu E. Divided by Grassmann into two roots. Meanings viveṣṭi 1 v & véṣati, Int véveṣti, PPP viṣṭá stir, bustle, work, be active, not rest (waters); serve, attend; accomplish, finish (food i.e. eat up), overcome, conquer. Caus. veṣayati clothe, dress. upa serve, attend. pari the same, dress (food); P. have a halo (sun or moon). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vi_s_t.html"> √ viṣṭ, veṣṭ    √ viṣṭ, veṣṭ, “wrap” Present I. veṣṭate etc. AV.+ Future Simple Future: veṣṭiṣyate Periphrastic Future: veṣṭitā Aorist RAo: aviveṣṭat avaveṣṭat -iṣ-Ao: aveṣṭiṣṭa Perfect viveṣṭe Causative veṣṭáyati etc. AV.+,-te etc. B.+ (veṣṭyate etc. B.+) Desiderative viveṣṭiṣa- Intensive veveṣṭ- Verbal Nouns PPP: viṣṭita V.B Derivatives veṣṭa S.+ veṣṭana S.+ -veṣṭitṛ U. veṣṭaka S.+ -veṣṭanīya C. Meanings véṣṭate v wind around (intrans.), cling or stick to (L). Caus. veṣṭáyati, te, PPP veṣṭitá wind or tie round; wrap, envelop, cover, enclose, surround. anu Caus. wrap, cover; spread. apa Caus. strip off. abhi wrap, cover. ā spread or expand over (L); Caus. wrap, cover, clothe; twist (a string); enclose, confine. ud unwind, unfasten, untwist, unseal. upa Caus. wind round, embrace. ni clutch, grasp, wrap. nis strip off, bare. pari wind or put around; wrap, cover, enclose, surround. vi strip off; wrap, envelop. sam roll or shrink together. Caus. wrap, envelop, cover; cause to roll or shrink together. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vii.html"> √ vī    √ vī, “enjoy” etc Present II. véti vyánti etc. V.B. (vihí RV., viyantu TS., vema V.S.), vyāná RV Passive vīyáte etc. AV.B Future Simple Future: veṣyati Periphrastic Future: vetā Aorist RAo: avīvayat -iṣ-Ao: avaiṣīt Perfect vivāya vivye RV Causative vāyayati , vāpayati Desiderative vivīṣa- Intensive veveti RV., vevīran TS., vevīyate RV Verbal Nouns vītá V.B Derivatives vī V.+ vayā́ RV. vāyú ? V.B. vetra ? E.+ -vī́ya RV. vayyà ? RV. vayúna V.+ vīrá ? V.+ -vāya AV. váyas V.+ vītí V.B. A very perplexing root in its varietics of meaning; divided into two or three roots (on different lines) by BR. and Grassmann. It is treated by the grammarians as filling up the conjugation of √ aj. Meanings véti v PPP vītá 1 (q.v.) seek, pursue, strive after, fall upon, attack, win, take hold of, enjoy; undertake, begin, urge, impel, further, promote; procure, get for, help to (2A). ati overtake, be superior to (A). apa turn away (intrans.). abhi drive on. ava seek after (A). ā approach, drive on or near, undertake, begin, seize, take hold of. upa strive after (A). ni (Int veveti) penetrate, rush into or among (L). pra drive on, set in motion; impel, inspire; strive on or after, enter into (A); fall upon, attack; inire, impregnate. prati receive. Cf. abhívīta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_viij.html"> √ vīj, vyaj    √ vīj, vyaj, “fan” Present I. vījati etc. E.+,-te E. vyajate ? C Perfect vivyajus E Causative vījayati etc. E.+ (vījyate E.+) Derivatives vījana C. vyajana E.+ Perhaps from vi + √ aj. Meanings vījati vījate v fan, blow on; Caus. vījayati kindle (fire). anu , abhi , ā , ud , upa , pari , sam = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vii_d.html"> √ vīḍ    √ vīḍ, “make strong” Causative vīḍáyati -te etc. V.B.S. Derivatives vīḍú V.B. Meanings vīḍáyati v (vīḷáyati) make (Ā te be) strong or firm; PPP vīḷitá = seq. a. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_v_r.html"> √ 1 vṛ    √ 1 vṛ, “cover” Present I. várati -te etc. (√-Ao ?) RV.C1 V. vṛṇóti vṛṇuté etc. V.+ (vṛṇvaté RV.); ūrṇóti (ūrṇvanti ūrṇuvanti) ūrṇuté (ūrṇvīta ūrṇuvīta) etc. V.+ (ūrṇauti ŚB.S.) IX. avṛṇīdhvam AV Passive vriyate E Future Simple Future: varī̆ṣyati Periphrastic Future: varī̆tā Aorist √-Ao: ávar avran etc. (vam ? vartam RV., vṛdhi RV.), avṛta V. (vrāṇá RV.); RAo: avīvarat AV., avāvarīt ? RV -s-Ao: varṣathas RV -iṣ-Ao: avārīt etc. B. avarī̆ṣṭa; aurṇāvīt Precative: vriyāt Ao/Ps/3/sg: ávāri RV Perfect vavāra vavrus vavré etc. V.+ (vavártha RV. vavaritha, vavṛma etc., vavrivā́ṃs vavavrúṣas RV.) ūrṇunāva Causative vāráyati -te etc. V.+ (vāryate etc. E.+; vivārayiṣate B.) Desiderative vivarī̆ṣa- Intensive avarīvar RV., várīvṛta TA. varvṛ-, vovur-, vevri- Verbal Nouns PPP: vṛtá V.+; Inf: vartum E., vártave RV., varitum C., varītum C.; 1Abs: vṛtvā́ V.B.,-tvī́ RV.,-tvā́ya B.; 2Abs: -vṛ́tya AV.+, ūrṇutya C Derivatives vā́r ? RV. urú V.+ várṇa V.+ vāra V.+ vára V.+ vṛ́t V.B. váruṇa V.+ vāraka E.+ -varaka E.+ vṛti V.+ ū́rṇā V.+ -vārin C. valá ? V.+ -vártu RV. várman V.+ vārya V.+ úrā ? RV. vartṛ́ RV. varī̆man V.B.S. vāraṇá V.+ vrá ? V. -varītṛ C. ūrmí ? V.+ -vāraṇīya E.+ váraṇa V.+ varūtṛ́ V.B. várīyas V.B. -ūrṇavana C1. varaṇá AV. vártra V.B.S. várivas V.+ vavrá V. varaṇīya C. vṛtrá V.+ váriṣṭha V.+ vavrí V. úraṇa V.+ varatrā́ V.+ úlba ? V.+ -vārayiṣṇu E. váras RV. várūtha V.+ ūrvá V.B. vivārayiṣu E. úras V.+ vārayitavya E. See the following root, √ 2 vṛ. The present-stem ūrṇu is by the grammarians artificially provided with a complete set of forms, as if a root or conjugationstem. As to varṣman etc., see under √ vṛṣ. Meanings vṛṇóti vṛṇuté várati vṛṇóti vṛṇuté várate 1 v (cf. also ūrṇu), PPP vṛtá (q.v.) cover, veil, hide; enclose, encompass, surround, guard; shut (a door); hold back or captive, ward off, hinder, restrain. Caus. vāráyati, te keep back, hold prisoner, hide, conceal, hinder, stop, ward off, exclude, forbid, withhold. anu cover, veil, enclose, surround; Caus. Ā hinder, stop. apa (ápā) uncover, open; Caus. hide. api veil. abhi cover, Caus. keep back, ward off. ā cover, veil, hide, surround, confine, bar, obstruct, occupy, fill. Caus. cover, hide, fill up, ward off. apā uncover, lay open, show, manifest. prā cover, veil; put on, don; fill. samā cover, veil, enclose, surround, fill, stop, hinder. ni ward off; Caus. keep back, withhold, forbid, remove, banish. vini Caus. keep back, hinder, stop, suppress, forbid, remove, dethrone. nis be satisfied or pleased. pari cover, veil, surround; shut up, obstruct, hinder. Caus. encompass, surround, attend. saṃpari Caus. surround, hem in. pra ward off, Caus. the same. prati Caus. keep or send back, ward off, prohibit, contradict. vi PĀ uncover, open, unsheathe (a sword), illumine, display, manifest, explain. sam PĀ cover over, hide, conceal, shut (a door); put together, bring in order; Ā intrans. gather, assemble, increase. abhisam cover, veil, surround, fill. Cf. apavārita, apavārya, ápāvṛta (sic!), ápīvṛta (add.), abhivṛta, ā́vṛta, nívṛta, nirvṛta, párivṛta, párīvṛta (sic!), paryāvṛta (add.), prā́vṛta, vivṛta, vrāṇá, sávṛta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_v_r.html"> √ 2 vṛ    √ 2 vṛ, “choose” Present V. vṛṇoti vṛṇute etc. U.E.+ IX. vṛṇīté etc. V.+, vṛṇāti etc. E.+ Passive vriyate S.C Future Simple Future: variṣyate B. varīṣyate Periphrastic Future: varī̆tā Aorist √-Ao: avṛta etc. V.+ (vurīta V.B., urāṇá RV.), váras etc. varanta RV -s-Ao: avṛṣi -ṣata etc. AV.B.U. (avṛḍhvam B.) -iṣ-Ao: avarī̆ṣṭa Ao/Ps/3/sg: avri V.+ Perfect vavre etc. V.+ (vavṛṣé vavṛmáhe RV.) Causative varayati -te etc. E.+ (varyáte B.); vārayati E Desiderative vivarī̆ṣa- , vovūrṣa- Intensive vevṛ- , varvṛ-, vovur- Verbal Nouns PPP: vṛtá V.+; Inf: varītum C. varitum; 1Abs: varītvā, varitvā S., vṛtvā S Derivatives vára V.+ -várya n. B. váreṇya V.+ vā̆rya V.+ vará V.+ -vū́rya V.S. varas- RV. -vāraṇa E.+ varaka S. varaṇa S.+ vṛ́thā ,-thak V. váriṣṭha V.+ varya E.+ varaṇīya U.C. vā́ra V.+ varīyas U.+ varayitavya E. Doubtless ultimately the same with the preceding, √ 1 vṛ; and the forms a little mixed up. Meanings vṛṇīté , vṛṇāti, vṛṇoti, vṛṇute, PPP vṛtá choose, esp. in marriage, woo, ask for; prefer, desire, wish, like. Caus. varayati, vṛṇīté, vṛṇāti, vṛṇoti, vṛṇute, PPP vṛtá choose, esp. in marriage, woo, ask for; prefer, desire, wish, like. Caus. varayate choose, ask, beg (2A); esp. choose in marriage (patim or patnīm), apa Ā content or satisfy with (I). abhi choose; prefer to (Ab). ā choose, desire; P grant. nis choose, pick out. pari Ā choose, select. pra Ā (P) choose, adopt. Cf. abhivṛta 2. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_v_r_mh.html"> √ vṛṃh, bṛṃh    √ vṛṃh, bṛṃh, “roar” Present I. vṛṃhati etc. E.+ Perfect vavṛṃhire C Verbal Nouns PPP: vṛṃhita E.+ 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_v_rj.html"> √ vṛj    √ vṛj, “twist” Present VII. vṛṇákti vṛṅkté etc. (vṛktām ? M1.) V.+ Passive vṛjyáte etc. V.B.S Future Simple Future: varkṣyati -te B. varjiṣyati Periphrastic Future: varjitā Aorist √-Ao: várk etc. (varktam avṛjan varjati vṛjyām etc. RV., avṛk AV.), ávṛkta RV. (várjate RV.) RAo: avavarjat -s-Ao: avārkṣīs B., avṛkṣmahi etc. V.B -sa- Ao: avṛkṣat etc. V.B Perfect vavṛjus etc. RV. (vavṛjyús vavṛktam RV.,-varjúṣī AV.), vāvṛje RV Causative varjayati etc. AV.+,-te etc. E.+ (varjyate etc. E.+; varīvarjáyant AV.) Desiderative vívṛkṣate B Intensive várīvṛjat RV. varvṛj- Verbal Nouns PPP: vṛktá V.+; vṛktvī́ RV.;-vṛ́jya B.S.;-vṛ́je vṛñjáse vṛjádhyai RV.; -várgam V.S Derivatives -vṛj V. varjaka E. vṛjána V. vṛñjana S.+ ū́rj etc. ? V.+ varjin E.+ vṛ́jana RV. vṛjiná V.+ varga V.+ varjya E.+ vṛjanī́ V. -vṛkti V.B. -vargyà AV.+ vrajá V.+ varjana B.+ varjayitavya C. -varja S.+ vrājá V. varjanīya B.+ varjayitṛ E.+ -vṛ́jya V.B.S. Meanings vṛṇákti vṛṅkté v PPP vṛktá turn, twist off, pluck out (the sacrificial grass), turn or set aside, remove; Ā avert, keep away, withhold. Caus. varjayati (te), PPP varjita (q.v.) abandon, shun, avoid, exempt, spare; renounce, resign; leave out, exclude. P. be deprived of or excluded from. apa avert, remove, scare away; turn or tear off; finish, conclude. Caus. abandon, avoid, renounce, yield, grant, present, offer (a funeral meal); keep (a promise), conclude, finish. api procure to, turn upon (L). ava turn off, sever; Caus. remove, destroy. ā procure, afford, furnish; take to one's self, appropriate; withhold from (Ab); be favourable to (A). Caus. bend, incline, make favourable, win over. vyā separate, divide. samā take to one's self, appropriate; Caus. bend, incline. ud remove, destroy. ni bend down, cause to fall, cast away. parā turn away (trans. & I), flee; tear off, remove, reject, abandon. pari turn round, give way, avoid, spare, exempt from (I); reject, turn out. Caus. keep off, remove, shun, avoid, abandon. pra strew (the sacrificial bed); set in or at the fire, heat or glow. sam take to one's self, appropriate. Cf. āvarjita, parivṛkta, vivarjita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_v_rt.html"> √ vṛt    √ vṛt, “turn” Present I. vártate etc. V.+,-ti etc. U.+ II. vartti RV1 III. vavartti vavṛtyām etc.-tīya etc.-tsva etc. ávavṛtran -ranta vavártat -tati vavṛtat V.B Future Simple Future: vartsyáti etc. AV.+ (avartsyat B.),-te etc. E.+; vartiṣyati -te etc. E.+ Periphrastic Future: vartitā B Aorist √-Ao: avart etc. (vártat vartta) RV., avṛtran V.B Th Ao: avṛtat etc. AV.B.C RAo: avīvṛtat etc. V. avavartat -s-Ao: avṛtsan C1., avṛtsata V.B.S -iṣ-Ao: vartithās M Perfect vavarta vavṛtus etc. V.+ (vāvárta -vṛtús V.), vavṛte etc. U.+ (vāvṛté V.) Causative vartayati -te etc. V.+ (vartayádhyai RV.; vartyate etc. B.+) Desiderative vívṛtsati etc. V.,-te B. vivartiṣa- Intensive várvartti etc. várvṛtāna V.; varīvartti etc. V.B. (avarīvur RV.), varīvṛtyate B Verbal Nouns PPP: vṛttá V.+; Inf: vartitum E.+; 2Abs: -vṛ́tya V.+;-vṛ́te RV.,-vṛ́tas B.;-vártam B.+ Derivatives vṛ́t V.+ vratá V.+ varti E.+ vratáti V.+ vṛtā́ RV. vráta AV. vartís RV. vártman V.+ -varta V.+ vártana V.+ vṛtti B.+ varīvṛtá AV. vartaka V.+ vartanīya E.+ várttu V.+ -vivṛtsu C. vartin V.+ vartaní V.B.U. -varttavya E. -vartayitavya E.+ -vartya E.+ vártas VS. vartitavya E.+ -vartayitṛ C. -vartitṛ V.+ Contracted in one or two forms with anu to anvart: see √ ṛt. Meanings vártate vártati vavartti 1 v (vartti), PPP vṛttá (q.v.) turn, revolve, roll, run off, pass away (time); go on, take place, happen, occur; abide, live, exist, be (also as simple copula), become; find one's self, feel (w. Adv); (vṛttim) deal with, act, proceed (Adv or I); behave towards (L), have intercourse with (saha, L with a woman); be concerned or occupied with (L or D); live or subsist on or by (I); conduce or tend to (D); be valid or supplying from a previous rule (g.). With mūrghni stand at the head, be chief in importance; w. hṛdi or manasi be turned or thought over in the mind; kiṃ vartate how is it with (G); ātmani na vartate he is beside himself (with joy etc.). Caus. vartáyati, vártate, vártati, vavartti 1 (vartti), PPP vṛttá (q.v.) turn, revolve, roll, run off, pass away (time); go on, take place, happen, occur; abide, live, exist, be (also as simple copula), become; find one's self, feel (w. Adv); (vṛttim) deal with, act, proceed (Adv or I); behave towards (L), have intercourse with (saha, L with a woman); be concerned or occupied with (L or D); live or subsist on or by (I); conduce or tend to (D); be valid or supplying from a previous rule (g.). With mūrghni stand at the head, be chief in importance; w. hṛdi or manasi be turned or thought over in the mind; kiṃ vartate how is it with (G); ātmani na vartate he is beside himself (with joy etc.). Caus. vartáyate cause to turn or roll, whirl about, brandish, turn i.e. fabricate by turning; spend, pass (time); lead a life, exist (jīvitam); live on or by (I); maintain, observe; perform, accomplish, make, do, utter; show, manifest; explain. tell, relate. Int várvartti, varīvartti, varīvṛtyate turn, roll, be present, exist. – accha Caus. bring near. ati intrans. pass away (time), cease or desist from (Ab); trans, pass by, cross over, go beyond; overcome, resist, escape, transgress, neglect, omit, forget. vyati intrans. = prec., trans. (w. A) cross over, pass, overcome, escape. samati intrans. run away, trans. (w. A) pass by, escape. adhi roll over (L); move or turn towards (Adv in tas). anu intrans. pass or rise after, last, continue, also = S. (g.); trans. (w. A) roll after, follow, pursue, adhere, cling to, equal in (I) consent, agree, obey, oblige, be devoted to or intent upon, conform one's self to or depend upon, fall, into or partake of. Caus. cause to roll on, cause to follow or pursue, join to (L); recite, answer. samanu go after, follow, conform one's self to (A). antar Caus. mix with (L). apa turn off or aside, go away, withdraw. vyapa the same, desist from (Ab). abhi move or turn towards (A or Adv in tas), rise, appear, take place; approach, advance (as friend or foe), meet, encounter, attack, conquer. samabhi approach, go against (A); come near or back; rise, appear. ā P (Ā) turn or roll hither, sc. ratham = come to; turn around, pass by (A); Ā roll near or back (intrans.), revolve; go down, set; (punar) return, also = be born anew; be repeated or renewed. Caus. turn or come to (ratham); bring near, attract; turn round, invert, disturb, destroy; bring back, repeat, recite. Int move quickly, stir. anvā Ā roll after or along, follow; Int the same. apā turn away from (Ab). abhyā turn towards, resort to (A). Caus. approach (sc. ratham), repeat. upā turn towards, resort to (A), arrive at (A or L); turn from (Ab), return, come back. Caus. turn hither (trans.), bring near or back; obtain, win. abhyupā turn towards, get to, partake of (A). paryā turn round or away, turn into (I). Caus. put instead of something else. anuparyā go after or along, follow. abhiparyā turn towards or around. pratyā turn towards (A); return, come back. vyā turn away or back (intrans.); separate from or part with, get rid of (I or Ab); open, burst, split into (Adv in dhā); cease, come to an end. Caus. sever or free from (I or Ab); remove, destroy, annul. samā turn back, return, go home (esp. of a pupil after his apprenticeship); approach, come hither; turn towards (A); come off, take place, pass away. Caus. drive home (cows), dismiss (a pupil). abhisamā & upasamā return. ud spring off, go out, disappear from (Ab), burst asunder, boil up, swell. Caus. burst asunder (trans.), destroy, ruin. upa tread upon, approach, appear, befall. ni turn round (trans. & intrans.); return (also into life i.e. be born again); turn away, flee, abstain or desist from, get rid of (Ab); end with or at (Ab); not belong to, be withheld from (Ab), stop, pause, cease, disappear. Caus. turn downwards, bring or lead back, keep off, avert from (Ab), give up, let go, withhold, suppress, annul; refuse, deny; grant, procure, perform, accomplish. abhini return; Caus. repeat. upani return, be repeated. pratini turn back from (Ab), escape. Caus. lead back, turn off, avert. vini turn back, desist from, renounce (Ab); cease, disappear, vanish, be extinguished (fire). Caus. lead or draw back, avert, annul, frustrate. saṃni turn back, return from (Ab); stop, pause; abstain or desist from (Ab), pass away. Caus. send or lead back, divert from (Ab); stop (trans.), suppress. nis roll out, come forth, develop, grow, become (N), be performed or finished, return. Caus. bring forth, create, effect, perform, accomplish. abhinis come forth, develop; Caus. bring about, accomplish. parā turn the back upon (Ab), turn round (udak towards the north), return; abstain or desist from (Ab). pari turn round, move in a circle, roll (w. hṛdaye run in the mind); roam, walk about (A); return, go back to (A), be reborn in (L), change, alter (anyathā); abide, dwell; act, proceed, behave. Caus. turn round (trans.), move about, upset, alter, change, renew; turn topsy turvy i.e. confuse, destroy. vipari turn round, roll (w. hṛdaye = prec.), roam about, change, alter. saṃpari the same + come back, return; get rid of (Ab). pra turn forward, set out, move on; come forth, rise, appear, originate from (Ab), come off, take place, happen, occur; undertake, begin, set about, prepare for (Inf, D, L, or artham); act, proceed, deal with (L); work, be valid, cause, effect; rest or be turned upon (L); last, continue; become, be present, exist; have the sense or meaning of (L). Caus. set in motion, hurl, cast, or send away; introduce, establish, appoint; produce, accomplish; form, make; show, exhibit; undertake, begin; use, employ. atipra come forth abundantly. abhipra move or roll towards, fall into (acc); set out, get in motion. saṃpra come forth, rise, begin, undertake, prepare for (D or L); deal with, behave towards (L). Caus. set in motion, set abroad, divulge, introduce; undertake, begin. vi roll, run, turn, wallow, struggle; sink (sun); turn or run away, part with (I); come forth, rise from (Ab), expand, develop. Caus. turn, roll, contract (the brows); form, shape, make of (I); remove, keep off or asunder. sam turn towards, approach, meet, encounter (as friends or foes), assemble, unite; take shape, come into being, originate or rise from (Ab), happen, take place, begin, be, become, be present, exist. Caus. turn to (A); roll, clinch (the fist); envelop, cover; hurl, cast; break, destroy; perform, accomplish. abhisam turn to (A), prepare for, begin (Inf). Cf. atipravṛtta, ativṛtta, anuvṛtta, apavṛtta, apāvṛtta, abhipravṛtta (add.); abhyā́vṛtta, abhyupāvṛtta, ā́vṛtta, udvṛtta, upā́vṛtta (sic!), nirvṛtta, nivṛtta, parivṛtta, pravṛtta, vinirvṛtta, vinivṛtta, vívṛtta, vyā́vṛtta, saṃvṛtta, saṃnivṛtta, samāvṛtta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_v_rdh.html"> √ vṛdh    √ vṛdh, “grow” Present I. várdhati -te etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: vartsyati C. vardhiṣyate Periphrastic Future: vardhitā Aorist Th Ao: avṛdhat etc. V.B.S. (vṛdhātas vṛdhātu B., vṛdhánt V., vṛdhāná RV.) RAo: avīvṛdhat etc. V.+,-dhata etc. V.B.S -iṣ-Ao: avardhiṣṭa etc. E.+ (vardhiṣīmáhi B.S.) Perfect vavárdha vavṛdhe etc. V.+ (vāvṛdhús etc. vāvṛdhé etc. V.; vāvṛdhāti -dhīthā́s -dhásva etc. RV.,-dhéte AV., vā̆vṛdhánt V.) Causative vardháyati -te etc. V.+ (vivardhayiṣa in d.); vardhāpayati C Desiderative vivṛtsa- , vivardhiṣa- Intensive varīvṛdh- Verbal Nouns PPP: vṛddhá V.+; Inf: vardhitum C.; 1Abs: vardhitvā, vṛddhvā; vṛdhé V., vṛdháse RV., vāvṛdhádhyai RV Derivatives vṛ́dh V.+ várdhana V.+ vardhitṛ́ RV. vardhiṣṇu C. vṛdhá V.+ vardhanīya E.+ vardhman C. vāvṛdhénya RV. várdha V.+ vṛdhás RV. várddhra ? AV.B. vardhayitṛ C. -vardhaka C. vṛdhīká RV. ūrdhvá V.+ vivardhayiṣu E.+ vardhin E.+ vṛ́ddhi V.+ vṛdhasāná RV. vardhāpana C. Compare √ ṛdh. The asserted √ 2 vṛdh “cut” (used only of the navelstring) rests on a too narrow foundation to be admitted; it is probably a specialized application of this root. Meanings várdhati várdhate v PPP vṛddhá 1 (q.v.) P make to grow, elevate, strengthen, cheer, gladden, rouse, inspire; Ā (P) grow, thrive, increase in (A); spread, expand, lengthen (days); be blessed or fortunate (diṣṭhyā). Caus. vardháyati, te P elevate, rear, bring up, promote, further, make great or strong; delight, cheer, inspire (Ā intrans. or refl.). ati grow beyond. anu grow after another or in proportion with (A); grow or increase gradually. abhi grow up, grow stronger or greater, thrive or increase in (I), spread, expand, grow beyond (A), surpass. ā P cause to grow, Ā grow, increase. pari grow up, increase, get stronger or mightier. Caus. cause to swell (the sea); rear up, foster; gladden, delight. pra P elevate, exalt, inspire; Ā (P) grow on or up, thrive, be animated or inspired. Caus. strengthen, augment, lengthen, bring up, promote, further, exalt. atipra grow beyond (A), surpass, exceed. saṃpra grow, increase, augment, thrive. vi grow, increase, swell, thrive, be blessed or fortunate; rise, originate. saṃvi thrive. sam P grant, fulfil (a wish); grow, increase. Caus. make to grow or thrive, bring up, rear, nourish, feed, strengthen, promote, cherish, embellish. Cf. atipravṛddha, ativṛddha, právṛddha (sic!), vivṛddha, saṃvṛddha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_v_r_s.html"> √ vṛṣ    √ vṛṣ, “rain” Present I. várṣati etc. V.+,-te etc. E VI. vṛṣate etc. RV.S., vṛṣant- RV Future Simple Future: varṣiṣyati etc. B.U.,-te E Periphrastic Future: vraṣṭā́ MS Aorist Th Ao: avṛṣāt ? TS RAo: avīvṛṣat etc. E. avavarṣat -iṣ-Ao: ávarṣīt etc. V.B Perfect vavarṣa vavṛṣus etc. E.+ (vavarṣus E., vavarṣvā́ṃs MS.), vavṛṣe etc. E. (vāvṛṣāṇá -ṣasva RV.) Causative varṣáyati etc. V.+ Desiderative vivarṣiṣa- (in d.) Intensive varīvṛṣ- Verbal Nouns PPP: vṛṣṭá V.+; Inf: varṣitum C.,-varṣṭos B.; 1Abs: varṣitvā, vṛṣṭvā B.,-ṭvī́ RV.; 2Abs: -vṛṣya C Derivatives -vṛṣ V.+ varṣya V.B.S. várṣṭṛ B. vṛ́ṣan V.+ vṛṣa- V.B.S. varṣaṇa S.+ varṣitṛ C. vṛṣṇi V.+ varṣá V.+ várṣuka B. vivarṣiṣu E. vṛṣabhá V.+ varṣin S.+ vṛṣṭí V.+ The connection of vṛ́ṣan etc. with this root is questionable; and yet more that of varṣman V.+, varṣimán VS., várṣīyas V.+, várṣiṣṭha V.+, all of which may come from an aoristically extended form of √ 1 vṛ (like párṣiṣṭha etc. from √ 2 pṛ). Meanings várṣati várṣate v PPP vṛṣṭá (q.v.) rain (either pers. w. Parjanya, Indra, etc. as subj., or impers.), pour down, shed or cover with (I); L varṣati while it is raining. Caus. varṣáyati cause to rain or let fall down as rain; sprinkle or cover with (I). abhi rain, pour down; sprinkle or cover with (I). ava & ā the same. pra begin to rain, pour or shower down; sprinkle or cover with (I). prati , vi Caus. , & sam = prec. w. I 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_v_rh.html"> √ vṛh, bṛh    √ vṛh, bṛh, “tear” Present VI. vṛháti bṛháti etc. V.B.U.S Passive vṛhyate etc. B Future Simple Future: varkṣyati, varhiṣyati Periphrastic Future: varḍhā, varhitā Aorist RAo: avīvṛhat, avavarhat -iṣ-Ao: barhīs -īt RV -sa- Ao: avṛkṣat etc. B Ao/Ps/3/sg: varhi RV Perfect vavárha babarha vavṛhus V.+ Causative barháyati etc. RV. (varhita C.) Desiderative vivṛkṣa- , vivarhiṣa- Intensive varīvṛh- Verbal Nouns PPP: vṛḍhá bṛḍha B.S.; 1Abs: vṛḍhvā, varhitvā; 2Abs: -vṛ́hya B.U.S.; -vṛhas K.;-várham -barham B Derivatives -vṛha S.+ barhin , va- E. várhaṇa , vá- AV.+ barhís ? V.+ barha , va- AV.+ Compare √ 2 bṛh. The confusion of b and v goes back to the oldest time. Meanings (vṛh), bṛháti (vṛháti), PPP bṛḍha (vṛḍhá) pluck, tear out. ā tear off, root out. ud & samud draw forth. ni throw down; Caus. the same, destroy, annihilate. pra tear out or off, snatch away; tear asunder, destroy; Ā = upapra Ā draw towards one's self, attract vi rend asunder, break up, split, destroy, remove. sam rend asunder, draw out (together). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ven.html"> √ ven    √ ven, “long” Present I. vénati etc. V.B Future Simple Future: veniṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: venitā Aorist RAo: avivenat -iṣ-Ao: avenīt -niṣṭa Perfect vivena -ne Causative venaya- Desiderative viveniṣa- Intensive veven- Derivatives vená V.B. venyá RV. Meanings vénati v long for, desire; be envious or jealous. anu strive to entice or win. apa & vi turn away disdainfully. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vell.html"> √ vell    √ vell, “stagger” Present I. vellati etc. C Verbal Nouns PPP: vellita E.+ Derivatives vellana C. Meanings vellati v PPP vellita move to and fro, tremble, reel, undulate. ud , vi & sam = S. Cf. udvellita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_ve_s_t.html"> √ veṣṭ    √ veṣṭ see √ viṣṭ. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vyac.html"> √ vyac, vic    √ vyac, vic, “extend” Present III. viviktás vivyácat avivyak aviviktām avivyacus etc. vivyacanta RV VI. vicati Future Simple Future: vyaciṣyati Periphrastic Future: vyacitā vicitā Aorist RAo: avivyacat -iṣ-Ao: avyā̆cīt; Precative: vicyāt Ao/Ps/3/sg: avyāci Perfect vivyāca V.B., vivyáktha RV.; viceca ? AV. vivicus Causative vyācaya- Desiderative vivyaciṣa- Intensive vevic- vāvyac- Verbal Nouns PPP: vicita 1Abs: vicitvā Derivatives vyácas V.B.S. vyáciṣṭha V.B. vī́ci ? V. Has a very suspicious likeness to vi + √ ac, añc. Meanings vivyakti v extend around, embrace, encompass sam = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vyaj.html"> √ vyaj    √ vyaj see √ vīj. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vyath.html"> √ vyath    √ vyath, “waver” Present I. vyáthate etc. V.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: vyathiṣyate Periphrastic Future: vyathitā Aorist RAo: vivyathas B -iṣ-Ao: vyathiṣi etc. AV.+, vyathiṣat B Ao/Ps/3/sg: avyā̆thi Perfect vivyathe E.+,-thus E Causative vyatháyati etc. V.+ (vyathayīs AV.; vyathyate C.) Desiderative vivyathiṣa- Intensive vāvyath- Verbal Nouns vyathitá AV.+; vyathiṣyai B.S Derivatives vyathā B.+ vyathana E.+ vyáthis RV. vyathayitṛ C. vyathaka C. vyáthi V. -vyātha B. -vyathya V.B. vyathí ? AV. vithurá V.B.S. vyathin C. Meanings vyáthate v (vyáthati), PPP vyathitá (q.v.) waver, reel, stagger, come to fall, go wrong, fail; tremble, be afraid or pained. Caus. vyatháyati cause to waver etc., bring to fall, make afraid or uneasy, distress, pain. pra , saṃpra, vi & sam = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vyadh.html"> √ vyadh, vidh    √ vyadh, vidh, “pierce” Present IV. vídhyati etc. V.+,-te E Passive vidhyate E Future Simple Future: vetsyati -te E. vyatsyati Periphrastic Future: veddhā E. vyaddhā Aorist RAo: avīvidhat E. avivyadhat -s-Ao: vyātsīs B Precative: vidhyāt Perfect vivyādha B.+, vivyadhus E., vividhus U., vividhvā́ṃs RV.; vivyadhe E Causative vyādhayati B.; vyadhayati C.; vedhayati etc. E Desiderative vivyatsati B Intensive vāvyadh- , vevidh- Verbal Nouns PPP: viddhá V.+; Inf: veddhum E.; 1Abs: viddhvā E.; 2Abs: -vidhya E.+;-vídhe RV Derivatives -vidh V.+ vedhin E.+ vyādha AV.+ veddhavya U.+ -vidhya E. vedhya C. vyādhin AV.B. veddhṛ E.+ vedha E.+ vyadha C. -vyādhyà AV. -vedhima C. vedhaka E.+ vyadhya C. vedhana E.+ vyadhvará ? AV. vyadhana AV.C. Meanings vídhyati v (vídhyate), PPP viddhá (q.v.) pierce, hit, wound, hurt, harm, injure, affect or afflict with (I). Caus. vedhayati pierce, hit, vyādhayati cause to pierce etc. ati & vyati pierce, perforate. anu pierce or wound (after another); intertwine, set or fill with (I). apa hurl or throw away, give up, neglect. abhi wound, hit. ava precipitate into (L) or from (Ab). ā throw, bore or break through; scare, drive away, also = vyā & samā wave, swing, brandish. ni throw down, overthrow; shoot at, hit, pierce. nis wound, kill, slay. parā hurl off wound, hit. pari shoot at. pra hurl, throw, shoot, perforate, wound. prati shoot, hit. vi pierce, shoot. sam shoot. Cf. anuviddha, apaviddha, ā́viddha, práviddha, vyapaviddha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vyay.html"> √ vyay    √ vyay, “expend” Present I. vyayati -te etc. C Perfect etc. vavyāya vavyaye etc.etc Verbal Nouns PPP: vyayita C Is only a conjugation of vi + √ 1 i, or denomminative of vyaya. Meanings vyayati vyayate v waste, squander, expend. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vyaa.html"> √ vyā, vī    √ vyā, vī, “envelop” Present IV ? vyáyati -te etc. V.+ Passive vīyáte B Future Simple Future: vyāsyati -te; vyayiṣye S Periphrastic Future: vyātā Aorist Th Ao: ávyat etc. RV., avyata etc. V -s-Ao: avyāsta, vyāsīṣṭa -siṣ-Ao: avyāsīt Precative: vīyāt Perfect vivyathus RV., vivyé etc. RV. vivyāya vivyayitha etc.; -vyayā́ṃ cakāra ŚB Causative vyāyaya- Desiderative vivyāsa- Intensive vāvyā- , vevī- Verbal Nouns PPP: vītá V.+; 2Abs: -vī́ya B.S.C.-vyāya Derivatives -vī V.+ -vyāya B.S. -vyāna C. -vyayana B.S. Meanings vyáyati vyáyate v PPP vītá (q.v.) wrap, veil, envelop; Ā refl. apa unveil, uncover; Ā extricate one's self i.e. deny. api cover. ā wrap round (A), hide one's self in (L). upa hang about (esp. the sacred cord over the left shoulder). ni wind or hang about. pari wrap around; Ā wind something as cover round one's self. sam P roll up, envelop; veil in (I), Ā refl. Cf. úpavīta, nívīta, párivīta, saṃvīta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vraj.html"> √ vraj    √ vraj, “proceed” Present I. vrájati etc. V.+,-te etc. C Passive vrajyate C Future Simple Future: vrajiṣyati etc. B.+ Periphrastic Future: vrajitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: avrājīt etc. B.U Perfect vavrā́ja etc. V.+ Causative vrājayati etc. B.+ (vrājyate E.) Desiderative vivrajiṣa- (in d.) Intensive vāvraj- Verbal Nouns PPP: vrajita B.+; Inf: vrajitum E.; 1Abs: vrajitvā S.+; 2Abs: -vrájya B.+;-vrājam S Derivatives -vrāj E.+ vrajyā E.+ -vrājaka E.+ vrájana V.+ -vrajya E.+ -vrāja V.+ -vrājin B.+ -vrājana E. -vivrajiṣu C. Meanings vrájati v (vrájate), PPP vrajita proceed, march, go (padbhyām on foot), go to (A, r. L or *D), go for i.e. to fetch (A), *be going to (Inf, D, or Adj in aka); attack, approach (a woman); go from, leave (Ab), pass away (time), get into a state or condition (A). With adhras go down i.e. be digested; w. punar return to life; w. saha agree, make peace. Caus. vrājayati drive. ati pass beyond, roam through. anu go along, accompany, follow; visit, go to or into (A). apa go away. abhi go to or through. ā come near, approach; come back, return (punar); go to arrive at (A). pratyā & samā come back, return. ud leave home. pratyud go to meet. upa come near, go to, follow. pratyupa march against, attack. pari walk about, circumambulate; roam, wander (esp. as a religious mendicant). pra march forth, go to, wander (= prec.). abhipra march forth towards or to meet. sam travel. anusam go after, follow. upasam enter (A). Cf. pravrajita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vrad.html"> √ vrad, vrand    √ vrad, vrand, “weaken” Present I. avradanta RV1. Derivatives vrandín RV. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vran.html"> √ vran    √ vran, “sound” (?) Present I. vraṇati C. Derivatives vraṇa E.+ No real root; the single occurrence artificial. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vrazc.html"> √ vraśc    √ vraśc, “cut up” Present I. vraścati ? C VI. vṛścáti etc. V.B.S.C Passive vṛścyáte etc. V.B. (vṛścáte AV.) Future Simple Future: vrakṣyánt ŚB. ? vraściṣyati Periphrastic Future: vraścitā, vraṣṭā Aorist RAo: avivraścat -s-Ao: avrākṣīt vṛkṣi B.S -iṣ-Ao: avraścīt Perfect vavraśca vavraścus vavṛktam ? RV Causative vraścaya- Desiderative vivraściṣa- , vivrakṣa- Intensive varīvṛśc- Verbal Nouns PPP: vṛkṇá V.+; 1Abs: vraścitvā, vṛṣṭā́ AV., vṛktvī RV.; 2Abs: -vṛścya S.C.;-vráścam B.S Derivatives vṛ́ka ? V.+ -vráśca B. -vraskya S. vráścana V.+ vṛ́ścika V.+ -vraska V.B.S. vṛkṣá ? V.+ Meanings vṛścáti v PPP vṛkṇá hew down, fell (a tree), cut to pieces. api hew off or asunder. ava cut off, sever. ā sever, separate, estrange or alienate from (D or L). ni hew down, fell. pari cut, mutilate. pra cut or split off. vi cut or split asunder. sam hew or cut in pieces. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vraadh.html"> √ vrādh    √ vrādh, “stir up” Present I. vrādhanta vrā́dhant RV. Meanings (vrādhate) stir up. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vrii_d.html"> √ vrīḍ    √ vrīḍ, “be abashed” Present I. vrīḍate etc. E.+ IV. vrīḍyati Future Simple Future: vrīḍiṣyati Periphrastic Future: vrīḍitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: avrīḍīt Perfect vivrīḍa Causative vrīḍayati C Verbal Nouns PPP: vrīḍita E.+ Derivatives vrīḍā̆ E.+ vrīḍana C. Meanings vrīḍate v PPP vrīḍita be ashamed or embarrassed. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vru_d.html"> √ vruḍ    √ vruḍ, “sink” Present etc I. vruḍati etc.etc Verbal Nouns PPP: vruḍita C The occurrence or two are doubtless artificial. Meanings PPP vruḍita sink. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vlag.html"> √ vlag, vlaṅg    √ vlag, vlaṅg, “pursue” (?) Verbal Nouns -vlágya RV2. Derivatives -vlaṅga RV. Only with abhi. Perhaps related with √ valg. Meanings w. abhi pursue, overtake. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_vlii.html"> √ vlī, blī    √ vlī, blī, “crush” Present IX. vlīnāti etc. B.; vlināti etc. ŚB.S Passive vlīyate etc. B.U. (blīya- K., vliyeran AB.) Future Simple Future: vleṣyati B Periphrastic Future: vletā Aorist -s-Ao: vleṣīs S Perfect vivlāya Causative vlepayati , avivlipat Desiderative vivlīṣa- Intensive avevlīyanta B Verbal Nouns PPP: vlīna B., blīna AV.;-vlī́ya B Derivatives -vlaya B.S. vlayana B. vráyas ? RV. Meanings vlīnāti vlināti crush, fell; P. vlīyate shrink, decay. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_za_ms.html"> √ śaṃs    √ śaṃs, “praise” Present I. śáṃsati -te etc. V.+ (śaṃsīyāt C1.) Passive śasyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: śaṃsiṣyati B.S Periphrastic Future: śaṃsitā Aorist √-Ao: śasta ( 2p.) RV., śastāt AB.; śaṃsi RV RAo: aśaśaṃsat -iṣ-Ao: aśaṃsīt etc. V.+ (śaṃsiṣat etc. V.B.) Precative: śasyāt Perfect śaśaṃsa -se etc. B.+ (śaṃsus -sire E.) Causative śaṃsáyati etc. V.+,-te C Desiderative śiśaṃsiṣa- Intensive śāśas- , śāśaṃs- Verbal Nouns PPP: śastá V.+, śaṃsita E.+; Inf: śaṃsitum E.; 1Abs: śastvā́ B.; 2Abs: -śasya S.+,-śaṃsya E.;-śáse RV.;-śaṃsam B.S Derivatives -śas V.B. śáṃsa V.+ śaṃsanīya C. -śastavya E. -śās V. śaṃsā B.+ -śaṃsu S. śaṃsitṛ B.+ -śasa B. -śaṃsaka E. -śaṃsuka B. śáṃstṛ V.B. śásā RV. śaṃsin V.+ śastí V.+ śastrá B.+ śásya V.+ śáṃsya V.+ -śastenya B. śaṃsatha S. śaṃsana E.+ śaṃstavya B.E. śásman RV. Compare the related √ 1 śās. Meanings śáṃsati v (śáṃsate), PPP śastá (q.v.) & śaṃśita say in a loud and solemn voice, recite, praise, vow, unfold, betray, announce, communicate, declare, foretell, prophesy. Caus. śaṃsayati cause to recite; announce, foretell. ati recite beyond (2A or I & A); omit in reciting. anu recite or praise (after another). abhi accuse, defame; praise, commend. ā Ā (P) hope or trust in, strive after (L, A, D, or Inf), try to master (A), suppose, expect, fear; wish, desire (A or – & – Inf). beg for (A); praise, commend, recite, announce, foretell. samā P adjudge to (D); Ā hope or trust in (A). ud call upon, invoke. pra tell forth, proclaim aloud; stir up, excite; praise, extol, recommend to (G). vi recite, divide in reciting. sam recite (together). upasam recite in addition. Cf. abhiśasta, praśastá. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zak.html"> √ śak    √ śak, “be able” Present V. śaknoti -nuvánti etc. V.+ Passive śakyate etc. E.+,-ti etc. E Future Simple Future: śakṣyati -te etc. B.+ Periphrastic Future: śaktā Aorist √-Ao: śagdhí śaktam śákat etc. śakyām V Th Ao: áśakat etc. V.+ (śakéyam etc. V.B.S., śakemahi U.) RAo: aśīśakat Perfect śaśā́ka śekús etc. V.+ Causative śākayati Desiderative śíkṣati -te etc. V.+ (śikṣāṇa E.; śiśikṣa C.; śikṣyate etc. C.; śikṣayati -te etc. E.+) Intensive śāśak- Verbal Nouns PPP: śakta E.+, śakita E.+;-śaktave RV Derivatives -śáka RV. śákti V.+ śikvá AV. śikṣaka E. śakya U.S.+ śaktí RV. śákvan V.B.S. -śikṣin C. śā́ka V. śákman RV. śíkvan V.B. śikṣaṇa C. śāká RV. śā́kman RV. śíkvas RV. śikṣaṇīya C. śā́kī ? RV. -śíkman MS. śáciṣṭha V.B.S. śikṣeṇya S. śácī V.+ śagmá V.B.S. śikṣā V.+ śikṣú RV. śāci ? RV. śakrá V.+ śīkṣā B.+ śikṣuka GB. The desiderative śikṣ has won a so independent use and value that it might well enough have been treated (like bhakṣ etc.) as a separate root. BR. devide śak (and śikṣ) into two roots, the second meaning “help”, but favor their ultimate identity. There are other groups of words, not connectable with this or any other verbal root: thus, śakuná, śakúni, śakúnta, śakúnti V.+; śáka, śakán, śákṛt V.+; śaṅkú V.+, śakti (”spear”) E.+ Meanings śaknoti v PPP śakta (q.v.) & śakita be able, P. śakyate impers. it is possible to (Inf) or pers. he is able to be, he can or may be (Inf w. pass. mg); be serviceable or helpful to (D), make another partake of (G). Des. śikṣati (q.v.). anu be equal in (A). ā assist (D), help a pers. (D) to (G), invite to (A). upa help, impart. pari master, overpower. pra be able to (Inf). sam be able to (Inf), w. na not be equal to or a match for (L or I). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_za_gk.html"> √ śaṅk    √ śaṅk, “doubt” Present I. śáṅkate etc. B.+,-ti etc. E Passive śaṅkyate etc. C Future Simple Future: śaṅkiṣyate Periphrastic Future: śaṅkitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: śaṅkīs śaṅkiṣṭhās E.+ (śaṅkithās E.) Perfect śaśaṅke Causative śaṅkayati C Verbal Nouns PPP: śaṅkita E.+; Inf: śaṅkitum E.+; 2Abs: -śaṅkya C Derivatives śaṅkā́ ? B.+ -śaṅkya S.+ śaṅkana E. ? śaṅkitavya E.+ śaṅkin E.+ śaṅkanīya E.+ Meanings śáṅkate v (śáṅkati), PPP śaṅkita (q.v.) doubt, hesitate, be anxious or suspicious, be afraid of (A or Ab); suppose, expect, believe. Caus. śaṅkayati make anxious about (L). ati suspect strongly or falsely. abhi distrust, doubt, hesitate at (A or G). ā be doubtful or afraid, distrust (A); suppose, think to be (iti or 2A). upa suspect, accuse of (I). pari be anxious or doubtful, distrust, suspect, disbelieve (A); suppose, expect, think to be (2A). vi be anxious or afraid of (A or Ab), distrust, doubt, suspect (A); think to be (2A). sam suspect. Cf. atiśaṅkita, abhiśaṅkita, upaśaṅkita (add.), pariśaṅkita, viśaṅkita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zat.html"> √ śat    √ śat, “cut in pieces” Causative śātáyati etc. AV.+ -te B. Derivatives śata C. śātin C. śātana E.+ śātayitṛ C. Called by the grammarians the causative of √ 2 śad. Meanings śātáyati śātáyate v cut in pieces, cause to fall off, break or throw down, destroy. apa hurl away. vyava scatter, dispense, remove. ni hew down, defeat (an army). pra break, pluck. vi hew down, crush, disperse, chase away. sam crush, destroy. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_zad.html"> √ 1 śad    √ 1 śad, “prevail” Perfect śāśadús RV.; śāśadmahe etc. (śā́śadāna) V. Derivatives śátru ? V.+ Meanings only Pf (Cappeller: Int) śāśadús 1 etc., PPP śā́śadāna distinguish one's self, prevail. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_zad.html"> √ 2 śad    √ 2 śad, “fall” Future Simple Future: śatsyati AV Periphrastic Future: śattā Aorist Th Ao: aśadat Perfect śaśāda śedus B Causative śādaya- Desiderative śiśatsa- Intensive śāśad- Verbal Nouns PPP: śanna S Derivatives śada AV.B.S. śā́da V.B. śādana C. Compare √ śat, assigned by the grammarians to this root as another causative, and √ 1 śī, regarded by them as its present-system. Meanings Pf śaśāda, PPP śanna 2 fall, decay. vyava fall off or asunder. pari fall by the side. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zap.html"> √ śap    √ śap, “curse” Present I. śápati etc. V.+-te etc. B.+ IV. śapyati -te Passive śapyate C Future Simple Future: śapiṣye E. śapsyati -te Periphrastic Future: śaptā Aorist RAo: aśīśapat -s-Ao: śāpta (2p.) B.S. aśapta Perfect śaśā́pa śepus AV.+, śepé etc. V.+ Causative śāpayati etc. AV.+ Desiderative śiśapsa- Intensive śāśap- , śaṃśap- Verbal Nouns PPP: śapta B.+, śapita E.; Inf: śapitum E., śaptum E.; 1Abs: śaptvā, śapitvā E Derivatives śāpa E.+ śápana AV. śaptṛ́ AV. śapátha V.+ śapaná ŚB. Meanings śápati śápate v (śapyati), PPP śaptá (q.v.) & śapita curse, execrate, revile, scold, blame; Ā (P) curse one's self if, i.e. assert with an oath that not (yadi), swear by (I), conjure (A or D); implore, entreat for (A) by (I). Caus. śāpayati cause to swear, conjure by (I). abhi curse, blame, accuse; Caus. conjure. pari curse, blame, revile. prati curse in return. sam curse. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_zam.html"> √ 1 śam, śim    √ 1 śam, śim, “labor” Present I. śámant SV II. śamīṣva śamiṣva śamīdhvam B.S IV. śamyati etc. B., śimyati etc. B IX. śamnīṣe -īṣva -īthās B.; ścámnan RV. ? Aorist -iṣ-Ao: áśamiṣṭhās RV Perfect śaśamé -māná V.B. (śaśámate RV.) Verbal Nouns PPP: śamitá B Derivatives śáma RV. śíma B. śamitṛ́ V.B. śamiṣṭha S. śámī̆ V.B. śímī B. Compare the two following roots: √ 2 śam, √ 3 śam. Meanings śámati śamyati v PPP śamitá 1 labour, work; make ready, prepare (r.). Cf. śaśamāná. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_zam.html"> √ 2 śam    √ 2 śam, “be quiet” Present I. śamet E IV. śā́myati etc. B.+,-te etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: śamiṣyati Periphrastic Future: śamitā Aorist Th Ao: aśamat B RAo: aśīśamat etc. AV.+ -iṣ-Ao: aśamīt Precative: śamyāt Ao/Ps/3/sg: aśā̆mi Perfect śaśāma śemus B.+ Causative śamáyati AV.+,-te etc. B.+; śāmayati etc. E.+ (śāmyate E.+) Desiderative śiśamiṣa- Intensive śaṃśam- Verbal Nouns PPP: śāṃtá AV.+ 1Abs: śamitvā, śāṃtvā Derivatives śám ? V.+ -śāmaka C. śaṃti- AV. śamatha C. śama B.+ śāmya E.+ śā́ṃti AV.+ śamayitavya S. śamin C. śámana AV.+ śamitṛ E.+ śamayitṛ S.+ śamanīya S.+ Probably ultimately the same with the preceding: √ 1 śam. Meanings śāmyati śāmyate 2 v (śamati), PPP śāntá (q.v.) be quiet, still, or content; be allayed or extinguished; cease, desist, stop. Caus. śamáyati (śāmayati) quiet, still, pacify, allay, extinguish, subdue, destroy, kill. abhi cease, stop. samava Caus. pacify, still. upa cease, stop, be allayed or extinguished. Caus. tranquillize, pacify, cool, allay. vyupa & samupa cease, leave off. ni & pari Caus. appease, allay. pra become calm or tranquil, be extinguished, stop, cease. Caus. appease, quench, allay, subdue, kill, destroy. (prati Caus. appease, allay*). sam become thoroughly calm or pacified, make peace with (I saha), be allayed or extinguished, stop (trans. & intrans.). Caus. mitigate, calm, soothe, allay, extinguish, finish, kill, destroy. Cf. abhyupaśānta, avaśānta, upaśānta, praśānta, saṃśānta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_3_zam.html"> √ 3 śam    √ 3 śam, “note” Passive -śamyate etc. E.+ Perfect śemuṣī ? C Causative -śāmayati etc. E.+ (-śāmyate E.) Verbal Nouns PPP:-śāṃta S.; 2Abs:-śamya E.+ Derivatives -śāmana S. -śamaya C. -śāmayitavya C. Only with prefix ni-, except in the strange śemuṣī; hence obviously a specialization from the preceding root √ 2 śam, meaning “settle in one's mind”, or the like. Meanings śamayati 4 v & śāmayati w. ni note, perceive, hear, learn. – anuni, samanuni, abhini, upani, praṇi, vini, saṃni = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zal.html"> √ śal    √ śal, “leap” Present I.-śalant C Future Simple Future: śaliṣyate śa Periphrastic Future: litā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aśaliṣṭa Perfect śele Verbal Nouns PPP:-śalita C Only with prefix ud, and probably from √ śri, śṛ. Meanings śalati v w. ud 1 leap, jump, rise. Cf. ucchalant, ucchalita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zaz.html"> √ śaś    √ śaś, “leap” Present I. śaśati etc. C Future Simple Future: śaśiṣyati Periphrastic Future: śaśitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aśaśīt Perfect śaśāśa , śaśaśus Verbal Nouns PPP: śaśita C Derivatives śaśá V.+ Doubtless a denominative formation from śaśá. Only two or three occurrences. Meanings śaśati v leap. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zas.html"> √ śas, śās    √ śas, śās, “cut” Present I. śasatha S., śásanti B., aśasat C II. śasta (2p.) RV.; śāsti B.S., śā́sati -atu (3p.) B., aśāt (3s.) B Passive śasyáte etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: śasiṣyati B Periphrastic Future: śasitā Perfect śaśāsa śaśasus E Desiderative śiśāsiṣant S Verbal Nouns PPP: śasta E.; 2Abs: -śasya E.;-śásas B Derivatives -śas B. śásana V.+ śástṛ V.+ -śāstṛ B.S. śāsá AV.B.S. śasitṛ B.+ śastrá B.+ -śiśāsiṣu B. Meanings śásati śasti & śāsti v PPP śasta cut to pieces, slaughter. vi = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zaa.html"> √ śā, śi    √ śā, śi, “sharpen” Present III. śiśāti śiśīmasi śíśīte etc. V.+ (śiśanti -ntu S.) VI ? śyáti etc. V.B.S., śyāna B.S Passive śāya- Future Simple Future: śāsyati Periphrastic Future: śātā Aorist √-Ao: áśīta ? RV. aśāt; śāyāt -siṣ-Ao: aśāsīt Perfect śaśau -śaśāná AV Causative śāyaya- Desiderative śiśāsa- , śīśāṃsa- Intensive śāśā- Verbal Nouns PPP: śitá V.+ , śāta E.+; 2Abs:-śā́ya V Derivatives -śāna B.S. śāṇa ? C. -śiti V.B. śiśayá RV. Divided by BR. into two separate roots, with identical forms. Meanings śiśāti śíśīte śyáti v PPP śāta & śitá (q.v.) sharpen, whet; excite, make eager, strengthen, promote; communicate, impart; present with, help to (A of pers., I, D, or G of thing). ati strike at. ava rid of (A). ā help to, cause to partake of (L). ni sharpen, whet; offer, present; lay down, spread. sam sharpen, whet; excite, make eager or ready for (D). Cf. níśita, sáśita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_zaas.html"> √ 1 śās, śiṣ    √ 1 śās, śiṣ, “order” Present I. śāsati etc. E.+,-te E II. śā́sti śā́sati etc. (śiṣṭas etc. śāstána RV., śiṣyāt etc. U.S.+; aśāt B.+) V.+, śā́ste śāsīta śā́sāna etc. V.+ Passive śāsyate etc. E.+; śiṣyate etc. C Future Simple Future: śāsiṣyati -te etc. B.+ Periphrastic Future: śāsitā Aorist Th Ao: aśiṣat etc. V.B.U. (śiṣánt RV.), śiṣāmahi RV. (-he SV.AV.) RAo: aśaśāsat Perfect śaśāsa śaśāsus etc. V.+ (śaśādhi śaśās RV.) Causative śāsaya- Desiderative śiśāsiṣa- Intensive śāśās- , śeśiṣ- Verbal Nouns PPP: śiṣṭá V.+, śāsta S.+, śāsita E.+; Inf: śāstum S.+, śāsitum E.+; 1Abs: śiṣṭvā, śāsitvā C.; 2Abs: -śiṣya B.U.,-śāsya E.+ Derivatives śā́s RV. śā́sa RV. śā́sana V.+ -śiṣṭi V.B.S. -śis V.+ -śāsaka C. śāsanīya C. śāsitṛ E.+ śāsá V. śāsin C. śā́sus RV. śāstṛ́ V.+ śāsā́ RV. śā́sya V.+ śāsti C. śāstrá V.+ śiṣya B.+ Compare the apparently related root √ śaṃs. Meanings śā́sti śā́ste (śāsati śāsate) v PPP śiṣṭá 1 (q.v.), śāsta, & śāsita chasten, punish, correct, rule, govern, manage, direct, instruct, teach, order, command, announce, proclaim, foretell, avow, confess. anu teach, instruct, order, command (2A); direct, indicate; rule, govern (rājyam or svarājyam); chastise, punish. abhyanu indicate, designate. samanu teach, impart (2A); w. rājyam rule, bear sway. abhi indicate, direct, rule. ā Ā(P) wish, pray or hope for (A); expect from (Ab); āśíṣam & āśiṣas make supplication, utter wishes for (D or L). ud direct upwards (to the gods). pra instruct, teach, direct, order, command; dispose of, decide (A adhi ); rule, govern (rājyam). saṃpra w. rājyam bear sway, reign. vi give various instructions about (A). sam direct, bid, invite. Cf. ánuśiṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_zaas.html"> √ 2 śās    √ 2 śās, “cut” see √ śas. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zik_s.html"> √ śikṣ    √ śikṣ see √ śak. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zi_ggh.html"> √ śiṅgh    √ śiṅgh, “snuff” The occurrences of ucchiṅghana and upaśiṃhana in Suśr. are doubtless artificial. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zi_jj.html"> √ śiñj    √ śiñj, “twang” Present II. śiṅkte śiñjate etc. V.+, śiñjant C Future Simple Future: śiñjiṣyate Periphrastic Future: śiñjitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aśiñjiṣṭa Perfect śiśiñje Causative śiñjayati etc. B.S Verbal Nouns PPP: śiñjita E.+ Derivatives śiñjin C. śiñjā́ra ? RV. (n.pr.) Probably an imitative root. Meanings śiṅkte v PPP śiñjita (q.v.) twang, tinkle. vi warble. sam = S. Cf. āśiñjita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zip.html"> √ śip    √ śip, “be smooth” (?) Such a root may possibly be inferred from śípi V.+, śíprā RV. and śipitá ŚB. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zim.html"> √ śim    √ śim see √ 1 śam. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zi_s.html"> √ śiṣ    √ śiṣ, “leave” Present I. śeṣant C1 VI ? śiṃṣati etc. B.S VII. śináṣṭi etc. B.+ Passive śiṣyate etc. AV.+ Future Simple Future: śekṣyati -te B Periphrastic Future: śeṣṭā Aorist √-Ao: śeṣi AV.B.S. Th Ao: aśiṣat etc. V.B. (-śíṣat RV.), śíṣātai AV RAo: aśīśiṣat Precative: śiṣyāt Perfect śiśiṣe etc. B. śiśeṣa Causative śeṣayati etc. E.+,-te E. (śeṣyate C.) Desiderative śiśikṣa- Intensive śeśiṣ- Verbal Nouns PPP: śiṣṭá V.+; 1Abs: -śiṣṭvā S.; 2Abs: -śiṣya B.+;-śeṣam S.+ Derivatives -śiṣa C. śeṣa B.+ -śeṣin C. śéṣaṇa AV.+ -śeṣaka E.+ śeṣya C. śéṣas V. Meanings śináṣṭi śiṃṣati v PPP śiṣṭá (q.v.) leave; P. śiṣyate be left, remain, w. na want, be missing. Caus. śeṣayati, te leave, spare. ati leave remaining; P. remain. apa leave out. ava leave remaining (also Caus. ); P. be left, remain. ūd & pari the same. vi leave apart i.e. separate, distinguish, characterize. P. be distinguished by (I), differ from (Ab); be eminent among (G or L), be better or more excellent than (Ab or I). Caus. distinguish, characterize; pick out, prefer; exceed, surpass (A). pravi increase, augment. Cf. átiśiṣṭa, avaśiṣṭa, úcchiṣṭa, páriśiṣṭa (sic!), víśiṣṭa, sáśiṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_zii.html"> √ 1 śī    √ 1 śī, “fall” Present IV ? śī́yate etc. AV.B.U.S. (śīyánte ? ŚB1.) Derivatives -śāyana C. Reckoned by the grammarians as present-system to √ 2 śad; and this is curiously supported by JB., which has (ii. 81) upaśīyate tasmād upaśadam, and (ii. 82) avaśīyante tasmāc chadaḥ. So far as the meaning is concerned, it might well be a specialization of √ 2 śī. Meanings śī́yate 1 v fall, cease, perish. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_zii.html"> √ 2 śī    √ 2 śī, “lie” Present I. śáyate etc. V.+,-ti etc. E. (áśayat V.B.) aśāyatam -yata (3s.) RV II. śéte śérate etc. V.+ (śáye 3s. V.B., śére 3p. AV.B., śayire C.; śayām 3s. AV., áśeran V.B.) Passive śayyate ; śīyant M1 Future Simple Future: śayiṣyate -ti B.+; śeṣyate -ti E Periphrastic Future: śayitā U.C. (-tā́se ŚB.) Aorist RAo: aśīśayat E -s-Ao: śéṣan RV1 -iṣ-Ao: aśayiṣṭa etc. V.+ Ao/Ps/3/sg: aśāyi Perfect śiśye -yire B.+; śaśayāná V Causative śāyayati etc. S.+,-te E Desiderative śiśayiṣate C Intensive śeśī- , śāśay- Verbal Nouns PPP: śayita E.+; Inf: śayitum E.; 1Abs: śayitvā U.+; 2Abs: -śayya C.; śayádhyai RV Derivatives -śī V.B. śayyā B.+ -śāyana C. -śī́ma V.B.S. -śa ? B.+ -śāyaka C. śayú V. -śéyya V. -śaya V.+ -śāyin S.+ śayitavya C. śayālu C. śayā́ RV. śáyana AV.+ śayátha RV. -śī́van V.B. śayin C. -śayanīya C. -śītha E.+ śiśayiṣu C. Meanings śéte 2 v & śáyate (śáyati), PPP śayita (q.v.) lie, sleep, rest. Caus. śāyayati, te cause to lie down or go to sleep, lay down, put on or in (L). Des śiśayiṣate wish to sleep. ati sleep or go to rest before another (A); also = Caus. surpass, excel. vyati reach beyond, surpass (A). adhi lie in or on, mount, enter (A, r. L). anu lie on or in (A or L), lie down after another (A); rue, repent. abhi lie upon (A). ā lie in or on (A). anvā stretch, extend. pratyā lie before or in front of (A). upa lie by or on (A or L). pari lie about, surround, encompass; be at or in (A). pra lie down upon (A). sam be undecided or in doubt, despair of (L); P disagree about (A). Cf. atiśayita, saṃśayita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zuc.html"> √ śuc    √ śuc, “gleam” Present I. śócati etc. V.+,-te etc. V.+ II. śocimi E1 IV. śúcyati B1 Future Simple Future: śociṣyati etc. E.+,-te E Periphrastic Future: śocitā Aorist Th Ao: aśucat etc. V.+ (śucánt V., śucámāna RV.) RAo: śūśucat etc. AV.B -iṣ-Ao: śocīs B Precative: śucyāsam Ao/Ps/3/sg: áśoci RV Perfect śuśóca etc. V.+ (śuśukvā́ṃs RV., śuśugdhí V.), śuśucāná RV. (-cita RV.) Causative śocáyati etc. V.+ (śocyate C.); śucáyant RV Desiderative śuśuciṣa- , śuśociṣa-; śuśukṣa- (in d.) Intensive śóśuan etc. śóśucāna etc. V.B Verbal Nouns PPP: śuktá ? (adj.) B.+; Inf: śocitum E.+, śoktum M.; 1Abs: śocitvā E. śucitvā; śucádhyai RV Derivatives śúc V.+ śóka V.+ śocí V. -śúkvan RV. śucá RV.C. śoká AV. śucis- RV.C. śóciṣṭha RV. śúka ? V.+ -śócana AV.+ śocís V.+ śuśukvaná RV. -śoca AV. śocanīya C. śukti S.+ śuśukváni RV. -śocin C. -śokas RV. śocitavya E.+ -śuśukṣáṇi RV. śocya E.+ śúci V.+ śukrá V.+ -śocayiṣṇu AV. śuklá AV.+ Meanings śócati śócate (śúcyati 1 & śociti) v flame, light, shine, glow, burn; suffer burning pain; grieve at, mourn (A prati, L, or I). Caus. śocáyati inflame, burn (lit. & fig. = afflict); grieve at, mourn, regret (A). Int śócucan etc. flame brightly. anu grieve for (A), mourn with (A); Caus. = samanu bewail, deplore. apa Int flame away, remove by flaming. abhi burn, torment (also Caus. & Int); grieve, mourn. ā flame hither, bring by flaming. ud flame up. ni be burning hot. nis flame forth. pari feel grief or sorrow, mourn (absol. or trans. w. A). Caus. torment, afflict, bewail, deplore. pra shine forth (also Int). anupra bewail, deplore. prati flame against (A). sam flame together; lament, regret (also Caus. ). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zuj.html"> √ śuj    √ śuj, “swell” (?) Intensive śū́śujāna RV. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zudh.html"> √ śudh, śundh    √ śudh, śundh, “purify” Present I. śundhati -te etc. V.B.S II. śunddhi AGS IV. śudhyati etc. B.+,-te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: śotsyati śundhiṣyati Periphrastic Future: śoddhā śundhitā Aorist Th Ao: aśudhat RAo: aśūśudhat -iṣ-Ao: aśundhīt Perfect śuśodha , śuśundha Causative śodhayati etc. B.+ (śodhyate E.+); śundhayati V.B Desiderative śuśutsat S Intensive śośudh- Verbal Nouns PPP: śuddhá V.+ Derivatives -śodha C. śodhya C. śodhana S.+ śundhyú V.B. śodhaka E.+ śúndhana B. śodhanīya C. śodhayitavya C. śodhin C. śúddhi B.+ Meanings śundh , PPP śuddhá v (q.v.), śúndhati, PPP śuddhá (q.v.), śúndhate purify, Ā mostly intrans. or refl; śúdhyati(te) become pure or clear, be justified or excused. Caus. śodháyati purify (also śundhayati); mend, correct; wash or clear off, remove (what is impure or noxious); pay back, restore; examine, try; acquit, justify; make clear, explain. pari (śudhyati, te) become pure or clean, clear or justify one's self. Caus. pay back, restore; examine, try, explain. vi (śudhyati, te) become thoroughly clean or pure. Caus. clear, purify, purge, justify, mend, correct, improve. sam Caus. cleanse, purify; pay back, restore; mend, improve. Cf. pariśuddha, viśuddha, saṃśuddha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zubh.html"> √ śubh, śumbh    √ śubh, śumbh, “beautify” Present I. śóbhate etc. V.+ (śóbhe 3s. RV.),-ti etc. E.+; śúmbhase etc. V., śúmbhati etc. AV VI. śumbháti etc. V.C.,-ámāna RV.C Future Simple Future: śobhiṣyati E. śumbhiṣyati Periphrastic Future: śobhitā, śumbhitā Aorist √-Ao: śúmbhāna śubhāná RV Th Ao: aśubhat RAo: áśūśubhan RV.,-bhanta B -iṣ-Ao: aśobhiṣṭa, aśumbhīt Ao/Ps/3/sg: aśobhi C. Perfect śuśobha śuśubhe E.+ śuśumbha Causative śobhayati etc. AV.+; śubháyati -te etc. V.B Desiderative śuśobhiṣate C. śuśubhiṣa- Intensive śośubhyate E Verbal Nouns PPP: śubhitá B., śumbhita AV.; śubhé RV., śobháse RV Derivatives śúbh V.B. śumbha E.+ śumbhū́ B. śúbhvan RV. śubha E.+ -śumbhaka E. śobhátha SV. śóbhiṣṭha RV. śobha C. śóbhana V.+ śubhrá V.+ śobhayitṛ C. śobhā B.+ śobhaná B.+ śubhrí RV. -śobhin E.+ śúmbhana AV.+ This root is, with considerable plausibility, devided by BR. into two: √ 1 śubh “glide along”, and √ 2 śubh “beautify”; the former only in V.B. Meanings śumbh , śóbhate (ti); śumbháti, śúmbhate v (the nasalized forms more frequent in the Veda, the strong forms in l.l.) P adorn, embellish, prepare, make ready; Ā adorn one's self, or make one's self ready, look beautiful, make a show, shine, glitter (w. iva & yathā also look like, appear or seem to be). With na be unpleasant, look ugly. Caus. śobhayati (cf. also śubhay 2) adorn, embellish, cause to shine. ati look very beautiful, w. na displease. abhi Ā lay round or put on for ornament, also = samabhi shine, make a show; Caus. = S.Caus. upa , pari , prati , vi Caus. = S.Caus. sam Ā be beautiful or as beautiful as (I). Caus. adorn, embellish. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_zu_s.html"> √ 1 śuṣ    √ 1 śuṣ, “dry” Present IV. śúṣyati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: śokṣyati Periphrastic Future: śoṣṭā Aorist Th Ao: aśuṣat RAo: aśūśuṣat Perfect śuśoṣa Causative śoṣáyati etc. AV.+,-te E. (śoṣyate C.) Desiderative śuśukṣa- Intensive śośuṣ- Verbal Nouns -śúsya B Derivatives śuṣa ? V. śoṣin E.+ śoṣaṇa E.+ śúṣka V.+ śoṣa E.+ -śoṣya E.+ śoṣaṇīya C. śúṣṇa ? V.B.S. śoṣaka C. śóṣuka E. śoṣayitṛ C. Meanings śúṣyati (śúṣyaṃte) 1 v dry, wither, fade. Caus. śoṣayati (śoṣayate) make dry, dry up, parch, emaciate, afflict, destroy. anu dry by slow degrees or after another. ud , samud, upa , pari , vi , sam dry or shrink in; Caus. make dry, dry up. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_zu_s.html"> √ 2 śuṣ    √ 2 śuṣ, “blow” see √ śvas. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zuu.html"> √ śū, śvā, śvi    √ śū, śvā, śvi, “swell” Present I ? śváyati etc. V.B Passive śūyate Future Simple Future: śvayiṣyati Periphrastic Future: śvayitā Aorist Th Ao: áśvat B RAo: aśiśviyat, aśūśuvat, aśiśvayat -iṣ-Ao: aśvayīt Precative: śūyāt Perfect śuśāva , śiśvāya śūśuvus etc. (śūśuvat śūśávāma śūśuyā́ma) śūśuve śū́śuvāna RV Causative śvāyaya- Desiderative śiśvayiṣa- Intensive śośu- , śeśvi- Verbal Nouns PPP: śūná C.; Inf: śváyitum B.; śūṣáṇi RV Derivatives -śū ? RV. śáviṣṭha V.B. śivá V.+ śvayathu C. śáva B.+ śotha C. śéva V.+ śvātrá V.B. śāva E.+ śuná V.B.S. -śévas AV. śvāntá RV. -śvan V.+ śū́na ,-nyá V.+ -śvāyin B. śíśu V.+ śávas V.+ śū́ra V.+ śvayana C. -śíśvan RV. śavasāná RV. śávīra RV. śvayátha B. -śiśvi RV. The perfect forms in RV. are ascribed by BR. (perhaps with better reason) to a separate root śū “prevail”. The connection of a part of the derivatives given here with one another and with any assignable root is open to much question. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_z_r.html"> √ 1 śṛ    √ 1 śṛ, “crush” Present IV. śī́ryate ŚB VI. śṛṇa AV IX. śṛṇā́ti etc. V.B.C1., śṛṇāná RV1 Passive śīryate etc. V.+,-ti etc. U.E.+ Future Simple Future: śariṣyate B. śarī̆ṣyati Periphrastic Future: śarī̆tā Aorist RAo: aśīśarat -iṣ-Ao: aśarīt etc. AV.B. (-rait AV.) Precative: śīryāt Ao/Ps/3/sg: aśāri V.B. Perfect śaśāra śaśaritha śaśarus śaśrus śaśré AV Causative śāraya- Desiderative śiśariṣa- (in d.), śiśarīṣa-, śiśīrṣa- Intensive śāśṛ- , śeśīrya- Verbal Nouns PPP: śīrṇá AV.+,-śīrta MS., śūrtá ? RV1.; śárītos RV., śaritos AA.;-śī́rya B Derivatives -śir C. śīrya B.S. śárīra V.+ śīrti B. -śar AB. śū́la V.+ śarā́ru RV. śalúna AV. -śara V.+ śaraṇa C. śā́ri RV. śarabhá V.+ śará V.+ śaráṇi V. śáru V.+ śalala ,-lī́ B.+ śalá AV.B. śū́raṇa RV. śarvá AV.+ śalā́ka B.+ śalyá V.+ -śarīka AV. -śāruka B.C. -śiśariṣu C. Part of the derivatives are of very questionable belongings. Meanings śṛṇā́ti (śṛṇati) v PPP śīrṇá (q.v.) crush, break, tear, hurt, kill. P. śīryate (ti) be crushed or broken etc., go asunder, fall out or off, wither, moulder, decay, perish. api break off. ava break down (trans.); P. be shattered, vanish. ni break off. nis break asunder. parā break, crush. pari P. fly into pieces, burst. pra break off or asunder. vi P. be broken or scattered, fall into pieces, perish. sam break, crush, destroy; P. break down, be scattered or dispersed. Cf. avaśīrṇa, viśīrṇa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_z_r.html"> √ 2 śṛ    √ 2 śṛ see √ śrā. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_3_z_r.html"> √ 3 śṛ    √ 3 śṛ see √ śri. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_z_rdh.html"> √ śṛdh    √ śṛdh, “be defiant” Present I. śárdhati etc. V.,-te etc. B.C Future Simple Future: śartsyati śardhiṣyate Periphrastic Future: śardhitā Aorist Th Ao: aśṛdhat RAo: aśīśṛdhat -iṣ-Ao: aśardhiṣṭa Perfect śaśṛdhe Causative śardháyati etc. RV.C Desiderative śiśardhiṣa- , śiśṛtsa- Intensive śarīśṛdh- Derivatives śárdha RV. śárdhya RV. śardhana C. -śardhayitṛ C. -śardhin V. śrdhyā́ RV. śárdhas V.B. Not worth dividing into two roots. Meanings śárdhati v fart (only w. ava & vi); be defiant or strong. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zcand.html"> √ ścand, cand    √ ścand, cand, “shine” Present etc I. candati, cacanda etc.etc Intensive cániścadat RV1 Derivatives candana ? E.+ ścandrá V.+ candrá V.+ The fuller form ścandra survives after V. only in the n.pr. háriścandra. Meanings only Int cániṣṛcadat shine, glance. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zcam.html"> √ ścam    √ ścam The single doubtful form ścámnan RV. was entered above under √ 1 śam. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zcut.html"> √ ścut    √ ścut, “drip” Present I. ścótati etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: ścotiṣyati Periphrastic Future: ścotitā Aorist Th Ao: aścutat RAo: acuścutat S -iṣ-Ao: aścotīt Perfect cuścota B.S Causative ścotayati etc. B.S. (-ścotayitavaí ŚB.) Desiderative cuścotiṣa- , cuścutiṣa- Intensive coścut- Verbal Nouns PPP: ścutita B.+ Derivatives -ścut V.+ -ścotana C. The forms are often, especially later, written with ścyu, and sometimes with cyu. Meanings later ścyut, ścótati 1 & ścyotati drip (trans. & intrans.); Caus. ścotayati only trans. abhi Caus. cause to drip or trickle; besprinkle. ava & vyava drip, drop or fall down. ni Ā ooze, trickle down. pra drip forth (trans. & intrans.); Caus. cause to drip or flow. vi drip out. Cf. ā́ścutita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_znath.html"> √ śnath    √ śnath, “pierce” Present I. śnathati II. śnathihi śnáthat RV Future Simple Future: śnathiṣyati Periphrastic Future: śnathitā Aorist RAo: aśiśnat śiśnáthat etc. RV -iṣ-Ao: śnathiṣṭam -ṭana RV Perfect śaśnātha Causative śnatháyati -te etc. RV Verbal Nouns PPP: śnathitá RV.;-śnáthas RV Derivatives śnáthana RV. śnáthitṛ RV. śiśnátha RV. Meanings (śnathiti) v PPP śnathitá pierce, perforate; Caus. = S. apa push back, repel. ni & parini strike down. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zyaa.html"> √ śyā, śī    √ śyā, śī, “coagulate” Present IV ? śā́yati B.,-te C Passive śīyáte etc. B Future Simple Future: śyāsyate Periphrastic Future: śyātā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aśyāsta Perfect śaśye Causative śyāpaya- ; śyāyayati GB Desiderative śiśyāsa- Intensive śāśyā- Verbal Nouns PPP: śītá V.+, śīná VS., śyāna C. śyāta Derivatives śyā́ TS.C. -śyāya E.+ śíśira ? AV.+ Meanings śyā́yati v PPP śītá, śīná & śyāna (q.v.) freeze, coagulate (trans.); P. śīyáta intrans. ā Ā dry (intrans.). Cf. āśyāna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zrath.html"> √ śrath, ślath    √ śrath, ślath, “slacken” Present I. śrathati śranthate; ślathati -te etc. C VI ? śṛnthati TS1 IX. áśrathnan śrathnās RV., śrathnīté etc. V Future Simple Future: śranthiṣyati Periphrastic Future: śranthitā Aorist RAo: śiśráthat etc. V.B. (śiśrathantu RV.) -iṣ-Ao: aśranthīt -thiṣṭa Perfect śaśrathe RV. śaśrantha śaśranthus śrethus Causative śratháyati etc. V.B.,-te RV.; ślathayati C. (ślathyate C.) śrāthayati, śranthayati Verbal Nouns PPP: śṛthitá RV., ślathita C.; 1Abs: śrathitvā, śranthitvā; 2Abs: -śrathya C Derivatives śratha- V. śrathar- RV. ślatha E.+ Meanings śrathnā́ti śrathnīté v & (– ṃ) śrṛnthati become loose, give way; make loose or weak, Ā untie. Caus. śratháyati slacken, release, give room; Ā become loose, give way. anu dissolve, Ā scatter about. Caus. let go or in peace. vi Ā & Caus. loosen, untie, release, remove, destroy. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zran.html"> √ śran    √ śran, “give” Present etc I. śraṇati etc.etc Causative śrāṇayati etc. S.+ aśiśraṇat, aśaśrāṇat; śraṇayati Derivatives -śrāṇana C. -śrāṇika C. Only with prefix vi. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zram.html"> √ śram    √ śram, “be weary” Present I. śramati -te etc. E.+ IV. śrā́myati etc. V.+ Passive śramyate E.+ Future Simple Future: śramiṣyati Periphrastic Future: śramitā M Aorist Th Ao: áśramat etc. V -iṣ-Ao: śramiṣma RV.B Ao/Ps/3/sg: aśrā̆mi Perfect śaśrāma śaśramus V.+ (śremus KB.), śaśramāṇá RV Causative śramayati etc. S.+; śrāmayati etc. E.+ (śrāmyate E.+) Desiderative śiśramiṣa- (in d.) Verbal Nouns PPP: śrāṃtá V.+; 2Abs: -śrámya B.+ Derivatives śráma V.+ śramaṇá B.+ śrāṃti E.+ -śiśramiṣu C. -śrāma E.+ -śramaṇa V.+ -śramiṣṭha RV. Meanings śrā́myati śramati śrā́myati śramate v PPP śrāntá (q.v.) be weary, take pains, exert or castigate one's self. Caus. śramayati or śrāmayati weary, tire, bring down, subdue. abhi weary, tire. upa rest, repose. pari take great pains, torment one's self. vi rest, recreate one's self; pause, cease; rely upon, trust in (L). Caus. cause to rest or repose; bring to rest i.e. appease, quench, finish. Cf. pariviśānta, pariśānta, viśānta, saṃśānta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zrambh.html"> √ śrambh    √ śrambh, “trust” Present I. śrambhate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: śrambhiṣyate Periphrastic Future: śrambhitā Aorist Th Ao: aśrabhat -iṣ-Ao: aśrambhiṣṭa Perfect śaśrambhe Causative śrambhayati etc. S.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: śrabdha E.+; 2Abs: -śrabhya C Derivatives -śṛmbhá RV. -śrambha E.+ -śrambhana C. -śrabdhi C. -śrambhin C. -śrambhanīya C. Meanings śrambhate v w. vi trust, confide, place confidence in (L). Caus. loose, untie; comfort, encourage. Cf. viśabdha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zraa.html"> √ śrā, 2 śrī, 2 śṛ    √ śrā, 2 śrī, 2 śṛ, “boil” Present II. śrāti IV ? śrā́yati etc. V.B IX. śrīṇā́ti etc. V.B Future Simple Future: śrāsyati Periphrastic Future: śrātā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aśrāsīt; Precative: śrāyāt Ao/Ps/3/sg: śreyāt Perfect śaśrau Causative śrapáyati etc. AV.+,-te etc. E. (aśiśrapat etc. B.; śrapyáte etc. B.+) Desiderative śiśrāsa- Intensive śāśrā- Verbal Nouns PPP: śrātá V.B.S.; śṛtá V.+ śrāṇa Derivatives śīrá ? RV. śáras ? B. -śrápa B. śrápaṇa B.+ śrāpin S. śrapayitṛ́ B. Meanings PPP śrātá & śṛtá (q.v.), Caus. śrapáyati (te) roast, boil, cook i.g. Cf. āśṛta, praśta (add.). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zri.html"> √ śri, 3 śṛ    √ śri, 3 śṛ, “resort” Present I. śráyati etc. AV.+,-te etc. V.+ Passive śrīyate etc. B.+ (śriyate etc. B.S.) Future Simple Future: śrayiṣyati -te etc. B.+ Periphrastic Future: śrayitā Aorist √-Ao: áśret -riyan etc. RV. RAo: áśiśriyat etc. AV.+ (aśiśret V.B.,-śrema S.,-śrayus RV.;-śriyus E.,-śriyan C.; śiśrītá ? RV.) -s-Ao: aśrait AV -iṣ-Ao: aśrā̆yiṣṭa Precative: śrīyāt Ao/Ps/3/sg: áśrāyi RV Perfect śiśrā́ya śiśriyé etc. V.+ Causative śrāpayati VS1. śrāyayati, aśiśrayat Desiderative śiśrayiṣa- , śiśrīṣa- Intensive śeśri- Verbal Nouns PPP: śritá V.+; Inf: śrayitum E.,-tavaí B.S.; 1Abs: śrayitvā E.+ śritvā; 2Abs: -śrítya B.+ Derivatives -śrī B.U. -śāra AV. śaraṇá V.+ śretṛ E. -śraya AV.+ śā́lā AV.+ -śrit V.+ śréṇi V.+ -śrayin C. śrayaṇa B.+ śrití RV.C. śárman V.+ śrāyá V.+ śrayaṇīya C. -śrayitavya C. śárīra ? V.+ The derivatives from the root-form śṛ are probably best referred to a separate root śṛ or śar, śal, meaning “cover” or the like. Meanings śráyati śráyate v PPP śritá (q.v.) P trans. lean, lay against or on, turn or transfer to, spread (esp. light) over (L); ĀP.(P) intrans. lean or rest upon, lie or be situated in or on, join one's self with (A or L); Ā(P) resort to, strive after (A); get entrance, befall (A or L); incur, undergo, get into a state or condition. adhi P spread over (A or L); put on (L, esp. on the fire agnau); lie or sit down upon (A). pratyadhi P place near (the fire). samadhi P (agnau) place over the fire. apa Ā lean, rest. abhi bring near; resort to (A). ā P fix on (L); touch, befall (A). PĀ cling to, lean or rest upon (A); resort or have recourse to, seek protection from, come to, arrive at; undergo, incur, get; partake of, choose, take to (A). apā P (trans.) lean against, hang on (L); PĀ (intrans.) lean or rest upon, have recourse to, take to, choose, seize, occupy. vyapā approach for protection; take to, use, employ. upā & samupā lean against, resort to, rest or depend on (A). samā the same + take to, indulge in (A); seize, occupy. ud P lift, raise; Ā arise, stand upright. Caus. ucchrāpayati lift, raise, increase, enhance. abhyud Ā rise, get up. pratyud rise against (A). samud lift, raise. upa P (trans.) lean against (L); Ā lean or rest upon (A); PĀ join, meet (A). pari lay about; enclose, fence, surround. pra lean forward or against; join with, add to (L). vi P put asunder, open, expand; Ā refl. sam P put together, mix, mingle, join (Ā refl.); Ā(P) betake one's self to, seek protection from, depend on, take to, partake of. abhisam seek help from or in; take to, partake of, use, employ (A). upasam go to meet, join, attend, depend on (A). Cf. ádhiśita, abhyúcchrita, āśita, úcchrita, praśita, procchrita (add.), sā́śata, samāśita, samucchrita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zri_s.html"> √ śriṣ    √ śriṣ see √ śliṣ. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_zrii.html"> √ 1 śrī, śṛ    √ 1 śrī, śṛ, “mix” Present IX. śrīṇā́ti śrīṇīté etc. V.B Aorist RAo: aśiśrayus RV Perfect śiśriye V Verbal Nouns PPP: śrītá RV., śīrta RV., 1Abs: śrītvā S Derivatives -śir V.B.S. -śira S.+ -śrī V. śrayaṇa S. Is probably only a form of √ śri, from which it is at some points hardly separable. The interrelations of the roots śṛ, śrā, śri, śrī are intricate, and not yet fully worked out. Especially doubtful is it what is the connection with them of the noun śrī́ V.+ “fortune”, and the related śriyás RV., śréyas V.+, śréṣṭha V.+, śremán B. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_zrii.html"> √ 2 śrī    √ 2 śrī see √ śrā. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zru.html"> √ śru    √ śru, “hear” Present II. śróṣi RV V. śṛṇóti etc. V.+, śṛṇuté etc. V.+ (śṛṇviṣé -viré RV.) Passive śrūyáte etc. V.+,-ti etc. E Future Simple Future: śroṣyáti etc. B.+,-te E Periphrastic Future: śrotā M Aorist √-Ao: áśravam -rot -ravan V.B. (śrávat -vathas etc. V.B.S.; śrudhí śrótu etc. V.B.) Th Ao ? śruvam TA RAo: aśuśruvat B.,-ravus RV. aśiśravat -s-Ao: aśrauṣīt etc. B.+ Precative: śrūyā́sam etc. V.C. Ao/Ps/3/sg: aśrāvi śrā́vi V.C Perfect śuśrā́va śuśruve etc. V.+ (śuśrumas U.+; śuśravat śuśrūyā́s -yā́tam áśuśravi RV.) Causative śrāváyati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ (śrāvyate etc. E.+); śraváyati etc. RV Desiderative śúśrūṣate etc. V.+,-ti etc. E.+ (śuśrūṣyate etc. E.+) Intensive śośru- Verbal Nouns PPP: śrutá V.+; Inf: śrotum E.+; 1Abs: śrutvā́ V.+; 2Abs: -śrútya AV.+;-śrāvam S.C Derivatives -śrū B. -śrā́vaṇa B.S. śrótra V.+ śuśrūṣaka E.+ śráva B.+ śrāvaṇīya E.+ śrāvitṛ E. śuśrūṣin E. śravya E.+ śrávas V.+ śrudhi- RV. śuśrūṣya E.+ śravā́yya RV. ślóka V.+ -śrúṇa RV. śuśrūṣaṇa E.+ śrāva V.+ -śrut V.+ śrómata RV. śuśrūṣéṇya B.S. śrāvaka C. śrúti V.+ śráviṣṭha AV.+ śuśrūṣú B.+ śrāvin C. śrútya V.+ śraúṣaṭ V.B. śuśrūṣitṛ E. śrāvya E.+ -śrótu RV. -śuśruka ? E. śuśrūṣitavya E. śrávaṇa V.+ śrotavyà B.+ śuśrūs E. -śrāvayitṛ U. śravaṇīya B.+ śrotṛ V.+ śuśrūṣā S.+ śrāvayitavya C. Compare √ śruṣ; for √ 2 śru, see √ sru. Meanings śrṛṇóti śrṛṇuté v PPP śrutá (q.v.) hear, learn (A) from (G, Ab, I, & mukhāt or śrakāśāt); hear – to be (2A); listen or give ear to (A of th. or G of pers.); hear a teacher i.e. learn, study. ĀP. be heard of, be known as or to be (2 N); be studied, taught, or read. Caus. śraváyati & śāváyati (te) cause a person to hear, i.e. address, inform of, communicate to, tell (A of thing & A, G, or D of pers.); let hear i.e. proclaim, announce, recite. Des śrúśūṣate (ti) wish or like to hear i.e. attend to, obey, wait on, serve (A). ati Ā be heard of i.e. be celebrated above (all). anu hear or learn (again); Caus. relate, tell (2A); DesĀ obey. abhi hear, learn – to be (2A). Caus. cause to hear, speak to, address (A). ā listen to (A of th., G or D of pers.); hear, learn; promise. Caus. proclaim, make known; address, invoke, summon. abhyā Caus. address. upa listen to (A or G), hear, learn from (mukhāt or sakāśāt), hear that – is (2A). samupa hear, listen to (A or G), learn from (Ab). pari hear, learn, understand that – is (2A). pra Ā be heard; become known or famous. prati listen or give ear; say yes, promise. Caus. answer. vi hear, learn; P. be heard of, become known or famous. Caus. let hear, announce, proclaim, tell; make known or famous, make resound. sam hear (mukhāt), listen to (A); accede to the request of, make a promise to (L or D). Caus. let hear, announce, proclaim; make resound. abhisam hear, learn. pratisam make a promise to (G). Cf. abhiviśuta, abhiśutá, āśuta, pariśuta, víśuta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zru_s.html"> √ śruṣ    √ śruṣ, “hear” Present I. śroṣan RV., śroṣantu V., śróṣamāṇa RV. Derivatives śruṣṭí RV. śrúṣṭi AV. śraúṣṭi V.B. A secondary root, growing out of the s-aorist-stem of √ śru. Meanings (śroṣati śroṣate) ā v hear. Cf. śróṣamāṇa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zlath.html"> √ ślath    √ ślath see √ śrath. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zlaa.html"> √ ślā    √ ślā, “dissolve” (?) Present IV. ślāyati JB Only in the passage tasmāt ... vī ’va ślāyanti taruṇam iva hi tarhi reto bhavati JB. ii. 23. Probably a variant to √ śrā. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zlaagh.html"> √ ślāgh    √ ślāgh, “extol” Present I. ślā́ghate etc. ŚB1.E.+,-ti E Passive ślāghyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: ślāghiṣyate Periphrastic Future: ślāghitā Aorist RAo: aśaślāghat -iṣ-Ao: aślāghiṣṭa Perfect śaślāghire C Causative ślāghayati etc. E.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: ślāghita C Derivatives ślāghā B.+ ślāghin E.+ ślāghana E.+ ślāghiṣṭha B. ślāghya E.+ ślāghanīya E.+ Meanings ślāghate (ślāghaṃti) v trust, have confidence in (D), speak confidently, brag, boast of (I or L); praise, extol. Caus. ślāghayati comfort, console, praise, extol. sam brag, boast of (I). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zli_s.html"> √ śliṣ, śriṣ    √ śliṣ, śriṣ, “clasp” Present I. śreṣāma RV. (√ śri?) IV. ślíṣyati etc. B.+,-te U Passive śliṣyate etc. C Future Simple Future: ślekṣyati Periphrastic Future: śleṣṭā Aorist Th Ao: aśliṣat E.+, śriṣat RV RAo: aśiśliṣat -sa- Ao: aślikṣat Perfect śiśléṣa B.+ Causative śleṣayati etc. B.+,-te C Desiderative śiślikṣa- (in d.) ? Intensive śeśleṣ- Verbal Nouns PPP: śliṣṭa B.+; Inf: śleṣṭum C.; 1Abs: śliṣṭvā C.; 2Abs: -śliṣya E.+;-śríṣas V Derivatives -śriṣ AV. -śreṣiṇa AV. śleṣin B.C. -śreṣman AV. -śliṣ B.C. śleṣa AV.+ -śleṣaṇa B.+ śleṣmán B.+ -śréṣa AV.B. śleṣaka C. -śiślikṣu ? AV. Meanings ślíṣyati ślíṣyate v p. śliṣṭa (q.v.) adhere, cling or stick to (L, r. A); clasp, embrace; melt or join together (trans. & intrans.). Caus. śleṣayati join, close. ā stick or cling to (L or A); approach, touch, clasp, embrace. Caus. fasten on (L), embrace, encircle. upā clasp, grasp. samā cling to (A), embrace. Caus. join, unite. upa cling to (A), step near (samīpam). Caus. bring or draw near, join with (saha). vi get loose or unfastened; fall asunder or aside, miss the aim; also = Caus. disjoin, separate from, deprive of (Ab). sam cleave or stick to (A), step near, approach, clasp, embrace; bring into immediate contact with (I). Caus. join, connect, put together, bring into contact with (I or L), transfer to (L). abhisam cling together (anyónyam); Caus. join tight or closely. upasam connect, unite. Cf. ā́śliṣṭa, úpaśliṣṭa (sic!), viśliṣṭa, sáṃśliṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zva_jc.html"> √ śvañc    √ śvañc, “spread” Present I. śváñcate etc. V. (śmañc- TA.) Aorist RAo ? śaśvacaí RV Causative śvañcáyas RV Derivatives -śvaṅka B. Meanings śváñcate v open (intrans.) for (D), receive with open arms. Caus. śvañcáyati cause to open or burst. ud = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zvas.html"> √ śvas, śuṣ    √ śvas, śuṣ, “blow” Present I. śvásati -te etc. AV.+ II. śvasiti etc. V.+ (śvasihí AV.+; aśvasīt B.+, aśvasat E.+); śuṣántam śuṣe śuṣāṇá RV Future Simple Future: śvasiṣyati E Periphrastic Future: śvasitā Aorist RAo: aśiśvasat -iṣ-Ao: (or Pr.). śvasīs C Perfect śaśvāsa etc. E.+ Causative śvāsayati etc. V.+ (śvasayati C1. ?) Desiderative śiśvasiṣa- Intensive śā́śvasat RV Verbal Nouns PPP: śvasita B.+, śvasta E.+; Inf: śvasitum E.; 2Abs: -śvasya S.+;-śvásas RV Derivatives -śvasa AV. śūṣá V.B.S. -śvāsana E.+ śvasátha V.B. śvāsa V.+ śóṣa ? VS. -śvāsanīya C. śúṣma V.B. śvāsin B.+ śvasaná V.+ śvási- RV. śuṣman C. -śvāsya E.+ -śvasanīya C. -śvasitavya B.+ Meanings śvásiti śvásati śvásiti śvásate v PPP śvasta 1 & śvasita (q.v.) blow, bluster, hiss, whistle, snort, breathe, sigh. Int only śā́śvasat snorting. abhi blow hither, hiss, whistle, groan. ā , paryā, pratyā, & samā get breath, recover, become quiet. Caus. quiet, comfort. ud hiss, pant, gasp, groan, sigh; breathe upwards or out; stop or pause from (Ab), recover; heave (intrans.), get loose, open, expand. Caus. cause to take breath, refresh, lift up; tear, rend asunder, interrupt, disturb. proda pant, breathe heavily. samud take breath, recover; rise, spring up. Caus. lift swell (trans.). ni & vini hiss, pant, sigh. nis hiss, pant, breathe out or in, sigh. vinis hiss, pant, snort; heave a sigh. pra blow forth or in, exhale or inhale. Caus. cause to breathe; quiet, comfort. abhipra blow forth upon (A). vi have confidence, be fearless, trust in (L, G, or A). Caus. inspire confidence (A). ativi have (too) great confidence in (L or A). abhivi Caus. inspire confidence. parivi Caus. quiet, comfort. Cf. ucchvasita, niśvasita, pariviśvasta (add.), viśvasta, samucchvasita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zvaa.html"> √ śvā, śvi    √ śvā, śvi see √ śū. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_zvit.html"> √ śvit    √ śvit, “be bright” Present etc śvetate ; śiśvite Future Simple Future: śvetiṣyate Periphrastic Future: śvetitā Aorist √-Ao: aśvitan śvitāná RV RAo: áśiśvitat RV -s-Ao: aśvait RV -iṣ-Ao: aśvetiṣṭa Verbal Nouns PPP: śvitta Derivatives -śvit V.C. śvetá V.+ śviti- RV. śvítna RV. śvetanā́ RV. śvitrá V.+ Meanings (śvetate) v be bright, shine. ava shine down. vi = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root__s_thiiv.html"> √ ṣṭhīv    √ ṣṭhīv, “spew” Present I. ṣṭhīvati etc. AV.+ IV. ṣṭhīvyati Future Simple Future: ṣṭheviṣyati Periphrastic Future: ṣṭhevitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aṣṭhaviṣam ? GB.S. aṣṭhevīt Perfect tiṣṭheva B. ṭiṣṭheva Causative ṣṭhevayati Desiderative tiṣṭhīviṣa- ṭiṣ-, tuṣṭhyūṣe ṭuṣ- Intensive teṣṭhīv- , ṭeṣṭhīv- Verbal Nouns PPP: ṣṭyūta B.+, ṣṭhīvita C.; 2Abs: ṣṭhutv S.;-ṣṭhīvya C Meanings ṣṭhīv , ṣṭhīvati, PPP ṣṭhayūta v spew, spit. abhi bespit. ni spit out. abhini & avani spit out upon (A). vini, nis , pra spit out. prati bespit. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sak_s.html"> √ sakṣ    √ sakṣ For the participle sákṣant, see √ sah. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sagh.html"> √ sagh    √ sagh, “be equal to” Present V. ásaghnos RV Future Simple Future: saghiṣyati Periphrastic Future: saghitā Aorist √-Ao: sághat RV.; saghyāsam B.S RAo: asīṣaghat -iṣ-Ao: asā̆ghīt Perfect sasāgha Causative sāghaya- Desiderative sisaghiṣa- Intensive sāsagh- Derivatives sághan B. Doubtless another form of √ sah. Meanings saghnoti v be equal to or a match for; undergo, incur. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sac.html"> √ sac    √ sac, “accompany” Present I. sácate, etc. V.B.,-ti RV1 sáścasi etc. saśce RV III. síṣakti etc. RV.; sáścati (3p.) RV., saścata (3p.) RV Future Simple Future: saciṣyate Periphrastic Future: sacitā Aorist √-Ao: sacāná RV -s-Ao: asakṣata etc. (sakṣat -ṣīmáhi) RV -iṣ-Ao: asaciṣṭa Perfect secire AV.; saścima V.B., saścus etc. RV., saściré RV Verbal Nouns sacádhyai RV.; sakṣáṇi ? RV Derivatives -sā̆c V.S. sā́cya RV. sācí ? V.B. -sakra RV. -saca V.B. sacaná RV. sákhi ? V.+ sakṣáṇi RV. sácā RV.B. sacas- RV. sacátha RV. saścát V. -sācin B.+ sáci V.+ sákman ,-mya RV. sācayá ŚB. Meanings sácate v (sácati), síṣakti, sáścaci (sáścacite) be united, have intercourse with, deal with, be possessed of or obnoxious to (I); belong, be attached or devoted to, attend on, accompany, follow, pursue, visit (A); help to (D); stay or be in (L). anu go after, follow, pursue; stick to (A). apa withdraw, escape. abhi seek, turn towards (A). ā & upa seek, look for (A). ni be closely connected with (I) pra pursue. prati pursue with vengeance. sam be united or connected with (I). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_saj.html"> √ saj, sañj    √ saj, sañj, “hang” Present I. sájati etc. V.+,-te S Passive sajyáte etc. B.+,-ti E.; sajjate etc. E.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: saṅkṣyati Periphrastic Future: saṅktā Aorist RAo: asasañjat -s-Ao: sāṅkṣīt etc. U.+, ásakthās -ta V.B Precative: sajyāt Ao/Ps/3/sg: asañji B. Perfect sasañja B.+ (sasajus sasañjus C., sasajjatus ? M., sejus ŚB.) Causative sañjayati etc. E.+; sajjayati etc. E.+,-te E Desiderative sisaṅkṣati ŚB. siṣaṅkṣa- Intensive sāsaj- , sāsañj- Verbal Nouns PPP: saktá V.+; Inf: saktum E., saṅktos B.; 2Abs: -sajya B.+;-sáṅgam B.S Derivatives -saj V. saṅga V.+ -sañjana B.+ sakti V.+ -saja RV. saṅgin AV.+ -sañjanīya C. sáktu ? V.+ -sajya C. -saṅgya B.S. sajjana C. -saktavya C. -sañja C. -saṅktavya C. Meanings saj , sájati, sájate, PPP saktá v (q.v.) P trans, hang on or together; Ā intrans. hang on (A), cleave or stick to (L); P. sajyáte hang on (L), sajjate (ti) be hung on or attached to (L); cleave, stick; lag, tarry; be intent upon or devoted to (L). Caus. sañjayati attach, connect with (L); sajjayati fix on, attach to (L); copulate i.e. prostitute. vyati mix or join mutually. anu hang or stick with (I), add; P. anuṣajjate hang on, adhere or cling to (A or L), devote one's self to or occupy one's self with (L). abhi utter a curse; lay a claim upon (L). ava P hang or fasten upon, commit or transfer to (L). P. avasajyate be hung or fastened; avasajjate cling or attach one's self to. ā hang or suspend on (L); impose upon, transfer to (L); lean on, cling to (A), follow close to a person's (A) heels (also āsajjate). Caus. suspend, cause a pers. (intrans.) to hang or put on (L); appoint to (loc). vyā get engaged in a quarrel or fight. samā hang on or round; lay (a change) on, commit or transfer to (L). ni Ā hang round (one's self) on down. pra P attach (one's self) to (L); hang, stick, or furnish with (I); approach as an enemy, engage in a quarrel with (L); (cause to) happen, occur, or result. P. (in both forms) cling or stick to, be occupied with (L). saṃpra (sajyate, ti), be attached to (L). vi P hang on, suspend; P. (ṣajjate) be devoted or attached to (L), esp. to the world or to a beloved person; be followed close by (I). sam (sajjate, ti) stick, adhere, cling to (L); get into a quarrel or fight with (I), attack, assail (A); stop, falter (voice); flow together, join; be engaged, commence (fight). Cf. átiṣakta, ánuṣakta, ā́ṣakta, níṣakta, prasakta, víṣakta, vyátiṣakta, vyāsakta (add.), saṃsakta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sad.html"> √ sad    √ sad, “sit” Present I. sī́dati etc. V.+,-te etc. RV1.E.+ II. sátsi V Passive sadyate B Future Simple Future: satsyati etc. B.S.; sīdiṣyati C Periphrastic Future: sattā Aorist √-Ao: sā́di RV Th Ao: ásadat etc. V.+ (sádathas RV., sadas etc. V.+, sadeyam etc. V.B.S., sadatu etc. sádatam V.B.S., sádant RV., sadantām AV., sādat- RV.) RAo: asīṣadat etc. B -s-Ao: sátsat RV -iṣ-Ao: asādīt TA Ao/Ps/3/sg: ásādi RV Perfect sasā́da sedús etc. V.+ (sasáttha RV.; sasadyāt AV.; sīdatus E.), sedire RV Causative sādáyati etc. V.+,-te etc. V.+ (sādyate etc. B.+; sisādayiṣa- in d.) Desiderative siṣatsa- Intensive sāsad- Verbal Nouns PPP: sanná AV.+, sattá V.; Inf: sattum B., sīditum E.; 2Abs: -sádya V.+;-sádam RV.,-sáde V.B.;-sādam B Derivatives sád V.+ sādín AV.+ sādi E. sanni C. sada B.+ -sādya E.+ sedí AV.B.S. sádman V.+ -sádya V.B.S. sádana V.+ -sandī ? AV.B.S. sadmán RV. -sádya n. V.B. sā́dana V.+ seduka E. -sádvan V.S. -sadyā ŚB. -sādanīya E.+, satti V.+ -sadvará B.S. sādá V.+ sádas V.+ sáttṛ V.B.U. -satsnu RV. -sādaka E.+ -sádi AV. sattrá V.+ sādayitavya E.+ -sisādayiṣu E. The stem sada, so far as accented sáda, is perhaps rather a present-stem. Meanings sī́dati 1 v (te), PPP sattá & sanná (q.v.) sit, seat one's self (esp. for a sacrifice) on, at, or in (A or L); lie down, around or in wait for (A); sink beneath a burden, feel ill, become feeble, tired or languid, be overcome, fall into trouble, distress, or despair; decay, vanish. Caus. sā́dayati cause to sit down; set or place in, at, or on (L); afflict, distress, bring down, ruin, destroy. ati die. anu sit down after another. ava stand opposite, threaten, menace (A). ava descend upon (A); sink down, fall away, grow lean or feeble, get into trouble or distress, despair, perish. Caus. sink (trans.), depress, bring down, afflict, pain, overcome, destroy. ā sit upon or near (A or L) preside over (A); waylay, watch; get to, arrive at, approach (as friend or foe), meet with, find, hit, gain, obtain. Caus. cause to sit down upon, set or place in (L or A), appoint to (Inf); cause, produce; approach, come near (A), encounter, meet with; overtake, attack, assail; get or fall into (A); gain, obtain; visit, befall; use, apply. adhyā sit down upon (A). abhyā the same; reach, attain. upā sit down upon (A). Caus. approach, obtain, receive. nyā sit down near, in, or upon (L or A). pratyā be near or imminent. samā get to, reach, attain; come near, approach (L or A); meet, encounter; attack, assail. Caus. = S. ud withdraw from (A), escape (G); disappear, perish. Caus. put aside, remove, extinguish, destroy; smear, anoint upod & pratyud betake one's self to (A). samud Caus. destroy, ruin. upa sit upon (A) or near; approach (as foe, pupil, or supplicant). Caus. put down or beside; get, obtain. abhyupa Caus. get to, attain. pratyupa sit down near (A). samupa betake one's self to, reach, attain (A). ni (ṣīdati) sit or lie down, take one's seat (r.), be seated upon (L), perform by sitting i.e. celebrate (a Sattra); sink, perish. Caus. cause to sit or kneel down; constitute, appoint (2A). adhini settle down in (L). abhini settle down about or near (A). upani approach, set about (A). parini sit or stay around. vini sit down separately. saṃni sit down (together). pari (ṣīdati) sit down about, surround, invest, besiege. pra decay, decline, fall into the power of (A); become clear (lit. & fig.), cheer up; be soothed or appeased; pardon, forgive, be gracious or favourable, deign to (Inf), succeed or speed well. Caus. clear, brighten up, gladden, soothe, appease, make favourable, beg pardon, ask for or to (Inf, D, or L, arthe or artham). abhipra settle down. Caus. propitiate, gladden, ask. saṃpra cheer up, be gracious or favourable. Caus. propitiate, make favourable. vi (ṣīdati be perplexed or dejected, despair, despond. Caus. vex, grieve, bring into despair. sam sit together with (I) upon (A); Ā settle down, shrink, perish, be dejected or distressed. Caus. set down (together); meet, join (A); depress, make sad. Cf. avasanna, ā́sanna, āsādya, útsanna, upasanna, niṣaṇá, níṣatta, pratyāsanna (add.), prasattá, prasanna, viṣaṇa, saṃsanná, samāsanna, samāsādya. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_san.html"> √ san, 2 sā    √ san, 2 sā, “gain” Present I ? sánat etc. sánema sána sánant RV VIII. sanóti etc. V.B.S Passive sanyate , sāyate Future Simple Future: saniṣyáti V.B Periphrastic Future: sanitā Aorist √-Ao: asāta Th Ao: asanam etc. V.B. (sanéyam etc. B.S.; sanem B.S.) RAo: asīṣaṇat -s-Ao ? seṣam set B -iṣ-Ao: asāniṣam RV. (saniṣat etc. V., sániṣantu SV.), asaniṣṭa (saniṣāmahe sániṣanta RV.) Precative: sanyāt, sāyāt Perfect sasā́na RV. (sasavā́ṃs V., sasanúṣī B.S.) sene Causative sānayati Desiderative síṣāsati etc. V.B. sisaniṣa- Intensive sansan- , sāsā-, saniṣṇata RV Verbal Nouns sātá V.B Derivatives -san RV. sani V.B. sanitr V.B. sanéru ? RV. sána RV. -sani V.+ sanítra RV. sánīyas B. sína ? RV. sānuká RV. sanutṛ RV. sániṣṭha RV. -sānin C. saniti RV. sanítvan RV. sānasí RV. -sanana RV. sanitva RV. sátvan ? V.+ sásni V.B. siṣṇu RV. -sā V.B. -seya V. sā́tu ? RV. siṣāsátu RV. -sa RV. sātí V. sāman ? V.+ siṣāsáni RV. siṣāsú V.B. Different from this is the root seen in sána “old” V.+ and the related words. Meanings sanóti v (sánati), PPP sātá win, conquer, acquire; receive as a present, possess, enjoy; win for another, procure, grant, bestow. Des síṣāsati wish to acquire, strive after; wish to present or bestow. ā win. pra Ā win = be successful. sam gain, acquire. Cf. abhíṣāta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sap.html"> √ sap    √ sap, “serve” Present I. sápati -te etc. V.B Future Simple Future: sapiṣyati Periphrastic Future: sapitā Aorist RAo: sīṣapanta RV Perfect sepus RV Causative sāpáyant ? B Derivatives -sāp RV. sápa B.S. sapar- V.+ sápti V.+ -sapin RV. The relations of part of these are very doubtful. Meanings sápati sápate 1 v follow after, be attached or devoted to, serve (A). Caus. Ā & abhi Ā = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sarj.html"> √ sarj    √ sarj, “creak” Present I. sárjati etc. V.B. Does not appear to admit of connection with √ sṛj. Meanings sárjati v creak. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sazc.html"> √ saśc    √ saśc see √ sac. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sas.html"> √ sas    √ sas, “sleep” Present II. sásti etc. (sastás sasánt etc.) V III. sasásti TS., sásasti VS., sasat C1 Future Simple Future: sasiṣyati Periphrastic Future: sasitā Aorist RAo: asīṣasat -iṣ-Ao: asā̆sīt Perfect sasāsa Causative sāsaya- Desiderative sisasiṣa- Intensive sāsas- Derivatives sasá ? RV. The single later occurrence is doubtless artificial. Meanings sásti sásasti sasásti slumber, be lazy or slothful. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sah.html"> √ sah    √ sah, “prevail” Present I. sáhate etc. V.+,-ti etc. E.+ (sáhant RV.); sā́hati etc. RV1.E1 II. sakṣi sákṣva sā́kṣva RV IV. sahyāmi M1 Passive sahyate etc. C Future Simple Future: sakṣyati etc. E.,-te B., sākṣye ? AV.; sahiṣyati -te etc. E.+ (asahiṣyat E.) Periphrastic Future: soḍhā E.+ sahitā Aorist √-Ao: sahāná RV.; sāhyā́ma V., sahyās etc. RV RAo: asīṣahat -s-Ao: asākṣi sākṣi RV., asakṣmahi B. (sākṣate RV.; sākṣīya etc. AV.B.), sākṣīt GB. (sakṣati AV., sakṣat RV., sā́kṣāma RV., sákṣat Part. RV.) -iṣ-Ao: ásahiṣṭa RV., sā̆hiṣīmáhi etc. V Perfect sehe (sehāná RV.; sasahe AV.; sasāhé etc. V.; sāsahāná V., sāsahīṣṭhā́s RV.), sehima -hus E. (sāsā́ha V.; sāsáhat etc. V., sāsahyā́ma etc. RV., sāsahvā́ṃs RV., sasahvā́ṃs TA., sāhvā́ṃs RV.) Causative sāhayati etc. E.+ Desiderative sī́kṣati -te etc. RV.TS. sisahiṣa- Intensive sāsah- Verbal Nouns PPP: sāḍhá V.+, soḍha C.; Inf: soḍhum E.+, sahitum E.; 1Abs: sāḍhvā, sahitvā; 2Abs: -sáhya V.+;-sáham B.; sáhadhyai RV.K Derivatives -sā̆h V.+ -sabha? E.+ séhu ? AV.K. sáhyu RV. sáha V.B. siṃhá ? V.+ sā́ḍhi MS. sahiṣṇu E.+ sahá V.+ sáhan ? RV. soḍhavya C. sáhvan B.S. sahaka C. sahana C. sahitavya E. sakṣa B. -sahya SV.+ sahanīya E.+ sā́ḍhṛ RV. -sakṣin RV. -sáhyan. RV. -sāhana E.+ soḍhṛ E.+ sakṣáṇa RV. sāhá V.+ sáhantya V.B. sáhuri V. sakṣáṇi V. -sā́ha RV. sáhas V.+ sáhīyas V.+ sāsahí V. -sāhin C. sahasāná RV. sáhyas RV. -sā́hya V.+ -sāhi C. sáhiṣṭha V.B. Meanings sáhate (sáhaṃti) 1 v PPP sāḍhá & soḍha overpower, win (battles), be victorious; be capable of or able to (Inf or L); master, withstand, suppress; bear, suffer, endure. Caus. sāhayati (mostly – ṃ) cause to endure, make supportable.* Des sī́kṣate wish to overcome. abhi overwhelm, subdue; violate (a woman); bear, suffer, pardon. ud hold out, endure; be able to or capable of (Inf prati, L, or D). Caus. urge on, impel to (L). abhyud be a match for (A), be able to (Inf), incline to (D). prod Caus. encourage, excite, impel. samud be able to (Inf); Caus. = prec. Caus. nis overpower. pra vanquish, master, check, restrain; bear, endure; be able to (Inf). saṃpra master, restrain, control, bear, suffer. prati resist, overcome. vi (ṣahate) overcome, sustain, withstand, resist, bear, suffer; be able to (Inf). sam be a match for, withstand, overcome. Cf. prasahya. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_saa.html"> √ 1 sā, si    √ 1 sā, si, “bind” Present I ? sāmi santi seyam set M V. asinot JB.,-sinvant RV. ? VI ? syáti etc. V.+,-te etc. V.+ IX. sinā́ti etc. V.B.U Passive sīyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: sāsyati siṣyati M. seṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: sātā, setā Aorist √-Ao: asāt etc. V.B. (sāhi sitam RV., sīmáhi RV.TS. ?) RAo: asīṣayat -s-Ao: asaiṣīt, aseṣṭa -siṣ-Ao: asāsīt Precative: seyāt Perfect sasau C.; siṣāya RV. (siṣet ? RV.) siṣye Causative sāyáyati etc. B.+ Desiderative siṣāsa- , sisīṣa- Intensive sāsā- , seṣi- Verbal Nouns PPP: sitá V.+; Inf: sātum JB., sétave AV.,-situm C.; 1Abs: sitvā S.; 2Abs: -sā́ya V.+,-sya E.+;-saí RV Derivatives -sā ? RV.+ -seya C. -sya E. setavya C. -sāya E.+ -sā́na V.+ -siti V. ? C. setṛ́ RV. -sāyin B.+ -sātṛ RV.C. sétu V.+ -sinva ? RV. It is not practicable to separate the two forms of this root. Its prevailing use with ava has led to its reduction to mere s in some of the forms made from it. Meanings si , syáti, syáte v (only – ṃ), sinā́ti (sinoti), PPP sitá (q.v.) bind. Caus. sāyáyati (only – ṃ). abhi fetter, destroy. ava unbind or unharness (the horses), turn in, stop, stay; go home or to rest; cease, finish, end; fix or insist upon (A); decide, ascertain. adhyava cease, stop, finish; fix upon (A), choose; resolve, venture, undertake (A, L, or Inf); suppose, conjecture; regard as, take for (2A). Caus. settle, determine. anvava stick or resort to, strive after, long for (A). udava set out (esp. from the place of sacrifice), conclude, finish; move off to (L). upāva settle down near (A). nirava Caus. furnish or satisfy with (I). paryava result, amount to or end in (L or A w. prati). vyava dwell separately; be at variance, differ; be persuaded or convinced of (A), regard as, take for (2A); decide, determine; settle, ascertain, resolve upon, undertake to (A, D, or Inf). samava decide for, fix upon (A). ud fetter, catch. vi make loose, untie, unyoke, open, set free. Cf. átiṣita (add.), adhyavasita, ávasita, útsita, paryávasita, prasita, vyavasita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_saa.html"> √ 2 sā    √ 2 sā see √ san. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_saadh.html"> √ sādh, sadh    √ sādh, sadh, “succeed” Present I. sā́dhati -te etc. RV IV. sādhyati V. sadhnoti etc. JB.; sādhnoti Future Simple Future: sātsyati Periphrastic Future: sāddhā Aorist RAo: sīṣadhāti -dhas etc.-dhema -dhātu V.B -s-Ao: asātsīt Perfect sasādha Causative sādháyati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ (sādhyate etc. E.+; siṣādhayiṣati etc. sisādh- C.) Desiderative siṣātsa- Intensive sāsādh- Verbal Nouns Inf: sādhitum (Caus. ?) C Derivatives -sādh RV. sādhyá V.+ sādhú V.+ sādhayitavya V. sā́dha RV. sā́dhana V.+ sā́dhu RV. sādhayitṛ C. sādhaka E.+ sādhanīya E.+ saddhi JB. siṣādhayiṣā C. sādhin C. sā́dhas V. sādhīyas B.+ siṣādhayiṣu S.+ sā́dhiṣṭha RV.U. Meanings sādhati sādhate 1 v come or lead straight (to the aim); succeed, be accomplished, give way, obey; direct, put in order, effect, accomplish, finish. Caus. sādháyati, te = S. tr ; also get, procure, acquire, recover (a debt), win, subdue; pay (taxes); make, render (2A); set out, go away. upa Caus. subdue, conquer; prepare (food). pari = prec ; obtain, recover (money). pra Caus. put in order, arrange, adorn, perform, accomplish, make one's own, acquire, win; find out, prove, demonstrate. sam subdue, conquer, make one's own, win, acquire, get, obtain, procure, perform, accomplish, prepare (food); recover (money), dismiss (a guest). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_si.html"> √ si    √ si, “bind” see √ 1 sā. From a root or roots si or sī appear to come sundry doubtful derivatives, as sā́yaka E.+, sénā V.+, sī́tā V.+, sīmán -mant -mā AV.+, sīrá V.+ 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sic.html"> √ sic    √ sic, “pour out” Present I. sécate RV1 VI. siñcáti etc. V.+,-te etc. V.+ Passive sicyáte etc. V.+,-ti E Future Simple Future: sekṣyati -te etc. B.E Aorist Th Ao: asicat etc. V.+,-cata etc. V.B. (sicāmahe V.B.) RAo: asīṣicat, asīsicat -s-Ao: asikta Precative: sicyāt B. (siñcyāt ? AŚS.) Ao/Ps/3/sg: aseci B.S Perfect siṣeca siṣice etc. V.+ (sisicus RV., sisice RV.C.) Causative secayati etc. S.+,-te S.+; siñcayati E1 Desiderative sisikṣa- , siṣikṣa- Intensive sesic- Verbal Nouns PPP: siktá V.+; Inf: sektum E.,-tavai B.; 1Abs: siktvā B.+, siñcitvā C.; 2Abs: -sícya AV.+;-secam S.,-sekam S Derivatives síc V.B.S. -sekin C. sécana V.+ séktṛ V.+ -sícya B. -sekyà B.+ -secanī́ya B. -secitṛ E. -sicya n. B. -secaka E. siktí V.B. siktha C. séka V.+ -secya E. sektavya C. Meanings siñcáti siñcáte v PPP siktá 1 pour out, sprinkle, scatter (also semen); pour in or upon (L), besprinkle with (I); cast (molten metal), form into (2A). Caus. secayati sprinkle, water. anu pour in or on (L). abhi pour upon, sprinkle, bathe, consecrate (Ā refl.); Caus. the same. samabhi sprinkle, wet, consecrate. ava pour upon, sprinkle, water; Caus. also bleed (trans.). ā pour or fill into, discharge one's self (river), pour off or out. Caus. pour into or to. avā & abhiparyā pour into (L). samā & abhisamā pour or shed together. ud pour upon, fill up, overfill. P. overflow, be puffed up, be haughty or arrogant. upa pour upon, sprinkle. ni pour down or in; infuse, instil; water, irrigate. Caus. sprinkle, wet. nis & parā pour or shake off, remove. pari pour around or upon; pour out or into another vessel. Caus. sprinkle, wet. pra pour out or upon; fill (a vessel); wet, moisten. P. be wetted or refreshed; flow forth. Caus. pour in. vi spill, shed. sam pour together, mingle; sprinkle, water. Cf. utsikta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_sidh.html"> √ 1 sidh    √ 1 sidh, “repel” Present I. sédhati etc. V.+,-te etc. S.+ Passive sidhyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: setsyati E., sedhiṣyati C Periphrastic Future: seddhā, sedhitā Aorist RAo: asīṣidhat -s-Ao: asaitsīt -iṣ-Ao: asedhīs etc. RV.E Ao/Ps/3/sg: asedhi C Perfect siṣedha etc. V.+, siṣidhe E Causative sedhayati etc. S.+ Desiderative sisedhiṣa- , sisidhiṣa-, siṣitsa- Intensive séṣidhat RV Verbal Nouns PPP: siddha B.+; Inf: seddhum B.+; 2Abs: -sídhya AV.+ Derivatives sedha AV.+ -sedhya C. -siddhi C. -seddhra B. -sedhaka E.+ -sedhana E.+ -seddhavya E.+ sidhmá ,-man ? B.+ -sedhin C. -sedhanīya C. -seddhṛ B.+ -sedhayitṛ C. See the following root: √ 2 sidh. Meanings sédhati sédhate 1 v drive off, scare away. apa & ava = S. ā Caus. āsedhayati cause to be arrested. vyā keep off, prevent. ud drive aside. ni drive away, keep off, hinder, prevent, forbid. Caus. ward off, keep back, interdict, deny. nis drive away. pra PĀ drive on. prati drive away, ward off, seek to divert from (Ab); omit, suppress; prevent, forbid, refuse, deny. Caus. ward off, keep back, refuse, forbid, deny. saṃprati keep back. Cf. pratiṣiddha, vipratiṣiddha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_sidh.html"> √ 2 sidh    √ 2 sidh, “succeed” Present IV. sídhyati etc. RV1.U.S.+,-te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: setsyati -te etc. E.+ Periphrastic Future: seddhā Aorist Th Ao: asidhat RAo: asīṣidhat -s-Ao: saitsīt C1 Precative: sidhyāsam Ao/Ps/3/sg: asedhi Perfect siṣedha RV1. ? Causative sedhaya- Desiderative siṣitsa- Intensive seṣidh- Verbal Nouns PPP: siddha B1.E.+ 1Abs: sedhitvā, sidhitvā, siddhvā Derivatives -sidh RV. siddhi U.+ sidhmá RV. -sídhvan RV. sidhrá RV. Appears to be a weakened form of √ sādh. Grassmann, however, considers √ 1 sidh and √ 2 sidh as one root, and there are in fact some difficulties in their separation. Meanings sídhyati (sídhyate) 2 v PPP siddha (q.v.) reach an aim, hit the mark; succeed, be fulfilled or accomplished; result, follow, be valid, boot, avail; submit to, obey (G); reach the highest aim, become perfect or blessed. abhi succeed, be accomplished or perfected; acquire, obtain. pra succeed; result, follow. sam succeed, be accomplished; become perfect or blessed. Cf. prásiddha, saṃsiddha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sii.html"> √ sī    √ sī see √ si. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_siiv.html"> √ sīv, syū    √ sīv, syū, “sew” Present IV. sī́vyati etc. V.+,-te V Future Simple Future: seviṣyati Periphrastic Future: sevitā Aorist RAo: asīṣivat -iṣ-Ao: asevīt Perfect siṣeva Causative sevayati ; sīvayati C Desiderative siseviṣa- . susyūṣa- Intensive seṣīv- Verbal Nouns PPP: syūtá V.+; 1Abs: syūtvā S.; 2Abs: -sī́vya AV Derivatives syū́ B. seva B. sevitavya C. syuman V.B. sīvaka C. sevana B.+ sū́tra AV.+ syoná ? V.B.S. sīvya C. sīvana B.+ sūná V.B.S. The noun sūcī́(of which sūcay “point out” is a denominative) can hardly be connected with this root. Meanings sī́vyati sī́vyate v PPP syūtá (q.v.) seq. – vyati & ā sew together. ud sew in. pari sew around, wrap in. pra sew up. prati sew on. vi sew on in different places. sam sew together. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_su.html"> √ su    √ su, “press out” Present III. suṣvati (3p.) RV V. sunóti etc. V.+, sunuté etc. V.+ (sunviré RV.) Passive sūyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: soṣyati KŚS., saviṣyati ŚB Periphrastic Future: sotā AB Aorist √-Ao: sótu sutám etc. RV., suvāná svāná V. RAo: asuṣavus AB. asūṣavat -s-Ao: asauṣīt, asoṣṭa -iṣ-Ao: asāvīt, asaviṣṭa Ao/Ps/3/sg: ásāvi RV Perfect suṣā́va suṣumá etc. V.E., suṣvāṇá RV Causative sāvayati S Desiderative susūṣa- Intensive soṣu- Verbal Nouns PPP: sutá V.+; sótave RV.,-tos V.B.; 2Abs: -sútya B.+;-sūya E Derivatives -suva B. sávana V.+ sótu RV. somán RV. savá V.B.S. -sut V.+ sótva RV. sūya E. sāvá RV. -suti V. sotṛ RV. súrā ? V.+ -sāvin RV. sutya S.+ sútvan V. -sunva RV. -sāvya S.+ sutyā B.S. sóma V.+ súṣvi RV. Doubtless the same with √ sū, and the forms and uses of the two not always clearly distinguishable. Meanings sunóti sunute v PPP sutá 1 (q.v.) press out, extract, esp. the Soma. adhi = S. abhi press out, prepare or win by extracting. ā & vi = S. sam & abhisam press out together. Cf. prásuta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sul.html"> √ sul    √ sul (?) Only in the single form prá sulāmi TS.TB., for which VS. has prá tilāmi: see √ til. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_subh.html"> √ subh, sumbh    √ subh, sumbh, “smother” (?) Present VI ? sumbhan K IX. asubhnan TS Verbal Nouns PPP: subdha TS Derivatives sóbharī̆ ? V. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_suu.html"> √ sū, su    √ sū, su, “generate, enliven, impel” Present I. savati etc. E.+ II. sū́te súvate etc. V.+ (suvāná svāná ? RV.), sauti B.+, sū̆hi S IV. sūyate etc. B1.+,-ti etc. E.+ VI. suváti etc. V.B.U. (sva AV.TA.), suvate etc. B Passive sūyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: soṣyáti -te etc. B.+ (sū́ṣyant RV1.C1.), saviṣyati -te etc. E.+ Periphrastic Future: sotā, savitā Aorist RAo: asūṣavat, asuṣot MS.,-ṣavus TB -s-Ao: asauṣīt, asoṣṭa U.+ -iṣ-Ao: asāvīt etc. V.B. (sāviṣat V.B.) asaviṣṭa Ao/Ps/3/sg: asāvi Perfect suṣāva etc. E.+, suṣuvé etc. AV.+ (sasū́va V.) Causative sāvaya- Desiderative susūṣa- Intensive soṣavīti RV Verbal Nouns PPP: sūtá V.+, suta B.+ sūna; Inf: sotum, sū́tave V.,-tavaí AV., sávitave AV.; 1Abs: sūtvā́ B.+;-sūya E.+; 2Abs: -sútya ŚB Derivatives sū́ V.+ -savas B.S. sūtrī́ AV. -sū́ya AV.+ savá V.+ sū́ti V.+ strī́ ? V.+ sū́ra ? V. sávya ? n.pr. RV. -suti RV. savatha ? C. sūrí ? V.+ -savin C. sū́tu AV. -sūna S.+ sávīman V.B.S. sávana V.+ savitṛ́ V.+ sūnú V.+ -sū́van V. -súvana AV. -savītṛ RV. -sū́ma V. sūṣā́ AV. sūṣaṇā ? AV. Usually divided into two roots, √ 1 sū̆ “impel”, and √ 2 sū̆ “give birth” (the verb-forms of the former, with three or four sporadic exceptions, limited to the older language); but their forms and meanings are mixed beyond the possibility of successful separation. Meanings sū́te sauti suváti suváte (sūyate sūyati) v PPP sūtá 1 & sutá (q.v.) generate, beget, bring forth, enliven, impel, set in motion. apa sent or drive away. abhi consecrate for (A), endow with (I). ā hurt upon (D), send, bestow, procure. nis & parā drive away, remove. pra bring forth, produce, impel, set in motion, cause, bid. saṃpra & sam beget, bring forth, produce. Cf. prásūta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_suud.html"> √ sūd    √ sūd, “put in order” Present I. sūdate Future Simple Future: sūdiṣyati Periphrastic Future: sūditā Aorist RAo: asūṣudanta TS Perfect suṣūde , suṣūdima RV. (súṣūdati etc. súṣūdat etc. RV., suṣūdáta AV.) Causative sūdáyati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ Desiderative suṣūdiṣa- Intensive soṣūd- Derivatives -sūd RV. -sūdaka E.+ sū́dana V.+ sūdayitnú RV. sū́da V.+ sūdin B. Meanings sūdáyati sūdáyate v lead straight on, keep agoing; put in order, arrange, bring about; finish, kill, destroy. abhi , ni , vini & saṃni finish, kill, destroy. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_suurk_s.html"> √ sūrkṣ    √ sūrkṣ, “heed” Present I. sūrkṣati etc. B.S Future Simple Future: sūrkṣiṣyáti Periphrastic Future: sūrkṣitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: asūrkṣīt Perfect suṣūrkṣa Derivatives sū́rkṣya B. Meanings sūrkṣati v heed, care for (A or G). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_s_r.html"> √ sṛ    √ sṛ, “flow” Present I. sarati etc. S1.E.+,-te etc. E.+ III. sísarti sísrat etc. RV., sísrate (3p.) etc. V. (sísratus RV1.) Future Simple Future: sariṣyáti etc. V.+ Periphrastic Future: sartā Aorist Th Ao: asarat etc. V.B. (sárat etc. sára RV.) -s-Ao: asārṣīt, sarṣat AV Precative: sriyāt Ao/Ps/3/sg: asāri B. Perfect sasā́ra sasré etc. V.+ (sasṛva ŚB., sasṛvā́ṃs V.+, sasrāṇá RV.; sasṛmāṇá RV.) Causative sārayati-te etc. V.+ (sāryate etc. B.+; sisārayiṣa- in d.); saráyante RV Desiderative sisīrṣati etc. B Intensive sararé etc. RV. (sársrāṇa V.) Verbal Nouns PPP: sṛtá B.+; Inf: sartum C., sártave RV.,-tavaí RV.; 1Abs: sṛtvā́ B.+; 2Abs: -sṛ́tya B.+;-sā́ram B Derivatives sará V.+ saraṇa V.+ -sṛ́tya AV. sarámā ? V.+ saraka E.+ saraṇi C. -sṛtyā JB. sṛmará B.+ sárin ? RV. sā́raṇa B.+ -sártu RV. saráyu V.+ sā́ra V.+ -sāraṇīya C. -sartavyà B.C. sarirá B. sāraka B.+ sáras V.+ sártṛ B. salilá V.+ sārin B.+ sarít V.+ sṛ́tvan V.B. sarala ? E.+ -sārya C. sáru ? AV. -sṛtvara C. sasrá RV. sirā́ V.+ -sṛt V.+ sárma RV. sásri RV. sīrā́ RV. sṛtí AV.+ -sarman RV. -sisārayiṣu C. sárīman RV. Meanings sísarti sarati sísarti sarate v PPP sūtá (– ṃ P & pass.), & sū́rta (q.v.) run, glide, flow, hasten, speed (w. vā́jam & ājim run a race); go to, pass over (A). Caus. sārayati cause to run or flow, (liquify, melt*), set in motion; Ā sāráyate begin to flow. Des sisīrṣati wish to run. Int sarīsarti run hither and thither. anu flow or run towards, go along or after, follow, conform one's self to (A). Caus. bid follow, pursue. apa glide down from (Ab); roll back (paścāt, waggon); go off, cease, pass away. Caus. remove, take off or out. vyapa go asunder, withdraw. api flow upon (A). abhi run or flow near, approach (as friend or foe); visit (esp. of lovers). Caus. lead to, bring together with (A); Ā (follow, persecute*), give an appointment or make a love-visit. samava descend; withdraw from (Ab); (Caus. put to flight*). ā run near, come; attack (A). ud run away. Caus. drive away or asunder, cast off, remove, dismiss, give up. prod go off; Caus. drive away. samud send away, dismiss. upa come near, approach, visit (cf. abhi ); resort to (A). nis flow out, come forth, appear. Caus. turn out, expel, remove. abhinis & vinis = prec. parā run away. pari flow or run around, circumambulate (A), spread everywhere. pra go forth, spread, appear, begin (also P.), set out, go towards (A), pass away. Caus. stretch forth or out, expose, divulge. vipra extend farther. saṃpra Caus. stretch out, draw asunder. prati rush against (A); go back, return. Caus. bring back, remove, replace. vi run asunder, spread (Ā w. tanvṛm open or unveil itself); part with (I); come from (Ab or tas), rush against (A). Caus. send forth. pravi rush forth; run away, escape. sam flow together, go about, roam, wander (esp. from one existence to another). Caus. cause to wander or to be return bring together, introduce, fix in (L); put off, defer. abhisam stream together. Cf. anusṛta, anusṛtya, abhisṛta, pravisṛta (add.), prásṛta, visṛta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_s_rk.html"> √ sṛk    √ sṛk, “be pointed” (?) A root sṛk or sṛc inferable with plausibility from the Derivatives sṛká V.B. sraktí V.B.S. sṛkva C. sṛ́kvan V.+ srákva RV. sṛkvi E.+ 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_s_rj.html"> √ sṛj    √ sṛj, “send forth” Present I. sárjatas AV.,-anti C. (sarájant RV1?) VI. sṛjáti -te etc. V.+ Passive sṛjyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: srakṣyati -te etc. B.+ Periphrastic Future: sraṣṭā ? PB Aorist √-Ao: ásṛgran -ram RV.; ásarji V.B.S.; aṛjāná RV RAo: asīsṛjat, asasarjat -s-Ao: asrākṣīt etc. V.+ (asrāk V.B.C1., asrāṭ B., srās AV.; srakṣat B.), ásṛkṣi ásṛṣṭa etc. V.B Perfect sasarja sasṛré etc. V.+ (sasarktha C. sasarjitha sasraṣṭha sasṛjmáhe -jrire RV., sasṛgmáhe SV.; sasṛjyāt asasṛgram RV.) Causative sarjayati -te etc. B.+ Desiderative sisṛkṣati etc. B.+ (sisṛkṣmas C1.),-te GB Intensive sarīsṛj- Verbal Nouns PPP: sṛṣṭá V.+; Inf: sraṣṭum E.+; 1Abs: sṛṣṭvā B.U.; 2Abs: -sṛ́jya B.+;-sárgam B.,-sárjam B Derivatives -sṛj V.+ -sargin S.+ sṛ́ṣṭi V.+ sṛjayá -yā́ B. sráj V.+ sarjá B.+ sṛṣṭí ŚB1. sisṛkṣā C. sṛ́jya B.+ -sarjya E. sraṣṭavya C. sisṛkṣu E.+ sárga V.+ sárjana V.+ sraṣṭṛ V.+ sarjayitavya U.+ Meanings sṛjáti sṛjáte sárjati v PPP sṛṣṭá 1 (q.v.) let loose, hurl, throw, pour out, emit, send forth; create, produce, beget, make; procure, bestow; use, employ. Caus. sarjayati, te. Des sisṛkṣati, te wish to let loose, Ā (P) wish to create. ati hurl off, let loose, give up, dismiss, give leave (A); deliver, free from (2A); yield, grant, bestow; Ā create beyond or as something higher. anu let loose, dismiss, pour out; deliver, grant, bestow; create after (A). api add to, mingle with (L). abhi hurl upon (A), let loose, give free, deliver, abandon, promise, grant, bestow. ava shoot off, pour out, let flow, give up (prāṇān), deliver over, grant, bestow; send away, dismiss (Ā abdicate); remit, pardon; place in, fix on (L). abhyava dismiss, send forth to (A), let loose, let go (the reins). upāva shoot off, admit (esp. the calf to the cow), give over to (A). vyava hurl upon (G), set down, send away, dismiss; hang or fix on (L). samava hurl upon (L), let loose, let go, abandon, omit. ā shoot hither, pour in or out, admit (esp. to copulation). samā hang, fasten to (L), entrust to (L). ud cast, hurl, pour out, shed, take off, lay down, depose, place in (L); stretch out, expand, open, set free, send forth, dismiss, give up; relinquish, abandon, despise, repudiate, renounce, resign; omit, pass over; entrust, commit; produce, create. samud hurl, send forth, utter, throw down, cast away, take off; dismiss, set free, let go, relinquish, abandon, expose; deliver up, hand over. upa hurl, cast, let flow, pour upon; send or bring to (A or D); admit, add, augment; affect or visit with (I), vex, plague. nis pour out, let flow, set free, dismiss, deliver from (Ab), separate, remove. pra let run or flow, open, set free, indulge, give up, resign, quit, abandon. prati hurl against (lit. & fig.), send back. vi throw, shoot, hurl (lit. & fig.), pour out, send forth, dismiss, emit, utter; let loose, set free, deliver from (Ab); cast away, relinquish, abandon; despise, repudiate, renounce, resign, Ā cease from (Ab); yield, grant, bestow; create, produce. Caus. hurl, send forth, emit, utter, set free, leave alone, spare avoid, shun; abandon, expose; yield, grant, bestow, hand over (L); create, produce. anuvi, abhivi & prativi shoot at (A). sam shoot or throw with (I); bring together, mix, unite (Ā P. refl.); endow or furnish with (I); create. Cf. upasṛṣṭa, nisṛṣṭa, sáṃsṛṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_s_rp.html"> √ sṛp    √ sṛp, “creep” Present I. sárpati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ Passive sṛpyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: srapsyati etc. B.+, sarpsyati B Periphrastic Future: sarptā, sraptā Aorist Th Ao: asṛpat etc. AV.B RAo: asīsṛpat B. asasarpat -s-Ao: asārpsīt, asrāpsīt; asṛpta B.S Perfect sasarpa etc. B.+ Causative sarpayati etc. S.+ Desiderative sísṛpsati etc. V.+ Intensive sarīsṛpant C.,-pyate B Verbal Nouns PPP: sṛpta B.+; Inf: sarpitum E.+; 1Abs: sṛptvā B.; 2Abs: -sṛ́pya AV.B.S.;-sṛ́pas B.;-sárpam B.S Derivatives -sṛp B.S. -sarpaka S. sarpi B. sṛprá RV. -sṛpya C. -sarpin B.+ sarpís V.+ sasarparī́ RV. sarpá V.+ sárpaṇa V.+ -sṛpti C. sarīsṛpá V.+ Meanings sárpati sárpate v PPP sṛpta (q.v.) creep, crawl, glide. Caus. sarpayati & Des sísṛpsati only – ṃ; Int sarīsṛpyate creep to and fro. ati glide along or over (A). adhi & samadhi glide over (A). anu glide after or along, approach (A). samanu approach. apa & vyapa move off, recede. abhi steal upon (A). ava glide down (of the setting sun); steal upon, cover gradually (A). anvava glide after. upāva, paryāva & pratyava approach gently. vyava creep into (A). ā creep near. upodā creep forth. ud creep out or up, rise (lit. & fig.); move gently on. Des wish to rise. upod & vyud creep forth. samud arise, appear, begin. upa go gently to, steal upon, creep or fall into (A); move on, come near, approach (also sexually). samupa approach. nis & vinis creep out. pari go round, roam through. pra creep near or into, steal upon (A), move on, break forth, spread, proceed. prati creep back or into. vi move about or along (A); move asunder, dispense, spread, expand. sam creep along or into (A); move onward, approach. anusam creep after. upasam creep near, steal upon (A). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sev.html"> √ sev    √ sev, “attend upon” Present I. sévate etc. V.+,-ti etc. RV1.E.+ Passive sevyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: seviṣyati E.-te Periphrastic Future: sevitā Aorist RAo: asiṣevat -iṣ-Ao: aseviṣṭa Perfect siṣeve etc. E.+,-va C Causative sevayati C. (siṣevayiṣa- in d.) Desiderative siseviṣa- Intensive seṣev- Verbal Nouns PPP: sevita E.+; Inf: sevitum C.; 1Abs: sevitvā E.; 2Abs: -sevya C Derivatives sevā E.+ sevin E.+ sevana E.+ sevitavya B.+ sevaka E.+ sevya E.+ sevanīya C. sevitṛ E.+ siṣevayiṣu C. Meanings sévate v (sévati), PPP sevita stay by (A or L), inhabit, frequent, visit; serve, revere, worship; attend upon, devote one's self to (A); practise, use, employ, enjoy (also sexually). Caus. sevayati serve, worship. anu stay or dwell in; wait on, reverence. ā = S. samā devote one's self to (A), practise, use, employ. upa = S. abhyupa worship, revere. ni (ṣevate) stay in, have intercourse with (L); inhabit, visit, frequent, etc. = S. pari (ṣevate & sevate) visit, follow, obey, revere; practise, like. sam be together, stay at or with, dwell in, frequent, visit etc. = S. Cf. niṣevita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_skand.html"> √ skand    √ skand, “leap” Present I. skándati etc. V.+,-te C Passive skadyate Future Simple Future: skantsyati B Periphrastic Future: skanttā Aorist √-Ao: askan skán V.B. Th Ao: askadat RAo: acaskandat -s-Ao: askāntsīt B. (áskān skān B.S.) Precative: skadyāt Perfect caskánda V.+,-de E.+ Causative skandayati etc. B.+ Desiderative ciskantsa- Intensive kániṣkan caniṣkadat RV Verbal Nouns PPP: skanná V.+; Inf: skanditum; 1Abs: skanttvā; 2Abs: -skándya B.+,-skádya B.;-skáde -skádas RV.;-skándam AV.B Derivatives skanda V.+ -skandya B. -skádvarī B. skandhá AV.+ skandin B.+ skandana B.+ skándhas ? V.B. Meanings sakándati sakándate v PPP skanná leap, spring, spurt; drop, be spilled, fall; leap upon i.e. cover, impregnate. Caus. skandayati pour out, spill; omit, neglect. Int kániṣkan leaping (of frogs). ati (ska & ṣka) leap upon or over, fall down. abhi (ska & ṣka) leap upon (for copulation). ava spring or spurt down; spring towards or upon, attack, overpower. abhyava spring down, in, or out; meet with, encounter. samava S. & Caus. assail. ā leap, resort to, depend on (A); also = samā attack, assail. pari (ska & ṣka) leap about (also Int caniṣkadat); spill, scatter. pra spring forth, down, upon (A); spurt, drop, fall; attack, assail. sam drop or spring off. Cf. pariskanna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_skambh.html"> √ skambh, skabh    √ skambh, skabh, “prop,” Present I. skambhate V. skabhnuvánt B IX. skabhnā́ti etc. V.B. (skabhāna B.) Future Simple Future: skambhiṣyati Periphrastic Future: skambhitā Aorist RAo: acaskambhat -iṣ-Ao: askambhīt Perfect caskambha C1. (cāskámbha skambháthus -bhus RV.), caskambhe caskabhāná AV Causative skambhayati (skambhita C.) Verbal Nouns PPP: skabhitá V.; Inf: skambhitum; skabhitvī́ RV.;-skábhe RV Derivatives skabha- V.B. -skambhaka C. skámbhana V.B. skábhīyas RV. skambhá V.+ -skambhin E. Meanings skabh , skabhnā́ti v or skabhnóti, PPP skabhitá prop, support, fix; stop, restrain, obstruct. Caus. skabhāyáti = S. ā fix in or at (L). upa hold up by supports. prati hold stand against; lean upon (A). vi (ṣka) fix, establish; Caus. the same. Cf. pratiṣkábhe (add.). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sku.html"> √ sku    √ sku, “tear” Present II. skauti ŚB V. skunoti AV. skunute IX. skunāti, skunīte Passive skūyáte MS Future Simple Future: skoṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: skotā Aorist RAo: acuskavat -iṣ-Ao: askauṣīt askoṣṭa Perfect cuskāva cuskuve Causative skāvayati Desiderative cuskūṣa- Intensive coṣkūyáte etc. RV Verbal Nouns PPP: skuta RV.;-skā́vam Derivatives -skava AV. -skavana S. The doubtful form skuptvā in Ap. Dh. S. (i. 31. 24) perhaps belongs here; compare dantaskavana ib. ii. 5. 9. Meanings skauti skunóti skunāti v stir (trans.), rake up (fire), pick (teeth). Int coṣkūyáte rake together, accumulate. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sk_r.html"> √ skṛ    √ skṛ see √ 1 kṛ. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_skhal.html"> √ skhal    √ skhal, “stumble” Present I. skhalati etc. E.+,-te AB Future Simple Future: skhaliṣyati Periphrastic Future: skhalitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: askhālīt Perfect caskhāla caskhalus E.+ Causative skhalayati etc. C. skhālayati Verbal Nouns skhalita B.+ Derivatives skhala B.+ skhalana E.+ Meanings skhalati skhalate v PPP skhalita (q.v.) stumble, totter, waver, stammer, folter, eor, fail. Caus. skhalayati cause to falter (voice). pari , pra & vi = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_stan.html"> √ stan    √ stan, “thunder” Present I. stanati etc. AV.E.+-se C1 II. stanihi stan RV Future Simple Future: staniṣyati Periphrastic Future: stanitā Aorist Th Ao: atiṣṭanat -iṣ-Ao: astānīt AV Perfect tastāna tastanus Causative stanáyati etc. V.+ Desiderative tistaniṣa- Intensive taṃstanīhi AV Verbal Nouns PPP: stanita S.+; 1Abs: stanitvā C Derivatives -stana V.E. stanana C. stanátha RV. iṣṭáni ? RV. -stānaka ? C. stāmú ? RV. stanáthu AV. stanayitnú V.+ Compare √ 2 tan. Meanings stanati v mostly stanáyati, PPP stanita (q.v.) thunder, roar, sound. abhi , nis & pra = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_stambh.html"> √ stambh, stabh    √ stambh, stabh, “prop” Present I. stambhant C., stambhate etc. C.; stabhamāna AA V. stabhnoti etc. B IX. stabhnā́ti etc. V.+ (stabhāná V.B.) Passive stabhyate C Future Simple Future: stambhiṣyati Periphrastic Future: stambhitā Aorist Th Ao: astabhat RAo: atastambhat -s-Ao: astāmpsīt TB -iṣ-Ao: ástambhīt stámbhīt RV Precative: stabhyāt Ao/Ps/3/sg: astambhi C Perfect tastámbha tastabhús etc. V. (tastámbhat RV.), tastambhe etc. E.+ (tastabhāná V.B.) Causative stambhayati -te etc. E.+ (stambhayiṣa ? in d.) Desiderative tistambhiṣa- Intensive tāstabh- Verbal Nouns PPP: stabhitá V., stabdha B.+; Inf: stabdhum C.; 1Abs: stabdhvā́ AV.E., stambhitvā E.; 2Abs: -stábhya B.+;-stambham B Derivatives stambha V.+ stabha- RV. stámbhana B.+ -stambhayitṛ C. stambhaka , E.+ -stabhya C. stambhanīya E.+ -stambhayiṣu E. stambhin E.+ stabhu- RV. -stabdhi B.+ Compare the parallel and equivalent root √ skambh. Meanings stabh , stabhnā́ti, stabhnoti, stambhate v (ti), PPP stabhitá & stabdha (q.v.) prop, support, uphold, make firm or steady; Ā become firm or rigid. Caus. stambhāyáti & stambhayati, stabhnā́ti, stabhnoti, stambhate (ti), PPP stabhitá & stabdha (q.v.) prop, support, uphold, make firm or steady; Ā become firm or rigid. Caus. stambhāyáti & stambhayate = S., the latter also = make stiff or lame, paralyze, stun, obstruct, suppress. ava (ṣṭa) fix, fasten, prop, support, intrans. lean upon (A); seize, take prisoner, obstruct, shut up. paryava (ṣṭa) surround. samava (ṣṭa) raise up (fig.); lean upon (A). ud (tta) prop up, fix, establish. Caus. lift up, raise (lit. & fig.); excite, impel. upa erect, uphold, support. prati (ṣṭa) hold against, Ā intrans. vi (ṣṭa) fix, establish, raise (lit. & fig.), make firm, stiff, or immovable, stop, obstruct; lean upon (A). Caus. stop, hold back. sam confirm, strengthen, make stiff or rigid, stop, suppress. Caus. the same. abhisam, parisam & pratisam confirm, strengthen. Cf. avaṣṭabdha, úttabdha & úttabhita, prástabdha, víṣṭabdha & víṣṭabhita, saṃstabdha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_staa.html"> √ stā    √ stā, “be stealthy” Is inferable from the Derivatives stāyát AV.GB. stāyú VS. stéya V.+ stāmán ? AV. stāyāt JB. tāyú ? V. stená V.+ GB. reads stāyan; JB. has na stāyād bhavati ii. 24 (ter). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_stigh.html"> √ stigh    √ stigh, “mount” Present V. stighnoti -nuyā́t MS. stighnute Future Simple Future: steghiṣyate Periphrastic Future: steghitā Aorist RAo: atiṣṭighat -iṣ-Ao: asteghiṣṭa Perfect tiṣṭighe Causative steghayati Desiderative tiṣṭighiṣati MS. tistighiṣa-, tisteghiṣa- Intensive teṣṭigh- Verbal Nouns -stígham MS These forms are somewhat amended from the MSS. (which have stiṅnoti etc.): see Schröder in ZDMG. xxxiii. 195. Meanings stighnoti stighnute v proceed, stride. ati mount, ascend. pra rise. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_stim.html"> √ stim, stīm    √ stim, stīm, “be stiff” Present IV. stī̆myati Perfect tiṣṭema , tiṣṭīma; etc.etc Verbal Nouns stimita E.+ Compare √ styā. Meanings only PPP stimita stiff, motionless, inactive; n. Adv or as abstrans. (also tā f., tva n.). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_stu.html"> √ 1 stu    √ 1 stu, “praise” Present I. stávate etc. (stave 3s.) RV II. staúti stuvánti etc. V.+, stute stuváte etc. V.+ (stavīmi C1., stoṣi RV., stuvāná V., stávāna V., stavāná RV.) V. stunvanti etc. U.C., stunvāna U. stuṣé (1s.) V VI ? astuvat E., stuvate etc. AV.E Passive stūyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: stoṣyati etc. B.+ (astoṣyat etc. B.U.),-te etc. B.+; staviṣyati -te etc. V Periphrastic Future: stotā Aorist RAo: átuṣṭavam RV.,-ṭuvam JB. (tuṣṭávat RV.) -s-Ao: astauṣīt etc. B.+ (stoṣat etc. stoṣāṇi RV.), ástoṣṭa etc. V.B -iṣ-Ao: astāvīt etc. B.S Precative: stūyāt Ao/Ps/3/sg: ástāvi RV Perfect tuṣṭāva tuṣṭuvús etc. V.+ tuṣṭuva -ma, tuṣṭuvé etc. V.+ Causative stāvayati etc. B.+,-te C.; stavayati C1 Desiderative tuṣṭūṣita C Intensive toṣṭu- Verbal Nouns PPP: stutá V.+; Inf: stotum B.+, stótave RV.; 1Abs: stutvā́ AV.+; 2Abs: -stútya B.+,-stūya E.+; stavádhyai RV. stuṣé RV Derivatives -stu RV. -stāvya S. stút V.S. stotrá V.+ stáva V.+ stavana S.+ stutí V.+ stavátha RV. stavya E. -stavanīya S. stútya V.+ stóma V.+ stāva B.+ -stāvanā E.+ stotavya B.+ stavā́n ? RV. stāvaka C. stotṛ́ V.+ stuṣéyya RV. Meanings staúti stute stávate v (stavīti, stuvate, stuvati), PPP stutá (q.v.) praise, extol, celebrate, sing, chant. Caus. stavayati praise, stāvayate cause to praise. Des tuṣṭūṣati wish to praise. anu (ṣṭauti), abhi (ṣṭauti), upa & pari (ṣṭauti) = S. pra praise; put forward, commence, begin; also = prastāvayati mention. vi sing praises. sam sing or praise (together). abhisam & parisam praise, extol. Cf. prástuta, víṣṭuta, sáṃstuta. (stuka m. &) stúkā f. lock or tuft of wool or hair; poss. stukāvín. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_stu.html"> √ 2 stu    √ 2 stu, “drip” Such a root is with probability inferable from the derivatives, -stu RV. -stāva AV. stúkā V.B.S. stupá AV.B. stoká V.+ stū́pa V.+ 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_stubh.html"> √ stubh    √ stubh, “praise” Present I. stóbhati V.B.S. -te II. stobdhi (3s.) JB., stubhāná RV Future Simple Future: stobhiṣyate Periphrastic Future: stobhitā Aorist RAo: astuṣṭubhat -iṣ-Ao: astobhiṣṭa Perfect tuṣṭubhe Causative stobhayati RV.C1 Verbal Nouns stubdha B.S Derivatives stúbh V.+ -stobha B.+ stobhana C. stúbhvan RV. stubha E. stobdhavya JB. Seems related with √ 1 stu. Meanings stóbhati 1 v (te) utter a sound, shout, exult, warble, etc. anu follow in shouting. abhi add by shouting. vyava separate by sounds. pari shout around. pra incite by shouting. prati shout in return, re-echo. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_st_r.html"> √ stṛ    √ stṛ, “strew” Present I. starati etc. E.+ V. stṛṇóti stṛṇute etc. V.+ IX. stṛṇā́ti stṛṇīté etc. V.+ Passive stīryate etc. S.+,-ti M. ?; striyáte ŚB. staryate Future Simple Future: stariṣyati -te B.C Periphrastic Future: startā Aorist √-Ao: ástar star RV., astṛta AB. (stárate starāmahe RV.) RAo: atastarat -s-Ao: astārṣīt astṛṣi B.; stṛṣīya AV -iṣ-Ao: astarīs AV. astariṣṭa, stariṣīṣṭa Precative: staryāt Ao/Ps/3/sg: ástāri RV Perfect tastāra tastarus B.+, tastare -rare C. (tastriré AV., tistiré 3s. -rāṇá RV.) Causative stārayati etc. E.+ Desiderative tistīrṣate JB.; tustūrṣate B.U.S Intensive testīrya- , tastarya- Verbal Nouns PPP: stṛta V.+, stīrṇá V.+; stártave B.,-tavai B., staritavai B., stárītave AV.B.,-starītavaí B.; 1Abs: stṛtvā́ B.S., stīrtvā́ B.S.; 2Abs: -stṛtya E.,-stī́rya B.+;-stíre RV.; stṛṇīṣáṇi RV Derivatives stṛ́ ? RV. stárya B. -stārin AV.+ -stárītu RV. -stir RV. -staryà B. stáraṇa V.+ -staritṛ C. -stur RV. -stāra V.+ stṛ́ti B.+ stárīman RV. -stára V.+ -stāraka C. stṛtya B. -stṛṇa C. Meanings stṛṇā́ti stṛṇīté stṛṇóti stṛṇute 1 v (starati), PPP stīrṇá & stṛta (q.v.) strew (esp. the sacrificial straw), spread out; strew over, cover; throw down, overthrow. Des tústūrṣáte wish to throw down. abhi , ava & samava strew, cover. ā strew, spread, expand; cover, smear. samā strew over. upa lay or pour over, (ājyam) form a coating with the sacrificial butter, cover or wrap with (I), strew, expand; (ājyam) pour the sacrificial butter over, ni throw down. pari strew around, cover, spread, expand. pra strew, scatter, spread out. vi spread or stretch out, expand, diffuse; also = Caus. vistārayati amplify on (A). sam spread or expand (together), strew, cover. Cf. āstīrṇa & ā́stṛta, upastīrṇa, prástīrṇa, vistīrṇa & vistṛta, saṃstīrṇa & saṃstṛta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_st_rh.html"> √ stṛh    √ stṛh, “crush,” Present VI. stṛhant S1 Perfect etc. tastarha etc.etc Seems to be a variant of √ tṛh. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_styaa.html"> √ styā, stī    √ styā, stī, “stiffen” Present IV. styāyate etc. B.C Future Simple Future: styāsyati Periphrastic Future: styātā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: astyāsīt Precative: styāyāt styeyāt Perfect tastyau Verbal Nouns PPP: styāna C. stīta, stīma; 2Abs: -styā́ya B Derivatives stíyā RV. -styāya C. -styāyana C. stīmá AV. -stīmin AV.B. The last two derivatives perhaps rather from √ stim, stīm (or this from them). Meanings styā́yate v PPP styāna (q.v.) coagulate, stiffen, thicken, strengthen (intrans.). Cf. saṃstyāna. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sthag.html"> √ sthag    √ sthag, “cover” Present I. sthagati Future Simple Future: sthagiṣyati Periphrastic Future: sthagitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: asthagīt Perfect tasthāga Causative sthagayati etc. C Derivatives sthagaka C. sthagana C. Meanings sthagayati v PPP sthagita cover, hide, conceal. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sthaa.html"> √ sthā    √ sthā, “stand” Present I. tíṣṭhati etc. V.+,-te etc. V.+ (tiṣṭhāsam ? GGS.) Passive sthīyate etc. B.+ (asthāyiṣi C1.) Future Simple Future: sthāsyati -te etc. B.+ Periphrastic Future: sthātā etc. E.+ Aorist √-Ao: ásthāt etc. V.+ (sthāti sthā́thas stheyāma sthā́nt RV.), ásthithās -ita V.+, ásthiran V.B. Th Ao ? āsthat AV.K -s-Ao: sthāsīṣṭa; stheṣam B., -ṣus ? AV. asthiṣi -ṣata B.+ Precative: stheyāsam Ao/Ps/3/sg: asthāyi C Perfect tasthaú tasthe etc. V.+ Causative sthāpayati etc. V.+,-te etc. V.+ (átiṣṭhipat etc. V.B.;-sthā́pam B.; sthāpyate etc. B.+;-sthāpayiṣati B.) Desiderative tiṣṭhāsati etc. B.+ (tiṣṭhā́set ? ŚB.) Intensive tāsthā- , teṣṭhīya- Verbal Nouns PPP: sthitá V.+; Inf: sthā́tum B.+,-tos B.S.,-sthitum R.; 1Abs: sthitvā E.+; 2Abs: -sthā́ya V.+;-sthā́yam V.B Derivatives sthā́ V.+ -sthu V.+ sthā́man V.C. tiṣṭhāsā C. -stha V.+ -sthṛ B. sthemán B.+ tiṣṭhāsu C. -sthin AV.+ sthāyuka B. sthéyas V.+ sthāpaka E.+ -sthāya E. sthíti B.+ sthirá V.+ sthāpin C. -sthāyaka C. sthití ŚB1. sthāla ,-lī́ ? V.+ sthā́pya B.+ sthāyin B.+ sthātavya E.+ -sthā́van V.B. sthāpana E.+ sthā́na V.+ sthātúr RV. sthāvará B.+ sthāpanīya B.+ -sthi RV. sthātṛ V.+ sthāsnu S.+ sthāpitṛ C. stheya B.+ sthātrá V. tasthu C. sthāpayitavya E.+ -sthéya n B. sthāṇú V.+ sthāpayitṛ E.+ A number of derivatives are also made from a root √ sthū, which appears to be only a form of √ sthā. They are: sthūrá V.B. sthávira V.+ sthū́ṇā V.+ stháviman B. sthūlá AV.+ sthā́vira RV. sthū́ri ? V.B. sthávīyas B.+ -sthāva B. stháviṣṭha B.+ Meanings tíṣṭhati tíṣṭhate v PPP sthitá 1 (q.v.) stand, stay, stop, remain, wait; stand by (L), declare for (D); hold out or bear up against (G puras); continue in a condition or action (N, esp. of a pp ; ger., I or L), exist, be present; belong to (D or G); serve for (D); be turned to, rest on, abide in (L); enter, mount, ascend (A), spring or arise from (G or Ab); cease, desist from (Ab); remain unmentioned, be left aside (esp. imper.). Caus. sthāpáyati, te cause to stand, stop, arrest, restrain; put, place, set in (L r. A, w. vaśe subdue), appoint to (L or artham, r. A); commit, entrust to (L or haste); found, erect, build, establish; fix, settle, determine; make, render (2A). Des tíṣṭhāsati wish to remain in (I). ati rise over; rule, master (A). adhi stand upon, mount, ascend; stay, abide, be fixed or situated in (L or A); be founded or based upon (L); use, employ, show, betray; also = prec. samadhi direct, guide, rule, manage, carry on. anu stand still after or together with (L or A); stay, abide, sit down upon (A); follow, obey, conform one's self to, imitate, help, assist; carry on, practise, commit, perform, do. antar bar the way, obstruct, arrest. apa stand aloof, forsake (Ab). api stand in the way of (A). abhi set the foot upon, rise over, step towards or against (A), withstand, overcome. ava Ā (P) stand off, withdraw; be deprived of, miss (Ab); go down, descend; enter, come to (A or L); fall to one's (D) share; stop, stand still; abide or remain in (L); continue doing or being (ger., N, or I); exist, be present; begin, undertake, determine. Caus. cause to stand, stop, restrain; let stand, leave behind; put, place, lay etc. in or on (L); establish, fix, settle; strengthen, comfort. paryava Ā become strong or firm; penetrate, pervade. Caus. excite, comfort. pratyava Ā come back, return (w. punar); resist, oppose. Caus. w. ātmānam compose one's self. vyava Ā be separated, part from (Ab); stop, stay, remain; prepare for (D); be valid, pass for, appear as (N). samava Caus. stop, arrest; fasten, strengthen. ā stand on (L); mount, ascend; step into, enter; take one's place at, resort to (A); get to, partake of, enjoy (A); undergo, incur; take, choose, use, employ. Ā accede to, acknowledge; stand by, set a value upon (L). Caus. cause to ascend or enter, introduce; cause to stay, keep back; put, place, lay; bring near, procure; fix in. fasten to (L). anvā enter, ascend, attain (after one another). upā go to, have intercourse with (A); attend to, observe. samupā step near; attend to, practise. samā ascend, resort to, enter, stop, stay; prepare for, set about, take to, choose, use, employ, practise, execute. ud stand up, rise (esp. from a sacrificial acts, i.e. finish, close), awake, appear, sprout, grow. Ā raise one's self to, prepare for (D or L). Caus. cause to stand up, raise, scare up, awaken (from sleep or death); lift up, erect, establish; pull or draw out; send off, expel, incite, instigate, urge on, encourage. Des wish to rise. anūd rise after, follow. abhyud rise towards, go to meet (A); begin, undertake. upod rise before or to meet, approach, go to (A). prod spring up, rise, appear. pratyud rise up to meet (A). vyud rise up in different directions; turn from, give up (Ab); forget one's duty (Ā). Caus. call in question, disagree about (A); alienate, remove, depose. samud rise (together), come out of, spring from (Ab); appear, become visible; go about to work, prepare for (L or Inf). Caus. cause or bid to rise, lift up, rouse, awaken. upa stand by, near, opposite, or round (A); come near, approach, resort to, attend on, serve, worship; present with (I); be present or at hand, be to one's disposal or fall to one's (A or G) share. Caus. cause to stand near or opposite (A); fetch, bring near. anūpa step near (after one another), approach (A). abhyupa worship. Caus. bring near. paryupa stand around (A); attend with (I). pratyupa Ā stand opposite, attend on (A). samupa stand near, approach, fall to one's lot (A). ni Caus. fix in (L). parini Caus. teach thoroughly (G of pers.). nis grow forth, rise from (Ab); bring to an end, accomplish, prepare, make ready. Caus. drive out; prepare, make ready. pari stand around or in the way; obstruct, hinder; be left, remain. pra P (Ā) rise, stand upright, stand before (A); Ā be up or awake, (P) set out to go, depart from (Ab), betake one's self to (A prati or L). Caus. send out, dismiss, banish, put away. atipra rise above (A), be prominent. anupra set out after (A), follow; Caus. send after. abhipra go out in pursuit of, have in view (A prati), prevail over (A). Caus. drive out (cattle). vipra Ā (P) rise or set out (in various directions); go asunder, spread, expand. saṃpra Ā stand or step together (before the altar); set out to go, betake one's self to (A or L). prati stand, stay, remain; stand still or firm, be established or founded upon (L); get a place or foothold, thrive, prosper; withstand, resist; spread over (A). Caus. set up, erect, fix, support; place in or upon, appoint to (L); present, offer, entrust or commit to (L). anuprati get on, thrive or prosper after (A). saṃprati apply to (L). vi Ā (P) stand apart, go asunder, be spread in or over (A); part with or be separated from (Ab); stand firm, not budge. Caus. spread, extend. anuvi & abhivi Ā spread over, pervade (A). sam Ā(P) stand by, remain with (L, w. vākye obey); stand still, stop, stay; meet (as foes); come to an end or to perfection; succeed, prosper; perish, die. Caus. lift up, raise, strengthen, comfort (w. ātmānam compose one's self); fix, erect, build, establish, settle; bring on or in (L); check, restrain; get through, finish, kill. anusam go along, pursue. Ā be finished later. abhisam stand still or end with (A). Caus. cause to stand still or to end with. Cf. adhiṣṭhita, ánuṣṭhita, anusaṃsthita, ábhiṣṭhita, abhyutthita, abhyupasthita, avasthita, ā́sthita, útthita, úpasthita, upā́sthita, niṣṭhita, níḥṣṭhita (sic!), pariniṣṭita, páriṣṭhita, paristhita, paryavasthita (add.), paryupasthita, prátiṣṭhita, pratyupasthita, prásthita, protthita, víṣṭhita, vyavasthita, vyutthita, sásthita, samavasthita, samāsthita, samutthita, samupasthita, saṃpratiṣṭhita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_snaa.html"> √ snā    √ snā, “bathe” Present II . snā́ti etc. V.+, snāyīta E IV . snāyate etc. E Future Simple Future : snāsyati -te etc. E.+ Periphrastic Future : snātā Aorist √-Ao: snāyāt, sneyāt; asnāyi C -siṣ-Ao: asnāsīt Perfect sasnus C Causative snāpáyati etc. RV.S.+ , -te GB.; snapáyati etc. AV.+ Desiderative siṣṇāsa- (in d.) Intensive sāsnā- Verbal Nouns PPP: snātá AV.+; Inf: snātum B.+; 1Abs: snātvā́ AV.+; 2Abs: -snā́ya V.B Derivatives -snā V.C. snéya B.+ snā́tva V.B. snāpaka E.+ -sna E.+ snāna AV.+ snātavya E.+ snāpana E.+ snāyin E.+ -snātṛ V.C. siṣṇāsu E. snápana AV.+ Meanings snā́ti v (snāyate), PPP snātá (q.v.) bathe, perform ablution (esp. at the end of religious studentship or of a vow), smear or anoint one's self with (I). Caus. snapáyati or snapáyati cause to bathe, wet, dip in (L). ud step out of the water. ni be steeped or absorbed in (L). pra go into the water; Caus. bathe in (A). sam Caus. bathe (trans.), wash. Cf. niṣṇāta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_snih.html"> √ snih    √ snih, “be sticky” Present IV. snihyati etc. E.+ ,-te E.+ Future Simple Future : snehiṣyati, snekṣyati Periphrastic Future : snehitā snegdhā sneḍhā Aorist Th Ao: asnihat RAo: asiṣṇihat Perfect siṣṇeha Causative sneháyati etc. RV.C Desiderative sisnehiṣa- , sisnihiṣa-, sisnikṣa- Intensive seṣṇih- Verbal Nouns PPP: snigdha E.+ snīḍha; 1Abs: snehitvā, snihitvā, snigdhvā, snīḍhvā Derivatives sníh TA. snehin C. snīhán B. snī́hiti V. sneha B.+ snehya C. snehana E.+ snéhiti RV. snehaka C. snehayitavya C. Meanings snihyati snihyate v PPP snigdha 1 (q.v.) be supple, greasy, or moist; stick to, be fixed upon (L), have affection for, be fond of (L or G). Caus. sneháyati make greasy, supple, or submissive. upa (also snihyate) become supple or moist. Caus. conciliate, win over. Cf. prasnigdha. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_snu.html"> √ snu    √ snu, “distil” Present II. snauti etc. B.+ snute Future Simple Future : snaviṣyati snoṣyate Periphrastic Future : snavitā snotā Aorist R Ao : asnoṣṭa, asnāvīt; Passive"> Ao/Ps/3/sg : asnāvi Perfect suṣṇāva suṣṇuve Causative snāvaya- Desiderative susnūṣa- Intensive soṣṇu- Verbal Nouns PPP: snuta S.? E.+ Derivatives -snu RV. -snava E.+ -snāvin C. Meanings snauti v PPP snuta 1 distil, drop, flow (esp. of the mother's breast or milk). pra = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_spand.html"> √ spand    √ spand, “quiver” Present I. spandate etc. V.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: spandiṣyate Periphrastic Future: spanditā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aspandiṣṭa Perfect paspande Causative spandayati -te etc. B.+ Desiderative pispandiṣa- Intensive paniṣpad- (in d.) Verbal Nouns Passive Preterital Participle">PPP: spandita C.; spanditum C Derivatives spanda E.+ spandin C. spandaná AV.+ paniṣpadá AV. Meanings spandate spandati v PPP spandita (q.v.) quiver, throb, quake, kick (of animals), budge. Caus. spandayati (te) make quiver. ā, pari, pra, vi , sam quiver, shake. 
