   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sphaa.html"> √ sphā    √ sphā, “fatten” Present IV. sphāyate Passive sphīyate B Future Simple Future: sphāyiṣyate Periphrastic Future: sphāyitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: apisphavat, asphāyiṣṭa Perfect pasphāye Causative sphāvaya- (in d.) Verbal Nouns sphīta E.+ Derivatives -sphāka AV. sphātí V.B.S. sphirá RV. sphāvayitṛ AB. -sphā́na V.C. sphīti C. Meanings sphāyate v PPP sphīta (q.v.) grow, fat, swell, increase. Caus. sphāvayati fatten, enlarge, augment. ā grow, increase. vi swell. Cf. sáṃsphīta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sphu_t.html"> √ sphuṭ    √ sphuṭ, “burst” Present I. sphóṭati B.E VI. sphuṭati etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: sphuṭiṣyati etc. E Periphrastic Future: sphuṭitā Aorist RAo: apusphuṭat -iṣ-Ao: asphoṭīt Perfect pusphoṭa C Causative sphoṭayati etc. E.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: sphuṭita E.+; 1Abs: sphuṭitvā C Derivatives sphuṭa E.+ sphoṭa E.+ sphuṭana C. sphoṭana E.+ Meanings sphuṭati & sphóṭati v burst, split, expand, open, blossom. Caus. sphoṭayati burst or rend asunder, shake, toss. ā Caus. cleave, crush, shake, toss. pra fly open, burst; Caus. cleave. vi burst, split, fly open. 
