   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sphuurj.html"> √ sphūrj    √ sphūrj, “rumble” Present I. sphū́rjati etc. AV.+ Future Simple Future: sphūrjiṣyati Periphrastic Future: sphūrjitā Aorist RAo: apusphūrjat -iṣ-Ao: asphūrjīt Perfect pusphūrja Causative sphūrjáyati etc. V.+ Desiderative pusphūrjiṣa- Intensive posphūrj- Verbal Nouns PPP: sphūrjita E.+; 2Abs: -sphūrjya E.? Derivatives sphūrja C. -sphūrjana C. -sphūrjathu C. -sphūrji C. sphū́rjaka B.+ Meanings sphū́rjati v PPP sphūrjita rumble, roar, thunder; burst forth, appear. Caus. sphṛrjáyati crackle, rustle. abhi & ava roar, thunder. vi rumble, snort; break forth, appear. Cf. visphūrjita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sph_r.html"> √ sphṛ, sphar, sphur, sphul    √ sphṛ, sphar, sphur, sphul, “jerk”etc. Present VI. sphuráti etc. V.+,-te etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: sphuriṣyati Periphrastic Future: sphuritā Aorist RAo: apusphurat -iṣ-Ao: spharīs RV. asphorīt Precative: spūryāt Perfect pusphora pusphure Causative sphārayati etc. E.+; sphurayati C. sphorayati Desiderative pusphuriṣa- Intensive posphur- Verbal Nouns PPP: sphurita E.+, sphulita C1.; 1Abs: spharitvā C Derivatives -sphur RV. -sphāra E.+ sphuraṇa S.+ -sphulíṅga V.+ -sphura V.+ -sphūrti C. Does not seem worth the attempt to divide into different roots, as the whole considerable range of meanings appears in the forms of sphur. Meanings sphar : Caus. sphārayati, PPP sphārita (q.v.) open widely, spread, expand, divulge, w. dhanus etc. bend the bow, shoot off. vi = S. Cf. visphārita. sphur : sphuráti sphuráte v PPP sphurita jerk, dart, kick (trans. & intrans.); quiver, tremble, glitter, sparkle, start into view, appear, arise. apa snap away, withdraw quickly. ava & nis hurl away. pari quiver, throb; glitter, shine; rise, appear. pra kick or hurl away, shake, tremble, quiver etc. = prec. vi fly asunder; tremble, quiver = prec. sphul : PPP sphulita sprung forth, appeared. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_smi.html"> √ smi    √ smi, “smile” Present I. smáyate etc. V.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: smeṣyate Periphrastic Future: smetā Aorist RAo: asiṣmayam -s-Ao: asmeṣṭa -iṣ-Ao: asmayiṣṭhās E Ao/Ps/3/sg: asmāyi Perfect siṣmiyé etc. V.B.; sismiye etc. E.+, sismāya etc. E.+;-smayām āsa E Causative smāpayati etc. E.+ (sismāpayiṣa- in d.); smāyayati C Desiderative sismayiṣa- Intensive seṣmi- Verbal Nouns PPP: smita E.+; 1Abs: smitvā C.,-smayitvā E.; 2Abs: -smitya E Derivatives smaya E.+ smayana S.+ smera RV.C. -smāpanīya C. smayā́ka TA. -smayanīya E.+ -smāpaka C. -smāpayanīya E. smāya C. smetavyà TA. -smāpana E.+ -sismāpayiṣu E. Meanings smáyate smáyati v PPP smita (q.v.) smile, blush, be proud or arrogant. ava blush down (of the dawn). ud smile up (with pride). abhyud & upa smile upon (A). pra break out into a laugh. vi be astounded or surprised by (I, L, or Ab); be proud, boast of (intrans.). Cf. vismita. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sm_r.html"> √ smṛ    √ smṛ“remember” Present I. smárati etc. V.+,-te etc. V.+ Passive smaryáte etc. B.+ Future Simple Future: smariṣyati E Periphrastic Future: smartā E Aorist RAo: asasmarat -s-Ao: asmārṣus M Precative: smaryāt Ao/Ps/3/sg: asmāri Perfect sasmāra sasmarus E Causative smārayati etc. E.+,-te etc. E.+ (smāryate etc. E.+); smarayati etc. C Desiderative susmūrṣa- Intensive sāsmṛ- Verbal Nouns PPP: smṛta V.+; Inf: smartum E.; 1Abs: smṛtvā S.+, smaritvā E.; 2Abs: -smṛtya S.+; smāram C Derivatives smará AV.+ smāraka C. smaraṇa E.+ smṛti AV.+ smarya C. smārin C. smaraṇīya E.+ smartavya E.+ smāra B.+ smāraṇa E.+ -smṛt C. smartṛ C. Meanings smárati smárate v PPP smṛta (q.v.) remember (G or A); recollect, call to mind; hand down, record, declare, teach (esp. P. smaryate be recorded or declared as a law or custom, pass for (N or L). Caus. smārayati & smarayati cause to remember, remind (2A or G of pers. & A of th.). anu remember, collect; confess. Caus. remind. apa lose conscience, forget. upa remember, call to mind (A). pra remember or forget. prati remember; Caus. remind. vi forget; Caus. cause to forget (2A). sam remember (A); Caus. remind of (2A). Cf. anusmṛta, vismṛta, saṃsmṛta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_syand.html"> √ syand, syad    √ syand, syad, “move on” Present I. syándate etc. V.+,-ti etc. E.+ Passive syandyate C Future Simple Future: syantsyáti B. syandiṣyate Periphrastic Future: syanttā, syanditā Aorist √-Ao: syándi ŚB Th Ao: asyadat RAo: ásiṣyadat -danta V -s-Ao: asyān RV -iṣ-Ao: asyandiṣṭa Perfect siṣyanda siṣyadús -de AV.B.; sasyande C.-dimahe -dmahe Causative syandayati etc. B.+ (syandayádhyai RV.) Desiderative sisyandiṣa- , sisyantsa- Intensive sániṣyadat V.B Verbal Nouns PPP: syanná V.+; Inf: syántum B.+; 1Abs: syanttvā́ B., syattvā́ B.; 2Abs: -syadya B.;-syáde RV Derivatives -syad V. syandaka E.+ syandaná V.+ syandrá RV. syáda B. syandin S.+ syédu AV. sasyád RV. syanda B.+ syandyā́ B.S. syánttṛ RV. saniṣyadá AV. Meanings syand syándate syándati v PPP syanná 1 flow, run, drive (in a carriage), hasten. Caus. syandayati = S. accha flow or run to (A). anu run towards or along. abhi the same, overflow. ava flow down. ā & upa run or flow towards (A). ni flow down. pra flow, run; drive away (in a carriage). pari flow around. vi flow forth or over, flow abundantly. sam flow or run together. Cf. víṣyaṇa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sra_ms.html"> √ sraṃs, sras    √ sraṃs, sras, “fall” Present I. sráṃsate etc. B.+,-ti etc. E.+ Passive srasyate Future Simple Future: sraṃsiṣyate Periphrastic Future: sraṃsitā Aorist √-Ao: asrat B Th Ao: asrasat etc. V.+ (srasema RV.) RAo: asisrasat etc. AV.B -iṣ-Ao: asraṃsiṣata B Perfect sasraṃsus B., sraṃsire ? C Causative sraṃsayati etc. AV.+ (sraṃsyate E.) Desiderative sisraṃsiṣa- Intensive sanisras- (in d.) Verbal Nouns PPP: srasta AV.+; 1Abs: sraṃsitvā, srastvā; 2Abs: -sráṃsya B.S., -srasya S.;-srásas V.B.U Derivatives -sras V.B. -srásya B. -sráṃsaka B. sraṃsana E.+ -srásā B.S. sraṃsa AV.+ sraṃsin C. sanisrasá AV. Meanings sráṃsate v (sráṃsati), PPP srasta (q.v.) fall, drop or hang down, decay, perish. Caus. sraṃsayati cause to fall, loosen. ava fall down. vyava fall asunder. vi fall asunder, break down, drop; Caus. cause to drop, loosen. Cf. āsrasta, utsrasta, vísrasta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sridh.html"> √ sridh    √ sridh, “blunder” (?) Present I. srédhati etc. RV Aorist Th Ao: sridhat sridhāna RV Derivatives srídh V. Meanings srédhati 1 v do or go amiss, fail. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sriiv.html"> √ srīv    √ srīv, “fail” Present IV. srīvyanti B1 Future Simple Future: sreviṣyati Periphrastic Future: srevitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: asrevīt Perfect sisreva Causative sreváyant RV., śrīvayati AV Desiderative sisreviṣa- , susrūṣa- Intensive sesrīv Verbal Nouns PPP: srūta , 1Abs: srevitvā srūtvā Derivatives -srīví ? B. -sreman ? RV. Sometimes found written with ś for s. Meanings srīvyati v fail. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_sru.html"> √ sru    √ sru, “flow” Present I. srávati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+; śrúvat RV Future Simple Future: sraviṣyati etc. E. sroṣyati Periphrastic Future: srotā Aorist RAo: ásusrot etc. V.B. asusruvat; asusravat asisravat -iṣ-Ao: asrāvīs JB Perfect susrāva susruvus AV.+ susruma, susruve etc. E.+ Causative srāvayati etc. AV.+,-te etc. B.; sravayati C Desiderative susrūṣa- Intensive sosru- Verbal Nouns PPP: srutá AV.+, śruta AV.; srávitave RV.,-tavaí RV Derivatives srū́ RV. srāvín B.+ sravát V. srótas V.+ sruvá V.+ srāvya E.+ srúc ? V.+ srotyā́ V.B. srava V.+ srávaṇa V.+ -srut V.+ sravátha RV. -sravin C. srāvaṇa AV.+ srútya B. srāvayitavyà MS.S. -srāva AV.+ -sravas E. srutí V.+ Apparent forms and derivatives of this root are occasionally found with initial ś, even in V.; and BR. recognize a root 2 śru, equivalent in meaning with sru. Meanings srávati v (srávate), PPP sruta flow, stream; flow with (I or A); drip, leak (vessel); flow or waste away, perish, be lost. Caus. srāvayati & sravayati cause to flow, spill, shed. ati flow over. adhi flow off (Ab). abhi flow hither. ava flow down; Caus. = anvava Caus. cause to flow down. ā & upa flow towards (A). ni flow down. nis flow asunder or out, flow forth, rise from (abl). pari flow around or abundantly; run away, pass (time). pra flow forth, stream from (Ab); let flow, discharge. abhipra & saṃpra stream forth. vi stream forth, flow from (Ab); let flow, discharge; melt away, perish. sam flow or run together. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_svaj.html"> √ svaj, svañj    √ svaj, svañj, “embrace” Present I. svájate etc. V.+,-ti etc. RV1.E.+ (svajāna E.) Passive svajya- Future Simple Future: svajiṣyate E. svaṅkṣyate Periphrastic Future: svaṅktā Aorist RAo: ásasvajat (plpf.?) RV -s-Ao: asvaṅkṣi Perfect sasvajé etc. V.+,-jus C. sasvañje Causative svañjaya- Desiderative sisvaṅkṣa- Intensive sāsvañj- , sāsvajya- Verbal Nouns PPP: svakta B.+; Inf: svaktum E.; 1Abs: svajitvā E.; 2Abs: -svajya E.+;-sváje V Derivatives svajá AV.B. -svaṅga E.+ -svajana C. -svañjalya AV. -svajya E. -svaṅgin C. -svajīyas AV. Meanings svájate svájati v PPP svakta embrace, encircle. abhi , pari , abhipari, saṃpari & vi (ṣva), sam , abhisam = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_svad.html"> √ svad, svād    √ svad, svād, “sweeten” Present I. svádati -te etc. V.+; svādate RV1 Future Simple Future: svā̆diṣyate Periphrastic Future: svā̆ditā Aorist RAo: asiṣvadat etc. V.B Perfect sasvade C. sasvāde Causative svadáyati -te etc. V.B., svādayati etc. E.+ (svādyate C.) Desiderative sisvā̆diṣa- Intensive sāsvā̆d- Verbal Nouns svāttá V.B.;-súde RV.;-svādam S Derivatives svada- ? RV. -svādya E.+ svādú V.+ svā́dman RV. svāde C. svā́dana RV.C. svā́dīyas V.+ svādmán RV. -svādaka C. svādanīya E. svā́diṣṭha V.+ svādiman C. svādin C. -svādas RV. svadayitṛ́ B. Compare √ sūd, which is perhaps related. Meanings svádati svádate v (svādate), PPP svāttá (q.v.) P sweeten, make savoury or agreeable; P (P.) be sweet or savoury, please; relish, taste, eat, enjoy; delight in (L). Caus. svadayati make savoury, season, cook; make soft i.e. calm, propitiate; svādayati relish, taste, eat. ā & samā (svādayati) relish, eat, enjoy. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_svan.html"> √ svan    √ svan, “sound” Present I. svanati -te etc. E II ? asvanīt RV Future Simple Future: svaniṣyati Periphrastic Future: svanitā Aorist √-Ao: sváni ? RV RAo: asisvanat -iṣ-Ao: svānīt RV Perfect sasvāna sasvanus E.+ svenus Causative svanayati etc. RV.C Desiderative sisvaniṣa- Intensive saniṣvanat RV. saṃsvan- Verbal Nouns PPP: svanita RV Derivatives -svan RV. svāná V.+ -svanas RV. svanáya RV. svaná V.+ svānín RV. sváni RV. Meanings svanati svanate v PPP svanita (q.v.) sound, roar, cry, hum. Caus. svanayati = S. ava cry or roar down. ā sound. pari (saniṣvat 1) clang. pra roar. prati sound back, re-echo. vi roar, howl, sound. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_svap.html"> √ svap    √ svap, “sleep” Present I. svápati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ II. svapiti-panti etc. V.+ (svapihi C., sváptu AV.), svapīta E Passive supyate etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: svapsyati etc. B.+,-te etc. E.+; svapiṣyati AV.,-te E Periphrastic Future: svaptā M Aorist √-Ao: supyāt S.; asvāpi C RAo: siṣvapas síṣvap RV. asūṣupat -s-Ao: asvāpsam etc. S.+ Perfect suṣvāpa suṣupus etc. V.+, suṣupāṇá RV. (suṣupthās B.S.) Causative svāpáyati etc. V.+; svapayati C1 Desiderative suṣupsa- (in d.) Intensive sāsvap- , soṣup- Verbal Nouns PPP: suptá AV.+; Inf: svaptum B.+; 1Abs: suptvā́ AV.+;-svā́pam RV Derivatives -sup RV. svapaná B.C. svaptavya B.+ suṣupsā E. svāpa E.+ svāpana S.+ svapitṛ C. suṣupsu B.+ -svāpin C. supti C. svápna V.+ Meanings svápiti & svápati svapáte v PPP suptá (q.v.) sleep, fall asleep, lie down, repose, be dead. Caus. svāpáyati (svapayati) make sleep, bring to rest, kill. Des suṣupsati wish to sleep. ni go to sleep, die; Caus. put to sleep, kill. pra fall asleep, go to rest, sleep. Caus. put to sleep, lull to rest. Cf. avasupta, prasupta, viṣupta, saṃsupta, saṃprasupta (add.). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_svar.html"> √ svar    √ svar, “sound” Present I. svárati etc. V.B.U.S Future Simple Future: svariṣyati Periphrastic Future: svartā svaritā Aorist RAo: asisvarat -s-Ao: ásvār asvārṣṭām RV -iṣ-Ao: asvārīs JB Perfect sasvāra sasvarus (sasvár ? RV.) Causative svaráyati AV.+ (svaryate C.) svārayati Desiderative sisvariṣa- , susvūrṣa- Intensive sāsvar- Verbal Nouns svaritos JB.;-svāram S Derivatives -svar RV. svaryà RV. sváraṇa RV. sváritṛ RV. svára AV.B. svārá V.+ -svaras RV. -svartṛ RV. svará V.+ -svārya C. svarí ? RV. svarīyas C. sváru ? V.B.S. svarayitavya C. Hardly to be separated from this root are the derivatives showing the radical sense of “brightness”: namely, svàr V.+ sū́ra V.B. sū́rya V.+ sū́rta ? V. -svara U.C. sūrí ? V.+ Meanings svárati 1 v sound, make resound; sing, praise; shine, be bright. Caus. svarayati (P. svaryate) pronounce with the Svarita accent. ati let a sound die away. abhi chime in. ava resound. sam & abhisam salute, invoke. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_svaad.html"> √ svād    √ svād see √ svad. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_svid.html"> √ svid    √ svid, “sweat” Present I. svedate B.U IV. svidyati etc. E.+,-te etc. C Future Simple Future: svetsyati Periphrastic Future: svettā Aorist √-Ao: svidyāt S Th Ao: asvidat RAo: asisvidat Perfect siṣvide E.-dāná RV. siṣveda Causative svedayati etc. B.+ Desiderative siṣvitsa- Intensive seṣvid- Verbal Nouns PPP: svinná AV.+;-svedam B Derivatives svéda V.+ svedin E.+ svedya C. svedana C. svédu- ? RV. Meanings svedate svidyati svedate svidyate v PPP svinná 1 sweat, perspire. Caus. svedayati cause to sweat, make warm, foment. pra begin to sweat, become moist. sam Caus. = S.Caus. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_had.html"> √ had    √ had, “discharge excrement” Present I. hadati C.-te Future Simple Future: hatsyate Periphrastic Future: hattā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: ahatta Perfect jahade Causative hādaya- Desiderative jihatsa- Intensive jāhad- Verbal Nouns PPP: hanna C Derivatives -hāda E.+ -hadana C. Meanings hadati v discharge excrement. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_han.html"> √ han    √ han, “smite” Present I. hanāmi TA., ahanat -nan B.+ I. jíghnate etc. RV.B.,-ti etc. B.; jaghnant E II. hánti hatás ghnánti etc. V.+, hate ghnate etc. V.+ (hanma E.; ghnīya -īta B.C1., hánīta etc. B.; jahí V.+, handhí TA.; ahata 3p. AB.) VI ? aghnam E., ghnata (2p.) E.+, aghnanta ghnamāna E VIII. hanomi PGS Passive hanyáte etc. V.+,-ti E Future Simple Future: haniṣyáti etc. V.+,-te etc. B.+ (ahaniṣyat E.+); haṃsyati E Periphrastic Future: hantā E Aorist RAo: ajīghanat etc. E.+ -s-Ao: ghān ? S. ahasta -iṣ-Ao: ahānīt JB Ao/Ps/3/sg: aghāni Perfect jaghā́na jaghnús etc. V.+ (jaghántha V.; jaghanvā́ṃs V.B., jaghnivā́ṃs B.+; jaghánat RV.), jaghne etc. B.+ Causative ghātayati etc. B.+,-te etc. E.+ (aghātayithās E.) ajīghatat Desiderative jíghāṃsati etc. V.+ (ajighāṃsīs ŚB.),-te etc. E.+ Intensive jáṅghanti etc.-ananta V.B., jaṅghanyate U.; ghánighnat RV.; jījahi ? E. jeghnīya-. Verbal Nouns PPP: hatá V.+, ghāta B.; Inf: hántum V.+,-tave V.B.,-tavaí V.B.S.,-tos V.B., hanitum C1.; 1Abs: hatvā́ V.+,-tvī́ RV.,-tvā́ya V.; 2Abs: -hátya V.+,-hanya E.+;-ghā́tam B.+ Derivatives -han V.+ -hanas ? V.B. hantṛ V.+ jighatnú RV. -ha V.+ hánu ? V.+ hátha RV. jighāṃsā E.+ -hána V.+ -hat RV. hatnú V. jighāṃsu B.+ -gha U.+ hati V.+ hánman V.B. -hāta C. ghaná V.+ -hátya n. V.+ hánīyas B. ghāta B.+ -ghna V.+ hatyā V.+ hániṣṭha RV. ghātaka E.+ -ghnya V.+ -hanti B. jaghána ? V.+ ghātin AV.+ -ghni AV. -hántu V.+ ghanāghaná V.+ ghātya C. -ghnī V.B. hántva V.B. jághni V.S. ghātana E.+ hánana AV.+ hantavya E.+ jáṅghā V.+ ghā́tuka AV.B. Meanings hánti hate jíghnate jíghnati 1 v (hanati), PPP hatá (q.v.) smite, beat, strike, strike down, hew off, hit, pierce, hurt, injure, throw (a spear or an arrow) upon (G or D), slay, kill, destroy (ātmānamātmanā one's self), suppress, give up, abandon. Caus. ghātayati (q.v.). Des jíghāṃsati (te) wish to strike down or kill. Int jáṅghanti (jaṅghanyate) tread upon (L or A) strike, slay, destroy; vex, afflict. apa beat off or out, repel, destroy, unhusk (corn). abhi strike at, beat (drum), smite, afflict, visit, touch. Des wish to strike down. ava throw down, strike, hit; scare away, repel, keep off. ā strike at (L or D, Ā strike a part of one's own body); hit, beat, attack, assault. abhyā hit, strike, wound, impede. pratyā ward off, repel. vyā strike, hit, impede, hinder, keep off. samā beat (together), strike at, hew down, kill. ud force up, raise; root up or out; dig or throw up; Ā hang one's self. upa beat, strike, touch; stick on, fix, fasten; hit, hurt, afflict, damage, destroy. ni strike in or down, hurl upon (L); hit at, touch; attack, assail; slay, destroy, bring to nought. abhini spit, put on; strike at (A). praṇi bring to nought, destroy (Aor G). pratini strike against (A). vini beat, strike down, kill, destroy. saṃni strike at, attack, kill. nis dash out or off, drive away, slay, destroy. parā strike off or down, overthrow; hit, touch. pari strike around, encompass; extinguish (fire). pra beat, strike at (A), hew down, kill. abhipra, (*nipra w. G), & vipra overwhelm. prati strike against (G), strike at, attack (A); strike down, break; pierce, broach; beat back, repel, hinder; frustrate, destroy. vi strike apart, break down, destroy; spread, extend; tear or beat off, repel, resist, frustrate. sam strike together, join or unite closely, conglomerate; strike or break down. P. thicken (intrans.), become firm or solid. Cf. abhihata, āhata, uddhata, vihata, saṃhata, samuddhata. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_har.html"> √ har    √ har, “be gratified” Present IV. háryati -te etc. V.B Future Simple Future: haryiṣyati Periphrastic Future: haryitā Aorist RAo: ajaharyat -iṣ-Ao: aharyīt Perfect jaharya Causative haryaya- Desiderative jiharyiṣa- Intensive jāharya- Derivatives haryatá V.B. Perhaps a derivative from √ hṛ. A conspicuous group of words show an inferable root har or hir “be yellow”: thus, hári V.+ hárita V.+ harimán V. híraṇya V.+ harít V.+ hariṇá V.+ híri- RV. Meanings háryati háryate v be gratified or comfortable, delight in (L), be fond of, desire, like (A). abhi love, long for. ā Ā love, cherish. prati be fond of, long for, also = vi dislike, reject. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_has.html"> √ has    √ has, “laugh” Present I. hásati etc. B.+,-te etc. E.+ Passive hasyate etc. C Future Simple Future: hasiṣyati E.+ Periphrastic Future: hasitā Aorist RAo: ajīhasat -iṣ-Ao: ahasīt Ao/Ps/3/sg: ahāsi C Perfect jahāsa jahasus E.+, jahase C Causative hāsayati etc. C Desiderative jihasiṣa- Intensive jāhasyate E Verbal Nouns PPP: hasita E.+; Inf: hasitum E.; 1Abs: hasitvā E.+; 2Abs: -hasya E.+ Derivatives has- RV. hāsa B.+ hasanā́ RV. hāsana C. hása V.+ hāsaka E. hasana E.+ hasrá RV. hasá AV. hāsin AV.+ hasanīya C. -hásvan RV. -hásya AV. hāsya E.+ Compare the derivative root √ 2 jakṣ. Meanings hásati 2 v (te), PPP hasita (q.v.) laugh, smile; laugh at (I or A), mock, ridicule, cut out. Caus. hāsayati make laugh; mock, ridicule. apa Caus. mock, deride. ava the same. upa smile; (also Caus. ) laugh at, ridicule. pari sport or jest with (A); scoff, deride. pra laugh out (hāsam); laugh with (A); laugh at, ridicule. Caus. make laugh. saṃpra laugh out; c. sport, jest. vi laugh out; mock, deride (A, r. G). saṃvi laugh out, laugh. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_haa.html"> √ 1 hā    √ 1 hā, “leave” Present I. jahat AB.,-hati etc. E.+ III. jáhāti jahati etc. V.+ (jahītam -īta -ītāt AV., jahīhi C. jahihi, jahāhi, jahimas etc. jahitam ajahitām AV.B., jahyāt etc. AV.+) Passive hīyáte etc. V.+ (hī́yate etc. TS.ŚB.), hīyanti E Future Simple Future: hāsyati etc. AV.+,-te etc. B.+; jahiṣyati etc. E.+ Periphrastic Future: hātā Aorist √-Ao: ahāt B.C. RAo: ajījahat C -s-Ao: ahās (3s.) RV., ahāsma hāsus etc. V.B., áhāsi -sthās etc. AV.B -siṣ-Ao: hāsiṣam etc. V.+ Precative: heyāt Ao/Ps/3/sg: ahāyi AV.B. Perfect jahau jahús etc. V.+ (jahā RV. ?), jahe B Causative hāpayati etc. E.+,-te C. (jīhipas RV. ajīhapat.) Desiderative jihāsati etc. C Intensive jāhā- , jehīya- Verbal Nouns PPP: hīná V.+, hāta, C., hāna AB., jahitá V.+; Inf: hātum B.+; 1Abs: hitvā́ V.+,-tvī́ RV.,-tvā́ya RV. hītvā; 2Abs: -hā́ya B.+;-hī́yam TS Derivatives -hā V.B. -hāyya B. -hi ? C. jihāsā C. -ha E.+ hāna B.+ heya C. jihāsu C. hāyaka E. -hāyas V.+ -hāvarī MS. jáhā̆ka B. hāyin JB. hātavya E.+ hāpana C. jahana C. hāni U.S.+ -hāpanīya C. Compare the next root. Two or three of the forms given above show the establishment of a secondary root-form jah. Meanings jahāti 2 v (jahati), PPP hīná & jahíta (q.v.) leave, forsake, abandon; emit, discharge, take off, cast aside, remove; give up, avoid, shun, lose. P.Ā hīyáte (hī́yate, ti) be left etc., remain behind, come short or be deprived of (Ab or I); come to harm, be a loser, fail (in a lawsuit etc.); decrease, wane, perish, be lost. Caus. hāpayati, te neglect, omit, give up, miss, lose. Des jihāsati wish to leave etc. apa leave, abandon; P.Ā fall short, decrease. ava leave, relinquish, give up. P.Ā remain behind, fall short or be deficient. ni P.Ā fall short, fail, be deprived of (I). pari leave, desert, forsake, omit, neglect, overlook. P.Ā be left etc., be deficient or wanting, decrease, wane, cease, vanish; fall short, fail; desist from, be deprived of (Ab). pra leave, abandon, give up, resign. P.Ā be left or omitted, cease, vanish, succumb, lose. vipra leave, quit, resign. prati disregard; P.Ā fail, lose. vi leave, desert, forsake, give up, lose, resign; cease, desist. P.Ā stay behind, yield to (Ab); be diminished or lost. pravi & prativi give up, abandon. sam leave (together); give up, resign. Cf. apahāya, nihīna (add.), parihīṇa, prahīṇa, vihāya, vihīna, hitvā́. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_haa.html"> √ 2 hā    √ 2 hā, “go forth” Present III. jíhīte jíhate etc. V.+ (jihīthām ŚB.) Passive hāyate Future Simple Future: hāsyate etc. B.E Periphrastic Future: hātā Aorist -s-Ao: ahāsta etc. V.+ Perfect jahiré AV Causative hāpayati etc. AV.B. ajīhapat Desiderative jihīṣate AV. ? Intensive jāhā- Verbal Nouns PPP: hāna B.; Inf: hā́tum B.E.; 1Abs: hātvā; 2Abs: -hā́ya V.+ This is only the middle conjugation of √ 1 hā, with the signification slightly weakened or generalized. The forms of the two cannot everywhere be distinctly separated, and one or two of the derivatives given under √ 1 hā have an equal or better claim to be placed here. Compare also √ hās, which is a secondary form of √ 1 hā & √ 2 hā (doubtless through the aorist-stem). Meanings jíhīte v PPP hāna 1 (only – ṃ) start up, go forth, move on; run away from, yield (D); rush upon (A), fly (arrow). ati leap or pass over. anu run after, follow, overtake, catch. apa run away. abhi catch, take. ud start up, rise, run away, escape. abhyud ascend with (A). prod rise, ascend. pratyud rise towards (A). samud rise, appear. ni descend, stoop. pra start up or off. vi burst open, gape. Caus. (hāpayati) open (trans.). sam arise, stand up. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_haas.html"> √ hās    √ hās, “go emulously” Present I. hā́sate etc. V Causative hāsayanti RV A secondary form of √ 1 hā, √ 2 hā (hā́sante AV. iv. 36. 5 is omitted in the Atharva-Veda Index). Meanings hā́sate v go emulously; Caus. hāsáyati. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_hi.html"> √ hi    √ hi, “impel” Present I. hínvati etc. V.+ jighyati -tu AB. háyant RV.TS. hiṣe (1s.) RV V. hinóti hinvánti etc. V.+, hinvé etc. V. (hinviré RV.) Passive hīyate C Future Simple Future: heṣyati etc. E.+ Periphrastic Future: hetā Aorist √-Ao: áhema áhetana ahyan heta RV., hiyāná RV.S. Th Ao: ahyam ? AV RAo: ajīhayat -s-Ao: ahaiṣīt B. (áhait AV.), aheṣata RV Precative: hīyāt Perfect jighāya jighyus B.+ Causative hāyaya- Desiderative jighīṣa- Intensive jeghīya- Verbal Nouns PPP: hitá V.+; -hyè RV Derivatives háya V.+ hetí V.+ hetṛ RV. hinvá RV. -héya AV.B. hetú V.+ -héman V.B. héṣas ? RV. -hit B. hétva RV. hemán RV. -hāyyà AV. -hiti RV. hetavya C. hítvan RV. Probably another form of √ 1 hā & √ 2 hā, with causative value. Some of its uses are equivalent with those of √ 1 hā & √ 2 hā; and the stem jighya perhaps belongs directly to the latter. Meanings hinóti hinute hínvati 1 v (háyati), PPP hitá impel, urge on, set in motion, hurl, send forth (Ā intrans. hasten, speed); further, help to (D); get, procure. ā Ā bring near. pra (hiṇoti) urge on, impel, hurl, cast, turn upon (D or L); call upon, summon; send out, dismiss, dispatch to (D, G antikam or pārśvam, A prati), in order to (D or Inf); bring near, get, procure, furnish. anupra send after. abhipra send hither. upapra send to (A). pratipra send or drive back. sam send out; bring together, join, combine, compose. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_hi_ms.html"> √ hiṃs    √ hiṃs, “injure” Present I. hiṃsati -te etc. B.+ VII. hinásti híṃsanti etc. V.+ (hiṃsyā́t etc. B.+; ahinat 3s. B.; hiṃsi 2s. E.), híṃste etc. V.B Passive hiṃsyate V.+ Future Simple Future: hiṃsiṣyati -te etc. B.+ Periphrastic Future: hiṃsitā Aorist RAo: ajihiṃsat -iṣ-Ao: ahiṃsīt etc. V.+ Perfect jihiṃsa -simá AV.B.S. (jíhiṃsīs AV.) Causative hiṃsayati E Desiderative jíhiṃsiṣati ŚB Intensive jehiṃs- Verbal Nouns PPP: hiṃsitá AV.+; Inf: hiṃsitum B.+, híṃsitos B.; 1Abs: hiṃsitvā AV.B.; 2Abs: -hiṃsya E Derivatives hiṃsā B.+ hiṃsaka E.+ hiṃsana E.+ hiṃsitavyà AV. hiṃsya S.+ hiṃsanīya E.+ hiṃsrá V.+ Probably an abbreviated desiderative of √ han. Meanings hinásti híṃste hiṃsati v PPP hiṃsitá (q.v.) injure, hurt, harm, kill, destroy. Caus. hiṃsayati the same. Des jíhiṃsiṣati wish to injure etc. upa & vi = S. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_hikk.html"> √ hikk    √ hikk, “sob” Present I. hikkati -te etc. C Future Simple Future: hikkiṣyati -te Periphrastic Future: hikkitā Aorist RAo: ajihikkat -iṣ-Ao: ahikkīt ahikkiṣṭa Perfect jihikka -de Causative hikkayati C Desiderative jihikkiṣa- Intensive jehikk- Derivatives hikkā E.+ hikkin C. Meanings hikkati v PPP hikkita (v. seq.) sob. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_hi_n_d.html"> √ hiṇḍ    √ hiṇḍ, “roam” Present I. ahiṇḍanta C1 Future Simple Future: hiṇḍiṣyate Periphrastic Future: hiṇḍitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: ahiṇḍiṣṭa Perfect jihiṇḍe Derivatives -hiṇḍaka E.+ -hiṇḍuka E.+ The single occurrence is probably artificial. Meanings hiṇḍate v w. to go, move, wander or roam about; to disregard, slight. ā roam. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_hii_d.html"> √ hīḍ, hel    √ hīḍ, hel, “be hostile” Present I. heḍant RV., heḍamāna RV., helamāna E., hīḍamāna B.; ahiḍat ? GB Future Simple Future: heḍiṣyate Periphrastic Future: heḍitā Aorist RAo: ajīhiḍat AV. ajiheḍat -iṣ-Ao: hīḍiṣātām TA Perfect jihīḍa RV. (jīhīḍa AV.), jihīḍé etc. V.B Causative heḍayant RV. (helayām āsa C.), helayate E Verbal Nouns PPP: hīḍitá V.B Derivatives hīḍá ? RV. helā E.+ helana E.+ héḍas V.B. héḍa V. -héḍana V. helanīya C. helitavya E. Meanings (heḍati, heḷate, helate), PPP hīḍitá P vex, afflict; Ā be angry or hostile. Caus. pluck out. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_hu.html"> √ hu    √ hu, “sacrifice” Present II. hoṣi RV1 III. juhóti júhvati etc. V.+, juhuté júhvate etc. V.+ (juhudhí B.S., jugvant E.+, ajuhavus V.B., -huvus ŚB. ?) Passive hūyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: hoṣyáti etc. AV.+,-te E. (ahoṣyat B.) Periphrastic Future: hotā Aorist RAo: ajūhavat -s-Ao: ahauṣīt etc. B.+ Precative: hūyāt Ao/Ps/3/sg: áhāvi RV. Perfect juhāva juhuvus E., juhuve E., juhvire B. (juhvé juhuré RV.); juhavā́ṃ cakāra etc. B.U Causative hāvayati etc. S.+ Desiderative juhūṣati etc. S.+ (juhuṣet ? GGS.) Intensive johavīti C Verbal Nouns PPP: hutá V.+; Inf: hótum B.S.,-tavaí B.S.,-tos B.S.; 1Abs: hutvā B.+ Derivatives -hava E.+ havís V.+ hótṛ ? V.+ hóman RV. havyá V.+ -hut V.B.S. hotrá V.+ -hoṣa RV. -hāva RV. -huti V.B. hótrā V.+ juhū́ V.+ hávana V.B.S. hotavyà B.+ hóma AV.+ juhūṣu C. Meanings juhóti juhuté v PPP hutá (q.v.) pour into the fire, cast into the fire, offer, sacrifice. Caus. hāvayati cause to sacrifice or be sacrificed. Des juhvaṣati wish to sacrifice. Int johavīti sacrifice repeatedly. adhi sacrifice upon or over (L). abhi pour out the libation upon, make an oblation to (A). ava pour out upon (L). ā offer in (L), offer an oblation to (D), worship with oblations (A). upa offer in addition. pra offer continually or successively. prati offer in return. sam sacrifice (together). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_hur.html"> √ hur    √ hur see √ hvṛ. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_huu.html"> √ hū, hvā, hve    √ hū, hvā, hve, “call” Present I. hávate etc. V.B II. hóma RV.,-hvatī KŚS., hūte K., hūmáhe RV III. juhūmási RV IV ? hváyati -te etc. V.+ (hvayāna E.) VI ? huvé etc. V.B. (huvéya etc. áhuve etc. huvāná V.B.; hve AV., hvāmahe VS.), huvat -véma -vánt RV Passive hūyáte etc. V.+ Future Simple Future: hvayiṣyati -te B., hvāsyate S Periphrastic Future: hvātā Aorist √-Ao: ahvi AV., áhūmahi RV. Th Ao: áhvat etc. V.B., ahvata etc. V.B RAo: ajūhavat -s-Ao: ahūṣata RV. ahvāsta -siṣ-Ao ? ahvāsīt GB Precative: hūyāt; Ao/Ps/3/sg: ahvāyi Perfect juhā́va juhuvus V.+, juhvé juhūré RV., juhuve -vire B.; hvayām āsa E., hvayāṃ cakre E Causative hvāyaya- (in d.) Desiderative juhūṣati B Intensive jóhavīti etc. V.C., johuvanta jóhuvāna V.B Verbal Nouns PPP: hūtá V.+; hávītave RV., hváyitum B.,-tavaí B.S., Inf: hvātum C.; 1Abs: hūtvā́ C.; 2Abs: -hū́ya B.+; huvádhyai RV.; -hāvam B.S Derivatives -hū V.+ huvana- RV. hótrā V.+ -hváyana E. -hū́ya V.B. hávana V.+ hóman RV. hvāna B.+ háva V.+ havás RV. hávīman RV. hvātavya C. havín AV.B. hūti V.+ haviṣṭha ? C. -hvayitavya E. hávya V.+ -hávītu RV. -hvā C. hvātṛ E.+ hávyā RV. -hūtavya C1. -hva AV.C. jihvā́ ? V.+ -hāva B.+ hótṛ V.+ -hvaya E.+ johū́tra RV.AA. -hvāyaka C. -hvāyayitavya C. Meanings (hvā), hváyati, hváyate, hávate, huváte, huváti etc., PPP hūtá call (avase or ūtaye for help), call upon, invoke, summon, invite, challenge (yuddhe to fight). Caus. hvāyayati & Des juhūṣati (only – ṃ). Int jóhavīti etc. call, invoke. ati call over. anu call again or back. abhi call near. ava call down or hither. ā call to or hither, invite, summon (r. & j.); utter, recite; Ā challenge. Caus. cause to invite or challenge. Int. call near, invoke. upā Ā invite, summon, challenge. pratyā answer a call. samā convoke, assemble, invite, challenge. ud call forth, elicit. upa Ā (P) call upon, summon or invite to (A, D, or L); call encouragingly to, approve, praise. paryupa & pratyupa call near. samupa convoke, assemble, invite; provoke, challenge. ni Ā call down, in, or near. nis call off. pra invoke. pratipra call to (A). prati invoke. vi Ā call hither and thither or emulously, quarrel about (A); call off. sam Ā convoke. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_huurch.html"> √ hūrch    √ hūrch, “fall away” Present I. hūrchati etc. B.U Future Simple Future: hūrchiṣyati Periphrastic Future: hūrchitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: ahūrchīt Perfect juhūrcha Causative hūrchayati B Verbal Nouns PPP: hūrchita hūrṇa Probably related with √ hvṛ. Meanings hū́rchati v fall away; Caus. hūrchayati cause to fall away. anu fall after (A). vi waddle, stagger, slip, fail. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_1_h_r.html"> √ 1 hṛ    √ 1 hṛ, “take” Present I. hárati etc. V.+,-te etc. V.+ II. harmi RV1 III. jiharti S1 Passive hriyáte etc. AV.+,-ti etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: hariṣyati -te etc. B.+ (ahariṣyat etc. B.U.) Periphrastic Future: hartā B.E Aorist √-Ao: ahṛthās JB.; ahāri C. hriyāt RAo: ajīharat -s-Ao: ahārṣīt etc. V.B.U.S.E. (ahār AV.B.; hāriṣīt S1.), ahṛṣata RV. hṛṣīṣṭa Perfect jahāra jahrus etc. AV.+ (jahártha B.+; jaharus ? AV.), jahre etc. B.+ Causative hārayati etc. B.+,-te etc. B.S. (hāryate etc. E.+); harayanta RV1 Desiderative jíhīrṣati etc. AV.+ (-ṣayte C.) Intensive jarīharti C. jarhṛ-, jehrīya- Verbal Nouns PPP: hṛtá V.+; Inf: hártum B.+,-tave C1., -tavaí B.S.,-tos B.S., haritum R1.; 1Abs: hṛtvā B.S.;-hṛ́tya AV.+; 2Abs: -hā́ram B.+ Derivatives -hara U.S.+ háraṇa AV.+ -hṛt V.+ jihīrṣā E.+ hāra V.+ -haraṇīya E.+ hṛti B.+ jihīrṣu E.+ -hāraka E.+ -hāraṇa C. -hṛ́tya B. -hārayitavya C. hārin E.+ háras V.+ hartavya E.+ hāryà AV.+ hā́ruka B. hartṛ B.+ Apparently a variant to √ bhṛ; making a very small figure in the oldest language, it gains rapidly in use, and becomes extremely common. Meanings hárati hárate v (harti, jiharti), PPP hṛtá (q.v.) P hold, carry, bring; offer, present (esp. balim); hand over to (G); seize, steal, carry away, remove, turn off (face); Ā (P) take, receive (taxes), come into possession of (as heir); take to wife, marry; get hold or become master of; overpower, outdo, surpass; win over, captivate, charm; seize upon, take away, withdraw, retain, destroy, frustrate. Caus. hārayati cause to hold or carry (2A), cause to be held, taken etc. by (I); get hold of, seize upon; permit to be carried of, lose (esp. in game). Des jíhīrṣati wish to take away, desire, covet. ati carry beyond (A). vyati transpose mutually. adhi carry over (A). anu imitate, resemble (A or G). apa carry away, take off, remove, separate from (Ab); seize, rob, steal; overpower, frustrate, destroy. abhi hand over, offer, present; Caus. place before, serve (food), put on (mail). ava draw in, move down, put off. abhyava throw down into (A), bring near, take, eat, enjoy. Caus. cause to throw or be thrown; attack, assail; eat, feed. vyava move hither and thither; transpose, exchange; communicate or have intercourse with (I or L); meet, encounter (as foes), fight with (I sārdham); proceed, act, deal with (L); trade or traffic (L, I, or G); be active, work; be intent upon (A); *bet, play (w. G of stake); *manage, use, employ (A). P. be called or named. ā bring near, attract, fetch, get, procure, offer, present, give; receive, accept; take to wife, marry; eat, enjoy; take away, sever, remove, destroy, turn off, withdraw from (Ab); utter show, betray; name, call. Caus. cause to bring near etc., cause to pay (taxes etc., 2A); procure, acquire; eat, enjoy; utter, manifest. Des be willing to procure or acquire. anvā repair, complete, supply. abhyā offer, present. udā bring near, fetch, bring out, say, tell, quote (esp. as an example), recite, enumerate, praise, commend; P. be called, mentioned, or quoted. abhyudā bring hither. prabhyudā answer; quote (as a counter example). samudā say, tell, mention. upā fetch, get, procure, offer, present, take hold of, win, acquire, undertake, accomplish. samupā fetch, procure, offer, present, undertake, commence. upanyā offer, present. paryā hand over; turn, invert. pratyā draw back, withdraw, get back, recover; take up again, carry on, prosecute; utter, tell, report. vyā bring out, utter, speak to or with (A or saha), sing (of birds). anuvyā utter successively or in its turn, (answer by singing*); abuse, revile, curse. abhivyā utter, pronounce, recite; bespeak, charm with words, conjure, curse. Caus. (cause to) utter or pronounce. pravyā utter, speak. samā bring together, gather, collect, assemble, combine, comprehend; draw back, withdraw, bring back, restore; captivate, charm. anusamā arrange or put in order (again). ud take out or from (Ab), stretch out (pāṇim); offer, present; lift up, raise, further, strengthen; set aside, select; choose, prefer; extricate, rescue, save; take away, cut off, sever (head), remove, destroy; except. Caus. (cause to) draw out or rescue. Des wish to save or relieve. abhyud take or draw out (in addition), lay aside; rescue, save, recover; start, further, promote. samabhyud, prod & pratyud draw out, lift up, rescue, relieve, promote, further. samud draw or take out, rescue, deliver from (Ab); deduct; remove, destroy; lift up etc. = prec. upa bring, fetch, proffer, present; Ā accept, receive, gather, collect. Caus. proffer, serve (food). nis take or carry out, extract, export (goods); Ā remove, exclude or deliver from (Ab); get rid of (A); change or mix with (I). vinis draw out, extract, take (vṛddhim interest); remove, destroy. pari carry or move about; surround, gird (Ā refl.); protect from (Ab); keep off, shun, avoid, beware, escape; save, spare, except. vipari transpose, interchange. pra stretch forth; fix in, hurl upon (L); offer, present; strike, hurt; attack, assail (A, L, D, or G); Ā fight, make war. anupra throw into the fire. saṃpra hurl, cast; attack, assail (A or L); Ā (P) engage in battle, fight hand to hand. prati throw, hold, or bring back; offer, present. Ā take, eat. vi take apart, divide, separate; take or carry away; shed (tears); transpose, interchange; roam about, pass one's time (A) pleasantly, enjoy one's self. sam bring or draw together, contract, collect, gather; take away, rob; suppress, absorb, destroy. upasam draw together or in, gather, contract, absorb, suppress. pratisam draw together or back, take off, avert, absorb, suppress, destroy, annihilate. Cf. abhivyā́hṛta (sic!), uddhṛta, vihṛta, vyāhṛta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_2_h_r.html"> √ 2 hṛ    √ 2 hṛ, “be angry” Present IX. hṛṇīté etc. V. (ahṛṇāt KB.?) Derivatives hṛṇāy- hṛṇīy- V. Compare the √ bhur beside √ bhṛ. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_h_r_s.html"> √ hṛṣ    √ hṛṣ, “be excited” Present I. hárṣate etc. V.C1., hárṣant RV1 IV. hṛṣyati etc. V1.B.+,-te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: harṣiṣyati Periphrastic Future: harṣitā Aorist Th Ao: ahṛṣat E RAo: ajīhṛṣat, ajaharṣat Perfect jaharṣa jahṛṣus E.+, jahṛṣe -ṣire E.+ (jāhṛṣāṇá RV.) Causative harṣáyati etc. V.+,-te V.E Desiderative jiharṣiṣa- Intensive jarhṛṣanta RV., járhṛṣāṇa V.B. jarīhṛṣ- Verbal Nouns PPP: hṛṣitá V.+, hṛṣṭa E.+; 2Abs: -hṛṣya E.+ Derivatives harṣa B.+ hárṣaṇa AV.+ harṣú- RV.E.+ ghṛ́ṣu RV. harṣaka E.+ hṛ́ṣī- RV.E.+ hṛṣṭi C. ghṛ́ṣvi RV. harṣin V.+ hárṣi RV. Meanings hṛṣyati hṛṣyate v (hárṣate, hṛṣyati, hṛṣyate (hárṣati), PPP hṛṣṭa & hṛṣitá (q.v.) be excited (with pleasure or fear), be delighted or amazed; bristle, stand on end (the hair). Caus. harṣáyati, harṣáyate cause (the hair) to bristle or stand erect; excite, make impatient, rejoice (trans. & intrans.). Int (jarhṛṣanta & járhṛṣāṇa) be very impatient or much excited. anu be excited or rejoice with (A). abhi & samabhi Caus. gladden. ud be excited, impatient, or glad. Caus. excite, gladden. pari & saṃpari Caus. delight greatly, enrapture. pra be merry, rejoice. saṃpra the same; Caus. gladden. prati be glad in return. sam be excited, rejoice, exult. Caus. gladden, delight. Cf. parihṛṣṭa, prahṛṣṭa, proddhṛṣita (add.), saṃhṛṣṭa. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_he_th.html"> √ heṭh    √ heṭh The apparent derivative vi-heṭhaka (or-ṭaka) M1. is probably only a misreading for-ḍaka; and vi-heṭhā C1. a like case or artificial. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_he_d.html"> √ heḍ, hel    √ heḍ, hel see √ hīḍ. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_he_s.html"> √ heṣ    √ heṣ, “whinney Present I. héṣati etc. V.+,-te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: heṣiṣyate Periphrastic Future: heṣitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: aheṣiṣṭa Perfect jiheṣire C Verbal Nouns PPP: heṣita E.+ Derivatives heṣá- ? RV. heṣā C. héṣas ? RV. Meanings héṣati héṣate v PPP heṣita (q.v.) neigh. abhi & prati neigh to. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_hnu.html"> √ hnu    √ hnu, “hide” Present I. hnave B.S., hnavanti E1 II. hnuté etc. V.+, hnauti (hnoti ?) E., hnutas RV., hnuyāt C Future Simple Future: hnoṣyate Periphrastic Future: hnotā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: ahnoṣṭa Perfect juhnuve Causative hnāvaya- Desiderative juhnūṣa- Intensive johnu- Verbal Nouns PPP: hnutá AV.+; Inf: hnotum C.; 2Abs: -hnutya C Derivatives -hnava B.+ -hnavana S.+ -hnuti C. -hnavāyya RV. -hnuvana S. -hnotṛ C. Meanings hvu : hvuté v (hvauti, hvate, hvati)* hide from (D). apa Ā conceal from (Ab), refuse, deny; satisfy (D), apologize. ni Ā make amends for (A) to (D), expiate; refuse, deny; hide, conceal (w. ātmānam refl.*). apani & vini hide, conceal, deny. Cf. nihvuta. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_hras.html"> √ hras    √ hras, “shorten” Present I. hrasati -te etc. S.+ Future Simple Future: hrasiṣyati Periphrastic Future: hrasitā Aorist RAo: ajihrasat -iṣ-Ao: ahrāsīt Perfect jahrāsa Causative hrāsayati etc. S.+ Desiderative jihrasiṣa- Intensive jāhras- Verbal Nouns PPP: hrasta S., hrasita C Derivatives hrāsa S.+ hrāsana C. hrásiṣṭha B. hrasvá B.+ hrāsanīya C. hrásīyas B.+ Meanings hrasati hrasate v (nis) become less or short; Caus. diminish. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_hraad.html"> √ hrād    √ hrād, “make a noise” Present I. hrādate etc. S.+ Future Simple Future: hrādiṣyate Periphrastic Future: hrāditā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: ahrādiṣṭa Perfect jahrāde Causative hrādayati etc. B.+ Verbal Nouns PPP: hrādita C Derivatives hrāda B.+ hrādin E.+ -hrādana E.+ -hrādi U.E. Meanings hrādate v sound, make a noise; Caus. hrādayati make resound. ni & nis Caus. = S.Caus. , beat (a drum). sam knock together (intrans.). Caus. the same (trans.); sound loudly. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_hrii.html"> √ hrī    √ hrī, “be ashamed” Present III. jihreti etc. B.+ (jíhriyat MS.) Future Simple Future: hreṣyati Periphrastic Future: hretā Aorist √-Ao: -hrayāṇa ? RV. -s-Ao: ahraiṣīt Precative: hrīyāt Perfect jihrāya C. jihrayām āsa Causative hrepayati etc. C. ajihripat Desiderative jihrīṣa- Intensive jehrīyate C Verbal Nouns PPP: hrīta B.+, hrīṇa E Derivatives hrī́ B.+ -hraya RV. hrīti E. hrepaṇa C. -hri RV. Meanings jihreti v PPP hrīta 1 (& hrīṇa) be ashamed or abashed. Caus. hrepayati put to shame, confound. Int jehrīyate be greatly ashamed. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_hru.html"> √ hru    √ hru see √ hvṛ. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_hre_s.html"> √ hreṣ    √ hreṣ, “neigh” Present I. hreṣati -te etc. E.+ Future Simple Future: hreṣiṣyate Periphrastic Future: hreṣitā Aorist -iṣ-Ao: ahreṣiṣṭa Perfect jihreṣe Causative hreṣayati etc. E Verbal Nouns PPP: hreṣita E.+ Derivatives hreṣin E. hreṣuka E. Meanings hreṣati hreṣate v PPP hreṣita (v. seq.) neigh. Caus. hreṣayati cause to neigh. 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_hlaad.html"> √ hlād    √ hlād, “refresh” Present I. hlādate etc. C Future Simple Future: hlādiṣyate Periphrastic Future: hlāditā Aorist RAo: ajihladat -iṣ-Ao: ahlādiṣṭa Perfect jahlāde Causative hlādayati -te etc. TA1.E.+ (ahlādayiṣata C.) Verbal Nouns PPP: hlanna Derivatives hradá V.+ hlādaka V.C. hlāduka TA. -hlādayitṛ C. hlāda U.+ hlādin E.+ hlāduni C. hlādana E.+ hrādúni V.B.U. Only one or two late sporadic forms outside the causative conjugation; and the proper form of the root seems to be hlad (or hrad). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_hval.html"> √ hval    √ hval, “go wrong” Present I. hválati etc. ŚB.E.+,-te E Future Simple Future: hvaliṣyati Periphrastic Future: hvalitā Aorist RAo: ajihvalat -iṣ-Ao: ahvālīt Perfect jahvāla Causative hvaláyati ŚB. hvālayati Verbal Nouns PPP: hvalita E.+; hválitos ŚB.;-hvā́lam ŚB.S Derivatives -hvala E.+ hvalā́ ŚB. -hvalin C. hvāla S. Is only a specialized form of the following root, √ hvṛ, hru, hur. Meanings hvalati v (hvalate) go wrong, stagger, fail. Caus. hvaláyati shake. vi stagger, tremble. Cf. vihvalita (add.). 
   <a target="_blank" href="http://www.warnemyr.com/skrgram/grammar/roots/root_hv_r.html"> √ hvṛ, hru, hur    √ hvṛ, hru, hur, “be or make crooked” Present I.-hvarant hvárate RV III ? juhuras RV., juhūrthās juhuranta -rāṇá RV IX. hruṇāti RV. hvṛṇāti Passive hvaryate Future Simple Future: hvadiṣyati ? TA Periphrastic Future: hvartā Aorist RAo: jihvaras V.,-ratam VS. (jīhv- TS.TA.) -s-Ao: hvārṣīt etc. B. (hvār B., hvāriṣus K.) Precative: hvaryāt Ao/Ps/3/sg: ahvāri Perfect jahvāra jahvartha jahvarus Causative hvārayati etc. B Desiderative juhvūrṣa- Intensive jāhvṛ- , jarīhvṛ- Verbal Nouns PPP: hvṛta RV., hvarita, hrutá V.+ Derivatives -hū́rya RV. hvārá V. -hvṛt RV. -hvṛti V.+ -hvara V.+ hurás RV. hrút V.B. -hruti V.C. ? hvaraka C. hváras V.B. Meanings hvarate v (only – ṃ), PPP hvṛta go crookedly, bend over, fall. Caus. hvārayati cause to go crookedly (fig.), lead astray; Ā deviate, go astray. ā lead astray or into trouble. upa go crookedly. vi stagger, fall; Caus. overturn. 
